{"abstract":"Opgavesamling til Lærebog om indkomstskat rummer flere end 400 test din viden-spørgsmål og over 200 opgaver, der kan anvendes som forberedelse til en skriftlig eller mundtlig eksamen i skatteret. I nogle opgaver ligger fokus på den juridiske afvejning, mens andre har mere fokus på konkrete beregninger. Opgavesamlingen kan derfor bruges ved professionshøjskoler og universiteter, for eksempel på jura-, erhvervsjura- og revisorkandidatstudiet.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Larsen, Anders","Rasmussen, Rene Yssing","Andersen, Henrik Vestergaard","Christensen, Jacob Engelsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-823521"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Eksamen","Opgavesamling","Skatteret"],"level":"edu","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opgavesamling til lærebog om indkomstskat 000000000002 udgave","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-823521","ids":["aau-5ce8ff86-6fe7-4a27-a3ab-49362078fe8f"],"keyword":["Opgavesamling","eksamen","skatteret"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A14F59440C879257533334D97AD3A340"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Law","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Law, Forskningsgruppen - Offentligret","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences and Humanities, Department of Law, Tax Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"larsenped","last":"Larsen","locid":"8c9066bf-83e3-4bac-b587-9341d328d70c","name":"Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-0179-0203","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rene Yssing","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fd2fdd34-9ce7-4e2e-8126-d161b9a2210c","name":"Rasmussen, Rene Yssing","orcid":"0000-0002-6245-3086","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Vestergaard","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"b0cfa509-97c4-418b-9300-6aa78305c651","name":"Andersen, Henrik Vestergaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jacob Engelsted","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"071df8fc-f593-4ea4-a797-105a050d41c6","name":"Christensen, Jacob Engelsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"publisher":"Djøf Forlag","publisher_org":"DJØF Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5ce8ff86-6fe7-4a27-a3ab-49362078fe8f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Opgavesamling til Lærebog om indkomstskat (2. udgave)","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-823521","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION Metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease (MASLD) is an increasing health challenge, with early diagnosis hindered by the lack of reliable and non-invasive biomarkers. The fatty acid transporter, CD36, plays a significant role in ectopic liver fat accumulation during MASLD development. Extracellular vesicle (EV) secretion is modulated by lipotoxicity and likely represent the phenotype of the cell of origin. MATERIALS AND METHODS Using high-resolution flow cytometry (hFCM) and our in-house-developed EV Array technology for high-throughput multiplexed phenotyping of EVs, our study is the first to characterize and report levels of circulating liver-derived and CD36+ EVs directly in plasma of obese individuals with MASLD (n=36) compared with obese (n=25) or lean (n=27) control individuals without MASLD. Moreover, these EV populations were assessed in the MASLD group before (baseline) and during weight-loss intervention (1 month and 5 months). RESULTS Using a panel of antibodies and labels to CD9, lactadherin (EV markers), asialoglycoprotein receptor 1 (ASGR1, liver marker), and CD36, hFCM analysis revealed that at baseline, liver-EVs were significantly increased in the MASLD group compared with the lean control group, while CD36+-EVs were significantly increased in the MASLD group compared with either control group. During the weight loss intervention, levels of liver-derived EVs, CD36⁺ EVs, and liver-EVs expressing CD36 were significantly reduced in the MASLD group as early as 1 month, with further reductions observed after 5 months. Preliminary results from EV Array analysis confirm these findings and reveal a significant correlation between CD36⁺ EVs and ectopic liver fat accumulation. CONCLUSION Our study advances the understanding of EVs in the development of MASLD and introduces a novel approach for characterizing organ-specific circulating EV phenotypes. Profiling the composition of these EV populations offers valuable insights into organ physiology and opens new avenues for biopsy-free diagnosis and monitoring of complex diseases such as MASLD.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Mellergaard, Maiken","Askeland, Anders","Rasmussen, Rikke Wehner","Eschen, Rikke Bülow","Lund Cliff, Katja","Donoso-Quezada, Javier","Bæk, Rikke","Christiansen, Gunna","Nielsen, Morten Hjuler","Jørgensen, Malene Møller","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Handberg, Aase"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-824106"],"event":{"end":"2025-08-22","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2025-08-20","title":"Nordic Flow Cytometry Meeting 2025","year":"2025"},"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamics of circulating liver derived and cd000000000036 extracellular vesicles in metabolic dysfunction associated steatotic liver disease during weight loss intervention","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://nfcm2025.dk/abstract/abstract-book","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-824106","ids":["aau-e7d26dd5-feda-4af9-bfbd-415046c79afb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0D6E2526808A87E32BA818E432ABA58E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://nfcm2025.dk/abstract/abstract-book","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Clinical Biochemistry","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maiken Mellergaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ba98915c-bd5d-4479-a18e-3c88e5e4e342","name":"Mellergaard, Maiken","name_org":"Pedersen, Maiken Mellergaard","orcid":"0000-0001-5854-1086","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"askelandpau","last":"Askeland","locid":"599f7daa-6bf9-4143-a5fa-0ad3063e296b","name":"Askeland, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Wehner","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"15fe53bf-9686-43ba-b76f-7af29863558d","name":"Rasmussen, Rikke Wehner","orcid":"0009-0006-7499-8821","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke Bülow","key":"eschenpau","last":"Eschen","locid":"5ca11a78-d0ec-492d-b179-2781b41f71b6","name":"Eschen, Rikke Bülow","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katja","key":"lundcliffpau","last":"Lund Cliff","name":"Lund Cliff, Katja","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Javier","key":"donosoquezadapau","last":"Donoso-Quezada","locid":"e634719c-ec3b-42b3-92a5-cde604eefd92","name":"Donoso-Quezada, Javier","orcid":"0000-0003-2225-3116","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"bækpau","last":"Bæk","locid":"9fe28c31-48ba-4a25-a7f7-89177ab610cc","name":"Bæk, Rikke","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gunna","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"3637a387-cafe-43c8-91f0-ba9dfb880ba7","name":"Christiansen, Gunna","orcid":"0000-0003-0540-1367","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Hjuler","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"c0476120-7038-4e7b-9bdf-2413207eb916","name":"Nielsen, Morten Hjuler","orcid":"0000-0003-0748-6296","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Malene Møller","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"8838d38e-52f3-42a8-83fd-e3e6342d235c","name":"Jørgensen, Malene Møller","orcid":"0000-0003-1381-3863","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Brøndum","key":"frøkjærpau","last":"Frøkjær","locid":"6e553b4c-cf1d-452b-963c-94942485d472","name":"Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","orcid":"0000-0001-8722-0070","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aase","key":"handbergpau","last":"Handberg","locid":"aba86271-7a2f-4bb7-83d0-426af197b6e5","name":"Handberg, Aase","orcid":"0000-0001-5719-203X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-e7d26dd5-feda-4af9-bfbd-415046c79afb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Dynamics of circulating liver-derived and CD36+ extracellular vesicles in metabolic dysfunction-associated steatotic liver disease during weight loss intervention","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-824106","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The impact of alcohol septal ablation (ASA) on exercise hemodynamics, symptoms, and quality of life in patients with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy is poorly described according to contemporary standards. This study aimed to evaluate the effect of ASA on filling pressures at rest and during exercise, left ventricular outflow tract obstruction, symptoms, and quality of life in patients with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy. METHODS: This prospective study enrolled 24 patients with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy referred for ASA. Right-heart catheterization and echocardiography were performed at rest and during exercise, before and ≈7 months after ASA. The primary outcome was the difference in pulmonary artery wedge pressure at 75 W. Secondary outcomes assessed left ventricular outflow tract gradients, New York Heart Association functional class, and the Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Clinical Summary Score. RESULTS: ASA significantly reduced pulmonary artery wedge pressure at 75 W (33±9 mm Hg versus 24±10 mm Hg; P<0.001), decreased left ventricular outflow tract gradients at rest (49 [interquartile range (IQR), 24-90] mm Hg versus 17 [IQR, 14-27] mm Hg; P<0.01), at peak exercise (45 [IQR, 29-90] mm Hg versus 32 [IQR, 21-61] mm Hg; P = 0.02), and after exercise (96 [IQR, 34-161] mm Hg versus 28 [IQR, 21-62] mm Hg; P<0.01). The Kansas City Cardiomyopathy Questionnaire Clinical Summary Score was significantly increased (65.4±16 versus 76.7±16; P<0.01). ASA improved New York Heart Association functional class, with 54% in class III before treatment, compared with 13% after treatment (P<0.001). CONCLUSIONS: ASA significantly reduced exercise-induced filling pressures and LVOT obstruction, leading to improved symptoms and quality of life in patients with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Dybro, Anne Mette","Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Ladefoged, Bertil","Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","Andersen, Mads Jønsson","Jensen, Morten Kvistholm","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-825266"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exercise hemodynamics","Obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy","septal reduction therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of alcohol septal ablation on exercise hemodynamics symptoms and quality of life in obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.125.041328","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-825266","identifier":[{"id":"40827012","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105013812816","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5ee3852c-5e9a-4e1c-bdfa-3c735da44e78"],"keyword":["alcohol ablation","exercise hemodynamics","obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy","septal reduction therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2BCDA4AA92F01B1FEA011D015DD50289"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.125.041328","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne M.","key":"dybropau","last":"Dybro","locid":"2e78d319-fc37-4dc3-9030-130d2d0c8a25","name":"Dybro, Anne Mette","name_org":"Dybro, Anne M.","orcid":"0000-0003-3175-9725","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten B.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"4bae5bd6-40ab-4bd9-a7ba-fc3d7fe970c7","name":"Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","name_org":"Rasmussen, Torsten B.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roni R.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"896f4a21-d29c-4ad9-b0ef-4e7f8616c234","name":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","name_org":"Nielsen, Roni R.","orcid":"0000-0001-9228-3869","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bertil T.","key":"ladefogedpau","last":"Ladefoged","locid":"f5413eb1-7cda-4cbe-a6ca-d418bbfce623","name":"Ladefoged, Bertil","name_org":"Ladefoged, Bertil T.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders L.D.","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7e7debe0-e391-4c37-9cbd-c136c98fc08a","name":"Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","name_org":"Pedersen, Anders L.D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian J.","key":"terkelsenpau","last":"Terkelsen","locid":"c0d7f995-6ff2-458e-996a-e9a0fccd663f","name":"Terkelsen, Christian Juhl","name_org":"Terkelsen, Christian J.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads J.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"19d72cda-3d6c-4f48-9d4b-6fe5dee888ba","name":"Andersen, Mads Jønsson","name_org":"Andersen, Mads J.","orcid":"0000-0002-9320-8227","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten K.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"da83202a-402f-4457-a557-3a787489909f","name":"Jensen, Morten Kvistholm","name_org":"Jensen, Morten K.","orcid":"0000-0003-1144-4603","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen H.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"ec1d0fd4-f6ae-4071-907f-1448dfe832fe","name":"Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","name_org":"Poulsen, Steen H.","orcid":"0000-0002-9586-835X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40827012"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/jaha.125.041328","issn":["20479980"],"issue":"16","journal":"Journal of the American Heart Association","paperid":"e041328","publisher":"American Heart Association Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Heart Association","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105013812816"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5ee3852c-5e9a-4e1c-bdfa-3c735da44e78"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Effects of Alcohol Septal Ablation on Exercise Hemodynamics, Symptoms, and Quality of Life in Obstructive Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-825266","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In 1877 after years of labor organizing in Europe, Louis Pio, the founder of the Danish Social Democratic Party, fled to America to escape persecution. In the United States, Pio attempted to establish a socialist commune, proposed a socialist thirdparty initiative, published a socialist newspaper in Chicago, involved himself in the Knights of Labor, and supported Edward Bellamy’s movement to nationalize production. Throughout his life, however, Pio’s commitment to equality, stretching back to his involvement in the International Workingmen’s Association, was undermined in practice by his ideas about European civilizational superiority. This article uncovers the roots of Pio’s racial ideology—which made him part of a broader pattern that few Northern European socialists managed to break from— and analyzes how it shaped Pio’s activities in postbellum America","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830962"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"socialism at the edges of civilization louis pio and colonial visions in scandinavia and the united states","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/105003599344","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830962","identifier":[{"id":"105003599344","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-39224b78-db73-4edb-8b1f-bbcae8e1fa31"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ECEBA01736C2521FF9CAE2D33C46EAB2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Center for American Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Bo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f284f3a3-297f-4882-81e1-b591c41ead80","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9817-9595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1353/cwe.2025.a952582","issn":["21544727"],"issue":"1","journal":"The Journal of the Civil War Era","pages":"55-80","publisher":"University of North Carolina Press","status":"p","title":"The Journal of the Civil War Era","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-39224b78-db73-4edb-8b1f-bbcae8e1fa31"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Socialism at the Edges of Civilization : Louis Pio and Colonial Visions in Scandinavia and the United States","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830962","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"In this study, a workplace measurement campaign was conducted during indoor renovation of two apartments following panel removal, wallpaper removal (dry/wet), sweeping (dry/wet), and floor removal (including insulation) tasks. Measurements with a low-cost sensor (LCS; OPC-N3; Alphasense) was compared to a benchmark optical particle sizer (OPS, TSI Model 3330) to assess the applicability of this LCS in a construction worker environment. Additionally, ultrafine particle concentrations (<0.1 mu m) were measured using a mobility particle sizer (NanoScan, TSI Model 3091) and a diffusion size classifier (DiSCmini). The highest particle number concentrations (PNC) were found during floor removal, dry sweeping, and wallpaper removal, where 63 % of particles were ultrafine (<0.1 mu m) and 96 % were smaller than 2.5 mu m (PM2.5). The PM10 (particulate matter with a diameter <10 mu m) concentrations measured during some tasks exceeded the occupational exposure limit of 10 mg m(-3) for total dust with values from 0.3 to 11 mg m(-3). Analytical electron microscopy analysis revealed exposure to compounds such as talc, titania, quartz, and potential asbestos. Water-based dust control methods reduced PNC by at least 84 %, highlighting their effectiveness in mitigating exposure. LCS generally underestimated particle concentrations, particularly for PM1, which was underestimated ranging from 31 % to 92 %. The largest discrepancies occurred during high concentrations in the presence of ultrafine particles, such as floor removal and dry wallpaper removal. This study also emphasizes the importance of multi-metric measurements and breathing zone assessments to accurately evaluate worker exposure and improve occupational safety.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Brostrøm, Anders","Thalmann, Josephine","Liisberg, Jesper Baldtzer","Husovská, Frederika","Møller, Søren Hanghøj","Rasmussen, Julie Tølbøl","Jensen, Thomas Nørregaard","Jensen, Søren Bendt","Jensen, Keld Alstrup","Cole-Hunter, Thomas","Fonseca, A.S."],"cuid":["S02-087.60-814041"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Construction","Dust","Indeklima","Indoor","Indoor air","Low cost sensor","Low cost sensors","Occupational Exposure","Particle emissions","Particles","Partikler","Quartz","Renovation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"task specific assessment of particle exposure and low cost sensor performance in indoor construction environments","src":["ku","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aeaoa.2025.100336","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-087.60-814041","identifier":[{"id":"001503120000001","type":"wos"},{"id":"105005940218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-64b1591b-1b40-4586-a30c-752c923070a2","nfa-1e225c74-ca7c-405c-9b02-a5ea3925ab0e"],"keyword":["Construction","Dust suppression","Indeklima","Indoor","Indoor air","Low-cost sensors","Occupational exposure","Particle emissions","Partikler","dust","low-cost sensor","particles","quartz","renovation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-DBFDB9E515D89C6529B1592B3B050B3E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aeaoa.2025.100336","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/453815524/1-s2.0-S2590162125000267-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"danish technological institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DTCI","l3nn":"Danish Technological Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Technological Institute","namevar":["Danish Technological Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DTCI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"brostrømanderspau","last":"Brostrøm","locid":"3d52f7b6-781f-470e-8f55-aa56034dfde9","name":"Brostrøm, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0128-1508","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Josephine","key":"thalmannjosephinepau","last":"Thalmann","name":"Thalmann, Josephine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Baldtzer","key":"liisbergjesperbaldtzerpau","last":"Liisberg","locid":"ebe63f6c-e5d6-4ca2-a548-0a4356f3e59b","name":"Liisberg, Jesper Baldtzer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederika","key":"husovskáfrederikapau","last":"Husovská","locid":"48f4c3d6-1442-4d48-881a-0aafeb052870","name":"Husovská, Frederika","orcid":"0009-0000-2764-5077","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Hanghøj","key":"møllersørenhanghøjpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Søren Hanghøj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Soren Hanghoj","key":"mollersorenhanghojpau","last":"Moller","name":"Moller, Soren Hanghoj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Julie Tølbøl","key":"rasmussenjulietølbølpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Julie Tølbøl","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Julie Tolbol","key":"rasmussenjulietolbolpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Julie Tolbol","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Nørregaard","key":"jensenthomasnørregaardpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thomas Nørregaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas Norregaard","key":"jensenthomasnorregaardpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thomas Norregaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Bendt","key":"jensensørenbendtpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"35e5dcc3-c2b8-448d-8ff8-108b326faa8e","name":"Jensen, Søren Bendt","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Keld A.","key":"jensenkeldalstruppau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b93ba18-9ef8-4419-8d4f-5b7c9634ba2f","name":"Jensen, Keld Alstrup","name_org":"Jensen, Keld A.","orcid":"0000-0002-2764-3634","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"colehunterthomaspau","last":"Cole-Hunter","locid":"1f34b1e1-e457-4eb5-a916-2cea947195eb","name":"Cole-Hunter, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-6827-6084","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ana S.","key":"fonsecaaspau","last":"Fonseca","locid":"66268c01-af09-49ce-bf3d-162a483b9946","name":"Fonseca, A.S.","name_org":"Fonseca, Ana S.","orcid":"0000-0002-1424-6365","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.aeaoa.2025.100336","issn":["25901621"],"journal":"Atmospheric Environment: X","paperid":"100336","publisher":"Elsevier Ltd","publisher_org":"Elsevier Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Atmospheric Environment: X","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105005940218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-64b1591b-1b40-4586-a30c-752c923070a2","nfa-1e225c74-ca7c-405c-9b02-a5ea3925ab0e"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Task specific assessment of particle exposure and low-cost sensor performance in indoor construction environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.60-814041","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Given the imbalance between high care demand and strained hospital capacity, hospital-at-home (HaH) models offer a potential solution by providing hospital-level care in patients’ homes. This scoping review maps the literature on hospital-led virtual health care within HaH models for acute infections, focusing on intervention characteristics and evaluation designs. Following Johanna Briggs Institute guidelines and PRISMA-ScR, we included studies on virtual and hybrid HaH models using telemedicine for remote monitoring and interventions. The literature searches were performed from October 3, 2022 to October 22, 2022, and updated on July 11, 2024 and identified 15,062 potentially relevant records. From these, 79 studies met the inclusion criteria, highlighting the diversity of HaH models and their evaluations. Hybrid models provided broader treatment options, but many studies lacked detailed intervention descriptions, complicating implementation and meta-analyses. Most studies evaluated patient outcomes, with limited attention to health care staff and relatives. Nearly 45,000 participants were assessed, but only 254 participated in randomized controlled trials, indicating a need for more high-level evidence. Relevant gaps remain, including model heterogeneity and inconsistent reporting.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Maria Normand","Dreisig, Tatjana Sandreva","Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","Schultz, Anders N.Ø.","Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","Fischer, Thea K."],"cuid":["S02-095.83-823065"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Larsen, Maria Normand"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"virtual health care in hospital at home models for patients with acute infections a scoping review","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpdig.2025.100250","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.83-823065","identifier":[{"id":"40791831","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105012145410","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC12337863","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-f95d3feb-7449-483d-ac7a-ef813fc41559","sdu-a9808402-9705-452f-a1b4-300fb2f186e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-054DEE2D3BD0D4908AC2EACA17B77271"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/295785416/PIIS2949761225000574.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/461090831/1-s2.0-S2949761225000574-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.mcpdig.2025.100250","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of CIMT - Centre for Innovative Medical Technology (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Global Health Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Normand","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Maria Normand","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tatjana Sandreva","key":"dreisigpau","last":"Dreisig","name":"Dreisig, Tatjana Sandreva","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja Kjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"cc76ec55-14ab-429b-ac2e-5ec2cd6ccc04","name":"Rasmussen, Maja Kjær","orcid":"0000-0002-7405-4373","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders N Ø","key":"schultzpau","last":"Schultz","locid":"3e178008-f465-473a-8421-712cb9135cec","name":"Schultz, Anders Nikolai Ørsted","name_org":"Schultz, Anders N Ø","orcid":"0000-0002-1908-6428","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thyge Lynghøj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Thea K.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"97c4bf8d-8bd1-470b-8e0b-91eb4faf7703","name":"Fischer, Thea K.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40791831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.mcpdig.2025.100250","issn":["29497612"],"issue":"3","journal":"Mayo Clinic Proceedings: Digital Health","paperid":"100250","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Mayo Clinic Proceedings: Digital Health","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105012145410"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f95d3feb-7449-483d-ac7a-ef813fc41559","sdu-a9808402-9705-452f-a1b4-300fb2f186e0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Virtual Health Care in Hospital-at-Home Models for Patients With Acute Infections : A Scoping Review","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.83-823065","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: The growing care demands of an aging population and a smaller workforce is a big societal problem. Therefore, knowledge on how to organize eldercare work without hampering workers` health is needed. We aimed to investigate if workers` daily number of residents cared for over 14 months is associated with low-back pain in eldercare workers. METHODS: We included 513 eldercare workers from 122 wards. In each ward, we gathered quarterly data over 14 months on the number of residents, workers, and work schedules and calculated the daily numbers of residents each worker cared for. Workers reported intensity and days with low-back pain via monthly text messages over 14 months. Using generalized linear mixed models adjusted for confounders, we investigated the association between the number of residents workers cared for daily and low-back pain among those workers. RESULTS: In 3-month periods over 14 months, caring for ≥1 resident per day was associated with a 4% [95% confidence interval (CI) 1.02-1.07] increased risk of more days with low-back pain, and a 2% (95% CI 1.00-1.03) increase in low-back pain intensity among workers. CONCLUSIONS: Eldercare workers are at a higher risk of experiencing low-back pain during periods when they care for a greater number of residents each day. Maintaining a consistent number of residents and workload for workers over a 14-month period could serve as an effective organizational strategy to prevent low-back pain.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Wester, Christian Tolstrup","Kyriakidis, Stavros","Frost, Anders Dreyer","Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","Holtermann, Andreas","Hallman, David M"],"cuid":["S02-099.58-814120"],"filters":{"added":"2025-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Wester, Christian Tolstrup"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Gävle"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Female","Follow up study","Healthcare","Humans","Low Back Pain epidemiology","Low back pain","Male","Middle Aged","Muskelskeletbesvær","Nursing Homes","Rygsmerter","Sosu","Workload distribution","eldercare worker","ældrepleje"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"organizational strategies of eldercare work and health is the daily number of residents cared for over 000000000014 months associated with back pain","src":["nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.4207","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.58-814120","identifier":[{"id":"105004299743","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39811960","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12067635","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["nfa-0e27c01a-ea77-4869-9727-a469c7e548c8","sdu-c0175816-0a4d-4e81-956f-3d7083cb912e"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Female","Humans","Low Back Pain/epidemiology","Male","Middle Aged","Muskelskeletbesvær","Nursing Homes","Rygsmerter","Sosu","eldercare worker","follow-up study","healthcare","low-back pain","staff ratio","workload distribution","Ældrepleje"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-EB1CDF88C4F65F285F16564764F25738"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/290913093/191_200_wester.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5271/sjweh.4207","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment","The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Musculoskeletal Disorders and Physical Workload"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"university of gävle","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Gävle","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian Tolstrup","key":"westerpau","last":"Wester","locid":"c6eadf35-e668-4b28-b196-54c960531585","name":"Wester, Christian Tolstrup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stavros","key":"kyriakidispau","last":"Kyriakidis","locid":"665a4636-fc27-43cf-99e3-e143767eb410","name":"Kyriakidis, Stavros","orcid":"0000-0002-3181-8871","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Dreyer","key":"frostpau","last":"Frost","locid":"bab16b2f-2e20-47b6-b77e-b10e8bdd97ba","name":"Frost, Anders Dreyer","orcid":"0009-0006-1093-4984","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"180d2a5d-fe8e-4956-b192-48aed7083301","name":"Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-1769-717X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"holtermannpau","last":"Holtermann","locid":"fd559bce-74b0-4973-a2d9-dd622af8b0c8","name":"Holtermann, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0003-4825-5697","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"David M","key":"hallmanpau","last":"Hallman","name":"Hallman, David M","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39811960"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5271/sjweh.4207","issn":["03553140","03566528"],"issn_org":["03553140"],"issue":"3","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","pages":"191-200","publisher":"Nordic Association of Occupational Safety and Health (NOROSH)","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Work, Environment & Health","volume":"51"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004299743"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["nfa-0e27c01a-ea77-4869-9727-a469c7e548c8","sdu-c0175816-0a4d-4e81-956f-3d7083cb912e"],"src":["NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Organizational strategies of eldercare work and health - Is the daily number of residents cared for over 14 months associated with back pain?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.58-814120","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Importance Surgeon training with a specific implant is often not considered in implant registry–based studies, which may lead to unobserved confounding bias. Discrepancies between registry and clinical trial outcomes for patellofemoral arthroplasty (PFA) may originate from differences in surgeon training levels. Objective To compare revision rates for knees operated on by knee surgeons specifically trained for PFA and knee surgeons who were not.Design, Setting, and Participants In this population-based cohort study, the framework of a target trial was used to compare outcomes for 2 patient groups: patients who underwent PFA performed by knee surgeons who had (trial surgeons) vs who had not (nontrial surgeons) received focused PFA training as part of a randomized clinical trial. All primary PFA procedures from January 1, 2008, through December 31, 2015, were identified using Danish registries and individual hospital notes with 6 years’ follow-up. Data were analyzed from January 24 to March 1, 2024. Exposure Focused PFA training. Main Outcomes and Measures The primary outcome was 6-year risk of revision. Analyses were conducted according to a prespecified statistical analysis plan, using multiple logistic regression to estimate marginal risk ratios for 6-year risks of revision, reoperation, and mortality, adjusting for potential confounders. Results Of 482 eligible knees of patients who had undergone PFA, 274 (57%; 206 female [75%]; mean [SD] age, 61 [13] years) were operated on by trial surgeons, and 208 (43%; 142 female [68%]; mean [SD] age, 57 [12] years) by nontrial surgeons. Trial surgeons operated on knees with higher patellofemoral Kellgren-Lawrence osteoarthritis grade (range 0-4, with 0 indicating no osteoarthritis and 4 indicating severe osteoarthritis) than nontrial surgeons (79% vs 53% with grade 3 to 4) and higher tibiofemoral Kellgren-Lawrence osteoarthritis grades (37% vs 17% with grade 2 to 4). The 6-year revision rate for trial surgeons was 8% (22 of 274 knees) vs 26% (54 of 208 knees) for nontrial surgeons, corresponding to an adjusted relative risk (RR) of 0.35 (95% CI, 0.22-0.56; P < .001). The reoperation rate was 12% (33 of 274 knees) for trial surgeons vs 19% (40 of 208 knees) for nontrial surgeons, with an adjusted RR of 0.71 (95% CI, 0.42-1.18; P = .19). There was no difference in mortality for trial vs nontribal surgeon groups (18 of 274 knees [7%] vs 12 of 208 knees [6%]; adjusted RR, 1.11 [95% CI, 0.53-2.33; P = .79). Conclusions and Relevance In this cohort study using a target trial emulation approach to assess the association of surgeon training with PFA outcomes, the cumulative 6-year revision rate for PFA was lower for knees operated on by PFA-trained knee surgeons, suggesting that such surgeon training was associated with a better outcome. This suggests that the level of training may be an important confounder for registry-based comparisons of implant outcome, and that this confounder may even obscure inherent implant outcomes.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Louise Eggers","Hoffmann, Adam Gorm","Blanche, Paul","Espersen, Frederik","Justesen, Tobias Freyberg","Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","Hangaard, Stine","Christensen, Robin","Odgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-099.96-814012"],"filters":{"added":"2025-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Louise Eggers"],"keyword":["Outcomes","Total knee arthroplasty"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"surgeon training and revision rates after patellofemoral arthroplasty","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2025.17825","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.96-814012","identifier":[{"id":"40577013","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12205405","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105009871777","type":"scopus"},{"id":"001518697500012","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-420f6b3a-4abb-4611-9b9e-371d64c50d61","sdu-135b3440-0a93-4432-95d2-73fa827943cc"],"keyword":["Outcomes","Total knee arthroplasty"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-027D2A142D70422ACE8C1CC01BCCFB13"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2025.17825","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/456325512/rasmussen_2025_oi_250563_1750871458.5577.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/292991857/rasmussen_2025_oi_250563_1750871458.5577.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Esbjerg og Grindsted Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Odense University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Køge"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Louise Eggers","key":"rasmussenlouiseeggerspau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Louise Eggers","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Adam Gorm","key":"hoffmannadamgormpau","last":"Hoffmann","locid":"33f86937-8708-470b-8427-a1b6b296a76a","name":"Hoffmann, Adam Gorm","orcid":"0009-0008-0058-3804","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Paul","key":"blanchepaulpau","last":"Blanche","locid":"92ff477f-3b2c-4873-a4f5-dbe701671e1c","name":"Blanche, Paul","orcid":"0000-0003-1415-7976","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik","key":"espersenfrederikpau","last":"Espersen","name":"Espersen, Frederik","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","first":"Tobias Freyberg","key":"justesentobiasfreybergpau","last":"Justesen","name":"Justesen, Tobias Freyberg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Enkebølle","key":"rasmussenlasseenkebøllepau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ada7d12e-e6cc-4568-b072-91b059d28c72","name":"Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stine","key":"hangaardstinepau","last":"Hangaard","name":"Hangaard, Stine","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robin","key":"christensenrobinpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"04bf2bf9-a6d8-4be8-93fd-82f3f2ddc9ba","name":"Christensen, Robin","orcid":"0000-0002-6600-0631","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","first":"Anders","key":"odgaardanderspau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"33eeba1f-407c-4aa4-bf69-5efb12863f82","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40577013"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamanetworkopen.2025.17825","issn":["25743805"],"issue":"6","journal":"JAMA network open","paperid":"e2517825","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA network open","title_org":"JAMA Network Open","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105009871777"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-420f6b3a-4abb-4611-9b9e-371d64c50d61","sdu-135b3440-0a93-4432-95d2-73fa827943cc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Surgeon Training and Revision Rates After Patellofemoral Arthroplasty","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.96-814012","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Severe asthma leads to considerable productivity loss; however, patients' financial impact and the potential reversal through biologic therapy remain unexplored. RESEARCH QUESTION: What is the financial burden of productivity loss among employed individuals with severe asthma, and does it change during biologic therapy? STUDY DESIGN AND METHODS: Employed individuals from the Danish Severe Asthma Register (2016-2022) were included. Salary data were sourced from national registries, while productivity loss was measured using the Workplace Productivity and Activity Impairment (WPAI) Questionnaire at baseline and after a minimum of four months of biologic therapy. RESULTS: A total of 132 employed individuals (mean age 47.9 years, 39% female, mean annual salary € 74,646) were included. Before biologic therapy, productivity impairment was 39.1%. presenteeism and absenteeism rates were 35.8% and 11.3%, respectively, equating to annual productivity losses of € 28,880 per individual.On treatment, overall impairment was 17.6%, with significant reductions in both presenteeism and absenteeism, corresponding to annual loss reductions of € 16,506 per individual. INTERPRETATION: The financial burden of productivity loss in severe asthma is substantial, primarily due to presenteeism. Biologic therapy significantly enhances productivity, suggesting that much of the individual financial burden can be reversed.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Håkansson, Kjell Erik Julius","Ibsen, Rikke","Steen Krogh, Niels","Soendergaard, Marianne Baastrup","Hansen, Susanne","Bjerrum, Anne Sofie","von Bülow, Anna","Hilberg, Ole","Løkke, Anders","Bertelsen, Barbara Bonnesen","Johnsen, Claus Rikard","Johansson, Sofie Lock","Dongo, Lycely","Borup, Maria Bisgaard","Vijdea, Roxana","Rasmussen, Linda Makowska","Schmid, Johannes Martin","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Porsbjerg, Celeste"],"cuid":["S03-099.95-822645"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count"