:27,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39939757"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-024-08516-4","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"issue":"8054","journal":"Nature","pages":"404-410","paperid":"6668","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"639"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85217739848"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-8e5db065-84da-4b88-b22a-cf9c490fe6b9","ku-d90b2ee6-482d-4744-938f-55b00cf01e3e","sdu-86f7e323-ba90-498d-97b1-9d08838cdf98"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genetic architecture in Greenland is shaped by demography, structure and selection","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-803749","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Retinal protonated Schiff base (RPSB), found in its all-trans conformer in Bacteriorhodopsin, undergoes barrier-controlled isomerization upon photoabsorption through polyene chain torsion. The effects of the protein environment on the active vibrations during photoabsorption and their redistribution are still not understood. This paper reports on femtosecond time-resolved action-absorption measurements of cryogenically cooled gas-phase all-trans RPSB, which exhibit two coherent vibrational oscillations, 167(14) cm (Formula presented.) and 117(1) cm (Formula presented.), of the first excited state with dephasing times of (Formula presented.) ps. The absence of the high-frequency vibration in solution and the low-frequency vibration in the protein indicates that these vibrations are sensitive to environments. An action-absorption spectrum of cryogenically cold all-trans RPSB, reveals a (Formula presented.) cm (Formula presented.) active vibration when using a hole-burning technique and 1500 cm (Formula presented.) C=C stretching modes.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Klinkby, Nikolaj","Rasmussen, Anne P.","Lauridsen, Anders G S","Andersen, Lars H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772863"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Gas phase","Laser spectroscopy","Molecular dynamics","Retinal chromophore"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"absorption and excited state coherences of cryogenically cold retinal protonated schiff base in vacuo","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85211142091","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772863","identifier":[{"id":"85211142091","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39570028","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-7ffe7b3e-e7b9-4146-bb4d-c58e655be5dc"],"keyword":["Coherent Vibrations","Gas Phase","Laser Spectroscopy","Molecular Dynamics","Retinal Chromophore"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0E62485F572E37F895C6AED4F0FAEC94"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Physics and Astronomy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nikolaj","key":"klinkbypau","last":"Klinkby","locid":"752dd279-9902-458c-bbea-3a839c776338","name":"Klinkby, Nikolaj","orcid":"0009-0008-0317-116X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Pilgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7564311a-7eef-4838-bdc6-3796232f0310","name":"Rasmussen, Anne P.","name_org":"Rasmussen, Anne Pilgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1093-6163","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders G S","key":"lauridsenpau","last":"Lauridsen","name":"Lauridsen, Anders G S","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars H","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8022bbb7-04f7-4757-8c18-8f80a8fb2896","name":"Andersen, Lars H.","name_org":"Andersen, Lars H","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39570028"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/cphc.202400878","issn":["14394235","14397641"],"issn_org":["14394235"],"issue":"3","journal":"ChemPhysChem","paperid":"e202400878","publisher":"Wiley-VCH Verlag","status":"p","title":"ChemPhysChem","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85211142091"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7ffe7b3e-e7b9-4146-bb4d-c58e655be5dc"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Absorption and Excited-State Coherences of Cryogenically Cold Retinal Protonated Schiff Base in Vacuo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-772863","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The saola is one of the most elusive large mammals, standing at the brink of extinction. We constructed a reference genome and resequenced 26 saola individuals, confirming the saola as a basal member of the Bovini. Despite its small geographic range, we found that the saola is partitioned into two populations with high genetic differentiation (FST = 0.49). We estimate that these populations diverged and started declining 5,000–20,000 years ago, possibly due to climate changes and exacerbated by increasing human activities. The saola has long tracts without genomic diversity; however, most of these tracts are not shared by the two populations. Saolas carry a high genetic load, yet their gradual decline resulted in the purging of the most deleterious genetic variation. Finally, we find that combining the two populations, e.g., in an eventual captive breeding program, would mitigate the genetic load and increase the odds of species survival.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Garcia-Erill, Genís","Liu, Shanlin","Le, Minh Duc","Hurley, Martha M.","Nguyen, Hung Dinh","Nguyen, Dzung Quoc","Nguyen, Dzung Huy","Santander, Cindy G.","Sánchez Barreiro, Fátima","Gomes Martins, Nuno Filipe","Hanghøj, Kristian","Salleh, Faezah Mohd","Ramos-Madrigal, Jazmín","Wang, Xi","Sinding, Mikkel Holger S.","Morales, Hernán E.","Stæger, Frederik Filip","Wilkinson, Nicholas","Meng, Guanliang","Pečnerová, Patrícia","Yang, Chentao","Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","Schubert, Mikkel","Dunn, Robert R.","Moltke, Ida","Zhang, Guojie","Chen, Lei","Wang, Wen","Cao, Trung Tien","Nguyen, Ha Manh","Siegismund, Hans R.","Albrechtsen, Anders","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Heller, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-806889"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Albrechtsen, Anders","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Heller, Rasmus"],"country":["China","Germany","Malaysia","Norway","United States","Vietnam"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","American Museum of Natural History","BGI-Shenzhen","CAS - Institute of Zoology","Center for Nature Conservation and Development","Ministry of Agriculture and Rural Development","Northwestern Polytechnical University Xian","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Universiti Teknologi Malaysia","University of North Carolina","Vietnam National University, Hanoi","Vinh University","Zhejiang University","Zoological Research Museum A. Koenig"],"keyword":["Conservation genomics","Evolutionary genomics","Genetic rescue","Phylogenomics","Zoology","degraded DNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genomes of critically endangered saola are shaped by population structure and purging","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2025.03.040","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-806889","identifier":[{"id":"105004399666","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40328258","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC12173715","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-8588a6fd-9e01-4b0f-85cc-1cca243e43db"],"keyword":["conservation genomics","degraded DNA","evolutionary genomics","genetic rescue","phylogenomics","saola","zoology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-A4362BED3FF5D5BA750DC09A5C3AFA53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2025.03.040","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus Universi