V.","status":"p","title":"Cell","volume":"188"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105004399666"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-8588a6fd-9e01-4b0f-85cc-1cca243e43db"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Genomes of critically endangered saola are shaped by population structure and purging","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806889","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Standard measures of linkage disequilibrium (LD) are affected by admixture and population structure, such that loci that are not in LD within each ancestral population appear linked when considered jointly across the populations. The influence of population structure on LD can cause problems for downstream analysis methods, in particular those that rely on LD pruning or clumping. To address this issue, we propose a measure of LD that accommodates population structure using the top inferred principal components. We estimate LD from the correlation of genotype residuals and prove that this LD measure remains unaffected by population structure when analyzing multiple populations jointly, even with admixed individuals. Based on this adjusted measure of LD, we can perform LD pruning to remove the correlation between markers for downstream analysis. Traditional LD pruning is more likely to remove markers with high differences in allele frequencies between populations, which biases measures for genetic differentiation and removes markers that are not in LD in the ancestral populations. Using data from moderately differentiated human populations and highly differentiated giraffe populations we show that traditional LD pruning biases FST and principal component analysis (PCA), which can be alleviated with the adjusted LD measure. In addition, we show that the adjusted LD leads to better PCA when pruning and that LD clumping retains more sites with the retained sites having stronger associations.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bercovich, Ulises","Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","Li, Zilong","Wiuf, Carsten","Albrechtsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809922"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"measuring linkage disequilibrium and improvement of pruning and clumping in structured populations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446050940/Measuring_linkage.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-809922","identifier":[{"id":"105001201905","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39907701","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-617b53e8-df4d-4012-88b3-6841ba5f7fc2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F8FCA493A0D83DCFD2FA0ACC1B3BE4CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/446050940/Measuring_linkage.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Ulises","key":"bercovichpau","last":"Bercovich","locid":"0e2d5027-1c22-4955-abd5-5623f8344479","name":"Bercovich, Ulises","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malthe Sebro","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c78f599c-157c-4a9a-9e7a-ab1d876ab28c","name":"Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Zilong","key":"lipau","last":"Li","locid":"99ad5bfa-5858-412e-8e78-0e671e26f529","name":"Li, Zilong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"wiufpau","last":"Wiuf","locid":"7fd38cb7-1794-49d3-b4ad-19844f67e6fc","name":"Wiuf, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0002-1302-4445","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"4b040c73-6b49-4e97-be60-5e34608e0615","name":"Albrechtsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-031X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39907701"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/genetics/iyaf009","issn":["00166731"],"issn_org":["19432631"],"issue":"3","journal":"Genetics","paperid":"iyaf009","status":"p","title":"Genetics","volume":"229"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105001201905"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-617b53e8-df4d-4012-88b3-6841ba5f7fc2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Measuring linkage disequilibrium and improvement of pruning and clumping in structured populations","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809922","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Aims: Studies have reported excess risk of mortality associated with digoxin in atrial fibrillation (AF). This study sought to investigate if these findings could be replicated and whether a potential association could be explained by bias. Methods: Using Danish Nationwide registers, a nested-case control study from 2012 to 2022 was conducted in a cohort of patients with AF. Cases were defined as death of any cause and the exposure was treatment with digoxin compared with beta blockers/verapamil. To investigate bias, additional analyses with negative control outcomes as case definitions—in which we would not expect a plausible association (eg, nursing home admission)—were employed. Associations were reported as hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% confidence intervals (95% CI). Results: A total of 59,748 cases were identified and matched 1:10 with controls (53% men, median age: 84 [IQR: 77-89]). Digoxin was associated with increased rates of mortality in the entire cohort (HR 1.85, 95% CI 1.78-1.92) as well as subgroups such as patients with heart failure (HR 1.84, 95% CI 1.65-2.06), diabetes (HR 1.85, 95% CI 1.6-2.14), and kidney disease (HR 1.37, 95% CI 1.04-1.8). Significant associations with all negative control outcomes were also found, most notably nursing home admissions (HR 1.79, 95% CI 1.67-1.93). Conclusion: Digoxin use was associated with increased mortality in AF. However, negative control outcomes were also associated with digoxin use indicating that the described association between digoxin and mortality is likely not causal and being prescribed digoxin is merely a marker of more advanced disease and frailty.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holt, Anders","Strange, Jarl Emanuel","Hansen, Morten Lock","Lamberts, Morten","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811476"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Digoxin","Pharmacoepidemiology","Residual confounding"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the bad reputation of digoxin in atrial fibrillation causality or bias nationwide nested case control study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajmo.2025.100093","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811476","identifier":[{"id":"105000103644","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11957803","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"40166486","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-f51280de-29ca-4a91-9f08-e8d72986c95b"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","Digoxin","Negative control outcomes","Pharmacoepidemiology","Residual confounding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4E030A6496AB1DF527CFD15AB24F0485"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ajmo.2025.100093","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444538507/1-s2.0-S266703642500007X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: Cardiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"holtpau","last":"Holt","name":"Holt, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jarl Emanuel","key":"strangepau","last":"Strange","name":"Strange, Jarl Emanuel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Lock","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Morten Lock","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Morten","key":"lambertspau","last":"Lamberts","locid":"ced953f0-cd5e-4af3-8c41-7311decea61f","name":"Lamberts, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Vibe","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40166486"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ajmo.2025.100093","issn":["26670364"],"journal":"American Journal of Medicine Open","paperid":"100093","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Medicine Open","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000103644"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f51280de-29ca-4a91-9f08-e8d72986c95b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Bad Reputation of Digoxin in Atrial Fibrillation—Causality or Bias? Nationwide Nested Case-Control Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-811476","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
