langetheispau","last":"Lange","locid":"e4664578-01fc-4a93-8efd-1dbffb72cdd6","name":"Lange, Theis","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-8347","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Anders","key":"perneranderspau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["40084471"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.70023","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","paperid":"e70023","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"69"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-105000407158"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care","prehospital emergency medical services"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5b8a4186-1792-4795-b30d-b527902a8206","au-71405ed2-21d6-4ea3-8927-450b365fde7d","ku-9c949384-4188-4ed6-a2b8-5a35f06fd747","sdu-ec02ee26-e998-4dfe-bc5c-5dc684530819"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"INCEPT : The Intensive Care Platform Trial-Design and protocol","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-090.69-803696","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVES: Randomized clinical trials informing clinical practice (e.g., like large, pragmatic, and late-phase trials) should ideally mostly use harmonized outcomes that are important to patients, family members, clinicians, and researchers. Core outcome sets for specific subsets of ICU patients exist, for example, respiratory failure, delirium, and COVID-19, but not for ICU patients in general. Accordingly, we aimed to develop a core outcome set for adult general ICU patients. DESIGN: We developed a core outcome set in Denmark following the Core Outcome Measures in Effectiveness Trials Handbook. We used a modified Delphi consensus process with multiple methods design, including literature review, survey, semi-structured interviews, and discussions with initially five Danish research panels. The core outcome set was internationally validated and revised based on feedback from research panels in all countries. SETTING: There were five Danish research panels and 17 panels in 13 other countries. Interviews and the three-round Delphi survey was conducted in Denmark, followed by validation of the core outcome set across 14 countries in Europe, Australasia, and India. SUBJECTS: Adult ICU survivors, family members, clinicians, and researchers. INTERVENTIONS: None. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: We identified 329 published outcomes, of which 50 were included in the 264 participant Delphi survey. In semi-structured interviews of 82, no additional outcomes were added. The first Delphi survey round was completed by 249 (94%) participants, and 202 (82%) contributed to the third and final round. The initial core outcome set comprised six outcomes. International validation involved 217 research panel members and resulted in the final core outcome set comprising survival, free of life support, free of delirium, out of hospital, health-related quality of life, and cognitive function. CONCLUSIONS: We developed and internationally validated a core outcome set with six core outcomes to be used in research, specifically clinical trials involving adult general ICU patients.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Bruun, Camilla Rahbek Lysholm","Granholm, Anders","Møller, Morten Hylander","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Mortensen, Camilla Bekker","Poulsen, Lone Museaus","Strøm, Thomas","Laerkner, Eva","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Haberlandt, Trine","Bunzel, Anne-Marie Gellert","Herløv, Louise Stenbryggen","Holm, Anna","Sivapalan, Praleene","Estrup, Stine","Cronhjort, Maria","Schandl, Anna","Laake, Jon Henrik","Hofsø, Kristin","Blokzijl, Fredrike","Keus, Frederik","Pfortmueller, Carmen Andrea","Ostermann, Marlies","Cole, Jade M.","Wise, Matt P.","Szczeklik, Wojciech","Wludarczyk, Anna","Jovaiša, Tomas","Cecconi, Maurizio","Sigurdsson, Martin Ingi","Nalos, Marek","Hästbacka, Johanna","Mäkinen, Marja","Hammond, Naomi","Litton, Edward","Haines, Kimberley","Myatra, Sheila Nainan","Vijayaraghavan, Bharath Kumar Tirupakuzhi","Yadav, Kavita","Jha, Vivekanand","Venkatesh, Balasubramanian","Egerod, Ingrid","Perner, Anders","Collet, Marie O."],"cuid":["S04-091.49-803636"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard"],"country":["Australia","Czechia","Finland","Iceland","India","Italy","Lithuania","Netherlands","Norway","Poland","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Apollo Hospitals Group","Cardiff University","Charles University","Danderyd Hospital","Danderyd University Hospital","Danderyds Hospital","Fiona Stanley Hospital","Gold Coast University Hospital","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Helsinki University Central Hospital","Helsinki University Hospital","Homi Bhabha National Institute","Humanitas Research Hospital","Humanitas University","IRCCS Istituto Clinico Hum