rticle","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-804556","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"The need for early non-invasive diagnostic tools for chronic liver fibrosis is growing, particularly in individuals with obesity, non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD), and the metabolic syndrome (MetS) since prevalence of these conditions is increasing. This case-control study compared non-invasive liver fibrosis markers in obesity with NAFLD and MetS (NAFLD-MetS, n = 33), in obese (n = 28) and lean (n = 27) control groups. We used MRI (T1 relaxation times (T1) and liver stiffness), circulating biomarkers (CK18, PIIINP, and TIMP1), and algorithms (FIB-4 index, Forns score, FNI, and MACK3 score) to assess their potential in predicting liver fibrosis risk. We found that T1 (892 ± 81 ms vs. 818 ± 64 ms, p < 0.001), FNI (15 ± 12% vs. 9 ± 7%, p = 0.018), CK18 (166 ± 110 U/L vs. 113 ± 41 U/L, p = 0.019), and MACK3 (0.18 ± 0.15 vs. 0.05 ± 0.04, p < 0.001) were higher in the NAFLD-MetS group compared with the obese control group. Moreover, correlations were found between CK18 and FNI (r = 0.69, p < 0.001), CK18 and T1 (r = 0.41, p < 0.001), FNI and T1 (r = 0.33, p = 0.006), MACK3 and FNI (r = 0.79, p < 0.001), and MACK3 and T1 (r = 0.50, p < 0.001). We show that liver fibrosis markers are increased in obese individuals with NAFLD and MetS without clinical signs of liver fibrosis. More studies are needed to validate the use of these non-invasive biomarkers for early identification of liver fibrosis risk.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Askeland, Anders","Rasmussen, Rikke Wehner","Gjela, Mimoza","Frøkjær, Jens Brøndum","Højlund, Kurt","Mellergaard, Maiken","Handberg, Aase"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-822295"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Handberg, Aase"],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers blood","Case Control Studies","Female","Humans","Liver Cirrhosis blood","Liver fibrosis risk","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Metabolic Syndrome complications","Middle Aged","Non alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease complications","Non alcoholic fatty liver disease","Non invasive biomarkers","Obesity","Obesity complications","Obesity phenotype","The metabolic syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"non invasive liver fibrosis markers are increased in obese individuals with non alcoholic fatty liver disease and the metabolic syndrome","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41598-025-85508-y","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by a research grant from the Danish Diabetes Academy, which is funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Grant No. NNF17SA0031406."],"id":"S02-100.00-822295","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11950363","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105002008635","type":"scopus"},{"id":"40148373","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-4389eb64-5d61-4965-9bf7-e20aa7c693ba","sdu-fa473867-0706-481d-86a0-1537fc8a86b0"],"keyword":["Adult","Biomarkers/blood","Case-Control Studies","Female","Humans","Liver Cirrhosis/blood","Liver fibrosis risk","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Male","Metabolic Syndrome/complications","Middle Aged","Non-alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease/complications","Non-alcoholic fatty liver disease","Non-invasive biomarkers","Obesity","Obesity phenotype","Obesity/complications","The metabolic syndrome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1695233E5735F5FE071DCE8892491BB1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/288871631/s41598-025-85508-y.pdf","version":"P