isette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, Lisette O.","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette O.","key":"jensenlisetteopau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lisette O.","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39461401"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.amjcard.2024.10.019","issn":["00029149","18791913"],"issn_org":["00029149"],"journal":"American Journal of Cardiology","pages":"1-8","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Cardiology","title_org":"The American Journal of Cardiology","volume":"235"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208463684"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-171ff0f6-4698-4833-a3a5-de806ba4b4c1","au-d8e16af8-3411-4470-a610-6e0494713e6d","sdu-7b9ab785-4cac-4e1b-9e93-878552bb8c35"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comparison of Outcome After Percutaneous Coronary Intervention for De Novo and In-Stent Restenosis Indications","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-784770","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"Background: Multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2A (MEN 2A) is a rare hereditary cancer syndrome caused by pathogenic variants in the rearranged during transfection (RET) gene and is characterized by medullary thyroid carcinoma (MTC), pheochromocytoma (PHEO), primary hyperparathyroidism (PHPT), cutaneous lichen amyloidosis (CLA), and Hirschsprung’s disease. Phenotypic data on the RET C611Y variant remain sparse. Consequently, we aimed to establish a clinical risk profile. Methods: We conducted a nationwide study of all cases (n = 128) born after 1 January 1930 and recognized as carrying the RET C611Y variant in Denmark before 1 April 2021. Results: The median follow-up after birth was 47 years (range, 3–92). Age-related penetrance at age 70 years for MTC was 98% (CI, 91–100), for PHEO 24% (CI, 16–37), and for PHPT 10% (CI, 5–20). None had CLA or Hirschsprung’s disease. The age-related progression of MTC was significant (p < 0.001). The median age at T0N0M0 was 11 years (2–62), at T1-4N0M0 was 37 years (12–65), at TxN1M0 was 47 years (16–79), and at TxNxM1 was 50 years (28–70). At the last follow-up, 56% of thyroidectomized cases (n = 103) were biochemically cured. Overall survival at 70 years was 74% (CI, 59–84). Conclusions: RET C611Y is associated with a very high penetrance of MTC and a low penetrance of PHEO and PHPT. CLA and Hirschsprung’s disease almost never occur. MTC seems moderately aggressive, but large variability can be seen. Overall survival may be comparable to that of the general population.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Hansen, Anders Würgler","Vestergaard, Peter","Poulsen, Morten Møller","Rasmussen, Åse Krogh","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Madsen, Mette","Næraa, Rune Weis","Hansen, Dorte","Main, Katharina","Pedersen, Henrik Baymler","Londero, Stefano Christian","Rolighed, Lars","Hahn, Christoffer Holst","Rask, Klara Bay","Maare, Christian","Nielsen, Heidi Hvid","Gaustadnes, Mette","Rossing, Maria","Hermann, Pernille","Mathiesen, Jes Sloth"],"cuid":["S04-099.83-803781"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corpau":["Danish Thyroid Cancer Group (DATHYRCA)","on behalf of Danish Thyroid Cancer Group (DATHYRCA)"],"corresponding_author":["Hansen, Anders Würgler"],"keyword":["C611Y","Genotype","Phenotype","RET","multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ret c000000000611y germline variant in multiple endocrine neoplasia type 000000000002a in denmark 000000001930 000000002021 a nationwide study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers17030374","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The work was supported by Odense University Hospital (grant number 142-A5632)."],"id":"S04-099.83-803781","identifier":[{"id":"85218016260","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39941743","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11816337","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-9f3310ba-c256-4494-8627-c8a3c76f3979","au-69f519d9-0645-406f-a605-03938d8e0153","ku-8350074f-2f54-48ec-9d51-db1a6f30a6cf","sdu-cadfad33-d4a9-4f18-a63b-cdad2d7af595"],"keyword":["C611Y","RET","genotype","multiple endocrine neoplasia type 2","phenotype"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C6C160345C7717E4273177E11AAE3AC2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/773023896/Hansen_et_al._2025_._R