icle","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-806927","year":"2025","yearsub":"2025"}
{"abstract":"This study presents findings captured in the first 1.5 years of the Virus Monitoring in Denmark (VMD) surveillance system. It describes trends in respiratory viruses, related symptoms, and participant demographics and behaviors. VMD used self-swabbing and self-reported symptoms to monitor respiratory viruses in the general population. Participants were recruited via digital invitations to a representative sample of the population or through workplaces. Symptomatic participants could self-swab and register their samples and report their symptoms via a dedicated smartphone web app. With 30 627 participants and 12 642 samples analyzed, VMD had a broad demographic representation. SARS-CoV-2 was the most frequently detected virus, with positivity rates peaking at over 50% in late 2023. Participants commonly self-swabbed because of fever, cough, and rhinorrhea, with influenza A linked to the highest median number of symptoms. Participants only provided samples after reaching a specific symptom threshold, and participation affected the health-seeking behaviors and work attendance of a few individuals. VMD continuously provided real-time insights into respiratory virus trends and symptomatology in the general non-healthcare-seeking population. Its accessibility – available to anyone with a Danish identification number, a smartphone, and an invitation – highlights its potential as a pandemic preparedness tool.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Larsen, Tine Graakjær","Ginty, Jonathan R.","Jessen, Randi","Nielsen, Ruben Bjerregaard","Jensen, Anders","Botnen, Amanda Bolt","Wilkowski, Bartlomiej","Rasmussen, Camilla","Brødbæk, Dalila Lepirica","Shaw, Daniel Steven","Benameur, Elias","Rasmussen, Morten","Trebbien, Ramona","Mortensen, Shila","Olsen, Stefan S.","Chong, Steven","Krause, Tyra Grove","Schneider, Uffe Vest","Vangsted, Anne Marie","Steenhard, Nina Ruth","Møller, Frederik Trier"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811399"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Centre for Disease Prevention and Control"],"keyword":["Pandemic preparedness","Public Health Surveillance","Respiratory tract infections","Self Testing","Symptom assessment","eHealth"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"virus monitoring in denmark a community based self sampling system to surveil respiratory viruses and associated symptoms","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmv.70293","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811399","identifier":[{"id":"40130741","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11934840","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"105001596026","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ecd4731f-1dec-4606-b667-424f83222033"],"keyword":["eHealth","pandemic preparedness","public health surveillance","respiratory tract infections","self-testing","symptom assessment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-2AF47D1705AC5083F039E0EFB2CC3D00"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/447761285/Virus_Monitoring_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jmv.70293","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"