"affno":"","first":"Janne","key":"frittrasmussenpedh","last":"Fritt-Rasmussen","name":"Fritt-Rasmussen, Janne","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Katrine","key":"raundruppedh","last":"Raundrup","name":"Raundrup, Katrine","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"mosbechpedh","last":"Mosbech","name":"Mosbech, Anders","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788771568394"],"issn":["22449981"],"pages":"128-139","publisher":"Aarhus University, DCE - Danish Centre for Environment and Energy","series":"Videnskabelig rapport fra DCE - Nationalt Center for Miljø og Energi","status":"p","title":"Uummannap Kangerlua and Sigguup Nunaa (Svartenhuk) - Regional environmental baseline assessment for mining activities"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c91445cc-800c-4659-a73f-5ab16143de5c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Appendix 1 : Fieldwork at Siggup Nunaa (Svartenhuk) 2022","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-718008","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Since the late 1990’s the “zero harmful discharge” regime related to offshore oil and gas extraction has been implemented on the Norwegian Continental Shelf. It has also gained traction in other areas of the North Sea due to OSPAR regulations. However, the holistic understanding of ecotoxicity drivers and biodegradation kinetics of this complex mixture is still lacking. The main goal of the MERIT project (Intelligent testing strategy for Minimizing EnviRonmental ImpacTs of produced water) was to develop a method for the quantitative estimation of drivers and the potential for reducing environmental impacts to acceptable levels. We summarize the findings of the project with focus on 1) identifying ecotoxicity drivers through whole effluent testing supported by toxicity identification evaluation and 2) determining environmentally relevant biodegradation kinetics of discharged chemicals in produced water. We present a testing strategy using empirical data and samples from five different platforms in the North Sea to align with the goals of minimizing environmental impacts of produced water.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Skjolding, Lars Michael","Møller, Mette Torsbjerg","Nielsen, Ann Flemming","Poulsen, T. F.","Rasmussen, S. B.","Birch, Heidi","Mayer, Philipp","Baun, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-729668"],"event":{"end":"2024-01-25","place":"Lyngby, dk","start":"2024-01-23","title":"22. Danske Havforskermøde","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"determining ecotoxicity drivers and biodegradation kinetics of discharged chemicals in produced water from oil and gas extraction in the north sea","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://havforsker2024.dtu.dk/abstract-book","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-729668","ids":["dtu-6ee0feac-2ee4-4c4a-8d9e-2bb1d3820aa1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2C96BAA9E60135C6E3950E9487B4186C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://havforsker2024.dtu.dk/abstract-book","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental and Resource Engineering, Circularity & Environmental Impact"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"L. M.","key":"skjoldingpau","last":"Skjolding","locid":"0f7dbfa4-64f2-449a-bb3e-f9d14d60b2ca","name":"Skjolding, Lars Michael","name_org":"Skjolding, L. M.","orcid":"0000-0002-3280-1836","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"M. T.","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"e9e5a58f-da1d-40b3-b1bb-5faabb1b9f03","name":"Møller, Mette Torsbjerg","name_org":"Møller, M. T.","orcid":"0000-0003-2216-6514","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. F.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"7865ecb3-ce06-4f08-b8d1-8f500d445f36","name":"Nielsen, Ann Flemming","name_org":"Nielsen, A. F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"T. F.","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","name":"Poulsen, T. F.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"S. B.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, S. B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H.","key":"birchpau","last":"Birch","locid":"5f3916d7-91bc-415c-a3b1-d31c4acd0a0d","name":"Birch, Heidi","name_org":"Birch, H.","orcid":"0000-0002-7152-3832","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"P.","key":"mayerpau","last":"Mayer","locid":"f732d693-1e5e-4940-8d29-9e5f59e43ef3","name":"Mayer, Philipp","name_org":"Mayer, P.","orcid":"0000-0001-5138-7506","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.","key":"baunpau","last":"Baun","locid":"f3cdf4a9-bfc7-4e0e-bf46-df0da8134f0d","name":"Baun, Anders","name_org":"Baun, A.","orcid":"0000-0003-1396-408X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"19-19","publisher":"Technical University of Denmark","status":"p","title":"22. Danske Havforskermøde Abstract book"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6ee0feac-2ee4-4c4a-8d9e-2bb1d3820aa1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Determining ecotoxicity drivers and biodegradation kinetics of discharged chemicals in produced water from oil and gas extraction in the North Sea","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-729668","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Acute high-risk abdominal (AHA) surgery is associated with a high short-term mortality rate. This might be partly attributed to myocardial injury after non-cardiac surgery (MINS) defined by elevated postoperative troponin levels. The myocardial injury is often asymptomatic; thus, troponin screening seems to be the best diagnostic method. We aimed to assess whether implementing troponin screening with subsequent individualised interventions as standard care is associated with reduced mortality after AHA surgery. We also explored the treatment implications in the screening period. Methods: A retrospective cohort of 558 patients undergoing surgery from February 2018 to March 2021 was included. The patients undergoing surgery before March 2019 served as the historical control group, while the screening group consisted of patients undergoing surgery from March 1, 2019. Troponin I was to be measured 6–12 h postoperatively and in the morning of the succeeding 4 days. Patients with myocardial injury were assessed, and treatment was individualised after multiple disciplinary consultations. The primary outcome was the unadjusted 30-day mortality rates. Inverse probability treatment weighting was used to adjust for selection bias. Results: We included 558 patients: 382 in the screening group and 176 in the historical control group. In the screening group, 15 patients (3.9%) died before the first blood sampling, and in 31 patients (8.1%), troponin screening was omitted, leaving only 336 patients screened. Myocardial injury was diagnosed in 81 patients (24.1%) of the 336 patients. Of these, 59 (72.8%) had a cardiac consultation. No interventions or alterations in relation to myocardial injury were done in 67 patients (82.7%). The 30-day mortality was 13.8% (95% CI 8.7%–18.9%) in the control group and 11.1% (95% CI 8.0%–14.3%) in the screening group. The absolute risk difference was −2.7% (95% CI −8.7%–3.3%; p =.38), which was unchanged after adjustment. The difference remained unchanged after 90 days and 1 year. Conclusion: The implementation of postoperative troponin screening was not associated with reduced mortality after AHA surgery. Research on the prevention and treatment of MINS is warranted before the implementation of standard troponin screening.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kanstrup, Charlotte T. B.","Svarre, Kristina Johansen","Rasmussen, Maja Christine","Serup, Camilla Mattesen","Lundstrøm, Lars Hyldborg","Kleif, Jakob","Bertelsen, Claus Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-739262"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Emergency surgery","Mortality","Myocardial injury","Troponin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the effects of troponin screening among patients undergoing acute high risk abdominal surgery a retrospective cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-739262","identifier":[{"id":"85182147025","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38213306","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6bcf40cd-e685-46bf-b9f4-4d0edc670087"],"keyword":["acute abdominal surgery","emergency surgery","mortality","myocardial injury","myocardial injury after non-cardiac surgery","troponin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ACB8CE8A7B86A0AF76DCD7076CE5D68F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital – North Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Charlotte T. B.","key":"kanstruppau","last":"Kanstrup","name":"Kanstrup, Charlotte T. B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristina Johansen","key":"svarrepau","last":"Svarre","name":"Svarre, Kristina Johansen","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maja Christine","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Maja Christine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Mattesen","key":"seruppau","last":"Serup","name":"Serup, Camilla Mattesen","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Lars Hyldborg","key":"lundstrømpau","last":"Lundstrøm","locid":"3c02fe75-6e40-49a3-a116-726fc8874dfc","name":"Lundstrøm, Lars Hyldborg","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jakob","key":"kleifpau","last":"Kleif","locid":"16ca332d-b612-4ab7-8b98-622d5d45d108","name":"Kleif, Jakob","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Claus Anders","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"0ea5cd22-b4bb-4c76-9ce7-77f7a44949f1","name":"Bertelsen, Claus Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38213306"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14371","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"476-484","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182147025"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6bcf40cd-e685-46bf-b9f4-4d0edc670087"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The effects of troponin screening among patients undergoing acute high-risk abdominal surgery : A retrospective cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-739262","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In Greenland, legacy mines provide testimony to how pollution still affects the sensitive Arctic environment. These legacy mines serve as valuable study sites that can improve future predictions on environmental consequences of mining operations in Greenland and other areas in the Arctic. Environmental studies at legacy mine sites in Greenland have previously focused on the leaching of pollutants into the marine environment and little is known about the spatial distribution of pollution in the terrestrial environment at these sites. In the current study, we present preliminary data from an environmental survey at the Blyklippen legacy mine. Blyklippen was a lead and zinc mine in East Greenland that operated between 1956-1963. Mining operations caused substantial pollution of lead (Pb), zinc (Zn), and other heavy minerals such as cadmium (Cd), barium (Ba) and copper (Cu), still measurable today. The primary sources of pollution today are the tailings storage facility and remains of ore concentrate spills along the haul road and at the quay areas at the harbor. Pollution is dispersed from these sites into the surrounding environment by wind and water. A total number of 995 discrete sediment samples were collected over 10 days at the Blyklippen mine site and surrounding area of Mestersvig from 178 sampling locations at depth intervals of 5 cm. The aim of the current study is to investigate and map the spatial distribution of heavy metals in the environment surrounding the Blyklippen legacy mine using both field measurements by portable X-Ray Fluorescence spectrometry (pXRF) on depth specific sediment samples at in situ conditions and laboratory measurements on freeze-dried samples to investigate the effect of soil moisture on the accuracy of the field screening. Field measurements were conducted using short measurement times of 5-10 seconds, whereas laboratory measurement times were 180 seconds. Our results demonstrate the effectiveness of pXRF as a field measurement tool for identifying the spatial delineation of soil pollution by comparing in situ measurements against pre-defined natural background values for heavy metals such as Pb and Zn. Comparison between Pb and Zn concentrations measured in the field versus in the laboratory on freeze-dried samples showed a good agreement for mineral soils. On organic and/or wet samples, field concentrations were underestimated for some elements. Overall, the approach shows that a fast and cost-effective large-scale field survey at legacy mines is obtainable using pXRF, enabling an effective identification of pollution ‘hotspots’ directly in the field. In combination with geostatistical mapping, the approach can improve the overall accuracy of environmental monitoring and mapping of pollution with enhanced environmental protection at both legacy, recent and future mines.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Christian Frigaard","Søndergaard, Jens","Downey, Arnold","Mosbech, Anders","Jørgensen, Christian Juncher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-743714"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-21","place":"Chania, gr","start":"2024-06-19","title":"International Conference on Geostatistics for Environmental Applications","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["Canada"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Montreal"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"x ray flourescence spectrometry pxrf as a tool for high resolution mapping of terrestrial pollution at legacy mine sites in east greenland","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu24-7632","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-743714","ids":["au-132fd7d9-9bec-4176-bf7f-5c1e97628db6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F9C3C8C016B74693D753BF36538C3A6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/382727991/Final_reduced.pdf","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/egusphere-egu24-7632","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ca","key":"university of montreal","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Montreal","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Frigaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c64d8832-0109-4466-b421-c42e314ae238","name":"Rasmussen, Christian Frigaard","orcid":"0000-0003-2497-2990","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"ed027e07-2df4-474c-b76a-b0ced3210d88","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-7680-9920","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Arnold","key":"downeypau","last":"Downey","name":"Downey, Arnold","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"mosbechpau","last":"Mosbech","locid":"0d8b3009-ff00-40a7-b738-abfa87e31ccf","name":"Mosbech, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-7581-7037","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Juncher","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"8c3aea27-e504-4762-87b5-ac06d899de02","name":"Jørgensen, Christian Juncher","orcid":"0000-0002-5184-7063","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-132fd7d9-9bec-4176-bf7f-5c1e97628db6"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"X-Ray Flourescence Spectrometry (pXRF) as a tool for high resolution mapping of terrestrial pollution at legacy mine sites in East Greenland.","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-743714","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Hypertension affects 25%-30% of the world population. Hydrochlorothiazide (HCTZ) is among the most used and cheapest medications but was in 2018 labeled with a warning stating the increased risk of nonmelanoma skin cancer (NMSC). This study describes geographical differences in the association between HCTZ and NMSC from the perspective of hypertensive heart disease (HHD). METHODS: We conducted a systematic literature search (PubMed, Embase, Clinicaltrial.gov, and Clinicaltrial.eu) using PICO/PECO acronyms, including case-control, cohort, and randomized controlled trials. We constructed a rate ratio of disability-adjusted life years (DALY) for HHD/NMSC in the global burden of disease (GBD) regions. RESULTS: No increased risk of NMSC with the use of HCTZ was found in Taiwan, India, and Brazil. A small (hazard ratio (HR)/odds ratio (OR) ≤1.5) but significantly increased risk was seen in Canada, the United States, and Korea. An increased risk (1.5< HR/OR ≤2.5) in Iceland, Spain, and Japan and a highly increased risk (HR/OR >2.5) in the United Kingdom, Denmark, the Netherlands, and Australia. HHD is associated with a more than tenfold DALY rate compared with NMSC in 13 of 21 GBD regions, corresponding to 77.2% of the global population. In none of these 13 regions was there an increased risk of HCTZ-associated NMSC. CONCLUSIONS: Despite limited information from many countries, our data point to large geographical differences in the association between HCTZ and NMSC. In all GBD regions, except Australasia, HHD constitutes a more than fivefold DALY rate compared to NMSC. This disproportionate risk should be considered before avoiding HCTZ from the antihypertensive treatment.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Almskou","Buus, Niels Henrik","Comerma Steffensen, Simon Gabriel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-753385"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South"],"country":["Venezuela"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Universidad Central de Venezuela"],"keyword":["Basal cell carcinoma","Blood Pressure","Hydrochlorothiazide","Hypertension","Hypertensive heart disease","Non melanoma skin cancer","Squamous cell carcinoma","antihypertensive treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"geographical differences in hydrochlorothiazide associated risk of skin cancer balanced against disability related to hypertensive heart disease","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206402333","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["No funding"],"id":"S01-000.00-753385","identifier":[{"id":"85206402333","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39115345","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-edcb7dbc-28fd-49a9-8b41-f5183f6d8594"],"keyword":["Basal cell carcinoma","Hypertension","Hypertensive heart disease","Non-melanoma skin cancer","Squamous cell carcinoma","antihypertensive treatment","blood pressure","hydrochlorothiazide"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E9C2719B009DB27CFBFF574A8C1241D"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest","Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Medicine and Nephrology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ve","key":"universidad central de venezuela","loc":["Venezuela","America, South"],"name":"Universidad Central de Venezuela","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Almskou","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Almskou","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Henrik","key":"buuspau","last":"Buus","locid":"cb682ed6-2fe3-4664-90d6-0690462e8f80","name":"Buus, Niels Henrik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Simon Gabriel","key":"comermasteffensenpau","last":"Comerma Steffensen","locid":"f58ce259-6d57-4b75-8890-639a8e751d2a","name":"Comerma Steffensen, Simon Gabriel","orcid":"0000-0001-6516-694X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39115345"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ajh/hpae101","issn":["08957061","11395990"],"issn_org":["08957061"],"issue":"11","journal":"American Journal of Hypertension","pages":"924-932","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Hypertension","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206402333"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-edcb7dbc-28fd-49a9-8b41-f5183f6d8594"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Geographical differences in hydrochlorothiazide associated risk of skin cancer balanced against disability related to hypertensive heart disease","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-753385","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Whether DNA methylation changes follow human physical trauma is uncertain. We aimed to investigate if severe trauma was associated with DNA methylation changes. In a prospective, observational, clinical study, we included severely injured adults and adults undergoing elective surgery (controls). Blood was obtained from trauma patients (n = 60) immediately- and 30-45 days post-trauma, and from surgical patients (n = 57) pre-, post-, and 30-45 days post-surgery. Epigenome-wide DNA methylation profiling was performed and analyzed for significant differentially methylated CpGs and -regions (DMRs) within and between groups. Within the trauma group we identified 10,126 significant differentially methylated CpGs and 1169 DMRs. No significant differential methylation was found in the surgical group. In the trauma group, differentially methylated sites were enriched in genes and pathways involved in blood coagulation and inflammatory response. Severe trauma was associated with profound alterations in the DNA methylome of circulating leucocytes, and differential methylation was located in trauma-relevant genes.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Eskesen, Trine O.","Almstrup, Kristian","Elgaard, Laurits","Arleth, Tobias","Lassen, Mathilde L.","Creutzburg, Andreas","Jensen, Alice Herrlin","Breindahl, Niklas","Dinesen, Felicia","Vang, Malene","Sørensen, Erik","Paulsen, Anders Wallin","Nielsen, Tatiana","Rasmussen, Lars S","Sillesen, Martin","Steinmetz, Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-777094"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"severe traumatic injury is associated with profound changes in dna methylation","src":["