mpany","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cancer Survivorship","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163863378"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-244942b6-c638-4c2e-b959-fe22823f433d","au-20e7d775-cbbd-4bb6-a5f1-b55b8a2a3d7a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Quality of life and symptom burden after rectal cancer surgery : a randomised controlled trial comparing patient‑led versus standard follow‑up","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-098.21-681208","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In 2020, Denmark buried approximately four million culled, farmed mink in mass graves treated with slaked lime due to widespread SARS-CoV-2 infections. After six months, environmental concerns prompted the exhumation of these cadavers. Our analysis encompassed visual inspections, soil pH measurements, and gas emission assessments of the grave environment. Additionally, we evaluated carcasses for decay status, cadaverine content, and the presence of various pathogens, including SARS-CoV-2 and mink coronavirus. Our findings revealed minimal microbial activity and limited carcass decomposition. Although viral RNA from SARS-CoV-2 and mink coronavirus, along with DNA from Aleutian mink disease virus, were detected, the absence of infectious SARS-CoV-2 in cell culture assays suggests slow natural degradation processes. This study provides critical insights for future considerations in managing mass burial scenarios during outbreaks of livestock-associated zoonotic pathogens.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Thamsborg, Kristian Key Milan","Hansen, Mette Sif","Scheutz, Charlotte","Klintø, Kasper","Kjeldsen, Peter","Kvisgaard, Lise Kirstine","Jensen, Henrik Elvang","Hjerpe, Freja Broe","Lohse, Louise","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Rasmussen, Lasse Dam","Bedsted, Amalie Ehlers","Belsham, Graham J.","Leisner, Jørgen J.","Dalsgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-761918"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Dalsgaard, Anders"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"microbiological and decomposition analysis of mass mink burial sites during the covi