{"abstract":"I dette kapitel får du viden om det danske beskæftigelsessystem. Vi introducerer kort til den særlige danske arbejdsmarkedsmodel, for derefter at rette fokus mod beskæftigelsessystemets formål og organisering. Du får indblik i de forskellige forsørgelsesordninger og beskæftigelsespolitiske indsatser, og vi runder kapitlet af med at redegøre for, hvordan socialområdet og beskæftigelsesområdet er tæt forbundne områder.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Anders Bøggild","Salado-Rasmussen, Julia"],"cuid":["S02-087.50-785411"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Inklusion"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum","soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"det danske beskæftigelsessystem","src":["kp","via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP","DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-087.50-785411","ids":["kp-fae37967-1db8-41d0-8a7e-a34199962488","via-81344d22-3cf7-485b-95fe-68941b295558"],"keyword":["inklusion"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities","Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-2043992A46857C071C168D4FEB68ECA9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for sundhed og samfund, Forsk.center for social udsathed","VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forskningsområde for sundhed og samfund, Research Programme for Employment and Social Work","VIA, Uddannelser, Social- og samfundsuddannelserne, Socialrådgiveruddannelsen Aarhus C team A-B-C"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Professionshøjskole, Rektors område, Fakultet for pædagogiske og samfundsfaglige uddannelser-Dekan, Socialrådgiveruddannelsen Forskning og Udvikling","Socialt Arbejde - Institut for Socialrådgiveruddannelse, Beskæftigelse","Socialt Arbejde - Institut for Socialrådgiveruddannelse, Udsatte voksne"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Bøggild","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"15d3eb85-8ffe-4c32-b970-43d444374d12","name":"Christensen, Anders Bøggild","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Julia","key":"saladorasmussenpau","last":"Salado-Rasmussen","locid":"545adcc2-0b84-48c1-9a92-3f1eb78bafac","name":"Salado-Rasmussen, Julia","orcid":"0000-0003-1372-1782","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Inge Storgaard","key":"bonfilspedh","last":"Bonfils","name":"Bonfils, Inge Storgaard","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Julia","key":"saladorasmussenpedh","last":"Salado-Rasmussen","name":"Salado-Rasmussen, Julia","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788750063728"],"pages":"31-52","place":"Akademisk Forlag","publisher":"Akademisk Forlag","series":"Professions serien","status":"p","subtitle":"Ved brug af Supported Employment og Individuelt Planlagt job med Støtte","title":"Arbejdsinkludering"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-fae37967-1db8-41d0-8a7e-a34199962488","via-81344d22-3cf7-485b-95fe-68941b295558"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","VIA University College"],"title":"Det danske beskæftigelsessystem","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-785411","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Oxygen supplementation is ubiquitous in intensive care unit (ICU) patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD) and acute hypoxaemia, but the optimal oxygenation target has not been established. Methods: This was a pre-planned subgroup analysis of the Handling Oxygenation Targets in the ICU (HOT-ICU) trial, which allocated patients with acute hypoxaemia to a lower oxygenation target (partial pressure of arterial oxygen [PaO2] of 8 kPa) vs a higher target (PaO2 of 12 kPa) during ICU admission, for up to 90 days; the allocation was stratified for presence or absence of COPD. Here, we report key outcomes for patients with COPD. Results: The HOT-ICU trial enrolled 2928 patients of whom 563 had COPD; 277 were allocated to the lower and 286 to the higher oxygenation group. After allocation, the median PaO2 was 9.1 kPa (inter-quartile range 8.7–9.9) in the lower group vs 12.1 kPa (11.2–12.9) in the higher group. Data for arterial carbon dioxide (PaCO2) were available for 497 patients (88%) with no between-group difference in time-weighted average; median PaCO2 6.0 kPa (5.2–7.2) in the lower group vs 6.2 kPa (5.4–7.3) in the higher group. At 90 days, 122/277 patients (44%) in the lower oxygenation group had died vs 132/285 patients (46%) in the higher (relative risk 0.98; 95% confidence interval 0.82–1.17; P=0.67). No statistically significant differences were found in any secondary outcome. Conclusions: In ICU patients with COPD and acute hypoxaemia, a lower vs a higher oxygenation target did not reduce mortality. There were no between-group differences in PaCO2 or in secondary outcomes. Clinical trial registration: NCT 03174002, EudraCT number 2017-000632-34.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Maria B.","Klitgaard, Thomas L.","Weinreich, Ulla M.","Nielsen, Frederik M.","Perner, Anders","Schjørring, Olav L.","Rasmussen, Bodil S."],"cuid":["S02-099.81-741261"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"keyword":["Chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","Critical care","Hyperoxia","Hypoxia","Intensive Care Units","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of a lower i versus i a higher oxygenation target in intensive care unit patients with chronic obstructive pulmonary disease and acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure a subgroup analysis of a randomised clinical trial","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bjao.2024.100281","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The HOT-ICU trial was funded by a grant from Innovation Fund Denmark (4108-00011A) and supported by Aalborg University Hospital, the Regions of Denmark (EMN-2017-00901 and EMN-2019-01055), the Obel Family Foundation (25457), the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine, and the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl. No additional funding was provided for this sub-study. Funders of this study had no role in the design, collection, analysis, interpretation of data, or writing of this report. The Department of Intensive Care at Rigshospitalet has received funding for other projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Pfizer, Sygeforsikringen \\u2018danmark\\u2019 and Fresenius Kabi and does contract research for AM Pharma. UMW has received fees, including transportation reimbursement for: Congress participation: Orion Pharma; Advisory boards: TEVA, Astra Zeneca, Chiesi and Novartis; Speaker\\u2019s fees: Astra Zeneca, Chiesi, Novartis, Boehringer Ingelheim, GSK, Orion Pharma, Fisher&Paykel Healthcare and ResMed; Writer\\u2019s fee: Astra Zeneca; Pharma-initiated research: Astra Zeneca, GSK, Novartis, Ins-Med, Sanofi, Novartis, Boehringer Ingelheim and Genetech; Research grant: Fisher&Paykel Healthcare and Liita Healthcare."],"id":"S02-099.81-741261","identifier":[{"id":"38711834","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11070685","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85191451287","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0a713809-dff0-4563-b77f-f8669f6e2e93","ku-c08334ea-715f-4fdf-8da3-a0e86d5ee95e"],"keyword":["chronic obstructive pulmonary disease","critical care","hyperoxia","hypoxia","intensive care units","oxygen inhalation therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E8AC706948AD35F439639614EBA2C7F0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/391210262/1_s2.0_S277260962400025X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.bjao.2024.100281","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/713506125/Nielsen_et_al._2024_._Effects_of_a_lower_versus_a_higher_oxygenation_target_in_intensive_care_unit_patients_with_chronic_obstructive_pulmonary_disease_and_acute_hypoxaemic_respiratory_failure_a_subgroup_analysis_of_a_randomised_cl.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Me