{"abstract":"Objectives: Little is known about whether induced abortions are associated with the final lifetime number of live births (life births). The objective of this study was to examine the association between the number of life births with the number of abortions a female has had in her lifetime. Methods: In a national cohort design, we followed all Danish females from ages 15 to 44 years through the period 1977–2017 for induced abortions and live births. For each lifetime number of induced abortions, the average number of life births was assessed, and rates with 95% CI were calculated. Results: The study included 409 497 females who completed 222 482 induced abortions and 831 742 live births. Of 265 573 (64.9%) females who did not have any induced abortion, the average number of life births was 2.09 (95% CI 2.08–2.10). For females with 1 (23.4%), 2 (7.4%), 3 (2.6%), 4 (1.0%), and ≥5 (0.7%) induced abortions during their reproductive lifespan, the average number of life births was 1.88 (1.87–1.89), 1.99 (1.98–2.00), 2.09 (2.06–2.11), 2.13 (2.09–2.15), and 2.25 (2.21–2.29), respectively. The increase in number of life births in females with 1 to females with 5+ induced abortions was 4.7% for each additional induced abortion. Conclusion: We found the number of induced abortions during a woman's reproductive lifespan to be positively correlated to the number of live births. This association is likely explained by a high fecundity in females with multiple pregnancies including induced abortions and suggests that even several induced abortions do not compromise a woman's general reproductive end points.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lidegaard, Øjvind","Borberg, Hjarn von Zernichow","Rasmussen, Steen C.","Mikkelsen, Anders P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760487"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Birth Rate","Deliveries","Induced abortion","Live Birth","Reproduction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lifetime induced abortions and live births a 000000000040 year historical cohort study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jogc.2024.102612","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-760487","identifier":[{"id":"39004402","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85201195443","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e6006b32-b3e2-4b11-a915-be7a89494068"],"keyword":["birth rate","deliveries","induced abortion","live birth","reproduction","therapeutic abortion"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-66E9A03D11DD8ACEC8ADD159B970C071"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jogc.2024.102612","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402816180/1_s2.0_S1701216324004353.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Obstetrics and Gynaecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Øjvind","key":"lidegaardpau","last":"Lidegaard","locid":"477519a8-a5d9-4dcf-970a-e11c7e4f936f","name":"Lidegaard, Øjvind","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hjarn V.","key":"zernichowborbergpau","last":"Zernichow Borberg","locid":"8181839c-ef4f-4ae1-a6db-8ec89b059d6f","name":"Borberg, Hjarn von Zernichow","name_org":"Zernichow Borberg, Hjarn V.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Steen C.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Steen C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders P.","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","name":"Mikkelsen, Anders P.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39004402"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jogc.2024.102612","issn":["17012163"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Canada","paperid":"102612","status":"p","title":"Journal of Obstetrics and Gynaecology Canada","volume":"46"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85201195443"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e6006b32-b3e2-4b11-a915-be7a89494068"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lifetime Induced Abortions and Live Births : A 40-Year Historical Cohort Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760487","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To improve health conditions among hypogonadal men ≥70 years of age using testosterone undecanoate (TU) injections, progressive strength training, and oral supplements of vitamin D, calcium, and protein. Methods: This study is a 1-year follow-up of a double-blind RCT lasting 20 weeks, including 148 older men ≥70 years old with low testosterone levels and mobility problems. During 52 weeks, 4 groups received either testosterone therapy (TU) or progressive resistance training (Training), both (Combo), or no intervention (Controls). Physiotherapists supported the training groups until week 20, while these participants continued trained on their own during weeks 21 to 52. The main outcome measure was the 30-s chair stand test. Results: The following numbers of participants completed the trial: 20 (Combo), 20 (Controls), 24 (TU), and 14 (Training). When examining 30-s chair stand test performance within each group at baseline, and at weeks 4, 20 and 52, only the Combo group improved (p = 0.001, Friedman Test). Compared to controls, only the Combo group experienced reduced fatigue and tiredness (p < 0.05). Conclusions: Fifty-two weeks of testosterone supplementation combined with progressive resistance training may enhance physical performance, alleviate fatigue, and had no notable detrimental impacts among males aged ≥70 suffering from mobility issues and testosterone insufficiency. Trial registration - Clinical Trials NCT02873559.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Rune Skovgaard","Midttun, Mette","Zerahn, Bo","Pedersen, Maria","Rashid, Anahita","Østergren, Peter Busch","Paulin, Tine Kolenda","Pødenphanth, Thea Winther","Karlsson, Linda Katharina","Rosendahl, Eva","Ragle, Anne Mette","Vinther, Anders","Overgaard, Karsten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-765319"],"filters":{"added":"2024-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Elderly","Falls","Physical exercise","Resistance Training","Testosterone therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"testosterone and resistance training improved physical performance and reduced fatigue in frail older men 000000000001 year follow up of a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/13685538.2024.2403519","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-765319","identifier":[{"id":"39289825","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85204512524","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ab03a4d3-e51c-4e36-bcd7-0279e1472263"],"keyword":["Falls","elderly","physical exercise","resistance training","testosterone therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D81B13EDFBF68FA73EE09EA23DEC4D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/407312219/Testosterone_and_resistance_training_improved_physical_performance_and_reduced_fatigue_in_frail_older_men_1_year_follow_up_of_a_randomized_clinical_t.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/13685538.2024.2403519","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc