"Overgaard, Karsten","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39289825"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/13685538.2024.2403519","issn":["13685538","14730790"],"issn_org":["13685538"],"issue":"1","journal":"Aging Male","paperid":"2403519","status":"p","title":"Aging Male","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85204512524"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ab03a4d3-e51c-4e36-bcd7-0279e1472263"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Testosterone and resistance training improved physical performance and reduced fatigue in frail older men : 1 year follow-up of a randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-765319","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The vibrationally resolved gas-phase electronic photoabsorption spectrum of protonated pentacenequinone was measured at a cryogenic temperature using a combination of a cryogenically cooled ion trap and an ion-storage ring. The spectrum reveals a distinct vibrational structure, with the lowest vibrational band measured at 16912cm-1 (591.3nm), assigned to the 0→0 transition. Excellent agreement is observed between the measured spectrum and the spectroscopic fingerprint predicted by time-dependent density functional theory. Our results show that oxygen-functionalized polycyclic aromatic hydrocarbons of this size can absorb and exhibit a vibrational structure in regions relevant to both extended red emission and diffuse interstellar bands.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anne P.","Klinkby, Nikolaj","Lauridsen, Anders G.S.","Andersen, Lars H."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-772145"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars H."],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vibrationally resolved gas phase electronic spectrum of cryogenic protonated pentacenequinone","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85211200168","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-772145","identifier":[{"id":"85211200168","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3bb9a185-96f0-411c-97f4-d25aa4b22a80"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C1655A1C4B2EB0BFA6FAEE3173A9A96E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe,