{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: A rising number of countries allow physicians to treat chronic pain with medical cannabis. However, recreational cannabis use has been linked with cardiovascular side effects, necessitating investigations concerning the safety of prescribed medical cannabis. METHODS: Using nationwide Danish registers, patients with chronic pain initiating first-time treatment with medical cannabis during 2018-21 were identified and matched 1:5 to corresponding control patients on age, sex, chronic pain diagnosis, and concomitant use of other pain medication. The absolute risks of first-time arrhythmia (atrial fibrillation/flutter, conduction disorders, paroxysmal tachycardias, and ventricular arrhythmias) and acute coronary syndrome were reported comparing medical cannabis use with no use. RESULTS: Among 1.88 million patients with chronic pain (46% musculoskeletal, 11% cancer, 13% neurological, and 30% unspecified pain), 5391 patients claimed a prescription of medical cannabis [63.2% women, median age: 59 (inter-quartile range 48-70) years] and were compared with 26 941 control patients of equal sex- and age composition. Arrhythmia was observed in 42 and 107 individuals, respectively, within 180 days. Medical cannabis use was associated with an elevated risk of new-onset arrhythmia {180-day absolute risk: 0.8% [95% confidence interval (CI) 0.6%-1.1%]} compared with no use [180-day absolute risk: 0.4% (95% CI 0.3%-0.5%)]: a risk ratio of 2.07 (95% CI 1.34-2.80) and a 1-year risk ratio of 1.36 (95% CI 1.00-1.73). No significant association was found for acute coronary syndrome [180-day risk ratio: 1.20 (95% CI 0.35-2.04)]. CONCLUSIONS: In patients with chronic pain, the use of prescribed medical cannabis was associated with an elevated risk of new-onset arrhythmia compared with no use-most pronounced in the 180 days following the initiation of treatment.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Holt, Anders","Nouhravesh, Nina","Strange, Jarl E","Kinnberg Nielsen, Sebastian","Schjerning, Anne-Marie","Vibe Rasmussen, Peter","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Gislason, Gunnar","Schou, Morten","McGettigan, Patricia","Lamberts, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-099.95-725146"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Holt, Anders"],"country":["New Zealand","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","The University of Auckland","University of Auckland"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Arrhythmia","Chronic pain","Drug safety","Heart failure","Medical cannabis","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cannabis for chronic pain cardiovascular safety in a nationwide danish study","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85184586558","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The lead investigator, A.H., and this study have been funded by external, independent grants from ‘IMK Almene Fond’ (J. nr. 30206-383), ‘Helsefonden’ (20-B-0035), ‘Snedkermester Sophus Jacobsen og hustru Astrid Jacobsens Fond’ (J 167/1), ‘Marie og M.B. Richters Fond’ (J. nr. 2020-0379), and ‘Dagmar Marshalls Fond’. None of the funds has had any influence on the conduction of this study."],"id":"S02-099.95-725146","identifier":[{"id":"38200679","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184586558","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-217c1ee6-8e42-4373-aced-3ccec251c205","sdu-f3aa20bc-fa31-496c-a881-c8fe1883ab70"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Arrhythmia","Chronic pain","Drug safety","Heart failure","Medical cannabis","Stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B5D613544F70986A847A6E263F3CC42B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"the university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nz","key":"university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Zealand University Hospital - Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-HJER","l3nn":"Danish Heart Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Heart Foundation","namevar":["Hjerteforeningen"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-HJER","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, National Institute of Public Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Anders","key":"holtpau","last":"Holt","name":"Holt, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina","key":"nouhraveshpau","last":"Nouhravesh","name":"Nouhravesh, Nina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jarl E","key":"strangepau","last":"Strange","name":"Strange, Jarl E","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"kinnbergnielsenpau","last":"Kinnberg Nielsen","name":"Kinnberg Nielsen, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","first":"Anne-Marie","key":"schjerningpau","last":"Schjerning","name":"Schjerning, Anne-Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"viberasmussenpau","last":"Vibe Rasmussen","name":"Vibe Rasmussen, Peter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 1","first":"Christian","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"f71bedc6-3736-4559-b937-6a18e770616e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6 5 7","first":"Gunnar H","key":"gislasonpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","name_org":"Gislason, Gunnar H","orcid":"0000-0002-0548-402X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"Morten","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"48fa6ec9-1941-4566-b931-14b0cc8cbae3","name":"Schou, Morten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Patricia","key":"mcgettiganpau","last":"McGettigan","name":"McGettigan, Patricia","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"Morten","key":"lambertspau","last":"Lamberts","locid":"ced953f0-cd5e-4af3-8c41-7311decea61f","name":"Lamberts, Morten","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38200679"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehad834","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"6","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"475-484","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"45"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184586558"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-217c1ee6-8e42-4373-aced-3ccec251c205","sdu-f3aa20bc-fa31-496c-a881-c8fe1883ab70"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cannabis for chronic pain : Cardiovascular safety in a nationwide Danish study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.95-725146","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To structurally characterize in detail the interactions between the phage repressor (CI) and the antirepressor (Mor) in the lysis-lysogeny switches of two Gram-positive bacteriophages, the lactococcal TP901-1 and staphylococcal φ13. Methods: We use crystallographic structure determination, computational structural modeling, and analysis, as well as biochemical methods, to elucidate similarities and differences in the CI:Mor interactions for the two genetic switches. Results: By comparing a newly determined and other available crystal structures for the N-terminal domain of CI (CI-NTD), we show that the CI interface involved in Mor binding undergoes structural changes upon binding in TP901-1. Most importantly, we show experimentally for the first time the direct interaction between CI and Mor for φ13, and model computationally the interaction interface. The computational modeling supports similar side chain rearrangements in TP901-1 and φ13. Conclusion: This study ascertains experimentally that, like in the TP901-1 lysogeny switch, staphylococcal φ13 CI and Mor interact with each other. The structural basis of the interaction of φ13 CI and Mor was computationally modeled and is similar to the interaction demonstrated experimentally between TP901-1 CI-NTD and Mor, likely involving similar rearrangement of residue side chains during the formation of the complex. The study identifies one CI residue, Glu69, which unusually interacts primarily through its aliphatic chain with an aromatic residue on Mor after changing its conformation compared to the un-complexed structure. This and other residues at the interface are suggested for investigation in future studies.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Varming, Anders K.","Huang, Zhiyu","Hamad, Ghofran M.","Rasmussen, Kim K.","Ingmer, Hanne","Kilstrup, Mogens","Lo Leggio, Leila"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-716232"],"filters":{"added":"2024-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lo Leggio, Leila"],"keyword":["Antirepressor","Corepressor","Human adaptation","Lysogeny switch","Pathogen","Repressor","Temperate phage"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ci mor interactions in the lysogeny switches of i lactococcus lactis i tp000000000901 000000000001 and i staphylococcus aureus i φ000000000013 bacteriophages","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20517/mrr.2023.50","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-716232","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11149083","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38841409","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85183350808","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-68bbca09-d286-4250-aa6a-dfebb386abbd","ku-647454c7-c0f7-4798-bb07-cf89d52eea6e"],"keyword":["Antirepressor","Corepressor","Human adaption","Lysogeny switch","Pathogen","Repressor","Temperate phage","human adaptation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1AFF0C4E1835ED443E500526409463AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.20517/mrr.2023.50","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381887011/mrr2050.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/351358443/mrr2050.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar"