":["38841409"],"pub":{"doi":"10.20517/mrr.2023.50","issn":["27715965"],"issue":"2","journal":"Microbiome Research Reports","paperid":"15","publisher":"OAE Publishing","status":"p","title":"Microbiome Research Reports","volume":"3"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85183350808"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-68bbca09-d286-4250-aa6a-dfebb386abbd","ku-647454c7-c0f7-4798-bb07-cf89d52eea6e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"CI:Mor interactions in the lysogeny switches of <i>Lactococcus lactis</i> TP901-1 and <i>Staphylococcus aureus</i> φ13 bacteriophages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-716232","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: In the COVID-STEROID 2 trial there was suggestion of heterogeneity of treatment effects (HTE) between patients enrolled from Europe vs. India on the primary outcome. Whether there was HTE for the remaining patient-centred outcomes is unclear. Methods: In this post hoc analysis of the COVID-STEROID 2 trial, which compared 12 mg vs. 6 mg dexamethasone in adults with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia, we evaluated HTE by geographical region (Europe vs. India) for secondary outcomes with analyses adjusted for stratification variables. Results are presented as risk differences (RDs) or mean differences (MDs) with 99% confidence intervals (CIs) and P-values from interaction tests. Findings: There were differences in mortality at day 28 (RD for Europe −8.3% (99% CI: −17.7 to 1.0) vs. India 0.1% (99% CI: −10.0 to 10.0)), mortality at day 90 (RD for Europe −7.4% (99% CI: −17.1 to 2.0) vs. India −1.4% (99% CI: −12.8 to 9.8)), mortality at day 180 (RD for Europe −6.7% (99% CI: −16.4 to 2.9) vs. India −1.0% (99% CI: −12.3 to 10.3)), and number of days alive without life support at day 90 (MD for Europe 6.1 days (99% CI: −1.3 to 13.4) vs. India 1.7 days (99% CI: −8.4 to 11.8)). For serious adverse reactions, the direction was reversed (RD for Europe −1.0% (99% CI: −7.1 to 5.2) vs. India −5.3% (99% CI: −16.2 to 5.0). Interpretation: Our analysis suggests higher dose dexamethasone may have less beneficial effects for patients in India as compared with those in Europe; however, the evidence is weak, and this could represent a chance finding. Funding: None for this analysis. The COVID STEROID 2 trial was funded by The Novo Nordisk Foundation and supported by Rigshospitalet's Research Council.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Tirupakuzhi Vijayaraghavan, Bharath Kumar","Granholm, Anders","Munch, Marie W.","Kjær, Maj Brit N.","Møller, Morten Hylander","Perner, Anders","Myatra, Sheila N.","Jha, Vivekanand","Jha, Vivekanand","Jha, Vivekanand","Hammond, Naomi","Micallef, Sharon","Venkatesh, Balasubramanian","Hammond, Naomi","Lange, Theis","Munch, Marie W.","Myatra, Sheila N.","Tirupakuzhi Vijayaraghavan, Bharath Kumar","Saseedharan, Sanjith","Benfield, Thomas","Wahlin, Rebecka R.","Rasmussen, Bodil S.","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Poulsen, Lone M.","Cioccari, Luca","Khan, Mohd S.","Kapadia, Farhad","Divatia, Jigeeshu V.","Brøchner, Anne C.","Bestle, Morten H.","Helleberg, Marie","Michelsen, Jens","Padmanaban, Ajay","Bose, Neeta","Møller, Anders","Borawake, Kapil","Kristiansen, Klaus Tjelle","Shukla, Urvi","Chew, Michelle S.","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Kjær, Maj Brit N.","Møller, Morten Hylander","Meyhoff, Tine S.","Vesterlund, Gitte K.","Gluud, Christian","Lange, Theis","Marcussen, Klaus V.","Nielsen, Henrik","Jensen, Thomas S.","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-724058"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["the COVID-STEROID 2 collaborators"],"corresponding_author":["Tirupakuzhi Vijayaraghavan, Bharath Kumar"],"country":["Australia","India","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Apollo Hospitals Group","Homi Bhabha National Institute","Imperial College London","Karolinska Institutet","Manipal Academy of Higher Education","Royal North Shore Hospital","Tata Memorial Hospital","The George Institute for Global Health","University of New South Wales"],"keyword":["Covid 19","Developing countries","Randomised controlled trials","Steroids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"heterogeneity of treatment effect of higher dose dexamethasone by geographic region europe vs india in patients with covid 000000000019 and severe hypoxemia a post hoc evaluation of the covid steroid 000000000002 trial","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lansea.2023.100293","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["None for this analysis. The COVID STEROID 2 trial was funded by The Novo Nordisk Foundation and supported by Rigshospitalet's Research Council."],"id":"S02-100.00-724058","identifier":[{"id":"85173170884","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38234702","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10794101","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-26871d67-174a-4629-9bd0-51490aba743b","ku-7fbdf1cd-50e6-465f-96d4-5b12da879f84"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Developing countries","Randomised controlled trials","Steroids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-78680A825DC10EE7B316FCA474D26C30"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lansea.2023.100293","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/385566345/1_s2.0_S2772368223001531_main_1_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/715025399/Vijayaraghavan_et_al._2024_._Heterogeneity_of_treatment_effect_of_higher_dose_dexamethasone_by_geographic_region_Europe_vs._India_in_patients_with_COVID-19_and_severe_hypoxemia_-_a_post_hoc_evaluation_of_the_COVID_STEROI.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"in","key":"apollo hospitals group","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Apollo Hospitals Group","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"in","key":"tata memorial hospital","loc":["India","Asia, South"],"name":"Tata Memorial Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-