key":"michelsenjenspau","last":"Michelsen","name":"Michelsen, Jens","rank":32,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ajay","key":"padmanabanajaypau","last":"Padmanaban","name":"Padmanaban, Ajay","rank":33,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Neeta","key":"boseneetapau","last":"Bose","name":"Bose, Neeta","rank":34,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"mølleranderspau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Anders","rank":35,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kapil","key":"borawakekapilpau","last":"Borawake","name":"Borawake, Kapil","rank":36,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Klaus T.","key":"kristiansenklaustjellepau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"c9a7668e-8428-415b-adc0-a7494477316d","name":"Kristiansen, Klaus Tjelle","name_org":"Kristiansen, Klaus T.","rank":37,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Urvi","key":"shuklaurvipau","last":"Shukla","name":"Shukla, Urvi","rank":38,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michelle S.","key":"chewmichellespau","last":"Chew","name":"Chew, Michelle S.","rank":39,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Charlotte S.","key":"ulrikcharlottesupplipau","last":"Ulrik","locid":"ea578010-4d8b-498b-b9d0-8f3d8cc424df","name":"Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","name_org":"Ulrik, Charlotte S.","rank":40,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Tine S.","key":"meyhofftinespau","last":"Meyhoff","name":"Meyhoff, Tine S.","rank":43,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gitte K.","key":"vesterlundgittekpau","last":"Vesterlund","name":"Vesterlund, Gitte K.","rank":44,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Christian","key":"gluudchristianpau","last":"Gluud","name":"Gluud, Christian","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","first":"Klaus V.","key":"marcussenklausvpau","last":"Marcussen","locid":"5e0dc42b-1269-4688-bf0e-b32d98a451ce","name":"Marcussen, Klaus V.","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Henrik","key":"nielsenhenrikpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Henrik","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas S.","key":"jensenthomasspau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Thomas S.","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38234702"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.lansea.2023.100293","issn":["27723682"],"journal":"The Lancet Regional Health - Southeast Asia","paperid":"100293","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Regional Health - Southeast Asia","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85173170884"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-26871d67-174a-4629-9bd0-51490aba743b","ku-7fbdf1cd-50e6-465f-96d4-5b12da879f84"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Heterogeneity of treatment effect of higher dose dexamethasone by geographic region (Europe vs. India) in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia – a post hoc evaluation of the COVID STEROID 2 trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-724058","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Bacterial meningitis can cause a life-threatening increase in intracranial pressure (ICP). ICP-targeted treatment including an ICP monitoring device and external ventricular drainage (EVD) may improve outcomes but is also associated with the risk of complications. The frequency of use and complications related to ICP monitoring devices and EVDs among patients with bacterial meningitis remain unknown. We aimed to investigate the use of ICP monitoring devices and EVDs in patients with bacterial meningitis including frequency of increased ICP, drainage of cerebrospinal fluid (CSF), and complications associated with the insertion of ICP monitoring and external ventricular drain (EVD) in patients with bacterial meningitis. Method: In a single-center prospective cohort study (2017–2021), we examined the frequency of use and complications of ICP-monitoring devices and EVDs in adult patients with bacterial meningitis. Results: We identified 108 patients with bacterial meningitis admitted during the study period. Of these, 60 were admitted to the intensive care unit (ICU), and 47 received an intracranial device (only ICP monitoring device N = 16; EVD N = 31). An ICP > 20 mmHg was observed in 8 patients at insertion, and in 21 patients (44%) at any time in the ICU. Cerebrospinal fluid (CSF) was drained in 24 cases (51%). Severe complications (intracranial hemorrhage) related to the device occurred in two patients, but one had a relative contraindication to receiving a device. Conclusions: Approximately half of the patients with bacterial meningitis needed intensive care and 47 had an intracranial device inserted. While some had conservatively correctable ICP, the majority needed CSF drainage. However, two patients experienced serious adverse events related to the device, potentially contributing to death. Our study highlights that the incremental value of ICP measurement and EVD in managing of bacterial meningitis requires further research.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Tetens, Malte M.","Roed, Casper","Bodilsen, Jacob","Omland, Lars H.","Mens, Helene","Lebech, Anne Mette","Obel, Niels","Møller, Kirsten","Rasmussen, Rune","Overgaard-Steensen, Christian","Perner, Anders","Ziebell, Morten","Andersen, Åse B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-751593"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Bacterial","Cohort Studies","Critical Care methods","Drainage methods","Female","Humans","Intracranial Pressure physiology","Intracranial pressure","Male","Meningitis","Meningitis Bacterial","Middle Aged","Monitoring Physiologic methods","Neurosurgery","Postoperative Complications","Prospective Studies","Ventriculostomy methods"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"use of intensive care intracranial pressure monitoring and external ventricular drainage devises in patients with bacterial meningitis a cohort study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00701-024-06188-7","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["MMT has received travel grants outside this work from GlaxoSmithKline Pharma A/S. AML reports speakers\\u2019 honorarium/travel grants/advisory board activity and unrestricted grant from Gilead, speakers honorarium /travel grants from GSK, speaker\\u2019s honorarium/advisory board activity from Pfizer outside this work. AP reports honorarium for advisory board work at Novartis. None of the authors report any conflict of interests in connection with this article."],"id":"S02-100.00-751593","identifier":[{"id":"85197819999","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38980542","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11233385","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-81e8cad6-2b67-4bd4-97a9-14bb2ccb535b","ku-30ecce1b-1981-48e1-affa-9ed42c4e16d8"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Bacterial","Cohort Studies","Critical Care/methods","Drainage/methods","Female","Humans","Intracranial Hypertension/surgery","Intracranial Pressure/physiology","Intracranial pressure","Male","Meningitis","Meningitis, Bacterial","Middle Aged","Monitoring, Physiologic/methods","Neurosurgery","Postoperative complications","Prospective Studies","Ventriculostomy/methods"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3005CD953BC7E9AE745D83887A3DFB9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00701-024-06188-7","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/398428701/s00701_024_06188_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/726159837/Tetens_et_al._2024_._Use_of_intensive_care_intracranial_pressure_monitoring_and_external_ventricular_drainage_devises_in_patients_with_bacterial_meningitis_a_cohort_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Infectious Diseases","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Malte M.","key":"tetenspau","last":"Tetens","name":"Tetens, Malte M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper","key":"roedpau","last":"Roed","name":"Roed, Casper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob","key":"bodilsenpau","last":"Bodilsen","locid":"260dd517-12cb-4490-b8c0-c69efb455878","name":"Bodilsen, Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-7398-814X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars H.","key":"omlandpau","last":"Omland","name":"Omland, Lars H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Helene","key":"menspau","last":"Mens","name":"Mens, Helene","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Anne Mette","key":"lebechpau","last":"Lebech","locid":"f9b459b7-e203-4824-9d80-e7c0e5b56232","name":"Lebech, Anne Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-0943-3289","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Niels","key":"obelpau","last":"Obel","locid":"47b44abc-6c99-4a76-b8b0-ca53b033951b","name":"Obel, Niels","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Kirsten","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"0781d3e6-9d76-4ba7-8a17-5a4d81e6ab87","name":"Møller, Kirsten","orcid":"0000-0003-3058-1072","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rune","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Rune","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"overgaardsteensenpau","last":"Overgaard-Steensen","name":"Overgaard-Steensen, Christian","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"ziebellpau","last":"Ziebell","name":"Ziebell, Morten","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Åse B.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Åse B.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38980542"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00701-024-06188-7","issn":["00016268","09420940"],"issn_org":["00016268"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Neurochirurgica","paperid":"287","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Acta Neurochirurgica","volume":"166"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197819999"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-81e8cad6-2b67-4bd4-97a9-14bb2ccb535b","ku-30ecce1b-1981-48e1-affa-9ed42c4e16d8"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Use of intensive care, intracranial pressure monitoring, and external ventricular drainage devises in patients with bacterial meningitis, a cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-751593","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Pleural effusion is present in half of the patients hospitalised with acute heart failure. The condition is treated with diuretics and/or therapeutic thoracentesis for larger effusions. No evidence from randomised trials or guidelines supports thoracentesis to alleviate pleural effusion due to acute heart failure. The Thoracentesis to Alleviate cardiac Pleural effusion Interventional Trial (TAP-IT) will investigate if a strategy of referring patients with acute heart failure and pleural effusion to up-front thoracentesis by pleural pigtail catheter insertion in addition to pharmacological therapy compared with pharmacological therapy alone can increase the number of days the participants are alive and not hospitalised during the 90 days following randomisation. Methods and analysis TAP-IT is a pragmatic, multicentre, open-label, randomised controlled trial aiming to include 126 adult patients with left ventricular ejection fraction ≤45% and a non-negligible pleural effusion due to heart failure. Participants will be randomised 1:1, stratified according to site and anticoagulant treatment, and assigned to referral to up-front ultrasound-guided pleural pigtail catheter thoracentesis in addition to standard pharmacological therapy or to standard pharmacological therapy only. Thoracentesis is performed according to local guidelines and can be performed in participants in the pharmacological treatment arm if their condition deteriorates or if no significant improvement is observed within 5 days. The primary endpoint is how many days participants are alive and not hospitalised within 90 days from randomisation and will be analysed in the intention-to-treat population. Key secondary outcomes include 90-day mortality, complications, readmissions, and quality of life. Ethics and dissemination The study has been approved by the Capital Region of Denmark Scientific Ethical Committee (H-20060817) and Knowledge Center for Data Reviews (P-2021-149). All participants will sign an informed consent form. Enrolment began in August 2021. Regardless of the nature, results will be published in a peer-reviewed medical journal. Trial registration number NCT05017753.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Glargaard, Signe","Thomsen, Jakob Hartvig","Løgstrup, Brian Bridal","Schou, Morten","Iversen, Kasper","Tuxen, Christian","Nielsen, Olav Wendelboe","Bang, Christian Axel","Lindholm, Matias Greve","Seven, Ekim","Barasa, Anders","Stride, Nis","Vraa, Søren","Tofterup, Marlene","Rasmussen, Rasmus Vedby","Høfsten, Dan E.","Rossing, Kasper","Køber, Lars","Gustafsson, Finn","Thune, Jens Jakob"],"cuid":["S04-099.95-724182"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Glargaard, Signe"],"keyword":["Adult","Cardiology","Clinical trial","Heart Failure complications","Heart failure","Humans","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Pleural Effusion therapy","Pragmatic Clinical Trials as Topic","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Stroke Volume","Thoracentesis","Ventricular Function Left"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thoracentesis to alleviate pleural effusion in acute heart failure study protocol for the multicentre open label randomised controlled tap it trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078155","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The trial is supported by The Independent Research Fund Denmark (grant number 1030-00121B) with additional funding from the Hartmann Foundation (grant number A36846), Per Henriksen's Fund and the Research Foundation at Copenhagen University Hospital—Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg, Denmark. SG has received a personal grant from the Research Foundation at Copenhagen University Hospital—Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg, Denmark."],"id":"S04-099.95-724182","identifier":[{"id":"001154790300030","type":"wos"},{"id":"38245015","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85182851760","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10806591","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-6a56e853-e78a-42de-9608-6f4a85f6c78c","au-dfd33bc4-8359-4bcf-9ea0-29552c7a687a","ku-be984a11-58ed-46a7-8aaf-e5b85f7c2bcf","sdu-45e876b4-de18-4496-b6ae-e7df1acc4424"],"keyword":["Adult","Cardiology","Clinical Trial","Heart Failure/complications","Heart failure","Humans","Multicenter Studies as Topic","Pleural Effusion/therapy","Pragmatic Clinical Trials as Topic","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trials as Topic","Stroke Volume","Thoracentesis","Ventricular Function, Left"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-1A4BE3CA471FC4CF28BD14DC652E150F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/bmjopen-2023-078155","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/381070912/e078155.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/254090443/e078155.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/668920075/Glargaard_et_al._2024_._Thoracentesis_to_alleviate_pleural_effusion_in_acute_heart_failure_-_study_protocol_for_the_multicentre_open-label_randomised_controlled_TAP-IT_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","co