","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180529245"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d5ea7d05-d5ba-4b23-82c6-ae0c033dbcfa"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"EOS - Environment &amp; Oil Spill Response. An analytic tool for environmental assessments to support oil spill response planning : Framework, principles, and proof-of-concept by an Arctic example","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-709395","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"We establish new results for estimation and inference in financial durations models, where events are observed over a given time span, such as a trading day, or a week. For the classical autoregressive conditional duration (ACD) models by Engle and Russell (1998), we show that the large sample behavior of likelihood estimators is highly sensitive to the tail behavior of the financial durations. In particular, even under stationarity, asymptotic normality breaks down for tail indices smaller than one or, equivalently, when the clustering behavior of the observed events is such that the unconditional distribution of the durations has no finite mean. Instead, we find that estimators are mixed Gaussian and have non-standard rates of convergence. The results are based on exploiting the crucial fact that for duration data the number of observations within any given time span is random. Our results apply to general econometric models where the number of observed events is random.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Cavaliere, Giuseppe","Mikosch, Thomas Valentin","Rahbek, Anders","Rasmussen, Frederik Vilandt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-721216"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Italy","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bologna","University of Exeter"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tail behavior of acd models and consequences for likelihood based estimation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.105613","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-721216","identifier":[{"id":"85178119759","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-98ffdcca-27a6-4045-807f-86f8ba3baef3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57315DA4E36476946D81B174F0E843F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/380353361/Tail_behavior_of_ACD_models.htm","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.105613","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"it","key":"university of bologna","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bologna","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of exeter","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Exeter","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Giuseppe","key":"cavalierepau","last":"Cavaliere","name":"Cavaliere, Giuseppe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Thomas Valentin","key":"mikoschpau","last":"Mikosch","locid":"c2ff63eb-87e4-4c5a-8256-7684a103112d","name":"Mikosch, Thomas Valentin","orcid":"0000-0003-3091-6661","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"rahbekpau","last":"Rahbek","locid":"b0f1764f-3474-4457-95a5-81c2e18ffbcc","name":"Rahbek, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2549-1913","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Frederik Vilandt","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"b85e98c3-6a8e-4276-a06e-ef4cfc6554f7","name":"Rasmussen, Frederik Vilandt","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jeconom.2023.105613","issn":["03044076","18726895"],"issn_org":["03044076"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Econometrics","paperid":"105613","status":"p","title":"Journal of Econometrics","volume":"238"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85178119759"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-98ffdcca-27a6-4045-807f-86f8ba3baef3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tail Behavior of ACD Models and Consequences for Likelihood-Based Estimation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-721216","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Introduction Lateral ankle sprain is the most common ankle injury and up to 40% of those who sustain a lateral ankle sprain will develop chronic ankle instability (CAI). The aim of this study was to explore the thoughts and expectations of CAI-patients concerning their condition and expectations of care in an orthopedic setting. Study Design Qualitative study Methods Nine semi-structured one-to-one interviews were conducted with CAI-patients who were referred to an orthopedic setting. Interviews were recorded, transcribed, and analyzed using systematic text condensation with an inductive goal free approach. Results Seven themes emerged. The themes were Injury history and symptoms (Lateral ankle sprain during sport, pain and instability), Information from health professional (conflicting information about management and prognosis), Management (mental and physical challenges), Expectation and hope (explanation of symptoms, prognosis and imaging to provide clarification of condition), Activity and participation (restriction in sport and daily life and feelings of uncertainty), Support (support from family/friends) and Identity (low ability to participate in sport and social life result in loss of identity). Conclusion The impact of CAI exceeds an experience of pain and instability. Patients experienced loss of identity, having to manage uncertainty regarding their diagnosis and prognosis and had hopes of being able to explain their condition.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Mohrsen, Anders","Sørensen, Thomas","Lund, Henrik","Rasmussen, Steven Zartov","Jensen, Asger Emil","Skov, Katrine Bruun","Rathleff, Michael Skovdal"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-726334"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Mohrsen, Anders"],"keyword":["Biopsychosocial","Chronic ankle instability","Musculoskeletal pain","Patient expectations","Psychological impact","Social impact"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"i feel like i have lost part of my identity a qualitative study exploring the impact of chronic ankle instability","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26603/001c.92908","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-726334","identifier":[{"id":"38439771","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10909303","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85186628199","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-db979e2b-641c-4232-a71d-263574379ed7"],"keyword":["Biopsychosocial","Chronic ankle instability","Loss of identity","Musculoskeletal pain","Patient expectations","Psychological impact","Social impact"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DE7C16CB652A36B5658F2C14F5FA5E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/676551206/92908-i-feel-like-i-have-lost-part-of-my-identity-a-qualitative-study-exploring-the-impact-of-chronic-ankle-instability.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.26603/001c.92908","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Health Science and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"mohrsenpau","last":"Mohrsen","locid":"d8948b45-1b02-41ed-80a4-745627ff409b","name":"Mohrsen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"78150348-fa6e-4898-8649-4847442f66c9","name":"Sørensen, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","locid":"e8d307fa-22a0-4c69-a1ab-0613ae50200a","name":"Lund, Henrik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steven Zartov","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"36bd1ee5-27d0-41a0-8741-1923be0c5c46","name":"Rasmussen, Steven Zartov","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Asger","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"eeea619d-6348-484b-bc1c-e4fa4eec75fe","name":"Jensen, Asger Emil","name_org":"Jensen, Asger","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrine Bruun","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Katrine Bruun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Michael Skovdal","key":"rathleffpau","last":"Rathleff","locid":"90c1260f-4cd4-497f-88ca-a98f412bbe7b","name":"Rathleff, Michael Skovdal","orcid":"0000-0003-1173-0335","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38439771"],"pub":{"doi":"10.26603/001c.92908","issn":["15586162","21592896"],"issn_org":["21592896"],"issue":"3","journal":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","pages":"316-325","publisher":"International Federation of Sports Physical Therapy (IFSPT)","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Sports Physical Therapy","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85186628199"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-db979e2b-641c-4232-a71d-263574379ed7"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"\"I Feel Like I Have Lost Part Of My Identity\" - A Qualitative Study Exploring The Impact Of Chronic Ankle Instability","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-726334","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This Generalized Systematic Review Registration Form is intended as a general-purpose registration form. The form is designed to be applicable to reviews across disciplines (i.e., psychology, economics, law, physics, or any other field) and across review types (i.e., scoping review, review of qualitative studies, meta-analysis, or any other type of review). That means that the reviewed records may include research reports as well as archive documents, case law, books, poems, etc. This form, therefore, is a fall-back for more specialized forms and can be used if no specialized form or registration platform is available. Below are some currently available specialized registration tools you may consider:","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Josephine Kvejborg","Christiansen, Lars Breum Skov","Larsen, Palle","Grandt, Vibeke","Holsgaard, Anders","Skovgaard, Thomas","Lexell, Jan","Larsen, Camilla Marie"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-740992"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring the quantitative and qualitative literature concerning frame running participation in all settings for people with physical disabilities a scoping review protocol","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.17605/OSF.IO/7AEJ2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-740992","ids":["ucl-757e61be-c29d-47f0-a275-017870e8bfe0"],"lang":"English","lev