ersen, Anders","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"117","publisher":"Elforsk","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","sdg":["17. Partnerships for the Goals","7. Affordable and Clean Energy","9. Industry, Innovation, and Infrastructure","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","centrica energy trading a/s","emd international a/s","greenport north p/s","nord energi net a/s","planenergi"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3dcb48a1-796a-40e7-bf86-9b90e1f73958"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"System Architecture and Scenario Development : For existing and future energy system at Port of Hirtshals","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-742724","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Metabolic syndrome encompasses amongst other conditions like obesity and type-2 diabetes and is associated with gut microbiome (GM) dysbiosis. Fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) has been explored to treat metabolic syndrome by restoring the GM; however, concerns on accidentally transferring pathogenic microbes remain. As a safer alternative, fecal virome transplantation (FVT, sterile-filtrated feces) has the advantage over FMT in that mainly bacteriophages are transferred. FVT from lean male donors have shown promise in alleviating the metabolic effects of high-fat diet in a preclinical mouse study. However, FVT still carries the risk of eukaryotic viral infections. To address this, recently developed methods are applied for removing or inactivating eukaryotic viruses in the viral component of FVT. Modified FVTs are compared with unmodified FVT and saline in a diet-induced obesity model on male C57BL/6 N mice. Contrasted with obese control, mice administered a modified FVT (nearly depleted for eukaryotic viruses) exhibits enhanced blood glucose clearance but not weight loss. The unmodified FVT improves liver pathology and reduces the proportions of immune cells in the adipose tissue with a non-uniform response. GM analysis suggests that bacteriophage-mediated GM modulation influences outcomes. Optimizing these approaches could lead to the development of safe bacteriophage-based therapies targeting metabolic syndrome through GM restoration.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Mao, Xiaotian","Larsen, Sabina Birgitte","Zachariassen, Line F.","Brunse, Anders","Adamberg, Signe","Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","Larsen, Frej","Adamberg, Kaarel","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Hansen, Axel Kornerup","Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-747582"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Estonia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Tallinn University of Technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"transfer of modified gut viromes improves symptoms associated with metabolic syndrome in obese male mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49152-w","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-747582","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11148109","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85195006914","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38830845","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-1c23bd00-19ed-4d14-9af9-e0fa49f300e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F013197CF325F5766CB43CE73B6BEB7B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-024-49152-w","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/394532699/Transfer_of_modified_gut_viromes_improves.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ee","key":"tallinn university of technology","loc":["Estonia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Tallinn University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaotian","key":"maoxiaotianpau","last":"Mao","locid":"b95866c7-bb3f-4bc8-be38-fc921bb75a01","name":"Mao, Xiaotian","orcid":"0000-0001-9425-683X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sabina Birgitte","key":"larsensabinabirgittepau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Sabina Birgitte","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Sidsel Fisker","key":"zachariassenlinefpau","last":"Zachariassen","locid":"cdafe75d-cfc9-4fca-adfe-20ae0c542b57","name":"Zachariassen, Line F.","name_org":"Zachariassen, Line Sidsel Fisker","orcid":"0000-0001-5425-9841","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"brunseanderspau","last":"Brunse","locid":"1413cafd-59f7-49d5-9c9b-00ff98f1df9c","name":"Brunse, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0199-3417","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Signe","key":"adambergsignepau","last":"Adamberg","name":"Adamberg, Signe","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josue Leonardo Castro","key":"castromejíajosuélpau","last":"Mejia","locid":"a37230a5-7baa-4222-a2f0-fb47090dd0ed","name":"Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","name_org":"Mejia, Josue Leonardo Castro","orcid":"0000-0002-1416-8205","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frej","key":"larsenfrejpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7779787c-d27c-40cb-afa1-a74630127b13","name":"Larsen, Frej","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kaarel","key":"adambergkaarelpau","last":"Adamberg","name":"Adamberg, Kaarel","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsendennissandrispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Kornerup","key":"hansenaxelkorneruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ecc439ea-5c9b-4e25-814a-3ee8960bc0d0","name":"Hansen, Axel Kornerup","orcid":"0000-0003-1575-2507","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Hartmann Friis","key":"hansencamillahartmannfriispau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d7f25dbd-3efc-483b-9805-8909e9597652","name":"Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","orcid":"0000-0002-1860-385X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Torben Sølbeck","key":"rasmussentorbensølbeckpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37b31216-f69f-4ff3-bc9c-ffd6b36fc003","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck","orcid":"0000-0002-9907-8953","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38830845"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-024-49152-w","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"4704","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195006914"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1c23bd00-19ed-4d14-9af9-e0fa49f300e0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Transfer of modified gut viromes improves symptoms associated with metabolic syndrome in obese male mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-747582","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Large-scale reduction of greenhouse gasses is necessary to abate the climate crisis, for which technological development will pave the way. Advancing research from academia to industry is crucial for technological progress. Pilot scale studies are the intermediate step from bench to industry. New challenges arise during technology upscaling, many of which have not been previously described in the literature. This article provides a guide of the do's and don'ts to researchers venturing into pilot work. The learnings and experiences gained by working with pilot-scale CO2 capture plant are presented and discussed. This work outlines the process challenges encountered during the commissioning and operation of a CO2 capture pilot using 30 wt% MEA and with a capacity to capture one tonne CO2/day from flue gas. Conducting pilot work in industrial facilities and outside controlled lab environments comes with unexpected problems. The issues faced during our pilot work are presented along with troubleshooting strategies and possible solutions. This work can aid researchers in identifying and rectifying operational challenges and conducting successful pilot campaigns.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Vinjarapu, Sai Hema Bhavya","Løge, Isaac Appelquist","Neerup, Randi","Larsen, Anders Hellerup","Rasmussen, Gorm","Jørsboe, Jens Kristian","Villadsen, Sebastian Nis Bay","Jensen, Søren","Karlsson, Jakob Lindkvist","Kappel, Jannik","Lassen, Henrik","Blinksbjerg, Peter","von Solms, Nicolas","Fosbøl, Philip Loldrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-758958"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Vinjarapu, Sai Hema Bhavya"],"keyword":["CO capture","Operation","Scale up"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Amager Ressourcecenter"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learnings from up scaling co sub 000000000002 sub capture challenges and experiences with pilot work","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ces.2024.120576","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-758958","identifier":[{"id":"85200969700","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1a3c6d0e-caa1-4c50-8ac8-caf14e95a4c1"],"keyword":["CO capture","Challenges and learnings","Operation","Pilot work","Scale-up"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0B7CC29EDD3E0EBC4920164AB3614C93"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ces.2024.120576","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/372042721/1-s2.0-S0009250924008765-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, CERE – Center for Energy Ressources Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Pentair Union Engineering A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":