urnal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-758958","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: High BMI is an established risk factor for asthma, but the underlying mechanisms remain unclear. Objective: To increase understanding of the BMI-asthma relationship by studying the association between genetic predisposition to higher body mass index (BMI) and asthma, infections, and other asthma-traits during childhood. Methods: Data was obtained from the two ongoing COPSAC mother-child cohorts. Polygenic risk score (PRS) for adult BMI were calculated for each child. Replication was done in the large-scale iPSYCH cohort using data on hospitalization for asthma and infections. Results: In the COPSAC cohorts (n=974), the adult BMI PRS was significantly associated with lower respiratory tract infections (LRTI) (IRR 1.20 95% CI 1.08–1.33, FDR=0.005) age 0-3 years and episodes of severe wheeze (IRR 1.30, 1.06–1.60, FDR=0.04) age 0-6 years. LRTI partly mediated the association between the adult BMI PRS and severe wheeze (proportion mediated: 0.59, 0.28–2.24, pACME 2E-16). In contrast, these associations were not mediated through the child’s current BMI and the PRS was not associated with an asthma diagnosis or reduced lung function up to age 18. The associations were replicated in iPSYCH (n=114,283), where the adult BMI PRS significantly increased the risk of hospitalizations for LRTI and wheeze or asthma during childhood to age 18 years. Conclusion: Children with genetic predisposition to higher BMI had increased risk of LRTI and severe wheeze, independent of the child’s current BMI. These results shed further light on the complex relationship between BMI and asthma.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Jensen, Signe Kjeldgaard","Pedersen, Casper Emil Tingskov","Fischer-Rasmussen, Kasper","Melgaard, Mathias Elsner","Brustad, Nicklas","Kyvsgaard, Julie Nyholm","Vahman, Nilo","Schoos, Ann Marie Malby","Stokholm, Jakob","Chawes, Bo","Eliasen, Anders","Bønnelykke, Klaus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760248"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Allergic rhinitis","Asthma","Atopic dermatitis","Atopic disease","BMI","Infections","Pneumonia","Polygenic risk score","Risk factor"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genetic predisposition to high bmi increases risk of early life respiratory infections and episodes of severe wheeze and asthma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-760248","identifier":[{"id":"85203473865","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38811044","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ad602c0a-8d78-4ecb-890d-415e2f71bebe"],"keyword":["Allergic rhinitis","Asthma","Atopic dermatitis","Atopic disease","BMI","BMI risk score","Infections","Persistent wheeze","Pneumonia","Polygenic risk score","Risk factor","Severe wheeze"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4521426950052AA82679F51BC867C0FD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Næstved, Slagelse and Ringsted"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"harvard university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Harvard University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Signe Kjeldgaard","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Signe Kjeldgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casper Emil Tingskov","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Casper Emil Tingskov","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"fischerrasmussenpau","last":"Fischer-Rasmussen","name":"Fischer-Rasmussen, Kasper","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mathias Elsner","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","name":"Melgaard, Mathias Elsner","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nicklas","key":"brustadpau","last":"Brustad","name":"Brustad, Nicklas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Julie Nyholm","key":"kyvsgaardpau","last":"Kyvsgaard","name":"Kyvsgaard, Julie Nyholm","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nilo","key":"vahmanpau","last":"Vahman","name":"Vahman, Nilo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Ann Marie Malby","key":"schoospau","last":"Schoos","locid":"bef73e0e-124e-4511-8642-26c781bd85c3","name":"Schoos, Ann Marie Malby","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Jakob","key":"stokholmpau","last":"Stokholm","locid":"a8a4f99a-ff12-4e00-9a1f-dde487d477b4","name":"Stokholm, Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-4989-9769","rank":9,"role