nal of Clinical Nutrition","title_org":"AMERICAN JOURNAL OF CLINICAL NUTRITION","volume":"119"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85182884241"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3345464b-ffb9-4a21-8001-7597d2c76f5d","ku-cb015b60-4c32-4170-b369-176268e405cb","sdu-6d41a1af-616a-42c4-8960-7de6d8176d95"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"High-dose vitamin D3 supplementation in pregnancy and risk of neurodevelopmental disorders in the children at age 10 : A randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.50-725020","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background This Danish cohort study aims to (1) compare patterns of care (POC) and survival of patients with multifocal glioblastoma (mGBM) to those with unifocal glioblastoma (uGBM), and (2) explore the association of patient-related factors with treatment assignment and prognosis, respectively, in the subgroup of mGBM patients. Methods Data on all adults with newly diagnosed, pathology-confirmed GBM between 2015 and 2019 were extracted from the Danish Neuro-Oncology Registry. To compare POC and survival of mGBM to uGBM, we applied multivariable logistic and Cox regression analysis, respectively. To analyze the association of patient-related factors with treatment assignment and prognosis, we established multivariable logistic and Cox regression models, respectively. Results In this cohort of 1343 patients, 231 had mGBM. Of those, 42% underwent tumor resection and 41% were assigned to long-course chemoradiotherapy. Compared to uGBM, mGBM patients less often underwent a partial (odds ratio [OR] 0.4, 95% confidence interval [CI] 0.2–0.6), near-total (OR 0.1, 95% CI 0.07–0.2), and complete resection (OR 0.1, 95% CI 0.07–0.2) versus biopsy. mGBM patients were furthermore less often assigned to long-course chemoradiotherapy (OR 0.6, 95% CI 0.4–0.97). Median overall survival was 7.0 (95% CI 5.7–8.3) months for mGBM patients, and multifocality was an independent poor prognostic factor for survival (hazard ratio 1.3, 95% CI 1.1–1.5). In mGBM patients, initial performance, O[6]-methylguanine-DNA methyltransferase promotor methylation status, and extent of resection were significantly associated with survival. Conclusions Patients with mGBM were treated with an overall less intensive approach. Multifocality was a poor prognostic factor for survival with a moderate effect. Prognostic factors for patients with mGBM were identified.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Trip, Anouk Kirsten","Dahlrot, Rikke Hedegaard","Haslund, Charlotte Aaquist","Muhic, Aida","Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","Laursen, Rene Johannes","Poulsen, Frantz Rom","Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","Lukacova, Slávka"],"cuid":["S04-098.94-751647"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Trip, Anouk Kirsten"],"keyword":["Glioblastoma","Patterns of care","Survival","crossing midline","multifocal"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"patterns of care and survival in patients with multifocal glioblastoma a danish cohort study","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85198722654","version":"Other Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center\\u2014Brain Tumor Center/Danish Cancer Society (R295-A16770) and Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center (2021-08). The authors would like to acknowledge the Danish Clinical Quality Program\\u2014National Clinical Registries, especially Henriette Engberg, for the contributions regarding the data, and Erik Thorlund Parner, Department of Public Health\\u2014Department of Biostatistics, Aarhus University, for the support regarding the statistical analyses. This work was supported by Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center\\u2014Brain Tumor Center/Danish Cancer Society (R295-A16770) and Danish Comprehensive Cancer Center (2021-08). Acknowledgments"],"id":"S04-098.94-751647","identifier":[{"id":"39006522","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11241377","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85198722654","type":"scopus"}],"i