","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Aida","key":"muhicpau","last":"Muhic","name":"Muhic, Aida","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Rosendal","key":"korshoejpau","last":"Korshoej","locid":"09d94078-676a-42ee-91c2-eb8ba8df356b","name":"Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","orcid":"0000-0003-4285-8171","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"René Johannes","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"0ab2e1c6-3018-44ee-b207-a30494b52f5b","name":"Laursen, Rene Johannes","name_org":"Laursen, René Johannes","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Frantz Rom","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"b50645f6-f0c4-4356-9f63-d44290b0dfd9","name":"Poulsen, Frantz Rom","orcid":"0000-0001-5715-6901","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","first":"Jane","key":"skjøthrasmussenpau","last":"Skjøth-Rasmussen","locid":"549d7d96-8a0c-4f6e-8a8e-2f9697a2aedc","name":"Skjøth-Rasmussen, Jane","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Slávka","key":"lukacovapau","last":"Lukacova","locid":"81d53ee1-129b-4fb9-9f5d-063576c06ad7","name":"Lukacova, Slávka","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39006522"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/nop/npae020","issn":["20542577","20542585"],"issn_org":["20542577"],"issue":"4","journal":"Neuro-Oncology Practice","pages":"421-431","paperid":"npae020","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Neuro-Oncology Practice","title_org":"Neuro-oncology practice","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198722654"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f7e1e7a6-a18d-45e5-9ffc-8d1429d34084","au-dff8e188-febc-42db-a050-e8d8dfbd2bec","ku-9a2074e7-93d1-4a55-a5bb-4fc04ecf3640","sdu-b90012cc-c523-4ba8-937e-1cfe9df6584f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Patterns of care and survival in patients with multifocal glioblastoma : A Danish cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-098.94-751647","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Objective: This is a secondary analysis of data from a previous study of anesthetized brain tumor patients receiving ephedrine or phenylephrine infusions. 18 patients with magnetic imaging verified tumor contrast enhancement were included. We hypothesized that vasopressors induce microcirculatory flow changes, characterized by increased capillary transit time heterogeneity (CTH) and decreased mean transit time (MTT), in brain regions exhibiting BBB leakage. Methods: This is a secondary analysis of data from a previous study of anesthetized brain tumor patients receiving ephedrine or phenylephrine infusions. 18 patients with magnetic imaging verified tumor contrast enhancement were included. Postvasopressor to prevasopressor ratios of CTH, MTT, relative transit time heterogeneity (RTH), cerebral blood flow (CBF), cerebral blood volume, and oxygen extraction fraction (OEF) were calculated in tumor, peritumoral, hippocampal, and contralateral grey matter regions. Comparisons were made between brain regions and vasopressors. Results: During phenylephrine infusion, ratios of CTH, RTH, and CBF were greater, and ratios of MTT and OEF were lower, in the tumor region with contrast leakage compared with corresponding contralateral grey matter ratios. During ephedrine infusion, ratios of CTH, MTT, RTH, CBF, and cerebral blood volume were higher in the tumor region with leakage compared with contralateral grey matter ratios. In addition, the ratio of CBF was higher in all regions, the ratio of RTH was lower in the leaking tumor region, and the ratio of OEF was lower in peritumoral, hippocampal, and grey matter regions with ephedrine compared with phenylephrine. Conclusions: Vasopressors can induce distinct microcirculatory flow alterations in regions with compromised brain tumor barrier or BBB. Ephedrine, a combined α and β-adrenergic agonist, appears to result in fewer flow alterations and less impact on tissue oxygenation compared with phenylephrine, a pure α-adrenergic agonist.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Mads","Koch, Klaus Ulrik","Espelund, Ulrick","Mohamad, Niwar","Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","Juul, Niels","Angleys, Hugo","Meng, Lingzhong","Østergaard, Leif","Mikkelsen, Irene Klærke"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-707470"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Mads"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Indiana University"],"keyword":["Blood Pressure","Blood brain barrier","Brain tumors","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Vasopressors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"blood brain barrier permeability may influence vasopressor effects in anesthetized patients with brain tumor an analysis of magnetic resonance imaging data","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85195035711","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-707470","identifier":[{"id":"85195035711","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38082495","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-4360e60b-1a91-4479-af3c-9ca482b618fd"],"keyword":["blood pressure","blood-brain barrier","brain tumors","cerebrovascular circulation","vasopressors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-763D197F643D9977C97FA9FB8E6B180F"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Anaesthesiology and Operation, Intensive care"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"indiana university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Indiana University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"10307123-564d-4db1-872d-d0a91168ce4e","name":"Rasmussen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-0416-6767","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klaus U.","key":"kochpau","last":"Koch","locid":"15824795-f9b9-4d8f-8bed-804eb3b1c28b","name":"Koch, Klaus Ulrik","name_org":"Koch, Klaus U.","orcid":"0000-0001-8784-094X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrick S.","key":"espelundpau","last":"Espelund","locid":"d6406dea-1bcb-447c-88ae-926841ba574d","name":"Espelund, Ulrick","name_org":"Espelund, Ulrick S.","orcid":"0000-0002-3659-650X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niwar","key":"mohamadpau","last":"Mohamad","locid":"8d178e66-652c-4987-86e2-b3f21119e0b2","name":"Mohamad, Niwar","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders R.","key":"korshøjpau","last":"Korshøj","locid":"09d94078-676a-42ee-91c2-eb8ba8df356b","name":"Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","name_org":"Korshøj, Anders R.","orcid":"0000-0003-4285-8171","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"88efc83f-3bc8-4166-89f8-b6df5729a5bc","name":"Juul, Niels","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hugo","key":"angleyspau","last":"Angleys","locid":"87ce7a33-0078-4b2e-9379-903e8601c5ec","name":"Angleys, Hugo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lingzhong","key":"mengpau","last":"Meng","name":"Meng, Lingzhong","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leif","key":"østergaardpau","last":"Østergaard","locid":"af45ec8c-f95a-4937-9e48-ffabe2b8933d","name":"Østergaard, Leif","orcid":"0000-0003-2930-6997","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Irene K.","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"449c9e73-c379-4921-993e-0ba5494ecc66","name":"Mikkelsen, Irene Klærke","name_org":"Mikkelsen, Irene K.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38082495"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ana.0000000000000948","issn":["08984921","15371921"],"issn_org":["08984921"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Neurosurgical Anesthesiology","pages":"357-362","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neurosurgical Anesthesiology","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85195035711"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-4360e60b-1a91-4479-af3c-9ca482b618fd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Blood-brain Barrier Permeability May Influence Vasopressor Effects in Anesthetized Patients with Brain Tumor : An Analysis of Magnetic Resonance Imaging Data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-707470","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background & aims: Cirrhosis is associated with insulin resistance and impaired glucose tolerance, which may be caused by impairments at different tissue levels (liver, skeletal muscle, and/or beta cell). Methods: Here, glucose kinetics at whole-body and skeletal muscle level in patients with cirrhosis (Child-Pugh A and B) were studied during parenteral nutrition using the isotope dilution technique and arteriovenous balance approach across the leg. As opposed to the euglycemic hyperinsulinemic clamp or glucose tolerance tests applied in previous studies, this approach provides a nutrient composition more similar to a normal meal while circumventing any possible portal-systemic shunting, impaired hepatic uptake and incretin effect. Results: We confirmed the presence of hepatic and peripheral insulin resistance in our patient population. Endogenous glucose production was less suppressed in response to parenteral nutrition. However, glucose uptake in skeletal muscle was increased. Conclusion: Our results suggests that in our study participants with cirrhosis, the hepatic and peripheral insulin resistance is compensated for by increased insulin secretion and thus, increased glucose uptake in muscle. Hereby, glucose homeostasis is maintained.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Trinh, Beckey","Rasmussen Rinnov, Anders","Iepsen, Ulrik Winning","Winding Munch, Gregers","Munch Winding, Kamilla","Lauridsen, Carsten","Gluud, Lise Lotte","van Hall, Gerrit","Ellingsgaard, Helga"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-730262"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cirrhosis","Glucose","Human","Skeletal muscle","Stable isotopes"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-UC-KP"]},"revi