{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: We aimed to investigate \"pain without loosening\" as an indication for knee arthroplasty revisions and to screen for other indications potentially hidden in this category to improve future registration and enhance data quality in the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register. METHODS: We included 104 patients undergoing revision knee arthroplasty for the indication \"pain without loosening\" from 1 January 2016 to 31 December 2018 at five Danish centres. Medical records, radiographs and computed tomographies were reviewed. RESULTS: In 103 of 104 cases, we confirmed \"pain without loosening\" as an indication for revision. We found hidden indications in 44 cases; malposition of components (n = 19), stiffness (n = 13), progression of arthrosis (n = 6), instability (n = 3), liner dislocation (n = 1), residual cement (n = 1) and aseptic loosening (n = 1). The Kellgren-Lawrence arthrosis grades prior to primary knee arthroplasty were 1-2 (31%) and 3-4 (69%). CONCLUSIONS: The indication \"pain without loosening\" covered patients revised due to pain, but other hidden indications were also present. Stiffness and malposition of components were hidden indications and these are not provided as indication options in the DKR and other registers. The relatively high frequency of arthrosis grade 1-2 prior to primary knee arthroplasty is concerning and may explain the occurrence of knee pain without any other pathology present. FUNDING: The Danish Rheumatism Association, the Region of Southern Denmark, the Research Fund of Region Zeeland and Region of Southern Denmark, and the University of Southern Denmark. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Not relevant.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","Schrøder, Henrik Morville","Troelsen, Anders","Andersen, Mikkel Rathsach","Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","Lindberg-Larsen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-733589"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Arndt, Kristine Bollerup"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pain without loosening revisions of knee arthroplasties in the danish knee arthroplasty register","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A04230242","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-733589","identifier":[{"id":"38314731","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85184402976","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-24933e7c-8c56-4836-8e5c-221b93f9f4f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-14E8006AA1B38F31130CF0D065C7122C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.61409/A04230242","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/255242146/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Næstved-Slagelse-Ringsted Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristine Bollerup","key":"arndtpau","last":"Arndt","locid":"a2513ef2-9214-48ee-b84f-bea6ef1717ac","name":"Arndt, Kristine Bollerup","orcid":"0000-0001-8258-7922","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Morville","key":"schrøderpau","last":"Schrøder","name":"Schrøder, Henrik Morville","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"troelsenpau","last":"Troelsen","name":"Troelsen, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Rathsach","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Mikkel Rathsach","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Enkebølle","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ada7d12e-e6cc-4568-b072-91b059d28c72","name":"Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"lindberglarsenpau","last":"Lindberg-Larsen","locid":"299608f9-db43-4744-984b-a7c428aca95b","name":"Lindberg-Larsen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4483-677X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38314731"],"pub":{"doi":"10.61409/a04230242","issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"2","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A04230242","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"71"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85184402976"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-24933e7c-8c56-4836-8e5c-221b93f9f4f8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"\"Pain without loosening\"-revisions of knee arthroplasties in the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-733589","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background   Neoantigens can serve as targets for T cell-mediated antitumor immunity via personalized neopeptide vaccines. Interim data from our clinical study NCT03715985 showed that the personalized peptide-based neoantigen vaccine EVX-01, formulated in the liposomal adjuvant, CAF09b, was safe and able to elicit EVX-01-specific T cell responses in patients with metastatic melanoma. Here, we present results from the dose-escalation part of the study, evaluating the feasibility, safety, efficacy, and immunogenicity of EVX-01 in addition to anti-PD-1 therapy.  Methods  Patients with metastatic melanoma on anti-PD-1 therapy were treated in three cohorts with increasing vaccine dosages (twofold and fourfold). Tumor-derived neoantigens were selected by the AI platform PIONEER and used in personalized therapeutic cancer peptide vaccines EVX-01. Vaccines were administered at 2-week intervals for a total of three intraperitoneal and three intramuscular injections. The study's primary endpoint was safety and tolerability. Additional endpoints were immunological responses, survival, and objective response rates.  Results  Compared with the base dose level previously reported, no new vaccine-related serious adverse events were observed during dose escalation of EVX-01 in combination with an anti-PD-1 agent given according to local guidelines. Two patients at the third dose level (fourfold dose) developed grade 3 toxicity, most likely related to pembrolizumab. Overall, 8 out of the 12 patients had objective clinical responses (6 partial response (PR) and 2 CR), with all 4 patients at the highest dose level having a CR (1 CR, 3 PR). EVX-01 induced peptide-specific CD4+ and/or CD8+T cell responses in all treated patients, with CD4+T cells as the dominating responses. The magnitude of immune responses measured by IFN-γELISpot assay correlated with individual peptide doses. A significant correlation between the PIONEER quality score and induced T cell immunogenicity was detected, while better CRs correlated with both the number of immunogenic EVX-01 peptides and the PIONEER quality score.  Conclusion  Immunization with EVX-01-CAF09b in addition to anti-PD-1 therapy was shown to be safe and well tolerated and elicit vaccine neoantigen-specific CD4+and CD8+ T cell responses at all dose levels. In addition, objective tumor responses were observed in 67% of patients. The results encourage further assessment of the antitumor efficacy of EVX-01 in combination with anti-PD-1 therapy.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Mørk, Sofie Kirial","Skadborg, Signe Koggersbøl","Albieri, Benedetta","Draghi, Arianna","Bol, Kalijn","Kadivar, Mohammad","Westergaard, Marie Christine Wulff","Stoltenborg Granhøj, Joachim","Borch, Annie","Petersen, Nadia Viborg","Thuesen, Nikolas","Rasmussen, Ida Svahn","Andreasen, Lars Vibe","Dohn, Rebecca Bach","Yde, Christina Westmose","Noergaard, Nis","Lorentzen, Torben","Soerensen, Anders Bundgaard","Kleine-Kohlbrecher, Daniela","Jespersen, Anders","Christensen, Dennis","Kringelum, Jens","Donia, Marco","Hadrup, Sine Reker","Marie Svane, Inge"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-746810"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mørk, Sofie Kirial"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Radboud University Nijmegen"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dose escalation study of a personalized peptide based neoantigen vaccine evx 000000000001 in patients with metastatic melanoma","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jitc-2024-008817","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-746810","identifier":[{"id":"85194128897","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC11116868","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"38782542","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-9853c773-d8c9-4fa8-83ef-1bc3fc470251"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4874747DC867267871B966CCCD05DEDC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/365514813/e008817.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/jitc-2024-008817","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Health Technology, Experimental & Translational Immunology, T-Cells and Cancer"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"radboud university nijmegen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Radboud University Nijmegen","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Evaxion Biotech A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Kirial","key":"mørkpau","last":"Mørk","name":"Mørk, Sofie Kirial","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Signe Koggersbøl","key":"skadborgpau","last":"Skadborg","locid":"db65f1dc-2b8f-4b56-8688-14b22bc9704b","name":"Skadborg, Signe Koggersbøl","orcid":"0000-0002-4042-8541","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Benedetta","key":"albieripau","last":"Albieri","name":"Albieri, Benedetta","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Arianna","key":"draghipau","last":"Draghi","name":"Draghi, Arianna","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalijn","key":"bolpau","last":"Bol","name":"Bol, Kalijn","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mohammad","key":"kadivarpau","last":"Kadivar","locid":"8712bc3c-4fd7-4b5a-a40a-75f3e4ec2b0e","name":"Kadivar, Mohammad","orcid":"0000-0003-1499-191X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Christine Wulff","key":"westergaardpau","last":"Westergaard","name":"Westergaard, Marie Christine Wulff","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"stoltenborggranhøjpau","last":"Stoltenborg Granhøj","name":"Stoltenborg Granhøj, Joachim","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Annie","key":"borchpau","last":"Borch","locid":"f4bf06f8-af03-4c37-ae51-da27fafa6d83","name":"Borch, Annie","orcid":"0000-0002-5423-756X"