Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Companies","Other Research","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","pharmakon as"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-1709ec21-7275-4441-9778-8814f5527eb9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pharmacists' empathy after a postgraduate course in narrative medicine : An observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-777051","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Inpatient rehabilitation improves health-related quality of life (HRQOL) for people with multiple sclerosis (MS). However, the obtained improvements decline once people return home. The challenge is to find ways to preserve the beneficial effects for the long term. We investigated whether monthly telecoaching after discharge would enhance the long-term carryover of improvements. METHODS: We conducted a 1-year exploratory study with 2 delivery methods: telephone coaching and web-based coaching. After discharge, the telephone group received monthly calls; the web-based group responded to monthly online coaching questions. Based on their rehabilitation goals, we put patients into a neuropsychological group or a physical group. In addition, we matched each patient with similar wait-list control patients and treatment patients from the main study. The primary outcome was HRQOL measured by the Functional Assessment in Multiple Sclerosis (FAMS). RESULTS: The neuropsychological group had long-term preservation of HRQOL with both delivery methods, with telephone coaching seeming to be superior. Mean differences in FAMS at the 12-month median follow-up for the neuropsychological group compared with the control wait-list control group were for the telephone group: + 15.4 (95% CI, 3.5-27.4; P =.011); for the web-based group: + 10.9 (95% CI, –3.3 to 25.2; P =.130); for the control treatment group: + 6.9 (95% CI, 0.6-13.3; P =.031). The physical group saw no beneficial effects from telecoaching. CONCLUSIONS: Following inpatient multidisciplinary rehabilitation, monthly telecoaching of individuals with MS with neuropsychological challenges enhanced the long-term carryover of HRQOL, with one-on-one telephone coaching showing more pronounced improvements than web-based automated coaching.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nørgaard, Michael","Boesen, Finn","Skjerbæk, Anders Guldhammer","Jensen, Ellen","Hansen, Jeanne","Rasmussen, Peter Vestergaard","Petersen, Thor","Trénel, Philipp"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-783554"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Nørgaard, Michael"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DTCI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DTCI","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"telecoaching of individuals with multiple sclerosis after inpatient multidisciplinary rehabilitation the danish ms hospitals rehabilitation study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7224/1537-2073.2023-038","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-783554","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11440362","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"39351583","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85207034156","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-aacbe541-97be-44f9-9d4d-f897206b9a1b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C34BBC9D19DC23745B2EA9095C17A64D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11440362/pdf/i1537-2073-26-266.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Kun læseadgang","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7224/1537-2073.2023-038","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["The Danish MS Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark R