{"abstract":"Introduktion: Artiklen sætter fokus på facilitatorers feedback på kreative skriveværksteder til mennesker medkroniske sygdomme i Danmark. Vi viser, hvordan oplæsning af deltagernes tekster og feedback fra facilitatorudspillede sig på fire skriveværksteder, samt diskuterer, hvordan feedback fik betydning for deltagerne. Metode:Artiklen er baseret på en antropologisk evaluering af et projekt om kreative skriveværksteder. Begrebet recognition– i betydningen genkendelse, erkendelse og anerkendelse – benyttes i analysen af det empiriske materiale.Resultater: Facilitators feedback på deltagertekster medvirkede til genkendelse og nye erkendelser hos deltagerneog en oplevelse af at blive anerkendt “som skribenter”. I få situationer, hvor deltagere ikke oplevede at blive “set oghørt”, førte feedback modsat til en oplevelse af manglende anerkendelse. Originalitet: Betydningen af facilitatorersfeedback for deltageres oplevelse af kreative skriveværksteder i sundhedsregi er hidtil ikke undersøgt. Resultaternedokumenterer, at facilitatorer er centrale aktører på kreative skriveværksteder, i forhold til om deltagerne oplevedeet virkningsfuldt skriveværksted.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Laursen, Sara Seerup","Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","Hansen, Helle Ploug"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-802305"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Laursen, Sara Seerup"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"facilitatorers feedback på kreative skriveværksteder til mennesker med kroniske sygdomme","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18261/njach.6.2.3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-802305","ids":["sdu-6fb208e2-08c3-4379-8771-37145a1aa3a6"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-477A099D552D2B9CFB0FB896003BC201"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.18261/njach.6.2.3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/284046073/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Research Unit of General Pratice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara Seerup","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"96243215-7e29-4653-bef7-bc421ab3e8e7","name":"Laursen, Sara Seerup","orcid":"0000-0003-2397-2139","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Ploug","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"aff3454d-836b-44db-9a85-391f83361116","name":"Hansen, Helle Ploug","orcid":"0000-0002-5075-8739","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.18261/njach.6.2.3","issn":["25357913"],"issn_org":["23357913"],"issue":"2","journal":"Nordic Journal of Arts, Culture and Health","publisher":"Idunn","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Arts, Culture and Health","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6fb208e2-08c3-4379-8771-37145a1aa3a6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Facilitatorers feedback på kreative skriveværksteder til mennesker med kroniske sygdomme","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-802305","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This new volume repositions narrative medicine and trauma studies in a global context with a particular focus on ethics. Trauma is a rapidly growing field of especially literary and cultural studies, and the ways in which trauma has asserted its relevance across disciplines, which intersect with narrative medicine, and how it has come to widen the scope of narrative research and medical practice constitute the principal concerns of this volume. This collection brings together contributions from established and emerging scholars coming from a wide range of academic fields within the faculty of humanities that include literary and media studies, psychology, philosophy, history, anthropology as well as medical education and health care studies. This crossing of disciplines is also represented by the collaboration between the two editors. Most of the authors in the volume use narrative medicine to refer to the methodology pioneered by Rita Charon and her colleagues at Columbia University, but in some chapters, the authors use it to refer to other methodologies and pedagogies utilizing that descriptor. Trauma is today understood both in the restricted sense in which it is used in the mental health field and in its more widespread, popular usage in literature. This collection aspires to prolong, deepen, and advance the field of narrative medicine in two important aspects: by bringing together both the cultural and the clinical side of trauma and by opening the investigation to a truly global horizon.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","Sodemann, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-090.62-793882"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Juhl Rasmussen, Anders"],"keyword":["Antropologi","Etik","Faculty of Humanities","Kultur","Litteratur","Medicin","Narrativ medicin","Traumer"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"introduction","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://vernonpress.com/book/1925","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.62-793882","ids":["ku-b9a681f7-5049-4c08-895b-348b7ffc57b2","sdu-05c4f072-e80c-45f9-bcbd-2efed602016d"],"keyword":["Faculty of Humanities","antropologi","etik","kultur","litteratur","medicin","narrativ medicin","traumer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-C5C2FA481A8C19655958B0DECE6CC613"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e1188ff-4cc9-42e2-86b3-59515e62f1af","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannpau","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"juhlrasmussenpedh","last":"Juhl Rasmussen","name":"Juhl Rasmussen, Anders","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"sodemannpedh","last":"Sodemann","name":"Sodemann, Morten","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781648898457"],"place":"Wilmington, DE","publisher":"Vernon Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Trauma and Ethics","title":"Narrative Medicine"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b9a681f7-5049-4c08-895b-348b7ffc57b2","sdu-05c4f072-e80c-45f9-bcbd-2efed602016d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Introduction","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-090.62-793882","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Inflammatory bowel diseases (IBDs) are associated with high healthcare utilization. This systematic review aimed to summarize what is known about the impact of sex, income, and education on the likelihood of bowel surgery, hospitalization, and use of corticosteroids and biologics among patients with IBD. Methods: We used EMBASE, MEDLINE, CINAHL, and Web of Science to perform a systematic literature search. Pooled hazard ratios (HRs) and odds ratios (ORs) with 95% confidence intervals (CIs) were calculated using random effects meta-analysis for the impact of sex on the likelihood of surgery and hospitalization. In addition, we performed subgroup analyses of the effect of IBD type (Crohn’s disease or ulcerative colitis) and age. Finally, meta-regression was undertaken for the year of publication. Results: In total, 67 studies were included, of which 23 studies were eligible for meta-analysis. In the main meta-analysis, male sex was associated with an increased likelihood of bowel surgery (HR 1.42 (95% CI 1.13;1.78), which was consistent with the subgroup analysis for UC only (HR 1.78, 95% CI 1.16; 2.72). Sex did not impact the likelihood of hospitalization (OR 1.05 (95% CI 0.86;1.30), although the subgroup analysis revealed an increased likelihood of hospitalization in CD patients (OR 1.42, 95% CI 1.28;1.58). In 9 of 10 studies, no significant sex-based differences in the use of biologics were reported, although in 6 of 6 studies, female patients had lower adherence to biologics. In 11 of 13 studies, no significant sex-based difference in the use of corticosteroids was reported. The evidence of the impact of income and education on healthcare utilization was sparse and pointed in different directions. The substantial heterogeneity between studies was explained, in part, by differences in IBD type and age. Conclusions: The results of this systematic review indicate that male patients with IBD are significantly more likely to have surgery than female patients with IBD but are not, overall, more likely to be hospitalized, whereas female patients appear to have statistically significantly lower adherence to biologics compared to male patients. Thus, clinicians should not underestimate the impact of sex on healthcare utilization. Evidence for income- and education-based differences remains sparse. Systematic review registration: PROSPERO CRD42022315788.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Nathalie Fogh","Moos, Caroline","Gregersen, Laura","Hikmat, Zainab","Andersen, Vibeke","Green, Anders","Jess, Tine","Madsen, Gunvor Iben","Pedersen, Andreas Kristian","Petersen, Sofie Ronja","Kjeldsen, Lene Juel"],"cuid":["S02-094.74-751555"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Nathalie Fogh"],"keyword":["Adrenal Cortex Hormones therapeutic use","Colitis Ulcerative surgery","Female","Hospitalization","Hospitalization statistics numerical data","Humans","Inflammatory Bowel Diseases drug therapy","Inflammatory bowel disease","Male","Sex Factors","Sex differences","Social Class","Socioeconomic differences","Surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of sex and socioeconomic status on the likelihood of surgery hospitalization and use of medications in inflammatory bowel disease a systematic review and meta analysis","src":["aau","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13643-024-02584-3","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Open access funding provided by University of Southern Denmark Nathalie Fogh Rasmussen was financially supported by Hospital S\\u00F8nderjylland, the University Hospital of Southern Denmark, the Research Unit of Molecular Diagnostic and Clinical Research, and the study was further supported by the Danish Beckett-Fonden (grant no. 20\\u20132-6128) and the Danish Knud and Edith Eriksens Mindefond. TJ is supported by the Danish National Research Foundation (DNRF148)."],"id":"S02-094.74-751555","identifier":[{"id":"38915086","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11194997","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85196730632","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-53db29ce-7eae-48dc-aa4b-820efe942145","sdu-3fd37f86-d82b-4783-bc4c-b4b5ff15e7b1"],"keyword":["Adrenal Cortex Hormones/therapeutic use","Colitis, Ulcerative/surgery","Female","Hospitalization","Hospitalization/statistics & numerical data","Humans","Inflammatory Bowel Diseases/drug therapy","Inflammatory bowel disease","Male","Sex Factors","Sex differences","Social Class","Socioeconomic differences","Surgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A2CFC57DFC139A3F2626847E0B58F0B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13643-024-02584-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/265940221/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/734681143/Rasmussen_et_al._2024_._Impact_of_sex_and_socioeconomic_status_on_the_likelihood_of_surgery_hospitalization_and_use_of_medications_in_inflammatory_bowel_disease_-_a_systematic_review_and_meta-analysis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Hospital Pharmacy (Aabenraa)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Regional Hospital Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Centers"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nathalie Fogh","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a587221d-2713-4f5b-82ea-1f4d3f163006","name":"Rasmussen, Nathalie Fogh","orcid":"0000-0003-3315-1094","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Caroline","key":"moospau","last":"Moos","locid":"9e113b4f-f3b4-47b0-8aaa-ca75820a597e","name":"Moos, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0003-4997-4319","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura Helene Keiding","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"162d4017-6ad5-4c6c-9193-eb46b17b48b9","name":"Gregersen, Laura","name_org":"Gregersen, Laura Helene Keiding","orcid":"0000-0003-4233-7026","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Zainab","key":"hikmatpau","last":"Hikmat","locid":"aa97f785-de79-46b1-be3e-45a0ac91ef01","name":"Hikmat, Zainab","orcid":"0000-0002-7376-0532","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vibeke","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"13a7e111-7511-412b-9e1e-4c3bc8982e21","name":"Andersen, Vibeke","orcid":"0000-0002-0127-2863","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"greenpau","last":"Green","locid":"efdbf426-9cae-4f5c-8c23-56c94fc85853","name":"Green, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5059-3655","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tine","key":"jesspau","last":"Jess","locid":"ab65eac5-33fc-4361-882d-e595188169d3","name":"Jess, Tine","orcid":"0000-0002-4391-7332","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gunvor Iben","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"d2769587-82f0-42f5-8ae7-01f1b805c4de","name":"Madsen, Gunvor Iben","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas Kristian","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"2aa75881-8923-493b-8ea0-9528b7334796","name":"Pedersen, Andreas Kristian","orcid":"0000-0001-5406-1675","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Ronja","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"aa8496e0-896f-439c-9cf5-164e3cf3d609","name":"Petersen, Sofie Ronja","orcid":"0000-0001-6177-8930","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lene Juel","key":"kjeldsenpau","last":"Kjeldsen","locid":"b3d44e3d-440c-41f1-b52d-838b0338bf55","name":"Kjeldsen, Lene Juel","orcid":"0009-0008-2559-9319","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38915086"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13643-024-02584-3","issn":["20464053"],"issue":"1","journal":"Systematic Reviews","paperid":"164","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Systematic Reviews","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196730632"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-53db29ce-7eae-48dc-aa4b-820efe942145","sdu-3fd37f86-d82b-4783-bc4c-b4b5ff15e7b1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Impact of sex and socioeconomic status on the likelihood of surgery, hospitalization, and use of medications in inflammatory bowel disease : a systematic review and meta-analysis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-094.74-751555","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Contaminants, such as heavy metals (HMs), accumulate in the Arctic environment and the food web. The diet of the Indigenous Peoples of North Greenland includes locally sourced foods that are central to their nutritional, cultural, and societal health but these foods also contain high concentrations of heavy metals. While bacteria play an essential role in the metabolism of xenobiotics, there are limited studies on the impact of heavy metals on the human gut microbiome, and it is so far unknown if and how Arctic environmental contaminants impact the gut microbes of humans living in and off the Arctic environment. Using a multiomics approach including amplicon, metagenome, and metatranscriptome sequencing, we identified and assembled a near-complete (NC) genome of a mercury-resistant bacterial strain from the human gut microbiome, which expressed genes known to reduce mercury toxicity. At the overall ecological level studied through α- and β-diversity, there was no significant effect of heavy metals on the gut microbiota. Through the assembly of a high number of NC metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs) of human gut microbes, we observed an almost complete overlap between heavy metal-resistant strains and antibiotic-resistant strains in which resistance genes were all located on the same genetic elements.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Hauptmann, Aviaja Lyberth","Johansen, Joachim","Stæger, Frederik Filip","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","Mulvad, Gert","Hanghøj, Kristian","Rasmussen, Simon","Hansen, Torben","Albrechtsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-785361"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Nordic"],"corresponding_author":["Hauptmann, Aviaja Lyberth"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Greenland"],"keyword":["Antimicrobial resistance","Arctic","Co resistance","Contaminants","Heavy metal resistance","Mer operon"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gut heavy metal and antibiotic resistome of humans living in the high arctic","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2024.1493803","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-785361","identifier":[{"id":"85208810719","type":"scopus"},{"id":"39539714","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC11557323","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-dadf6a6e-db80-42ed-8f51-e73239a706e9","ku-13dd2e7e-9f82-4a4d-bb86-03b107c1e312"],"keyword":["Arctic","antimicrobial resistance","co-resistance","contaminants","heavy metal resistance","mer-operon"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8BDD7522E6804AFAF8CE6C037478562E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/412381640/fmicb_15_1493803.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/386899086/fmicb-15-1493803.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3389/fmicb.2024.1493803","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Hologenomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"university of greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"University of Greenland","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Aviaja Lyberth","key":"hauptmannpau","last":"Hauptmann","locid":"d001572a-1c22-4e5e-8f8a-f8fe0dbd50ee","name":"Hauptmann, Aviaja Lyberth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","country":"dk","first":"Joachim","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"b8299ddc-b75d-46c7-8a6c-20ca2c9f36c0","name":"Johansen, Joachim","orcid":"0000-0001-7052-1870","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik Filip","key":"stægerpau","last":"Stæger","locid":"7b942180-8ba0-441b-8289-c4d2359e4f8e","name":"Stæger, Frederik Filip","orcid":"0000-0002-2295-8637","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Gert","key":"mulvadpau","last":"Mulvad","name":"Mulvad, Gert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"hanghøjpau","last":"Hanghøj","locid":"a17e9d55-e472-4c3b-b988-a1e924c30337","name":"Hanghøj, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-1941-5495","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"274c7fdf-d0c2-4c4e-8739-9b5e74d5005f","name":"Rasmussen, Simon","orcid":"0000-0001-6323-9041","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"6b6bfff1-8b14-468b-af77-e71b375018e0","name":"Hansen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0001-8748-3831","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"4b040c73-6b49-4e97-be60-5e34608e0615","name":"Albrechtsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-031X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39539714"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3389/fmicb.2024.1493803","issn":["1664302X"],"journal":"Frontiers in Microbiology","paperid":"1493803","publisher":"Frontiers Media SA","publisher_org":"Frontiers Media S.A.","status":"p","title":"Frontiers in Microbiology","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85208810719"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-dadf6a6e-db80-42ed-8f51-e73239a706e9","ku-13dd2e7e-9f82-4a4d-bb86-03b107c1e312"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Gut heavy metal and antibiotic resistome of humans living in the high Arctic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-785361","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Treatment with opioids is a mainstay in perioperative pain management. While the leading treatment paradigm has been procedure-specific pain management, efforts regarding personalized pain treatment are increasing. The OPI•AID project aims to develop personalized algorithms for perioperative pain management, taking demographic, surgical, and anaesthesiologic factors into account. We will undertake five parallel reviews to illuminate current evidence on different aspects of individual responses to perioperative opioid treatment. METHODS: Inclusion of adult populations in English-written studies. Review-specific searches are developed for the following databases: CENTRAL, MEDLINE, Embase, clinicaltrials.gov, and clinicaltrial.eu. Two authors will independently screen citations, extract data, and assess the risks of bias in each review (QUIPS, PROBAST and RoB2, as relevant). CONCLUSION: These reviews will evaluate various aspects of perioperative opioid treatment, including individualized treatment strategies, selection of specific opioids, and individual patient responses. These will guide future development of a personalized perioperative opioid treatment algorithm (OPI•AID) that will be validated and tested clinically against standard of care.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Karlsen, Anders Peder Højer","Sunde, Pernille Bjersand","Olsen, Markus Harboe","Laigaard, Jens","Folkersen, Caroline","Tran, Trang Xuan Minh","Rasmussen, Ida Houtved","Kjartansdóttir, Selma","Saito, Atena","Andersen, Michael Asger","Maagaard, Mathias","Papadomanolakis-Pakis, Nicholas","Dalhoff, Kim","Nikolajsen, Lone","Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","Meyhoff, Christian Sylvest","Jakobsen, Janus Christian","Mathiesen, Ole"],"cuid":["S03-087.30-767347"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, South"],"corresponding_author":["Karlsen, Anders Peder Højer"],"country":["Brazil"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pontifical Catholic University of Campinas","Pontificia Universidade Catolica de Campinas","Pontifícia Universidade Católica de Campinas"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Analgesia methods","Analgesics Opioid therapeutic use","Humans","Minimal important difference","Opioids","Pain Management","Pain Management methods","Pain Postoperative drug therapy","Perioperative Care","Perioperative Care methods","Personalized medicine","Pharmacogenetics","Postoperative pain","Precision Medicine methods","Review","Systematic Reviews as Topic"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"opioids and personalized analgesia in the perioperative setting a protocol for five systematic reviews","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14508","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-087.30-767347","identifier":[{"id":"39107975","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85200510778","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-31bdb8ea-4d0d-43f0-a684-61c94bd838a3","ku-79f9bd5e-d6b6-4703-8563-d20644124c12","sdu-d6af4088-270d-4d49-9bc4-ab04c8edfe2f"],"keyword":["Algorithms","Analgesia/methods","Analgesics, Opioid/therapeutic use","Humans","Pain Management/methods","Pain, Postoperative/drug therapy","Perioperative Care/methods","Precision Medicine/methods","Systematic Reviews as Topic","minimal important difference","opioids","pain management","perioperative care","personalized medicine","pharmacogenetics","postoperative pain","review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Globa