,"first":"Troels Haxholdt","key":"lunnpau","last":"Lunn","name":"Lunn, Troels Haxholdt","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8","first":"Christian Sylvest","key":"meyhoffpau","last":"Meyhoff","locid":"4d112eed-e878-476d-8f1f-df10d39439b2","name":"Meyhoff, Christian S.","name_org":"Meyhoff, Christian Sylvest","orcid":"0000-0002-4885-4609","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","corresponding":null,"first":"Janus Christian","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"06691aa2-020b-4869-a6d9-56ac223008cc","name":"Jakobsen, Janus Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-3642-2120","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 8","first":"Ole","key":"mathiesenpau","last":"Mathiesen","locid":"6cff39d5-4c65-460c-9bff-e8253a690086","name":"Mathiesen, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-4544-0619","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["39107975"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14508","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"10","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"1573-1580","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200510778"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-31bdb8ea-4d0d-43f0-a684-61c94bd838a3","ku-79f9bd5e-d6b6-4703-8563-d20644124c12","sdu-d6af4088-270d-4d49-9bc4-ab04c8edfe2f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Opioids and personalized analgesia in the perioperative setting : A protocol for five systematic reviews","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-087.30-767347","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"IMPORTANCE: Supplemental oxygen is ubiquitously used in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia, but a lower dose may be beneficial. OBJECTIVE: To assess the effects of targeting a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg vs 90 mm Hg in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia in the intensive care unit (ICU). DESIGN, SETTING, AND PARTICIPANTS: Multicenter randomized clinical trial including 726 adults with COVID-19 receiving at least 10 L/min of oxygen or mechanical ventilation in 11 ICUs in Europe from August 2020 to March 2023. The trial was prematurely stopped prior to outcome assessment due to slow enrollment. End of 90-day follow-up was June 1, 2023. INTERVENTIONS: Patients were randomized 1:1 to a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg (lower oxygenation group; n = 365) or 90 mm Hg (higher oxygenation group; n = 361) for up to 90 days in the ICU. MAIN OUTCOMES AND MEASURES: The primary outcome was the number of days alive without life support (mechanical ventilation, circulatory support, or kidney replacement therapy) at 90 days. Secondary outcomes included mortality, proportion of patients with serious adverse events, and number of days alive and out of hospital, all at 90 days. RESULTS: Of 726 randomized patients, primary outcome data were available for 697 (351 in the lower oxygenation group and 346 in the higher oxygenation group). Median age was 66 years, and 495 patients (68%) were male. At 90 days, the median number of days alive without life support was 80.0 days (IQR, 9.0-89.0 days) in the lower oxygenation group and 72.0 days (IQR, 2.0-88.0 days) in the higher oxygenation group (P = .009 by van Elteren test; supplemental bootstrapped adjusted mean difference, 5.8 days [95% CI, 0.2-11.5 days]; P = .04). Mortality at 90 days was 30.2% in the lower oxygenation group and 34.7% in the higher oxygenation group (risk ratio, 0.86 [98.6% CI, 0.66-1.13]; P = .18). There were no statistically significant differences in proportion of patients with serious adverse events or in number of days alive and out of hospital. CONCLUSION AND RELEVANCE: In adult ICU patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxemia, targeting a Pao2 of 60 mm Hg resulted in more days alive without life support in 90 days than targeting a Pao2 of 90 mm Hg. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT04425031.","author_count":53,"contributors":["Nielsen, Frederik M","Klitgaard, Thomas L","Siegemund, Martin","Laake, Jon H","Thormar, Katrin M","Cole, Jade M","Aagaard, Søren R","Bunzel, Anne-Marie G","Vestergaard, Stine R","Langhoff, Peter K","Pedersen, Caroline H","Hejlesen, Josefine Ø","Abdelhamid, Salim","Dietz, Anna","Gebhard, Caroline E","Zellweger, Nuria","Hollinger, Alexa","Poulsen, Lone M","Weihe, Sarah","Andersen-Ranberg, Nina C","Pedersen, Ulf G","Mathiesen, Ole","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Brix, Helene","Thomsen, Jonas J","Petersen, Christina H","Bestle, Morten H","Wichmann, Sine","Lund, Martin S","Mortensen, Karoline M","Brand, Björn A","Haase, Nicolai","Iversen, Susanne A","Marcussen, Klaus V","Brøchner, Anne C","Borup, Morten","Grøfte, Thorbjørn","Hildebrandt, Thomas","Kjær, Maj-Brit N","Engstrøm, Janus","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders","Schjørring, Olav L","Rasmussen, Bodil S"],"cuid":["S03-099.97-735023"],"filters":{"added":"2024-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["HOT-COVID Trial Group"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Bodil S.","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"country":["Iceland","Norway","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Landspitali University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","The National University Hospital of Iceland","University Hospital Basel","University Hospital Wales","University Hospital of Basel","University Hospital of Wales"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","COVID 19 therapy","Female","Humans","Hypoxia etiology","Male","Oxygen","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy methods","Respiration Artificial"],"level":"sci