"],"name":"NORCE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Bjørn Arild","key":"hattelandpau","last":"Hatteland","name":"Hatteland, Bjørn Arild","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jo S.","key":"hermansenpau","last":"Hermansen","name":"Hermansen, Jo S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lawrence","key":"kirkendallpau","last":"Kirkendall","name":"Kirkendall, Lawrence","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"24ea7809-dde1-44f9-ac17-63b508b998f7","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-1529-6548","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristin O.","key":"seljetunpau","last":"Seljetun","name":"Seljetun, Kristin O.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus","key":"sydenhampau","last":"Sydenham","name":"Sydenham, Markus","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Henning","key":"sørumpau","last":"Sørum","name":"Sørum, Henning","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul Ragnar","key":"bergpau","last":"Berg","name":"Berg, Paul Ragnar","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 8","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"brynpau","last":"Bryn","name":"Bryn, Anders","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjetil","key":"hindarpau","last":"Hindar","name":"Hindar, Kjetil","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Kyrre","key":"kausrudpau","last":"Kausrud","name":"Kausrud, Kyrre","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5 10","corresponding":null,"first":"Erlend B.","key":"nilsenpau","last":"Nilsen","name":"Nilsen, Erlend B.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Brett K.","key":"sandercockpau","last":"Sandercock","name":"Sandercock, Brett K.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Eva","key":"thorstadpau","last":"Thorstad","name":"Thorstad, Eva","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3 11","corresponding":null,"first":"Gaute","key":"vellepau","last":"Velle","name":"Velle, Gaute","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Tor Atle","key":"mopau","last":"Mo","name":"Mo, Tor Atle","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788282594400"],"issn":["25354019"],"issue":"4","pages":"135","publisher":"Vitenskapskomiteen for mat og miljø (VKM)","repno":"VKM Report , No. 4","series":"VKM Report","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d286c79d-44e5-459c-b14a-6a43edff9cca"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Risks posed by managed honey bees (Apis mellifera) to wild pollinators in Norway. Scientific Opinion of the Panel on Biodiversity of the Norwegian Scientific Committee for Food and Environment","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-745432","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Due to increasing older populations worldwide, injuries, disabilities and deaths caused by falls among the elderly represent a growing human and societal problem. We aimed to improve health among men of at least 70 years of age with low-normal to low testosterone and mobility problems by using testosterone undecanoate (TU) injections, progressive strength training, and oral supplements of vitamin D, calcium and protein. Methods: This was a single-centre, randomized, placebo-controlled, double-blind trial with 148 older men with a median age of 77 (73–81) years, testosterone levels at median 8 (5–9) nmol/L (full range from 1.1 to 12.9 nmol/L) and mobility problems, recruited at University Hospital of Copenhagen, Herlev Hospital, Denmark. Participants were randomized into four arms for 20 weeks: (1) TU therapy (n = 37); (2) progressive resistance training with supplements of calcium, vitamin D and protein (n = 36); (3) both interventions combined (n = 36); or (4) no intervention (n = 39). The main outcome measure was the 30-s chair stand test, due to test performance correlating with the risk of serious fall injuries and lower extremity muscle strength. Outcome measurements were performed at baseline and after 20 weeks. Results: After the intervention, the combination group receiving progressive resistance training, TU and supplements achieved a median score of 13 (11–15) compared to the control group at 10 (0–14) in the 30-s chair stand test (P = 0.003). This median improvement of 3.0 was clinically important. Compared to the control group, participants in the combination group also increased quality of life (P < 0.05) and reduced both tiredness (P < 0.05) and leg fat (P < 0.05) and had higher variability in the RR interval (P < 0.01). The group receiving TU reduced gynoid and leg fat compared to the control group (both P < 0.05). Blood tests improved for several variables, especially in the combination group. There was no statistically significant increase in adverse effects from either the supplements or training. Conclusions: In men ≥70 years old with low-normal to low testosterone and mobility problems, supplements of testosterone, calcium, vitamin D and protein combined with progressive resistance training improved 30-s chair stand test performance, muscle strength and quality of life. Both tiredness and leg fat were reduced, and RR interval variability was increased. Significant adverse effects were not observed.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Midttun, Mette","Overgaard, Karsten","Zerahn, Bo","Pedersen, Maria","Rashid, Anahita","Østergren, Peter Busch","Paulin, Tine Kolenda","Pødenphanth, Thea Winther","Karlsson, Linda Katharina","Rosendahl, Eva","Ragle, Anne-Mette","Vinther, Anders","Rasmussen, Rune Skovgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-754811"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Elderly","Falls","Physical exercise","Testosterone therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"beneficial effects of exercise testosterone vitamin d calcium and protein in older men a randomized clinical trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcsm.13498","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-754811","identifier":[{"id":"PMC11294024","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85196160536","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38890228","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-ba38b810-7227-4f83-8e0d-228919e35198"],"keyword":["elderly","falls","physical exercise","testosterone therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-449F25A441B1F5F72368DE46A46B2245"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/400868349/J_cachexia_sarcopenia_muscle_2024_Midttun_Beneficial_effects_of_exercise_testosterone_vitamin_D_calcium_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/jcsm.13498","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mette","key":"midttunpau","last":"Midttun","name":"Midttun, Mette","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Karsten","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","name":"Overgaard, Karsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"zerahnpau","last":"Zerahn","name":"Zerahn, Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anahita","key":"rashidpau","last":"Rashid","name":"Rashid, Anahita","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter Busch","key":"østergrenpau","last":"Østergren","locid":"27fc1e9b-5aa1-46e7-b217-73fb0c5e80e7","name":"Østergren, Peter Busch","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tine Kolenda","key":"paulinpau","last":"Paulin","name":"Paulin, Tine Kolenda","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thea Winther","key":"pødenphanthpau","last":"Pødenphanth","name":"Pødenphanth, Thea Winther","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linda Katharina","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","name":"Karlsson, Linda Katharina","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eva","key":"rosendahlpau","last":"Rosendahl","name":"Rosendahl, Eva","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne-Mette","key":"raglepau","last":"Ragle","name":"Ragle, Anne-Mette","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","name":"Vinther, Anders","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rune Skovgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Rune Skovgaard","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38890228"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/jcsm.13498","issn":["21905991","21906009"],"issn_org":["21905991"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Cachexia, Sarcopenia and Muscle","pages":"1451-1462","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cachexia, Sarcopenia and Muscle","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85196160536"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-ba38b810-7227-4f83-8e0d-228919e35198"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Beneficial effects of exercise, testosterone, vitamin D, calcium and protein in older men — A randomized clinical trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-754811","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: The natural history of symptomatic uncomplicated gallstone disease is largely unknown. We examined the risk of progressing from symptomatic uncomplicated to complicated gallstone disease in a large regional cohort of patients, where disruptions in elective surgical capacities have led to the indefinite postponement of surgery for benign conditions, including cholecystectomies. Methods: Patients with radiologically diagnosed incident symptomatic and uncomplicated gallstone disease were identified from outpatient clinics and emergency departments on the Island of Funen, Denmark. The absolute risk of complications (cholecystitis, cholangitis, pancreatitis, acute cholecystectomy for unremitting pain) was calculated using death and elective cholecystectomies as competing risks using the Aalen-Johansen method. Cox proportional hazards regression analysis was used to estimate hazard ratios (HRs) of gallstone complications associated with patient and gallstone characteristics. Results: Two hundred eighty-six patients diagnosed with incident symptomatic, uncomplicated gallstone disease from 1 January 2020 to 1 July 2023 were identified. During 79,170 person-years of observation, 176 (61.5%) patients developed a gallstone-related complication. The 6-, 12- and 24-month risk of developing gallstone-related complications were 36%, 55% and 81%. The risk of developing complications related to common bile duct stones was lowest with larger stones (aHR per millimeter increase = 0.89 (0.82–0.97), p < 0.01), while no covariates were statistically significantly associated with the risk of cholecystitis. Eighty-five (30%) patients underwent elective laparoscopic cholecystectomy, with one patient (1.2%) developing a gallstone-related complication afterward. Conclusions: The risk of developing complications to symptomatic gallstones in a general Scandinavian population is high, and prophylactic cholecystectomy should be considered.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kousgaard, Nivi","Rasmussen, Sofie Kuhlemeier Møllegaard","Möller, Sören","Koulaouzidis, Anastasios","Mark-Christensen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-755375"],"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Kousgaard, Nivi"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Cholangitis","Cholecystitis","Cohort Studies","Cohort study","Complications","Denmark epidemiology","Disease Progression","Elective Surgical Procedures adverse effects","Female","Gallstone disease","Gallstones complications","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pancreatitis","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"symptomatic uncomplicated gallstone disease is associated with a high short term risk of gallstone related complications a contemporary cohort study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00365521.2024.2361756","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-755375","identifier":[{"id":"38950569","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85197570037","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-4b4dfdc1-fbae-4300-9216-3863b11f655f"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Cholangitis/etiology","Cholecystectomy/adverse effects","Cholecystitis/etiology","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Disease Progression","Elective Surgical Procedures/adverse effects","Female","Gallstone disease","Gallstones/complications","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pancreatitis/etiology","Proportional Hazards Models","Risk Factors","cholangitis","cholecystitis","cohort study","complications","pancreatitis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7649B46135CC95650523621AB8BAAB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/00365521.2024.2361756","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/268486438/Symptomatic_uncomplicated_gallstone_disease_is_associated_with_a_high_short-term_risk_of_gallstone-related_complications_a_contemporary_cohort_study.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nivi","key":"kousgaardpau","last":"Kousgaard","name":"Kousgaard, Nivi","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Kuhlemeier Møllegaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Sofie Kuhlemeier Møllegaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sören","key":"möllerpau","last":"Möller","locid":"905018dc-c6c4-4a79-b50d-d0c08618e77a","name":"Möller, Sören","orcid":"0000-0003-0858-4269","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anastasios","key":"koulaouzidispau","last":"Koulaouzidis","locid":"499479fa-64b8-4045-b32d-7d1f71805ff9","name":"Koulaouzidis, Anastasios","orcid":"0000-0002-2248-489X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"markchristensenpau","last":"Mark-Christensen","locid":"1597abf4-991d-4dff-add8-f2de72b284ba","name":"Mark-Christensen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["38950569"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/00365521.2024.2361756","issn":["00365521","15027708"],"issn_org":["00365521"],"issue":"8","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","pages":"954-960","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Gastroenterology","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85197570037"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-4b4dfdc1-fbae-4300-9216-3863b11f655f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Symptomatic uncomplicated gallstone disease is associated with a high short-term risk of gallstone-related complications : a contemporary cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-755375","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In 2021 JET exploited its unique capabilities to operate with T and D–T fuel with an ITER-like Be/W wall (JET-ILW). This second major JET D–T campaign (DTE2), after DTE1 in 1997, represented the culmination of a series of JET enhancements—new fusion diagnostics, new T injection capabilities, refurbishment of the T plant, increased auxiliary heating, in-vessel calibration of 14 MeV neutron yield monitors—as well as significant advances in plasma theory and modelling in the fusion community. DTE2 was complemented by a sequence of isotope physics campaigns encompassing operation in pure tritium at high T-NBI power. Carefully conducted for safe operation with tritium, the new T and D–T experiments used 1 kg of T (vs 100 g in DTE1), yielding the most fusion reactor relevant D–T plasmas to date and expanding our understanding of isotopes and D–T mixture physics. Furthermore, since the JET T and DTE2 campaigns occurred almost 25 years after the last major D–T tokamak experiment, it was also a strategic goal of the European fusion programme to refresh operational experience of a nuclear tokamak to prepare staff for ITER operation. The key physics results of the JET T and DTE2 experiments, carried out within the EUROfusion JET1 work package, are reported in this paper. Progress in the technological exploitation of JET D–T operations, development and validation of nuclear codes, neutronic tools and techniques for ITER operations carried out by EUROfusion (started within the Horizon 2020 Framework Programme and continuing under the Horizon Europe FP) are reported in (Litaudon et al Nucl. Fusion accepted), while JET experience on T and D–T operations is presented in (King et al Nucl. Fusion submitted).","author_count":1075,"contributors":["Maggi, C. F.","Abate, D.","Abid, N.","Abreu, P.","Adabonyan, O.","Afzal, M.","Ahmad, I.","Akhtar, M.","Albanese, R.","Aleiferis, S.","Alessi, E.","Aleynikov, P.","Aleynikov, P.","Alguacil, J.","Alhage, J.","Ali, M.","Allen, H.","