","title":"European Respiratory Journal","volume":"64"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2f7c9cdf-da33-4f00-b69f-19b9da3c799f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Self-reported maintenance training in patients with COPD - a 56 months’ follow-up study after initial pulmonary rehabilitation : a 56 months’ follow-up study after initial pulmonary rehabilitation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-801874","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Guiden giver dig indsigter i videoproduktionens grundkomponenter: Indhold Struktur Fortællergreb Form og visuelt udtryk Guiden præsenterer dig for de teknikker, som professionelle filmproducenter anvender: Planlægning bringer dig halvvejs i mål: Sådan kan du spare tid med et grundigt forarbejde. Bliv skarp på formålet med din film. Hvad er filmens ’WHY’? Er du afklaret omkring formål og målgruppe, har du sat en tydelig retning for din produktion? Hvordan udvikler du en storyline? Fortællestrukturen er afgørende, da mennesker bedst husker, forstår og køber ind på et produkt eller koncept gennem fortællinger. Definer dine pointer og gør dem skarpe: Hvad ønsker du seeren vil gøre, lære og skal kunne efterfølgende? Uden pointer intet budskab. Sådan udvikler du billedfortællingen. Lær om hvordan vinkler og kompositioner understøtter din fortælling og fører seeren igennem filmen. Anbefalinger Samtidig giver guiden anbefalinger til det tekniske arbejde; hvordan du producerer dit råmateriale i form af brugbare videooptagelser og god lyd. Du får en kort introduktion til videoklipning, hvor du giver videofortællingen sin endelige form, og jeg anbefaler et par gratis videoredigeringsprogrammer. Guiden indeholder også en skabelon til informeret samtykke i forbindelse med optagelser af videomateriale. Sidst men ikke mindst er guidens budskab: Arbejd hele tiden med at forkorte og koncentrere billeder og tekst, men bevar samtidig budskaberne = skarpe pointer. Derfor stil hele tiden skarpt på, hvad vil du opnå med videoen (hvorfor), til hvem (målgruppe), og hvordan overbeviser videofortællingen seerne?","author_count":5,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Lifland, Anders","Kousgaard, Bo","Rasmussen, Lærke Schjødt","Jakobsen, Anne Wolff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-812734"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Elbæk, Lars"],"keyword":["Læremidler","Video"],"level":"edu","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vejledning i visuel fortælling guide til udvikling optagelse og redigering af faglige videoer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dln","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289288540/Visuelfort_lling-videoundervisning-36268839_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-812734","ids":["sdu-c466726f-d4b1-4578-b932-f7479793bfde"],"keyword":["Læremidler","Video","Visuel fortælling"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F91E6EA26926717237956501D21ECC18"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289288540/Visuelfort_lling-videoundervisning-36268839_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DR"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"liflandpau","last":"Lifland","name":"Lifland, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"kousgaardpau","last":"Kousgaard","locid":"308c1b32-dba3-4439-a79a-94da6c2cdb4c","name":"Kousgaard, Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lærke Schjødt","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"23a93545-409a-4491-8e5c-92ea6df501a9","name":"Rasmussen, Lærke Schjødt","orcid":"0009-0001-2867-4993","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Wolff","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"df930f1f-51aa-4812-a1f6-d79f0477e2e5","name":"Jakobsen, Anne Wolff","name_org":"Nilsson, Anne Wolff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","eisbn":["9788794345996"],"isbn":["9788794345989"],"pages":"32","publisher":"Institut for Idræt og Biomekanik, Syddansk Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c466726f-d4b1-4578-b932-f7479793bfde"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Vejledning i visuel fortælling : Guide til udvikling, optagelse og redigering af faglige videoer","type":"Lecture Notes","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-812734","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This guide provides an introduction to the different stages of video production – as well as how to produce a inspirational and instructional video that is both compelling and informative, or a PR video for a project or disseminating research results. This guide gives you insights into the basic components of video production: Contents Structure Narrative grip Form and visual expression The guide will introduce you to the techniques used by professional filmmakers: Planning will get you halfway to the finish line: How a thorough preparatory work can help you save time. Clarify the purpose of your film. What is the ‘WHY’ of your film? Have you settled on the purpose and target audience? Have you set a clear direction for your production? How do you develop a storyline? The narrative structure is crucial because people are more likely to remember, understand, and embrace a product or concept when it’s presented as a narrative. Define your points and make them clear: What do you want the viewer to do, learn and be able to afterwards? No points, no message. How to develop the pictorial narrative. Learn about how angles and compositions support your narrative and guide the viewer through the film. Recommendations At the same time, the guide gives recommendations for the technical work – how to produce your raw material in the form of usable footage and quality audio. You will get a brief introduction to video editing and learn how to give your video narrative its final shape. I will also recommend a few free video editors. The guide also provides a template for informed consent for the recording of video material. Last but not least, the message of this guide is: Constantly work on shortening and focusing on images and text while making your messages clear = crystal-clear points. therefore, constantly focus on what do you want to achieve with the video (why), to whom (target audience), and how does the video narration convince the viewers?","author_count":5,"contributors":["Elbæk, Lars","Lifland, Anders","Kousgaard, Bo","Rasmussen, Lærke Schjødt","Jakobsen, Anne Wolff"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-812775"],"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Elbæk, Lars"],"keyword":["Learning materials","Video"],"level":"edu","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["DR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"guide to visual storytelling how to develop record and edit academic videos","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dln","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289288809/Guide_to_visual_storytelling_ENG_online.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-812775","ids":["sdu-cb498726-d8ca-4b91-a99a-cb9e5a1c7200"],"keyword":["Video","Visuel storytelling","learning materials"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7D981A100B9A8713E38E7CBAC77903C3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/289288809/Guide_to_visual_storytelling_ENG_online.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Psychology of Sport, Excellence and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["DR"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"elbækpau","last":"Elbæk","locid":"38df74af-ed72-4c38-8044-5a47490810ba","name":"Elbæk, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-2771-7293","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"liflandpau","last":"Lifland","name":"Lifland, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bo","key":"kousgaardpau","last":"Kousgaard","locid":"308c1b32-dba3-4439-a79a-94da6c2cdb4c","name":"Kousgaard, Bo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lærke Schjødt","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"23a93545-409a-4491-8e5c-92ea6df501a9","name":"Rasmussen, Lærke Schjødt","orcid":"0009-0001-2867-4993","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Wolff","key":"nilssonpau","last":"Nilsson","locid":"df930f1f-51aa-4812-a1f6-d79f0477e2e5","name":"Jakobsen, Anne Wolff","name_org":"Nilsson, Anne Wolff","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","eisbn":["9788785268631"],"isbn":["9788785268624"],"pages":"32","publisher":"Institut for Idræt og Biomekanik, Syddansk Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-cb498726-d8ca-4b91-a99a-cb9e5a1c7200"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Guide to visual storytelling : How to develop, record and edit academic videos","type":"Lecture Notes","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-812775","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This new volume repositions narrative medicine and trauma studies in a global context with a particular focus on ethics. Trauma is a rapidly growing field of especially literary and cultural studies, and the ways in which trauma has asserted its relevance across disciplines, which intersect with narrative medicine, and how it has come to widen the scope of narrative research and medical practice constitute the principal concerns of this volume. This collection brings together contributions from established and emerging scholars coming from a wide range of academic fields within the faculty of humanities that include literary and media studies, psychology, philosophy, history, anthropology as well as medical education and health care studies. This crossing of disciplines is also represented by the collaboration between the two editors. Most of the authors in the volume use narrative medicine to refer to the methodology pioneered by Rita Charon and her colleagues at Columbia University, but in some chapters, the authors use it to refer to other methodologies and pedagogies utilizing that descriptor. Trauma is today understood both in the restricted sense in which it is used in the mental health field and in its more widespread, popular usage in literature. This collection aspires to prolong, deepen, and advance the field of narrative medicine in two important aspects: by bringing together both the cultural and the clinical side of trauma and by opening the investigation to a truly global horizon.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Juhl Rasmussen, Anders","Sodemann, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-083.33-769195"],"filters":{"added":"2024-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Juhl Rasmussen, Anders"],"keyword":["Antropologi","Etik","Faculty of Humanities","Kultur","Litteratur","Medicin","Narrativ medicin","Traumer"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narrative medicine trauma and ethics","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://vernonpress.com/book/1925","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-083.33-769195","ids":["ku-c0421f49-5d25-48b7-a770-c05ede767584","sdu-2907b81d-c0a4-4fb0-b9b9-ea73754efa20"],"keyword":["Faculty of Humanities","antropologi","etik","kultur","litteratur","medicin","narrativ medicin","traumer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-217BF36F986AB48AF3CC37537CA2200C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenped","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3e1188ff-4cc9-42e2-86b3-59515e62f1af","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"sodemannped","last":"Sodemann","locid":"e4e58879-7d72-4665-880c-38ad97d0ebe5","name":"Sodemann, Morten","orcid":"0000-0001-8992-2500","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9781648898457"],"pages":"275","place":"Delaware, USA","publisher":"Vernon Press","series":"Cognitive Science and Psychology","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c0421f49-5d25-48b7-a770-c05ede767584","sdu-2907b81d-c0a4-4fb0-b9b9-ea73754efa20"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Narrative Medicine : Trauma and Ethics","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.33-769195","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Background: Obesity rates have nearly tripled in the past 50 years, and by 2030 more than 1 billion individuals worldwide are projected to be obese. This creates a significant economic strain due to the associated non-communicable diseases. The root cause is an energy expenditure imbalance, owing to an interplay of lifestyle, environmental, and genetic factors. Obesity has a polygenic genetic architecture; however, single genetic variants with large effect size are etiological in a minority of cases. These variants allowed the discovery of novel genes and biology relevant to weight regulation and ultimately led to the development of novel specific treatments. Methods: We used a case-control approach to determine metabolic differences between individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in the small integral membrane protein 1 (SMIM1) and the general population, leveraging data from five cohorts. Metabolic characterization of SMIM1−/− individuals was performed using plasma biochemistry, calorimetric chamber, and DXA scan. Findings: We found that individuals homozygous for a loss-of-function genetic variant in SMIM1 gene, underlying the blood group Vel, display excess body weight, dyslipidemia, altered leptin to adiponectin ratio, increased liver enzymes, and lower thyroid hormone levels. This was accompanied by a reduction in resting energy expenditure. Conclusion: This research identified a novel genetic predisposition to being overweight or obese. It highlights the need to investigate the genetic causes of obesity to select the most appropriate treatment given the large cost disparity between them. Funding: This work was funded by the National Institute of Health Research, British Heart Foundation, and NHS Blood and Transplant.","author_count":496,"contributors":["Stefanucci, Luca","Moslemi, Camous","Tomé, Ana R.","Virtue, Samuel","Bidault, Guillaume","Gleadall, Nicholas S.","Watson, Laura P.E.","Kwa, Jing E.","Burden, Frances","Farrow, Samantha","Banasik, Karina","Bay, Jakob","Boldsen, Jens Kjærgaard","Brodersen, Thorsten","Brunak, Søren","Burgdorf, Kristoffer","Chalmer, Mona Ameri","Didriksen, Maria","Dinh, Khoa Manh","Dowsett, Joseph","Erikstrup, Christian","Feenstra, Bjarke","Geller, Frank","Gudbjartsson, Daniel","Hansen, Thomas Folkmann","Hindhede, Lotte","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Jacobsen, Rikke Louise","Jemec, Gregor","Jensen, Bitten Aagaard","Kaspersen, Kathrine Agergård","Kjerulff, Bertram","Kogelman, Lisette","Hørup Larsen, Margit Anita","Louloudis, Ioannis","Lundgaard, Agnete","Susan, no-firstname","Mikkelsen, Christina","Nissen, Ioanna","Nyegaard, Mette","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Pedersen, Ole B.","Henriksen, Alexander Pil","Rohde, Palle Duun","Rostgaard, Klaus","Schwinn, Michael","Stefansson, Kari","Stefánsson, Hreinn","Sørensen, Erik","þorsteinsdóttir, Unnur","Thørner, Lise Wegner","Bruun, Mie Topholm","Ullum, Henrik","Werge, Thomas","Westergaard, David","Chen, Ji","Spracklen, Cassandra N.","Marenne, Gaëlle","Varshney, Arushi","Corbin, Laura J.","Luan, Jian'an","Willems, Sara M.","Wu, Ying","Zhang, Xiaoshuai","Horikoshi, Momoko","Boutin, Thibaud S.","Mägi, Reedik","Waage, Johannes","Li-Gao, Ruifang","Katie Chan, Kei Hang","Yao, Jie","Anasanti, Mila D.","Chu, Audrey Y.","Claringbould, Annique","Heikkinen, Jani","Hong, Jaeyoung","Hottenga, Jouke Jan","Huo, Shaofeng","Kaakinen, Marika A.","Louie, Tin","März, Winfried","Moreno-Macias, Hortensia","Ndungu, Anne","Nelson, Sarah C.","Nolte, Ilja M.","North, Kari E.","Raulerson, Chelsea K.","Ray, Debashree","Rohde, Rebecca","Rybin, Denis","Schurmann, Claudia","Sim, Xueling","Southam, Loz","Stewart, Isobel D.","Wang, Carol A.","Wang, Yujie","Wu, Peitao","Zhang, Weihua","Ahluwalia, Tarunveer S.","Appel, Emil V.R.","Bielak, Lawrence F.","Brody, Jennifer A.","Burtt, Noël P.","Cabrera, Claudia P.","Cade, Brian E.","Chai, Jin Fang","Chai, Xiaoran","Chang, Li Ching","Chen, Chien Hsiun","Chen, Brian H.","Chitrala, Kumaraswamy Naidu","Chiu, Yen Feng","de Haa