{"abstract":"Background: Incrementing numbers of patients treated for attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder (ADHD) call for scrutiny concerning long-term drug-safety. Objectives: This study aims to investigate associations between long-term use of ADHD treatment and cardiovascular outcomes. Methods: Using nationwide registers, adult patients first-time initiated on ADHD treatment between 1998 and 2020 were identified. Exposure groups were prior users, <1 defined daily dose (DDD) per day, ≥1 DDD per day determined at start of follow-up, and 1 year after patients’ first claimed prescription. Outcomes were acute coronary syndromes, stroke, heart failure, and a composite of the above. Results: At start of follow-up, 26,357, 31,211, and 15,696 individuals were correspondingly categorized as prior users (42% female, median age: 30 years [Q1-Q3: 23-41 years]), <1 DDD per day (47% female, median age: 31 years [Q1-Q3: 24-41 years]), and ≥1 DDD per day (47% female, median age: 33 years [Q1-Q3: 25–41 years]), respectively. Comparing ≥1 DDD per day with prior users, elevated standardized 10-year absolute risk of stroke (2.1% [95% CI: 1.8%-2.4%] vs 1.7% [95% CI: 1.5%-1.9%]), heart failure (1.2% [95% CI: 0.9%-1.4%] vs 0.7% [95% CI: 0.6%-0.8%]), and the composite outcome (3.9% [95% CI: 3.4%-4.3%] vs 3.0% [95% CI: 2.8 %-3.2%]) was found—with corresponding risk ratios of 1.2 (95% CI: 1.0-1.5), 1.7 (95% CI: 1.3-2.2), and 1.3 (95% CI: 1.1-1.5). No apparent associations were found for acute coronary syndrome (1.0% [95% CI: 0.8%-1.2%] vs 0.9% [95% CI: 0.8%-1.0%]). Conclusions: Possible associations between elevated long-term cardiovascular risk and increasing dosage of ADHD treatment use in a young patient group should warrant further investigation.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Holt, Anders","Strange, Jarl E.","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","Nouhravesh, Nina","Nielsen, Sebastian Kinnberg","Sindet-Pedersen, Caroline","Fosbøl, Emil","Køber, Lars","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Gislason, Gunnar","McGettigan, Patricia","Schou, Morten","Lamberts, Morten"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-735558"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Holt, Anders"],"country":["New Zealand","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London","The University of Auckland","University of Auckland"],"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Adult","Attention Deficit Disorder with Hyperactivity epidemiology","Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder","Cardiovascular Diseases epidemiology","Central Nervous System Stimulants adverse effects","Drug safety","Female","Follow Up Studies","Heart Disease Risk Factors","Heart failure","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Pharmacoepidemiology","Registries","Stroke","Time Factors","Young Adult","attention deficit hyperactivity disorder treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"long term cardiovascular risk associated with treatment of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder in adults","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85190981733","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.24-735558","identifier":[{"id":"85190981733","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38719367","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b2eb7d05-7257-40ac-be84-a8363a3e64e8","sdu-c2fdcc8c-116b-4f3c-8449-d727fe090faa"],"keyword":["Adult","Attention Deficit Disorder with Hyperactivity/epidemiology","Cardiovascular Diseases/epidemiology","Central Nervous System Stimulants/adverse effects","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Heart Disease Risk Factors","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Registries","Time Factors","Young Adult","acute coronary syndrome","attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder","attention-deficit/hyperactivity disorder treatment","drug-safety","heart failure","pharmacoepidemiology","stroke"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-28B82AA5080826101AA2055EFB713B8A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Herlev and Gentofte"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"nz","key":"the university of auckland","loc":["New Zealand","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"The University of Auckland","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"danish heart foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-HJER","l3nn":"Danish Heart Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Danish Heart Foundation","namevar":["The Danish Heart Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-HJER","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","nameva