{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with multimorbidity are frequent users of healthcare, but fragmented care may lead to suboptimal treatment. Yet, this has never been examined across healthcare sectors on a national scale. We aimed to quantify care fragmentation using various measures and to analyze the associations with patient outcomes. METHODS: We conducted a register-based nationwide cohort study with 4.7 million Danish adult citizens. All healthcare contacts to primary care and hospitals during 2018 were recorded. Clinical fragmentation indicators included number of healthcare contacts, involved providers, provider transitions, and hospital trajectories. Formal fragmentation indices assessed care concentration, dispersion, and contact sequence. The patient outcomes were potentially inappropriate medication and all-cause mortality adjusted for demographics, socioeconomic factors, and morbidity level. RESULTS: The number of involved healthcare providers, provider transitions, and hospital trajectories rose with increasing morbidity levels. Patients with 3 versus 6 conditions had a mean of 4.0 versus 6.9 involved providers and 6.6 versus 13.7 provider transitions. The proportion of contacts to the patient's own general practice remained stable across morbidity levels. High levels of care fragmentation were associated with higher rates of potentially inappropriate medication and increased mortality on all fragmentation measures after adjusting for demographic characteristics, socioeconomic factors, and morbidity. The strongest associations with potentially inappropriate medication and mortality were found for ≥ 20 contacts versus none (incidence rate ratio 2.83, 95% CI 2.77-2.90) and ≥ 20 hospital trajectories versus none (hazard ratio 10.8, 95% CI 9.48-12.4), respectively. Having less than 25% of contacts with your usual provider was associated with an incidence rate ratio of potentially inappropriate medication of 1.49 (95% CI 1.40-1.58) and a mortality hazard ratio of 2.59 (95% CI 2.36-2.84) compared with full continuity. For the associations between fragmentation measures and patient outcomes, there were no clear interactions with number of conditions. CONCLUSIONS: Several clinical indicators of care fragmentation were associated with morbidity level. Care fragmentation was associated with higher rates of potentially inappropriate medication and increased mortality even when adjusting for the most important confounders. Frequent contact to the usual provider, fewer transitions, and better coordination were associated with better patient outcomes regardless of morbidity level.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Prior, Anders","Vestergaard, Claus Høstrup","Vedsted, Peter","Smith, Susan M","Virgilsen, Line Flytkjær","Rasmussen, Linda Aagaard","Fenger-Grøn, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-682768"],"filters":{"added":"2023-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Ireland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Dublin Dental University Hospital"],"keyword":["Adult","Almen praksis","Cohort Studies","Delivery of Health Care","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Kontinuitet","Multimorbidity","Potentially Inappropriate Medication List","fragmentering"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"healthcare fragmentation multimorbidity potentially inappropriate medication and mortality a danish nationwide cohort study","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-023-03021-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-682768","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10426166","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37580711","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85168211104","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c6d2204d-9ad2-49af-9174-f81b7be9de7e"],"keyword":["Adult","Cohort Studies","Delivery of Health Care","Denmark/epidemiology","Humans","Multimorbidity","Potentially Inappropriate Medication List","almen praksis","fragmentering","kontinuitet"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-622ABC4443CF59166150D96D06F31C4C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12916-023-03021-3","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Public Health, Department of Public Health - Forskningsenheden for Almen Praksis"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"ie","key":"dublin dental university hospital","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Dublin Dental University Hospital","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"priorpau","last":"Prior","locid":"91c66e03-635d-473b-861f-c214184aeb95","name":"Prior, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4053-3701","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus Høstrup","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"b6937f69-38e6-4b03-9793-61df4fc6224a","name":"Vestergaard, Claus Høstrup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vedstedpau","last":"Vedsted","locid":"bb00d9e7-866c-4f04-8e3b-a71c913c39b0","name":"Vedsted, Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-2113-5599","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Susan M","key":"smithpau","last":"Smith","name":"Smith, Susan M","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Line Flytkjær","key":"virgilsenpau","last":"Virgilsen","locid":"6ff51f4d-e27a-4646-8a7a-0123c17fddc7","name":"Virgilsen, Line Flytkjær","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Linda Aagaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"321bbf64-b73e-4077-8d16-ba3df95fbbe2","name":"Rasmussen, Linda Aagaard","orcid":"0000-0002-9753-2008","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"fengergrønpau","last":"Fenger-Grøn","locid":"cbedd7f4-1b1c-4ebd-91de-0f1665135ce1","name":"Fenger-Grøn, Morten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37580711"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12916-023-03021-3","issn":["17417015"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Medicine","paperid":"305","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Medicine","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85168211104"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c6d2204d-9ad2-49af-9174-f81b7be9de7e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Healthcare fragmentation, multimorbidity, potentially inappropriate medication, and mortality : a Danish nationwide cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-682768","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Since the beginning of the mpox (previously called monkeypox) outbreak in 2022, almost half of cases in Denmark have been diagnosed at the Department of Infectious Diseases, Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre Hospital. This article describes the patient cohort seen at the Department with a view to increasing knowledge of mpox among colleagues who are most likely to identify future cases. METHODS: A retrospective observational study reporting patient characteristics, coinfections, clinical presentation and diagnostic delay among mpox cases diagnosed at the department between 23 May 2022 and 8 February 2023. Furthermore, a case report of a patient hospitalised with severe rectal pain is presented to highlight anorectal symptoms. RESULTS: A total of 86 patients were diagnosed with mpox, all were men who have sex with men, with a median age of 39 years. Twenty-six patients (31%) took HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis, and 20 patients (24%) were people living with HIV. All patients (100%) presented with lesions, most frequently on or around the genitals. Twenty-nine patients (35%) had anorectal discomfort or pain. Seven patients (10%) had chlamydia, 19 (26%) gonorrhoea and two (5%) syphilis. In 13 cases (15%), mpox was not suspected at the first medical consultation, mainly because symptoms were attributed to a gonorrhoeal coinfection. Five patients (6%) were hospitalised for a median of three days. CONCLUSION: As mpox may become endemic in Denmark, clinicians should remain aware of its symptoms and the risk of coinfection with sexually transmitted infections. FUNDING: None. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Not relevant.","author_count":6,"contributors":["von Schreeb, Sebastian","Exsteen, Banoo Bakir","Zangenberg, Mike","Rasmussen, Morten","Fromsgaard, Anders","Kronborg, Gitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689510"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Hvidovre Infectious Diseases Group (HIDG)"],"keyword":["Adult","Coinfection","Delayed Diagnosis","Female","HIV Infections","Homosexuality Male","Hospitals University","Humans","Male","Pain","Sexual and Gender Minorities"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characteristics of 000000000086 individuals with mpox diagnosed at copenhagen university hospital","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/363816457/A09220544_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689510","identifier":[{"id":"37125825","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85159247775","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-35e8c53b-d3fb-4ca7-974c-72577f82acf5"],"keyword":["Adult","Coinfection","Delayed Diagnosis","Female","HIV Infections","Homosexuality, Male","Hospitals, University","Humans","Male","Monkeypox/diagnosis","Pain","Sexual and Gender Minorities"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7F64F5588E687906D4439F701B8C2F06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/363816457/A09220544_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/dmj/characteristics-86-individuals-mpox-diagnosed-copenhagen-university-hospital","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"hvidovre infectious diseases group","name":"Hvidovre Infectious Diseases Group (HIDG)","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Sebastian","key":"vonschreebpau","last":"von Schreeb","name":"von Schreeb, Sebastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Banoo Bakir","key":"exsteenpau","last":"Exsteen","name":"Exsteen, Banoo Bakir","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mike","key":"zangenbergpau","last":"Zangenberg","name":"Zangenberg, Mike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"fromsgaardpau","last":"Fromsgaard","name":"Fromsgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37125825"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"5","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","paperid":"A09220544","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"70"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85159247775"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-35e8c53b-d3fb-4ca7-974c-72577f82acf5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characteristics of 86 individuals with mpox diagnosed at Copenhagen University Hospital","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689510","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"As the most mature technology within the electrolysis field, alkaline electrolyzers are expected to play an important role in the energetic transition. Advantages as their simplicity, modularity and low-cost components make it an interesting technology for the near future. However, the fundamental physics are complex as it includes multicomponent, multiphase flow, porous media, electrochemistry and heat transfer. To have a better understanding of these phenomena, the presented work is devoted to the development of a computational fluid dynamic model to better understand the behavior of all the species that are part of this technology.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Martinho, Diogo Loureiro","Berning, Torsten","Abdollahzadehsangroudi, Mohammadmahdi","Rasmussen, Anders","Hærvig, Jakob","Araya, Samuel Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-693080"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Portugal"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Beira Interior"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a three dimensional multiphysics model of an alkaline electrolyzer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-693080","ids":["aau-dc76692b-a295-41e6-aafa-d1ecac4d7a22"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-062E59DDD6797978A51FDBA1419C61FD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty o