{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Christian Frigaard","Søndergaard, Jens","Hvidtfeldt Christiansen, Hanne","Mosbech, Anders","Jørgensen, Christian Juncher"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-699286"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"country":["Svalbard and Jan Mayen"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University Centre in Svalbard"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"road dust on svalbard a pilot study on the distribution mineral composition and impact of haul road dust in adventdalen","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.32607.02727","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-699286","ids":["au-17347dd0-2bf0-4b43-848e-f70bba4cee42"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-AB294D37CE5A710C47B31E583EF9448D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.13140/RG.2.2.32607.02727","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Arctic Environment"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"sj","key":"university centre in svalbard","loc":["Svalbard and Jan Mayen","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic"],"name":"University Centre in Svalbard","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Frigaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c64d8832-0109-4466-b421-c42e314ae238","name":"Rasmussen, Christian Frigaard","orcid":"0000-0003-2497-2990","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"ed027e07-2df4-474c-b76a-b0ced3210d88","name":"Søndergaard, Jens","orcid":"0000-0001-7680-9920","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanne","key":"hvidtfeldtchristiansenpau","last":"Hvidtfeldt Christiansen","name":"Hvidtfeldt Christiansen, Hanne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"mosbechpau","last":"Mosbech","locid":"0d8b3009-ff00-40a7-b738-abfa87e31ccf","name":"Mosbech, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-7581-7037","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian Juncher","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"8c3aea27-e504-4762-87b5-ac06d899de02","name":"Jørgensen, Christian Juncher","orcid":"0000-0002-5184-7063","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-17347dd0-2bf0-4b43-848e-f70bba4cee42"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Road dust on Svalbard – A pilot study on the distribution, mineral composition and impact of haul road dust in Adventdalen","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-699286","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Present study aims to investigate the lean-burn characteristics of ammonia in a pre-mixed SI (Spark Ignition) engine and the influence of spark energy and discharge characteristics on engine performance and emissions. A wide range of engine operation conditions have been explored with particular focus on emission measurement. Engine parameters have been systematically swept to explore engine control strategies that would be operational in real engine application with a wide range of engine loads and tight emission regulations. Most previous studies required more than 5 % addition of hydrogen to the ammonia in order to achieve stable ignition for wide operation conditions. This has been a major obstacle in the application of ammonia for SI engines due to safety and system complexity issues. In present work, a comprehensive effort was made to understand and optimize the spark ignition system in order to mitigate the need for an ignition improver and all experiments have been performed with 100 % neat ammonia. With present engine modifications, emissions of unburned ammonia was measured to be between 5000 and 10000 ppm and with a combustion efficiency above 95 %. The unburned ammonia is believed to originate from crevices, particularly at the ring-pack. The NOx emission was between 4000 and 8000 ppm even at high excess air ratios. The emission of N2O is critical to minimize, as it is a strong greenhouse gas. It was measured to be between 20 and 80 ppm and appear to be related to post oxidation reactions of ammonia released from crevices during expansion. Advancing the ignition timing has proved to be an efficient handle for balancing the emissions of NH3 and NOx. These emissions will be reduced to H2O and N2 in an SCR catalyst if they are correctly balanced. Fortunately, advancing ignition timing also minimizes the formation of N2O.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jespersen, Mads Carsten","Østerby Holst Rasmussen, Thomas","Ivarsson, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-700960"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Ivarsson, Anders"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"widening the operation limits of a si engine running on neat ammonia","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2023.130159","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-700960","identifier":[{"id":"85175714388","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-833798ff-9b20-4c20-9456-f5835ddf4752"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D5F88CEDF12164C5DF4EC97CB00DF2F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.fuel.2023.130159","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/339553644/1-s2.0-S0016236123027734-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Civil and Mechanical Engineering, Thermal Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"carstenjespersenpau","last":"Carsten Jespersen","locid":"ef4c2b34-7854-4d4c-af40-561dc1b390c1","name":"Jespersen, Mads Carsten","name_org":"Carsten Jespersen, Mads","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas","key":"østerbyholstrasmussenpau","last":"Østerby Holst Rasmussen","locid":"55acfdbf-f606-4c72-9c3f-d5bee2df20f9","name":"Østerby Holst Rasmussen, Thomas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"ivarssonpau","last":"Ivarsson","locid":"0b4d32bc-740b-4474-bfe9-43dad3fb3064","name":"Ivarsson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-9631-6012","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.fuel.2023.130159","issn":["00162361","18737153"],"issn_org":["00162361"],"journal":"Fuel","paperid":"130159","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Fuel","volume":"358"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175714388"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-833798ff-9b20-4c20-9456-f5835ddf4752"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Widening the operation limits of a SI engine running on neat ammonia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-700960","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"During the last century, the critically endangered cotton-top tamarin (Saguinus oedipus) has been threatened by multiple anthropogenic factors that drastically affected their habitat and population size. As the genetic impact of these pressures is largely unknown, this study aimed to establish a genetic baseline with the use of temporal sampling to determine the genetic makeup before detrimental anthropogenic impact. Genomes were resequenced from a combination of historical museum samples and modern wild samples at low-medium coverage, to unravel how the cotton-top tamarin population structure and genomic diversity may have changed during this period. Our data suggest two populations can be differentiated, probably separated historically by the mountain ranges of the Paramillo Massif in Colombia. Although this population structure persists in the current populations, modern samples exhibit genomic signals consistent with recent inbreeding, such as long runs of homozygosity and a reduction in genome-wide heterozygosity especially in the greater northeast population. This loss is likely the consequence of the population reduction following the mass exportation of cotton-top tamarins for biomedical research in the 1960s, coupled with the habitat loss this species continues to experience. However, current populations have not experienced an increase in genetic load. We propose that the historical genetic baseline established in this study can be used to provide insight into alteration in the modern population influenced by a drastic reduction in population size as well as providing background information to be used for future conservation decision-making for the species.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Linett","Fontsere, Claudia","Soto-Calderón, Iván D.","Guillen, Rosamira","Savage, Anne","Hansen, Anders Johannes","Hvilsom, Christina","Gilbert, M. Thomas P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701451"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, South","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Colombia","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Fundación Proyecto Tití","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","Universidad de Antioquia"],"keyword":["Conservation genomics","Genetic diversity","Historical DNA","Population genetics","Population structure"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessing the genetic composition of cotton top tamarins i saguinus oedipus i before sweeping anthropogenic impact","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/mec.17130","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-701451","identifier":[{"id":"37702122","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85170707889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-25e7e8c8-1386-4637-9b33-fc458f5294fb"],"keyword":["conservation genomics","cotton-top tamarin","genetic diversity","historical DNA","population genetics","population structure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49028ACA3B119C34B57A3CE5EA9BB11F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/mec.17130","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/371279166/Molecular_Ecology_2023_Rasmussen_Assessing_the_genetic_composition_of_cotton_top_tamarins_Saguinus_oedipus_before.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"