DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3e06d911-953b-4ae5-b78b-639d943d7795","ku-669f8601-4174-4560-877e-748161738f92"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Patient and public involvement in contemporary large intensive care trials : A meta-epidemiological study","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-087.50-681226","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Objective:Assessing whether the previously reported association between abacavir (ABC) and cardiovascular disease (CVD) remained amongst contemporarily treated people with HIV.Design:Multinational cohort collaboration.Methods:RESPOND participants were followed from the latest of 1 January 2012 or cohort enrolment until the first of a CVD event (myocardial infarction, stroke, invasive cardiovascular procedure), last follow-up or 31 December 2019. Logistic regression examined the odds of starting ABC by 5-year CVD or chronic kidney disease (CKD) D:A:D risk score. We assessed associations between recent ABC use (use within the past 6 months) and risk of CVD with negative binomial regression models, adjusted for potential confounders.Results:Of 29 340 individuals, 34% recently used ABC. Compared with those at low estimated CVD and CKD risks, the odds of starting ABC were significantly higher among individuals at high CKD risk [odds ratio 1.12 (95% confidence interval = 1.04-1.21)] and significantly lower for individuals at moderate, high or very high CVD risk [0.80 (0.72-0.88), 0.75 (0.64-0.87), 0.71 (0.56-0.90), respectively]. During 6.2 years of median follow-up (interquartile range; 3.87-7.52), there were 748 CVD events (incidence rate 4.7 of 1000 persons-years of follow up (4.3-5.0)]. The adjusted CVD incidence rate ratio was higher for individuals with recent ABC use [1.40 (1.20-1.64)] compared with individuals without, consistent across sensitivity analyses. The association did not differ according to estimated CVD (interaction P = 0.56) or CKD (P = 0.98) risk strata.Conclusion:Within RESPOND's contemporarily treated population, a significant association between CVD incidence and recent ABC use was confirmed and not explained by preferential ABC use in individuals at increased CVD or CKD risk.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Jaschinski, Nadine","Greenberg, Lauren","Neesgaard, Bastian","Miró, Jose M.","Grabmeier-Pfistershammer, Katharina","Wandeler, Gilles","Smith, Colette","De Wit, Stéphane","Wit, Ferdinand","Pelchen-Matthews, Annegret","Mussini, Cristina","Castagna, Antonella","Pradier, Christian","D'Arminio Monforte, Antonella","Vehreschild, Jörg","Sönnerborg, Anders","Anne, Alain V.","Carr, Andrew","Bansi-Matharu, Loveleen","Lundgren, Jens","Garges, Harmony","Rogatto, Felipe","Zangerle, Robert","Günthard, Huldrych F.","Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","Nescoi, Coca","Van Der Valk, Marc","Menozzi, Marianna","Muccini, Camilla","Mocroft, Amanda","Peters, Lars","Ryom, Lene"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-692296"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Jaschinski, Nadine"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["ASST Santi Paolo e Carlo","All Global Affiliations","Department of Gastroenterology, St. Vincent's Hospital, Sydney, NSW, Australia.","European AIDS Treatment Group","Gilead Sciences","Gilead Sciences Incorporated","GlaxoSmithKline","Goethe University Frankfurt","HIV Monitoring Foundation","Innsbruck Medical University","Institute for Global Health","Instituto de Salud Carlos III","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Medical University of Innsbruck","Medical University of Vienna","Saint-Pierre University Hospital","San Raffaele Scientific Institute","St Pierre University Hospital","St. Vincent's Hospital Sydney","University College London","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital Cologne","University Hospital Zurich","University Hospital Zürich","University Hospital of Bern","University of Barcelona","University of Cologne","University of Côte d'Azur","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of New South Wales","University of Zurich","University of Zürich","ViiV Healthcare","Vita-Salute San Raffaele University"],"keyword":["Abacavir","Antiretroviral therapy","Cardiovascular disease","antiretroviral drugs"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"recent abacavir use and incident cardiovascular disease in contemporary treated people with hiv","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/256189272/Recent_abacavir_use_and_incident_cardiovascular.102.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["RESPOND has received funding from ViiV Healthcare LLC, Gilead Sciences and Merck Sharp & Dohme. Additional support has been provided by participating cohorts contributing data in-kind and/or statistical support: Austrian HIV Cohort Study (AHIVCOS), The Australian HIV Observational Database (AHOD), CHU Saint-Pierre, University Hospital Cologne, EuroSIDA, Frankfurt HIV Cohort Study, Georgian National AIDS Health Information System (AIDS HIS), Modena HIV Cohort, San Raffaele Scientific Institute, Swiss HIV Cohort Study (SHCS), AIDS Therapy Evaluation in the Netherlands Cohort (ATHENA), Royal Free HIV Cohort Study. AHOD is further supported by grant No. U01-AI069907 from the US National Institutes of Health, and GNT1050874 of the National Health and Medical Research Council, Australia."],"id":"S02-088.24-692296","identifier":[{"id":"85145549321","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36001525","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-9c3b3789-3ead-404b-9a8a-0dbfd8e2d05d","sdu-b1aff050-dc76-4186-a9b7-c32bd0740a37"],"keyword":["abacavir","antiretroviral drugs","antiretroviral therapy","cardiovascular disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1D