-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9c3b3789-3ead-404b-9a8a-0dbfd8e2d05d","sdu-b1aff050-dc76-4186-a9b7-c32bd0740a37"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Recent abacavir use and incident cardiovascular disease in contemporary-treated people with HIV","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-692296","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background We hypothesized that insufficient intake of fish oil-derived omega-3 long-chain polyunsaturated fatty acids (n-3 LCPUFAs) during pregnancy is a contributing factor to gastroenteritis in early childhood. We examined the effect of n-3 LCPUFA supplementation on gastroenteritis symptoms in the offspring's first 3 years of life. Methods This was a double-blinded, randomized controlled trial whereby 736 mothers were administered n-3 LCPUFA or control from pregnancy week 24 until 1 week after birth. We measured the number of days with gastroenteritis, number of episodes with gastroenteritis, and the risk of having a gastroenteritis episode in the first 3 years of life. Results A median reduction of 2.5 days with gastroenteritis (P = .018) was shown, corresponding to a 14% reduction in the n-3 LCPUFA group compared with controls in the first 3 years of life (P = .037). A reduction in the number of gastroenteritis episodes (P = .027) and a reduced risk of having an episode (hazard ratio, 0.80 [95% confidence interval, .66-.97]; P = .023) were also shown. Conclusions Fish oil supplementation from the 24th week of pregnancy led to a reduction in the number of days and episodes with gastroenteritis symptoms in the first 3 years of life. The findings suggest n-3 LCPUFA supplementation as a preventive measure against gastrointestinal infections in early childhood. Supplementation with fish oil from the 24th week of pregnancy in a cohort of 736 mothers and their children resulted in fewer gastroenteritis days and episodes in the children's first 3 years of life.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Horner, David","Hjelmsø, Mathis Hjort","Thorsen, Jonathan","Rasmussen, Morten Arendt","Eliasen, Anders","Vinding, Rebecca Kofod","Schoos, Ann Marie Malby","Brustad, Nicklas","Sunde, Rikke Bjersand","Bønnelykke, Klaus","Chawes, Bo","Stokholm, Jakob","Bisgaard, Hans"],"cuid":["S02-095.32-692161"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Bisgaard, Hans"],"keyword":["Fish oil","Gastroenteritis","Pediatrics","Pregnancy supplementation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"supplementation with fish oil in pregnancy reduces gastroenteritis in early childhood","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85161687656","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.32-692161","identifier":[{"id":"000756760300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"34927195","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85161687656","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-362bf8b2-fea7-447f-aa58-b7db501a6be3","ku-dc898ee0-f12d-4e9b-a1c6-80fdeaff898b"],"keyword":["fish oil","gastroenteritis","pediatrics","pregnancy supplementation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DD4BA8548955CB0CA5A14C0F718310D6"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_co