of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152244502"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6be7e46e-a8a1-4f1a-a640-2d3a8057ae52"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Biomarker expression and survival in patients with non-small cell lung cancer receiving adjuvant chemotherapy in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-675108","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Research on cultural stratification often draws on Bourdieu's misrecognition model to interpret socioeconomic gradients in cultural tastes and participation. In this model, an assumed cultural hierarchy leads individuals to adopt cultural tastes and behaviours whose status is congruent with that of their socioeconomic position (SEP). Yet, this assumed cultural hierarchy remains opaque. In this paper, we derive and test three empirical implications of the cultural hierarchy: (1) cultural activities have different status (recognition); (2) individuals in high and low SEPs have similar perceptions of the status of cultural activities (necessary condition for misrecognition); and (3) individuals prefer and engage in cultural activities whose status matches that of their SEP (status congruence). We collected survey data in Denmark and find that cultural activities differ in terms of perceived status (e.g., opera has higher perceived status than flea market), status perceptions are similar in high- and low-SEP groups and individuals prefer activities whose status matches that of their SEP. These results are consistent with the idea that a cultural hierarchy exists that sustains SEP gradients in cultural tastes and participation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Jæger, Mads Meier","Rasmussen, Rikke Haudrum","Holm, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677826"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bourdieu","Cultural participation","Inequality","Misrecognition","Status","cultural taste"],"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"what cultural hierarchy cultural tastes status and inequality","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-677826","identifier":[{"id":"85150648949","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36908000","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2c9e2a2b-c227-402d-a0db-1365d94c44ca"],"keyword":["Bourdieu","cultural participation","cultural taste","inequality","misrecognition","status"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-967AE72F51F9D3A5A4E861319193EFEC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Sociology, Department of Sociology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Meier","key":"jægerpau","last":"Jæger","locid":"928d04fe-1b15-420a-bd64-c78c9dc02667","name":"Jæger, Mads Meier","orcid":"0000-0003-3666-8398","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rikke Haudrum","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Rikke Haudrum","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"f1efb14e-f9d3-4be6-8cc3-4feeff34b299","name":"Holm, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36908000"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/1468-4446.13012","issn":["00071315","14684446"],"issn_org":["00071315"],"issue":"3","journal":"British Journal of Sociology","pages":"402-418","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Sociology","volume":"74"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150648949"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2c9e2a2b-c227-402d-a0db-1365d94c44ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"What cultural hierarchy? : Cultural tastes, status and inequality","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677826","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
