.14317","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"10","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"1383-1394","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85171846745"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-94e85b52-393c-4f7d-bc1b-1c7789234464","ku-7fb77b3b-811c-4495-8419-8f271224ea3d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A survey of preferences for respiratory support in the intensive care unit for patients with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.90-741467","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The aim of this study was to describe the pattern of revision indications for unicompartmental knee arthroplasty (UKA) and total knee arthroplasty (TKA) and any change to this pattern for UKA patients over the last 20 years, and to investigate potential associations to changes in surgical practice over time. METHODS: All primary knee arthroplasty surgeries performed due to primary osteoarthritis and their revisions reported to the Danish Knee Arthroplasty Register from 1997 to 2017 were included. Complex surgeries were excluded. The data was linked to the National Patient Register and the Civil Registration System for comorbidity, mortality, and emigration status. TKAs were propensity score matched 4:1 to UKAs. Revision risks were compared using competing risk Cox proportional hazard regression with a shared γ frailty component. RESULTS: Aseptic loosening (loosening) was the most common revision indication for both UKA (26.7%) and TKA (29.5%). Pain and disease progression accounted for 54.6% of the remaining UKA revisions. Infections and instability accounted for 56.1% of the remaining TKA revision. The incidence of revision due to loosening or pain decreased over the last decade, being the second and third least common indications in 2017. There was a decrease associated with fixation method for pain (hazard ratio (HR) 0.40; 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.17 to 0.94) and loosening (HR 0.29; 95% CI 0.10 to 0.81) for cementless compared to cemented, and units UKA usage for pain (HR 0.67, 95% CI 0.50 to 0.91), and loosening (HR 0.51; 95% CI 0.37 to 0.70) for high usage. CONCLUSION: The overall revision patterns for UKA and TKA for the last 20 years are comparable to previous published patterns. We found large changes to UKA revision patterns in the last decade, and with the current surgical practice, revision due to pain or loosening are significantly less likely.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Mikkelsen, Mette","Rasmussen, Lasse E","Price, Andrew","Pedersen, Alma Becic","Gromov, Kirill","Troelsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-091.13-704145"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mikkelsen, Mette"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does changes in unicompartmental knee arthroplasty practice pattern influence reasons for revision a study of 000000000009 000000000639 cases","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/2633-1462.412.BJO-2023-0096.R1","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["K. Gromov discloses funding for the the organizational set-up for the entire fast-track project, including dedicated research at all centres, data monitoring, and follow-up on complications, from Novo Nordisk foundation (Grant no. NNF21SA0073760). In addition, the author also discloses grants or contracts from Zimmer Biomet, which are unrelated to this article. L. E. Rasmussen declares consulting fees from Stryker, which is unrelated. A. Troelsen reports research support, consultig fees, and being an advisory board member for Zimmer Biomet and Denmark, and payment or honoraria for lectures, presentations, speakers bureaus, manuscript writing or educational events from Zimmer Biomet, all of which is also unrelated to this work."],"id":"S02-091.13-704145","identifier":[{"id":"85178929325","type":"scopus"},{"id":"38043568","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC10693936","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["au-6472ecb3-ad41-4265-b6d0-a523a82071db","sdu-4f2892c0-b507-4c70-bc4d-97a63a7f78cc"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2DD6B6DBC38CB75773C590EBAA5DBE9F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/251333627/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1302/2633-1462.412.BJO-2023-0096.R1","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Amager and Hvidovre Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universit