y of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-16cff872-d159-4667-9c85-f957df9c0e3a","au-49bcfb67-0c0d-4f23-a346-fc1015fabaed","ku-357781f5-bd54-4f4e-b7e2-66e29a4be965","sdu-dded98f3-12ae-4b02-a0b5-73bef0734931"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term effects of restriction of intravenous fluid in adult ICU patients with septic shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.92-813304","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Risk stratification in patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) is important to facilitate guideline-directed therapies. The Calculator of Absolute Stroke Risk (CARS) scheme enables an individualized estimation of 1-year absolute risk of stroke in AF. We aimed to investigate the predicted and absolute risks of ischaemic stroke, and evaluate whether CARS (and CHA2DS2-VASc score) may be useful for identifying high risk patients with AF despite contemporary treatment. METHODS: We utilized the EORP-AF General Long-Term Registry which prospectively enrolled patients with AF from 250 centres across 27 participating European countries. Patients with sufficient data to determine CARS and CHA2DS2-VASc score, and reported outcomes of ischaemic stroke were included in this analysis. The primary outcome of ischaemic stroke was recorded over a 2-year follow-up period. RESULTS: A total of 9444 patients were included (mean age 69.1 [±11.4] years; 3776 [40.0%] females). There was a high uptake (87.9%) of anticoagulation therapy, predominantly with vitamin K antagonist (50.0%). Over a mean follow-up period of 24 months, there were a total of 101 (1.1%) ischaemic stroke events. In the entire cohort, the median CARS and absolute annual risks of ischaemic stroke were 2.60 (IQR 1.60-4.00) and 0.53% (95%CI 0.43-0.64%), respectively. There was no statistical difference between the predictive performance of CARS and CHA2DS2-VASc score (0.621 [95%CI 0.563-0.678] vs. 0.626 [95%CI 0.573-0.680], P = 0.725). CONCLUSION: Contemporary management of AF was associated with a low risk of ischaemic stroke. CARS and CHA2DS2-VASc score may be useful to identify high risk patients despite treatment who may benefit from more aggressive treatment and follow-up.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Ding, Wern Yew","Blomström-Lundqvist, Carina","Fauchier, Laurent","Marin, Francisco","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Boriani, Giuseppe","Lip, Gregory Y H","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-103665"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["France","Italy","Serbia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital of Modena","University of Belgrade","University of Liverpool","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia","Örebro University"],"keyword":["Aged","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Atrial fibrillation","Brain Ischemia diagnosis","CARS","CHA DS VASc score","CHA2DS2 VASc score","EORP AF","Female","Humans","Ischaemic stroke","Ischemic stroke","Male","Registries","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Stroke diagnosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"contemporary management of atrial fibrillation and the predicted vs absolute risk of ischaemic stroke despite treatment a report from esc ehra eorp af long term general registry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euac214","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-103665","identifier":[{"id":"85148254244","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36427202","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b8b2f866-8cc6-4b29-a48e-fd9450a3d869"],"keyword":["Absolute stroke risk","Aged","Anticoagulants/therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation/complications","Atrial fibrillation","Brain Ischemia/diagnosis","CARS","CHA DS -VASc score","CHA2DS2-VASc score","EORP-AF","Female","Humans","Ischaemic stroke","Ischemic Stroke","Male","Predictive stroke risk","Registries","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Stroke/diagnosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-29E48D8BD713A5EDFCCC9C9D3D1DDCCA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/europace/euac214","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/539418873/euac214.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of liverpool","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Liverpool","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"liverpool heart and chest hospital nhs foundation trust","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"örebro university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Örebro University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fr","key":"hôpital trousseau chu de tours","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"es","key":"university of murcia","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Murcia","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"es","key":"hospital virgen de la arrixaca","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"es","key":"instituto murciano de investigación biosanitaria","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Instituto Mur