pau","last":"Espelund","name":"Espelund, Ulrick Skipper","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Vibeke","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"9ef41012-736f-44df-90ab-54346f56c3c2","name":"Jørgensen, Vibeke L.","name_org":"Jørgensen, Vibeke","rank":27,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Nicolai","key":"haasepau","last":"Haase","name":"Haase, Nicolai","rank":28,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":29,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36263897"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14157","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"1","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"76-85","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141525308"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3d18c52a-b741-4e39-983e-7ec7883b3b97"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Thromboembolic and bleeding events in ICU patients with COVID-19 : A nationwide, observational study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-429942","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Probiotics are intended to improve gastrointestinal health when consumed. However, the probiotics marketed today only colonize the densely populated gut to a limited extent. Bacteriophages comprise the majority of viruses in the human gut virome and there are strong indications that they play important roles in shaping the gut microbiome. Here, we investigate the use of fecal virome transplantation (FVT, sterile filtrated feces) as a mean to alter the gut microbiome composition to lead the way for persistent colonization of two types of probiotics: Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus GG (LGG) representing a well-established probiotic and Akkermansia muciniphila (AKM) representing a putative next-generation probiotic. Male and female C57BL/6NTac mice were cohoused in pairs from 4 weeks of age and received the following treatment by oral gavage at week 5 and 6: AKM+FVT, LGG+FVT, probiotic sham (Pro-sham)+FVT, LGG+Saline, AKM+Saline, and control (Pro-sham+Saline). The FVT donor material originated from mice with high relative abundance of A. muciniphila. All animals were terminated at age 9 weeks. The FVT treatment did not increase the relative abundance of the administered LGG or AKM in the recipient mice. Instead FVT significantly (p < 0.05) increased the abundance of naturally occurring A.muciniphila compared to the control. This highlights the potential of propagating the existing commensal “probiotics” that have already permanently colonized the gut. Being co-housed male and female, a fraction of the female mice became pregnant. Unexpectedly, the FVT treated mice were found to have a significantly (p < 0.05) higher fertility rate independent of probiotic administration. These preliminary observations urge for follow-up studies investigating interactions between the gut microbiome and fertility.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck","Mentzel, Caroline M. Junker","Danielsen, Malene Refslund","Jakobsen, Rasmus Riemer","Zachariassen, Line F.","Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","Brunse, Anders","Hansen, Lars H.","Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","Hansen, Axel Kornerup","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-679489"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Akkermansia muciniphila","Fecal virome transplantation","Fertility","Gut microbiome","Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fecal virome transfer improves proliferation of commensal gut i akkermansia muciniphila i and unexpectedly enhances the fertility rate in laboratory mice","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19490976.2023.2208504","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-679489","identifier":[{"id":"37150906","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000982442600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85157966363","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10167882","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-f5de68c0-b98d-459f-b8f1-9c702e6031e6"],"keyword":["Akkermansia muciniphila","Fecal virome transplantation","Fertility","Gut microbiome","Lacticaseibacillus rhamnosus","Probiotic engraftment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E31202609AB16E9EBB2B6D991DA7B74A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/347695878/Fecal_virome_transfer_improves_proliferation_of_commensal_gut_Akkermansia_muciniphila_and_unexpectedly_enhances_the_fertility_rate_in_laboratory_mice.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/19490976.2023.2208504","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Torben Sølbeck","key":"rasmussentorbensølbeckpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37b31216-f69f-4ff3-bc9c-ffd6b36fc003","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck","orcid":"0000-0002-9907-8953","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline M.Junker","key":"mentzelcarolinemjunkerpau","last":"Mentzel","locid":"2f4bbdfb-bd14-4dc0-9280-4acf3c694239","name":"Mentzel, Caroline M. Junker","name_org":"Mentzel, Caroline M.Junker","orcid":"0000-0003-4688-7367","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Malene Refslund","key":"danielsenmalenerefslundpau","last":"Danielsen","name":"Danielsen, Malene Refslund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Riemer","key":"jakobsenrasmusriemerpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"80dbaf1b-0cb5-48fe-ab84-4254c687ba73","name":"Jakobsen, Rasmus Riemer","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Line Sidsel Fisker","key":"zachariassenlinefpau","last":"Zachariassen","locid":"cdafe75d-cfc9-4fca-adfe-20ae0c542b57","name":"Zachariassen, Line F.","name_org":"Zachariassen, Line Sidsel Fisker","orcid":"0000-0001-5425-9841","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josue Leonardo","key":"castromejíajosuélpau","last":"Castro Mejia","locid":"a37230a5-7baa-4222-a2f0-fb47090dd0ed","name":"Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","name_org":"Castro Mejia, Josue Leonardo","orcid":"0000-0002-1416-8205","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"brunseanderspau","last":"Brunse","locid":"1413cafd-59f7-49d5-9c9b-00ff98f1df9c","name":"Brunse, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0199-3417","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Hestbjerg","key":"hansenlarshpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"2e041f09-bf9d-434a-b82a-d6e2763bb262","name":"Hansen, Lars H.","name_org":"Hansen, Lars Hestbjerg","orcid":"0000-0003-0027-1524","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Camilla Hartmann Friis","key":"hansencamillahartmannfriispau","last":"Hansen","locid":"d7f25dbd-3efc-483b-9805-8909e9597652","name":"Hansen, Camilla Hartmann Friis","orcid":"0000-0002-1860-385X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Axel Kornerup","key":"hansenaxelkorneruppau","last":"Hansen","locid":"ecc439ea-5c9b-4e25-814a-3ee8960bc0d0","name":"Hansen, Axel Kornerup","orcid":"0000-0003-1575-2507","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Dennis Sandris","key":"nielsendennissandrispau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"08539a0e-05f4-454e-ad2a-de195363dbd1","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Sandris","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37150906"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/19490976.2023.2208504","issn":["19490976","19490984"],"issn_org":["19490976"],"issue":"1","journal":"Gut Microbes","paperid":"2208504","status":"p","title":"Gut Microbes","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85157966363"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f5de68c0-b98d-459f-b8f1-9c702e6031e6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fecal virome transfer improves proliferation of commensal gut <i>Akkermansia muciniphila </i>and unexpectedly enhances the fertility rate in laboratory mice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-679489","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"During recent years, electrofuels (fuels from electricity, water, and carbon) have gained increased interest as substitute for fossil fuels in all energy and chemical sectors. The feasibility of electrofuels has been assessed from a range of aspects but no study has assessed the land area needed if scaling up the production based on renewables. The amount of land on Earth is limited and the competition for land, in a long-term perspective, imposes a risk of, e.g., increased food prices and biodiversity losses. The aim of this paper is to assess how much land area it would require if all fossil fuels were substituted by electrofuels (‘All electrofuel’-scenario) and compare this with the area needed if all fossil fuels were substituted by bioenergy (‘All biomass’-scenario) or by electricity (‘All electric’-scenario). Each scenario represents extreme cases towards fully renewable energy systems to outline the theoretical area needed. Main conclusions are (1) the electricity demand, if substituting all fossil fuels with electrofuels, is huge (1540 EJ) but technically obtainable, demanding 1.1% of the Earth's surface, for solar panels, in the most optimistic case, and (2) the sustainable technical potential for biomass cannot alone substitute all fossil fuels, unless radical energy demand reductions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Winther Mortensen, Anders","Dalgas Rasmussen, Kasper","Grahn, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-680436"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grahn, Maria"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chalmers University of Technology"],"keyword":["E Fuels","Hydrogen","Power to X","PtX","Synthetic fuels"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how replacing fossil fuels with electrofuels could influence the demand for renewable energy and land area","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.segy.2023.100107","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work was supported by a research grant ( 9455 ) from VILLUM FONDEN . Funding has further been received through two Swedish competence centra (1) The Competence Centre for Catalysis (KCK) which is hosted by Chalmers University of Technology and financially supported by the Swedish Energy Agency (Project No. 52689-1 ) and the member companies Johnson Matthey, Perstorp, Powercell, Preem, Scania CV, Umicore, and Volvo Group, and (2) The Competence Centre TECHnologies and innovations For a future green HYDROGEN economy (TechForH2) also hosted by Chalmers University of Technology and is financially supported by the Swedish Energy Agency ( P2021-90268 ) and the member companies Volvo, Scania, Siemens Energy, GKN Aerospace, PowerCell, Oxeon, RISE, Stena Rederier AB, Johnson Matthey, and Insplorion."],"id":"S01-000.00-680436","identifier":[{"id":"85163139200","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-7e52de16-2541-42e6-ae50-7ec47aa2a9ee"],"keyword":["Area efficiency","Area footprint","E-Fuels","Fully renewable energy systems","Hydrogen","PTX","Power-to-X","Synthetic fuels"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F20C1DF4C4B39AAEE5CC9C44DEEF3AE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/235184889/1_s2.0_S266695522300014X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.segy.2023.100107","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT), SDU Life Cycle Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"chalmers university of technology","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Chalmers University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Winther","key":"rennuitmortensenpau","last":"Rennuit-Mortensen","locid":"ebbcbd07-3eef-424a-b1de-c445aff55b37","name":"Winther Mortensen, Anders","name_org":"Rennuit-Mortensen, Anders Winther","orcid":"0000-0001-9510-4854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"dalgasrasmussenpau","last":"Dalgas Rasmussen","locid":"75d6a28c-74bb-4f8a-8455-43130eeed994","name":"Dalgas Rasmussen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8209-2871","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"grahnpau","last":"Grahn","name":"Grahn, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.segy.2023.100107","issn":["26669552"],"journal":"Smart Energy","paperid":"100107","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Smart Energy","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163139200"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-7e52de16-2541-42e6-ae50-7ec47aa2a9ee"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"How replacing fossil fuels with electrofuels could influence the demand for renewable energy and land area","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-680436","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
