Dan A.","key":"klaerkepau","last":"Klaerke","locid":"e41a45df-206e-4d33-b4fc-cd83cc788418","name":"Klærke, Dan Arne","name_org":"Klaerke, Dan A.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Jes","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"c5fe564b-1354-4d3c-8173-9778df35d33f","name":"Olesen, Jes","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 8 9","country":"dk","first":"David M.","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"974319d1-cbac-46f5-b3f3-9801a48206c9","name":"Kristensen, David Møbjerg","name_org":"Kristensen, David M.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37909725"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1289/ehp12413","issn":["00916765","15529924"],"issn_org":["00916765"],"issue":"11","journal":"Environmental Health Perspectives","pages":"117003","paperid":"117003","status":"p","title":"Environmental Health Perspectives","volume":"131"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85175878443"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Roskilde University","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6585cf84-7c26-4026-842c-afaf2cf96f8a","ruc-7019ef01-09ec-4e88-9f74-5daa76969078"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Xenobiotic Exposure and Migraine-Associated Signaling : A Multimethod Experimental Study Exploring Cellular Assays in Combination with Ex Vivo and In Vivo Mouse Models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.60-716418","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To investigate the effects of lower versus higher oxygenation targets in adult intensive care unit (ICU) patients with hypoxaemic respiratory failure after cardiac arrest. Methods: Subgroup analysis of the international Handling Oxygenation Targets in the ICU (HOT-ICU) trial which randomised 2928 adults with acute hypoxaemia to targets of arterial oxygenation of 8 kPa or 12 kPa in the ICU for up to 90 days. Here, we report all outcomes up to one year in the subgroup of patients enrolled after cardiac arrest. Results: The HOT-ICU trial included 335 patients after cardiac arrest: 149 in the lower-oxygenation group and 186 in the higher-oxygenation group. At 90 days, 96/147 patients (65.3%) in the lower-oxygenation group and 111/185 patients (60.0%) in the higher-oxygenation group had died (adjusted relative risk (RR) 1.09, 95% confidence interval (CI) 0.92–1.28, p = 0.32); similar results were found at one year (adjusted RR 1.05, 95% CI 0.90–1.21, p = 0.53). Serious adverse events (SAEs) in the ICU occurred in 23% of patients in the lower-oxygenation group and 38% in the higher-oxygenation group (adjusted RR 0.61, 95% CI 0.43–0.86, p = 0.005); the difference was mainly due to more new episodes of shock in the higher-oxygenation group. No statistically significant differences were observed in other secondary outcomes. Conclusion: A lower oxygenation target in adult ICU patients with hypoxaemic respiratory failure after cardiac arrest did not result in lower mortality, but fewer SAEs occurred in this group compared to the higher-oxygenation group. All analyses are exploratory only, large-scale trials are needed for confirmation. Clinical Trial Registry: Clinicaltrials.gov number NCT03174002 (registered May 30, 2017); EudraCT 2017-000632-34 (registered February 14, 2017).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Crescioli, Elena","Lass Klitgaard, Thomas","Perner, Anders","Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-685638"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Crescioli, Elena"],"keyword":["Intensive Care Units","Mortality","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Post cardiac arrest syndrome","Quality of Life","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lower versus higher oxygenation targets in hypoxaemic icu patients after cardiac arrest","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109838","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The HOT-ICU trial was supported by a grant from Innovation Fund Denmark (4108-00011A), by Aalborg University Hospital, by grants from the Regions of Denmark (EMN-2017-00901 and EMN-2019-01055), by a grant from the Obel Family Foundation (25457), by the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine, and by the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl. No additional funding was provided for this sub-study."],"id":"S02-100.00-685638","identifier":[{"id":"37196799","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85160085484","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-50806a80-05f4-4e1b-acb8-6163d682dabc","ku-c94d6550-06a2-43d2-a4b3-34b5c3a8b2dd"],"keyword":["Intensive care units","Mortality","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Post-Cardiac Arrest Syndrome","Quality of life","Randomized Controlled Trial"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-C5DB5D919C00B00C32135C75BDF6EB77"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/366001182/1_s2.0_S030095722300151X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/538892940/1-s2.0-S030095722300151X-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109838","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elena","key":"cresciolipau","last":"Crescioli","locid":"7cb438f9-7215-4caa-835a-9743ead87ba7","name":"Crescioli, Elena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas","key":"lassklitgaardpau","last":"Lass Klitgaard","locid":"f3e0e4b8-0772-4f4f-8be2-b99763b3917c","name":"Lass Klitgaard, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8781-1206","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Olav","key":"lilleholtschjørringpau","last":"Lilleholt Schjørring","locid":"7dac619e-9b5c-46ac-9170-10ac13165da5","name":"Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","name_org":"Lilleholt Schjørring, Olav","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil","key":"steenrasmussenpau","last":"Steen Rasmussen","locid":"3162c449-94c3-4d28-8dbb-c134d6eb76e1","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","name_org":"Steen Rasmussen, Bodil","orcid":"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37196799"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.resuscitation.2023.109838","issn":["03009572","18731570"],"issn_org":["03009572"],"journal":"Resuscitation","paperid":"109838","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"188"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85160085484"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-50806a80-05f4-4e1b-acb8-6163d682dabc","ku-c94d6550-06a2-43d2-a4b3-34b5c3a8b2dd"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Lower versus higher oxygenation targets in hypoxaemic ICU patients after cardiac arrest","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-685638","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Trials in critically ill patients increasingly focus on days alive without life support (DAWOLS) or days alive out of hospital (DAOOH) and health-related quality of life (HRQoL). DAWOLS and DAOOH convey more information than mortality and are simpler and faster to collect than HRQoL. However, whether these outcomes are associated with HRQoL is uncertain. We thus aimed to assess the associations between DAWOLS and DAOOH and long-term HRQoL. Methods: Secondary analysis of the COVID STEROID 2 trial including adults with COVID-19 and severe hypoxaemia and the Handling Oxygenation Targets in the Intensive Care Unit (HOT-ICU) trial including adult intensive care unit patients with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure. Associations between DAWOLS and DAOOH at day 28 and 90 and long-term HRQoL (after 6 or 12 months) using the EuroQol 5-dimension 5-level survey (EQ VAS and EQ-5D-5L index values) were assessed using flexible models and evaluated using measures of fit and prediction adequacy in both datasets (comprising internal performance and external validation), non-parametric correlation coefficients and graphical presentations. Results: We found no strong associations between DAWOLS or DAOOH and HRQoL in survivors at HRQoL-follow-up (615 and 1476 patients, respectively). There was substantial variability in outcomes, and predictions from the best fitted models were poor both internally and externally in the other trial dataset, which also showed inadequate calibration. Moderate associations were found when including non-survivors, although predictions remained uncertain and calibration inadequate. Conclusion: DAWOLS and DAOOH were poorly associated with HRQoL in adult survivors of severe or critical illness included in the COVID STEROID 2 and HOT-ICU trials.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Granholm, Anders","Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Jensen, Aksel Karl Georg","Kaas-Hansen, Benjamin Skov","Munch, Marie Warrer","Lass Klitgaard, Thomas","Crescioli, Elena","Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Strøm, Thomas","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Møller, Morten Hylander"],"cuid":["S03-091.15-672250"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Granholm, Anders"],"keyword":["Adult","Covid 19","Critical care","Days alive out of hospital","Days alive without life support","Follow up","Health related quality of life","Hospitals","Humans","Hypoxia","Intensive Care Units","Outcomes","Quality of Life","TRIALS","outcome selection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between days alive without life support out of hospital and health related quality of life","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14231","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Sygeforsikringen \"danmark\"; Grosserer Jakob Ehrenreich og Hustru Grete Ehrenreichs Fond; Dagmar Marshalls Fond; the Novo Nordisk Foundation; Rigshospitalet; the Innovation Fund Denmark; Aalborg University Hospital; the Regions of Denmark; the Obel Family Foundation; the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine; the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl Funding information This study was conducted as part of the Intensive Care Platform Trial (INCEPT; www.incept.dk ) research programme, which has received funding by Sygeforsikringen ‘danmark’, Grosserer Jakob Ehrenreich og Hustru Grete Ehrenreichs Fond and Dagmar Marshalls Fond. The COVID STEROID 2 trial was funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and supported by Rigshospitalet. The HOT‐ICU trial was funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark, Aalborg University Hospital, the Regions of Denmark, the Obel Family Foundation, the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine and the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl. None of the funders had any influence on planning, analysis, reporting or decision to publish regarding this study.","We thank all involved in the COVID STEROID 2 and HOT-ICU trials, including patients and their relatives, clinical staff, investigators and research staffs and funders of the COVID STEROID 2 trial, the HOT-ICU trial and the INCEPT research programme. The Department of Intensive Care at Rigshospitalet has received funding for other research projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Pfizer, Ferring and Fresenius Kabi and conducts contract research for AM-Pharma. The Department of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care at Aalborg University Hospital has received funding for other research projects from the Novo Nordisk Foundation and conducts contract research for AM-Pharma. This study was conducted as part of the Intensive Care Platform Trial (INCEPT; www.incept.dk ) research programme, which has received funding by Sygeforsikringen ‘danmark’, Grosserer Jakob Ehrenreich og Hustru Grete Ehrenreichs Fond and Dagmar Marshalls Fond. The COVID STEROID 2 trial was funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation and supported by Rigshospitalet. The HOT‐ICU trial was funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark, Aalborg University Hospital, the Regions of Denmark, the Obel Family Foundation, the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine and the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl. None of the funders had any influence on planning, analysis, reporting or decision to publish regarding this study. Sygeforsikringen \"danmark\"; Grosserer Jakob Ehrenreich og Hustru Grete Ehrenreichs Fond; Dagmar Marshalls Fond; the Novo Nordisk Foundation; Rigshospitalet; the Innovation Fund Denmark; Aalborg University Hospital; the Regions of Denmark; the Obel Family Foundation; the Danish Society of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine; the Intensive Care Symposium Hindsgavl Funding information"],"id":"S03-091.15-672250","identifier":[{"id":"000956439600001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85151089883","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36915265","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-204384da-b774-4e04-a8ad-b73f182235f0","ku-bb873983-5c88-4f85-b35c-765170360d5a","sdu-1b7ebe61-87cc-4874-b651-ca8d9bddfe0e"],"keyword":["Adult","COVID-19","FOLLOW-UP","Hospitals","Humans","Hypoxia","Intensive Care Units","OUTCOMES","Quality of Life","TRIALS","VENTILATOR-FREE DAYS","critical care","days alive out of hospital","days alive without life support","health-related quality of life","outcome selection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-74DBCBEBA1FAFB259FC87ADA7E7E13A3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14231","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/356957001/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/226578677/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2023_Granholm_Association_between_days_alive_without_life_support_out_of_hospital_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/536127469/Acta_Anaesthesiol_Scand_2023_Granholm_Association_between_days_alive_without_life_support_out_of_hospital_and.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capi