"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 6","first":"Morten Hylander","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"9463b017-3c43-470d-b95b-cf3cba8a27d4","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","name_org":"Moller, Morten Hylander","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Hylander","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Morten Hylander","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36915265"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.14231","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"762-771","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"67"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85151089883"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-204384da-b774-4e04-a8ad-b73f182235f0","ku-bb873983-5c88-4f85-b35c-765170360d5a","sdu-1b7ebe61-87cc-4874-b651-ca8d9bddfe0e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Association between days alive without life support/out of hospital and health-related quality of life","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-091.15-672250","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Abdominal aortic aneurysm (AAA) is a common disease with substantial heritability. In this study, we performed a genome-wide association meta-analysis from 14 discovery cohorts and uncovered 141 independent associations, including 97 previously unreported loci. A polygenic risk score derived from meta-analysis explained AAA risk beyond clinical risk factors. Genes at AAA risk loci indicate involvement of lipid metabolism, vascular development and remodeling, extracellular matrix dysregulation and inflammation as key mechanisms in AAA pathogenesis. These genes also indicate overlap between the development of AAA and other monogenic aortopathies, particularly via transforming growth factor β signaling. Motivated by the strong evidence for the role of lipid metabolism in AAA, we used Mendelian randomization to establish the central role of nonhigh-density lipoprotein cholesterol in AAA and identified the opportunity for repurposing of proprotein convertase, subtilisin/kexin-type 9 (PCSK9) inhibitors. This was supported by a study demonstrating that PCSK9 loss of function prevented the development of AAA in a preclinical mouse model.","author_count":98,"contributors":["Roychowdhury, Tanmoy","Klarin, Derek","Levin, Michael G.","Spin, Joshua M.","Rhee, Yae Hyun","Deng, Alicia","Headley, Colwyn A.","Tsao, Noah L.","Gellatly, Corry","Zuber, Verena","Shen, Fred","Hornsby, Whitney E.","Laursen, Ina Holst","Verma, Shefali S.","Locke, Adam E.","Einarsson, Gudmundur","Thorleifsson, Gudmar","Graham, Sarah E.","Dikilitas, Ozan","Pattee, Jack W.","Judy, Renae L.","Pauls-Verges, Ferran","Nielsen, Jonas B.","Wolford, Brooke N.","Brumpton, Ben M.","Dilmé, Jaume","Peypoch, Olga","Juscafresa, Laura Calsina","Edwards, Todd L.","Li, Dadong","Banasik, Karina","Brunak, Søren","Jacobsen, Rikke Vita Borre","Garcia-Barrio, Minerva T.","Zhang, Jifeng","Rasmussen, Lars M.","Lee, Regent","Handa, Ashok","Wanhainen, Anders","Mani, Kevin","Lindholt, Jes S.","Obel, Lasse M.","Strauss, Ew