{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Patients with obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy (HCM) often experience symptoms of heart failure upon exertion despite having normal left ventricular (LV) ejection fractions. Longitudinal strain (LS) may be a more sensitive marker of systolic dysfunction in patients with LV hypertrophy. The aims of this study were to characterize LV segmental LS and global LS (GLS) at rest and during exercise and to assess if first-line treatment with β-blockers improves LV systolic performance. METHODS: Twenty-nine patients with obstructive HCM and New York Heart Association functional class ≥ II symptoms were enrolled in a double-blind, placebo-controlled, randomized crossover trial. Patients received metoprolol 150 mg or placebo for two consecutive 2-week periods in random order. Echocardiographic assessment with speckle-tracking-derived LS was performed at rest and during peak exercise at the end of each treatment period. RESULTS: During placebo treatment, resting values of segmental LS showed an apical-basal difference of -10.3% (95% CI, -12.7% to -7.8%; P < .0001), with a severely abnormal value of the basal segment of -9.3 ± 4.2%. Treatment with metoprolol was associated with more negative LS values of the apical segment (-2.8%; 95% CI, -4.2% to -1.3%; P < .001) and the mid segment (-1.1%; 95% CI, -2.0% to -0.3%; P = .007). During peak exercise there was a deterioration in LV GLS, but treatment with metoprolol was associated with more negative peak exercise LV GLS (-1.3 %; 95% CI, -2.6% to -0.1%; P = .03). CONCLUSIONS: Systolic performance assessed by LV GLS showed impaired values at rest and during exercise, with severely depressed values of the basal and mid segments. Treatment with metoprolol improved LV GLS upon exercise, indicating a beneficial effect of β-blocker treatment on LV systolic function.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Dybro, Anne Mette","Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","Andersen, Mads Jønsson","Jensen, Morten Kvistholm","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-231590"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Exercise","Longitudinal strain","Metoprolol","Myocardial function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"metoprolol improves left ventricular longitudinal strain at rest and during exercise in obstructive hypertrophic cardiomyopathy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85140312047","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-231590","identifier":[{"id":"36444740","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85140312047","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-b3342c01-4ed3-4d9e-ac3a-de81ee612efb"],"keyword":["Exercise","Longitudinal strain","Metoprolol","Myocardial function","Obstructive HCM"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-90FC27A3A5916252133E0189CA3076CE"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne M","key":"dybropau","last":"Dybro","locid":"2e78d319-fc37-4dc3-9030-130d2d0c8a25","name":"Dybro, Anne Mette","name_org":"Dybro, Anne M","orcid":"0000-0003-3175-9725","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten B","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"4bae5bd6-40ab-4bd9-a7ba-fc3d7fe970c7","name":"Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","name_org":"Rasmussen, Torsten B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Roni R","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"896f4a21-d29c-4ad9-b0ef-4e7f8616c234","name":"Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","name_org":"Nielsen, Roni R","orcid":"0000-0001-9228-3869","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders L D","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7e7debe0-e391-4c37-9cbd-c136c98fc08a","name":"Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","name_org":"Pedersen, Anders L D","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads J","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"19d72cda-3d6c-4f48-9d4b-6fe5dee888ba","name":"Andersen, Mads Jønsson","name_org":"Andersen, Mads J","orcid":"0000-0002-9320-8227","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten K","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"da83202a-402f-4457-a557-3a787489909f","name":"Jensen, Morten Kvistholm","name_org":"Jensen, Morten K","orcid":"0000-0003-1144-4603","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen H","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"ec1d0fd4-f6ae-4071-907f-1448dfe832fe","name":"Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","name_org":"Poulsen, Steen H","orcid":"0000-0002-9586-835X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36444740"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.echo.2022.09.008","issn":["08947317","10976795"],"issn_org":["08947317"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the American Society of Echocardiography","pages":"196-204","publisher":"Elsevier Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Society of Echocardiography","volume":"36"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140312047"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b3342c01-4ed3-4d9e-ac3a-de81ee612efb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Metoprolol Improves Left Ventricular Longitudinal Strain at Rest and during Exercise in Obstructive Hypertrophic Cardiomyopathy","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-231590","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Moe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274854"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"jacobi and kierkegaard two critics of modern thinking and he beginning of existential philosophy","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-274854","ids":["au-ff036cb8-683b-442a-8d37-faad106c636f"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-3A365C09AC56087064F41F4735EE2FF0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Philosophy, subject"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Moe","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"e9773c7c-a46d-4591-b659-4151bea40a43","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Moe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1017/9781009244978.016","eisbn":["9781009244978"],"pages":"200-244","place":"Cambridge","publisher":"Cambridge University Press","status":"p","subtitle":"Religion, Philosophy and the Reason at the Crux of Modernity","title":"Friedrich Jacobi and the End of Enlightenment"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ff036cb8-683b-442a-8d37-faad106c636f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Jacobi and Kierkegaard : Two Critics of Modern Thinking and he Beginning of Existential Philosophy","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-274854","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Background: Viral shedding and neutralizing antibody (NAb) dynamics among patients hospitalized with severe coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) and immune correlates of protection have been key questions throughout the pandemic. We investigated the duration of reverse transcriptase-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) positivity, infectious viral shedding and NAb titers as well as the association between NAb titers and disease severity in hospitalized COVID-19 patients in Denmark 2020–2021. Materials and methods: Prospective single-center observational cohort study of 47 hospitalized COVID-19 patients. Oropharyngeal swabs were collected at eight time points during the initial 30 days of inclusion. Serum samples were collected after a median time of 7 (IQR 5 – 10), 37 (IQR 35 – 38), 97 (IQR 95 – 100), and 187 (IQR 185 – 190) days after symptom onset. NAb titers were determined by an in-house live virus microneutralization assay. Viral culturing was performed in Vero E6 cells. Results: Patients with high disease severity had higher mean log2 NAb titers at day 37 (1.58, 95% CI [0.34 –2.81]), 97 (2.07, 95% CI [0.53–3.62]) and 187 (2.49, 95% CI [0.20– 4.78]) after symptom onset, compared to patients with low disease severity. Peak viral load (0.072, 95% CI [− 0.627 – 0.728]), expressed as log10 SARS-CoV-2 copies/ml, was not associated with disease severity. Virus cultivation attempts were unsuccessful in almost all (60/61) oropharyngeal samples collected shortly after hospital admission. Conclusions: We document an association between high disease severity and high mean NAb titers at days 37, 97 and 187 after symptom onset. However, peak viral load during admission was not associated with disease severity. Trial registration. The study is registered at https://clinicaltrials.gov/ (NCT05274373).","author_count":15,"contributors":["Sejdic, Adin","Frische, Anders","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Rasmussen, Lasse Dam","Trebbien, Ramona","Dungu, Arnold Matovu","Holler, Jon G.","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Eriksson, Robert","Søborg, Christian","Nielsen, Thyge Lynghøj","Fischer, Thea K.","Lindegaard, Birgitte","Franck, Kristina Træholt","Harboe, Zitta Barrella"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489293"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Disease severity","Neutralizing antibodies","Viral Load"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high titers of neutralizing sars cov 000000000002 antibodies six months after symptom onset are associated with increased severity in covid 000000000019 hospitalized patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12985-023-01974-8","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489293","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9875770","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85146878971","type":"scopus"},{"id":"36698135","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a054084b-1410-4b15-ba42-fbdf61352f8b"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Disease severity","Neutralizing antibodies","Viral culturing","Viral load"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A2A91AB5820DEDED2B15B35C30DC1AD8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12985-023-01974-8","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/336447493/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","E