ced genetic diversity in Cape buffalo","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671152","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","Kragh Hansen, Johanne","Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","Thiele, Maja"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-671858"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl"],"keyword":["Intervention","Narrativ medicin","Stigmatisering"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narrativ medicin som modvægt til stigma og selvstigma om læse og skriveværkstederne i decide projektet på odense universitetshospital","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-671858","ids":["sdu-c4cd925c-dbc1-4578-8a41-a5e8a81c844a"],"keyword":["intervention","narrativ medicin","stigmatisering"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-68757E1B5113AAE6D7F0B8B7E23B7FC5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Literature","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Uses of Literature"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6612df8e-d9f9-4004-b959-a9c30b0762a5","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7718-5208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Johanne","key":"kraghansenpau","last":"Krag Hansen","locid":"8b87c873-1ff1-4f76-8866-39dd23e8b368","name":"Kragh Hansen, Johanne","name_org":"Krag Hansen, Johanne","orcid":"0000-0003-2898-5369","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette Søgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"63429b82-37e7-4fc5-84dd-f73ef3f5658a","name":"Nielsen, Anette Søgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8569-4165","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"thielepau","last":"Thiele","locid":"b876b26d-ab19-4944-ad68-70d557cf0b56","name":"Thiele, Maja","orcid":"0000-0003-1854-1924","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09065407"],"issue":"1","journal":"Bibliotek for Læger","pages":"40-59","publisher":"Lægeforeningen","status":"p","title":"Bibliotek for Læger","volume":"2023"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c4cd925c-dbc1-4578-8a41-a5e8a81c844a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Narrativ medicin som modvægt til stigma og selvstigma : Om læse- og skriveværkstederne i DECIDE-projektet på Odense Universitetshospital","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-671858","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"The Ordovician of Scandinavia (i.e. Denmark, Norway and Sweden) has been investigated for over two centuries and, through time, various chronostratigraphic schemes have been introduced, facilitating regional correlation. However, a modern chronostratigraphy has never been proposed. Here, we delineate ten regional stages for the Ordovician of Scandinavia, comprising, in ascending order, the Slemmestadian, Ottenbyan, Billingenian, Volkhovian, Kundan, Segerstadian, Dalbyan, Moldåan, Jerrestadian and Tommarpian. We propose to discontinue the use of the term Hunnebergian Regional Stage despite its Scandinavian origin; this interval is included in the new Ottenbyan Stage. The base of each stage, as (re)defined here, is selected to coincide with the appearance of a characteristic fossil taxon and delimited at the top by the base of the overlying stage. The stage boundaries generally coincide with or approximate to significant changes in the depositional environment that are recognizable across Scandinavia from the carbonate platform to the foreland basin. Local efficacy has been the primary criterion for the recognition of Scandinavian stage boundaries rather than approximating to the global or East Baltic stage boundaries. It is proposed to abolish the Baltoscandian regional series and subseries, as correlation with the global series is sufficiently precise to make these higher rank regional schemes redundant.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Nielsen, Arne Thorshøj","Ahlberg, Per","Ebbestad, Jan Ove R.","Hammer, Øyvind","Harper, David Alexander Taylor","Lindskog, Anders","Mac Ørum Rasmussen, Christian","Stouge, Svend"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-677715"],"filters":{"added":"2023-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Durham University","Lund University","University of Oslo","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the ordovician of scandinavia a revised regional stage classification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1144/SP532-2022-157","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-677715","identifier":[{"id":"85167697142","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-22609073-9785-419a-a13d-c3d881709a9c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6F542F1DB4BE8D3BEC3D5184CA6BE015"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/356959386/The_Ordovician_of_Scandinavia.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"rem","url":"https://www.lyellcollection.org/doi/10.1144/SP532-2022-157","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1144/SP532-2022-157","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Geosciences and Natural Resource Management, Geology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"durham university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Durham University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Arne Thorshøj","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"4cfac6f1-300e-4069-8cb5-fe41702bd81f","name":"Nielsen, Arne Thorshøj","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per","key":"ahlbergpau","last":"Ahlberg","name":"Ahlberg, Per","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Jan Ove R.","key":"ebbestadpau","last":"Ebbestad","name":"Ebbestad, Jan Ove R.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Øyvind","key":"hammerpau","last":"Hammer","name":"Hammer, Øyvind","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"David Alexander Taylor","key":"harperpau","last":"Harper","name":"Harper, David Alexander Taylor","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"lindskogpau","last":"Lindskog","name":"Lindskog, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Mac Ørum","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0b668780-f8e1-4def-bc48-8c6f6a6a6e43","name":"Mac Ørum Rasmussen, Christian","name_org":"Rasmussen, Christian Mac Ørum","orcid":"0000-0003-2982-9931","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Svend","key":"stougepau","last":"Stouge","locid":"22487e67-6bd9-4920-8e1e-89b0f33fe4d5","name":"Stouge, Svend","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1144/sp532-2022-157","issn":["03058719","20414927"],"issn_org":["03058719"],"journal":"Geological Society Special Publication","pages":"267-315","status":"p","title":"Geological Society Special Publication","title_org":"Geological Society, London, Special Publications","volume":"532"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85167697142"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-22609073-9785-419a-a13d-c3d881709a9c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Ordovician of Scandinavia : a revised regional stage classification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-677715","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION. Since the beginning of the mpox (previously called monkeypox) outbreak in 2022, almost half of cases in Denmark have been diagnosed at the Department of Infectious Diseases, Copenhagen University Hospital – Amager and Hvidovre Hospital. This article describes the patient cohort seen at the Department with a view to increasing knowledge of mpox among colleagues who are most likely to identify future cases. METHODS. A retrospective observational study reporting patient characteristics, coinfections, clinical presentation and diagnostic delay among mpox cases diagnosed at the department between 23 May 2022 and 8 February 2023. Furthermore, a case report of a patient hospitalised with severe rectal pain is presented to highlight anorectal symptoms. RESULTS. A total of 86 patients were diagnosed with mpox, all were men who have sex with men, with a median age of 39 years. Twenty-six patients (31%) took HIV pre-exposure prophylaxis, and 20 patients (24%) were people living with HIV. All patients (100%) presented with lesions, most frequently on or around the genitals. Twenty-nine patients (35%) had anorectal discomfort or pain. Seven patients (10%) had chlamydia, 19 (26%) gonorrhoea and two (5%) syphilis. In 13 cases (15%), mpox was not suspected at the first medical consultation, mainly because symptoms were attributed to a gonorrhoeal coinfection. Five patients (6%) were hospitalised for a median of three days. CONCLUSION. As mpox may become endemic in Denmark, clinicians should remain aware of its symptoms and the risk of coinfection with sexually transmitted infections.","author_count":6,"contributors":["von Schreeb, Sebastian","Exsteen, Banoo Bakir","Zangenberg, Mike","Rasmussen, Morten","Fomsgaard, Anders","Kronborg, Gitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-689265"],"filters":{"added":"2023-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characteristics of 000000000086 individuals with mpox diagnosed at copenhagen university hospital","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/366344144/A09220544_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-689265","identifier":[{"id":"85163768833","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-04a116cc-1309-43ff-afec-50ea2c1149f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DB60C9F37AFB1678EB885C1052AA2FC7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/366344144/A09220544_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"rem","url":"https://content.ugeskriftet.dk/sites/default/files/2023-04/A09220544_WEB.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Amager and Hvidovre"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal medicine: infection medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Sebastian","key":"vonschreebpau","last":"von Schreeb","name":"von Schreeb, Sebastian","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Banoo Bakir","key":"exsteenpau","last":"Exsteen","name":"Exsteen, Banoo Bakir","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mike","key":"zangenbergpau","last":"Zangenberg","name":"Zangenberg, Mike","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardpau","last":"Fomsgaard","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"issue":"10","journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","pages":"988-996","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","title_org":"Ugeskrift for Laeger","volume":"185"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163768833"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-04a116cc-1309-43ff-afec-50ea2c1149f8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Characteristics of 86 individuals with mpox diagnosed at Copenhagen University Hospital","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-689265","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"One of the aspects that policymakers should consider when promoting cycling is the route choice behaviour of current cyclists. This study develops a behaviourally realistic route choice model for different types of everyday cyclists and cycling trips. The analysis is based on a large-scale crowdsourced dataset of GPS trajectories including 134,169 trips from 6,523 cyclists. The model is estimated as a joint path-size logit model and accounts for a wide range of bicycle network attributes, such as bicycle infrastructure type, land use, surface type or cycle superhighways. The findings of the model reveal, for example, that infrequent cyclists feel less safe on large roads, but this effect can be accommodated with protected bicycle tracks. Interaction with other motorised and non-motorised transport modes is found to be a deterring factor for cyclists and they prefer scenic water and green areas over high-rise urban environments, especially on long trips. The model performs very well on a hold-out sample, also when considering the similarity between the observed and predicted route, not only their binary consistency. Finally, we formulate several policy measures relevant to promote cycling. Building long, continuous stretches of dedicated, protected bicycle infrastructure outside of the high-rise urban environments has the greatest potential to make cycling attractive.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Łukawska, Mirosława","Paulsen, Mads","Rasmussen, Thomas Kjær","Jensen, Anders Fjendbo","Nielsen, Otto Anker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-694837"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Łukawska, Mirosława"],"keyword":["Crowdsourced GPS data","Preference heterogeneity","Route choice"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a joint bicycle route choice model for various cycling frequencies and trip distances based on a large crowdsourced gps dataset","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tra.2023.103834","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-694837","identifier":[{"id":"85172190530","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-33dfefc2-f3b6-4548-886e-a4fd331b3454"],"keyword":["Crowdsourced GPS data","Cycling behaviour","Joint path-size logit model","Preference heterogeneity","Route choice"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-49CE26A5E10669B57ABF69E6C221D4D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/336600051/1-s2.0-S0965856423002549-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.tra.2023.103834","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Technology, Management and Economics, Transportation Science, Transportation Systems Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mirosława","key":"łukawskapau","last":"Łukawska","locid":"dbfb7929-685a-42a7-8974-af4b53a95c8c","name":"Łukawska, Mirosława","orcid":"0000-0002-2581-9210","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"paulsenpau","last":"Paulsen","locid":"961ea410-f030-4c7a-bd08-d2220efc55d7","name":"Paulsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-1445-0876","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Kjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6499d80a-6f70-4824-91c8-d34b630c2e24","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Kjær","orcid":"0000-0003-0979-9667","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Fjendbo","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"a2c7f544-715a-412f-9cb7-cd660c27004b","name":"Jensen, Anders Fjendbo","orcid":"0000-0002-1952-7617","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Otto Anker","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"0b46cbc2-23db-4c0b-bc64-91094ef11adb","name":"Nielsen, Otto Anker","orcid":"0000-0001-7901-7021","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.tra.2023.103834","issn":["09658564","18792375"],"issn_org":["09658564"],"journal":"Transportation Research Part A: Policy and Practice","paperid":"103834","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Transportation Research Part A: Policy and Practice","title_org":"Transportation Research Part A","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85172190530"],"sdg":["15. Life on Land","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-33dfefc2-f3b6-4548-886e-a4fd331b3454"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A joint bicycle route choice model for various cycling frequencies and trip distances based on a large crowdsourced GPS dataset","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-694837","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Cold water swimming (CWS) involves taking a regular dip in cold, natural waters throughout the winter. The evidence for the health benefits of CWS has been anecdotal, or from small-sample size studies. The available literature reports that CWS abolishes general tiredness, improves mood, boosts self-esteem and improves general well-being. However, research on the effects and safety of CWS as an add-on to the regular treatment of depression is limited. The aim of this study was to investigate whether it is possible and safe for patients with depression to participate in CWS. Material and methods: The study was designed as an open-label feasibility study. All patients aged 20–69 years with a diagnosis of depression from an outpatient clinic were eligible for inclusion. The intervention consisted of twice-weekly, group-based CWS. Results: Thirteen patients were initially recruited, and five patients participated on a regular basis. Although several patients had somatic comorbidities, all patients passed the somatic evaluation and were physically fit to participate in CWS. Patients who participated regularly in the CWS sessions had a well-being score of 39.2; at the end of the study, their score had increased to 54.0 and PSQI score at baseline was 10.4 (3.7); at the end of the study it was 8.0 ((3.7). Conclusion: This study indicates that it is possible and safe for patients with depression to participate in regular, supervised CWS. Furthermore, regular participation in CWS may improve sleep and well-being.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hjorth, Peter","Sikjær, Melina Gade","Løkke, Anders","Jørgensen, Anne Marie","Jørgensen, Nina","Kaasgaard, Didde Marie","Rasmussen, Mikkel Rune Vossen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697462"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Hjorth, Peter"],"keyword":["Depression","Feasibility study","Physical health","Treatment"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cold water swimming as an add on treatment for depression a feasibility study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85163707811","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697462","identifier":[{"id":"37381680","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85163707811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-fcc61e42-fc25-491e-84ac-227e491cb3ed"],"keyword":["Depression","cold water swimming","feasibility study","physical health","treatment"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-160B0A8B9985551C52CA39FB8AD38EE0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Mental Health Services in the Region of Southern Denmark, Research Unit of Mental Health Services Vejle"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Psykiatrien i Region Syddanmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"hjorthpeterpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"5b44d6ad-54df-4334-866c-1f5c5bb53ada","name":"Hjorth, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-7548-5848","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melina Gade","key":"sikjærmelinagadepau","last":"Sikjær","locid":"573062a8-c283-4b3f-9aac-1e98c0345915","name":"Sikjær, Melina Gade","orcid":"0000-0002-5061-5367","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"løkkeanderspau","last":"Løkke","locid":"db3d3870-0459-4783-8f0b-6a8e5d9dce78","name":"Løkke, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-4141","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Marie","key":"jørgensenannemariepau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Anne Marie","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nina","key":"jørgensenninapau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Nina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Didde Marie","key":"kaasgaarddiddemariepau","last":"Kaasgaard","locid":"23902d2a-8d2b-488e-95f0-1ae529f1a892","name":"Kaasgaard, Didde Marie","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Rune Vossen","key":"rasmussenmikkelrunevossenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Rune Vossen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37381680"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/08039488.2023.2228290","issn":["08039488","08039496"],"issn_org":["08039488"],"issue":"7","journal":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","pages":"706-711","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"Nordic Journal of Psychiatry","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85163707811"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-fcc61e42-fc25-491e-84ac-227e491cb3ed"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Cold water swimming as an add-on treatment for depression : a feasibility study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697462","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"Analysis of wastewater is used in many settings for surveillance of SARS-CoV-2, but it remains unclear how well wastewater testing results reflect incidence. Denmark has had an extensive wastewater analysis system that conducts 3 weekly tests in ≈200 sites and has 85% population coverage; the country also offers free SARSCoV- 2 PCR tests to all residents. Using time series analysis for modeling, we found that wastewater data, combined with information on circulating variants and the number of human tests performed, closely fitted the incidence curve of persons testing positive. The results were consistent at a regional level and among a subpopulation of frequently tested healthcare personnel. We used wastewater analysis data to estimate incidence after testing was reduced to a minimum after March 2022. These results imply that data from a large-scale wastewater surveillance system can serve as a good proxy for COVID-19 incidence and for epidemic control.","author_count":15,"contributors":["McManus, Oliver","Christiansen, Lasse Engbo","Nauta, Maarten","Krogsgaard, Lene Wulff","Bahrenscheer, Naja Stolberg","von Kappelgaard, Lene","Christiansen, Tobias","Hansen, Mikkel","Hansen, Nicco Claudio","Kähler, Jonas","Rasmussen, Anders","Richter, Stine Raith","Rasmussen, Lasse Dam","Franck, Kristina Træholt","Ethelberg, Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-702493"],"filters":{"added":"2023-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Centre for disease Prevention and Control (ECDC)"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"predicting covid 000000000019 incidence using wastewater surveillance data denmark october 000000002021 june 000000002022","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3201/eid2908.221634","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-702493","identifier":[{"id":"PMC10370843","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85166363814","type":"scopus"},{"id":"37486168","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-e9118e85-fd2c-408d-b988-dc9e9242e013"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D05EDAB933FBCFDA05543F6898DFDEA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3201/eid2908.221634","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/370567658/22_1634.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"european centre for disease prevention and control","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"European Centre for disease Prevention and Control (ECDC)","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Global Health Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Oliver","key":"mcmanusoliverpau","last":"McManus","name":"McManus, Oliver","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lasse Engbo","key":"christiansenlasseengbopau","last":"Christiansen","name":"Christiansen, Lasse Engbo","rank":2,"ro