{"abstract":"Degradation and emissions of amine-containing solvents from CO2 capture plants are important to address as we are getting closer to full-scale deployment. Solvent degradation and air emissions from CO2 capture with 30 wt% monoethanolamine (MEA) were monitored at a mobile capture pilot, treating flue gas from a waste-to-energy facility in Denmark. The release of nitrosamines and nitramines was shown to be below the detection limit. Preliminary results showed that the installation of an acid wash removes gaseous degradation products from the depleted flue gas by up to 83% for MEA. However, a more in-depth investigation of the acid wash performance is needed to fully make any conclusions. The release of CO, NO, NO2, SO2, NH3, and HCl was monitored over several days. Results showed that the release of these components in the depleted flue gas is affected by both the temperature in the wash tower and the process configurations. The emissions of CO, NO, NO2, SO2, NH3 and HCl in the CO2 product stream were below 5 mg/m3. Heat stable salts accumulate over time in 30 wt% MEA with formate and acetate being the main degradation products. Accumulation of iron in the solvent did not exceed 10 mg/L during the 4 month campaign. The solvent degradation and emission results obtained in this study create a solid basis for understanding potential solvent emissions to the environment from waste-to-energy plants. Currently, the accumulation of heat stable salts in amine-based solvent seems to be the main challenge.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Neerup, Randi","Rasmussen, Valdemar E.","Vinjarapu, Sai Hema Bhavya","Larsen, Anders Hellerup","Shi, Meng","Andersen, Christina","Fuglsang, Karsten","Gram, Lars K.","Nedenskov, Jonas","Kabbel, Jannik","Blinksbjerg, Peter","Jensen, Søren","Karlsson, Jakob L.","Borgquist, Sebastian","Jørsboe, Jens Kristian","Villadsen, Sebastian Nis Bay","Fosbøl, Philip Loldrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-712034"],"filters":{"added":"2024-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Fosbøl, Philip Loldrup"],"keyword":["CO2 capture","CO2 corrosion","Degradation","Emissions","Monoethanolamine MEA","Waste to energy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-FORC"],"OT":["Amager Ressource Center"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-FORC","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"solvent degradation and emissions from a co sub 000000000002 sub capture pilot at a waste to energy plant","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jece.2023.111411","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-712034","identifier":[{"id":"85176233230","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bf5d8257-5ce9-46b2-9a9c-0aa54a30eea5"],"keyword":["CO2 capture","CO2 corrosion","degradation","emissions","monoethanolamine (MEA)","nitrosamine","utilization and storage (CCUS)","waste-to-energy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-004FC20200ED60D2D7FEA599A11522B3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/344915485/1-s2.0-S2213343723021504-main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jece.2023.111411","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Bioch