{"abstract":"The application of multiple omics technologies in biomedical cohorts has the potential to reveal patient-level disease characteristics and individualized response to treatment. However, the scale and heterogeneous nature of multi-modal data makes integration and inference a non-trivial task. We developed a deep-learning-based framework, multi-omics variational autoencoders (MOVE), to integrate such data and applied it to a cohort of 789 people with newly diagnosed type 2 diabetes with deep multi-omics phenotyping from the DIRECT consortium. Using in silico perturbations, we identified drug-omics associations across the multi-modal datasets for the 20 most prevalent drugs given to people with type 2 diabetes with substantially higher sensitivity than univariate statistical tests. From these, we among others, identified novel associations between metformin and the gut microbiota as well as opposite molecular responses for the two statins, simvastatin and atorvastatin. We used the associations to quantify drug-drug similarities, assess the degree of polypharmacy and conclude that drug effects are distributed across the multi-omics modalities.","author_count":55,"contributors":["Allesøe, Rosa Lundbye","Lundgaard, Agnete Troen","Hernandez Medina, Ricardo","Aguayo-Orozco, Alejandro","Johansen, Joachim","Nissen, Jakob Nybo","Brorsson, Caroline","Mazzoni, Gianluca","Niu, Lili","Biel, Jorge Hernansanz","Brasas, Valentas","Webel, Henry","Benros, Michael Eriksen","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Chmura, Piotr Jaroslaw","Jacobsen, Ulrik Plesner","Mari, Andrea","Koivula, Robert","Mahajan, Anubha","Vinuela, Ana","Tajes, Juan Fernandez","Sharma, Sapna","Haid, Mark","Hong, Mun-Gwan","Musholt, Petra B","De Masi, Federico","Vogt, Josef Korbinian","Pedersen, Helle Krogh","Gudmundsdottir, Valborg","Jones, Angus","Kennedy, Gwen","Bell, Jimmy","Thomas, E Louise","Frost, Gary","Thomsen, Henrik S","Hansen, Elizaveta","Hansen, Tue Haldor","Vestergaard, Henrik","Muilwijk, Mirthe","Blom, Marieke T","'t Hart, Leen M","Pattou, Francois","Raverdy, Violeta","Brage, Soren","Ridderstråle, Martin","Pedersen, Oluf","Hansen, Torben","Banasik, Karina","Rasmussen, Simon","Brunak, Søren"],"cuid":["S02-096.16-672879"],"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["IMI-DIRECT consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Brunak, Søren","Rasmussen, Simon"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Singapore","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","German Research Center for Environmental Health","Helmholtz Zentrum München - German Research Center for Environmental Health","Imperial College London","KTH Royal Institute of Technology","Leiden University","Lund University","National Research Council of Italy","National University of Singapore","Newcastle University","Pfizer","Sanofi-Aventis","Technical University of Munich","University of Cambridge","University of Dundee","University of Exeter","University of Geneva","University of Lille","University of Oxford","University of Westminster","Vrije Universiteit Amsterdam"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"OT":["C.N.R. Institute of Neuroscience"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovery of drug omics associations in type 000000000002 diabetes with generative deep learning models with author correction","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-022-01520-x","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We are grateful to IMI-DIRECT study participants who volunteered for phenotyping, and clinical and technical staff across involved European study centers who contributed to recruitment and clinical assessment of study participants. The work leading to this publication has received support from the Innovative Medicines Initiative Joint Undertaking under grant agreement 115317 (DIRECT), resources of which are composed of financial contribution from the European Union’s Seventh Framework Programme (FP7/2007-2013) and EFPIA companies’ in kind contribution. Information on the initiatives and activities of the IMI-DIRECT research consortium is available at https://directdiabetes.org . R.L.A., A.T.L, R.H.M., J.J., V.B., H.W., J.N.N., C.B., G.M., L.N., P.J.C., U.P.J, K.B., S.R., and S.B. were supported also by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grants NNF14CC0001 and NNF17OC0027594). Additionally, R.H.M. was supported by Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant NNF20SA0035590). Figure a was partly created using BioRender.com. Finally, we would like to thank Tugce Karaderi for critical comments on the manuscript."],"id":"S02-096.16-672879","identifier":[{"id":"36593394","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000909067600016","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC10017515","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85145508974","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0673c22b-1410-4518-b3fb-51b4e20af2bc","ku-88eb674c-a6cf-4bab-b529-a9e4015dbaec"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B8A72C44D38F9F426B3E435B5AF3FF10"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/325283734/s41587_022_01520_x_3_.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41587-022-01520-x","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/342495117/s41587_022_01520_x.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Univers