e_org":"Nielsen, Dennis S.","orcid":"0000-0001-8121-1114","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["37037943"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41564-023-01345-7","issn":["20585276"],"journal":"Nature Microbiology","pages":"986-998","publisher":"Nature Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"Nature Microbiology","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85152465966"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bc4de17c-0937-4dd3-a736-f576f6e6c0bd","ku-43016fe6-a1a5-4617-9ec9-d2c53a61b291"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Expanding known viral diversity in the healthy infant gut","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.50-666697","year":"2023","yearsub":"2023"}
{"abstract":"There has been considerable research into the understanding of the healthy skin microbiome. Similarly, there is also a considerable body of research into whether specific microbes contribute to skin disorders, with atopic dermatitis (AD) routinely linked to increased Staphylococcus aureus (S. aureus) colonisation. In this study, the epidermal surface of participants was sampled using swabs, while serial tape-stripping (35 tapes) was performed to sample through the stratum corneum. Samples were taken from AD patients and healthy controls, and the bacterial communities were profiled by metabarcoding the universal V3-V4 16S rRNA region. Results show that the majority of bacterial richness is located within the outermost layers of the stratum corneum, however there were many taxa that were found almost exclusively at the very outermost layer of the epidermis. We therefore hypothesise that tape-stripping can be performed to investigate the ‘core microbiome’ of participants by removing environmental contaminants. Interestingly, significant community variation between AD patients and healthy controls was only observable at the epidermal surface, yet a number of individual taxa were found to consistently differ with AD status across the entire epidermis (i.e. both the epidermal surface and within the epidermis). Sampling strategy could therefore be tailored dependent on the hypothesis, with sampling for forensic applications best performed using surface swabs and outer tapes, while profiling sub-surface communities may better reflect host genome and immunological status.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Barnes, Christopher James","Asplund, Maria","Clausen, Maja-Lisa","Rasmussen, Linett","Olesen, Caroline Meyer","Yüksel, Yasemin Topal","Andersen, Paal Skytt","Litman, Thomas","Holmstrøm, Kim","Bay, Lene","Fritz, Blaine Gabriel","Bjarnsholt, Thomas","Agner, Tove","Hansen, Anders Johannes"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-697953"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Barnes, Christopher James"],"keyword":["Atopic dermatitis","Bacteria","Epidermis","Fluorescent in situ hybridisation","Skin microbiome","Staphylococcus aureus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-BION"],"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LEO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-BION","DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-PR-LEO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a simplified bacterial community found within the epidermis than at the epidermal surface of atopic dermatitis patients and healthy controls","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12866-023-03012-7","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-697953","identifier":[{"id":"85173566123","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10540355","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"37773096","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-81410fb5-3e1e-44ca-a599-429ee06c5972","ku-5c81e32d-5d5a-46ad-94b8-0800781f8799"],"keyword":["Atopic dermatitis","Bacteria","Epidermis","Fluorescent in situ hybridisation","Skin microbiome","Staphylococcus aureus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7509883F4552AE0A67E5F205366853BD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/369974775/s12866_023_03012_7.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12866-023-03012-7","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"Un