shing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117123924"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6f565446-da2e-4443-a5f1-2188f78b44db"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Progress from ASDEX Upgrade experiments in preparing the physics basis of ITER operation and DEMO scenario development","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-337809","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The site frequency spectrum (SFS) is an important summary statistic in population genetics used for inference on demographic history and selection. However, estimation of the SFS from called genotypes introduce bias when working with low-coverage sequencing data. Methods exist for addressing this issue, but sometimes suffer from two problems. First, they can have very high computational demands, to the point that it may not be possible to run estimation for genome-scale data. Second, existing methods are prone to overfitting, especially for multi-dimensional SFS estimation. In this article, we present a stochastic expectation-maximisation algorithm for inferring the SFS from NGS data that addresses these challenges. We show that this algorithm greatly reduces runtime and enables estimation with constant, trivial RAM usage. Further, the algorithm reduces overfitting and thereby improves downstream inference. An implementation is available at github.com/malthesr/winsfs.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","Garcia-Erill, Genís","Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","Wiuf, Carsten","Albrechtsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-419923"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of site frequency spectra from low coverage sequencing data using stochastic em reduces overfitting runtime and memory usage","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://academic.oup.com/pages/standard-publication-reuse-rights","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/genetics/iyac148","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-419923","identifier":[{"id":"85156227449","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9713400","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36173322","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-2c7044d7-4b97-47f2-875a-d08eba7444d5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-024E989EAA5EA87AF8D815DA55EE3E8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://academic.oup.com/pages/standard-publication-reuse-rights","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/genetics/iyac148","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://academic.oup.com/pages/standard-publication-reuse-rights","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332049775/iyac148.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Malthe Sebro","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c78f599c-157c-4a9a-9e7a-ab1d876ab28c","name":"Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Genís","key":"garciaerillpau","last":"Garcia-Erill","locid":"a03971a5-00fa-4ccf-ae13-f15fdcd34405","name":"Garcia-Erill, Genís","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thorfinn Sand","key":"korneliussenpau","last":"Korneliussen","locid":"9b3a5a0a-4792-430d-9a69-00990d6eee1b","name":"Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","orcid":"0000-0001-7576-5380","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"wiufpau","last":"Wiuf","locid":"7fd38cb7-1794-49d3-b4ad-19844f67e6fc","name":"Wiuf, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0002-1302-4445","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"albrechtsenpau","last":"Albrechtsen","locid":"4b040c73-6b49-4e97-be60-5e34608e0615","name":"Albrechtsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-7306-031X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36173322"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/genetics/iyac148","issn":["00166731"],"issn_org":["19432631"],"issue":"4","journal":"Genetics","paperid":"iyac148","status":"p","title":"Genetics","volume":"222"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85156227449"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2c7044d7-4b97-47f2-875a-d08eba7444d5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Estimation of site frequency spectra from low-coverage sequencing data using stochastic EM reduces overfitting, runtime, and memory usage","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-419923","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Common bunt is a seed borne disease of wheat whose importance is likely to increase due to the growing organic seed market, which, in addition to seed phytosanitary measures, relies on genetic resistances towards the disease. Genome wide association studies in wheat have been proven to be a useful tool in the detection of genetic polymorphisms underlying phenotypic trait variation in wheat. Here 248 wheat landraces and cultivars representing 130 years of breeding history were screened for two years in the field for their resistance reactions towards common bunt. The majority of lines exhibited high levels of susceptibility towards common bunt, while 25 accessions had less than 10% infection. Using Diversity Array Technology (DArT) markers for genotyping and correcting for population stratification by using a compressed mixed linear model, we identified two significant marker trait associations (MTA) for common bunt resistance, designated QCbt.cph-2B and QCbt.cph-7A, located on wheat chromosomes 2B and 7A, respectively. This shows that genome wide association studies (GWAS) are applicable in the search for genetic polymorphisms for resistance towards less studied plant diseases such as common bunt in the context of an under representation of resistant lines.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Steffan, Philipp Matthias","Borgen, Anders","Torp, Anna Maria","Backes, Gunter","Rasmussen, Søren Kjærsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-420405"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Kassel"],"keyword":["Organic agriculture","Quantitative Trait Loci","Triticum aestivum"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Agrologica"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association mapping for common bunt resistance in wheat landraces and cultivars","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy12030642","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-420405","identifier":[{"id":"85126439123","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000776899600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-2d3ac6cd-0c5c-4ea4-b04b-1560870c0d76"],"keyword":["Bt resistance gene","DArT markers","Dwarf bunt","Organic agriculture","Quantitative trait loci","Seed borne disease","Triticum aestivum"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D3B8614EB9532B929A102B5036F4CAB6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/agronomy12030642","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/303583418/agronomy_12_00642_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Plant and Environmental Sciences, Section for Plant and Soil Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Agrologica"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"university of kassel","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kassel","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Philipp Matthias","key":"steffanpau","last":"Steffan","locid":"ba016d6c-38a3-43d8-9b76-60b1a73dac84","name":"Steffan, Philipp Matthias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"borgenpau","last":"Borgen","name":"Borgen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Maria","key":"torppau","last":"Torp","locid":"48b42851-8540-4054-81c4-4ee820ea115f","name":"Torp, Anna Maria","orcid":"0000-0001-8199-1480","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Gunter","key":"backespau","last":"Backes","name":"Backes, Gunter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren K.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"95b8db6a-2621-49dc-bf1f-dbba5884b8da","name":"Rasmussen, Søren Kjærsgaard","name_org":"Rasmussen, Søren K.","orcid":"0000-0001-6169-2504","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/agronomy12030642","issn":["20734395"],"issue":"3","journal":"Agronomy","paperid":"642","status":"p","title":"Agronomy","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126439123"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2d3ac6cd-0c5c-4ea4-b04b-1560870c0d76"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association Mapping for Common Bunt Resistance in Wheat Landraces and Cultivars","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-420405","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background Fluid retention is a known but underappreciated side-effect of non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug (NSAID) use. As type 2 diabetes mellitus (T2DM) has been linked to both subclinical cardiomyopathy and a decline in kidney function, short-term NSAID use could lead to subsequently development of heart failure (HF) due to aberrations in fluid balances. Purpose We investigated associations between short-term NSAID use and the risk of HF in a nationwide cohort of patients with T2DM. Methods Using nationwide Danish registers, we identified patients diagnosed with T2DM during 1998–2018. Follow-up began 120 days after first-time T2DM diagnosis among patients without prior heart failure or a rheumatological diagnosis indicating long-term NSAID use. To describe use of NSAID among patients with T2DM, we reported proportions of patients claiming at least 1, 2, 3 or 4 prescriptions of NSAID within one year of start of follow-up. We investigated associations between use of NSAIDs (celecoxib, diclofenac, ibuprofen and naproxen) and new-onset HF hospitalizations using a case-crossover design with 28-day exposure windows and reported odds ratios (OR) with 95% confidence intervals (CI). The case-crossover design uses each individual as his or her own control making it suitable to study the effect of short-term exposure on immediate events while mitigating unmeasured confounding. Sensitivity analyses using exposure windows of 14 and 42 days were performed as well. Results A total of 334,950 patients with T2DM was included (47.7% female, median age of 61 [interquartile range 50–70]). Celecoxib and naproxen were rarely used; on the contrary, prescriptions of diclofenac and ibuprofen were claimed at least once within one year from the beginning of follow-up by 4.9% and 15.5% of patients, respectively–0.9% and 2.7% claimed at least four prescriptions (Figure 1). The risk of new-onset HF hospitalization was increased following use of diclofenac or ibuprofen with corresponding ORs of 1.3 (95% CI 1.0 to 1.7) and 1.3 (95% CI 1.1 to 1.5) using 28-day exposure windows. An increased risk following use of celecoxib or naproxen was not found (Figure 2). Conclusion NSAIDs diclofenac and ibuprofen were both widely used and associated with an increased risk of new-onset HF hospitalization in patients with T2DM. This suggests a previously unknown and serious, clinically relevant concern of NSAID use in patients with T2DM.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Holt, Anders","Strange, Jarl Emanuel","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","Blanche, Paul","Nouhravesh, N.","Jensen, M. H.","Schjerning, A. M.","Schou, M.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Gislason, Gunnar","Hansen, M. L.","McGettigan, P.","Lamberts, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-523751"],"filters":{"added":"2023-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Queen Mary University of London"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of heart failure following short term non steroidal anti inflammatory drug use in patients with type 000000000002 diabetes mellitus","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-523751","identifier":[{"id":"000894947902901","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-da34cb03-9d2a-44ef-820a-306a96450504"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-3F9EDFEEC421731A2900C9E8C818BE82"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"queen mary university of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Queen Mary University of London","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"A.","key":"holtpau","last":"Holt","locid":"7b64b1ed-698a-4d01-8987-02e878b5674c","name":"Holt, Anders","name_org":"Holt, A.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"J. E.","key":"strangepau","last":"Strange","locid":"8abc6f65-e1b6-4c15-9876-3985f814fe09","name":"Strange, Jarl Emanuel","name_org":"Strange, J. E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"P. V.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca186b96-3318-42e7-8fe1-34aa087a51b0","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","name_org":"Rasmussen, P. V.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"P.","key":"blanchepau","last":"Blanche","locid":"92ff477f-3b2c-4873-a4f5-dbe701671e1c","name":"Blanche, Paul","name_org":"Blanche, P.","orcid":"0000-0003-1415-7976","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"N.","key":"nouhraveshpau","last":"Nouhravesh","name":"Nouhravesh, N.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M. H.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, M. H.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A. M.","key":"schjerningpau","last":"Schjerning","name":"Schjerning, A. M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M.","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","name":"Schou, M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"C.","key":"torppedersenpau","last":"Torp-Pedersen","locid":"f71bedc6-3736-4559-b937-6a18e770616e","name":"Torp-Pedersen, Christian","name_org":"Torp-Pedersen, C.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"G. H.","key":"gislasonpau","last":"Gislason","locid":"c0f678a6-eb13-49a3-9485-8fae1e72e2a1","name":"Gislason, Gunnar","name_org":"Gislason, G. H.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"M. L.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, M. L.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"P.","key":"mcgettiganpau","last":"McGettigan","name":"McGettigan, P.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"M. K.","key":"lambertspau","last":"Lamberts","locid":"ced953f0-cd5e-4af3-8c41-7311decea61f","name":"Lamberts, Morten","name_org":"Lamberts, M. K.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehac544.802","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"Supplement 2","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"802","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"43"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-da34cb03-9d2a-44ef-820a-306a96450504"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of heart failure following short-term non-steroidal anti-inflammatory drug use in patients with type 2 diabetes mellitus","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-523751","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Stochastic sample-based estimators are among the most fundamental and universally applied tools in statistics. Such estimators are particularly important when processing huge amounts of data, where we need to be able to answer a wide range of statistical queries reliably, yet cannot afford to store the data in its full length. In many applications we need the sampling to be coordinated which is typically attained using hashing. In previous work, a common strategy to obtain reliable sample-based estimators that work within certain error bounds with high probability has been to design one that works with constant probability, and then boost the probability by taking the median over r independent repetitions. Aamand et al. (STOC’20) recently proposed a fast and practical hashing scheme with strong concentration bounds, Tabulation-1Permutation, the first of its kind. In this paper, we demonstrate that using such a hash family for the sampling, we achieve the same high probability bounds without any need for repetitions. Using the same space, this saves a factor r in time, and simplifies the overall algorithms. We validate our approach experimentally on both real and synthetic data. We compare Tabulation-1Permutation with other hash functions such as strongly universal hash functions and various other hash functions such as MurmurHash3 and BLAKE3, both with and without resorting to repetitions. We see that if we want reliability in terms of small error probabilities, then Tabulation-1Permutation is significantly faster.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aamand, Anders","Das, Debarati","Kipouridis, Evangelos","Knudsen, Jakob B.T.","Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-535231"],"event":{"end":"2022-09-09","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2022-09-05","title":"48th International Conference on Very Large Data Bases, VLDB 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Pennsylvania State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no repetition fast and reliable sampling with highly concentrated hashing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14778/3565838.3565851","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-535231","identifier":[{"id":"85147795979","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-ed8ffab8-abb7-48b4-b849-5f5cde23830d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-792EC688F5052E78D9831341271CCA1A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.14778/3565838.3565851","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/340710367/No_Repetition.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"pennsylvania state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pennsylvania State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"aff