10.1111/aas.14113","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"8","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"987-995","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135270856"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a27404b9-fcd1-40d7-a257-66dc43e978b2","au-f65f3db5-ae5c-45e1-a003-382285d603a1","ku-3dc1872d-ff7b-4609-9087-81a88d1a5412","sdu-be85f827-bb2d-47ce-940b-920015566cc1"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Changes over time in characteristics, resource use and outcomes among ICU patients with COVID-19-A nationwide, observational study in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-095.83-007852","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Atrial fibrillation (AF) and renal impairment share a bidirectional relationship with important pathophysiological interactions. We evaluated the impact of renal impairment in a contemporary cohort of patients with AF. Methods: We utilised the ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry. Outcomes were analysed according to renal function by CKD-EPI equation. The primary endpoint was a composite of thromboembolism, major bleeding, acute coronary syndrome and all-cause death. Secondary endpoints were each of these separately including ischaemic stroke, haemorrhagic event, intracranial haemorrhage, cardiovascular death and hospital admission. Results: A total of 9306 patients were included. The distribution of patients with no, mild, moderate and severe renal impairment at baseline were 16.9%, 49.3%, 30% and 3.8%, respectively. AF patients with impaired renal function were older, more likely to be females, had worse cardiac imaging parameters and multiple comorbidities. Among patients with an indication for anticoagulation, prescription of these agents was reduced in those with severe renal impairment, p <.001. Over 24 months, impaired renal function was associated with significantly greater incidence of the primary composite outcome and all secondary outcomes. Multivariable Cox regression analysis demonstrated an inverse relationship between eGFR and the primary outcome (HR 1.07 [95% CI, 1.01–1.14] per 10 ml/min/1.73 m 2 decrease), that was most notable in patients with eGFR <30 ml/min/1.73 m 2 (HR 2.21 [95% CI, 1.23–3.99] compared to eGFR ≥90 ml/min/1.73 m 2). Conclusion: A significant proportion of patients with AF suffer from concomitant renal impairment which impacts their overall management. Furthermore, renal impairment is an independent predictor of major adverse events including thromboembolism, major bleeding, acute coronary syndrome and all-cause death in patients with AF.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Ding, Wern Yew","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Blomström-Lundqvist, Carina","Boriani, Giuseppe","Marin, Francisco","Fauchier, Laurent","Lip, Gregory Y H","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-063125"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["France","Italy","Serbia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital of Modena","University of Belgrade","University of Liverpool","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome complications","Anticoagulants therapeutic use","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Atrial fibrillation","Brain Ischemia","Chronic kidney disease","Death","Female","Hemorrhage chemically induced","Humans","Kidney failure","Major bleeding","Male","Outcome","Registries","Renal Insufficiency chemically induced","Risk Factors","Stroke complications","Thromboembolism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of renal impairment on atrial fibrillation esc ehra eorp af long term general registry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"acce