Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2d17da8d-9f9a-4b1e-8ef6-c97af5c0eaba"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of renal impairment on atrial fibrillation : ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-063125","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Shoulder arthroscopy can result in substantial postoperative pain. Sucrose acetate isobutyrate extended-release bupivacaine (SABER-Bupivacaine; trade name Posimir) is a novel depot formulation of bupivacaine designed to provide analgesia at the surgical site for up to 72 hours. The objective of this study was to evaluate the effect of SABER-Bupivacaine on pain and opioid consumption after arthroscopic subacromial decompression and to assess short-term and long-term safety. METHODS: In this double-blind, placebo-controlled trial, 78 subjects were randomized in a 2:1 ratio to SABER-Bupivacaine 5 mL or SABER-placebo 5 mL injected into the subacromial space just before skin closure. Twenty-nine additional subjects were randomized on an exploratory basis to bupivacaine hydrochloride 20 mL, also injected subacromially. Subjects rated pain intensity on a 0 to 10 scale over the first 3 postoperative days and received intravenous or oral morphine for breakthrough pain. The coprimary efficacy end points were pain intensity on 90° shoulder flexion and cumulative morphine intake from 0 to 72 hours after surgery. The time to first use of opioid rescue analgesia was a secondary end point. RESULTS: The mean (SD) pain intensity was 5.16 (1.94) for SABER-Bupivacaine and 6.43 (1.77) for placebo (P = 0.012). The median consumption of intravenous morphine equivalents was 4.0 mg for SABER-Bupivacaine and 12.0 mg for placebo (P = 0.010). The median time to first use of morphine rescue was 12.4 hours for SABER-Bupivacaine and 1.2 hours for placebo (P = 0.014). The corresponding values for bupivacaine hydrochloride were 5.16 (2.38), 8.0 mg, and 1.4 hours. The incidence and severity of treatment-emergent adverse events were similar for all treatment groups, and no functional or radiographic differences were noted at the 6-month follow-up. DISCUSSION: Compared with placebo, SABER-Bupivacaine reduced pain and opioid analgesic consumption over 72 hours after arthroscopic subacromial decompression and prolonged the time to first use of opioid rescue analgesia. No safety signals were noted during the immediate postoperative period or at 6-month follow-up.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ekelund, Anders","Peredistijs, Andrejs","Grohs, Josef","Meisner, Jon","Verity, Neil","Rasmussen, Sten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107599"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Sten"],"country":["Austria","Ireland","Latvia","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Clinic of Traumatology and Orthopaedics","DURECT Corporation","Innocoll Pharmaceuticals","Medical University of Vienna","Saint Göran Hospital"],"keyword":["Analgesics Opioid therapeutic use","Anesthetics Local therapeutic use","Decompression","Humans","Pain Postoperative drug therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"saber bupivacaine reduces postoperative pain and opioid consumption after arthroscopic subacromial decompression a randomized placebo controlled trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5435/JAAOSGlobal-D-21-00287","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107599","identifier":[{"id":"85130219889","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35584248","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c645f18d-6251-4f29-a164-0dbbe274f6a0"],"keyword":["Analgesics, Opioid/therapeutic use","Anesthetics, Local/therapeutic use","Bupivacaine/adverse effects","Decompression","Humans","Morphine Derivatives/therapeutic use","Pain, Postoperative/drug therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-E81CA1BB5D9C3823BAC77AE65B99327C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5435/JAAOSGlobal-D-21-00287","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/472477909/Ekelund_et_al._2022_._SABER_Bupivacaine_Reduces_Postoperative_Pain_and_Opioid_Consumption_After_Arthroscopic_Subacromial_Decompression_A_Randomized_Placebo_Controlled_Trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"saint göran hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Saint Göran Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"lv","key":"clinic of traumatology and orthopaedics","loc":["Latvia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Clinic of Traumatology and Orthopaedics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"medical university of vienna","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Medical University of Vienna","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ie","key":"innocoll pharmaceuticals","loc":["Ireland","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Innocoll Pharmaceuticals","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"durect corporation","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"DURECT Corporation","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"ekelundpau","last":"Ekelund","name":"Ekelund, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Andrejs","key":"peredistijspau","last":"Peredistijs","name":"Peredistijs, Andrejs","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Josef","key":"grohspau","last":"Grohs","name":"Grohs, Josef","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon","key":"meisnerpau","last":"Meisner","name":"Meisner, Jon","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Neil","key":"veritypau","last":"Verity","name":"Verity, Neil","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"05d1d595-13be-4295-8ad1-8d29206859c8","name":"Rasmussen, Sten","orcid":"0000-0002-8664-352X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35584248"],"pub":{"doi":"10.5435/jaaosglobal-d-21-00287","issn":["24747661"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of the American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons. Global research & reviews","paperid":"e21.00287","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer","status":"p","title":"Journal of the American Academy of Orthopaedic Surgeons. Global research & reviews","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-c645f18d-6251-4f29-a164-0dbbe274f6a0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"SABER-Bupivacaine Reduces Postoperative Pain and Opioid Consumption After Arthroscopic Subacromial Decompression : A Randomized, Placebo-Controlled Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-107599","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The prevalence of atrial fibrillation(AF) and diabetes mellitus is rising to epidemic proportions. We aimed to assess the impact of diabetes on the management and outcomes of patients with AF. METHODS: The EORP-AF General Long-Term Registry is a prospective, observational registry from 250 centres across 27 European countries. Outcomes of interest were as follows: i)rhythm control interventions; ii)quality of life; iii)healthcare resource utilisation; and iv)major adverse events. RESULTS: Of 11,028 patients with AF, the median age was 71 (63-77) years and 2537 (23.0%) had diabetes. Median follow-up was 24 months. Diabetes was related to increased use of anticoagulation but less rhythm control interventions. Using multivariable analysis, at 2-year follow-up, patients with diabetes were associated with greater levels of anxiety (p = 0.038) compared to those without diabetes. Overall, diabetes was associated with worse health during follow-up, as indicated by Health Utility Score and Visual Analogue Scale. Healthcare resource utilisation was greater with diabetes in terms of length of hospital stay (8.1 (±8.2) vs. 6.1 (±6.7) days); cardiology and internal medicine/general practitioner visits; and emergency room admissions. Diabetes was an independent risk factor of major adverse cardiovascular event (MACE; HR 1.26 [95% CI, 1.04-1.52]), all-cause mortality (HR 1.28 [95% CI, 1.08-1.52]), and cardiovascular mortality (HR 1.41 [95% CI, 1.09-1.83]). CONCLUSION: In this contemporary AF cohort, diabetes was present in 1 in 4 patients and it served as an independent risk factor for reduced quality of life, greater healthcare resource utilisation and excess MACE, all-cause mortality and cardiovascular mortality. There was increased use of anticoagulation therapy in diabetes but with less rhythm control interventions.","author_count":18,"contributors":["Ding, Wern Yew","Kotalczyk, Agnieszka","Boriani, Giuseppe","Marin, Francisco","Blomström-Lundqvist, Carina","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Fauchier, Laurent","Lip, Gregory Y H","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121255"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["France","Italy","Poland","Serbia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Medical University of Silesia in Katowice","Silesian Centre for Heart Diseases","University Hospital of Modena","University of Belgrade","University of Liverpool","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Cohort","Healthcare resource utilisation","MACE","Mortality","Prevalence","Prognosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"impact of diabetes on the management and outcomes in atrial fibrillation an analysis from the esc ehra eorp af long term general registry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejim.2022.04.026","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121255","identifier":[{"id":"85129918095","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35527179","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-f4f93382-d06e-458c-8cfe-91b1f