"first":"Carina","key":"blomströmlundqvistpau","last":"Blomström-Lundqvist","name":"Blomström-Lundqvist, Carina","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11 12","corresponding":null,"first":"Tatjana S.","key":"potparapau","last":"Potpara","name":"Potpara, Tatjana S.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurent","key":"fauchierpau","last":"Fauchier","name":"Fauchier, Laurent","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y. H.","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","name_org":"Lip, Gregory Y. H.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Albert Marni","key":"joensenoth","last":"Joensen","locid":"8ac1d105-5ddb-4f1f-9c02-f8c175b09fbd","name":"Joensen, Albert Marni","orcid":"0000-0002-9963-9511","rank":9,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"gammelmarkoth","last":"Gammelmark","locid":"81d0fbd3-822b-42fb-9450-9f3dc39f1d70","name":"Gammelmark, Anders","rank":10,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenoth","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":11,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia","key":"danstrupdinesenoth","last":"Danstrup-Dinesen","locid":"42f1d760-b397-42b5-9506-f47ad71fe8b5","name":"Dinesen, Pia Thisted","name_org":"Danstrup-Dinesen, Pia","rank":12,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sam","key":"riahioth","last":"Riahi","locid":"9e5489d8-981a-469c-bd84-20b2e24832de","name":"Riahi, Sam","orcid":"0000-0003-1849-9463","rank":13,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Krogh","key":"venøoth","last":"Venø","locid":"f8bc3484-c65b-49fa-8646-45280454d73f","name":"Venø, Stine Krogh","orcid":"0000-0001-9325-4875","rank":14,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Bodil Ginnerup","key":"sørensenoth","last":"Sørensen","locid":"3a9d9dd7-243c-41a2-9851-6c57b00d769e","name":"Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","rank":15,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Marie","key":"korsgaardoth","last":"Korsgaard","locid":"7d947205-facd-4578-b298-a5dc4da5c077","name":"Korsgaard, Anne Marie","rank":16,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen Petrea","key":"andersenoth","last":"Andersen","locid":"ab91cea9-8536-4269-842e-f42133246cba","name":"Andersen, Karen Petrea","rank":17,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"14","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Fragtrup","key":"hellumoth","last":"Hellum","locid":"fd7755f7-451a-448c-8679-baccccd2d85a","name":"Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup","rank":18,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["35527179"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejim.2022.04.026","issn":["09536205","11218967"],"issn_org":["09536205"],"journal":"European Journal of Internal Medicine","pages":"41-49","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Internal Medicine"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129918095"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-f4f93382-d06e-458c-8cfe-91b1f4a632ef"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of diabetes on the management and outcomes in atrial fibrillation : an analysis from the ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-121255","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Prognostic markers of survival have been identified in wild-type transthyretin amyloidosis (ATTRwt), but limited data exist with respect to hospitalizations with worsening heart failure (WHF). Predictive markers of WHF have yet to be identified. METHODS: From April 2017 to February 2021, 104 patients with ATTRwt were diagnosed and prospectively followed from the time of diagnosis to the time of death or the censoring date of 1 February 2021. Baseline patient characteristics, biomarkers, and advanced echocardiography were used to predict hospitalization with WHF. RESULTS: During the median follow-up period of 23 months, 51% of patients were hospitalized due to WHF. Seventy-three per cent of patients with WHF were admitted at least twice. Patients with WHF during the first year had significantly poorer survival (P < 0.001). Independent predictors of WHF during follow-up were pacemaker implantation prior to diagnosis (PMI, P = 0.037) and right atrial volume index (RAVi, P = 0.008). Patients with PMI had a higher left ventricular mass index and poorer left ventricular and right ventricular systolic function indicating a more advanced stage of amyloid disease. CONCLUSIONS: A high incidence and recurrence of hospital admissions with WHF were demonstrated in contemporary patients with ATTRwt, which was associated with reduced survival. Patients with pacemaker devices prior to ATTRwt diagnosis experienced more frequent hospitalizations with WHF. PMI and right atrial enlargement were identified as independent predictors of WHF during follow-up.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Ladefoged, Bertil","Dybro, Anne Mette","Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","Vase, Henrik","Clemmensen, Tor Skibsted","Gillmore, Julian","Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-268852"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Pacemaker","Wild type transthyretin cardiac amyloidosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"incidence and predictors of worsening heart failure in patients with wild type transthyretin cardiac amyloidosis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ehf2.14000","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-268852","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9715879","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85132412865","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35733407","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-f4a9f82e-3172-4c24-82c4-e4e5657ee95f"],"keyword":["Heart failure","Pacemaker","Wild-type transthyretin cardiac amyloidosis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-880609B98F3D3CCA389134AE1136071B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ehf2.14000","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Cardiological Medicine B"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bertil Thyrsted","key":"ladefogedpau","last":"Ladefoged","locid":"f5413eb1-7cda-4cbe-a6ca-d418bbfce623","name":"Ladefoged, Bertil","name_org":"Ladefoged, Bertil Thyrsted","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne","key":"dybropau","last":"Dybro","locid":"2e78d319-fc37-4dc3-9030-130d2d0c8a25","name":"Dybro, Anne Mette","name_org":"Dybro, Anne","orcid":"0000-0003-3175-9725","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Lehmann","key":"dahlpedersenpau","last":"Dahl Pedersen","locid":"7e7debe0-e391-4c37-9cbd-c136c98fc08a","name":"Pedersen, Anders Lehmann Dahl","name_org":"Dahl Pedersen, Anders Lehmann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torsten Bloch","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"4bae5bd6-40ab-4bd9-a7ba-fc3d7fe970c7","name":"Rasmussen, Torsten Bloch","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik Ølholm","key":"vasepau","last":"Vase","locid":"aac9f515-f357-49af-b2df-84200398112b","name":"Vase, Henrik","name_org":"Vase, Henrik Ølholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tor Skibsted","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"80bbaf86-59cd-42d7-8f6c-e7c7604776cb","name":"Clemmensen, Tor Skibsted","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"gillmorepau","last":"Gillmore","name":"Gillmore, Julian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen Hvitfeldt","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"ec1d0fd4-f6ae-4071-907f-1448dfe832fe","name":"Poulsen, Steen Hvitfeldt","orcid":"0000-0002-9586-835X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35733407"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ehf2.14000","issn":["20555822"],"issue":"5","journal":"ESC Heart Failure","pages":"2978-2987","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"ESC Heart Failure","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132412865"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f4a9f82e-3172-4c24-82c4-e4e5657ee95f"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Incidence and predictors of worsening heart failure in patients with wild-type transthyretin cardiac amyloidosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-268852","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Quantum chemical (QC) calculations can yield direct insight into an atmospheric cluster formation mechanism and cluster formation rates. However, such calculations are extremely computationally demanding as more than millions of cluster configurations might exist and need to be computed. We present an efficient approach to produce high quality QC data sets for applications in cluster formation studies and how to train an accurate quantum machine learning model on the generated data. Using the two-component sulfuric acid-water system as a proof of concept, we demonstrate that a kernel ridge regression machine learning model with Δ-learning can be trained to accurately predict the binding energies of cluster equilibrium configurations with mean absolute errors below 0.5 kcal mol-1. Additionally, we enlarge the training data set with nonequilibrium configurations and show the possibility of predicting the binding energies of new structures of clusters several molecules larger than those in the training set. Applying the trained machine learning model leads to a drastic reduction in the number of relevant clusters that need to be explicitly evaluated by QC methods. The presented approach is directly transferable to clusters of arbitrary composition and will lead to faster and more efficient exploration of the configurational space of new cluster systems.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Kubečka, Jakub","Christensen, Anders S.","Rasmussen, Freja Rydahl","Elm, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274688"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Elm, Jonas"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantum machine learning approach for studying atmospheric cluster formation","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/261196397/Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-274688","identifier":[{"id":"85124297131","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-feb9b5a6-63c0-4dbb-8903-fa25f99f21d1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-722C41C718BDD70B41F012E1911E74B5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/261196397/Manuscript.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Chemistry","Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change, iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change - iCLIMATE Aarhus University Interdisciplinary Centre for Climate Change, Langelandsgade"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakub","key":"kubečkapau","last":"Kubečka","locid":"411c3b01-f20c-47a0-86e4-9985172feea5","name":"Kubečka, Jakub","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders S.","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Anders S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Freja Rydahl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87b80add-745f-4d09-aad0-139158aaf11c","name":"Rasmussen, Freja Rydahl","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"elmpau","last":"Elm","locid":"1cf322e2-4552-4a27-bdf3-be1c6e4d5409","name":"Elm, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0003-3736-4329","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1021/acs.estlett.1c00997","issn":["23288930"],"issue":"3","journal":"Environmental Science & Technology Letters","pages":"239-244","publisher":"American Chemical Society","status":"p","title":"Environmental Science & Technology Letters","title_org":"Environmental Science and Technology Letters","volume":"9"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124297131"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-feb9b5a6-63c0-4dbb-8903-fa25f99f21d1"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Quantum Machine Learning Approach for Studying Atmospheric Cluster Formation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-274688","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"We present an overview of results from a series of L-H transition experiments undertaken at JET since the installation of the ITER-like-wall (JET-ILW), with beryllium wall tiles and a tungsten divertor. Tritium, helium and deuterium plasmas have been investigated. Initial results in tritium show ohmic L-H transitions at low density and the power threshold for the L-H transition (PLH) is lower in tritium plasmas than in deuterium ones at low densities, while we still lack contrasted data to provide a scaling at high densities. In helium plasmas there is a notable shift of the density at which the power threshold is minimum ( ¯ne,min ) to higher values relative to deuterium and hydrogen references. Above ¯ne,min (He) the L-H power threshold at high densities is similar for D and He plasmas. Transport modelling in slab geometry shows that in helium neoclassical transport competes with interchange-driven transport, unlike in hydrogen isotopes. Measurements of the radial electric field in deuterium plasmas show that Er shear is not a good indicator of proximity to the L-H transition. Transport analysis of ion heat flux in deuterium plasmas show a non-linearity as density is decreased below ¯ne,min. Lastly, a regression of the JET-ILW deuterium data is compared to the 2008 ITPA scaling law.","author_count":77,"contributors":["Solano, E. R.","Delabie, E.","Birkenmeier, G.","Silva, C.","Hillesheim, J. C.","Vincenzi, P.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Baciero, A.","Aleiferis, S.","Balboa, I.","Boboc, A.","Bourdelle, C.","Carvalho, I. S.","Carvalho, P.","Chernyshova, M.","Coelho, R.","Craciunescu, T.","Dumont, R.","Dumortier, P.","Luna, E. De La","Flanagan, J.","Fontana, M.","Fontdecaba, J. M.","Frassinetti, L.","Gallart, D.","Garcia, J.","Giovannozzi, E.","Giroud, C.","Gromelski, W.","Henriques, R.","Horvath, L.","Jacquet, P.","Jepu, I.","Kappatou, A.","Keeling, D. L.","King, D.","Kowalska-Strzȩciwilk, E.","Lennholm, M.","Lerche, E.","Litherland