],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Overview of JET results for optimising ITER operation","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-352436","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The scrape-off layer power width (λ q ) is an important parameter for characterizing the divertor heat loads. Many experimental, theoretical, and numerical studies on λq have been performed in recent years. In this paper, a 2D electrostatic turbulence code, BOUT-HESEL, has been upgraded to simulate H-mode plasmas for the first time. The code is validated against the previous implementation and the experimental λq scalings for L-mode plasmas and experiments with a typical EAST H-mode discharge. The simulated λ q is found to agree quite well with the Eich scaling [Eich et al 2013 Nucl. Fusion 53 093031] for the EAST H-mode discharge and the comparison of the probability distribution function of the parallel particle flux with the measurements by reciprocating probes is also consistent. The code is utilized to simulate the ITER 15 MA baseline scenario [Kim et al 2018 Nucl. Fusion 58 056013]. The ITER simulation reveals that the radial particle/heat transports are dominated by blobby transports, and predicts λ q,ITER = 9.6 mm, which is much larger than the prediction by the Eich scaling (λ q,ITER ≈ 1 mm). Based on the EAST modified cases, an estimated HESEL H-mode scaling, λq=0.51Rc1.1Bt-0.3q951.1 is proposed. This scaling predicts λ q,ITER = 9.3 mm, which agrees surprisingly well with that for the ITER case. A further investigation combined with the basic parameters in the database of the Eich scaling shows that the missing positive scaling dependence on the machine size (Rc) in the Eich scaling appears to be shaded by the negative scaling dependence on the toroidal magnetic field (Bt) for current devices. This is however not the case for ITER, explaining why simulations in recent studies and this paper can reproduce the Eich scaling for current devices, but predict a much larger λ q for ITER. According to the simulation results, the strong positive scaling dependence of λq on Rc is due to a combination of slowing down the parallel heat transports by increasing the parallel connection length and the enhancement of the radial E × B turbulent heat transports when the machine size is increased.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Liu, X.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Naulin, Volker","Wang, L.","Ding, R.","Li, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-361909"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Liu, X."],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Blob","Divertor","ITER","Turbulence"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulations of scrape off layer power width for east h mode plasma and iter 000000000015 ma baseline scenario by 000000000002d electrostatic turbulence code","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/337665797/2203.09039.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The author X. Liu thanks Dr. Ning Yan, Dr. Xiang Han, Mr. Tianfu Zhou, Mr. Shengyu Fu, and Mr. Yifei Jin for providing EAST experimental data, and appreciates the help from Dr. Sun Hee Kim, Dr. Zeyu Li and Dr. Xueqiao Xu for sharing plasma profiles of the ITER 15 MA baseline scenario. This work was supported by the Natural Science Foundation of China (Nos. 12005260, 11922513), and the National Key Research and Development Program (No. 2017YFE0301300). This work was also partially supported by Institute of Energy, Hefei Comprehensive National Science Center under Grant No. GXXT-2020-004. Numerical computations were performed on the ShenMa High Performance Computing Cluster in Institute of Plasma Physics, Chinese Academy of Sciences."],"id":"S01-000.00-361909","identifier":[{"id":"85130352305","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-bfcf72ff-51b4-4fe9-aafd-9dc7de526f2d"],"keyword":["Blob","Divertor","ITER","Magnetic drift","SOL power width","Turbulence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8BFC17D291653C9E36A64E05D2A4D0F6"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/337665797/2203.09039.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"X.","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, X.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","name_org":"Nielsen, A. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Rasmussen, J. J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"V.","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","name_org":"Naulin, V.","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, L.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"dingpau","last":"Ding","name":"Ding, R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/ac5eab","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"7","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"076022","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"62"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85130352305"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-bfcf72ff-51b4-4fe9-aafd-9dc7de526f2d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simulations of scrape-off layer power width for EAST H-mode plasma and ITER 15 MA baseline scenario by 2D electrostatic turbulence code","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-361909","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to investigate the early-life development of the skin microbiome in atopic derma-titis. Nineteen infants with atopic dermatitis and 19 healthy infants were evaluated 3 times, at 3 months intervals, within the first 30 months of life. Tape-strips were collected from volar forearms, cheeks, and ec-zema lesions, and the skin microbiome was assessed by 16S rRNA sequencing. Both the community struc-ture and richness of the skin microbiome of infants with atopic dermatitis differed significantly from that of healthy infants, with greater richness in healthy infants. For infants with atopic dermatitis, the community composition was not dominated by Staphylo-cocci. For healthy infants, community composition and richness correlated significantly with age, while such a pattern was not revealed in infants with atopic der-matitis. This suggests a slower maturation of the skin microbiome in atopic dermatitis, which precedes the staphylococcal predominance observed in older children and adults.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Olesen, Caroline Meyer","Clausen, Maja Lisa","Agner, Tove","Asplund, Maria","Rasmussen, Linett","Yüksel, Yasemine T.","Andersen, Paal S.","Litman, Thomas","Hansen, Anders Johannes","Barnes, Christopher James"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-425528"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Atopic dermatitis","Infant","Skin microbiome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"altered maturation of the skin microbiome in infants with atopic dermatitis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/actadv.v102.2275","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-425528","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9811288","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"35818733","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85142377375","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-35fb64f0-1304-4490-a45d-b59105dee305"],"keyword":["atopic dermatitis","infant","skin microbiome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-377EA14BA57B7E989529BB8B073741B7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/327473457/2275.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/actadv.v102.2275","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Caroline M.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"8001c05e-2b42-4c6f-a139-7c18c8093f4a","name":"Olesen, Caroline Meyer","name_org":"Olesen, Caroline M.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maja Lisa","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","name":"Clausen, Maja Lisa","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tove","key":"agnerpau","last":"Agner","locid":"fead5c49-b790-42e2-8793-e16de84b7bee","name":"Agner, Tove","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria","key":"asplundpau","last":"Asplund","locid":"6ed20771-3a51-4e77-b434-89b50a38ec30","name":"Asplund, Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linett","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0543380d-1a58-4cdf-b490-9c1861185f30","name":"Rasmussen, Linett","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yasemine T.","key":"yükselpau","last":"Yüksel","name":"Yüksel, Yasemine T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Paal S.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Paal S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"litmanpau","last":"Litman","locid":"3affc55b-df0a-436a-b3bd-2cb3bf560602","name":"Litman, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-6068-901X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders J.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"846e4329-bfc5-4ddb-968c-445cdb16825a","name":"Hansen, Anders Johannes","name_org":"Hansen, Anders J.","orcid":"0000-0002-1890-2702","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher J.","key":"barnespau","last":"Barnes","locid":"369a0b39-cf9f-4240-b9b4-4eb69c878bcd","name":"Barnes, Christopher James","name_org":"Barnes, Christopher J.","orcid":"0000-0001-6800-4233","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35818733"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2340/actadv.v102.2275","issn":["00015555","16512057"],"issn_org":["00015555"],"journal":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","paperid":"adv00817","status":"p","title":"Acta Dermato-Venereologica","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142377375"],"se