{"abstract":"Coastal waters are highly productive and diverse ecosystems, often dominated by marine Submerged Aquatic Vegetation (SAV) and strongly affected by a range of human pressures. Due to their important ecosystem functions, both researchers and managers have for decades investigated changes in SAV abundance and growth dynamics to understand linkages to human perturbations. In European coastal waters monitoring of marine SAV communities traditionally combines diver observations and/or video recordings to determine e.g. spatial coverage and species composition. While these techniques provide very useful data, they are rather time consuming, labour intensive and limited in their spatial coverage. In this manuscript, we compare traditional and emerging remote sensing technologies used to monitor marine SAV, which include satellite and occupied aircraft operations, aerial drones and acoustics. We introduce these techniques and identify their main strengths and limitations. Finally, we provide recommendations for researchers and managers to choose the appropriate techniques for future surveys and monitoring programs. This article is protected by copyright. All rights reserved.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Lønborg, Christian","Thomasberger, Aris","Stæhr, Peter A.","Stockmarr, Anders","Sengupta, Sayantan","Rasmussen, Mikkel Lydholm","Nielsen, Lisbeth Tangaa","Hansen, Lars Boye","Timmermann, Karen"],"cuid":["S02-097.55-017246"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lønborg, Christian"],"keyword":["Classification","Depth","Ecosystem","Eelgrass Zostera marina","Environmental Monitoring methods","Habitat","High resolution","Humans","Image analysis","Indicators","Long term changes","Monitoring programs","Observations","Plants","Remote Sensing Technology methods","Remote sensing","Submerged aquatic vegetation","Technology","side scan sonar"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"submerged aquatic vegetation overview of monitoring techniques used for the identification and determination of spatial distribution in european coastal waters","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/229258417/Submerged_Final_L_nborg.etal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-097.55-017246","identifier":[{"id":"34750976","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000725119200001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85120460824","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-3e84cf0c-028d-4822-bf55-45f5b9c38e74","dtu-8388eedc-f235-41f7-bc8a-e2068b28aa5b"],"keyword":["AERIAL SYSTEMS","CLASSIFICATION","DEPTH","EELGRASS ZOSTERA-MARINA","Ecosystem","Environmental Monitoring/methods","HABITAT","HIGH-RESOLUTION","Humans","INDICATORS","Image analysis","LONG-TERM CHANGES","Monitoring programs","Observations","Plants","Remote Sensing Technology/methods","Remote sensing","SEAGRASS COVER","SIDE-SCAN SONAR","Submerged aquatic vegetation","Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5DB0C27796B52ECE32AB0E7A672300A0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/229258417/Submerged_Final_L_nborg.etal.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/262807068/ieam.4552.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Applied Marine Ecology and Modelling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Coastal Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"lønborgpau","last":"Lønborg","locid":"8b3df852-bf56-4f89-954a-f8b76330e002","name":"Lønborg, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-8380-0238","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aris","key":"thomasbergerpau","last":"Thomasberger","locid":"cb86f5d0-2d36-4832-bc19-1c823ed35daa","name":"Thomasberger, Aris","orcid":"0000-0002-0829-3771","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter A U","key":"staehrpau","last":"Staehr","locid":"1d2daf18-7ace-48c9-b950-7fb3bdc0a173","name":"Stæhr, Peter A.","name_org":"Staehr, Peter A U","orcid":"0000-0002-1580-4875","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"stockmarrpau","last":"Stockmarr","locid":"f8ce8f15-f38a-4f99-a8c6-08b0cd7b0f6a","name":"Stockmarr, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8681-2370","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sayantan","key":"senguptapau","last":"Sengupta","locid":"b01a10cb-1fbb-43ed-8941-c8cce0dcb297","name":"Sengupta, Sayantan","orcid":"0000-0003-3820-495X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Lydholm","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Lydholm","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth Tangaa","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lisbeth Tangaa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Boye","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars Boye","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"timmermannpau","last":"Timmermann","locid":"abfd7b7d-0497-46ec-a26c-ba1772c111df","name":"Timmermann, Karen","orcid":"0000-0001-5989-4692","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34750976"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/ieam.4552","issn":["15513777","15513793"],"issn_org":["15513777"],"issue":"4","journal":"Integrated Environmental Assessment and Management","pages":"892-908","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Integrated Environmental Assessment and Management","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85120460824"],"sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3e84cf0c-028d-4822-bf55-45f5b9c38e74","dtu-8388eedc-f235-41f7-bc8a-e2068b28aa5b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Submerged aquatic vegetation : Overview of monitoring techniques used for the identification and determination of spatial distribution in European coastal waters","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.55-017246","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Ice-core timescales are vital for the understanding of past climate; hence they should be updated whenever significant amounts of new data become available. Here, the Greenland ice-core chronology GICC05 was revised for the last 3835 years by synchronizing six deep ice cores and three shallow ice cores from the central Greenland ice sheet. A new method was applied by combining automated counting of annual layers on multiple parallel proxies and manual fine-tuning. A layer counting bias was found in all ice cores because of site-specific signal disturbances; therefore the manual comparison of all ice cores was deemed necessary to increase timescale accuracy. After examining sources of error and their correlation lengths, the uncertainty rate was quantified to be 1 year per century. The new timescale is younger than GICC05 by about 13 years at 3835 years ago. The most recent 800 years are largely unaffected by the revision. Between 800 and 2000 years ago, the offset between timescales increases steadily, with the steepest offset occurring between 800 and 1100 years ago. Moreover, offset oscillations of about 5 years around the average are observed between 2500 and 3800 years ago. The non-linear offset behavior is attributed to previous mismatches of volcanic eruptions, to the much more extensive dataset available to this study, and to the finer resolution of the new ice-core ammonium matching. By analysis of the common variations in cosmogenic radionuclides, the new ice-core timescale is found to be in alignment with the IntCal20 curve (Reimer et al., 2020).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Sinnl, Giulia","Winstrup, Mai","Erhardt, Tobias","Cook, Eliza","Jensen, Camilla Marie","Svensson, Anders","Vinther, Bo Mollesoe","Muscheler, Raimund","Rasmussen, Sune Olander"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035416"],"filters":{"added":"2022-07","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Sinnl, Giulia"],"country":["Sweden","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","University of Bern"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a multi ice core annual layer counted greenland ice core chronology for the last 000000003800 years gicc000000000021","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/cp-18-1125-2022","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-035416","identifier":[{"id":"85131088959","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000799217500001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["dtu-7b1d70c3-1ef5-4bc4-af0b-a2aab7350f9b","ku-339884e8-ff76-4775-9031-1ebf5e98d112"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3F1CC6EC476D22F0902463F3BBD5CFD2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/308325417/cp_18_1125_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.5194/cp-18-1125-2022","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277917538/cp_18_1125_2022.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Space Research and Technology, Geodesy and Earth Observation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Giulia","key":"sinnlpau","last":"Sinnl","locid":"0685a93a-f60f-4801-956b-c86d65590e7f","name":"Sinnl, Giulia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mai","key":"winstruppau","last":"Winstrup","locid":"5b8bc307-4b30-4668-9e2c-646716b77fcd","name":"Winstrup, Mai","orcid":"0000-0002-4794-4004","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tobias","key":"erhardtpau","last":"Erhardt","name":"Erhardt, Tobias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Eliza","key":"cookpau","last":"Cook","locid":"5f8d7356-0509-430c-9dc6-4f8ca38bb482","name":"Cook, Eliza","orcid":"0000-0001-7927-7974","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Marie","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Camilla Marie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"e0501b84-a817-417e-9c70-9601c6b26cb8","name":"Svensson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-4364-6085","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Møllesøe","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"0179bd8e-644a-4f98-a641-1bc374aabdd8","name":"Vinther, Bo Møllesøe","orcid":"0000-0002-6078-771X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Raimund","key":"muschelerpau","last":"Muscheler","name":"Muscheler, Raimund","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sune Olander","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3f1d51b2-26a1-4a40-af3f-05f030c7bb9d","name":"Rasmussen, Sune Olander","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3611","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.5194/cp-18-1125-2022","issn":["18149324","18149332"],"issn_org":["18149324"],"issue":"5","journal":"Climate of the Past","pages":"1125-1150","publisher":"Copernicus GmbH","status":"p","title":"Climate of the Past","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131088959"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-7b1d70c3-1ef5-4bc4-af0b-a2aab7350f9b","ku-339884e8-ff76-4775-9031-1ebf5e98d112"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A multi-ice-core, annual-layer-counted Greenland ice-core chronology for the last 3800 years: GICC21","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-035416","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: We compared dexamethasone 12 versus 6 mg daily for up to 10 days in patients with coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19) and severe hypoxaemia in the international, randomised, blinded COVID STEROID 2 trial. In the primary, conventional analyses, the predefined statistical significance thresholds were not reached. We conducted a pre-planned Bayesian analysis to facilitate probabilistic interpretation. METHODS: We analysed outcome data within 90 days in the intention-to-treat population (data available in 967 to 982 patients) using Bayesian models with various sensitivity analyses. Results are presented as median posterior probabilities with 95% credible intervals (CrIs) and probabilities of different effect sizes with 12 mg dexamethasone. RESULTS: The adjusted mean difference on days alive without life support at day 28 (primary outcome) was 1.3 days (95% CrI -0.3 to 2.9; 94.2% probability of benefit). Adjusted relative risks and probabilities of benefit on serious adverse reactions was 0.85 (0.63 to 1.16; 84.1%) and on mortality 0.87 (0.73 to 1.03; 94.8%) at day 28 and 0.88 (0.75 to 1.02; 95.1%) at day 90. Probabilities of benefit on days alive without life support and days alive out of hospital at day 90 were 85 and 95.7%, respectively. Results were largely consistent across sensitivity analyses, with relatively low probabilities of clinically important harm with 12 mg on all outcomes in all analyses. CONCLUSION: We found high probabilities of benefit and low probabilities of clinically important harm with dexamethasone 12 mg versus 6 mg daily in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxaemia on all outcomes up to 90 days.","author_count":49,"contributors":["Granholm, Anders","Munch, Marie Warrer","Myatra, Sheila Nainan","Vijayaraghavan, Bharath Kumar Tirupakuzhi","Cronhjort, Maria","Wahlin, Rebecka Rubenson","Jakob, Stephan M.","Cioccari, Luca","Kjær, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Vesterlund, Gitte Kingo","Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Helleberg, Marie","Møller, Morten Hylander","Benfield, Thomas","Venkatesh, Balasubramanian","Hammond, Naomi E.","Micallef, Sharon","Bassi, Abhinav","John, Oommen","Jha, Vivekanand","Kristiansen, Klaus Tjelle","Ulrik, Charlotte Suppli","Jørgensen, Vibeke Lind","Smitt, Margit","Bestle, Morten H.","Andreasen, Anne Sofie","Poulsen, Lone Musaeus","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Strøm, Thomas","Møller, Anders","Khan, Mohd Saif","Padmanaban, Ajay","Divatia, Jigeeshu Vasishtha","Saseedharan, Sanjith","Borawake, Kapil","Kapadia, Farhad","Dixit, Subhal","Chawla, Rajesh","Shukla, Urvi","Amin, Pravin","Chew, Michelle S.","Wamberg, Christian Aage","Gluud, Christian","Lange, Theis","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-098.46-002011"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Granholm, Anders"],"country":["Australia","India","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Apollo Hospitals Group","Bombay Hospital Institute of Medical Sciences","Bombay Hospital and Medical Research Centre","Chennai Critical Care Consultants","Hinduja Hospital","Homi Bhabha National Institute","Imperial College London","Indraprastha Apollo Hospitals","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Linköping University","Manipal Academy of Higher Education","P.D. Hinduja National Hospital and Medical Research Centre","Prasanna School of Public Health","Rajendra Institute of Medical Sciences","Royal North Shore Hospital","S.L. Raheja Hospital","Sanjeevan Hospital","Symbiosis University Hospital and Research Centre","Tata Memorial Hospital","The George Institute for Global Health","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital of Bern","University of Bern","University of New South Wales","Vishwaraj Hospital"],"keyword":["Bayes Theorem","Bayesian analysis","COVID 19 drug therapy","Corticosteroids","Covid 19","Critical Illness","Dexamethasone","Humans","Hypoxaemia","Hypoxia","SARS CoV 2","Steroids"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dexamethasone 000000000012 mg versus 000000000006 mg for patients with covid 000000000019 and severe hypoxaemia a pre planned secondary bayesian analysis of the covid steroid 000000000002 trial","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8579417/pdf/134_2021_Article_6573.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["AG, MWM, MBNK, GKV, TSM, MHM and AP are affiliated with the Department of Intensive Care at Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, which has received grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation during the conduct of the trial; and grants from Pfizer, Fresenius Kabi, The Novo Nordisk Foundation, and Sygeforsikringen “danmark” outside the submitted work. SMJ and LC are affiliated with Inselspital, Bern University Hospital, University of Bern, Bern, Switzerland, which has received grants from Edwards Lifesciences Services GmbH, Phagenesis Limited, and Nestlé; all outside the submitted work. TB has received grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation, Simonsen Foundation, Lundbeck Foundation, Kai Hansen Foundation, and Erik and Susanna Olesen’s Charitable Fund; grants and personal fees from GSK, Pfizer, and Gilead; personal fees from Boehringer Ingelheim, MSD, and Pentabase ApS; all outside the submitted work. BV and NEH have received grants from Baxter outside the submitted work. VJ has received grants and personal fees from Baxter Healthcare; personal fees from Astra Zeneca, Visterra, Chinook, and NephroPlus; all outside the submitted work. CSU has received grants and personal fees from GSK, Sanofi Genzyme, Astra Zeneca, Teva, OrionPharma, Boehringer-Ingelheim, Actelion and Chiesi; grants, personal fees and non-financial support from Novartis; all outside the submitted work.JVD has received personal fees (paid to his institution) from Edwards India outside the submitted work. PA has received personal fees from CIPLA, Dr. Reddy’s Laboratories, Abbott Nutrition and Sanofi; all outside the submitted work. The remaining authors declared no known conflicts of interest. The COVID STEROID 2 trial was funded by the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant number 0062998) and supported by Rigshospitalet’s Research Council (E-22703–06). None of the funders had any influence on trial design, conduct, analysis, or decision to report. AG’s salary is paid by a grant from Sygeforsikringen “danmark”, which had no influence on this trial."],"id":"S03-098.46-002011","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8579417","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000716840800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85118888068","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34757439","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-27f05eb5-feee-4a06-8485-11c7e2500de7","ku-b9dbadcd-ebf1-47d1-a3a8-00f80dba0da5","sdu-0c535312-63ec-4f59-8461-236657a1a2ae"],"keyword":["Bayes Theorem","Bayesian analysis","COVID-19","COVID-19/drug therapy","Corticosteroids","Critical illness","Dexamethasone","Humans","Hypoxaemia","Hypoxia","SARS-CoV-2","Steroids"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-30E3816E5FFEFDB25B7B1B4AA4B298A5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8579417/pdf/134_2021_Article_6573.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://europepmc.org/copyright","type":"rem","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/pmc8579417?pdf=render","version"