,"first":"Mehul S.","key":"shahmehulspau","last":"Shah","name":"Shah, Mehul S.","rank":45,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"45","corresponding":null,"first":"Iben S.","key":"darfeltibenspau","last":"Darfelt","name":"Darfelt, Iben S.","rank":46,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 26","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"gluudchristianpau","last":"Gluud","locid":"9a304637-8b8a-4eb6-88a4-2108c618ce38","name":"Gluud, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-8861-0799","rank":47,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Theis","key":"langetheispau","last":"Lange","locid":"e4664578-01fc-4a93-8efd-1dbffb72cdd6","name":"Lange, Theis","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-8347","rank":48,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 1 2 8 18 3","first":"Anders","key":"perneranderspau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":49,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35359168"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00134-022-06677-2","issn":["03424642","09351701"],"issn_org":["03424642"],"issue":"5","journal":"Intensive Care Medicine","pages":"580-589","publisher":"Springer Science and Business Media Deutschland GmbH","status":"p","title":"Intensive Care Medicine","volume":"48"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85127422999"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Undetermined","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","collaboration for research in intensive care"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-ded9c1cd-d80d-43a0-b3e1-2a8824caf961","au-bd391860-8026-45f5-9afb-bcc76754b06d","ku-a2b2943f-5fc1-4888-8848-85b57fb2b277","sdu-42add2bf-1966-4beb-b283-fe190b988edb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Long-term outcomes of dexamethasone 12 mg versus 6 mg in patients with COVID-19 and severe hypoxaemia","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-098.88-010626","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The management of patients with atrial fibrillation (AF) and malignancy is challenging given the paucity of evidence supporting their appropriate clinical management. PURPOSE: To evaluate the outcomes of patients with active or prior malignancy in a contemporary cohort of European AF patients. METHODS: Patients enrolled in the EURObservational Research Programme in AF General Long-Term Registry were categorized into 3 categories: No Malignancy (NoMal), Prior Malignancy (PriorMal) and Active Malignancy (ActiveMal). The primary outcomes were all-cause death and the composite outcome MACE. RESULTS: A total of 10 383 patients were analysed. Of these, 9597 (92.4%) were NoMal patients, 577 (5.6%) PriorMal and 209 (2%) ActiveMal. Lack of any antithrombotic treatment was more prevalent in ActiveMal patients (12.4%) as compared to other groups (5.0% vs 6.3% for PriorMal and NoMal, p < .001). After a median follow-up of 730 days, there were 982 (9.5%) deaths and 950 (9.7%) MACE events. ActiveMal was independently associated with a higher risk for all-cause death (HR 2.90, 95% CI 2.23-3.76) and MACE (HR 1.54, 95% CI 1.03-2.31), as well as any haemorrhagic events and major bleeding (OR 2.42, 95% CI 1.49-3.91 and OR 4.18, 95% CI 2.49-7.01, respectively). Use of oral anticoagulants was not significantly associated with a higher risk for all-cause death or bleeding in ActiveMal patients. CONCLUSIONS: In a large contemporary cohort of AF patients, active malignancy was independently associated with all-cause death, MACE and haemorrhagic events. Use of anticoagulants was not associated with a higher risk of all-cause death in patients with active malignancies.","author_count":25,"contributors":["Malavasi, Vincenzo L.","Vitolo, Marco","Proietti, Marco","Diemberger, Igor","Fauchier, Laurent","Marin, Francisco","Nabauer, Michael","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Dan, Gheorghe-Andrei","Kalarus, Zbigniew","Tavazzi, Luigi","Maggioni, Aldo Pietro","Lane, Deirdre A.","Lip, Gregory Y H","Boriani, Giuseppe","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-074812"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Boriani, Giuseppe"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Associazione Nazionale Medici Cardiologi Ospedalieri","Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Bologna Policlinico S. Orsola – Malpighi","Azienda USL di Modena","Carol Davila University of Medicine and Pharmacy","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Colentina Hospital","GVM Care and Research S.p.A.","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","IRCCS Istituti Clinici Scientifici Maugeri S.p.A. SB - Pavia","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Maria Cecilia Hospital","Medical University of Silesia in Katowice","Silesian Centre for Heart Diseases","University of Belgrade","University of Bologna","University of Liverpool","University of Milan","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia"],"keyword":["All cause death","Anticoagulants","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Atrial fibrillation","Cancer","Hemorrhage chemically induced","Humans","Malignancy","NOACs","Neoplasms drug therapy","Registries","Registry","Risk Factors","Stroke complications"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"