cid":"fd7755f7-451a-448c-8679-baccccd2d85a","name":"Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup","rank":25,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["35305020"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/eci.13773","issn":["00142972","0960135X"],"issn_org":["00142972"],"issue":"7","journal":"European Journal of Clinical Investigation","paperid":"e13773","publisher":"Wiley","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Clinical Investigation","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131903509"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5553c5f3-4e50-4e25-978c-1c01d5cd95cb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of malignancy on outcomes in European patients with atrial fibrillation : A report from the ESC-EHRA EURObservational Research Programme in Atrial Fibrillation General Long-Term Registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-074812","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aims: The safety of digoxin therapy in atrial fibrillation (AF) remains ill-defined. We aimed to evaluate the effects of digoxin over beta-blocker therapy in AF. Methods and results: Patients with AF who were treated with either digoxin or a beta blocker from the ESC-EHRA EORP AF (European Society of Cardiology-European Heart Rhythm Association EURObservational Research Programme Atrial Fibrillation) General Long-Term Registry were included. Outcomes of interest were all-cause mortality, cardiovascular (CV) mortality, non-CV mortality, quality of life, and number of patients with unplanned hospitalizations. Of 6377 patients, 549 (8.6%) were treated with digoxin. Over 24 months, there were 550 (8.6%) all-cause mortality events and 1304 (23.6%) patients with unplanned emergency hospitalizations. Compared to beta blocker, digoxin therapy was associated with increased all-cause mortality [hazard ratio (HR) 1.90 (95% confidence interval, CI, 1.48-2.44)], CV mortality [HR 2.18 (95% CI 1.47-3.21)], and non-CV mortality [HR 1.68 (95% CI 1.02-2.75)] with reduced quality of life [health utility score 0.555 (±0.406) vs. 0.705 (±0.346), P < 0.001] but no differences in emergency hospitalizations [HR 1.00 (95% CI 0.56-1.80)] or AF-related hospitalizations [HR 0.95 (95% CI 0.60-1.52)]. On multivariable analysis, there were no differences in any of the outcomes between both groups, after accounting for potential confounders. Similar results were obtained in the subgroups of patients with permanent AF and coexisting heart failure. There were no differences in outcomes between AF patients receiving digoxin with and without chronic kidney disease. Conclusion: Poor outcomes related to the use of digoxin over beta-blocker therapy in terms of excess mortality and reduced quality of life are associated with the presence of other risk factors rather than digoxin per se. The choice of digoxin or beta-blocker therapy had no influence on the incidence of unplanned hospitalizations.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Ding, Wern Yew","Boriani, Giuseppe","Marin, Francisco","Blomström-Lundqvist, Carina","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Fauchier, Laurent","Lip, Gregory Y H","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-078083"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Lip, Gregory Y H"],"country":["France","Italy","Serbia","Spain","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","University Hospital of Modena","University of Belgrade","University of Liverpool","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Adrenergic beta Antagonists adverse effects","Atrial Fibrillation complications","Atrial fibrillation","Beta blocker","CKD","Digoxin","Digoxin adverse effects","EORP AF","Heart failure","Hospitalizations","Humans","Mortality","Quality of Life","Rate control","Registries","Registry"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"outcomes of digoxin vs beta blocker in atrial fibrillation report from esc ehra eorp af long term general registry","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url"