{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Kaasgaard, Mette","Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","Løkke, Anders","Vuust, Peter","Hilberg, Ole","Bodtger, Uffe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-603880"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-04","start":"2022-06-02","title":"Nordic Lung Congress 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sing a lung are changes in physical exercise capacity and quality of life associated after a 000000000010 weeks singing for lung health programme within pulmonary rehabilitation for patients with copd","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-603880","ids":["sdu-6b5cbee9-2c68-448d-94fc-6fd0d5099e02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-ABE058FC0F45B4AA2E7D14CE93EE1C9C"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Zealand University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"kaasgaardpau","last":"Kaasgaard","locid":"2b472c7a-7c51-482b-9155-59dea1d8ae37","name":"Kaasgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-3833-2943","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Bech","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"18525822-35fd-4cd8-afdd-a608be44cc84","name":"Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","orcid":"0000-0003-1213-9483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Løkke","key":"ottesenpau","last":"Ottesen","locid":"db3d3870-0459-4783-8f0b-6a8e5d9dce78","name":"Løkke, Anders","name_org":"Ottesen, Anders Løkke","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-4141","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"vuustpau","last":"Vuust","name":"Vuust, Peter","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hilbergpau","last":"Hilberg","locid":"6c545c65-1d94-45a3-a8b4-f90eae06d248","name":"Hilberg, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-3463","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe","key":"bodtgerpau","last":"Bodtger","locid":"2f4e70da-63bb-4b8d-af09-2a959d6df5e8","name":"Bodtger, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-1231-9209","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6b5cbee9-2c68-448d-94fc-6fd0d5099e02"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sing-a-Lung: Are changes in physical exercise capacity and quality of life associated after a 10 weeks’ Singing for Lung Health programme within pulmonary rehabilitation for patients with COPD?","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-603880","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Importance: Children and adults spend large amounts of their leisure time using screen media, which may affect their health and behavior. Objective: To investigate the effect of reducing household recreational screen media use on physical activity and sleep in children and adults. Design, Setting, and Participants: This was a cluster randomized clinical trial with a 2-week follow-up. Enrollment began on June 6, 2019, and ended on March 30, 2021. This study included a population-based sample from 10 Danish municipalities. A total of 89 families (181 children and 164 adults) were recruited based on a population-based survey on screen media habits in families with children. To be eligible, the responding parent had to list self-reported recreational screen use greater than the 40th percentile of recreational screen time use in the source population (>2.4 hours per day). In addition, the parent had to be full-time employed (with no regular night shifts) or enrolled in full-time education. Interventions: Families were randomly assigned to the screen media reduction intervention (45 families, 86 children, 82 adults) designed to ensure participant compliance to a maximum use of screen media (≤3 hours per week) for a 2-week period. Families randomly assigned to the control group (44 families, 95 children, 82 adults) were instructed to carry on as usual. Main Outcomes and Measures: The primary outcome was between-group difference in leisure nonsedentary activity (in minutes per day) measured by combined thigh and waist accelerometry. Secondary outcomes included other physical activity and sleep parameters measured by single-channel electroencephalography. Results: Among the 89 randomized families (intervention group [45 families]: 86 children; mean [SD] age, 8.6 [2.7] years; 44 boys [51%]; 42 girls [49%]; control group [44 families]: 95 children, mean [SD] age, 9.5 [2.5] years; 38 boys [40%]; 57 girls [60%]), 157 children (87%) had complete data on the primary outcome. Eighty-three children (97%) in the intervention group were compliant to the screen use reduction during the intervention. The mean (SD) change in leisure nonsedentary activity in the intervention group was 44.8 (63.5) minutes per day and in the control group was 1.0 (55.1) minute per day (intention-to-treat between-group mean difference, 45.8 minutes per day; 95% CI, 27.9-63.6 minutes per day; P < .001). No significant between-group mean differences were observed between intervention and control for the electroencephalography-based sleep outcomes. Conclusions and Relevance: In this cluster randomized clinical trial, a recreational screen media reduction intervention resulted in a substantial increase in children's engagement in physical activity. The large effect size suggests that the high levels of recreational screen media use seen in many children should be a public health concern. Trial Registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT04098913.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jesper","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Sørensen, Sarah Overgaard","Mortensen, Sofie Rath","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Brønd, Jan Christian","Brage, Søren","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-604665"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grøntved, Anders"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Cambridge"],"keyword":["Accelerometry","Adult","Child","Exercise","Female","Humans","Male","Parents education","Screen time","Sleep"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO"],"OT":["PROgrez: Patient-Related Objectives: Generating better Rehabilitation, Treatment, Exercise and Diagnostics - Region Zealand"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-U-SDU","PROgrez: Patient-Related Objectives: Generating better Rehabilitation, Treatment, Exercise and Diagnostics - Region Zealand"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of limiting recreational screen media use on physical activity and sleep in families with children a cluster randomized clinical trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9127712","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-604665","identifier":[{"id":"35604678","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9127712","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85131162374","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6e0ba4da-f94d-42e2-ab64-7030b345f402"],"keyword":["Accelerometry","Adult","Child","Exercise","Female","Humans","Male","Parents/education","Screen Time","Sleep"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-095A520DFAE2FC004C104128D3DE86F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC9127712","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-STENO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["PROgrez: Patient-Related Objectives: Generating better Rehabilitation, Treatment, Exercise and Diagnostics - Region Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of cambridge","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Cambridge","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f321394d-8abe-49b2-ab02-1b528e734f63","name":"Pedersen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9475-0341","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Gillies Banke","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8b86a1ef-e6c1-4de3-8300-e30d144bbf60","name":"Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","orcid":"0000-0002-2114-2185","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Overgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"ee7fa7d0-8bb4-4eca-a31d-26ce06940514","name":"Sørensen, Sarah Overgaard","orcid":"0000-0002-3953-3387","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Sofie Rath","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"ce405612-8eed-42e1-9ba3-63ca26241605","name":"Mortensen, Sofie Rath","orcid":"0000-0002-9550-1507","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Grønholt","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"e9ad7180-8cce-4e88-9707-18dedc4c73e0","name":"Olesen, Line Grønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-6588-8878","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Christian","key":"brøndpau","last":"Brønd","locid":"da4ecea2-2b7f-4027-9859-416024dca432","name":"Brønd, Jan Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6718-3022","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"bragepau","last":"Brage","locid":"5dc5eeb6-2ba6-4478-9111-eb87dc9d54d9","name":"Brage, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-1265-7355","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"751d26de-66d4-4ef9-8183-880c48c96dc7","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-5666-9614","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedpau","last":"Grøntved","locid":"393b1ca1-e658-437c-9ca3-73aea925ad58","name":"Grøntved, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1584-679X","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35604678"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jamapediatrics.2022.1519","issn":["21686203","21686211"],"issn_org":["10724710"],"issue":"8","journal":"JAMA Pediatrics","pages":"741-749","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA Pediatrics","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131162374"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6e0ba4da-f94d-42e2-ab64-7030b345f402"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effects of Limiting Recreational Screen Media Use on Physical Activity and Sleep in Families With Children : A Cluster Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-604665","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Studies have linked higher digital screen use with poorer mental health. However, there is limited experimental evidence to suggest a causal relationship. In this trial, we aimed to investigate the effects of limiting recreational digital screen use on mental well-being, mood, and biomarkers of stress in healthy young and middle-aged adults. We randomly allocated 89 families (including 164 adults) to participate in an extensive screen media reduction intervention or control. Participants in the intervention group were instructed to decrease their recreational screen use to less than 3 hours/week/person. Intervention compliance was assessed using applications and tv-monitors. Overall subjective mental well-being and mood, and collected daily biomarkers of stress (salivary cortisol and cortisone) was assessed at baseline and 2-week follow-up. Reducing recreational digital screen use resulted in significantly improved self-reported well-being and mood in adults allocated to the intervention compared to control. We observed no intervention effects for biomarkers of stress. (ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT04098913, 23/09/2019).","author_count":9,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jesper","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Sørensen, Sarah Overgaard","Mortensen, Sofie Rath","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Brage, Søren","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Puterman, Eli","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-629855"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Grøntved, Anders"],"country":["Canada","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of British Columbia (UBC)","University of Cambridge"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-STENO","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of limiting digital screen use on well being mood and biomarkers of stress in adults","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44184-022-00015-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-629855","identifier":[{"id":"37521498","type":"pmid"},{"id":"105006459590","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9554843","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-c5b68fee-e14e-4896-a00c-29118cf48755"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E59C751ABEF6E01FE51C3106F2B4BC06"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/210580756/s44184_022_00015_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s44184-022-00015-6","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"steno diabetes centers","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-STENO","l3nn":"Steno Diabetes Centers","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Steno Diabetes Centers","namevar":["Steno Diabetes 