l,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"graffpau","last":"Graff","locid":"2312aabc-cecb-4598-aede-4aa22cc2f298","name":"Graff, Claus","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-9781","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Gaarsdal","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","name":"Holst, Anders Gaarsdal","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas Bille","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jonas Bille","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten Wagner","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Morten Wagner","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34673253"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.hrthm.2021.09.041","issn":["15475271","15563871"],"issn_org":["15475271"],"issue":"2","journal":"Heart Rhythm","pages":"252-259","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Heart Rhythm","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118526253"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","copenhagen general practitioners’ laboratory"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-96fde0f7-9e23-4b60-8249-460caa1e8ed7","ku-5b44f1da-1bd3-49f8-9cdd-3ff06053e316"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Fascicular heart blocks and risk of adverse cardiovascular outcomes : Results from a large primary care population","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.96-007317","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"SARS coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) continues to evolve and new variants emerge. Using nationwide Danish data, we estimate the transmission dynamics of SARS-CoV-2 Omicron subvariants BA.1 and BA.2 within households. Among 22,678 primary cases, we identified 17,319 secondary infections among 50,588 household contacts during a 1–7 day follow-up. The secondary attack rate (SAR) was 29% and 39% in households infected with Omicron BA.1 and BA.2, respectively. BA.2 was associated with increased susceptibility of infection for unvaccinated household contacts (Odds Ratio (OR) 1.99; 95%–CI 1.72-2.31), fully vaccinated contacts (OR 2.26; 95%–CI 1.95–2.62) and booster-vaccinated contacts (OR 2.65; 95%–CI 2.29–3.08), compared to BA.1. We also found increased infectiousness from unvaccinated primary cases infected with BA.2 compared to BA.1 (OR 2.47; 95%–CI 2.15–2.84), but not for fully vaccinated (OR 0.66; 95%–CI 0.57–0.78) or booster-vaccinated primary cases (OR 0.69; 95%–CI 0.59–0.82). Omicron BA.2 is inherently more transmissible than BA.1. Its immune-evasive properties also reduce the protective effect of vaccination against infection, but do not increase infectiousness of breakthrough infections from vaccinated individuals.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Lyngse, Frederik Plesner","Kirkeby, Carsten","Denwood, Matt","Christiansen, Lasse Engbo","Mølbak, Kåre","Holten Møller, Camilla","Skov, Robert Leo","Krause, Tyra Grove","Rasmussen, Morten","Sieber, Raphael","Johannesen, Thor Bech","Lillebaek, Troels","Fonager, Jannik","Fomsgaard, Anders","Møller, Frederik Trier","Stegger, Marc","Overvad, Maria","Spiess, Katja","Mortensen, Laust Hvas"],"cuid":["S02-097.96-033881"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Lyngse, Frederik Plesner"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Danish Ministry of Health"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"household transmission of sars cov 000000000002 omicron variant of concern subvariants ba 000000000001 and ba 000000000002 in denmark","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-33498-0","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Frederik Plesner Lyngse is supported in part by grants from the Independent Research Fund Denmark (Grant no. 9061-00035B.); Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF17OC0026542); the Danish National Research Foundation through its grant (DNRF-134) to the Center for Economic Behavior and Inequality (CEBI) at the University of Copenhagen. Laust Hvas Mortensen is supported in part by grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF17OC0027594, NNF17OC0027812). We thank Statens Serum Institut and The Danish Health Data Authority for collecting and providing access to data access. We also thank the rest of the Expert Group for Mathematical Modeling of COVID-19 at Statens Serum Institut for helpful discussions. The authors wish to thank the Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium for genotyping SARS-CoV-2 positive samples. We thank Simon Kyllebæk Andersen and Carl Benjamin Simpson (Department of Economics, University of Copenhagen) for proofreading the manuscript. Frederik Plesner Lyngse is supported in part by grants from the Independent Research Fund Denmark (Grant no. 9061-00035B.); Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF17OC0026542); the Danish National Research Foundation through its grant (DNRF-134) to the Center for Economic Behavior and Inequality (CEBI) at the University of Copenhagen. Laust Hvas Mortensen is supported in part by grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (grant no. NNF17OC0027594, NNF17OC0027812)."],"id":"S02-097.96-033881","identifier":[{"id":"36180438","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85139243925","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9524324","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-3a03f7b5-3b86-49d0-b778-525e2588569f","ku-ae8199cc-bb2d-4e2f-b526-083fb38af823"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2FE8DA8E0FD9779C7FE89F4D7ED3E950"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-022-33498-0","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321955464/Fulltext.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/296748136/s41467_022_33498_0.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Economics, Department of Economics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Ministry of Health"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science, Dynamical Systems"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2 3","first":"Frederik Plesner","key":"lyngsefrederikplesnerpau","last":"Lyngse","locid":"818371f1-eab1-4624-b7a7-efc8dfd282b7","name":"Lyngse, Frederik Plesner","orcid":"0000-0002-0584-6115","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Carsten","key":"kirkebycarstenpau","last":"Kirkeby","locid":"ea24c9a4-7aa6-40f3-9afb-0af19f1e962d","name":"Kirkeby, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0001-9292-5526","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Matt","key":"denwoodmattpau","last":"Denwood","locid":"e86ecd1c-385d-49a7-a2ca-45dfc187bc6e","name":"Denwood, Matt","orcid":"0000-0001-5212-4273","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Engbo","key":"christiansenlasseengbopau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"9d379f06-f620-404a-8397-3dfdaf9a3804","name":"Christiansen, Lasse Engbo","orcid":"0000-0001-5019-1931","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Kåre","key":"mølbakkårepau","last":"Mølbak","locid":"d94c7db7-f909-4a03-bdb7-185bb3eb5a96","name":"Mølbak, Kåre","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Camilla","key":"holtenmøllercamillapau","last":"Holten Møller","name":"Holten Møller, Camilla","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Holten","key":"møllercamillaholtenpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Camilla Holten","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Robert Leo","key":"skovrobertleopau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Robert Leo","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Tyra Grove","key":"krausetyragrovepau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Tyra Grove","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenmortenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Raphael","key":"sieberraphaelpau","last":"Sieber","name":"Sieber, Raphael","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Raphael Niklaus","key":"sieberraphaelniklauspau","last":"Sieber","name":"Sieber, Raphael Niklaus","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thor Bech","key":"johannesenthorbechpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Thor Bech","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","first":"Troels","key":"lillebaektroelspau","last":"Lillebæk","locid":"4c4e219b-6ac0-4067-a078-ef52b9c2beff","name":"Lillebaek, Troels","name_org":"Lillebæk, Troels","orcid":"0000-0002-2601-2718","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jannik","key":"fonagerjannikpau","last":"Fonager","name":"Fonager, Jannik","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardanderspau","last":"Fomsgaard","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Frederik Trier","key":"møllerfrederiktrierpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Frederik Trier","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marc","key":"steggermarcpau","last":"Stegger","name":"Stegger, Marc","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Maria","key":"overvadmariapau","last":"Overvad","name":"Overvad, Maria","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katja","key":"spiesskatjapau","last":"Spiess","name":"Spiess, Katja","rank":18,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Laust Hvas","key":"mortensenlausthvaspau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"d0e91c79-42a7-44be-a8a8-5a1d560fdeb0","name":"Mortensen, Laust Hvas","orcid":"0000-0002-6399-495X","rank":19,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36180438"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-022-33498-0","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"5760","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85139243925"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3a03f7b5-3b86-49d0-b778-525e2588569f","ku-ae8199cc-bb2d-4e2f-b526-083fb38af823"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Household transmission of SARS-CoV-2 Omicron variant of concern subvariants BA.1 and BA.2 in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.96-033881","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"In this analysis including 29 340 individuals from RESPOND and 1078 cancer events, the incidence of cancer decreased as cumulative INSTI exposure increased in ART-naive individuals, however there was no association between cancer risk and INSTI exposure in ART-experienced individuals. Background Limited data exist examining the association between incident cancer and cumulative integrase inhibitor (INSTI) exposure. Methods Participants were followed from baseline (latest of local cohort enrollment or January 1, 2012) until the earliest of first cancer, final follow-up, or December 31, 2019. Negative binomial regression was used to assess associations between cancer incidence and time-updated cumulative INSTI exposure, lagged by 6 months. Results Of 29 340 individuals, 74% were male, 24% were antiretroviral treatment (ART)-naive, and median baseline age was 44 years (interquartile range [IQR], 36-51). Overall, 13 950 (48%) individuals started an INSTI during follow-up. During 160 657 person-years of follow-up ([PYFU] median 6.2; IQR, 3.9-7.5), there were 1078 cancers (incidence rate [IR] 6.7/1000 PYFU; 95% confidence interval [CI], 6.3-7.1). The commonest cancers were non-Hodgkin lymphoma (n = 113), lung cancer (112), Kaposi's sarcoma (106), and anal cancer (103). After adjusting for potential confounders, there was no association between cancer risk and INSTI exposure (6-12 months; 0.97 [95% CI, 0.71-1.32], >12-24 months; 0.84 [95% CI, 0.64-1.11], >24-36 months; 1.10 [95% CI, 0.82-1.47], >36 months; 0.90 [95% CI, 0.65-1.26] [P = .60]). In ART-naive participants, cancer incidence decreased with increasing INSTI exposure, mainly driven by a decreasing incidence of acquired immune deficiency syndrome cancers; however, there was no association between INSTI exposure and cancer for those ART-experienced (interaction P < .0001). Conclusions Cancer incidence in each INSTI exposure group was similar, despite relatively wide CIs, providing reassuring early findings that increasing INSTI exposure is unlikely to be associated with an increased cancer risk, although longer follow-up is needed to confirm this finding.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Greenberg, Lauren","Ryom, Lene","Neesgaard, Bastian","Miró, Jose M.","Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","Zangerle, Robert","Grabmeier-Pfistershammer, Katharina","Günthard, Huldrych F.","Kusejko, Katharina","Smith, Colette","Mussini, Cristina","Menozzi, Marianna","Wit, Ferdinand","Van Der Valk, Marc","D'Arminio Monforte, Antonella","De Wit, Stcrossed D.Sign©phane","Necsoi, Coca","Pelchen-Matthews, Annegret","Lundgren, Jens","Peters, Lars","Castagna, Antonella","Muccini, Camilla","Vehreschild, Jörg Janne","Pradier, Christian","Bruguera Riera, Andreu","Sönnerborg, Anders","Petoumenos, Kathy","Garges, Harmony","Rogatto, Felipe","Dedes, Nikos","Bansi-Matharu, Loveleen","Mocroft, Amanda"],"cuid":["S02-098.42-042571"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corpau":["RESPOND Study Group","RESPOND Study Grp"],"corresponding_author":["Greenberg, Lauren"],"country":["Australia","Austria","Belgium","France","Germany","Italy","Netherlands","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["ASST Santi Paolo e Carlo","All Global Affiliations","CHRU Nice","Centre Estudis Epidemiologics de ITS i VIH de Catalunya (CEEISCAT)","European AIDS Treatment Group","Gilead Sciences Incorporated","Goethe University Frankfurt","HIV Monitoring Foundation","Karolinska Institute","Medical University of Innsbruck","Medical University of Vienna","National Institutes of Health","San Raffaele Scientific Institute","St Pierre University Hospital","University College London","University Hospital Cologne","University Hospital Zurich","University of Amsterdam","University of Barcelona","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","Univ