111/aas.14007","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"375-385","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"66"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85121116321"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-44bb0278-8df0-415b-ab44-686b12cf0bd2","sdu-e67a8dce-abad-4383-8a50-26e54f6233b2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Management of acute atrial fibrillation in the intensive care unit : An international survey","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-741355","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Following emergence of the SARS-CoV-2 variant Omicron in November 2021, the dominant BA.1 sub-lineage was replaced by the BA.2 sub-lineage in Denmark. We analysed the first 2,623 BA.2 cases from 29 November 2021 to 2 January 2022. No epidemiological or clinical differences were found between individuals infected with BA.1 versus BA.2. Phylogenetic analyses showed a geographic east-to-west transmission of BA.2 from the Capital Region with clusters expanding after the Christmas holidays. Mutational analysis shows distinct differences between BA.1 and BA.2.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Fonager, Jannik","Bennedbæk, Marc","Bager, Peter","Wohlfahrt, Jan","Ellegaard, Kirsten Maren","Ingham, Anna Cäcilia","Edslev, Sofie Marie","Stegger, Marc","Sieber, Raphael Niklaus","Lassauniere, Ria","Fomsgaard, Anders","Lillebaek, Troels","Svarrer, Christina Wiid","Møller, Frederik Trier","Møller, Camilla Holten","Legarth, Rebecca","Sydenham, Thomas Vognbjerg","Steinke, Kat","Paulsen, Sarah Juel","Castruita, José Alfredo Samaniego","Schneider, Uffe Vest","Schouw, Christian Højte","Nielsen, Xiaohui Chen","Overvad, Maria","Nielsen, Rikke Thoft","Marvig, Rasmus L.","Pedersen, Martin Schou","Nielsen, Lene","Nilsson, Line","Bybjerg-Grauholm, Jonas","Tarpgaard, Irene Harder","Ebsen, Tine Sneibjerg","Lam, Janni Uyen Hoa","Gunalan, Vithiagaran","Rasmussen, Morten"],"cuid":["S03-088.12-014836"],"filters":{"added":"2022-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Fonager, Jannik"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Twin Research and Genetic Epidemiology"],"keyword":["BA 1","BA 2","COVID 19 epidemiology","Covid 19","Denmark epidemiology","Humans","Molecular epidemiology","Omicron","Phylogeny","SARS CoV 2","SARS CoV 2 genetics","Variant of concern"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{