, Andr Crossed D.sign© P.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 12","first":"Michael P.","key":"wajnrajchpau","last":"Wajnrajch","name":"Wajnrajch, Michael P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9","first":"Roy","key":"gomezpau","last":"Gomez","name":"Gomez, Roy","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"13","first":"Kevin C.J.","key":"yuenpau","last":"Yuen","name":"Yuen, Kevin C.J.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35368070"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgac199","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"1906-1919","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"107"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85132454167"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-0316ab54-b1c4-4346-9d9e-8505a2b02bc9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Long-term Safety of Growth Hormone in Adults With Growth Hormone Deficiency : Overview of 15 809 GH-Treated Patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-395306","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Aims Given the pivotal role played by the gut microbiota in regulating the host immune system, great interest has arisen in the possibility of controlling fish health by modulating the gut microbiota. Hence, there is a need to better understand of the host-microbiota interactions after disease responses to optimize the use of probiotics to strengthen disease resilience and recovery. Methods and Results We tested the effects of a probiotic feed additive in rainbow trout and challenged the fish with the causative agent for enteric red mouth disease, Yersinia ruckeri. We evaluated the survival, host immune gene expression and the gut microbiota composition. Results revealed that provision of probiotics and exposure to Y. ruckeri induced immune gene expression in the host, which were associated with changes in the gut microbiota. Subsequently, infection with Y. ruckeri had very little effect on microbiota composition when probiotics were applied, indicating that probiotics increased stabilisation of the microbiota. Our analysis revealed potential biomarkers for monitoring infection status and fish health. Finally, we used modelling approaches to decipher interactions between gut bacteria and the host immune gene responses, indicating removal of endogenous bacteria elicited by non-specific immune responses. Conclusions We discuss the relevance of these results emphasizing the importance of host-microbiota interactions, including the protective potential of the gut microbiota in disease responses. Significance and Impact of the Study Our results highlight the functional consequences of probiotic-induced changes in the gut microbiota post infection and the resulting host immune response.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jacob Agerbo","Villumsen, Kasper Rømer","Jørgensen, Louise von Gersdorff","Forberg, Torunn","Zuo, Shaozhi","Kania, Per Walter","Buchmann, Kurt","Kristiansen, Karsten","Bojesen, Anders Miki","Limborg, Morten T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-422995"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Qingdao-Europe Advanced Institute for Life Sciences"],"keyword":["Aquaculture","Communities","Gene expression","Host microbiota interactions","Infection","Intestinal microbiology","Modelling","Probiotics","Rainbow trout","Salmon Salmo salar","Vibrio anguillarum","Yersinia ruckeri"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrative analyses of probiotics pathogenic infections and host immune response highlight the importance of gut microbiota in understanding disease recovery in rainbow trout i oncorhynchus mykiss i","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320391838/LINI_J_of_Applied_Microbiology_2022_Rasmussen_Integrative_analyses_of_probiotics_pathogenic_infections_and_host_immune.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-422995","identifier":[{"id":"85124006847","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35032344","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000751654700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-31a98608-d6b4-4276-834b-4df4096f0adc"],"keyword":["COMMUNITIES","GENE-EXPRESSION","PCR DATA","SALMON SALMO-SALAR","VIBRIO-ANGUILLARUM","Yersinia ruckeri","aquaculture","biomarker predictions","host-microbiota interactions","infection","intestinal microbiology","modelling","probiotics","rainbow trout"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C5A5A9F2C91F93CDFA19A569C73B737D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/320391838/LINI_J_of_Applied_Microbiology_2022_Rasmussen_Integrative_analyses_of_probiotics_pathogenic_infections_and_host_immune.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Hologenomics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Biomar A/S (Biz)"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cn","key":"qingdao europe advanced institute for life sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Qingdao-Europe Advanced Institute for Life Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob Agerbo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f89cd3c8-6ae8-4cbc-831a-7471eed8e5f5","name":"Rasmussen, Jacob Agerbo","orcid":"0000-0002-7710-8912","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper Rømer","key":"villumsenpau","last":"Villumsen","locid":"ca610eea-47a5-4c84-b276-35745c1d6513","name":"Villumsen, Kasper Rømer","orcid":"0000-0002-0616-4095","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise von Gersdorff","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"ebe23595-5c4c-4086-9363-0a61fb2dcedf","name":"Jørgensen, Louise von Gersdorff","orcid":"0000-0002-6005-3249","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Torunn","key":"forbergpau","last":"Forberg","name":"Forberg, Torunn","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Shaozhi","key":"zuopau","last":"Zuo","locid":"ff9d41f5-27d1-4845-a677-f8216dd9e3a2","name":"Zuo, Shaozhi","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per Walter","key":"kaniapau","last":"Kania","locid":"c0c490cd-08cc-4f60-a788-f028f71b1a82","name":"Kania, Per Walter","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kurt","key":"buchmannpau","last":"Buchmann","locid":"943a8c9c-1a7a-436d-8fc2-ceec17d4cdba","name":"Buchmann, Kurt","orcid":"0000-0002-2747-237X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 3","first":"Karsten","key":"kristiansenpau","last":"Kristiansen","locid":"941041b1-1b8f-4be5-9a65-5e98f662c07e","name":"Kristiansen, Karsten","orcid":"0000-0002-6024-0917","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Miki","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"404f5838-4d57-4c72-809d-ba35461a74e8","name":"Bojesen, Anders Miki","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Tonsberg","key":"limborgpau","last":"Limborg","locid":"e0cb3d32-1c00-4ec6-a083-d1d14862135b","name":"Limborg, Morten T.","name_org":"Limborg, Morten Tonsberg","orcid":"0000-0002-7718-6531","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35032344"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/jam.15433","issn":["13645072"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","pages":"3201-3216","status":"p","title":"Journal of Applied Microbiology","volume":"132"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85124006847"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","biomar a/s (biz)"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-31a98608-d6b4-4276-834b-4df4096f0adc"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Integrative analyses of probiotics, pathogenic infections and host immune response highlight the importance of gut microbiota in understanding disease recovery in rainbow trout (<i>Oncorhynchus mykiss</i>)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-422995","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Objective: To analyze the effectiveness and safety of growth hormone (GH) replacement treatment in adult patients with Langerhans cell histiocytosis (LCH) and GH deficiency (GHD) enrolled in KIMS (Pfizer International Metabolic Database). Patients and methods: Patients with LCH and GHD were studied at baseline and some of them after 1 year of GH treatment. The effectiveness of GH is presented as change after 1 year of treatment (mean, 95% CI). The LCH population was compared to two other groups of patients enrolled in KIMS, granulomatous and lymphocytic hypophysitis. Results: At baseline, 81 adults with LCH (27 with childhood onset, 56% females), mean age at GHD onset of 29 (15) years were studied. Diabetes insipidus was diagnosed in 86% of patients. Analysis of 1 year of GH treatment was possible in 37 patients. One-year cross-sectional values for the GH dose were 0.39 (S.D. ± 0.21) mg and -0.5 (-1.2 to 0.2) for insulin-like growth factor-1 S.D. Total cholesterol decreased 0.9 (-1.5 to -0.3 (mmol/L); P < 0.05); AGHDA-QoLscore (n = 20) was improved by 2.8 points (-5.6 to 0.0; P < 0.05), while mean BMI increased 0.6 ± 3 kg/m2 (95% CI: -0.2 to 1.4). All these effects did not differ from the two other groups after adjusting for age, gender, and baseline values. In 20 of 77 patients included in the safety analysis, 36 serious adverse events were reported during 435 patient-years (82.8/1000); no new safety signals were reported. Conclusion: After 1 year of GH treatment in patients with LCH, metabolic variables and quality of life improved, with no new safety signals.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Touraine, Philippe","Sagna, Yempabou","Mattsson, Anders F.","Burman, Pia","Van Beek, André P.","Carlsson, Martin Ove","Aydin, Ferah","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Camacho-Hübner, Cecilia"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-439349"],"filters":{"added":"2022-11","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa","America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Burkina Faso","France","Netherlands","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Pfizer","Sorbonne University","University of Groningen","Université Nazi Boni"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pituitary function and the response to gh therapy in patients with langerhans cell histiocytosis analysis of the kims database","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-22-0160","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-439349","identifier":[{"id":"35830276","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85135375980","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9346264","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-4cfd462c-35b6-49c5-928b-bc4336912c41"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-21A1484CB25E6B1A14AAF094739532BB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EJE-22-0160","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/321831915/1479_683X_EJE_22_0160.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"fr","key":"sorbonne university","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Sorbonne University","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"bf","key":"université nazi boni","loc":["Burkina Faso","Africa"],"name":"Université Nazi Boni","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"pfizer","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Pfizer","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"nl","key":"university of groningen","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Groningen","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Philippe","key":"tourainepau","last":"Touraine","name":"Touraine, Philippe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Yempabou","key":"sagnapau","last":"Sagna","name":"Sagna, Yempabou","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders F.","key":"mattssonpau","last":"Mattsson","name":"Mattsson, Anders F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Pia","key":"burmanpau","last":"Burman","name":"Burman, Pia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"André P.","key":"vanbeekpau","last":"Van Beek","name":"Van Beek, André P.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Martin Ove","key":"carlssonpau","last":"Carlsson","name":"Carlsson, Martin Ove","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ferah","key":"aydinpau","last":"Aydin","name":"Aydin, Ferah","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"Ulla","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","locid":"b5898535-d448-4e2f-9f41-d5199873676b","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Cecilia","key":"camachohübnerpau","last":"Camacho-Hübner","name":"Camacho-Hübner, Cecilia","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35830276"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1530/eje-22-0160","issn":["00214787"],"issue":"3","journal":"Yosetsu Gakkai Shi/Journal of the Japan Welding Society","pages":"373-381","status":"p","title":"Yosetsu Gakkai Shi/Journal of the Japan Welding Society","volume":"187"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85135375980"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4cfd462c-35b6-49c5-928b-bc4336912c41"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pituitary function and the response to GH therapy in patients with Langerhans cell histiocytosis : analysis of the KIMS database","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-439349","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"α-synucleinopathy is driven by an imbalance of synthesis and degradation of α-synuclein (αSyn), causing a build up of αSyn aggregates and post-translationally modified species, which not only interfere with normal cellular metabolism but also by their secretion propagates the disease. Therefore, a better understanding of αSyn degradation pathways is needed to address α-synucleinopathy. Here, we used the nerve growth factor-differentiated catecholaminergic PC12 neuronal cell line, which was conferred α-synucleinopathy by inducible expression of αSyn and tubulin polymerization-promoting protein p25α. p25α aggregates αSyn, and imposes a partial autophagosome-lysosome block to mimic aspects of lysosomal deficiency common in neurodegenerative disease. Under basal conditions, αSyn was degraded by multiple pathways but most prominently by macroautophagy and Nedd4/Ndfip1-mediated degradation. We found that expression of p25α induced strong p38MAPK activity. Remarkably, when opposed by inhibitor SB203580 or p38MAPK shRNA knockdown, endolysosomal localization and degradation of αSyn increased, and αSyn secretion and cytotoxicity decreased. This effect was specifically dependent on Hsc70 and the endosomal sorting complex required for transport machinery, but different from classical microautophagy, as the αSyn Hsc70 binding motif was unnecessary. Furthermore, in a primary neuronal (h)-αSyn seeding model, p38MAPK inhibition decreased pathological accumulation of phosphorylated serine-129-αSyn and cytotoxicity. In conclusion, p38MAPK inhibition shifts αSyn degradation from various forms of autophagy to an endosomal sorting complex required for transport-dependent uptake mechanism, resulting in increased αSyn turnover and cell viability in p25α-expressing cells. More generally, our results suggest that under conditions of autophagolysosomal malfunction, the uninterrupted endosomal pathway offers a possibility to achieve disease-associated protein degradation.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Madsen, Helena Borland","Rasmussen, Izabela","Bjerregaard-Andersen, Kaare","Rasmussen, Michel","Olsen, Anders","Vilhardt, Frederik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-474617"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Autophagy","Chaperone mediated autophagy","ESCRT","Endosomes","Lysosomes","TPPP p25α","microautophagy","α Synuclein"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-LUND"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-LUND","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"α synuclein buildup is alleviated via escrt dependent endosomal degradation brought about by p000000000038mapk inhibition in cells expressing p000000000025α","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbc.2022.102531","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-474617","identifier":[{"id":"PMC9637583","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"36162505","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85142940846","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-87b9bb0c-eb33-4ddd-8aa8-99824d9b21d6"],"keyword":["ESCRT","TPPP/p25α","autophagy","chaperone-mediated autophagy","endosomes","lysosomes","microautophagy","α-synuclein"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-5EEA1996E134FA7EF60F92254AB6DE28"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/330391363/1_s2.0_S0021925822009747_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jbc.2022.102531","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Cellular and Molecular Medicine, Morphogenesis and Differentiation Program"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"lundbeck","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-LUND","l3nl":"Lundbeck Pharma","l3nn":"Lundbeck","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lundbeck","namevar":["Lundbeck"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-LUND","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","first":"Helena","key":"madsenhelenaborlandpau","last":"Borland","locid":"81e08ec6-528b-4b91-afc8-3d9d3c7f7765","name":"Madsen, Helena Borland","name_org":"Borland, Helena","orcid":"0009-0002-6351-2700","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Izabela","key":"rasmussenizabelapau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"40cf76a0-c5c8-4ac6-a0a5-49d94e044229","name":"Rasmussen, Izabela","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Kaare","key":"bjerregaardandersenkaarepau","last":"Bjerregaard-Andersen","name":"Bjerregaard-Andersen, Kaare","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michel","key":"rasmussenmichelpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Michel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"olsenanderspau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frederik","key":"vilhardtfrederikpau","last":"Vilhardt","locid":"e4d61a4c-867d-4828-aa75-9f9c6e69a5fd","name":"Vilhardt, Frederik","orcid":"0000-0001-8604-7165","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36162505"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jbc.2022.102531","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"issue":"11","journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","paperid":"102531","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","title_org":"The Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"298"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85142940846"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Lundbeck Pharma","Private Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-87b9bb0c-eb33-4ddd-8aa8-99824d9b21d6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"α-synuclein buildup is alleviated via ESCRT-dependent endosomal degradation brought about by p38MAPK inhibition in cells expressing p25α","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-474617","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"A polyomino is a polygonal region with axis-parallel edges and corners of integral coordinates, which may have holes. In this paper, we consider planar tiling and packing problems with polyomino pieces and a polyomino container P. We give polynomial-time algorithms for deciding if P can be tiled with k × k squares for any fixed k which can be part of the input (that is, deciding if P is the union of a set of non-overlapping k × k squares) and for packing P with a maximum number of non-overlapping and axis-parallel 2 × 1 dominos, allowing rotations by 90?. As packing is more general than tiling, the latter algorithm can also be used to decide if P can be tiled by 2 × 1 dominos. These are classical problems with important applications in VLSI design, and the related problem of finding a maximum packing of 2 × 2 squares is known to be NP-hard [J. Algorithms 1990]. For our three problems there are known pseudo-polynomial-time algorithms, that is, algorithms with running times polynomial in the area or perimeter of P. However, the standard, compact way to represent a polygon is by listing the coordinates of the corners in binary. We use this representation, and thus present the first polynomial-time algorithms for the problems. Concretely, we give a simple O(n log n)-time algorithm for tiling with squares, where n is the number of corners of P. We then give a more involved algorithm that reduces the problems of packing and tiling with dominos to finding a maximum and perfect matching in a graph with O(n3) vertices. This leads to algorithms with running times O(n3loglog2 log3 nn ) and O(n3logloglog2 nn ), respectively.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aamand, Anders","Abrahamsen, Mikkel","Ahle, Thomas","Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489638"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-10","place":"Berlin, de","start":"2022-06-07","title":"38th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2023-05","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Massachusetts Institute of Technology"],"keyword":["Packing","Tiling","polyominos"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tiling with squares and packing dominos in polynomial time","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489638","identifier":[{"id":"85134355587","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a0e0ebc6-632f-4483-a346-34aadb3d7ff8"],"keyword":["packing","polyominos","tiling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-C4CF63C82F139262EDA2FB7502FF65E0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2022.1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/342673668/LIPIcs_SoCG_2022_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"massachusetts institute of technology","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Massachusetts Institute of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mikkel","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"63596832-461f-409a-a2cc-81023b9b8e46","name":"Abrahamsen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0003-2734-4690","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Thomas","key":"ahlepau","last":"Ahle","name":"Ahle, Thomas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter M.R.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca3d1668-64f4-4f81-92ed-9d7e18be5f43","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","name_org":"Rasmussen, Peter M.R.","orcid":"0000-0001-9219-8410","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Xavier","key":"goaocpedh","last":"Goaoc","name":"Goaoc, Xavier","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"kerberpedh","last":"Kerber","name":"Kerber, Michael","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2022.1","eisbn":["9783959772273"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"38th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2022"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85134355587"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a0e0ebc6-632f-4483-a346-34aadb3d7ff8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tiling with Squares and Packing Dominos in Polynomial Time","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489638","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Consumption of unprocessed red meat in randomized trials has no adverse effects on cardiovascular risk factors and body weight, but its physiological effects during weight loss maintenance are not known. Objectives: We sought to investigate the effects of healthy diets that include small or large amounts of red meat on the maintenance of lost weight after successful weight loss, and secondarily on body composition (DXA), resting energy expenditure (REE; indirect calorimetry), and cardiometabolic risk factors. Methods: In this 5-mo parallel randomized intervention trial, 108 adults with BMI 28-40 kg/m2 (45 males/63 females) underwent an 8-wk rapid weight loss period, and those who lost ≥8% body weight (n = 80) continued to ad libitum weight maintenance diets for 12 wk: a moderate-protein diet with 25 g beef/d (B25, n = 45) or a high-protein diet with 150 g beef/d (B150, n = 35). Results: In per protocol analysis (n = 69), mean body weight (-1.2 kg; 95% CI: -2.1, -0.3 kg), mean fat mass (-2.7 kg; 95% CI: -3.4, -2.0 kg), and mean body fat content (-2.6%; 95% CI: -3.1, -2.1%) decreased during the maintenance phase, whereas mean lean mass (1.5 kg; 95% CI: 1.0, 2.0 kg) and mean REE (51 kcal/d; 95% CI: 15, 86 kcal/d) increased, with no differences between groups (all P > 0.05). Results were similar in intention-to-treat analysis with multiple imputation for dropouts (20 from B150 compared with 19 from B25, P = 0.929). Changes in cardiometabolic risk factors were not different between groups, the general pattern being a decrease during weight loss and a return to baseline during weight maintenance (and despite the additional mild reduction in weight and fat mass). Conclusions: Healthy diets consumed ad libitum that contain a little or a lot of unprocessed beef have similar effects on body weight, energy metabolism, and cardiovascular risk factors during the first 3 mo after clinically significant rapid weight loss.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Magkos, Faidon","Ingemann Rasmussen, Sidse Ida","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Asping, Sarah","Rosenkrans, Maria I","Sjödin, Anders Mikael","Astrup, Arne","Geiker, Nina Rica Wium"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494574"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Body composition","Cardiovascular risk","Faculty of Science","Meat intake","Overweight","Prediabetes","Red meat","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"unprocessed red meat in the dietary treatment of obesity a randomized controlled trial of beef supplementation during weight maintenance after successful weight loss","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ajcn/nqac152","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-494574","identifier":[{"id":"36307956","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85150198555","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC9761757","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a9550b1a-51c6-46b9-b128-c0fde740a688"],"keyword":["Body composition","Cardiovascular risk","Faculty of Science","Meat intake","Overweight","Prediabetes","Red meat","Weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC2CA2B335A51C5734D90CBE6E4F5142"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/329610771/Magkos_et_al_American_Journal_of_Clinical_Nutrition_2022_Vol_116_6_1820_1830.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/ajcn/nqac152","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Faidon","key":"magkospau","last":"Magkos","locid":"ac8c9eed-7c49-41f0-8015-fc4ea0f595ee","name":"Magkos, Faidon","orcid":"0000-0002-1312-7364","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidse I","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a427a000-d7ed-48b8-8886-4b435869957e","name":"Ingemann Rasmussen, Sidse Ida","name_org":"Rasmussen, Sidse I","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-3939","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Fiil","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"00918fa0-7b1e-4128-919e-a0af9497026b","name":"Hjorth, Mads Fiil","orcid":"0000-0001-9440-2737","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"aspingpau","last":"Asping","locid":"0a50b1b8-9b35-4dc2-bc4a-dd62f0d64cd8","name":"Asping, Sarah","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria I","key":"rosenkranspau","last":"Rosenkrans","locid":"edb2a616-87db-446f-902c-c01e150aff95","name":"Rosenkrans, Maria I","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Mikael","key":"sjödinpau","last":"Sjödin","locid":"24ea7b85-2a13-44ec-93f5-fb419b0ab4fd","name":"Sjödin, Anders Mikael","orcid":"0000-0002-6451-3847","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Arne","key":"astruppau","last":"Astrup","locid":"5d943631-c9fc-4b63-8aaa-263ba4248735","name":"Astrup, Arne","orcid":"0000-0001-8968-8996","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina Rica Wium","key":"geikerpau","last":"Geiker","locid":"36dfc94c-330a-452a-b2c9-5fa775754a9a","name":"Geiker, Nina Rica Wium","orcid":"0000-0001-8063-5820","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36307956"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/ajcn/nqac152","issn":["00029165","19383207"],"issn_org":["00029165"],"issue":"6","journal":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"1820-1830","status":"p","title":"American Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"116"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85150198555"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a9550b1a-51c6-46b9-b128-c0fde740a688"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Unprocessed red meat in the dietary treatment of obesity: a randomized controlled trial of beef supplementation during weight maintenance after successful weight loss","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494574","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Early detection of pathogens at the point of care helps reduce the threats to human and animal health from emerging pathogens. Initially, the disease-causing agent will be unknown and needs to be identified; this often requires specific laboratory facilities. Here we describe the development of an unbiased detection assay for RNA and DNA viruses using metagenomic Nanopore sequencing and simple methods that can be transferred into a field setting. Human clinical samples containing the RNA virus SARS-CoV-2 or the DNA viruses human papillomavirus (HPV) and molluscum contagiosum virus (MCV) were used as a test of concept. Firstly, the virus detection potential was optimized by investigating different pretreatments for reducing non-viral nucleic acid components. DNase I pretreatment followed by filtration increased the proportion of SARS-CoV-2 sequenced reads > 500-fold compared with no pretreatments. This was sufficient to achieve virus detection with high confidence and allowed variant identification. Next, we tested individual SARS-CoV-2 samples with various viral loads (measured as CT-values determined by RT-qPCR). Lastly, we tested the assay on clinical samples containing the DNA virus HPV and co-infection with MCV to show the assay's detection potential for DNA viruses. This protocol is fast (same day results). We hope to apply this method in other settings for point of care detection of virus pathogens, thus eliminating the need for transport of infectious samples, cold storage and a specialized laboratory.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fomsgaard, Anna S.","Rasmussen, Morten","Spiess, Katja","Fomsgaard, Anders","Belsham, Graham","Fonager, Jannik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-503820"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["HPV","Metagenomics","Nanopore sequencing","Point of care detection","SARS CoV 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improvements in metagenomic virus detection by simple pretreatment methods","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcvp.2022.100120","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-503820","identifier":[{"id":"36945677","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85141826745","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC10024160","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b8eb4f00-74de-4b27-9622-30d7719be3f0"],"keyword":["HPV","Metagenomics","Nanopore sequencing","Point of care detection","SARS-CoV-2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F911D5E7CC251C643E4BF34AD0360A81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jcvp.2022.100120","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/330900835/1_s2.0_S266703802200059X_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Veterinary Clinical Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anna S.","key":"fomsgaardannaspau","last":"Fomsgaard","locid":"48777f5f-a1ff-4591-b340-1727e68cfee7","name":"Fomsgaard, Anna S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenmortenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Katja","key":"spiesskatjapau","last":"Spiess","name":"Spiess, Katja","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardanderspau","last":"Fomsgaard","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Graham J.","key":"belshamgrahampau","last":"Belsham","locid":"ba6d2fb9-3c15-4f09-b7b0-9f902a9c8932","name":"Belsham, Graham","name_org":"Belsham, Graham J.","orcid":"0000-0003-1187-4873","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jannik","key":"fonagerjannikpau","last":"Fonager","name":"Fonager, Jannik","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36945677"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jcvp.2022.100120","issn":["26670380"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Clinical Virology Plus","paperid":"100120","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Virology Plus","volume":"2"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141826745"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b8eb4f00-74de-4b27-9622-30d7719be3f0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Improvements in metagenomic virus detection by simple pretreatment methods","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-503820","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background: Anthracycline induced cardiotoxicity is well recognized but only few data exist in sarcoma patients. This study retrospectively aimed to analyze sequential Cadmium Zinc Telluride (CZT)-multigated equilibrium radionuclide angiography (ERNA) for monitoring left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) and to assess the real-life incidence of cardiotoxicity in sarcoma patients receiving doxorubicin based chemotherapy. Materials and methods: A retrospective analysis was performed on all sarcoma patients referred to Herlev University Hospital between 2012 and 2015. Cardiotoxicity was defined as a decline in LVEF of > 10% percentage point to a LVEF < 50% as compared to baseline. Early cardiotoxicity was defined as < 1 year and late cardiotoxicity as ≥ 1 year. Recovery of cardiotoxicity was defined as a LVEF ≥ 50%. Results: A total of 149 patients were referred, 75 (50%) sarcoma patients were included. The main reason for exclusion was that only one CZT-ERNA had been performed in 50 (68%) of the patients. Twenty-three (31%) of the patients experienced cardiotoxicity, 11 (48%) were female, mean age was 56.9 years. Early cardiotoxicity was observed in 16 (70%) of the patients and 11 (48%) experienced clinical symptoms of cardiotoxicity at diagnosis. Recovery of LVEF was seen in 12 (55%) of the patients and persistent recovery in 10 (45%). The diastolic blood pressure at baseline was positively and significantly associated with a higher risk of developing cardiotoxicity (Relative Risk (RR): 1.039 (95% CI= 1.001 − 1.079; p = 0.042)). The median survival was 1.4 years (range 0.5 − 2.2 years) for patients with metastatic disease versus 3.9 years (range 1.5 − 6.4 years) (p = 0.009) for localized disease at baseline. Conclusion: Cardiotoxicity is a relative frequent complication in sarcoma patients treated with doxorubicin based chemotherapy and the diastolic blood pressure at baseline was significantly associated with a higher risk of developing cardiotoxicity.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Vitfell-Rasmussen, Joanna","Krarup-Hansen, Anders","Vaage-Nilsen, Merete","Kümler, Thomas","Zerahn, Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-512984"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cardiotoxicity","Sarcoma"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"real life incidence of cardiotoxicity and associated risk factors in sarcoma patients receiving doxorubicin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-512984","identifier":[{"id":"85131753482","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35695121","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c83c3a97-09db-4df0-9312-c1529644dcc6"],"keyword":["Sarcoma","anthracycline and doxorubicin","cardiotoxicity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-534E533F0BE5AF52CD0970418615C1BA"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Joanna","key":"vitfellrasmussenpau","last":"Vitfell-Rasmussen","name":"Vitfell-Rasmussen, Joanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"kraruphansenpau","last":"Krarup-Hansen","locid":"5fb06b4f-2517-4150-923a-06d5cde8fc83","name":"Krarup-Hansen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Merete","key":"vaagenilsenpau","last":"Vaage-Nilsen","name":"Vaage-Nilsen, Merete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"kümlerpau","last":"Kümler","name":"Kümler, Thomas","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"zerahnpau","last":"Zerahn","name":"Zerahn, Bo","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["35695121"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2022.2082884","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"801-808","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85131753482"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c83c3a97-09db-4df0-9312-c1529644dcc6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Real-life incidence of cardiotoxicity and associated risk factors in sarcoma patients receiving doxorubicin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-512984","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"The transitions from foraging to farming and later to pastoralism in Stone Age Eurasia (c. 11-3 thousand years before present, BP) represent some of the most dramatic lifestyle changes in human evolution. We sequenced 317 genomes of primarily Mesolithic and Neolithic individuals from across Eurasia combined with radiocarbon dates, stable isotope data, and pollen records. Genome imputation and co-analysis with previously published shotgun sequencing data resulted in &gt;1600 complete ancient genome sequences offering fine-grained resolution into the Stone Age populations. We observe that: 1) Hunter-gatherer groups were more genetically diverse than previously known, and deeply divergent between western and eastern Eurasia. 2) We identify hitherto genetically undescribed hunter-gatherers from the Middle Don region that contributed ancestry to the later Yamnaya steppe pastoralists; 3) The genetic impact of the Neolithic transition was highly distinct, east and west of a boundary zone extending from the Black Sea to the Baltic. Large-scale shifts in genetic ancestry occurred to the west of this “Great Divide”, including an almost complete replacement of hunter-gatherers in Denmark, while no substantial ancestry shifts took place during the same period to the east. This difference is also reflected in genetic relatedness within the populations, decreasing substantially in the west but not in the east where it remained high until c. 4,000 BP; 4) The second major genetic transformation around 5,000 BP happened at a much faster pace with Steppe-related ancestry reaching most parts of Europe within 1,000-years. Local Neolithic farmers admixed with incoming pastoralists in eastern, western, and southern Europe whereas Scandinavia experienced another near-complete population replacement. Similar dramatic turnover-patterns are evident in western Siberia; 5) Extensive regional differences in the ancestry components involved in these early events remain visible to this day, even within countries. Neolithic farmer ancestry is highest in southern and eastern England while Steppe-related ancestry is highest in the Celtic populations of Scotland, Wales, and Cornwall (this research has been conducted using the UK Biobank resource); 6) Shifts in diet, lifestyle and environment introduced new selection pressures involving at least 21 genomic regions. Most such variants were not universally selected across populations but were only advantageous in particular ancestral backgrounds. Contrary to previous claims, we find that selection on the FADS regions, associated with fatty acid metabolism, began before the Neolithisation of Europe. Similarly, the lactase persistence allele started increasing in frequency before the expansion of Steppe-related groups into Europe and has continued to increase up to the present. Along the genetic cline separating Mesolithic hunter-gatherers from Neolithic farmers, we find significant correlations with trait associations related to skin disorders, diet and lifestyle and mental health status, suggesting marked phenotypic differences between these groups with very different lifestyles. This work provides new insights into major transformations in recent human evolution, elucidating the complex interplay between selection and admixture that shaped patterns of genetic variation in modern populations.Competing Interest StatementThe authors have declared no competing interest.","author_count":163,"contributors":["Allentoft, Morten E.","Sikora, Martin","Refoyo-Martínez, Alba","Irving-Pease, Evan K.","Fischer, Anders","Barrie, William","Ingason, Andrés","Stenderup, Jesper","Sjögren, Karl-Göran","Pearson, Alice","Mota, Barbara","Paulsson, Bettina Schulz","Halgren, Alma","Macleod, Ruairidh","Jørkov, M L S","Demeter, Fabrice","Novosolov, Maria","Sørensen, Lasse","Nielsen, Poul-Otto","Henriksen, Rasmus Amund","Vimala, Tharsika","McColl, Hugh","Margaryan, Ashot","Ilardo, Melissa","Vaughn, Andrew","Mortensen, Morten Fi