{"abstract":"This anthology is the first of its kind which integrates chapters on legitimizing narrative medicine in education, practice and research, on analyzing types of patient narratives and on studying interventions applying vulnerable or shared reading, creative writing, or Socratic dialogue as a means of rehabilitation and mental care.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","Mai, Anne-Marie","Hansen, Helle Ploug"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584456"],"filters":{"added":"2022-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Humanistisk sundhedsforskning","Litteratur og Medicin","Narrativ medicin"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"narrative medicine in education practice and interventions","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://anthempress.com/narrative-medicine-in-education-practice-and-interventions-pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584456","ids":["sdu-27400faa-4277-4bd3-9a03-e87829adf918"],"keyword":["humanistisk sundhedsforskning","litteratur og medicin","narrativ medicin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-C0DDD847B05BC696D77EA27E533F9688"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Literature","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Uses of Literature","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Human Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenped","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6612df8e-d9f9-4004-b959-a9c30b0762a5","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7718-5208","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne Marie","key":"maiped","last":"Mai","locid":"1e8e5a77-fe91-4704-9b4a-60a3a453f6b5","name":"Mai, Anne-Marie","name_org":"Mai, Anne Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-2859-634X","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Ploug","key":"hansenped","last":"Hansen","locid":"aff3454d-836b-44db-9a85-391f83361116","name":"Hansen, Helle Ploug","orcid":"0000-0002-5075-8739","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781839988189"],"isbn":["9781839988165"],"pages":"194","place":"London","publisher":"Anthem Press","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85180378607"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-27400faa-4277-4bd3-9a03-e87829adf918"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Narrative Medicine in Education, Practice, and Interventions","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-584456","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background:Narrative medicine is an innovative approach where empathetic skills are nurtured throughclosereading ofliterary texts and creative writing. The aim of this study was to evaluate the feasibility of a course in narrative medicine for pharmacists.Methods: A 2-day course of narrative medicine was offered to community and hospital pharmacists. Feasibility was assessed using focus group interviews, participant observation, and a questionnaire. Pharmacists’ self-reported level of empathy was also assessed.Results:Eight pharmacists participated in the course. They found participation acceptable, even though some of the sessions required a personal investment far from their routines. The pharmacists were generally satisfied with the course and found it helpful in their daily patient communication. There was no significant change in the pharmacists’ level of empathy. Conclusion:A course in narrative medicine has the potential to improve pharmacist communication with patients but needs further testing, including patient-reported outcomes.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Graabæk, Trine","Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","Mai, Anne-Marie","Rossing, Charlotte","Hedegaard, Ulla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-621206"],"filters":{"added":"2023-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Graabæk, Trine"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Pharmakon"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can literary reading and writing improve pharmacists medication counselling a feasibility study of pharmacists efforts to achieve competence in narrative medicine","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85164569877","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-621206","identifier":[{"id":"85164569877","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-a7906b2f-e1c9-4254-85ba-6db9c844bb8b"],"keyword":["narrativ medicin, uddannelse af farmaceuter"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-95FC085D2819E2CFAC88E1DB4104DC8F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Public Health, Clinical Pharmacology, Pharmacy and Environmental Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Pharmakon"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine","key":"graabækpau","last":"Graabæk","locid":"67e97b89-6918-4950-9557-f5e3939a3c57","name":"Graabæk, Trine","orcid":"0000-0001-6848-3107","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6612df8e-d9f9-4004-b959-a9c30b0762a5","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7718-5208","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Marie","key":"maipau","last":"Mai","locid":"1e8e5a77-fe91-4704-9b4a-60a3a453f6b5","name":"Mai, Anne-Marie","name_org":"Mai, Anne Marie","orcid":"0000-0002-2859-634X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte","key":"rossingpau","last":"Rossing","name":"Rossing, Charlotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulla","key":"hedegaardpau","last":"Hedegaard","locid":"82b24eb2-1cc9-49b6-bd97-07f2cb6a6d2b","name":"Hedegaard, Ulla","orcid":"0000-0002-8958-2187","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.46542/pe.2022.221.744760","issn":["14772701","15602214"],"issn_org":["14772701"],"issue":"1","journal":"Pharmacy Education","pages":"744-760","publisher":"International Pharmaceutical Federation","status":"p","title":"Pharmacy Education","volume":"22"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85164569877"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-a7906b2f-e1c9-4254-85ba-6db9c844bb8b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Can literary reading and writing improve pharmacists’ medication counselling? : A feasibility study of pharmacists’ efforts to achieve competence in narrative medicine.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-621206","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Background and purpose — High alcohol intake is associated with increased risk of postoperative complications. Alcohol cessation intervention is recommended prior to elective surgery. We investigated short-and long-term effects of perioperative intensive alcohol intervention in relation to acute ankle fracture surgery. Patients and methods — 70 patients requiring ankle fracture surgery and consuming ≥ 21 drinks weekly (1 drink = 12 g ethanol) were randomized to a manual-based 6-week intensive standardized alcohol cessation program, the Gold Standard Program (GSP-A), or treatment as usual (TAU), on the day of operation. GSP-A included 5 personal meetings, patient education, and motivational and pharmacological support (alcohol withdrawal prophylaxis, B vitamins, and low-dose disulfiram). Complications requiring treatment were measured after 6 weeks and 1 year. Alcohol intake was validated by biomarkers. Quality of life (QoL) was measured by the SF-36. Hospital costs were obtained from the National Hospital Costs Register. Results — Postoperatively, complete alcohol cessation was higher in the GSP-A than in the TAU group (18/35 vs. 5/35, number needed to treat = 3, p ≤ 0.001), but not low-risk consumption in the long term (10/35 vs. 7/33, p = 0.5). Number of complications in the short and long term (12/35 vs. 14/33, 16/35 vs. 18/33), the SF-36 score, or hospital costs in the short and long term (€6,294 vs. €8,024, €10,662 vs. €12,198), were similar between the groups. Interpretation — Despite an effect on alcohol cessation and a positive tendency as regards the other outcomes, the postoperative complications, QoL, and costs were similar. Better perioperative strategies for acute surgical patients with high alcohol intake therefore need to be developed.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Egholm, Julie Weber Melchior","Pedersen, Bolette","Oppedal, Kristian","Madsen, Bjørn Lindegård","Lauritzen, Jes Bruun","Rasmussen, Mette","Helander, Anders","Adami, Johanna","Tønnesen, Hanne"],"cuid":["S02-099.87-041494"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Egholm, Julie Weber"],"country":["Norway","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Lund University","Sophiahemmet University College","Sophiahemmet University, Stockholm","Stavanger University Hospital"],"keyword":["Alcohol Intervention","Ankle fracture","Postoperative Complications","Surgery"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"minor effect of patient education for alcohol cessation intervention on outcomes after acute fracture surgery a randomized trial of 000000000070 patients","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2022.2482","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.87-041494","identifier":[{"id":"35417027","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9006589","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85128117121","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-376489d4-63ae-416d-a021-933d8a700f91","sdu-f4e8ce26-f9ee-4626-8e2e-8c3321be5a18"],"keyword":["alcohol intervention","ankle fracture","postoperative complications","surgery"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1F1CE98851A3F18A4F66ACF28C8BD47F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/201823925/Open_Access_Version.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2340/17453674.2022.2482","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/313089211/document_8_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Orthopedic Surgery (Sønderborg/Aabenraa)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Bispebjerg and Frederiksberg Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"stavanger university hospital","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Stavanger University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"karolins