:"Bjarkam","locid":"a05346d7-147b-4c78-8bc5-1f6c771af2c6","name":"Bjarkam, Carsten Reidies","orcid":"0000-0002-0164-9595","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Mads","key":"grønhøjpau","last":"Grønhøj","locid":"c3b774fa-6d98-40ae-8ee3-514bde5a9170","name":"Grønhøj, Mads Hjortdal","name_org":"Grønhøj, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-1473-9872","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","corresponding":null,"first":"Frantz Rom","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"b50645f6-f0c4-4356-9f63-d44290b0dfd9","name":"Poulsen, Frantz Rom","orcid":"0000-0001-5715-6901","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Rosendal","key":"korshøjpau","last":"Korshøj","locid":"09d94078-676a-42ee-91c2-eb8ba8df356b","name":"Korshoej, Anders Rosendal","name_org":"Korshøj, Anders Rosendal","orcid":"0000-0003-4285-8171","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["36581996"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-022-07043-9","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issn_org":["17456215"],"issue":"1","journal":"Trials","paperid":"1062","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85145129335"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-585df232-4e37-43c3-9eb0-1e1c67646121","au-d6e85eb5-2284-41b9-9796-9cb5b25ad7b6","sdu-52457d1c-513a-4b69-b5d4-1d2affbbcab0"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Study protocol for ACTIVE study : safety and feasibility evaluation of external ventricular drainage with ACTIVE fluid exchange in intraventricular hemorrhage—a phase 2, multi-center, randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.98-665810","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Choosing the optimal radiographic methods to diagnose the cartilage height and degree of knee osteoarthritis is crucial to determine suitability for unicompartmental knee replacement. This study aims to evaluate and compare articular cartilage thickness measured using the Rosenberg view and coronal stress radiography. Intra- and interrater agreement and test–retest reliability of each method were determined. The hypothesis of the study was that the Rosenberg view and coronal stress radiographs provide similar assessments of articular cartilage height in the medial and lateral knee compartments of osteoarthritic knees. Methods: A prospective diagnostic study, including 73 patients was performed. Inclusion criteria were enrollment for either a medial unicompartmental or a total knee replacement. Radiographs were taken as the Rosenberg view, and coronal stress radiography using the Telos stress device. Repeated measurements were performed. Experienced knee surgeons performed measurements of cartilage height at a standardized location of joint space width (JSW), and a rater-perceived location of minimal joint space width (mJSW), thus allowing for reliability and agreement analysesusing weighted kappa. Coronal stress measurements were ultimately compared to the Rosenberg view using Spearman’s rank correlation. Results: A total of 12,264 measurements were performed. The radiographic methods proved substantial reliability. Intra- and interrater agreement showed substantial to almost perfect agreement. A very strong correlation was observed in the medial knee compartment (r = 0.91; CI = 0.84–0.95; p < 0.001), with a mean difference of 0.1 mm and limits of agreement of − 1.5 to 1.7 mm, when comparing JSW between the Rosenberg view and varus stress. Only a strong correlation was observed medially when using mJSW, and when using this measurementmore incidences of bone-on-bone were observed than when measuring with JSW. A Strong correlation was observed in the lateral knee compartment (r = 0.83; CI = 0.71–0.89; p < 0.001), with a mean difference of 0.62 mm and limits of agreement of − 1.5 to 2.7 mm, when comparing JSW between the Rosenberg view and valgus stress. Conclusion: The Rosenberg view is similar to 20° coronal valgus–varus stress radiography for determining articular cartilage thickness. Both techniques can be used in a clinical setting. Therefore, extra radiographs, equipment and expertise could be saved, when solely utilizing the Rosenberg view which is simple to perform. Level of evidence: III.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Mortensen, Jacob F.","Kappel, Andreas","Rasmussen, Lasse E.","Østgaard, Svend E.","Odgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-004661"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Mortensen, Jacob F."],"keyword":["Arthroplasty","Cartilage Articular diagnostic imaging","Humans","Knee Joint diagnostic imaging","Medial unicompartmental knee replacement UKR","Osteoarthritis Knee diagnostic imaging","Prospective Studies","Radiography","Reproducibility of Results","Rosenberg","Stress radiography","Telos","Total knee arthroplasty TKR","Valgus","Varus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the rosenberg view and coronal stress radiographs give similar measurements of articular cartilage height in knees with osteoarthritis","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85114166292&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-004661","identifier":[{"id":"34477925","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85114166292","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5ff1a068-8c44-49ee-91e8-09c43540efec","ku-65d381c6-7b23-4862-9cd6-a776ba9c44ff","sdu-e0548f72-4138-4845-a3e4-bea4b2d04852"],"keyword":["Arthroplasty","Cartilage, Articular/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Knee Joint/diagnostic imaging","Medial unicompartmental knee replacement (UKR)","Osteoarthritis, Knee/diagnostic imaging","Prospective Studies","Radiography","Reproducibility of Results","Rosenberg","Stress radiography","Telos","Total knee arthroplasty (TKR)","Valgus","Varus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F0C3C4FF6EFC92A8FABEF4D84E0E28B5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Orthopaedic Surgery","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hoved-Orto","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"north denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-NDR","l3nl":"North Denmark Region","l3nn":"North Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"North Denmark Region","namevar":["Aalborg University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-NDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Orthopaedics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Regional Hospital Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"6","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Orthopaedic Surgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob F.","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","name":"Mortensen, Jacob F.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Andreas","key":"kappelpau","last":"Kappel","locid":"8c042227-bd3b-4e95-a0b2-fa2dfdd79328","name":"Kappel, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0001-8385-3567","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4 5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse E.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ada7d12e-e6cc-4568-b072-91b059d28c72","name":"Rasmussen, Lasse Enkebølle","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lasse E.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Svend E.","key":"østgaardpau","last":"Østgaard","name":"Østgaard, Svend E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 1","first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"33eeba1f-407c-4aa4-bf69-5efb12863f82","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34477925"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00402-021-04136-z","issn":["09368051","14343916"],"issn_org":["09368051"],"issue":"9","journal":"Archives of Orthopaedic and Trauma Surgery","pages":"2349-2360","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Archives of Orthopaedic and Trauma Surgery","volume":"142"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85114166292"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5ff1a068-8c44-49ee-91e8-09c43540efec","ku-65d381c6-7b23-4862-9cd6-a776ba9c44ff","sdu-e0548f72-4138-4845-a3e4-bea4b2d04852"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Rosenberg view and coronal stress radiographs give similar measurements of articular cartilage height in knees with osteoarthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-004661","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The aim of the current study was to determine if treatment with senicapoc, improves the PaO 2 /FiO 2 ratio in patients with COVID-19 and severe respiratory insufficiency. METHODS: Investigator-initiated, randomized, open-label, phase II trial in four intensive care units (ICU) in Denmark. We included patients aged ≥18 years and admitted to an ICU with severe respiratory insufficiency due to COVID-19. The intervention consisted of 50 mg enteral senicapoc administered as soon as possible after randomization and again after 24 h. Patients in the control group received standard care only. The primary outcome was the PaO 2 /FiO 2 ratio at 72 h. RESULTS: Twenty patients were randomized to senicapoc and 26 patients to standard care. Important differences existed in patient characteristics at baseline, including more patients being on non-invasive/invasive ventilation in the control group (54% vs. 35%). The median senicapoc concentration at 72 h was 62.1 ng/ml (IQR 46.7-71.2). The primary outcome, PaO 2 /FiO 2 ratio at 72 h, was significantly lower in the senicapoc group (mean 19.5 kPa, SD 6.6) than in the control group (mean 24.4 kPa, SD 9.2) (mean difference -5.1 kPa [95% CI -10.2, -0.04] p = .05). The 28-day mortality in the senicapoc group was 2/20 (10%) compared with 6/26 (23%) in the control group (OR 0.36 95% CI 0.06-2.07, p = .26). CONCLUSIONS: Treatment with senicapoc resulted in a significantly lower PaO 2 /FiO 2 ratio at 72 h with no differences for other outcomes.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Granfeldt, Asger","Andersen, Lars W","Vallentin, Mikael F","Hilberg, Ole","Hasselstrøm, Jørgen B","Sørensen, Lambert K","Mogensen, Susie","Christensen, Steffen","Grejs, Anders M","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Kristiansen, Klaus T","Strøm, Thomas","Johansen, Isik S","Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Simonsen, Ulf"],"cuid":["S04-094.63-009915"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Granfeldt, Asger"],"keyword":["ARDS","Acetamides","Adolescent","Adult","Covid 19","Humans","Respiration Artificial","Respiratory Insufficiency","Respiratory Insufficiency therapy","SARS CoV 2","Senicapoc","Trityl Compounds"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"senicapoc treatment in covid 000000000019 patients with severe respiratory insufficiency a randomized open label phase ii trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.14072","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["The trial was funded by a grant from the Independent Research Fund Denmark (DFF‐6110‐00622B). We thank Professors John Olichney and Heike Wulff, University of Davies, California for making senicapoc available for the present clinical trial Funding information"],"id":"S04-094.63-009915","identifier":[{"id":"35403225","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC9111301","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85132616375","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-ce91a3d0-e2fc-4832-87c9-10bacca0fb80","au-193ffe39-0a48-4c84-b88d-0ec56cfaaef8","ku-c80edc29-7852-494b-a9ff-3a93eb1475e3","sdu-857906b6-d43e-4866-bb01-c6c939c18f6f"],"keyword":["ARDS","Acetamides","Adolescent","Adult","COVID-19","Humans","Respiration, Artificial","Respiratory Insufficiency/therapy","SARS-CoV-2","Senicapoc","Trityl Compounds","respiratory insufficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-FF0456533BDFC5D43ECB077A34A8AAC3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":