":"perneranderspau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":68,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"23","corresponding":null,"first":"Rine Moulvad","key":"siegumfeldtrinemoulvadoth","last":"Siegumfeldt","locid":"e57237fc-4c35-458a-95f8-221a377c8734","name":"Siegumfeldt, Rine Moulvad","rank":69,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"23","corresponding":null,"first":"Stine Rom","key":"vestergaardstineromoth","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"f841510b-8964-42ea-b510-22e1baf0b226","name":"Vestergaard, Stine Rom","rank":70,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["35709019"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1056/nejmoa2202707","issn":["00284793","15334406"],"issn_org":["00284793"],"issue":"26","journal":"The New England Journal of Medicine","pages":"2459-2470","publisher":"Massachussetts Medical Society","status":"p","title":"The New England Journal of Medicine","title_org":"New England Journal of Medicine","volume":"386"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85133214877"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","North Denmark Region","Other Research","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9eac7765-86f2-4d3c-856f-6537ab1cecb6","au-34a83b86-7b4a-467d-9ec7-adf72b6e7b09","ku-637bb267-bce9-4d5e-8032-f7b892c52dc0","sdu-126603fd-5865-4179-9637-4c1cd22c7ff5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Restriction of Intravenous Fluid in ICU Patients with Septic Shock","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-096.18-007689","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The primary results from the Vasopressin and Methylprednisolone for In-Hospital Cardiac Arrest (VAM-IHCA) trial have previously been reported. The objective of the current manuscript is to report long-term outcomes. METHODS: The VAM-IHCA trial was a multicenter, randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial conducted at ten hospitals in Denmark. Adult patients (age ≥ 18 years) were eligible for the trial if they had an in-hospital cardiac arrest and received at least one dose of epinephrine during resuscitation. The trial drugs consisted of 40 mg methylprednisolone (Solu-Medrol®, Pfizer) and 20 IU of vasopressin (Empressin®, Amomed Pharma GmbH) given as soon as possible after the first dose of epinephrine. This manuscript report outcomes at 6 months and 1 year including survival, survival with favorable neurological outcome, and health-related quality of life. RESULTS: 501 patients were included in the analysis. At 1 year, 15 patients (6.3%) in the intervention group and 22 patients (8.3%) in the placebo group were alive corresponding to a risk ratio of 0.76 (95% CI, 0.41-1.41). A favorable neurologic outcome at 1 year, based on the Cerebral Performance Category score, was observed in 14 patients (5.9%) in the intervention group and 20 patients (7.6%) in the placebo group (risk ratio, 0.78 [95% CI, 0.41-1.49]. No differences existed between groups for favorable neurological outcome and health-related quality of life at either 6 months or 1 year. CONCLUSIONS: Administration of vasopressin and methylprednisolone, compared with placebo, in patients with in-hospital cardiac arrest did not improve long-term outcomes in this trial.","author_count":37,"contributors":["Granfeldt, Asger","Sindberg, Birthe","Isbye, Dan","Kjærgaard, Jesper","Kristensen, Camilla M.","Darling, Søren","Zwisler, Stine T.","Fisker, Stine","Christian Schmidt, Jens","Kirkegaard, Hans","Grejs, Anders M.","Rossau, Jørgen R. G.","Larsen, Jacob Moesgaard","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Riddersholm, Signe","Iversen, Kasper","Schultz, Martin","Nielsen, Jakob L.","Løfgren, Bo","Lauridsen, Kasper G.","Sølling, Christoffer","Pælestik, Kim","Kjærgaard, Anders G.","Due-Rasmussen, Dorte","Folke, Fredrik","Charlot, Mette G.","Jepsen, Rikke Malene H. G.","Wiberg, Sebastian","Høybye, Maria","Holmberg, Mathias J.","Andersen, Lars W."],"cuid":["S04-099.05-002368"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Andersen, Lars W."],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Children’s Hospital of Philadelphia","University of Pennsylvania"],"keyword":["In hospital cardiac arrest","Long term","Methylprednisolone","Outcomes","Vasopressin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effect of vasopressin and methylprednisolone vs placebo on long term outcomes in patients with in hospital cardiac arrest a randomized clinical trial","src":["aau","au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.resuscitation.2022.04.017","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding for the trial was provided by Aarhus University Research Foundation; the Department of Clinical Medicine, Aarhus University; the Central Denmark Region; and the Independent Research Fund Denmark. Empressin and corresponding placebo ampoules were provided free of charge by Amomed Pharma GmbH. Dr Andersen reported receiving grants from Aarhus University Research Foundation, the Department of Clinical Medicine at Aarhus University, and Independent Research Fund Denmark, and nonfinancial support from Amomed Pharma GmbH, which provided trial drug during the conduct of the study. Dr J. Kjærgaard reported receiving grants from the Novo Nordisk Foundation (NNF17OC0028706) outside the submitted work. Dr Lauridsen reported receiving grants from Independent Research Fund Denmark during the conduct of the study. Dr Granfeldt reported receiving personal fees from Noorik Biopharmaceuticals outside the submitted work. No other disclosures were reported."],"id":"S04-099.05-002368","identifier":[{"id":"35490936","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85129770063","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-2f4d42f1-7e14-4934-a12b-0c2f1b103f55","au-ca4e2548-c968-4347-929e-d3dc08d3e5bb","ku-b3e35d64-a999-4717-9cd5-0186b3394885","sdu-11604bf5-280e-45a2-bd13-340fdf50ad90"],"keyword":["In-hospital cardiac arrest","Long-term","Methylprednisolone","Outcomes","Vasopressin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-49B6006BDF034E570DE17E07767D3863"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/316396612/1_s2.0_S0300957222001356_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/475422357/Granfeldt_et_al._2022_._Effect_of_vasopressin_and_methylprednisolone_vs._placebo_on_long_term_outcomes_in_patients_with_in_hospital_cardiac_arrest_a_randomized_clinical_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/335290813/Effect_of_vasopressin_and_methylprednisolone_vs._placebo_on_long_term_outcomes_in_patients_with_in_hospital_cardiac_arrest_a_randomized_clinical_trial.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","t