":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Resuscitation","volume":"175"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85129770063"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Other Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","prehospital emergency medical services"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-2f4d42f1-7e14-4934-a12b-0c2f1b103f55","au-ca4e2548-c968-4347-929e-d3dc08d3e5bb","ku-b3e35d64-a999-4717-9cd5-0186b3394885","sdu-11604bf5-280e-45a2-bd13-340fdf50ad90"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effect of Vasopressin and Methylprednisolone vs. Placebo on Long-Term Outcomes in Patients with In-Hospital Cardiac Arrest A Randomized Clinical Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.05-002368","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"AIM: To investigate the association of anthropometric parameters [height, weight, body mass index (BMI), body surface area (BSA), and lean body mass (LBM)] with outcomes in atrial fibrillation (AF). METHODS AND RESULTS: Ten-thousand two-hundred twenty patients were enrolled [40.3% females, median age 70 (62-77) years, followed for 728 (interquartile range 653-745) days]. Sex-specific tertiles were considered for the five anthropometric variables. At the end of follow-up, survival free from all-cause death was worse in the lowest tertiles for all the anthropometric variables analyzed. On multivariable Cox regression analysis, an independent association with all-cause death was found for the lowest vs. middle tertile when body weight (hazard ratio [HR] 1.66, 95%CI 1.23-2.23), BMI (HR 1.65, 95%CI 1.23-2.21), and BSA (HR 1.49, 95%CI 1.11-2.01) were analysed in female sex, as well as for body weight in male patients (HR 1.61, 95%CI 1.25-2.07). Conversely, the risk of MACE was lower for the highest tertile (vs. middle tertile) of BSA and LBM in males and for the highest tertile of weight and BSA in female patients. A higher occurrence of haemorrhagic events was found for female patients in the lowest tertile of height [odds ratio (OR) 1.90, 95%CI 1.23-2.94] and LBM (OR 2.13, 95%CI 1.40-3.26). CONCLUSIONS: In AF patients height, weight, BMI, BSA, and LBM were associated with clinical outcomes, with all-cause death being higher for patients presenting lower values of these variables, i.e. in the lowest tertiles of distribution. The anthropometric variables independently associated with other outcomes were also different between male and female subjects.","author_count":26,"contributors":["Boriani, Giuseppe","Vitolo, Marco","Malavasi, Vincenzo L.","Proietti, Marco","Fantecchi, Elisa","Diemberger, Igor","Fauchier, Laurent","Marin, Francisco","Nabauer, Michael","Potpara, Tatjana S.","Dan, Gheorghe-Andrei","Kalarus, Zbigniew","Tavazzi, Luigi","Maggioni, Aldo Pietro","Lane, Deirdre A.","Lip, Gregory Y H","Joensen, Albert Marni","Gammelmark, Anders","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Dinesen, Pia Thisted","Riahi, Sam","Venø, Stine Krogh","Sørensen, Bodil Ginnerup","Korsgaard, Anne Marie","Andersen, Karen Petrea","Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-112954"],"filters":{"added":"2022-08","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corpau":["ESC-EHRA EORP-AF Long-Term General Registry Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Boriani, Giuseppe"],"country":["France","Germany","Italy","Poland","Romania","Serbia","Spain","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Associazione Nazionale Medici Cardiologi Ospedalieri","Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Bologna Policlinico S. Orsola – Malpighi","Carol Davila University of Medicine and Pharmacy","Centro de Investigación Biomédica en Red (CIBER)","Clinical Center of Serbia","Colentina Clinical Hospital","Hospital Virgen de la Arrixaca","Hôpital Trousseau, CHU de Tours","IRCCS Istituti Clinici Scientifici Maugeri S.p.A. SB - Pavia","Instituto Murciano de Investigación Biosanitaria","Liverpool Heart and Chest Hospital NHS Foundation Trust","Ludwig Maximilian University of Munich","Maria Cecilia Hospital","Medical University of Silesia in Katowice","Silesian Centre for Heart Diseases","University Hospital of Modena","University of Belgrade","University of Bologna","University of Liverpool","University of Milan","University of Modena and Reggio Emilia","University of Murcia"],"keyword":["Atrial Fibrillation diagnosis","Atrial fibrillation","Body Mass Index","Body Weight","Cardiology","Female","Humans","Infant","Lean body mass","Male","Obesity","Outcome","Registries","Risk Factors","Stroke"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["