 Karen Petrea","rank":25,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"},{"affno":"23","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Fragtrup","key":"hellumoth","last":"Hellum","locid":"fd7755f7-451a-448c-8679-baccccd2d85a","name":"Hellum, Camilla Fragtrup","rank":26,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["35671129"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurjpc/zwac115","issn":["20474873","20474881"],"issn_org":["20474873"],"issue":"15","journal":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","pages":"1967-1981","paperid":"zwac115","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Preventive Cardiology","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85141893888"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d87f732a-8ec8-4958-a1e2-d39ac6528b79"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Impact of anthropometric factors on outcomes in atrial fibrillation patients : analysis on 10 220 patients from the European Society of Cardiology (ESC)-European Heart Rhythm Association (EHRA) EurObservational Research Programme on Atrial Fibrillation (EORP-AF) general long-term registry","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-112954","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"DNA repair gene mutations are frequent in castration-resistant prostate cancer (CRPC), suggesting eligibility for poly(ADP-ribose) polymerase inhibitor (PARPi) treatment. However, therapy resistance is a major clinical challenge and genes contributing to PARPi resistance are poorly understood. Using a genome-wide CRISPR-Cas9 knockout screen, this study aimed at identifying genes involved in PARPi resistance in CRPC. Based on the screen, we identified PARP1, and six novel candidates associated with olaparib resistance upon knockout. For validation, we generated multiple knockout populations/clones per gene in C4 and/or LNCaP CRPC cells, which confirmed that loss of PARP1, ARH3, YWHAE, or UBR5 caused olaparib resistance. PARP1 or ARH3 knockout caused cross-resistance to other PARPis (veliparib and niraparib). Furthermore, PARP1 or ARH3 knockout led to reduced autophagy, while pharmacological induction of autophagy partially reverted their PARPi resistant phenotype. Tumor RNA sequencing of 126 prostate cancer patients identified low ARH3 expression as an independent predictor of recurrence. Our results advance the understanding of PARPi response by identifying four novel genes that contribute to PARPi sensitivity in CRPC and suggest a new model of PARPi resistance through decreased autophagy.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Ipsen, Malene Blond","Sørensen, Ea Marie Givskov","Thomsen, Emil Aagaard","Weiss, Simone","Haldrup, Jakob","Dalby, Anders","Palmfeldt, Johan","Bross, Peter","Rasmussen, Martin","Fredsøe, Jacob","Klingenberg, Søren","Jochumsen, Mads Ryø","Bouchelouche, Kirsten","Ulhøi, Benedicte Parm","Borre, Michael","Mikkelsen, Jacob Giehm","Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-198758"],"filters":{"added":"2022-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Sørensen, Karina Dalsgaard"],"keyword":["Activation","Autophagy","Cell free DNA","Olaparib","Repair"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a genome wide crispr cas000000000009 knockout screen identifies novel parp inhibitor resistance genes in prostate cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85135518048","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-198758","identifier":[{"id":"85135518048","type":"scopus"},{"id":"35933519","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000836761200001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-795a60ae-9143-4e4f-828f-abc0f92fe599"],"keyword":["ACTIVATION","AUTOPHAGY","CELL-FREE DNA","OLAPARIB","POLY(ADP-RIBOSE)","REPAIR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-073494886F51081C362469253F3E9975"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2022","yearSub":"2022"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Molecular Medicine (MOMA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Teitur Trophics ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Malene Blond","key":"ipsenmaleneblondpau","last":"Ipsen","locid":"73e52588-9d69-4440-9b87-56af923201e3","name":"Ipsen, Malene Blond","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}