"","first":"Bruce","key":"vaughnpau","last":"Vaughn","name":"Vaughn, Bruce","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"e0501b84-a817-417e-9c70-9601c6b26cb8","name":"Svensson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-4364-6085","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo Møllesøe","key":"vintherpau","last":"Vinther","locid":"0179bd8e-644a-4f98-a641-1bc374aabdd8","name":"Vinther, Bo Møllesøe","orcid":"0000-0002-6078-771X","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"J. W. C.","key":"whitepau","last":"White","name":"White, J. W. C.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33833238"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41467-021-22241-w","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"2106","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104051347"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9f6ae0ee-a3f4-44f9-b9a9-12a3fb17adf1"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The anatomy of past abrupt warmings recorded in Greenland ice","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-488727","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The hypothalamic–pituitary–thyroid hormone axis might be affected in COVID-19, but existing studies have shown varying results. It has been hypothesized that hyperinflammation, as reflected by the secretion of cytokines, might induce thyroid dysfunction among patients with COVID-19. We explored thyroid hormone involvement in the acute phase of symptomatic COVID-19 and its possible associations with cytokine levels and mortality risk. This was a single-center study of 116 consecutive patients hospitalized for moderate-to-severe COVID-19 disease. Serum concentrations of thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), free thyroxine (T4), and 45 cytokines/chemokines were measured in all patients within 3 days of admission. Data were extracted retrospectively through a manual review of health records. At admission, 95 (81.9%) were euthyroid; while 21 (18.1%) had biochemically thyroid dysfunction including subclinical thyrotoxicosis (n = 11), overt thyrotoxicosis (n = 2), hypothyroidism (n = 1), non-thyroidal illness (n = 2), and normal TSH but high free T4 (n = 5). TSH levels were inversely correlated with IL-8 (rs = –0.248), IL-10 (rs = –0.253), IL-15 (rs = –0.213), IP-10 (rs = –0.334), and GM-CSF (rs = –0.254). Moreover, IL-8 levels, IP-10, and GM-CSF were significantly higher in patients with serum TSH < 0.4 mIU/L. Lastly, a two-fold increment of IL-8 and IL-10 was associated with significantly higher odds of having TSH < 0.4 mIU/L (odds ratio 1.86 (1.11–3.10) and 1.78 (1.03–3.06)). Serum TSH was not associated with 30-or 90-day mortality. In conclusion, this study suggests that fluctuations of TSH levels in patients with COVID-19 may be influenced by circulating IL-8, IL-10, IL-15, IP-10, and GM-CSF as previously described in autoimmune thyroid diseases.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Clausen, Clara Lundetoft","Rasmussen, Åse Krogh","Johannsen, Trine Holm","Hilsted, Linda Maria","Skakkebæk, Niels Erik","Szecsi, Pal Bela","Pedersen, Lise","Benfield, Thomas","Juul, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507718"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Cytokines","IL 10","IL 8","Mortality","SARS CoV 2","Thyroid Gland","Thyroid function"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thyroid function in covid 000000000019 and the association with cytokine levels and mortality","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-21-0301","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-507718","identifier":[{"id":"85117616395","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34468398","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8494417","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-bf822ea8-9e70-4a5b-a511-66df40539f43"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Cytokines","IL-10","IL-8","Mortality","SARS-CoV-2","Thyroid function","Thyroid gland"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B24E201D96C760B31091C3FEEE4A8AB0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284105232/_20493614_Endocrine_Connections_Thyroid_function_in_COVID_19_and_the_association_with_cytokine_levels_and_mortality.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1530/EC-21-0301","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"region zealand","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-ZEA","l3nl":"Region Zealand","l3nn":"Region Zealand","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region Zealand","namevar":["Holbæk Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-ZEA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Clara Lundetoft","key":"clausenpau","last":"Clausen","locid":"6dd24999-daa5-468b-8eca-c65e875c37a5","name":"Clausen, Clara Lundetoft","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Åse Krogh","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Åse Krogh","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Trine Holm","key":"johannsenpau","last":"Johannsen","name":"Johannsen, Trine Holm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Linda Maria","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","name":"Hilsted, Linda Maria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Niels Erik","key":"skakkebækpau","last":"Skakkebæk","locid":"79cf30ee-3d35-4c17-bd83-b233c78d01b9","name":"Skakkebæk, Niels Erik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Pal Bela","key":"szecsipau","last":"Szecsi","name":"Szecsi, Pal Bela","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lise","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Lise","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"benfieldpau","last":"Benfield","locid":"03fdbbba-4bc0-41aa-845b-81ba0bded9ba","name":"Benfield, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0003-0698-9385","rank":8,"rolec