{"abstract":"The foliar microbiome can extend the host plant phenotype by expanding its genomic and metabolic capabilities. Despite increasing recognition of the importance of the foliar microbiome for plant fitness, stress physiology, and yield, the diversity, function, and contribution of foliar microbiomes to plant phenotypic traits remain largely elusive. The recent adoption of high-throughput technologies is helping to unravel the diversityand spatiotemporal dynamics of foliar microbiomes, but we have yet to resolve their functional importance for plant growth, development, and ecology. Here, we focus on the processes that govern the assembly of the foliar microbiome and the potential mechanisms involved in extended plant phenotypes. We highlight knowledge gaps and provide suggestions for new research directions that can propel the field forward. These efforts will be instrumental in maximizing the functional potential of the foliar microbiome for sustainable crop production.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hawkes, Christine V.","Kjøller, Rasmus","Raaijmakers, Jos M.","Riber, Leise","Christensen, Svend","Rasmussen, Simon","Christensen, Jan H.","Dahl, Anders Bjorholm","Westergaard, Jesper Cairo","Nielsen, Mads","Brown-Guedira, Gina","Hestbjerg Hansen, Lars"],"cuid":["S02-095.45-033283"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","North Carolina State University","Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","The Netherlands Institute of Ecology"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Fungi","Omics","Phages","Phyllosphere","Plant microbe interactions"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"extension of plant phenotypes by the foliar microbiome","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85108349563","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-095.45-033283","identifier":[{"id":"000669645400030","type":"wos"},{"id":"34143648","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85108349563","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-1fe6d5b8-4c93-40c7-b179-4ae21fa5d086","ku-e7240586-37cf-4087-be36-6aac3a8d7812"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Fungi","Omics","Phages","Phyllosphere","Plant microbe interactions"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-61E038C3D34B2F56F5DBFA83A749CBF6"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"us","key":"north carolina state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"North Carolina State University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Terrestrial Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"royal netherlands academy of arts and sciences","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Royal Netherlands Academy of Arts and Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"the netherlands institute of ecology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"The Netherlands Institute of Ecology","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic",