{"abstract":"Background: Adjuvant radiation therapy (RT) for breast cancer has improved overall survival. However, incidental exposure of the heart has been linked to development of radiation-induced heart disease. The aim of this study was, in a cohort of asymptomatic post-irradiation breast cancer patients, to investigate changes in myocardial blood flow (MBF) and presence of perfusion defects in myocardial perfusion positron-emission-tomography (PET) in the irradiated myocardium. Methods and Results: Twenty patients treated with RT for left-sided breast cancer underwent 13N-ammonia myocardial perfusion PET 7(± 2) years after breath adapted RT to a total dose of 48 Gy given in 24 fractions. No differences in rest or stress MBF were noted between the irradiated and non-irradiated myocardium (1.29 (± 0.29) vs 1.33 (± 0.29) mL/g/min, ns; 2.74 (± 0.59) vs 2.78 (± 0.66) mL/g/min, ns, respectively). One patient demonstrated a myocardial perfusion defect localized in the irradiated anterior wall myocardium. Conclusion: Although limited by a small sample size, early signs of cardiac injury detected by NH3 myocardial perfusion PET was at least not frequent in our cohort of patients treated with a modern RT technique for left-sided breast cancer, even 7 years after treatment. The findings however, may not rule out subsequent development of myocardial injury.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Thomas","Kjaer, Andreas","Lassen, Martin Lyngby","Pedersen, Anders Navrsted","Specht, Lena","Aznar, Marianne C.","Hasbak, Philip"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-413051"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Breast cancer","Myocardial perfusion","Radiation therapy","cardiac positron emission tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no changes in myocardial perfusion following radiation therapy of left sided breast cancer a positron emission tomography study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-413051","identifier":[{"id":"85075233536","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31741325","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-20e1df1b-babd-40f8-a70d-af4530446459"],"keyword":["Myocardial perfusion","ammonia cardiac PET","breast cancer","cardiac positron-emission-tomography","radiation therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D3F75FD9D97DA484BA1015D9C30C145"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin Lyngby","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","name":"Lassen, Martin Lyngby","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Navrsted","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","name":"Pedersen, Anders Navrsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Marianne C.","key":"aznarpau","last":"Aznar","locid":"1006f89a-135a-444b-9752-476cee077579","name":"Aznar, Marianne C.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Philip","key":"hasbakpau","last":"Hasbak","name":"Hasbak, Philip","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31741325"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s12350-019-01949-9","issn":["10713581","15326551"],"issn_org":["10713581"],"journal":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","pages":"1923-1932","status":"p","title":"Journal of Nuclear Cardiology","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85075233536"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-20e1df1b-babd-40f8-a70d-af4530446459"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"No changes in myocardial perfusion following radiation therapy of left-sided breast cancer : A positron emission tomography study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-413051","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background & aims: The European Food Safety Authority recently recommended an increase in the protein content of total diet replacement (TDR) products from 50 to 75 g/day. The rationale was to minimize reductions in lean mass (LM) and resting metabolic rate (RMR) that occur with weight loss, and thereby facilitate maintenance of lost weight. We sought to directly compare the efficacy of TDR regimens with the new vs the current protein requirement. Methods: We randomized 108 adults with overweight or obesity (body mass index 28-40 kg/m2) to very-low-calorie diets (VLCD) with either 52 or 77 g/day protein for 8 weeks (total energy intake of 600 or 700 kcal/day, respectively). LM was determined by dual energy X-ray absorptiometry and RMR by indirect calorimetry. Results: Attrition rate was 22% in both groups. Both VLCDs decreased body weight, fat mass, LM, and RMR (all P < 0.05). Significant time-by-group interactions were detected for weight and fat mass (both P < 0.05), with corresponding reductions being smaller in the higher-protein than the standard-protein VLCD, likely because of the added calories. On the other hand, reductions in LM (6% from baseline) and RMR (9-10% from baseline) did not differ between groups (P = 0.155 and P = 0.389, respectively), and the contribution of LM to total weight loss was identical (27 ± 2% of lost weight, P = 0.973). Conclusions: Our results indicate that the proposed increase in the protein content of TDR products does not attenuate reductions in LM and RMR in individuals with overweight and obesity who are treated with <800 kcal/day VLCDs for 2 months. Clinical trial registry: ClinicalTrials.gov # NCT04156165.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Magkos, Faidon","Hjorth, Mads Fiil","Asping, Sarah","Rosenkrans, Maria I","Ingemann Rasmussen, Sidse Ida","Ritz, Christian","Sjödin, Anders Mikael","Geiker, Nina Rica Wium"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440809"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Fat free mass","Low calorie diet","Protein","Resting energy expenditure","Weight loss"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a protein supplemented very low calorie diet does not mitigate reductions in lean mass and resting metabolic rate in subjects with overweight or obesity a randomized controlled trial","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clnu.2021.10.006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440809","identifier":[{"id":"85118556899","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34749132","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-4f5c2795-c7a7-4d6a-8d01-3280adc08a04"],"keyword":["Faculty of Science","Fat-free mass","Low-calorie diet","Protein","Resting energy expenditure","Weight loss"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DBA4CA18AF7E1AE6CED13F8F17B00663"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284397704/Magkos_et_al_Clinical_Nutrition_2021_Vol_40_12_5726_5733.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.clnu.2021.10.006","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Lifecourse Nutrition & Health","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Nutrition, Exercise and Sports, Obesity Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Faidon","key":"magkospau","last":"Magkos","locid":"ac8c9eed-7c49-41f0-8015-fc4ea0f595ee","name":"Magkos, Faidon","orcid":"0000-0002-1312-7364","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Fiil","key":"hjorthpau","last":"Hjorth","locid":"00918fa0-7b1e-4128-919e-a0af9497026b","name":"Hjorth, Mads Fiil","orcid":"0000-0001-9440-2737","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"aspingpau","last":"Asping","locid":"0a50b1b8-9b35-4dc2-bc4a-dd62f0d64cd8","name":"Asping, Sarah","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria I","key":"rosenkranspau","last":"Rosenkrans","locid":"edb2a616-87db-446f-902c-c01e150aff95","name":"Rosenkrans, Maria I","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sidse Ingemann","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a427a000-d7ed-48b8-8886-4b435869957e","name":"Ingemann Rasmussen, Sidse Ida","name_org":"Rasmussen, Sidse Ingemann","orcid":"0000-0002-9967-3939","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"ritzpau","last":"Ritz","locid":"c881424f-d529-443e-b60e-bc2edb674ede","name":"Ritz, Christian","orcid":"0000-0002-5095-0624","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"sjödinpau","last":"Sjödin","locid":"24ea7b85-2a13-44ec-93f5-fb419b0ab4fd","name":"Sjödin, Anders Mikael","name_org":"Sjödin, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6451-3847","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Nina Rica Wium","key":"geikerpau","last":"Geiker","locid":"36dfc94c-330a-452a-b2c9-5fa775754a9a","name":"Geiker, Nina Rica Wium","orcid":"0000-0001-8063-5820","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34749132"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnu.2021.10.006","issn":["02615614","15321983"],"issn_org":["02615614"],"issue":"12","journal":"Clinical Nutrition","pages":"5726-5733","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition","volume":"40"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85118556899"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4f5c2795-c7a7-4d6a-8d01-3280adc08a04"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A protein-supplemented very-low-calorie diet does not mitigate reductions in lean mass and resting metabolic rate in subjects with overweight or obesity: A randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-440809","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: To determine the prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 at a Danish tertiary referral otorhinolaryngology clinic during the first wave of the COVID-19 pandemic among patients with suspected acute upper airway infection (UAI) and patients operated for head and neck cancer (HNC), respectively. To monitor changes in the number of patient encounters for acute UAI and the number of referrals for the workup of HNC. Trial registration: NCT-04356560 (Clinicaltrials.gov). Methods: Prospective enrolled case series of all patients with suspected acute UAI (n = 88) and of patients undergoing surgery for HNC (n = 96), respectively, from March 23rd to May 5th, 2020, at a public tertiary referral otorhinolaryngology clinic in Denmark. SARS-CoV-2 was diagnosed with nasopharyngeal and oropharyngeal swabbing. Patients with suspected acute UAI had symptoms and definitive diagnoses registered in a database. Trends in the number of referrals and patient encounters were retrieved from an electronic patient journal system and analyzed retrospectively. Results: Eighty-eight patients with acute UAI were enrolled including 55 men and 34 women, median age of 31 years (range: 10 months to 82 years). One patient (1.1%) tested positive. Among 96 patients operated for HNC, zero tested positive. The number of referrals for HNC workup, and patient encounters for peritonsillar abscesses, decreased markedly in the first 3 weeks. Conclusion: The prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 during the first 6 weeks of the first wave was minimal among patients with acute UAI and zero among patients operated for HNC. The decrease in referrals for the workup of HNC may increase time to treatment initiation and patient morbidity.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen, Peter Anders","Rasmussen, Kasper Møller Boje","Channir, Hani Ibrahim","von Buchwald, Christian","Cayé-Thomasen, Per","Klokker, Mads","Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","Kirkby, Nikolai Søren","Aanaes, Kasper","Jensen, Ramon Gordon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453863"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Head and Neck Neoplasms","Otolaryngology","Respiratory tract infections","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","Tertiary Care Centers"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the impact and prevalence of sars cov 000000000002 in patients with head and neck cancer and acute upper airway infection in a tertiary otorhinolaryngology referral center in denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7778690/pdf/405_2020_Article_6514.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-453863","identifier":[{"id":"33388982","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85098710040","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7778690","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-65231263-8170-4f02-90e8-6a3757aa1648"],"keyword":["COVID-19","Head and neck neoplasms","Otolaryngology","Respiratory tract infections","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2","Tertiary care centers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-25A17490263347864F8C5B12E310B281"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC7778690/pdf/405_2020_Article_6514.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Peter Anders","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Peter Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper Møller Boje","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Kasper Møller Boje","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hani Ibrahim","key":"channirpau","last":"Channir","name":"Channir, Hani Ibrahim","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Per","key":"cayéthomasenpau","last":"Cayé-Thomasen","locid":"51411e35-b4a9-4e04-b2ef-538ebf70b337","name":"Cayé-Thomasen, Per","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"klokkerpau","last":"Klokker","locid":"be74f452-48e9-4e56-8de1-f0ed083b9c77","name":"Klokker, Mads","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jenny Dahl","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"ace82a97-ed40-44ae-9619-37b98fdaf285","name":"Knudsen, Jenny Dahl","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolai Søren","key":"kirkbypau","last":"Kirkby","name":"Kirkby, Nikolai Søren","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"aanaespau","last":"Aanaes","locid":"8bf39677-0bde-4163-ae14-19cf5b84d4bf","name":"Aanaes, Kasper","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ramon Gordon","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"bbbd5d78-5cb2-4f8a-9cf2-e19601100ef9","name":"Jensen, Ramon Gordon","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33388982"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00405-020-06514-6","issn":["09374477","09428992"],"issn_org":["09374477"],"issue":"9","journal":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","pages":"3409-3415","status":"p","title":"European Archives of Oto-Rhino-Laryngology","volume":"278"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85098710040"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-65231263-8170-4f02-90e8-6a3757aa1648"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The impact and prevalence of SARS-CoV-2 in patients with head and neck cancer and acute upper airway infection in a tertiary otorhinolaryngology referral center in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453863","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: Glycated haemoglobin A1c (HbA1c) has limitations as a glycemic marker for patients with diabetes and CKD and for those receiving dialysis. Glycated albumin is an alternative glycemic marker, and some studies have found that glycated albumin more accurately reflects glycemic control than HbA1c in these groups. However, several factors are known to influence the value of glycated albumin including proteinuria. Continuous glucose monitoring (CGM) is another alternative to HbA1c. CGM allows one to assess mean glucose, glucose variability, and the time spent in hypo-, normo-, and hyperglycemia. Currently, several different CGM models are approved for use in patients receiving dialysis; CKD (not on dialysis) is not a contraindication in any of these models. Some devices are for blind recording, while others provide real-time data to patients. Small studies suggest that CGM could improve glycemic control in hemodialysis patients, but this has not been studied for individual CKD stages. Summary: Glycated albumin and CGM avoid the pitfalls of HbA1c in CKD and dialysis populations. However, the value of glycated albumin may be affected by several factors. CGM provides a precise estimation of the mean glucose. Here, we discuss the strengths and limitations for using HbA1c, glycated albumin, or CGM in CKD and dialysis population. Key Messages: Glycated albumin is an alternative glycemic marker but is affected by proteinuria. CGM provides a precise estimation of mean glucose and glucose variability. It remains unclear if CGM improves glycemic control in the CKD and dialysis populations.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bomholt, Tobias","Adrian, Therese","Nørgaard, Kirsten","Ranjan, Ajenthen G.","Almdal, Thomas","Larsson, Anders","Vadstrup, Mette","Rix, Marianne","Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","Hornum, Mads"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-494142"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease","Continuous glucose monitoring","Diabetes","Dialysis","Glycated albumin"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of hba000000000001c glycated albumin and continuous glucose monitoring to assess glucose control in the chronic kidney disease population including dialysis","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-494142","identifier":[{"id":"85097385249","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33264783","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a89748dc-61ab-44f8-860a-5e59187e7655"],"keyword":["Chronic kidney disease","Continuous glucose monitoring","Diabetes","Dialysis","Glycated albumin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B34204E95CC36119AE7DFECD60D5BB82"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"bomholtpau","last":"Bomholt","locid":"00f4e3a0-ae66-4b1e-9ecb-26b698195aaf","name":"Bomholt, Tobias","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Therese","key":"adrianpau","last":"Adrian","name":"Adrian, Therese","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kirsten","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"771b216e-eeb8-449e-8cde-2cdd59ae6dbc","name":"Nørgaard, Kirsten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ajenthen G.","key":"ranjanpau","last":"Ranjan","name":"Ranjan, Ajenthen G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"almdalpau","last":"Almdal","locid":"cae595b0-e059-48f9-b1e4-153595fd7455","name":"Almdal, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mette","key":"vadstruppau","last":"Vadstrup","name":"Vadstrup, Mette","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marianne","key":"rixpau","last":"Rix","name":"Rix, Marianne","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bo","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","locid":"cdd06e7b-83c5-4118-8808-eb4591586aac","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Bo","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads","key":"hornumpau","last":"Hornum","locid":"6e7135d6-13c5-4f40-a3da-e8adf896bc7d","name":"Hornum, Mads","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33264783"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1159/000511614","issn":["16602110","16608151"],"issn_org":["16608151"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nephron","pages":"14-19","status":"p","title":"Nephron","volume":"145"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097385249"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a89748dc-61ab-44f8-860a-5e59187e7655"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Use of HbA1c, Glycated Albumin and Continuous Glucose Monitoring to Assess Glucose Control in the Chronic Kidney Disease Population including Dialysis","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-494142","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"We report high resolution measurements of the stable isotope ratios of ancient ice (delta O-18, delta D) from the North Greenland Eemian deep ice core (NEEM, 77.45 degrees N, 51.06 degrees E). The record covers the period 8-130 ky b2k (y before 2000) with a temporal resolution of approximate to 0.5 and 7 y at the top and the bottom of the core respectively and contains important climate events such as the 8.2 ky event, the last glacial termination and a series of glacial stadials and interstadials. At its bottom part the record contains ice from the Eemian interglacial. Isotope ratios are calibrated on the SMOW/SLAP scale and reported on the GICC05 (Greenland Ice Core Chronology 2005) and AICC2012 (Antarctic Ice Core Chronology 2012) time scales interpolated accordingly. We also provide estimates for measurement precision and accuracy for both delta O-18 and delta D.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Gkinis, Vasileios","Vinther, Bo Møllesøe","Popp, Trevor James","Quistgaard, Thea","Faber, Anne-Katrine","Holme, Christian","Jensen, Camilla-Marie","Lanzky, Mika","Luett, Anine-Maria","Mandrakis, Vasileios","Orum, Niels-Ole","Pedersen, Anna-Sofie","Vaxevani, Nikol","Weng, Yongbiao","Capron, Emilie","Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","Hoerhold, Maria","Jones, Tyler R.","Jouzel, Jean","Landais, Amaelle","Masson-Delmotte, Valerie","Oerter, Hans","Rasmussen, Sune Olander","Steen-Larsen, Hans Christian","Steffensen, Jørgen Peder","Sveinbjornsdottir, Arny-Erla","Svensson, Anders","Vaughn, Bruce","White, James W. C."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-515292"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["France","Germany","Iceland","Norway","United States"],"glorg":["Alfred Wegener Institute - Helmholtz Centre for Polar and Marine Research","All Global Affiliations","Paris-Saclay University","University of Bergen","University of Colorado Boulder","University of Iceland"],"keyword":["ANTARCTIC ICE","CHRONOLOGY AICC2012","Continuous flow analysis","Deuterium","Diffusion","Hydrogen","RATIOS","Stable water isotopes","Variability"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a 000000000120 000000000000 year long climate record from a nw greenland deep ice core at ultra high resolution","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-021-00916-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-515292","identifier":[{"id":"34040008","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85106943398","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8155095","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"000658733200002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["ku-cc0b8f47-eff5-4ca5-8309-f9718bbcc21e"],"keyword":["ANTARCTIC ICE","CHRONOLOGY AICC2012","CONTINUOUS-FLOW ANALYSIS","DEUTERIUM","DIFFUSION","H-2/H-1","HYDROGEN","RATIOS","STABLE WATER ISOTOPES","VARIABILITY"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FF7FC7C3579B38E5253D33509A007238"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-021-00916-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/272406555/s41597_021_00916_9.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate