{"abstract":"Background Sleep is a crucial part of our lives and insufficient sleep has been linked to several health disorders in both children and adults. However, most studies are based on single night laboratory polysomnography, actigraphy, or sleep diaries. The primary aim of this study was to evaluate compliance to and perceived feasibility of the Zmachine insight+ for assessment of habitual sleep parameters in a sample of children and adults for six nights. The secondary aim was to report sleep parameters derived from the Zmachine. Methods We analyzed data from 12 families who participated in the SCREENS pilot trial (2018–2019). Children (n=14) and adults (n=19) had to undergo three nights of EEG-based sleep assessment at baseline and follow-up. We assessed compliance to the sleep assessment protocol and summarized perceived feasibility in children and adults. Summary estimates were computed for total sleep time, sleep onset latency, wake after sleep onset, light sleep, deep sleep, and rapid eye movement sleep. Results Compliance to the sleep assessment protocol was high with 92.9 and 89.4% of children and adults meeting the a priori specified compliance goal of at least two out of three nights of complete sleep data at both baseline and follow-up. In general, the protocol was perceived as feasible, with low prevalence of sleep disruption and only minor issues, e.g. difficulties with removing sensors. Results on sleep parameters indicate large within group variation. Conclusions Our findings support the use of a self-administered EEG-based habitual sleep assessment protocol, including multiple days of measurement, in children and adults. Trial registration Cilinicaltrials.gov: NCT03788525 [Secondary outcome measures; Retrospectively registered; 27th December, 2018].","author_count":5,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jesper","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584281"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Pedersen, Jesper"],"keyword":["Children","Compliance","Electroencephalography","Feasibility"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self administered electroencephalography based sleep assessment compliance and perceived feasibility in children and adults","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41606-021-00059-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584281","ids":["sdu-2693f5ef-c51f-46be-8841-6fdc3f040656"],"keyword":["Children","Compliance","Electroencephalography","Feasibility"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-B48241B360B9D98D5FCD59A32AA139D1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s41606-021-00059-1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/180401710/s41606_021_00059_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f321394d-8abe-49b2-ab02-1b528e734f63","name":"Pedersen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9475-0341","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin Gillies Banke","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8b86a1ef-e6c1-4de3-8300-e30d144bbf60","name":"Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","orcid":"0000-0002-2114-2185","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Grønholt","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"e9ad7180-8cce-4e88-9707-18dedc4c73e0","name":"Olesen, Line Grønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-6588-8878","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"751d26de-66d4-4ef9-8183-880c48c96dc7","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-5666-9614","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedpau","last":"Grøntved","locid":"393b1ca1-e658-437c-9ca3-73aea925ad58","name":"Grøntved, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1584-679X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s41606-021-00059-1","issn":["23982683"],"journal":"Sleep Science and Practice","paperid":"8","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Sleep Science and Practice","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2693f5ef-c51f-46be-8841-6fdc3f040656"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Self-administered electroencephalography-based sleep assessment: compliance and perceived feasibility in children and adults","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-584281","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Aims: To examine prospective and cross-sectional associations between screen time and blood pressure (BP) in preschool children. Methods: The Odense Child Cohort study started in January 2010. Children who were born in the municipality of Odense underwent a clinical examination at 3 and 5 years of age and their parents were asked to complete a questionnaire. A total of 628 children were included in the prospective analysis and 964 children were included in two cross-sectional analyses at 5 years of age. Multivariable adjusted linear and logistic regression models were computed to examine prospective and cross-sectional associations between screen time and BP with adjustment for putative confounding factors. Results: No significant prospective association was found between a 2-year change in screen time and systolic BP (0.55 BP percentile change per 1 h increase in screen time, 95% confidence interval (CI) −1.51 to 2.60) and diastolic BP (0.74 BP percentile change per 1 h increase in screen time, 95% CI −1.09 to 2.57). No significant cross-sectional association was observed between screen time (⩽1 h/day, >1–2 h/day, >2 h/day) and the prevalence of high BP at 5 years of age. Exposure to screen time before bedtime 2–5 days/week and ⩾6 days/week was significantly associated with a greater prevalence of high BP compared with screen time before bedtime 0–1 day/week (odds ratios 1.57 (95% CI 1.02–2.42) and 1.82 (95% CI 1.18–2.89), respectively. Conclusions: No prospective association was found between screen time and BP. However, a significant cross-sectional association was found between screen time before bedtime and high BP in preschool children.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jesper","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Neland, Mette","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-614791"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Grøntved, Anders"],"keyword":["Child Preschool","Cohort study","Cross Sectional Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hypertension","Hypertension epidemiology","Male","Mass Media statistics numerical data","Preschool","Prevalence","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Screen time","Surveys and Questionnaires","Time Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"screen based media use and blood pressure in preschool aged children a prospective study in the odense child cohort","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/168783218/Manuscript_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-614791","identifier":[{"id":"32267814","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85083088914","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-911b88ff-ba79-4176-b5c2-d4dcdfb65284"],"keyword":["Child, Preschool","Cross-Sectional Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Hypertension/epidemiology","Male","Mass Media/statistics & numerical data","Prevalence","Prospective Studies","Risk Factors","Surveys and Questionnaires","Time Factors","cohort study","hypertension","preschool","screen time"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6C96F76869F80DE8CCC52A9255606269"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/168783218/Manuscript_postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f321394d-8abe-49b2-ab02-1b528e734f63","name":"Pedersen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9475-0341","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8b86a1ef-e6c1-4de3-8300-e30d144bbf60","name":"Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","name_org":"Rasmussen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-2114-2185","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"nelandpau","last":"Neland","locid":"dad16075-d1c3-447d-a22c-202e48d08cf2","name":"Neland, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedpau","last":"Grøntved","locid":"393b1ca1-e658-437c-9ca3-73aea925ad58","name":"Grøntved, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1584-679X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32267814"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/1403494820914823","issn":["14034948","16511905"],"issn_org":["14034948"],"issue":"5","journal":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health","pages":"495-502","publisher":"SAGE Publications","status":"p","title":"Scandinavian Journal of Public Health","volume":"49"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083088914"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-911b88ff-ba79-4176-b5c2-d4dcdfb65284"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Screen-based Media Use and Blood Pressure in Preschool-aged Children : A Prospective Study in The Odense Child Cohort","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-614791","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Anders Rasmussen sætter fokus på feedback og datainformeret undervisning. Et praksis-eksempel fra SOSU-uddannelsen viser, hvordan underviseren med feedback kan lade sin undervisningspraksis datainformere.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-649701"],"filters":{"added":"2023-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Erhvervsuddannelse","Feedback i undervisningen","Klasseledelse","Læring pædagogik og undervisning","Skoler fag og institutioner","Transfer","Uddannelse professioner og erhverv"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-UCL"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spørg eleverne hvordan de oplever feedback i undervisningen","src":["ucl"],"src-code":["DI-UC-UCL"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://emu.dk/eud/paedagogik-og-didaktik/evaluering-og-feedback/spoerg-eleverne-hvordan-de-oplever-feedback-i","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-649701","ids":["ucl-e7f501a8-f116-4098-a08a-9ae2386f3cf4"],"keyword":["Erhvervsuddannelse","Feedback i undervisningen","Klasseledelse","Læring, pædagogik og undervisning","SOSU-uddannelsen","Skoler, fag og institutioner","Uddannelse, professioner og erhverv","pædagogiske data","transfer"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E0514D29B926D8C631E6AA7DD7AAAEEF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"rem","url":"https://emu.dk/eud/paedagogik-og-didaktik/evaluering-og-feedback/spoerg-eleverne-hvordan-de-oplever-feedback-i","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["UCL Erhvervsakademi og Professionshøjskole, Direktion, Kompetence- og Organisationsudvikling, Pædagogik og Læring"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"2a136974-b782-43e4-9ff2-f630c2ddb5a1","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"journal":"EMU : Danmarks undervisningsportal","publisher":"UNI-C","status":"p","title":"EMU : Danmarks undervisningsportal"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","UCL University College","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ucl-e7f501a8-f116-4098-a08a-9ae2386f3cf4"],"src":["UCL University College"],"title":"Spørg eleverne hvordan de oplever feedback i undervisningen","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-649701","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"A recurrent concern in nature conservation is the potential competition for forage plants between wild bees and managed honey bees. Specifically, that the highly sophisticated system of recruitment and large perennial colonies of honey bees quickly exhaust forage resources leading to the local extirpation of wild bees. However, different species of bees show different preferences for forage plants. We here summarize known forage plants for honey bees and wild bee species at national scale in Denmark. Our focus is on floral resources shared by honey bees and wild bees, with an emphasis on both threatened wild bee species and foraging specialist species. Across all 292 known bee species from Denmark, a total of 410 plant genera were recorded as forage plants. These included 294 plant genera visited by honey bees and 292 plant genera visited by different species of wild bees. Honey bees and wild bees share 176 plant genera in Denmark. Comparing the pairwise niche overlap for individual bee species, no significant relationship was found between their overlap and forage specialization or conservation status. Network analysis of the bee-plant interactions placed honey bees aside from most other bee species, specifically the module containing the honey bee had fewer links to any other modules, while the remaining modules were more highly inter-connected. Despite the lack of predictive relationship from the pairwise niche overlap, data for individual species could be summarized. Consequently, we have identified a set of operational parameters that, based on a high foraging overlap (>70%) and unfavorable conservation status (Vulnerable+Endangered+Critically Endangered), can guide both conservation actions and land management decisions in proximity to known or suspected populations of these species.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Claus","Dupont, Yoko Luise","Madsen, Henning Bang","Bogusch, Petr","Goulson, Dave","Herbertsson, Lina","Maia, Kate Pereira","Nielsen, Anders","Olesen, Jens M.","Potts, Simon G.","Roberts, Stuart P. M.","Sydenham, Markus Arne Kjær","Kryger, Per"],"cuid":["S02-081.06-015057"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, South","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Claus"],"country":["Brazil","Czechia","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University","Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","Norwegian Institute of Bioeconomy Research","Universidade Federal de Sao Paulo","Universidade de São Paulo","University of Hradec Kralove","University of Oslo","University of Reading","University of Sussex"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"evaluation competition for forage plants between honey bees and wild bees in denmark","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0250056","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-081.06-015057","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8081269","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"33909661","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85104917181","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-21da796e-e5b2-4812-a59d-64c1257d3798","ku-1359f4c5-ad63-43f3-ae3d-a1a20372a61d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-8E4D8F97718B670AC3606120D5E8C33A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/272515444/Evaluating_competition_for_forage_plants_between_honey_bees_and_wild_bees_in_Denmark.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0250056","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Agroecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"cz","key":"university of hradec kralove","loc":["Czechia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Hradec Kralove","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of sussex","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sussex","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"se","key":"lund university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Lund University","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"br","key":"universidade federal de sao paulo","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade Federal de Sao Paulo","used":1},{"affno":"7","country":"br","key":"universidade de são paulo","loc":["Brazil","America, South"],"name":"Universidade de São Paulo","used":1},{"affno":"8","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute of bioeconomy research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute of Bioeconomy Research","used":1},{"affno":"9","country":"no","key":"university of oslo","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Oslo","used":1},{"affno":"10","country":"gb","key":"university of reading","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Reading","used":1},{"affno":"11","country":"no","key":"norwegian institute for nature research","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Norwegian Institute for Nature Research","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"24ea7809-dde1-44f9-ac17-63b508b998f7","name":"Rasmussen, Claus","orcid":"0000-0003-1529-6548","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yoko Luise","key":"dupontpau","last":"Dupont","locid":"2a165175-a558-448c-9b2e-8fe1150a0fac","name":"Dupont, Yoko Luise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Henning Bang","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"5a019b54-29c1-4317-a128-a51e2f4a4121","name":"Madsen, Henning Bang","orcid":"0000-0003-2542-3109","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Petr","key":"boguschpau","last":"Bogusch","name":"Bogusch, Petr","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Dave","key":"goulsonpau","last":"Goulson","name":"Goulson, Dave","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lina","key":"herbertssonpau","last":"Herbertsson","name":"Herbertsson, Lina","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7","corresponding":null,"first":"Kate Pereira","key":"maiapau","last":"Maia","name":"Maia, Kate Pereira","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8 9","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Anders","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens M.","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"5beee907-781b-4998-8f99-97083ea86835","name":"Olesen, Jens M.","orcid":"0000-0003-1998-1083","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Simon G.","key":"pottspau","last":"Potts","name":"Potts, Simon G.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"10","corresponding":null,"first":"Stuart P. M.","key":"robertspau","last":"Roberts","name":"Roberts, Stuart P. M.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus Arne Kjær","key":"sydenhampau","last":"Sydenham","name":"Sydenham, Markus Arne Kjær","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"11","first":"Markus Arne","key":"kjærsydenhampau","last":"Kjær Sydenham","name":"Kjær Sydenham, Markus Arne","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Per","key":"krygerpau","last":"Kryger","locid":"608d6893-28dc-4991-83f4-a1884a46b9d6","name":"Kryger, Per","orcid":"0000-0001-5306-3230","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33909661"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0250056","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"4","journal":"PLOS ONE","paperid":"e0250056","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85104917181"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-21da796e-e5b2-4812-a59d-64c1257d3798","ku-1359f4c5-ad63-43f3-ae3d-a1a20372a61d"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Evaluation competition for forage plants between honey bees and wild bees in Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-081.06-015057","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Mink, on a farm with about 15,000 animals, became infected with SARS-CoV-2. Over 75% of tested animals were positive for SARS-CoV-2 RNA in throat swabs and 100% of tested animals were seropositive. The virus responsible had a deletion of nucleotides encoding residues H69 and V70 within the spike protein gene as well as the A22920T mutation, resulting in the Y453F substitution within this protein, seen previously in mink. The infected mink recovered and after free-testing of 300 mink (a level giving 93% confidence of detecting a 1% prevalence), the animals remained seropositive. During further follow-up studies, after a period of more than 2 months without any virus detection, over 75% of tested animals again scored positive for SARS-CoV-2 RNA. Whole genome sequencing showed that the viruses circulating during this re-infection were most closely related to those identified in the first outbreak on this farm but additional sequence changes had occurred. Animals had much higher levels of anti-SARS-CoV-2 antibodies in serum samples after the second round of infection than at free-testing or during recovery from initial infection, consistent with a boosted immune response. Thus, it was concluded that following recovery from an initial infection, seropositive mink were readily re-infected by SARS-CoV-2.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Fonager, Jannik","Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","Lassaunière, Ria","Hammer, Anne Sofie","Quaade, Michelle Lauge","Boklund, Anette","Lohse, Louise","Strandbygaard, Bertel","Rasmussen, Morten","Michaelsen, Thomas Yssing","Mortensen, Sten","Fomsgaard, Anders","Belsham, Graham J.","Bøtner, Anette"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-005476"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Belsham, Graham J."],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"OT":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"infection recovery and re infection of farmed mink with sars cov 000000000002","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010068","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-005476","identifier":[{"id":"85119930268","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8629378","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34780574","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-70f631cc-bc97-4fe9-8853-0a6cd62c457f","ku-b492d07f-b689-4660-8991-db5a09010c63"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-38AC86E1163FE335D2FE548097CF3447"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/286630835/journal.ppat.1010068.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/466933391/journal.ppat.1010068.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.ppat.1010068","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Veterinary and Animal Sciences, Pathobiological Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Functional Genomics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Danish Veterinary and Food Administration"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Bruun","key":"rasmussenthomasbruunpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik","key":"fonagerjannikpau","last":"Fonager","name":"Fonager, Jannik","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Charlotte Sværke","key":"jørgensencharlottesværkepau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Charlotte Sværke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ria","key":"lassaunièreriapau","last":"Lassaunière","name":"Lassaunière, Ria","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Sofie","key":"hammerannesofievedstedpau","last":"Hammer","locid":"d86de80d-40da-4128-b0d2-55a9f244b129","name":"Hammer, Anne Sofie Vedsted","name_org":"Hammer, Anne Sofie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Mi