{"abstract":"The case presented here illustrates that interdisciplinary teamwork can be essential for the understanding of the COVID-19 disease presentation and enlightening of the pathophysiology. A 60-year-old woman without any comorbidities, apart from overweight, was found dead in her apartment after 14 days of home isolation due to suspicion of COVID-19. A forensic autopsy was performed. This revealed severely condensed, almost airless, firm lungs, and the cause of death was severe acute respiratory distress syndrome-associated with COVID-19 (SARS-CoV-2). In addition, SARS-CoV-2 was detected with reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) in cerebrospinal fluid, lung tissue, and tracheal sample and specific antibodies for SARS-CoV-2 were detected in cerebrospinal fluid and serum. Subsequent sequencing of the SARS-CoV-2 virus showed variation in nucleotides at 3 sites between SARS-CoV-2 isolates recovered from the tracheal sample, cerebrospinal fluid, and tissues from both lungs, and phylogenetic analysis revealed that the spinal fluid sample differed the most from the other 3 samples. This case supports the hypothesis that SARS-CoV-2 may be neuroinvasive and cause central nervous system infection.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Høy Marbjerg, Lis","Jacobsen, Christina","Fonager, Jannik","Bøgelund, Claus","Rasmussen, Morten","Fomsgaard, Anders","Banner, Jytte","Vorobieva Solholm Jensen, Veronika"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-417513"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Division of Infectious Disease Preparedness"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"possible involvement of central nervous system in covid 000000000019 and sequence variability of sars cov 000000000002 revealed in autopsy tissue samples a case report","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2632010X211006096","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-417513","identifier":[{"id":"85103220553","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33855294","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8013633","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-2848f39e-7288-47ab-a50a-e2cee38a2859"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A3C7314F34956CB8A35FB5A50F5BED5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/274275851/2632010x211006096.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1177/2632010X211006096","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Division of Infectious Disease Preparedness"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Section of Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lis","key":"høymarbjergpau","last":"Høy Marbjerg","name":"Høy Marbjerg, Lis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christina","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"524f7da6-c932-4471-99c3-5864c66059df","name":"Jacobsen, Christina","orcid":"0000-0001-7257-0772","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1