, Anders","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Annette","key":"kampannettepedh","last":"Kamp","name":"Kamp, Annette","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birger Steen","key":"nielsenbirgersteenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Birger Steen","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Klaus T.","key":"nielsenklaustpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Klaus T.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788772164052"],"issue":"1","pages":"140-160","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Frydenlund Academic","series":"Menneskelig udvikling, profession og hverdagsliv i forandring","status":"p","subtitle":"Problemstillinger og tendenser","title":"Arbejdslivet i kritisk perspektiv"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-c8b50ea8-d438-41a7-a93f-85d333d67782"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Koncepter i arbejdslivet","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-569476","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background Advancements in screen media devices has transformed the way families engage with screen media. Although these modern devices offer many opportunities, e.g. communication and research online, an in-depth understanding of how these devices affect our health, is lacking. Before a definite randomized controlled trial, the SCREENS pilot study was conducted to assess compliance to and feasibility of two interventions, a measurement protocol, and a survey-based recruitment strategy. Also, the potential of the interventions to impact leisure time spent non-sedentary in children six-to-ten years of age was explored. Methods Families (N = 12) were recruited through a population-based survey sent out in October of 2018 to adults (N = 1,675) in the Municipality of Middelfart, Denmark. Families were randomized to one of two two-week interventions; an Evening Restriction intervention (no screen media use after six pm) and a General Restrict intervention (limit entertainment-based screen media to three hours/week/person). Intervention compliance was assessed objectively by measuring household TV usage, smartphone and tablet activity via an application, and via screen media diaries. During baseline and follow-up, as part of larger protocol, family members wore two triaxial accelerometers for seven consecutive days. The potential of the interventions to impact non-sedentary time was explored based on means and standard errors (SEs). Results Despite almost 85% and 75% reductions in leisure screen media use 0% and 50% of families were compliant in the Evening Restrict group and General Restrict group, respectively, based on strict a priori criteria. Participant feedback indicated that the General Restrict intervention generally was feasibly. Compliance to the accelerometry wear protocol was high (median non-wear was <1 hour/week). Moreover, the recruitment strategy was implemented and was feasible. The General restrict intervention might increase children’s non-sedentary time (mean (SE): 36.6 (23) min/day, N = 6). Conclusions The General Restriction intervention, the accelerometer wear protocol and recruitment strategy, appeared feasible. Trial registration NCT03788525 at https://clinicaltrials.gov [Retrospectively registered; 27th of December, 2018].","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Pedersen, Jesper","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Brønd, Jan Christian","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580249"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke"],"keyword":["Compliance","Feasibility","Physical activity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of two screen media reduction interventions results from the screens pilot trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0259657","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580249","identifier":[{"id":"85119280481","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34780511","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8592478","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-18835dc1-a57d-49bf-942a-65100cee9a05"],"keyword":["Compliance","Feasibility","Physical activity","Screen media"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-51992E21D744AF5E0C1BD5B31A50034A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0259657","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/195290329/journal.pone.0259657.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin G. B.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8b86a1ef-e6c1-4de3-8300-e30d144bbf60","name":"Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","name_org":"Rasmussen, Martin G. B.","orcid":"0000-0002-2114-2185","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"f321394d-8abe-49b2-ab02-1b528e734f63","name":"Pedersen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9475-0341","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Grønholt","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"e9ad7180-8cce-4e88-9707-18dedc4c73e0","name":"Olesen, Line Grønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-6588-8878","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"751d26de-66d4-4ef9-8183-880c48c96dc7","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-5666-9614","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan Christian","key":"brøndpau","last":"Brønd","locid":"da4ecea2-2b7f-4027-9859-416024dca432","name":"Brønd, Jan Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6718-3022","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedp