:"Jensen, Svend E","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Svend E.","key":"jensensvendepau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Svend E.","rank":24,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik S.","key":"hansenhenriksteenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"bedce5f9-b000-4dec-9b5e-c4a0a45180fb","name":"Hansen, Henrik Steen","name_org":"Hansen, Henrik S.","orcid":"0000-0001-6477-9832","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik S","key":"hansenhenrikspau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Henrik S","rank":25,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette O.","key":"jensenlisetteokkelspau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b78c452e-5a69-41fe-ba49-0096c84d1d4d","name":"Jensen, Lisette Okkels","name_org":"Jensen, Lisette O.","orcid":"0000-0002-4838-2429","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisette O","key":"jensenlisetteopau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Lisette O","rank":26,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33823606"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1161/circulationaha.120.052766","issn":["00097322","15244539"],"issn_org":["00097322"],"issue":"22","journal":"Circulation","pages":"2155-2165","publisher":"Lippincott Williams and Wilkins","status":"p","title":"Circulation","volume":"143"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85107046528"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cf269f51-6a1f-4627-ba16-542a39439f54","au-3cbbbb44-f187-4fe3-b04b-6b6eebfda013","sdu-e77d67fb-adf5-400f-bd9f-4accc6af6c99"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Randomized Clinical Comparison of the Dual-Therapy CD34 Antibody-Covered Sirolimus-Eluting Combo Stent With the Sirolimus-Eluting Orsiro Stent in Patients Treated With Percutaneous Coronary Intervention : The SORT OUT X Trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-098.78-009935","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: OptimalTTF-2 is a randomized, comparative, multi-center, investigator-initiated, interventional study aiming to test skull remodeling surgery in combination with Tumor Treating Fields therapy (TTFields) and best physicians choice medical oncological therapy for first recurrence in glioblastoma patients. OptimalTTF-2 is a phase 2 trial initiated in November 2020. Skull remodeling surgery consists of five burrholes, each 15 mm in diameter, directly over the tumor resection cavity. Preclinical research indicates that this procedure enhances the effect of Tumor Treating Fields considerably. We recently concluded a phase 1 safety/feasibility trial that indicated improved overall survival and no additional toxicity. This phase 2 trial aims to validate the efficacy of the proposed intervention. Methods: The trial is designed as a comparative, 1:1 randomized, minimax two-stage phase 2 with an expected 70 patients to a maximum sample size of 84 patients. After 12-months follow-up of the first 52 patients, an interim futility analysis will be performed. The two trial arms will consist of either a) TTFields therapy combined with best physicians choice oncological treatment (control arm) or b) skull remodeling surgery, TTFields therapy and best practice oncology (interventional arm). Major eligibility criteria include age ≥ 18 years, 1st recurrence of supratentorial glioblastoma, Karnofsky performance score ≥ 70, focal tumor, and lack of significant co-morbidity. Study design aims to detect a 20% increase in overall survival after 12 months (OS12), assuming OS12 = 40% in the control group and OS12 = 60% in the intervention group. Secondary endpoints include hazard rate ratio of overall survival and progression-free survival, objective tumor response rate, quality of life, KPS, steroid dose, and toxicity. Toxicity, objective tumor response rate, and QoL will be assessed every 3rd month. Endpoint data will be collected at the end of the trial, including the occurrence of suspected unexpected serious adverse reactions (SUSARs), unacceptable serious adverse events (SAEs), withdrawal of consent, or loss-to-follow-up. Discussion: New treatment modalities are highly needed for first recurrence glioblastoma. Our proposed treatment modality of skull remodeling surgery, Tumor Treating Fields, and best practice medical oncological therapy may increase overall survival significantly. Trial registration: ClinicalTrials.gov Identifier: NCT0422399, registered 13. January 2020.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Mikic, N.","Poulsen, F. R.","Kristoffersen, K. B.","Laursen, Rene Johannes","Guldberg, Trine Lignell","Skjøth-Rasmussen, J.","Wong, E. T.","Møller, S.","Dahlrot, R. H.","Sørensen, J. C.H.","Korshøj, A. R."],"cuid":["S03-100.00-006435"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Mikic, N.","Mikic, Nikola"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Beth Israel Deaconess Medical Center","Harvard Medical School","Harvard University"],"keyword":["Craniectomy","Craniectomy glioblastoma neuro oncology neurosurgery tumour treating fields","Glioblastoma","Neuro oncology","Neurosurgery","tumour treating fields"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study protocol for optimalttf 000000000002 enhancing tumor treating fields with skull remodeling surgery for first recurrence glioblastoma a phase 000000000002 multi center randomized prospective interventional trial","src":["aau","au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-021-08709-4","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We sincerely thank the neurosurgical and oncological department heads at Rigshospitalet, Aarhus-, Odense- and Aalborg University Hospital for their support of the trial. Furthermore, we would sincerely like to thank the following individuals: S?ren Ole Stigaard Cortnum, MD, for helping with managing the trial and recruitment of patients Marianne Esbjerg from the Good Clinical Practice Unit, Aarhus University for monitoring the trial with dedication. Rikke Beese Dalby, MD, PhD and Christian Rahbek, MD for participating and helping us organize the infrastructure of the central review Karen Risgaard and Hanne Lisby from the Danish Brain Tumor Association for their support and Hanne Lisby?s participation in the DMC as a layperson Jakob Hjort for creating the randomization module and troubleshooting the Redcap database OptimalTTF-2 is funded by Novocure, Aarhus University, Danish Cancer Society, and Independent Research Fund Denmark. The trial protocol was designed by sponsor-investigator Aarhus University Hospital and modified by the Trial Steering Committee."],"id":"S03-100.00-006435","identifier":[{"id":"PMC8427888","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85114688517","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34503460","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-84fbea90-cad6-4db9-aa82-3a92d70c7396","au-ef5f531d-a960-489d-8bfc-be7c0216f608","sdu-9d760712-3694-45d5-afb6-e877a748b2d0"],"keyword":["Craniectomy","Craniectomy | glioblastoma | neuro-oncology | neurosurgery | tumour treating fields |","glioblastoma","neuro-oncology","neurosurgery","tumour treating fields"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-610B714860BC83BCDEE6E53B4F7BDF9B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/449747917/Mikic_e