{"abstract":"Background: PD-L1 expression on tumor cells (TCs) or immune cells (ICs) may be used as a prognostic marker for survival in patients with NSCLC. We characterized PD-L1 expression on TCs or ICs in a patient cohort with NSCLC to determine associations between PD-L1 expression and overall survival (OS), according to EGFR and KRAS mutation status. Methods: Danish patients aged >18 years diagnosed with NSCLC before 2014 on first- (N = 491), second- (N = 368), or third-line (N = 498) therapy were included. Data were extracted from population-based medical registries. Tumor samples from pathology archives were tested for biomarkers. High PD-L1 expression was defined as expression on ≥25 % of TCs or ICs based on first diagnostic biopsy or surgical resection. KRAS and EGFR mutation status were tested using PCR-based assays. Cox regression analysis was used to compute adjusted HRs and associated 95 % CIs. Results: PD-L1 TC and IC ≥ 25 % were observed in 24.3 %–31.0 % and 11.7–14.7 % of patients, respectively. EGFR and KRAS mutations were detected in 4.7 %–8.8 % and 26.5 %–30.7 % of patients, respectively. PD-L1 TC ≥ 25 % was not associated with survival advantage in first- (HR = 0.96, 95 % CI: 0.75–1.22), second- (1.08, 0.81–1.42), or third-line (0.94, 0.74–1.20) therapy. PD-L1 IC ≥ 25 % was associated with survival advantage in second-line (HR = 0.56, 95 % CI: 0.36–0.86) and third-line (0.69, 0.49–0.97) but not first-line (1.00, 0.70–1.41) therapy. Conclusion: No association was observed between PD-L1 TC ≥ 25 % and OS in any therapy line. PD-L1 IC ≥ 25 % may confer survival benefit among some patients who reach second-line therapy.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Hedgeman, Elizabeth","Nørgaard, Mette","Dalvi, Tapashi","Pedersen, Lars","Hansen, Hanh Pham","Walker, Jill","Midha, Anita","Shire, Norah","Boothman, Anne Marie","Fryzek, Jon P.","Rigas, James","Mellemgaard, Anders","Rasmussen, Torben Riis","Hamilton-Dutoit, Stephen Jacques","Cronin-Fenton, Deirdre"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-143947"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Cronin-Fenton, Deirdre"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","AstraZeneca UK"],"keyword":["EGFR mutation","KRAS mutation","Non small cell lung cancer","PD L1 expression"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"programmed cell death ligand 000000000001 expression and survival in a cohort of patients with non small cell lung cancer receiving first line through third line therapy in denmark","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85109203022","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-143947","identifier":[{"id":"85109203022","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000677480900013","type":"wos"},{"id":"34217914","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-196e822b-13eb-4dc7-b7f2-6b6ebc5c20d6"],"keyword":["EGFR mutation","KRAS mutation","Non-small cell lung cancer","PD-L1 expression"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6824A2F5F34BA83B5E31DA5BEE3183A5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"astrazeneca uk","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"AstraZeneca UK","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Elizabeth","key":"hedgemanpau","last":"Hedgeman","name":"Hedgeman, Elizabeth","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"nørgaardpau","last":"Nørgaard","locid":"3cb2ae19-c1b9-4dad-9928-adbd1c51b4b7","name":"Nørgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0001-6110-5891","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Tapashi","key":"dalvipau","last":"Dalvi","name":"Dalvi, Tapashi","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"a0fdd247-3fb1-4c38-a1b2-f37d89f8f5c9","name":"Pedersen, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-9341-3888","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hanh Pham","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Hanh Pham","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jill","key":"walkerpau","last":"Walker","name":"Walker, Jill","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anita","key":"midhapau","last":"Midha","name":"Midha, Anita","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Norah","key":"shirepau","last":"Shire","name":"Shire, Norah","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno