f Human Genetics","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097275969"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Non-Profit Organisations","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7128cdb9-37cb-43d0-b59f-9cce90014ea3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Correction : Immunity and mental illness: findings from a Danish population-based immunogenetic study of seven psychiatric and neurodevelopmental disorder (European Journal of Human Genetics, (2019), 27, 9, (1445-1455), 10.1038/s41431-019-0402-9)","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-193956","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Fluid models used to study the edge plasma region need to be benchmarked against similar conditions given that models can strongly differ in complexity and therefore the results they produce. Via this validation study undertaken through the framework of EUROfusion Enabling Research, four state-of-the art models—GBS, Hermes/BOUT++, hot-edge-sol-electrostatic and TOKAM3X—are compared to experimental plasma turbulence measurements on the ISTTOK tokamak. Statistical comparisons of simulation and experiment data show that fluid models used here can replicate most of the experiment in terms of Isat and Vfloat fluctuations despite their differences. Furthermore, it is shown that without including more complex information (like core turbulence information and domain geometry details and magnetic topological aspects) in fluid models, the results recovered vary from their experimental counterparts. Via the simulations using these codes, it is demonstrated that fluid models continue to be a good cost-effective tool in recovering many global aspects of edge plasma behaviour.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Dudson, B. D.","Gracias, W. A.","Jorge, R.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Olsen, Jeppe Miki Busk","Ricci, P.","Silva, C.","Tamain, P.","Ciraolo, G.","Fedorczak, N.","Galassi, D.","Madsen, Jens","Militello, F.","Nace, N.","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Riva, F.","Serre, E."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-330228"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Dudson, B. D."],"country":["France","Portugal","Spain","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","CNRS","Commissariat à l’énergie atomique et aux énergies alternatives","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","United Kingdom Atomic Energy Authority","Universidad Carlos III de Madrid","University of Lisbon","University of York"],"keyword":["Simulation","Tokamak","Validation"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"edge turbulence in isttok a multi code fluid validation","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277418246/ISTTOK_validation_submitted.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"funding_acknowledgement":["This work has been carried out within the framework of the EUROfusion Consortium and has received funding from the Euratom research and training programme 2014?2018 and 2019?2020 under Grant Agreement No. 633053. The views and opinions expressed herein do not necessarily reflect those of the European Commission. The simulations presented herein were carried out in part using Archer computing resources under Plasma HEC consortium grants EP/L000237/1 and EP/R029148/1."],"id":"S01-000.00-330228","identifier":[{"id":"85105036772","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-565e1483-f0c9-4780-b350-2e1c98df5d9b"],"keyword":["Simulation","Tokamak","Validation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-94C323D2C05037412912CA3F57E73F83"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/277418246/ISTTOK_validation_submitted.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"gb","key":"university of york","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of York","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"es","key":"universidad carlos iii de madrid","loc":["Spain","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Universidad Carlos III de Madrid","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],