 university aquatic biology and chemistry","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Kristianstad University, Aquatic Biology and Chemistry","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Arne Redsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"242dafc1-ebc5-4ad0-bcd9-e8b2aea28bde","name":"Redsted Rasmussen, Arne","name_org":"Rasmussen, Arne Redsted","orcid":"0000-0001-5454-4423","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","locid":"f0f495a2-fe48-4cdf-8f27-ea207182bda8","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9984-7014","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Farnis","key":"bonekapau","last":"Boneka","name":"Boneka, Farnis","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 5","first":"Morten E.","key":"allentoftpau","last":"Allentoft","locid":"ff98a169-a9d1-4497-8694-c2e6e9e0ab5b","name":"Allentoft, Morten E.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6 7 8","first":"Kate Laura","key":"sanderspau","last":"Sanders","name":"Sanders, Kate Laura","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"9 10","first":"Johan","key":"elmbergpau","last":"Elmberg","name":"Elmberg, Johan","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.26757/pjsb2020b14013","issn":["19086865","25080342"],"issn_org":["25080342"],"issue":"2","journal":"Philippine Journal of Systematic Biology","pages":"1-16","publisher":"Association of Systematic Biologists of the Philippines","status":"p","title":"Philippine Journal of Systematic Biology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85123555320"],"search":{"DAF":["All Artistic Higher Education Institutions","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","Artistic Higher Education Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-ART","DI-ART-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["arkc-7ae2464c-2826-497e-9668-0374054e224a","ku-a968b87c-314a-4532-8bb6-0156b597ad21"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","Royal Danish Academy - Architecture, Design, Conservation"],"title":"Viviparous sea snakes can be used as bioindicators for diverse marine environments","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.49-012421","year":2021,"yearsub":2021}
{"abstract":"Background: Pulmonary rehabilitation (PR) is a cornerstone in COPD care, however, maintaining high adherence rates can be challenging. In the Sing-a-Lung multicentre randomised controlled trial, we demonstrated that singing training was as efficacious as physical training in improving 6-Minutes Walk Test (6MWT) and superior concerning quality of life1. There is no knowledge about the impact of adherence on change in 6MWT and St George’s Respiratory Questionnaire (SGRQ), and factors related to high adherence to singing training vs. physical training. Methods: Post hoc analyses of the Sing-a-Lung trial (of the effects of singing training compared to physical training in a 10 weeks’ PR program for COPD patients). Multivariable logistic regression analysing 1) the relationship between adherence (low: 0-49% attendance; medium: 50-74%; high: 75-100%) and achieving a significant improvement of 6MWT (30 meters) and SGRQ total score (4 points) from baseline to post-PR, and 2) factors related to high adherence. The regression models included baseline characteristics, COPD severity, and expectations towards singing. Results: 270 patient were included in Sing-a-Lung. Number of patients with high adherence was similar in the two study arms (physical training 71 [56.8%], singing training 88 [60.7%], p=0.90). Patients with medium and high adherence had significantly higher odds for improving 6MWT (OR 5.6 [95%CI 1.4-22.4], p=0.02; and OR 10.5 [3.0-36.6], p<0.001, respectively) and SGRQ (OR 8.3 [2.1-32.7], p=0.003; and OR 17.0 [4.9-58.3], p<0.001, respectively) with low adherence as reference. There was no significant factors related adherence. Conclusions: There was a similar dose-response relationship between adherence and improvement of 6MWT and SGRQ, and adherence were similar for singing training and physical training. 1. Kaasgaard M, et al. Sing-a-Lung: Group singing as training modality in pulmonary rehabilitation for patients with Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD): A multicenter, cluster-randomised, non-inferiority controlled trial. Abstract 4663, ERS International Virtual Congress 2020, 7-9 Sept.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kaasgaard, Mette","Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","Hjerrild Andreasson, Karen","Løkke, Anders","Vuust, Peter","Hilberg, Ole","Bodtger, Uffe"],"cuid":["S02-089.09-013777"],"event":{"end":"2021-09-08","start":"2021-09-05","title":"European Respiratory Society International Congress 2021 - Virtual","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adherence to singing training vs physical training in copd rehabilitation post hoc analyses from the sing a lung trial","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/13993003.congress-2021.PA320","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.09-013777","ids":["au-1056bcfa-84f6-4fea-b072-222ae82eda59","sdu-7bcd879c-e76a-4c27-b064-7cdc130c68ea"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-F1B5D7187F2A74812DA8B7F752245EFA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1183/13993003.congress-2021.PA320","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center for Music In the Brain"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark (SDU)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital (AUH)"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Lillebælt Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"kaasgaardpau","last":"Kaasgaard","locid":"fc5784b6-66d8-4b92-8c4a-74bf4628c9c3","name":"Kaasgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-3833-2943","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Bech","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"18525822-35fd-4cd8-afdd-a608be44cc84","name":"Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","orcid":"0000-0003-1213-9483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"hjerrildandreassonpau","last":"Hjerrild Andreasson","locid":"8af88feb-2896-4499-89bd-750df2e82461","name":"Andreasson, Karen Hjerrild","name_org":"Hjerrild Andreasson, Karen","orcid":"0000-0002-8752-9614","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3 1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"løkkepau","last":"Løkke","name":"Løkke, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vuustpau","last":"Vuust","locid":"2c697ab6-9b06-4a16-a687-c8cdbd56f661","name":"Vuust, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hilbergpau","last":"Hilberg","name":"Hilberg, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-3463","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe","key":"bodtgerpau","last":"Bodtger","locid":"2f4e70da-63bb-4b8d-af09-2a959d6df5e8","name":"Bodtger, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-1231-9209","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1183/13993003.congress-2021.pa320","issn":["09031936","13993003"],"issn_org":["09031936"],"journal":"European Respiratory Journal","paperid":"PA320","publisher":"European Respiratory Society","status":"p","title":"European Respiratory Journal","volume":"2021"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-1056bcfa-84f6-4fea-b072-222ae82eda59","sdu-7bcd879c-e76a-4c27-b064-7cdc130c68ea"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Adherence to singing training vs. physical training in COPD rehabilitation : Post hoc analyses from the Sing-a-Lung trial","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.09-013777","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Reports have suggested an increased risk of aortic and mitral regurgitation associated with oral fluoroquinolones (FQs) resulting in a safety warning published by the European Medicines Agency (EMA). However, these findings have not yet been replicated. METHODS AND RESULTS: Using Danish administrative registers, we conducted a nested case-control study in a nationwide cohort of individuals between 2005 and 2018. Cases were defined as the first occurrence of aortic or mitral regurgitation. Exposure of interest was the use of oral FQs. Hazard ratios (HRs) with 95% confidence intervals (95% CI) were obtained by fitting time-dependent Cox regression models, with penicillin V as comparator, to assess the association between FQ use and incident valvular regurgitation. We identified 38 370 cases of valvular regurgitation with 1 115 100 matched controls. FQ exposure was not significantly associated with increased rates of aortic or mitral regurgitation (HR 1.02, 95% CI 0.95-1.09) compared with penicillin V users. Investigating the cumulative defined daily doses (cDDD) of FQs yielded similar results with no significant association between increasing FQ use and valvular regurgitation (e.g. HR 1.08, 95% CI 0.95-1.23 for cDDD >10 compared with cDDD 1-5). These results were consistent across several analyses including a cohort of patients with hypertension and using a case definition based on valvular surgical interventions. CONCLUSIONS: In a nationwide nested case-control study, FQs were not significantly associated with increased rates of valvular regurgitation. Our findings do not support a possible causal connection between FQ exposure and incident valvular regurgitation.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Strange, Jarl Emanuel","Holt, Anders","Blanche, Paul","Gislason, Gunnar","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Christensen, Daniel Mølager","Hansen, Morten Lock","Lamberts, Morten","Schou, Morten","Olesen, Jonas Bjerring","Fosbøl, Emil Loldrup","Køber, Lars","Rasmussen, Peter Vibe"],"cuid":["S02-097.82-007289"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Strange, Jarl Emanuel"],"keyword":["Antibiotics","Aortic regurgitation","Bias","Ciprofloxacin","Danish","Fluoroquinolones","Mitral regurgitation","Valvular heart disease"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR"],"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-HJER"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-NP-HJER","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oral fluoroquinolones and risk of aortic or mitral regurgitation a nationwide nested case control study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-097.82-007289","identifier":[{"id":"34245252","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85113794128","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000687750800008","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-968d80b4-f9d4-4cb8-a5b2-0211f92969eb","ku-1b6e1c55-c001-4ce3-92b1-2192bfe3a581"],"keyword":["Antibiotics","Aortic regurgitation","BIAS","CIPROFLOXACIN","DANISH","Fluoroquinolones","Mitral regurgitation","Valvular heart disease"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-5B84EE272D20D46485AF334174E5BB34"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"