ey":"køberpau","last":"Køber","name":"Køber, Lars","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter Vibe","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca186b96-3318-42e7-8fe1-34aa087a51b0","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Vibe","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34245252"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/eurheartj/ehab374","issn":["0195668X","15229645"],"issn_org":["0195668X"],"issue":"30","journal":"European Heart Journal","pages":"2899-2908","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"European Heart Journal","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85113794128"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Non-Profit Organisations","North Denmark Region","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-968d80b4-f9d4-4cb8-a5b2-0211f92969eb","ku-1b6e1c55-c001-4ce3-92b1-2192bfe3a581"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Oral fluoroquinolones and risk of aortic or mitral regurgitation : a nationwide nested case-control study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.82-007289","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"The Goldilocks Work Principle expresses that productive work should be redesigned to comprise physical behaviors of different intensities in a composition promoting workers’ health and fitness. This study is the first to assess the feasibility of redesigning work in an industrial setting according to the Goldilocks Work Principle. We recruited workers (n = 20) from a brewery in Den-mark, and we conducted a participatory 16‐week intervention including a workshop and two con-sultations. The workshop aimed to support the workers in modifying their work, while the consul-tations assisted the eventual implementation. Feasibility was evaluated as per three aspects: (1) developing modifications of work, (2) implementing these modifications, and (3) changing physical behavior and self‐reported fatigue, pain and energy. The three aspects were addressed through rec-ords completed by the workers, measurements of workers’ physical behavior and intensity during ‘control’ workdays (i.e., usual work) and ‘intervention’ workdays (i.e., modified work), and self-reported fatigue, pain and energy level following both types of workday. Five modifications to work were developed, and three of these five modifications were implemented. To some extent, physical behavior and intensity changed as intended during ‘intervention’ workdays compared to ‘control’ workdays. Workers were also less fatigued, had less pain, and had more energy after ‘intervention’ workdays. These results suggest that it is feasible to develop and implement modified work based on the Goldilocks Work Principle among industrial workers. However, we also identified several barriers to the implementation of such modifications.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Lerche, Anders Fritz","Mathiassen, Svend Erik","Rasmussen, Charlotte Lund","Straker, Leon","Søgaard, Karen","Holtermann, Andreas"],"cuid":["S02-099.46-769577"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Lerche, Anders Fritz"],"country":["Australia","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Centre for Musculoskeletal Research, Department of Occupational and Public Health Sciences, University of Gävle, Gävle, Sweden.","Curtin University","School of Allied Health, Curtin University, Perth, Australia.","University of Gävle"],"keyword":["Goldilocks Work Principle","Health","Intervention","Interventioner","Muskelskeletbesvær","Physical behavior","Sundhedsmiljø","Workplace"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"development and implementation of just right physical behavior in industrial work based on the goldilocks work principle a feasibility study","src":["nfa","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/ijerph18094707","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research was funded by the Danish Working Environment Research Fund (grant no. 18‐ 2018‐03)."],"id":"S02-099.46-769577","identifier":[{"id":"85104774856","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33925078","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8125316","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["nfa-c097310c-2d4f-4f5a-b1d0-a0839e696b33","sdu-b9eea129-e275-4e2f-812a-73ca0d30404c"],"keyword":["Goldilocks Work Principle","Health","Intervention","Interventioner","Muskelskeletbesvær","Physical behavior","Sundhedsmiljø","Workplace"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7EA6DB6C6443E8FBFBD671F2C0CA8BFD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/