{"abstract":"Har du et ravsmykke – eller et stykke rav, fundet mellem opskyl af tang og drivgods på stranden? Tag botanikerluppen og hold ravet op mod lyset: der er store chancer for, at det indeholder stjernehår fra egetræer, der groede i en tid med et globalt klima, der var langt varmere end det ”kølehus” vi lever i nu.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Finn N.","Johansen, Bo","Damgård, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-433753"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"pop","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"botanik i smykkeskrinet en hilsen fra en varm tid","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-433753","ids":["ku-4382bef7-1503-47db-ab81-99441cedcb80"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-93295734FD64C9F6FAA0C286870C14B3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Finn N.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"62367347-ff97-4b8c-b393-36d697edf389","name":"Rasmussen, Finn N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bo","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","name":"Johansen, Bo","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"damgårdpau","last":"Damgård","name":"Damgård, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["01053795"],"issue":"2","journal":"URT","pages":"12-17","status":"p","title":"URT","volume":"2021"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4382bef7-1503-47db-ab81-99441cedcb80"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Botanik i smykkeskrinet : en hilsen fra en varm tid","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-433753","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Context: Illicit use of anabolic androgenic steroids (AAS) is frequently observed in men and is associated with subsequent testosterone deficiency although the long-term effect on gonadal function is still unclear. Serum insulin-like factor 3 (INSL3) has been suggested to be a superior biomarker of Leydig cell secretory capacity compared to testosterone. Objective: This study aimed to investigate serum INSL3 concentrations in AAS users. Methods: This community-based, cross-sectional study included men aged 18 to 50 years, involved in recreational strength training and allocated to 1 of 3 groups: never-AAS users as controls (n = 44), current (n = 46), or former AAS users (n = 42) with an average duration since AAS cessation of 32 (23; 45) months. Results: Serum INSL3 was lower in current AAS users and former AAS users than in controls, median (interquartile range), 0.04 μg/L (nondetectable [ND]-0.07 μg/L) and 0.39 μg/L (0.24-0.62 μg/L) vs 0.59 μg/L (0.45-0.72 μg/L), P less than. 001. Former AAS users exhibited lower serum INSL3 levels than controls in a multivariable linear regression even after adjusting for serum total testosterone (TT) and other relevant confounders, (B) (95% CI), -0.16 μg/L (95% CI, -0.29 to -0.04 μg/L), P equal to. 011. INSL3 and TT were not associated in the model, P equal to. 821. Longer accumulated AAS duration (log2) was associated with lower serum INSL3 in former AAS users, (B) (95% CI), -0.08 (95% CI, -0.14 to -0.01), P equal to. 022. Serum INSL3, but not inhibin B or testosterone, was associated with testicular size in a multivariate linear regression, (B) (95% CI); 4.7 (95% CI, 0.5 to 8.9), P equal to. 030. Conclusion: Serum INSL3 is reduced years following AAS cessation in men, independently of testosterone, suggesting persistently impaired Leydig cell capacity.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jon Jarløv","Albrethsen, Jakob","Frandsen, Mikkel Nicklas","Jørgensen, Niels","Juul, Anders","Kistorp, Caroline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434007"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Anabolic androgenic steroids","Androgens","Male infertility","Testosterone","insulin like factor 3","male hypogonadism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"serum insulin like factor 000000000003 levels are reduced in former androgen users suggesting impaired leydig cell capacity","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-434007","identifier":[{"id":"33693710","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85108386765","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-43efa04b-a22a-474c-93dd-dadfd1ee54d4"],"keyword":["anabolic androgenic steroids","androgens","insulin-like factor 3","male hypogonadism","male infertility","testosterone"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D16916BC86D050B0990AB67701A2B5FF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jon Jarløv","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jon Jarløv","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jakob","key":"albrethsenpau","last":"Albrethsen","name":"Albrethsen, Jakob","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel Nicklas","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"2bfee443-cbdd-4b29-9f24-b8c380217c45","name":"Frandsen, Mikkel Nicklas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Niels","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Niels","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Caroline","key":"kistorppau","last":"Kistorp","locid":"42328645-d772-4f53-9f70-438ff40291b9","name":"Kistorp, Caroline","orcid":"0000-0002-3019-6775","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33693710"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/clinem/dgab129","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","volume":"106"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108386765"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-43efa04b-a22a-474c-93dd-dadfd1ee54d4"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Serum Insulin-like Factor 3 Levels Are Reduced in Former Androgen Users, Suggesting Impaired Leydig Cell Capacity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-434007","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Radiotherapy planning based only on positron emission tomography/magnetic resonance imaging (PET/MRI) lacks computed tomography (CT) information required for dose calculations. In this study, a previously developed deep learning model for creating synthetic CT (sCT) from MRI in patients with head and neck cancer was evaluated in 2 scenarios: (1) using an independent external dataset, and (2) using a local dataset after an update of the model related to scanner software-induced changes to the input MRI. Methods and Materials: Six patients from an external site and 17 patients from a local cohort were analyzed separately. Each patient underwent a CT and a PET/MRI with a Dixon MRI sequence over either one (external) or 2 (local) bed positions. For the external cohort, a previously developed deep learning model for deriving sCT from Dixon MRI was directly applied. For the local cohort, we adapted the model for an upgraded MRI acquisition using transfer learning and evaluated it in a leave-one-out process. The sCT mean absolute error for each patient was assessed. Radiotherapy dose plans based on sCT and CT were compared by assessing relevant absorbed dose differences in target volumes and organs at risk. Results: The MAEs were 78 ± 13 HU and 76 ± 12 HU for the external and local cohort, respectively. For the external cohort, absorbed dose differences in target volumes were within ± 2.3% and within ± 1% in 95% of the cases. Differences in organs at risk were <2%. Similar results were obtained for the local cohort. Conclusions: We have demonstrated a robust performance of a deep learning model for deriving sCT from MRI when applied to an independent external dataset. We updated the model to accommodate a larger axial field of view and software-induced changes to the input MRI. In both scenarios dose calculations based on sCT were similar to those of CT suggesting a robust and reliable method.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Olin, Anders B.","Thomas, Christopher","Hansen, Adam Espe","Rasmussen, Jacob H.","Krokos, Georgios","Urbano, Teresa Guerrero","Michaelidou, Andriana","Jakoby, Björn","Ladefoged, Claes N.","Berthelsen, Anne K.","Håkansson, Katrin","Vogelius, Ivan R.","Specht, Lena","Barrington, Sally F.","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Fischer, Barbara Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-435752"],"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","King's Health Partners","Siemens","St. Thomas' Hospital","University of Surrey"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"robustness and generalizability of deep learning synthetic computed tomography for positron emission tomography magnetic resonance imaging based radiation therapy planning of patients with head and neck cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.adro.2021.100762","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-435752","identifier":[{"id":"85122681519","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8452789","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"34585026","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-46e00f35-8951-453a-a1e6-3ed24e1acfe6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-24E82F2E3363997638B20127B27A8522"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/302072647/1_s2.0_S2452109421001202.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.adro.2021.100762","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"st thomas hospital","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"St. Thomas' Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Radiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"king s health partners","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"King's Health Partners","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"de","key":"siemens","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Siemens","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"gb","key":"university of surrey","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Surrey","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders B.","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","name":"Olin, Anders B.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christopher","key":"thomaspau","last":"Thomas","name":"Thomas, Christopher","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Adam E.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E.","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacob H.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jacob H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Georgios","key":"krokospau","last":"Krokos","name":"Krokos, Georgios","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Teresa Guerrero","key":"urbanopau","last":"Urbano","name":"Urbano, Teresa Guerrero","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Andriana","key":"michaelidoupau","last":"Michaelidou","name":"Michaelidou, Andriana","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5 6","first":"Björn","key":"jakobypau","last":"Jakoby","name":"Jakoby, Björn","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claes N.","key":"ladefogedpau","last":"Ladefoged","name":"Ladefoged, Claes N.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anne K.","key":"berthelsenpau","last":"Berthelsen","name":"Berthelsen, Anne K.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Katrin","key":"håkanssonpau","last":"Håkansson","name":"Håkansson, Katrin","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Ivan R.","key":"vogeliuspau","last":"Vogelius","locid":"66f4607a-ae94-4767-aaf0-79279bb24c31","name":"Vogelius, Ivan R.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Sally F.","key":"barringtonpau","last":"Barrington","name":"Barrington, Sally F.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Flemming L.","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","name_org":"Andersen, Flemming L.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Barbara M.","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a87f805a-ba44-45e2-b257-59a6f2976711","name":"Fischer, Barbara Malene","name_org":"Fischer, Barbara M.","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["34585026"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.adro.2021.100762","issn":["24521094"],"issue":"6","journal":"Advances in Radiation Oncology","paperid":"100762","status":"p","title":"Advances in Radiation Oncology","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85122681519"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-46e00f35-8951-453a-a1e6-3ed24e1acfe6"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Robustness and Generalizability of Deep Learning Synthetic Computed Tomography for Positron Emission Tomography/Magnetic Resonance Imaging–Based Radiation Therapy Planning of Patients With Head and Neck Cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-435752","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Let A be a convex body in the plane and A1,..., An be translates of A. Such translates give rise to an intersection graph of A, G = (V, E), with vertices V = {1,..., n} and edges E = {uv | Au ∩Av ≠ ∅}. The subgraph G′ = (V, E′) satisfying that E′ ⊂ E is the set of edges uv for which the interiors of Au and Av are disjoint is a unit distance graph of A. If furthermore G′ = G, i.e., if the interiors of Au and Av are disjoint whenever u ≠ v, then G is a contact graph of A. In this paper, we study which pairs of convex bodies have the same contact, unit distance, or intersection graphs. We say that two convex bodies A and B are equivalent if there exists a linear transformation B′ of B such that for any slope, the longest line segments with that slope contained in A and B′, respectively, are equally long. For a broad class of convex bodies, including all strictly convex bodies and linear transformations of regular polygons, we show that the contact graphs of A and B are the same if and only if A and B are equivalent. We prove the same statement for unit distance and intersection graphs.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aamand, Anders","Abrahamsen, Mikkel","Houen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-448110"],"event":{"acronym":"SCG","end":"2021-06-11","place":"Virtual, Buffalo, us","start":"2021-06-07","title":"37th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Convex body"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"classifying convex bodies by their contact and intersection graphs","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-448110","identifier":[{"id":"85108217218","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-5b5be2e8-518c-48f3-95b8-8f4c6356b3d2"],"keyword":["Contact graph","Convex body","Intersection graph"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-0D1A585FAE7754B3FCFAAB1B8C63F834"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.4230/LIPIcs.SoCG.2021.3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/273638048/Classifying_Convex_Bodies_by_Their_Contact_and_Intersection_Graphs.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","locid":"9a5990a0-c966-4fe5-97d0-a65ea981a0a7","name":"Aamand, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"abrahamsenpau","last":"Abrahamsen","locid":"63596832-461f-409a-a2cc-81023b9b8e46","name":"Abrahamsen, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0003-2734-4690","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"6c81a8c1-02dc-431a-b0b5-cbd75ba533ee","name":"Houen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","name_org":"Knudsen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Michael Reichstein","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca3d1668-64f4-4f81-92ed-9d7e18be5f43","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","orcid":"0000-0001-9219-8410","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Kevin","key":"buchinpedh","last":"Buchin","name":"Buchin, Kevin","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Eric Colin","key":"deverdierepedh","last":"de Verdiere","name":"de Verdiere, Eric Colin","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.4230/lipics.socg.2021.3","eisbn":["9783959771849"],"issn":["18688969"],"publisher":"Schloss Dagstuhl- Leibniz-Zentrum fur Informatik GmbH, Dagstuhl Publishing","series":"Leibniz International Proceedings in Informatics, LIPIcs","status":"p","title":"37th International Symposium on Computational Geometry, SoCG 2021"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85108217218"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5b5be2e8-518c-48f3-95b8-8f4c6356b3d2"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Classifying convex bodies by their contact and intersection graphs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-448110","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Salmonids are important sources of protein for a large proportion of the human population. Mycoplasma species are a major constituent of the gut microbiota of salmonids, often representing the majority of microbiota. Despite the frequent reported dominance of salmonid-related Mycoplasma species, little is known about the phylogenomic placement, functions and potential evolutionary relationships with their salmonid hosts. In this study, we utilise 2.9 billion metagenomic reads generated from 12 samples from three different salmonid host species to I) characterise and curate the first metagenome-assembled genomes (MAGs) of Mycoplasma dominating the intestines of three different salmonid species, II) establish the phylogeny of these salmonid candidate Mycoplasma species, III) perform a comprehensive pangenomic analysis of Mycoplasma, IV) decipher the putative functionalities of the salmonid MAGs and reveal specific functions expected to benefit the host. Our data provide a basis for future studies examining the composition and function of the salmonid microbiota.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jacob Agerbo","Villumsen, Kasper Rømer","Duchêne, David A.","Puetz, Lara","Delmont, Tom O.","Sveier, Harald","Jørgensen, Louise von Gersdorff","Præbel, Kim","Martin, Michael D.","Bojesen, Anders Miki","Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","Kristiansen, Karsten","Limborg, Morten T."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-486570"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["China","France","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI","Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique (CNRS)","Lerøy Seafood Group","Norwegian University of Science and Technology","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genome resolved metagenomics suggests a mutualistic relationship between i mycoplasma i and salmonid hosts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-021-02105-1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-486570","identifier":[{"id":"33990699","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85105843507","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8121932","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9bc74391-8154-47fd-a209-4d3db7522657"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-83BE36FDBF134C9FF2AB59945E49DD4B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/263001267/Genome_resolved_metagenomics_suggests_a_mutualistic_relationship_between_Mycoplasma_and_salmonid_hosts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s42003-021-02105-1","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Globe Institute, Section for Hologenomics","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Genome Research and Molecular Bio Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"fr","key":"centre national de la recherche scientifique","loc":["France","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Centre National de la Recherche Scientifique (CNRS)","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"no","key":"lerøy seafood group","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU"