U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-aa4f08a6-e19a-4abd-bba9-ab22fdc60543","au-df7597b6-1061-47b2-9e44-472fe0d91b7c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Severe or critical hypotension during post cardiac arrest care is associated with factors available on admission - a post hoc analysis of the TTH48 trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-008213","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Background: The more infectious SARS-CoV-2 lineage B.1.1.7 rapidly spread in Europe after December, 2020, and a concern that B.1.1.7 could cause more severe disease has been raised. Taking advantage of Denmark's high RT-PCR testing and whole genome sequencing capacities, we used national health register data to assess the risk of COVID-19 hospitalisation in individuals infected with B.1.1.7 compared with those with other SARS-CoV-2 lineages. Methods: We did an observational cohort study of all SARS-CoV-2-positive cases confirmed by RT-PCR in Denmark, sampled between Jan 1 and March 24, 2021, with 14 days of follow-up for COVID-19 hospitalisation. Cases were identified in the national COVID-19 surveillance system database, which includes data from the Danish Microbiology Database (RT-PCR test results), the Danish COVID-19 Genome Consortium, the National Patient Registry, the Civil Registration System, as well as other nationwide registers. Among all cases, COVID-19 hospitalisation was defined as first admission lasting longer than 12 h within 14 days of a sample with a positive RT-PCR result. The study population and main analysis were restricted to the proportion of cases with viral genome data. We calculated the risk ratio (RR) of admission according to infection with B.1.1.7 versus other co-existing lineages with a Poisson regression model with robust SEs, adjusted a priori for sex, age, calendar time, region, and comorbidities. The contribution of each covariate to confounding of the crude RR was evaluated afterwards by a stepwise forward inclusion. Findings: Between Jan 1 and March 24, 2021, 50 958 individuals with a positive SARS-CoV-2 test and at least 14 days of follow-up for hospitalisation were identified; 30 572 (60·0%) had genome data, of whom 10 544 (34·5%) were infected with B.1.1.7. 1944 (6·4%) individuals had a COVID-19 hospitalisation and of these, 571 (29·4%) had a B.1.1.7 infection and 1373 (70·6%) had an infection with other SARS-CoV-2 lineages. Although the overall number of hospitalisations decreased during the study period, the proportion of individuals infected with B.1.1.7 increased from 3·5% to 92·1% per week. B.1.1.7 was associated with a crude RR of hospital admission of 0·79 (95% CI 0·72–0·87; p<0·0001) and an adjusted RR of 1·42 (95% CI 1·25–1·60; p<0·0001). The adjusted RR was increased in all strata of age and calendar period—the two covariates with the largest contribution to confounding of the crude RR. Interpretation: Infection with SARS-CoV-2 lineage B.1.1.7 was associated with an increased risk of hospitalisation compared with that of other lineages in an analysis adjusted for covariates. The overall effect on hospitalisations in Denmark was lessened due to a strict lockdown, but our findings could support hospital preparedness and modelling of the projected impact of the epidemic in countries with uncontrolled spread of B.1.1.7. Funding: None.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Bager, Peter","Wohlfahrt, Jan","Fonager, Jannik","Rasmussen, Morten","Albertsen, Mads","Michaelsen, Thomas Yssing","Møller, Camilla Holten","Ethelberg, Steen","Legarth, Rebecca","Button, Mia Sarah Fischer","Gubbels, Sophie","Voldstedlund, Marianne","Mølbak, Kåre","Skov, Robert Leo","Fomsgaard, Anders","Krause, Tyra Grove","Østergaard, Stine Karstenskov"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-010138"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","The Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Bager, Peter"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk of hospitalisation associated with infection with sars cov 000000000002 lineage b 000000000001 000000000001 000000000007 in denmark an observational cohort study","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1473-3099(21)00290-5","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We received no specific funding for this work. The study was done by the governmental institution Staten Serum Institut as a health authority task."],"id":"S02-100.00-010138","identifier":[{"id":"34171231","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85117642711","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC8219488","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["aau-d3f9696c-bc37-47c1-b72e-9c7b8b76d81e","ku-198e4c8c-832d-40c7-868b-9df3f9c27233"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AD31E29FED14820EF812804CD49E5E9A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/S1473-3099(21)00290-5","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/about/copyright/","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC8219488/pdf/main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Center for Microbial Communities","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Functional Genomics","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Chemistry and Bioscience, Section of Biotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Global Health Section"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"danish covid 19 genome consortium","name":"Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","role":"oau"},{"affno":5,"key":"the danish covid 19 genome consortium","name":"The Danish Covid-19 Genome Consortium","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"bagerpau","last":"Bager","name":"Bager, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"wohlfahrtpau","last":"Wohlfahrt","name":"Wohlfahrt, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jannik","key":"fonagerpau","last":"Fonager","name":"Fonager, Jannik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads","key":"albertsenpau","last":"Albertsen","locid":"6c728ec9-5a0d-40c7-b3f3-1741c6e01ccc","name":"Albertsen, Mads","orcid":"0000-0002-6151-190X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Yssing","key":"michaelsenpau","last":"Michaelsen","locid":"1ff007ee-2593-4078-b832-372e163c6d6b","name":"Michaelsen, Thomas Yssing","orcid":"0000-0001-8399-7640","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Camilla Holten","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","name":"Møller, Camilla Holten","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","first":"Steen","key":"ethelbergpau","last":"Ethelberg","locid":"64f5243a-54cc-4250-a37f-e72f1dd94aa3","name":"Ethelberg, Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-9709-356X","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rebecca","key":"legarthpau","last":"Legarth","name":"Legarth, Rebecca","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mia Sarah Fischer","key":"buttonpau","last":"Button","name":"Button, Mia Sarah Fischer","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sophie","key":"gubbelspau","last":"Gubbels","name":"Gubbels, Sophie","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"voldstedlundpau","last":"Voldstedlund","name":"Voldstedlund, Marianne","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Kåre","key":"mølbakpau","last":"Mølbak","locid":"d94c7db7-f909-4a03-bdb7-185bb3eb5a96","name":"Mølbak, Kåre","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Robert Leo","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","name":"Skov, Robert Leo","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardpau","last":"Fomsgaard","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tyra Grove","key":"krausepau","last":"Krause","name":"Krause, Tyra Grove","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Karstenskov","key":"østergaardoth","last":"Østergaard","locid":"3d1bf941-988e-4bca-8161-226b2e3cf514","name":"Østergaard, Stine Karstenskov","orcid":"0009-0001-1092-0826","rank":17,"role":"Other","rolecode":"oth"}],"pmid":["34171231"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s1473-3099(21)00290-5","issn":["14733099","14744457"],"issn_org":["14733099"],"issue":"11","journal":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","pages":"1507-1517","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"The Lancet Infectious Diseases","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85117642711"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d3f9696c-bc37-47c1-b72e-9c7b8b76d81e","ku-198e4c8c-832d-40c7-868b-9df3f9c27233"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Risk of hospitalisation associated with infection with SARS-CoV-2 lineage B.1.1.7 in Denmark : an observational cohort study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-010138","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer-related death worldwide. This population-based longitudinal study investigates survival rates and the burden of comorbidity before and after being diagnosed with lung cancer in Denmark. Methods: From the Danish National Patient Registry (NPR) and the Danish Civil Registration System (CPR), 53,749 patients with lung cancer were identified and matched with 214,304 controls on age, gender, region of residence and marital status in the period 1998–2010. From the NPR, data on survival and comorbidity, registered as ICD-10 diagnoses, were extracted. Comorbidity was assessed using the Deyo-Charlson comorbidity score (DCcs) and mortality using Kaplan-Meier survival curves. Results: 1-year survival rate for Danish lung cancer patients was 51.7 % (CI 51.3-52.1) and 5-year survival rate was 14.7 % (CI 14.3-15.0) compared to 96.8 % (CI 96.7-96.8) and 84.0 % (CI 83.9-84.2) for controls respectively. Overall, cases had significantly more comorbidity compared to controls before being diagnosed with lung cancer. Prior to being diagnosed with lung cancer, more cases than controls had been diagnosed with other malignancies (11.4 % vs 6.0 % p<0.005), diseases of the circulatory system (16.4 % vs 13.0 % p<0.005) and respiratory diseases (12.2 % vs 4.8 % p<0.005). Among lung cancer patients 21.8 % had a DCcs ≥ 1 compared to 13.3 % among controls (P<0.005). The 1-year survival for DCcs =0 was 54.8 % (CI 54.3-55.3) for lung cancer patients and 97.8 % (CI 97.7-97.9) for controls. Decreasing survival with increasing DCcs was found in both groups. Conclusion: This study provides unique nationwide comorbidity data on patients before and after being diagnosed with lung cancer. We found increased mortality with increasing comorbidity, however more pronounced among controls compared to patients with lung cancer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Gouliaev, Anja","Hilberg, Ole","Christensen, Niels Lyhne","Rasmussen, Torben Riis","Ibsen, Rikke","Løkke, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013610"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Gouliaev, Anja"],"keyword":["Case control study","Comorbidity","Lung cancer","Mortality"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comorbidity among danish lung cancer patients before and after initial cancer diagnosis","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20018525.2020.1861579","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013610","identifier":[{"id":"33425261","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7758043","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"85097938509","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-0e12bd33-c8a8-4c72-97b4-62dabbc178d4","sdu-38310326-3ebb-4e55-a2ff-87c9de22a581"],"keyword":["Lung cancer","case-control study","comorbidity","mortality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-64FED413E24CA5C10787218EBF73D734"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/20018525.2020.1861579","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178602843/Comorbidity_among_Danish_lung_cancer_patients_before_and_after_initial_cancer_diagnosis.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Respiratory Diseases and Allergy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Medicine (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["i2minds"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anja","key":"gouliaevpau","last":"Gouliaev","locid":"d48d50b4-27b5-42a6-a489-667d1e3be97e","name":"Gouliaev, Anja","orcid":"0000-0002-6161-5936","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hilbergpau","last":"Hilberg","locid":"6c545c65-1d94-45a3-a8b4-f90eae06d248","name":"Hilberg, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-3463","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Lyhne","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"602d74ce-1885-499c-90da-05dd61bb3148","name":"Christensen, Niels Lyhne","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"311942d4-5b0f-4c92-879f-8d32a246ebf6","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Riis","name_org":"Rasmussen, Torben","orcid":"0000-0002-7030-9260","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"ibsenpau","last":"Ibsen","name":"Ibsen, Rikke","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"løkkepau","last":"Løkke","locid":"db3d3870-0459-4783-8f0b-6a8e5d9dce78","name":"Løkke, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-4141","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33425261"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/20018525.2020.1861579","issn":["20018525"],"issue":"1","journal":"European Clinical Respiratory Journal","paperid":"1861579","publisher":"Taylor & Francis","status":"p","title":"European Clinical Respiratory Journal","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85097938509"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Private Research","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Companies","Private Research","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark","i2minds"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0e12bd33-c8a8-4c72-97b4-62dabbc178d4","sdu-38310326-3ebb-4e55-a2ff-87c9de22a581"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Comorbidity among Danish lung cancer patients before and after initial cancer diagnosis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013610","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Pulmonary rehabilitation (PR) is a cornerstone in COPD care, however, maintaining high adherence rates is challenging. In a multicenter, randomized, controlled trial (RCT), we demonstrated that singing training (ST) was as effective as standard physical training (PT) in PR in improving Six-Minute Walk Test (6MWT) and superior concerning quality of life. There is no knowledge about impact of adherence on change in 6MWT and St George’s Respiratory Questionnaire (SGRQ), or factors related to adherence. Thus, we performed Post hoc analyses of the RCT (effects of ST compared to PT in a 10 weeks’ PR programme in COPD). We did multivariable logistic regression analyses of 1) relationship between adherence (low: 0-49%; medium: 50-74%; high: 75-100%) and achieving clinically significant improvement of 6MWT (30 meters) and SGRQ score (4 units) from baseline to post-PR, and 2) factors related to medium or high adherence. We adjusted the regression models for training modality (ST or PT), baseline characteristics, COPD severity, and expectations towards singing. We included 270 patients in the RCT and found the proportions of patients with high adherence were similar between groups (ST: 60.7%; PT: 56.8%, p=0.90). Medium adherence and high adherence carried higher odds for improving 6MWT (medium: OR 5.6 [95%CI 1.4-22.4], p=0.02; high: OR 10.5 [3.0-36.6], p<0.001) and SGRQ (medium: OR 8.3 [2.1-32.7], p=0.003; high: OR 17.0 [4.9-58.3], p<0.001) (reference: low adherence) in the full sample. No single factor was related to adherence. We found positive dose-response relationships between adherence and improvements of 6MWT and SGRQ, and equal adherence in patients receiving singing training or physical training as part of PR.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Kaasgaard, Mette","Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","Hjerrild Andreasson, Karen","Ottesen, Anders Løkke","Vuust, Peter","Hilberg, Ole","Bodtger, Uffe"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-016459"],"event":{"end":"2021-11-27","start":"2021-11-26","title":"Danish Respiratory Society Congress 2021","year":"2021"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adherence to singing training vs physical training in copd rehabilitation","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-100.00-016459","ids":["au-3488b623-dc77-48bd-a80c-cb9b35601308","sdu-40604b0a-2c4d-47db-a6e7-9209ec279623"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-2-9F6E52C75FF468D0481DEE7AA887B4DB"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Center for Music In the Brain"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU"}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"kaasgaardpau","last":"Kaasgaard","locid":"fc5784b6-66d8-4b92-8c4a-74bf4628c9c3","name":"Kaasgaard, Mette","orcid":"0000-0003-3833-2943","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Daniel Bech","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"18525822-35fd-4cd8-afdd-a608be44cc84","name":"Rasmussen, Daniel Bech","orcid":"0000-0003-1213-9483","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Karen","key":"hjerrildandreassonpau","last":"Hjerrild Andreasson","locid":"8af88feb-2896-4499-89bd-750df2e82461","name":"Andreasson, Karen Hjerrild","name_org":"Hjerrild Andreasson, Karen","orcid":"0000-0002-8752-9614","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Løkke","key":"ottesenpau","last":"Ottesen","name":"Ottesen, Anders Løkke","orcid":"0000-0002-6905-4141","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vuustpau","last":"Vuust","locid":"2c697ab6-9b06-4a16-a687-c8cdbd56f661","name":"Vuust, Peter","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hilbergpau","last":"Hilberg","locid":"4cec668c-4042-4069-9e37-b09fe84ed3b1","name":"Hilberg, Ole","orcid":"0000-0002-3075-3463","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Uffe","key":"bodtgerpau","last":"Bodtger","locid":"2f4e70da-63bb-4b8d-af09-2a959d6df5e8","name":"Bodtger, Uffe","orcid":"0000-0002-1231-9209","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-3488b623-dc77-48bd-a80c-cb9b35601308","sdu-40604b0a-2c4d-47db-a6e7-9209ec279623"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Adherence to singing training vs. physical training in COPD rehabilitation","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-016459","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Product configuration systems (PCSs) have been successful applications of artificial intelligence principles in engineer-to-order (ETO) companies in recent decades. Such applications mainly focus on quotation or production processes rather than multiple business processes. However, in some cases, there could be a benefit of applying multistage PCSs, that is, PCSs that can support several business processes. To investigate the conditions required for the beneficial application of multistage PCSs, this study examines the costs and the benefits associated with this approach. This is done by outlining a framework that defines multistage configuration, hereunder the identification of costs and benefits, as well as the strategies for implementing the approach. The framework is tested through a case study of an ETO company, which provides empirical evidence of the feasibility and the potential benefits of multistage configuration projects. Specifically, the case study shows that investments are modest when moving from a single-stage configurator strategy to a multistage strategy, while demonstrating significant benefits. This paper thereby provides two novel contributions: (1) a definition of multistage configuration, hereunder two strategies for its implementation and (2) empirical evidence that identifies costs and benefits of multistage product configuration, thereby, supporting its feasibility.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jeppe Bredahl","Haug, Anders","Shafiee, Sara","Hvam, Lars","Mortensen, Niels Henrik","Myrodia, Anna"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-035718"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Haug, Anders"],"keyword":["Engineer to order","Mass customization","Process improvement","Product configuration system"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-FLS"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-FLS","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the costs and benefits of multistage configuration a framework and case study","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178499718/Bredahl_rasmussen_2021_The_costs_and_benefits_of_multistag.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-035718","identifier":[{"id":"85099461617","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-8836a374-828f-42ec-9d2c-55ff27077124","sdu-21272d92-9292-4c23-a0b4-9acb07e854cf"],"keyword":["Engineer-to-order","Mass customization","Multistage product configuration","Process improvement","Product configuration system"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3835A146991350EC3782B89402B1018F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/237835497/1_s2.0_S0360835220307658_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178499718/Bredahl_rasmussen_2021_The_costs_and_benefits_of_multistag.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering, Engineering Design and Product Development"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business and Sustainability","SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business and Sustainability, Entrepreneurship and Organization"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"flsmidth","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-FLS","l3nn":"FLSmidth","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"FLSmidth","namevar":["FLSmidth & Co. A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-FLS","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeppe Bredahl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7a36a9ec-d9bc-4b60-867b-dd245501d935","name":"Rasmussen, Jeppe Bredahl","orcid":"0000-0001-7241-3638","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"haugpau","last":"Haug","locid":"13ea9c7a-ffd0-4c3e-abf2-18373b8f1f4b","name":"Haug, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-6173-6925","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"shafieepau","last":"Shafiee","locid":"76628cde-f929-46be-9175-c75a32932cea","name":"Shafiee, Sara","orcid":"0000-0001-9433-5060","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"hvampau","last":"Hvam","locid":"40379baf-979d-4b21-934f-45232e5c41c6","name":"Hvam, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-7617-2971","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Henrik","key":"mortensenpau","last":"Mortensen","locid":"3c76e390-158f-485c-9d64-f15130baecf2","name":"Mortensen, Niels Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1886-5358","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"myrodiapau","last":"Myrodia","name":"Myrodia, Anna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cie.2020.107095","issn":["03608352","18790550"],"issn_org":["03608352"],"journal":"Computers & Industrial Engineering","paperid":"107095","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Computers & Industrial Engineering","volume":"153"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85099461617"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8836a374-828f-42ec-9d2c-55ff27077124","sdu-21272d92-9292-4c23-a0b4-9acb07e854cf"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The costs and benefits of multistage configuration: A framework and case study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-035718","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: The number of persons with gender incongruence referred to health care is increasing, but national data on the incidence of gender incongruence are lacking. The aim of this study was to quantify the development in number of individuals with gender incongruence over time and to estimate the national incidence in Denmark. Material and methods: Historical descriptive cohort study. Individuals older than 18 years with legal sex-change in their person registration number were achieved from Statistics Denmark, and the National Health Register provided data on contact diagnoses related to gender-identity conditions. By combining these two data sources, we made estimates on incidence and incidence rates for individuals with gender incongruence in Denmark through a 41-year period 1980–2020. Results: Through 1980–2020, the annual number of legal sex-changes increased in individuals assigned female at birth from 5 to approximately 170 and among individuals assigned male at birth from 10 to approximately 150. The cumulative number of legal sex-changes at the end of 2019 was 1275 assigned female at birth and 1422 assigned male at birth and 66% of the legal sex-changes were in individuals below 30 years. Correspondingly, the annual number of contacts with the healthcare system due for gender-identity-related conditions increased from 30 during 1990–1999 to around 500 in 2017 (both genders combined), with a 10-fold increase from 2010 to 2017. Conclusions: The number of legal sex-changes and healthcare contacts due to gender-identity-related diagnoses increased substantially over the last 40 years with a more than 10-fold increase during the last decade. This calls for research on possible explanations for this increase, for research on the short-term and long-term health consequences of hormonal and surgical treatment regimens and for ensuring adequate healthcare facilities.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Hilden, Malene","Glintborg, Dorte","Andersen, Marianne Skovsager","Kyster, Natacha","Rasmussen, Steen Christian","Tolstrup, Anders","Lidegaard, Øjvind"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-041434"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corresponding_author":["Hilden, Malene"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Cohort Studies","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Gender Dysphoria","Gender Dysphoria epidemiology","Gender Identity","Gender incongruence","Healthcare Disparities","Humans","Incidence","Male","Registries","Transgender","Transgender Persons statistics numerical data","Young Adult","gender non conformity","trans sexualism"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gender incongruence in denmark a quantitative assessment","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332191167/Gender_incongruence_in_Denmark_2_20.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-041434","identifier":[{"id":"85110949465","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34296426","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-35710c4f-5ac2-478c-a296-28be6c09d11e","sdu-46dad614-7125-46f5-a569-dd0ad2db2e91"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Cohort Studies","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Gender Dysphoria/epidemiology","Healthcare Disparities","Humans","Male","Registries","Transgender Persons/statistics & numerical data","Young Adult","gender dysphoria","gender identity","gender incongruence","gender non-conformity","incidence","trans-sexualism","transgender"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-CB1A2CEB1365485DCEF1EB71B97CEA4A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type"