,"scoID":["2-s2.0-85106213430"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","North Denmark Region","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-78dcf849-e694-447e-ad65-7d6d07cb11e6","ku-94579d11-9b7e-4cc1-bd7a-2cf53ff0a936","sdu-99227698-b40a-416c-a7f5-1f96069f010c"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"MRi of the knee compared to specialized radiography for measurements of articular cartilage height in knees with osteoarthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-005869","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: No data are available on the quality of targeted temperature management (TTM) provided to out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) patients and its association with outcome. METHODS: Post hoc analysis of the TTH48 study (NCT01689077), which compared the effects of prolonged TTM at 33 °C for 48 h to standard 24-h TTM on neurologic outcome. Admission temperature, speed of cooling, rewarming rates, precision (i.e. temperature variability), overcooling and overshooting as post-cooling fever (i.e. >38.0 °C) were collected. A specific score, ranging from 1 to 9, was computed to define the \"quality of TTM\". RESULTS: On a total of 352 patients, most had a moderate quality of TTM (n = 217; 62% - score 4-6), while 80 (23%) patients had a low quality of TTM (score 1-3) and only 52 (16%) a high quality of TTM (score 7-9). The proportion of patients with unfavorable neurological outcome (UO; Cerebral Performance Category of 3-5 at 6 months) was similar between the different quality of TTM groups (p = 0.90). Although a shorter time from arrest to target temperature and a lower proportion of time outside the target ranges in the TTM 48-h than in the TTM 24-h group, quality of TTM was similar between groups. Also, the proportion of patients with UO was similar between the different quality of TTM groups when TTM 48-h and TTM 24-h were compared. CONCLUSIONS: In this study, high quality of TTM was provided to a small proportion of patients. However, quality of TTM was not associated with patients' outcome.","author_count":13,"contributors":["De Fazio, Chiara","Skrifvars, Markus B","Søreide, Eldar","Grejs, Anders M","Di Bernardini, Eugenio","Jeppesen, Anni Nørgaard","Storm, Christian","Kjaergaard, Jesper","Laitio, Timo","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Tianen, Marjaana","Kirkegaard, Hans","Taccone, Fabio Silvio"],"cuid":["S03-100.00-007977"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["TTH48 Investigators"],"corresponding_author":["Taccone, Fabio Silvio"],"country":["Belgium","Finland","Germany","Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Charité – Universitätsmedizin Berlin","Free University of Brussels","Helsinki University Hospital","Hôpital Erasme","Stavanger University Hospital","Turku University Central Hospital","University of Bergen","University of Helsinki","University of Turku","Université libre de Bruxelles"],"keyword":["Association","Body Temperature","CARE","Cardiac arrest","Cardiopulmonary","Core temperature","Duration","Fever","Humans","Hyperthermia","Hypothermia Induced","IMPROVE","Implementation","Out of Hospital Cardiac Arrest therapy","Outcome","Quality","Resuscitation","Targeted temperature management","Temperature","Therapeutic hypothermia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quality of targeted temperature management and outcome of out of hospital cardiac arrest patients a post hoc analysis of the tth000000000048 study","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/314066477/De_Fazio_et_al._Resuscitation_2021_DRAFT_2_28.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S03-100.00-007977","identifier":[{"id":"85108403537","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000678542100016","type":"wos"},{"id":"34166741","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a50c4319-5109-4cc0-bc41-6ccf659b3702","au-5654e462-fa4e-4f3d-aa39-6615cf2b17cc","ku-9ee82f1d-6d07-4b8b-ace3-b5a33843e09f"],"keyword":["ASSOCIATION","Body Temperature","CARDIOPULMO