{"abstract":"RATIONALE: Tumor biopsy cannot detect heterogeneity and an association between heterogeneity in functional imaging and molecular biology will have an impact on both diagnostics and treatment possibilities. PURPOSE: Multiparametric imaging can provide 3D information on functional aspects of a tumor and may be suitable for predicting intratumor heterogeneity. Here, we investigate the correlation between intratumor heterogeneity assessed with multiparametric imaging and multiple-biopsy immunohistochemistry. METHODS: In this prospective study, patients with primary or recurrent head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC) underwent PET/MRI scanning prior to surgery. Tumors were removed en bloc and six core biopsies were used for immunohistochemical (IHC) staining with a predefined list of biomarkers: p40, p53, EGFR, Ki-67, GLUT1, VEGF, Bcl-2, CAIX, PD-L1. Intratumor heterogeneity of each IHC biomarker was quantified by calculating the coefficient of variation (CV) in tumor proportion score among the six core biopsies within each tumor lesion. The heterogeneity in the imaging biomarkers was assessed by calculating CV in 18F-fluorodeoxyglucose (FDG)-uptake, diffusion and perfusion. Concordance of the two variance measures was quantified using Spearman's rank correlation RESULTS: Twenty-eight patients with a total of 33 lesions were included. There was considerable heterogeneity in most of the IHC biomarkers especially in GLUT1, PD-L1, Ki-67, CAIX and p53, however we only observed a correlation between the heterogeneity in GLUT1 and p53 and between Ki-67 and EGFR. Heterogeneity in FDG uptake and diffusion correlated with heterogeneity in cell density. CONCLUSION: Considerable heterogeneity of IHC biomarkers was found, however, only few and weak correlations between the studied IHC markers were observed. The studied functional imaging biomarkers showed weak associations with heterogeneity in some of the IHC biomarkers. Thus, biological heterogeneity is not a general tumor characteristic but depends on the specific biomarker or imaging modality.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jacob H","Olin, Anders B.","Lelkaitis, Giedrius","Hansen, Adam Espe","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Johannesen, Helle H","Kjaer, Andreas","Fischer, Barbara Malene","Specht, Lena","Bentzen, Søren M.","von Buchwald, Christian","Wessel, Irene","Vogelius, Ivan R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-465767"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomarkers","Biomarkers Tumor","Fluorodeoxyglucose F18","Head and Neck Neoplasms diagnostic imaging","Humans","Neoplasm Recurrence Local","Positron Emission Tomography","Prospective Studies","Squamous Cell Carcinoma of Head and Neck"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intratumor heterogeneity is biomarker specific and challenges the association with heterogeneity in multimodal functional imaging in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-465767","identifier":[{"id":"85103972548","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33848777","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-78cf54bf-0ca1-4cae-bf78-d38827ae2aec"],"keyword":["Biomarkers","Biomarkers, Tumor","Fluorodeoxyglucose F18","Head and Neck Neoplasms/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Neoplasm Recurrence, Local","Positron-Emission Tomography","Prospective Studies","Squamous Cell Carcinoma of Head and Neck"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3B814992E0660F86DC19559DD18EA85C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jacob H","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jacob H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders B","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"d81d9238-eddc-4496-b609-4e95fafdd9c3","name":"Olin, Anders B.","name_org":"Olin, Anders B","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Giedrius","key":"lelkaitispau","last":"Lelkaitis","locid":"f7aba425-cebc-418e-a5f5-99a6e1ad6c16","name":"Lelkaitis, Giedrius","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","name_org":"Andersen, Flemming L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Helle H","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","locid":"f6e969fe-c996-468f-96b1-3f255ef8a2b1","name":"Johannesen, Helle H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Barbara M","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a87f805a-ba44-45e2-b257-59a6f2976711","name":"Fischer, Barbara Malene","name_org":"Fischer, Barbara M","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren M","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","locid":"fbb03c8f-3547-4eb0-a2af-1f9302471149","name":"Bentzen, Søren M.","name_org":"Bentzen, Søren M","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Irene","key":"wesselpau","last":"Wessel","locid":"873c4b02-5cc0-4171-bd3d-12ba84e56ded","name":"Wessel, Irene","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ivan R","key":"vogeliuspau","last":"Vogelius","locid":"66f4607a-ae94-4767-aaf0-79279bb24c31","name":"Vogelius, Ivan R.","name_org":"Vogelius, Ivan R","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["33848777"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejrad.2021.109668","issn":["0720048X","18727727"],"issn_org":["0720048X"],"journal":"European Journal of Radiology","paperid":"109668","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Radiology","volume":"139"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85103972548"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-78cf54bf-0ca1-4cae-bf78-d38827ae2aec"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Intratumor heterogeneity is biomarker specific and challenges the association with heterogeneity in multimodal functional imaging in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-465767","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Large carnivores are generally sensitive to ecosystem changes because their specialized diet and position at the top of the trophic pyramid is associated with small population sizes. Accordingly, low genetic diversity at the whole-genome level has been reported for all big cat species, including the widely distributed leopard. However, all previous whole-genome analyses of leopards are based on the Far Eastern Amur leopards that live at the extremity of the species' distribution and therefore are not necessarily representative of the whole species. We sequenced 53 whole genomes of African leopards. Strikingly, we found that the genomic diversity in the African leopard is 2- to 5-fold higher than in other big cats, including the Amur leopard, likely because of an exceptionally high effective population size maintained by the African leopard throughout the Pleistocene. Furthermore, we detected ongoing gene flow and very low population differentiation within African leopards compared with those of other big cats. We corroborated this by showing a complete absence of an otherwise ubiquitous equatorial forest barrier to gene flow. This sets the leopard apart from most other widely distributed large African mammals, including lions. These results revise our understanding of trophic sensitivity and highlight the remarkable resilience of the African leopard, likely because of its extraordinary habitat versatility and broad dietary niche.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Pečnerová, Patrícia","Garcia-Erill, Genís","Liu, Xiaodong","Nursyifa, Casia","Waples, Ryan K.","Santander, Cindy G.","Quinn, Liam","Frandsen, Peter","Meisner, Jonas","Stæger, Frederik Filip","Rasmussen, Malthe Sebro","Brüniche-Olsen, Anna","Jørgensen, Christian Hviid Friis","da Fonseca, Rute R.","Siegismund, Hans Redlef","Albrechtsen, Anders","Heller, Rasmus","Moltke, Ida","Hanghøj, Kristian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-501590"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Purdue University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"high genetic diversity and low differentiation reflect the ecological versatility of the african leopard","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies/open-access-licenses/elsevier-user-license","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2021.01.064","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-501590","identifier":[{"id":"85105271860","type":"scopus"},{"id":"33636121","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-b512c4f1-c54e-4bb9-bda4-b59284d9dd5e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8D92497B1418158E3B402B8A88FE769A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies/open-access-licenses/elsevier-user-license","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/332042095/1_s2.0_S0960982221001299_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"https://www.elsevier.com/about/policies/open-access-licenses/elsevier-user-license","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cub.2021.01.064","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Copenhagen Zoo"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"purdue university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Purdue University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Patrícia","key":"pečnerovápau","last":"Pečnerová","locid":"840078a0-bb20-4c9f-87ab-33b4d3058bfc","name":"Pečnerová, Patrícia","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Genís","key":"garciaerillpau","last":"Garcia-Erill","locid":"a03971a5-00fa-4ccf-ae13-f15fdcd34405","name":"Garcia-Erill, Genís","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Xiaodong","key":"liupau","last":"Liu","locid":"e20c5ca2-aa50-4de3-9ee9-ce2aee1875dc","name":"Liu, Xiaodong","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Casia","key":"nursyifapau","last":"Nursyifa","locid":"cf7361b1-42f8-4773-9458-ab5a73c35f5d","name":"Nursyifa, Casia","orcid":"0000-0002-7803-9664","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ryan K.","key":"waplespau","last":"Waples","locid":"d197c61e-c664-436e-b709-7dea17d3ad2c","name":"Waples, Ryan K.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cindy G.","key":"santanderpau","last":"Santander","locid":"7fb91780-169e-48b7-80ed-6741e9f3af9e","name":"Santander, Cindy G.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Liam","key":"quinnpau","last":"Quinn","locid":"51f8bb78-3a6e-4579-9b13-a376374277dc","name":"Quinn, Liam","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","first":"Peter","key":"frandsenpau","last":"Frandsen","locid":"f77299e6-4860-4284-9567-6b95635b10e6","name":"Frandsen, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonas","key":"meisnerpau","last":"Meisner","locid":"9747ddc4-b8f6-4f7c-b6d4-f00952d283ca","name":"Meisner, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0002-9540-6673","rank":9,"