{"abstract":"Diagnosing lung cancer requires invasive procedures with high risk of complications. Methylated tumor DNA in bronchial lavage has previously shown potential as a diagnostic biomarker. We aimed to develop and validate methylated HOXA9 in bronchial lavage as a diagnostic biomarker of lung cancer. Participants were referred on suspicion of lung cancer. Ten mL lavage fluid was collected at bronchoscopy for analysis of methylated HOXA9 based on droplet digital PCR according to our previously published method. HOXA9 status was compared with the final diagnosis. The Discovery and Validation cohorts consisted of 101 and 95 consecutively enrolled participants, re-spectively. In the discovery cohort, the sensitivity and specificity were 73.1% (95% CI 60.9–83.2%) and 85.3% (95% CI 68.9–95.0%), respectively. In the validation cohort, the values were 80.0% (95% CI 66.3–90.0%) and 75.6% (95% CI 60.5–87.1%), respectively. A multiple logistic regression model including age, smoking status, and methylated HOXA9 status resulted in an AUC of 84.9% (95% CI 77.3–92.4%) and 85.9% (95% CI 78.4–93.4%) for the Discovery and Validation cohorts, respectively. Methylated HOXA9 in bronchial lavage holds potential as a supplementary tool in the diagnosis of lung cancer with a clinically relevant sensitivity and specificity. It remained significant when adjusting for age and smoking status.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Wen, Sara Witting Christensen","Andersen, Rikke Fredslund","Rasmussen, Kristian","Brenner Thomsen, Caroline Emilie","Hansen, Torben Frøstrup","Nederby, Line","Hager, Henrik","Jakobsen, Anders","Hilberg, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-617747"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Wen, Sara Witting Christensen"],"keyword":["Lung cancer","circulating tumor DNA"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"validating methylated hoxa000000000009 in bronchial lavage as a diagnostic tool in patients suspected of lung cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers13164223","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Funding: This research was funded by the Region of Southern Denmark (granted to O.H.) and grants from the Department of Oncology, Vejle Hospital, University Hospital of Southern Denmark."],"id":"S01-000.00-617747","identifier":[{"id":"85113165032","type":"scopus"},{"id":"34439376","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC8393370","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-9b85b9a0-a00b-4ddf-a729-3376f63b1172"],"keyword":["Circulating tumor DNA","Lung cancer","Methylated HOXA9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EE8330258D34C50563B84A090DCC406C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/191110948/cancers_13_04223.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/cancers13164223","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"D