{"abstract":"Overvågningen af den marine bundvegetation foregår i dag hovedsageligt ved transekt observationer, som er dyre og tidskrævende, og som ikke giver overblik over den arealmæssige udbredelse af vegetationen. Nye teknologier, som fx droner og satellitter, bliver i stigende omfang anvendt i kystzonen og i SeaStatus projektet har vi undersøgt om og hvordan disse nye teknologier kan bidrage til at forbedre overvågningen af den marine bundvegetation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Timmermann, Karen","Thomasberger, Aris","Boye Hansen, Lars","Stæhr, Peter A.","Rasmussen, Mikkel Lydholm","Stockmarr, Anders","Sengupta, Sayantan","Nielsen, Lisbeth T.","Lønborg, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-095.15-016186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"nye overvågningsteknikker til marin vegetation","src":["au","dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/257658194/Vand_og_Jord_2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-095.15-016186","ids":["au-313b1f88-ca02-4390-a80f-0aca592c371c","dtu-8493a645-855b-442d-85e8-555b623e48ff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-2-3DCDD16D6455EF2BAF5261A028941863"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/257658194/Vand_og_Jord_2021.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2021","yearSub":"2021"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Coastal Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"dhi danish hydraulic institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-DHYI","l3nn":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DHI Danish Hydraulic Institute","namevar":["DHI Water - Environment - Health"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-DHYI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Diversity and Experimental Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Karen","key":"timmermannpau","last":"Timmermann","locid":"abfd7b7d-0497-46ec-a26c-ba1772c111df","name":"Timmermann, Karen","orcid":"0000-0001-5989-4692","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aris","key":"thomasbergerpau","last":"Thomasberger","locid":"cb86f5d0-2d36-4832-bc19-1c823ed35daa","name":"Thomasberger, Aris","orcid":"0000-0002-0829-3771","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"boyehansenpau","last":"Boye Hansen","name":"Boye Hansen, Lars","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Boye","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Lars Boye","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter A.","key":"stæhrpau","last":"Stæhr","locid":"1d2daf18-7ace-48c9-b950-7fb3bdc0a173","name":"Stæhr, Peter A.","orcid":"0000-0002-1580-4875","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mikkel Lydholm","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Lydholm","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"stockmarrpau","last":"Stockmarr","locid":"f8ce8f15-f38a-4f99-a8c6-08b0cd7b0f6a","name":"Stockmarr, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8681-2370","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sayantan","key":"senguptapau","last":"Sengupta","locid":"b01a10cb-1fbb-43ed-8941-c8cce0dcb297","name":"Sengupta, Sayantan","orcid":"0000-0003-3820-495X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lisbeth T.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Lisbeth T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"lønborgpau","last":"Lønborg","locid":"8b3df852-bf56-4f89-954a-f8b76330e002","name":"Lønborg, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-8380-0238","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["09087761"],"issue":"1","journal":"Vand & Jord","pages":"8-11","status":"p","title":"Vand & Jord","volume":"28"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["14. Life Below Water","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-313b1f88-ca02-4390-a80f-0aca592c371c","dtu-8493a645-855b-442d-85e8-555b623e48ff"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Nye overvågningsteknikker til marin vegetation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-095.15-016186","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"In addition to humans, severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) can transmit to animals that include hamsters, cats, dogs, mink, ferrets, tigers, lions, cynomolgus macaques, rhesus macaques, and treeshrew. Among these, mink are particularly susceptible. Indeed, 10 countries in Europe and North America reported SARS-CoV-2 infection among mink on fur farms. In Denmark, SARS-CoV-2 spread rapidly among mink farms and spilled-over back into humans, acquiring mutations/deletions with unknown consequences for virulence and antigenicity. Here we describe a mink-associated SARS-CoV-2 variant (Cluster 5) characterized by 11 amino acid substitutions and four amino acid deletions relative to Wuhan-Hu-1. Temporal virus titration, together with genomic and subgenomic viral RNA quantitation, demonstrated a modest in vitro fitness attenuation of the Cluster 5 virus in the Vero-E6 cell line. Potential alterations in antigenicity conferred by amino acid changes in the spike protein that include three substitutions (Y453F, I692V, and M1229I) and a loss of two amino acid residues 69 and 70 (ΔH69/V70), were evaluated in a virus microneutralization assay. Compared to a reference strain, the Cluster 5 variant showed reduced neutralization in a proportion of convalescent human COVID-19 samples. The findings underscore the need for active surveillance SARS-CoV-2 infection and virus evolution in susceptible animal hosts.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Lassaunière, Ria","Fonager, Jannik","Rasmussen, Morten","Frische, Anders","Polacek, Charlotta","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","Lohse, Louise","Belsham, Graham J","Underwood, Alexander","Winckelmann, Anni Assing","Bollerup, Signe","Bukh, Jens","Weis, Nina","Sækmose, Susanne Gjørup","Aagaard, Bitten","Alfaro-Núñez, Alonzo","Mølbak, Kåre","Bøtner, Anette","Fomsgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002159"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","clus