{"abstract":"Thieno-fused subporphyrazines (TPs) containing a central and axially substituted boron atom are a class of compounds with interesting optical and redox properties. Here we present our efforts towards expanding this class of compounds using various thiophene substrates that were prepared by cyanation or nitration of 3,4-dibromothiophene. Moreover, we show that one TP derivative forms a 2:1 complex in the solid state with C70.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Mads Georg","Gotfredsen, Henrik","Kadziola, Anders","Nielsen, Mogens Brøndsted"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-396210"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"towards novel thieno fused subporphyrazines via functionalized thiophene precursors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-396210","identifier":[{"id":"85083721590","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-04947704-1ff2-482f-938a-92489368edb8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AAC5285167318AA39A79DB60549FFB88"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Chemistry, Department of Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Georg","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"cf2a36eb-a45a-49f4-9302-f7cd3b6fc61e","name":"Rasmussen, Mads Georg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik","key":"gotfredsenpau","last":"Gotfredsen","locid":"3a0ea228-c804-46bf-af1a-2de90a977ca3","name":"Gotfredsen, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-9559-7190","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kadziolapau","last":"Kadziola","locid":"f1ba1c8e-3218-4dc7-94be-f55516c6b742","name":"Kadziola, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-2698-113X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mogens Brøndsted","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"d5a042aa-d63e-45b0-a022-f3de910fde75","name":"Nielsen, Mogens Brøndsted","orcid":"0000-0001-8377-0788","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17415993.2020.1753190","issn":["17415993","17416000"],"issn_org":["17415993"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Sulfur Chemistry","pages":"357-368","status":"p","title":"Journal of Sulfur Chemistry","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85083721590"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-04947704-1ff2-482f-938a-92489368edb8"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Towards novel thieno-fused subporphyrazines via functionalized thiophene precursors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-396210","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Purpose: Multiparametric positron emission tomography (PET)/magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) as a one-stop shop for radiation therapy (RT) planning has great potential but is technically challenging. We studied the feasibility of performing multiparametric PET/MRI of patients with head and neck cancer (HNC) in RT treatment position. As a step toward planning RT based solely on PET/MRI, a deep learning approach was employed to generate synthetic computed tomography (sCT) from MRI. This was subsequently evaluated for dose calculation and PET attenuation correction (AC). Methods and Materials: Eleven patients, including 3 pilot patients referred for RT of HNC, underwent PET/MRI in treatment position after a routine fluorodeoxyglucose-PET/CT planning scan. The PET/MRI scan protocol included multiparametric imaging. A convolutional neural network was trained in a leave-one-out process to predict sCT from the Dixon MRI. The clinical CT-based dose plans were recalculated on sCT, and the plans were compared in terms of relative differences in mean, maximum, near-maximum, and near-minimum absorbed doses for different volumes of interest. Comparisons between PET with sCT-based AC and PET with CT-based AC were assessed based on the relative differences in mean and maximum standardized uptake values (SUVmean and SUVmax) from the PET-positive volumes. Results: All 11 patients underwent PET/MRI in RT treatment position. Apart from the 3 pilots, full multiparametric imaging was completed in 45 minutes for 7 out of 8 patients. One patient terminated the examination after 30 minutes. With the exception of 1 patient with an inserted tracheostomy tube, all dosimetric parameters of the sCT-based dose plans were within ±1% of the CT-based dose plans. For PET, the mean difference was 0.4 ± 1.2% for SUVmean and –0.5 ± 1.0% for SUVmax. Conclusions: Performing multiparametric PET/MRI of patients with HNC in RT treatment position was clinically feasible. The sCT generation resulted in AC of PET and dose calculations sufficiently accurate for clinical use. These results are an important step toward using multiparametric PET/MRI as a one-stop shop for personalized RT planning.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Olin, Anders B.","Hansen, Adam Espe","Rasmussen, Jacob H.","Ladefoged, Claes N.","Berthelsen, Anne K.","Håkansson, Katrin","Vogelius, Ivan R.","Specht, Lena","Gothelf, Anita B.","Kjaer, Andreas","Fischer, Barbara Malene","Andersen, Flemming Littrup"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-434118"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feasibility of multiparametric positron emission tomography magnetic resonance imaging as a one stop shop for radiation therapy planning for patients with head and neck cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijrobp.2020.07.024","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-434118","identifier":[{"id":"85089457116","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32682955","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-441bd8dd-726e-4c99-b11c-3b21f6ddfec5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E2E67CE97F06C11413781A6DC533A8BC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijrobp.2020.07.024","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284653991/Feasibility_of_Multiparametric_Positron_Emission_Tomography_Magnetic_Resonance_Imaging_as_a_One_Stop_Shop_for_Radiation_Therapy_Planning_for_Patients_with_Head_and_Neck_Cancer_publisher_version_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{