ssn":["19487193"],"issue":"9","journal":"ACS Chemical Neuroscience","pages":"1270-1282","status":"p","title":"ACS Chemical Neuroscience","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084272615"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-52d3d174-1dc1-4ce6-a261-4a19fbb5cb20"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Neurotrophic effects of vascular endothelial growth factor B and novel mimetic peptides on neurons from the central nervous system","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442880","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: The case presented here illustrates that interdisciplinary teamwork can be essential for the understanding of the COVID-19 disease presentation and enlightening of the pathophysiology. Case presentation: A 60-years-old overweight woman without any comorbidities was found dead in her apartment after 14 days of home isolation due to suspicion on the Coronavirus disease 2019 (COVID-19). She had reported symptoms of tachycardia, fever, and increasing respiratory difficulty one day before her death. Due to the Danish legal act on sudden deaths a forensic autopsy was performed including a thorough examination and biosampling. The results of the forensic autopsy displayed sever densified, almost airless, firm lungs, and an unspecific reactive minimal focal perivascular inflammation consisting of macrophages of the brain tissue. The final diagnosis, COVID-19 with involvement of the central nervous system was established by use of the RT-RNA analysis on cerebrospinal fluid, as well as by serologic detection of the specific antibodies for SARS-CoV-2 in cerebrospinal fluid and serum. The genetic analysis displayed a 2 % variation between SARS-CoV-2 isolates recovered from the tracheal sample, cerebrospinal fluid, and tissues from both lungs. Conclusion: The combination of all available results revealed that the cause of death was COVID-19 with severe pulmonary disease and neuroinvasion, as well as renal affection resulting in hyponatremia. To our knowledge, it was not shown previously that neuroinvasion could be confirmed by the detection of specific antibodies for SARS-CoV-2 and SARS-CoV-2 specific RNA in cerebrospinal fluid. This case supports hypotheses that SARS-CoV-2 may cause central nervous system infection. The genetic distinction between SARS-CoV-2 isolates was done by whole-genome sequencing, where the isolate recovered from the cerebrospinal fluid was the most different.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Marbjerg, Lis Høy","Jacobsen, Christina","Fonager, Jannik","Bøgelund, Claus","Rasmussen, Morten","Fomsgaard, Anders","Banner, Jytte","Jensen, Veronika Vorobieva Solholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-442997"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the involvement of central nervous system and sequence variability of severe adult respiratory syndrome coronavirus 000000000002 revealed in autopsy tissue samples a case report","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-61471/v1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-442997","ids":["ku-530b10c0-385e-4ed0-a3fc-9f5ebf25c6b7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-E7199912CB186D667F9B21CDFF54297C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-61471/v1","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/300683006/366a9fcf_df5d_4bb7_b153_88928608b164.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Forensic Medicine, Section of Forensic Pathology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Lis Høy","key":"marbjergpau","last":"Marbjerg","name":"Marbjerg, Lis Høy","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christina","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","locid":"524f7da6-c932-4471-99c3-5864c66059df","name":"Jacobsen, Christina","orcid":"0000-0001-7257-0772","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jannik","key":"fonagerpau","last":"Fonager","name":"Fonager, Jannik","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Claus","key":"bøgelundpau","last":"Bøgelund","name":"Bøgelund, Claus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardpau","last":"Fomsgaard","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jytte","key":"bannerpau","last":"Banner","locid":"de232254-f016-4135-9a31-ed55db6d92a7","name":"Banner, Jytte","orcid":"0000-0002-7559-1285","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Veronika Vorobieva Solholm","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Veronika Vorobieva Solholm","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21203/rs.3.rs-61471/v1","pages":"16","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-530b10c0-385e-4ed0-a3fc-9f5ebf25c6b7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The involvement of Central Nervous System and sequence variability of Severe Adult Respiratory Syndrome – Coronavirus-2 revealed in autopsy tissue samples: a case report.","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-442997","year":"2020","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"Gut microbiome (GM) composition and function are linked to human health and disease, and routes for manipulating the GM have become an area of intense research. Due to its high treatment efficacy, the use of fecal microbiota transplantation (FMT) is generally accepted as a promising experimental treatment for patients suffering from GM imbalances (dysbiosis), e.g. caused by recurrent Clostridioides difficile infections (rCDI). Mounting evidence suggests that bacteriophages (phages) play a key role in successful FMT treatment by restoring the dysbiotic bacterial GM. As a refinement to FMT, removing the bacterial component of donor feces by sterile filtration, also referred to as fecal virome transplantation (FVT), decreases the risk of invasive infections caused by bacteria. However, eukaryotic viruses and prophage-encoded virulence factors remain a safety issue. Recent in vivo studies show how cascading effects are initiated when phage communities are transferred to the gut by e.g. FVT, which leads to changes in the GM composition, host metabolome, and improve host health such as alleviating symptoms of obesity and type-2-diabetes (T2D). In this review, we discuss the promises and limitations of FVT along with the perspectives of using FVT to treat various diseases associated with GM dysbiosis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck","Koefoed, Anna Kirstine","Jakobsen, Rasmus Riemer","Deng, Ling","Castro-Mejía, Josué L.","Brunse, Anders","Neve, Horst","Vogensen, Finn Kvist","Nielsen, Dennis Sandris"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-544186"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Rubner Institut"],"keyword":["Bacteriophages","Cascading effects","Dysbiosis","Fecal virome transplantation","Gut microbiome","Phage therapy"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bacteriophage mediated manipulation of the gut microbiome promises and presents limitations","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-544186","identifier":[{"id":"85088881452","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32495834","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-fc8eae73-860e-4353-ac4c-d414780c6525"],"keyword":["bacteriophages","cascading effects","dysbiosis","fecal virome transplantation","gut microbiome","phage therapy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8452FC50E0437A9A2571F67348835550"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Food Science, Food Microbiology, Gut Health, and Fermentation"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max rubner institut","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Rubner Institut","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Torben Sølbeck","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37b31216-f69f-4ff3-bc9c-ffd6b36fc003","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Sølbeck","orcid":"0000-0002-9907-8953","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anna Kirstine","key":"koefoedpau","last":"Koefoed","locid":"0e8522ee-b55e-4e46-9ce0-23c322e0025b","name":"Koefoed, Anna Kirstine","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Rasmus Riemer","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"80dbaf1b-0cb5-48fe-ab84-4254c687ba73","name":"Jakobsen, Rasmus Riemer","rank":3,"rolecode":"pa