,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Jesper Sølver","key":"schoupau","last":"Schou","locid":"e9d20fb4-4b3f-40ce-9fba-acfb58217c0b","name":"Schou, Jesper Sølver","orcid":"0000-0001-5030-4035","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.-C.","key":"svenningpau","last":"Svenning","locid":"33c3c4e2-57ab-478c-889d-06c594e57b8b","name":"Svenning, Jens Christian","name_org":"Svenning, J.-C.","orcid":"0000-0002-3415-0862","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"søndergaardpau","last":"Søndergaard","locid":"8a770bfc-7b53-42eb-80fb-be3ef9c2f5a3","name":"Søndergaard, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-1514-0482","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"17","publisher":"Det danske IPBES-samarbejde","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-b0769fee-e13b-435b-ac0f-c623615a194c","ku-cb607a53-2e2e-421e-ac42-8d558659fdfc","sdu-9161fae8-b5f4-46c4-bd0e-acb656bc402e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Genopretning af biodiversitet og økosystemer i Danmark : Ekspertudtalelse","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-094.40-025529","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Aim: To assess the effect of liraglutide, a glucagon-like peptide-1 receptor agonist, on urinary sodium excretion as well as on circulating adrenomedullin and copeptin levels in patients with type 2 diabetes (T2D). Materials and methods: In the LIVE study, patients (n = 241) with left ventricular ejection fraction ≤45% were randomized to liraglutide 1.8 mg daily or placebo for 24 weeks, and 30% had a concomitant diagnosis of T2D. Plasma levels of N-terminal brain-natriuretic-peptide (NT-proBNP) (a predefined secondary endpoint), midregional pro-atrial-natriuretic-peptide (MR-proANP), midregional pro-adrenomedullin (MR-proADM) and copeptin were measured at baseline and after 24 weeks in this substudy. The potential effect modification of T2D was assessed. Results: In the eligible subgroup of 231 patients with available biomarkers (115 randomized to liraglutide and 116 to placebo), MR-proANP decreased by 12% (P =.002) and NT-proBNP by 9% (P =.009) during liraglutide treatment compared with placebo at week 24. Interaction with T2D for the treatment effect of change in MR-proANP and NT-proBNP levels was P =.003 and P =.03, respectively. Consequently, in patients with T2D, liraglutide decreased MR-proANP by 27% (P <.001) and NT-proBNP by 25% (P =.02) compared with placebo, whereas no change was observed in patients without T2D. There was no effect of liraglutide on MR-proADM (P =.10) or copeptin (P =.52). Conclusion: Liraglutide decreased the A- and B-type natriuretic peptides significantly in patients with heart failure with reduced ejection fraction (HFrEF) and concomitant T2D, suggesting a beneficial mechanism of liraglutide in T2D patients with HFrEF.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Nielsen, Bent Roni Ranghøj","Jorsal, Anders","Tougaard, Rasmus Stilling","Rasmussen, Jon J.","Schou, Morten","Videbaek, Lars","Gustafsson, Ida","Faber, Jens","Flyvbjerg, Allan","Wiggers, Henrik","Tarnow, Lise","Kistorp, Caroline"],"cuid":["S03-097.88-014420"],"filters":{"