{"abstract":"The fueling efficiency of supersonic molecular beam injection (SMBI) depends on injection parameters. In this article, we report on simulations of SMBI into turbulent edge fusion plasmas. Density continuity equations, which describe the dynamics of molecules and Franck-Condon atoms, are coupled with the plasma equations in the hot-edge-sol-electrostatic (HESEL) drift-fluid model. Numerical simulations, with parameters relevant to experimental conditions, are performed in order to investigate the dependency of the fueling efficiency of SMBI on the molecular beam density, velocity, and beam width. In all conditions, the efficiency grows with the increase in the molecular beam velocity. The variation in efficiency with respect to the beam density depends on the plasma pressure and the ratio of the density source, produced by ionization of neutrals, to the plasma density source provided by core fueling. The effect of the molecular beam width is pronounced only if the beam density is high and the plasma, into which the beam is injected, is relatively dense and hot. The influence of plasma fluctuations on SMBI is weak; however, a strong neutral injection leads to suppression of a turbulence transport due to relaxation of pressure gradient profiles.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Avdeeva, G.","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Thrysøe, Alexander Simon"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371058"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Naulin, Volker"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of injection parameters on fueling efficiency of supersonic molecular beam injection into turbulent fusion plasmas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0002858","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371058","identifier":[{"id":"000545724300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85088362669","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-de4b6e51-1481-4803-b8f0-3b061d4ee476"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-901B0537CFABFF8819DF3D6E6B2ECA8F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/234947404/5.0002858.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/5.0002858","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"avdeevapau","last":"Avdeeva","locid":"807d4014-63ed-4994-9b95-d57fc45409a0","name":"Avdeeva, G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"V.","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","name_org":"Naulin, V.","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. H.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","name_org":"Nielsen, A. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J.","key":"juulrasmussenpau","last":"Juul Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Juul Rasmussen, J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A.S.","key":"thrysøepau","last":"Thrysøe","locid":"39b78f9b-adc1-4e59-9d7c-7072f09a73bc","name":"Thrysøe, Alexander Simon","name_org":"Thrysøe, A.S.","orcid":"0000-0002-7761-5156","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/5.0002858","issn":["1070664X","10897674"],"issn_org":["1070664X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Physics of Plasmas","paperid":"062515","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Physics of Plasmas","volume":"27"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85088362669"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-de4b6e51-1481-4803-b8f0-3b061d4ee476"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Influence of injection parameters on fueling efficiency of supersonic molecular beam injection into turbulent fusion plasmas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-371058","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"QuantumATK is an integrated set of atomic-scale modelling tools developed since 2003 by professional software engineers in collaboration with academic researchers. While different aspects and individual modules of the platform have been previously presented,&#13; the purpose of this paper is to give a general overview of the platform. The QuantumATK simulation engines enable electronic-structure calculations using density functional theory or tight-binding model Hamiltonians, and also offers bonded or reactive empirical force fields in many different parametrizations. Density functional theory is implemented using either a plane-wave basis or expansion of electronic states in a linear combination of atomic orbitals. The platform includes a long list of advanced modules, including Green's-function methods for electron transport simulations and surface calculations, first-principles electron-phonon and electron-photon couplings,&#13; simulation of atomic-scale heat transport, ion dynamics, spintronics, optical properties of materials, static polarization, and more.&#13; Seamless integration of the different simulation engines into a common platform allows for easy combination of different simulation methods into complex workflows. Besides giving a general overview and presenting a number of implementation details&#13; not previously published, we also present four different application examples. These are calculations of the phonon-limited mobility of Cu, Ag and Au, electron transport in a gated 2D device, multi-model simulation of lithium ion drift through a battery cathode in an external electric field, and electronic-structure calculations of the composition-dependent band gap of SiGe alloys.&#13.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Smidstrup, Søren","Markussen, Troels","Vancraeyveld, Pieter","Wellendorff, Jess","Schneider, Julian","Gunst, Tue","Verstichel, Brecht","Stradi, Daniele","Khomyakov, Petr A.","Vej-Hansen, Ulrik Grønbjerg","Lee, Maeng-Eun","Chill, Samuel T.","Rasmussen, Filip","Penazzi, Gabriele","Corsetti, Fabiano","Ojanpera, Ari","Jensen, Kristian","Palsgaard, Mattias Lau Nøhr","Martinez, Umberto","Blom, Anders","Brandbyge, Mads","Stokbro, Kurt"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371949"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corresponding_author":["Smidstrup, Søren"],"keyword":["Density functional theory","First principles simulations","Force fields","Non equilibrium Green s function","Semi empirical methods","Tight binding"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"quantumatk an integrated platform of electronic and atomic scale modelling tools","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-648X/ab4007","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371949","identifier":[{"id":"85072793056","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31470430","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-e1579037-0501-48c5-afc0-c3ca4c25670a"],"keyword":["Atomic-scale modelling","Density functional theory","First-principles simulations","Force fields","Non-equilibrium Green's function","Semi-empirical methods","Tight-binding"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-03AAC8263979E0ED71B586BB7ABDC22E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-648X/ab4007","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/191318826/Postprint.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/195076412/Smidstrup_2020_J._Phys._Condens._Matter_32_015901.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Synopsys Denmark ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Centers, Center for Nanostructured Graphene","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"smidstruppau","last":"Smidstrup","name":"Smidstrup, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels","key":"markussenpau","last":"Markussen","name":"Markussen, Troels","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pieter","key":"vancraeyveldpau","last":"Vancraeyveld","name":"Vancraeyveld, Pieter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jess","key":"wellendorffpau","last":"Wellendorff","name":"Wellendorff, Jess","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Julian","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Julian","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Tue","key":"gunstpau","last":"Gunst","locid":"64bb0a75-96d6-46a7-b52e-5a9a9575016c","name":"Gunst, Tue","orcid":"0000-0002-3000-5940","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Brecht","key":"verstichelpau","last":"Verstichel","name":"Verstichel, Brecht","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresp