se","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85092562697"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-386291d3-55d6-44a9-abda-0354991a2be0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Dickkopf-1 Overexpression<i> in vitro</i> Nominates Candidate Blood Biomarkers Relating to Alzheimer's Disease Pathology","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-426962","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Testicular germ cell tumours (TGCTs) are characterised by an overall high cisplatin-sensitivity which has been linked to their continued expression of pluripotency factors. Recently, the Nodal signalling pathway has been implicated in the regulation of pluripotency factor expression in fetal germ cells, and the pathway could therefore also be involved in regulating expression of pluripotency factors in malignant germ cells, and hence cisplatin-sensitivity in TGCTs. Methods: We used in vitro culture of the TGCT-derived cell line NTera2, ex vivo tissue culture of primary TGCT specimens and xenografting of NTera2 cells into nude mice in order to investigate the consequences of manipulating Nodal and Activin signalling on pluripotency factor expression, apoptosis, proliferation and cisplatin-sensitivity. Results: The Nodal signalling factors were markedly expressed concomitantly with the pluripotency factor OCT4 in GCNIS cells, seminomas and embryonal carcinomas. Despite this, inhibition of Nodal and Activin signalling either alone or simultaneously did not affect proliferation or apoptosis in malignant germ cells in vitro or ex vivo. Interestingly, inhibition of Nodal signalling in vitro reduced the expression of pluripotency factors and Nodal pathway genes, while stimulation of the pathway increased their expression. However, cisplatin-sensitivity was not affected following pharmacological inhibition of Nodal/Activin signalling or siRNA-mediated knockdown of the obligate co-receptor CRIPTO in NTera2 cells in vitro or in a xenograft model. Conclusion: Our findings suggest that the Nodal signalling pathway may be involved in regulating pluripotency factor expression in malignant germ cells, but manipulation of the pathway does not appear to affect cisplatin-sensitivity or tumour cell proliferation.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Harpelunde Poulsen, K.","Nielsen, J. E.","Grønkær Toft, B.","Joensen, Ulla Nordström","Rasmussen, Lene Juel","Blomberg Jensen, M.","Mitchell, R. T.","Juul, Anders","Rajpert-De Meyts, E.","Jorgensen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-430680"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Edinburgh"],"keyword":["Testicular cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of nodal signalling on pluripotency factor expression tumour cell proliferation and cisplatin sensitivity in testicular germ cell tumours","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-430680","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7181506","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32326899","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85084031253","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-3e54273b-50aa-4ee4-bfc4-c82b7d88230f"],"keyword":["Cisplatin-sensitivity","Expression of pluripotency factors","GCNIS","Nodal and Activin signalling","Testicular cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1478F4A2AF65C665204596D90B7ECDF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/243007378/s12885_020_06820_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Urology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of edinburgh","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Edinburgh","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"K.","key":"harpelundepoulsenpau","last":"Harpelunde Poulsen","name":"Harpelunde Poulsen, K.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"J. E.","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, J. E.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"B.","key":"grønkærtoftpau","last":"Grønkær Toft","name":"Grønkær Toft, B.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"U. N.","key":"joensenpau","last":"Joensen","locid":"8df5abc2-4b6f-462e-b702-5079bdf76876","name":"Joensen, Ulla Nordström","name_org":"Joensen, U. N.","orcid":"0000-0001-5400-4531","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"L. J.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"54d5267c-3c91-45bc-ace5-1d0edb1b250d","name":"Rasmussen, Lene Juel","name_org":"Rasmussen, L. J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M.","key":"blombergjensenpau","last":"Blomberg Jensen","name":"Blomberg Jensen, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"R. T.","key":"mitchellpau","last":"Mitchell","name":"Mitchell, R. T.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A.","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","name_org":"Juul, A.","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"E.","key":"rajpertdemeytspau","last":"Rajpert-De Meyts","name":"Rajpert-De Meyts, E.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"A.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"46015f76-041c-4177-aa3a-8bcfd13eda19","name":"Jorgensen, Anders","name_org":"Jørgensen, A.","orcid":"0000-0001-6012-6965","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32326899"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12885-020-06820-6","issn":["14712407"],"issue":"1","journal":"BMC Cancer","paperid":"349","status":"p","title":"BMC Cancer","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85084031253"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-3e54273b-50aa-4ee4-bfc4-c82b7d88230f"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Influence of Nodal signalling on pluripotency factor expression, tumour cell proliferation and cisplatin-sensitivity in testicular germ cell tumours","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-430680","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this study was to compare the sensitivity of self-collected versus healthcare worker (HCW)-collected swabs for Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2 (SARS-CoV-2) testing. Symptomatic individuals referred for SARS-CoV-2 testing were invited to provide mobile-phone video-instructed self-collected oropharyngeal and nasal samples followed by a HCW-collected oropharyngeal sample. All samples were sent for analysis to the same microbiology laboratory, and the number of SARS-CoV-2-positive participants in the two tests was compared. A total of 109 participants were included, and 19 participants had SARS-CoV-2-positive results. The diagnostic sensitivity of the self-collected and HCW-collected swabs was 84.2% and 89.5%, respectively, with an acceptable agreement, Cohens kappa 0.82, p < 0.001. Further, results from a questionnaire answered by the participants found that loss of smell as a self-reported symptom was a strong predictor for a SARS-CoV-2-positive test. In conclusion, we found that self-collected oropharyngeal and nasal swabs for SARS-CoV-2 testing can be reliable compared to HCW-collected oropharyngeal samples.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Therchilsen, Johan H.","von Buchwald, Christian","Koch, Anders","Nielsen, Susanne Dam","Rasmussen, Daniel B.","Thudium, Rebekka Faber","Kirkby, Nikolai S.","Raaschou-Pedersen, Daniel E.T.","Bundgaard, Johan S.","Iversen, Kasper","Bundgaard, Henning","Todsen, Tobias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-489314"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Covid 19","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"self collected versus healthcare worker collected swabs in the diagnosis of severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 000000000002","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics10090678","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-489314","identifier":[{"id":"85090858275","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7554687","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32916801","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-a05a8c05-dc29-4e05-b247-fc2fd59f73b0"],"keyword":["COVID-19","COVID-19 diagnostic testing","Severe acute respiratory syndrome coronavirus 2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-868E2340AC75E15C36180307AFB0120A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/diagnostics10090678","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/250068696/Self_Collected_versus_Healthcare_Worker_Collected_Swabs_in_the_Diagnosis_of_Severe_Acute_Respiratory_Syndrome_Coronavirus_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Otorhinolaryngology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Johan H.","key":"therchilsenjohanhpau","last":"Therchilsen","name":"Therchilsen, Johan H.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldchristianpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kochanderspau","last":"Koch","locid":"67a64c38-b855-4715-a55b-1f62133b2f0e","name":"Koch, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Susanne Dam","key":"nielsensusannedampau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"2baa36fa-2709-482a-9595-52c5b9537801","name":"Nielsen, Susanne Dam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel B.","key":"rasmussendanielbpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Daniel B.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rebekka Faber","key":"thudiumrebekkafaberpau","last":"Thudium","name":"Thudium, Rebekka Faber","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nikolai S.","key":"kirkbynikolaispau","last":"Kirkby","name":"Kirkby, Nikolai S.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Daniel E.T.","key":"raaschoupedersendanieletpau","last":"Raaschou-Pedersen","name":"Raaschou-Pedersen, Daniel E.T.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Johan S.","key":"bundgaardjohanspau","last":"Bundgaard","name":"Bundgaard, Johan S.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"iversenkasperpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"558df261-ca9f-440a-8bee-7d38813c253f","name":"Iversen, Kasper","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henning","key":"bundgaardhenningpau","last":"Bundgaard","locid":"254c7f8d-79dd-4a5d-870f-3ed78cb56464","name":"Bundgaard, Henning","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Tobias","key":"todsentobiaspau","last":"Todsen","locid":"16d5c332-f162-4f76-aa1c-b0306b8222e2","name":"Todsen, Tobias","orcid":"0000-0003-3267-3560","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32916801"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/diagnostics10090678","issn":["20754418"],"issue":"9","journal":"Diagnostics","paperid":"678","status":"p","title":"Diagnostics","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090858275"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a05a8c05-dc29-4e05-b247-fc2fd59f73b0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Self-Collected versus Healthcare Worker-Collected Swabs in the Diagnosis of Severe Acute Respiratory Syndrome Coronavirus 2","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-489314","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The purpose of this study is to test if functional multiparametric imaging with 18F-FDG-PET/MRI correlates spatially with immunohistochemical biomarker status within a lesion of head and neck squamous cell carcinoma (HNSCC), and also whether a biopsy with the highest FDG uptake was more likely to have the highest PD-L1 expression or the highest percentage of vital tumour cells (VTC) compared with a random biopsy. METHODS: Thirty-one patients with HNSCC were scanned on an integrated PET/MRI scanner with FDG prior to surgery in this prospective study. Imaging was quantified with SUV, ADC and Ktrans. A 3D-morphometric MRI scan of the specimen was used to co-register the patient and the specimen scans. All specimens were sectioned in consecutive slices, and slices from six different locations were selected randomly from each tumour. Core biopsies were performed to construct TMA blocks for IHC staining with the ten predefined biomarkers. The spatial correlation was assessed with a partial correlation analysis. RESULTS: Twenty-eight patients with a total of 33 lesions were eligible for further analysis. There were significant correlations between the three imaging biomarkers and some of the IHC biomarkers. Moreover, a biopsy taken from the most FDG-avid part of the tumour did not have a statistically significantly higher probability of higher PD-L1 expression or VTC, compared with a random biopsy. CONCLUSION: We found statistically significant correlations between functional imaging parameters and key molecular cancer markers.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jacob H","Olin, Anders B.","Lelkaitis, Giedrius","Hansen, Adam Espe","Andersen, Flemming Littrup","Johannesen, Helle H","Kjaer, Andreas","Vogelius, Ivan R.","Specht, Lena","Bentzen, Søren M.","Wessel, Irene","von Buchwald, Christian","Fischer, Barbara Malene"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"does multiparametric imaging with sup 000000000018 sup f fdg pet mri capture spatial variation in immunohistochemical cancer biomarkers in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-0876-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-526065","identifier":[{"id":"85085070256","type":"scopus"},{"id":"32382113","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC7341803","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-de0322d6-dd6b-47b5-a954-d1139ff69f4a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7E0461020550C8E07A42E2E04724AD14"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/s41416-020-0876-9","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/284654097/Does_multiparametric_imaging_with_18F_FDG_PET_MRI_capture_spatial_variation_in_immunohistochemical_cancer_biomarkers_in_head_and_neck_squamous_cell_carcinoma_publisher_version_.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Biomedical Sciences, Cluster for Molecular Imaging"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Jacob H","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jacob H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","locid":"d81d9238-eddc-4496-b609-4e95fafdd9c3","name":"Olin, Anders B.","name_org":"Olin, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Giedrius","key":"lelkaitispau","last":"Lelkaitis","locid":"f7aba425-cebc-418e-a5f5-99a6e1ad6c16","name":"Lelkaitis, Giedrius","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"b36de088-99f8-4b75-bef2-96150f50a6e7","name":"Hansen, Adam Espe","name_org":"Hansen, Adam E","orcid":"0000-0002-6457-1537","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Flemming L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"abbdc93c-3b5b-4a18-a96f-3be1e9e7da09","name":"Andersen, Flemming Littrup","name_org":"Andersen, Flemming L","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Helle H","key":"johannesenpau","last":"Johannesen","name":"Johannesen, Helle H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Andreas","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"23e31554-6330-4153-9443-43d6e2951b3d","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","name_org":"Kjær, Andreas","orcid":"0000-0002-2706-5547","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ivan R","key":"vogeliuspau","last":"Vogelius","locid":"66f4607a-ae94-4767-aaf0-79279bb24c31","name":"Vogelius, Ivan R.","name_org":"Vogelius, Ivan R","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Søren M","key":"bentzenpau","last":"Bentzen","locid":"fbb03c8f-3547-4eb0-a2af-1f9302471149","name":"Bentzen, Søren M.","name_org":"Bentzen, Søren M","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Irene","key":"wesselpau","last":"Wessel","name":"Wessel, Irene","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"vonbuchwaldpau","last":"von Buchwald","locid":"fc76b0d1-1263-48f7-a4d0-685e60bbc1b6","name":"von Buchwald, Christian","orcid":"0000-0001-6753-8129","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Barbara M","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","locid":"a87f805a-ba44-45e2-b257-59a6f2976711","name":"Fischer, Barbara Malene","name_org":"Fischer, Barbara M","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32382113"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41416-020-0876-9","issn":["00070920","15321827"],"issn_org":["00070920"],"issue":"1","journal":"British Journal of Cancer","pages":"46-53","status":"p","title":"British Journal of Cancer","volume":"123"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85085070256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-de0322d6-dd6b-47b5-a954-d1139ff69f4a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Does multiparametric imaging with <sup>18</sup>F-FDG-PET/MRI capture spatial variation in immunohistochemical cancer biomarkers in head and neck squamous cell carcinoma?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-526065","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"To get estimators that work within a certain error bound with high probability, a common strategy is to design one that works with constant probability, and then boost the probability using independent repetitions. Important examples of this approach are small space algorithms for estimating the number of distinct elements in a stream, or estimating the set similarity between large sets. Using standard strongly universal hashing to process each element, we get a sketch based estimator where the probability of a too large error is, say, 1/4. By performing $r$ independent repetitions and taking the median of the estimators, the error probability falls exponentially in $r$. However, running $r$ independent experiments increases the processing time by a factor $r$. Here we make the point that if we have a hash function with strong concentration bounds, then we get the same high probability bounds without any need for repetitions. Instead of $r$ independent sketches, we have a single sketch that is $r$ times bigger, so the total space is the same. However, we only apply a single hash function, so we save a factor $r$ in time, and the overall algorithms just get simpler. Fast practical hash functions with strong concentration bounds were recently proposed by Aamand {\\em et al.} (to appear in {\\em STOC 2020}). Using their hashing schemes, the algorithms thus become very fast and practical, suitable for online processing of high volume data streams.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Aamand, Anders","Das, Debarati","Kipouridis, Evangelos","Houen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-527843"],"filters":{"added":"2022-03","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"no repetition fast streaming with highly concentrated hashing","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257869915/2004.01156.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-527843","ids":["ku-e0f2fb83-e01c-40e0-a632-4fc6371c4709"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-0941988655025F94E44C2B3D829490E8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Andet","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/257869915/2004.01156.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","locid":"9a5990a0-c966-4fe5-97d0-a65ea981a0a7","name":"Aamand, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Debarati","key":"daspau","last":"Das","locid":"16386c6d-a673-47ce-9579-6bdee2a2baa1","name":"Das, Debarati","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Evangelos","key":"kipouridispau","last":"Kipouridis","locid":"6d34bf14-8110-412c-909a-eb3b0516df7a","name":"Kipouridis, Evangelos","orcid":"0000-0002-5830-5830","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jakob Bæk Tejs","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","locid":"6c81a8c1-02dc-431a-b0b5-cbd75ba533ee","name":"Houen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","name_org":"Knudsen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter Michael Reichstein","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ca3d1668-64f4-4f81-92ed-9d7e18be5f43","name":"Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","orcid":"0000-0001-9219-8410","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mikkel","key":"thoruppau","last":"Thorup","locid":"9a753f32-9b71-4058-8b1e-a94b71903f10","name":"Thorup, Mikkel","orcid":"0000-0001-5237-1709","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"10","publisher":"arxiv.org","publisher_org":"arXiv.org","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e0f2fb83-e01c-40e0-a632-4fc6371c4709"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"No Repetition : Fast Streaming with Highly Concentrated Hashing","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-527843","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Stinne Eika","Østgård, René Drage","Keller, Kresten Krarup","Rasmussen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-668186"],"filters":{"added":"2023-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inflammatorisk rygsygdom","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/inflammatorisk-rygsygdom","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-668186","ids":["au-5c0898ae-9682-4af0-b4d2-5aa784816f88"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-DAE29CBDC2D9D3CD00F85F9A61D1BE1D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://ugeskriftet.dk/videnskab/inflammatorisk-rygsygdom","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Clinical Skills Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stinne Eika","key":"rasmussenstinneeikapau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3b272082-d553-47f0-b02f-d2701c63674d","name":"Rasmussen, Stinne Eika","orcid":"0009-0001-4306-6654","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"René Drage","key":"østgårdrenédragepau","last":"Østgård","locid":"55d0f083-27c9-4d6b-95d4-92ec4d785e87","name":"Østgård, René Drage","orcid":"0000-0001-6124-8972","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kresten Krarup","key":"kellerkrestenkraruppau","last":"Keller","locid":"a13c7405-9555-41cf-9bc3-311bb925bb9c","name":"Keller, Kresten Krarup","orcid":"0000-0003-2474-3389","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenanderspau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00415782","13994174"],"issn_org":["00415782"],"journal":"Ugeskrift for Læger","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Ugeskrift for Læger","volume":"V09190502"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85126927231"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5c0898ae-9682-4af0-b4d2-5aa784816f88"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Inflammatorisk rygsygdom","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-668186","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Human skin microbiota has been described as a \"microbial fingerprint\" due to observed differences between individuals. Current understanding of the cutaneous microbiota is based on sampling the outermost layers of the epidermis, while the microbiota in the remaining skin layers has not yet been fully characterized. Environmental conditions can vary drastically between the cutaneous compartments and give rise to unique communities. We demonstrate that the dermal microbiota is surprisingly similar among individuals and contains a specific subset of the epidermal microbiota. Variability in bacterial community composition decreased significantly from the epidermal to the dermal compartment but was similar among anatomic locations (hip and knee). The composition of the epidermal microbiota was more strongly affected by environmental factors than that of the dermal community. These results indicate a well-conserved dermal community that is functionally distinct from the epidermal community, challenging the current dogma. Future studies in cutaneous disorders and chronic infections may benefit by focusing on the dermal microbiota as a persistent microbial community.IMPORTANCE Human skin microbiota is thought to be unique according to the individual's lifestyle and genetic predisposition. This is true for the epidermal microbiota, while our findings demonstrate that the dermal microbiota is universal between healthy individuals. The preserved dermal microbial community is compositionally unique and functionally distinct to the specific environment in the depth of human skin. It is expected to have direct contact with the immune response of the human host, and research in the communication between host and microbiota should be targeted to this cutaneous compartment. This novel insight into specific microbial adaptation can be used advantageously in the research of chronic disorders and infections of the skin. It can enlighten the alteration between health and disease to the benefit of patients suffering from long-lasting socioeconomic illnesses.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Bay, Lene","Barnes, Christopher James","Fritz, Blaine Gabriel","Thorsen, Jonathan","Restrup, Marlene Elise Møller","Rasmussen, Linett","Sørensen, Johan Kløvgaard","Hesselvig, Anne Brun","Odgaard, Anders","Hansen, Anders Johannes","Bjarnsholt, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-778396"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["16S rRNA genes","DNA sequencing","Dermal microbiota","Skin biopsies","Skin microbiome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"universal dermal microbiome in human skin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mBio.02945-19","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-778396","identifier":[{"id":"32047129","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85079339449","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7018652","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9144279a-c027-4365-8aee-4ddfa42baa9a"],"keyword":["16S rRNA genes","DNA sequencing","cutaneous compartments","dermal microbiota","dry habitat","skin biopsies","skin microbiome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-17CD10F70F614645F646D4BDE6521BA5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/236721356/mBio_2020_Bay_e02945_19.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/mBio.02945-19","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Bacteriology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Lene","key":"baypau","last":"Bay","locid":"22f49c41-e569-43c4-8978-94bc9e411869","name":"Bay, Lene","orcid":"0000-0002-4164-5900","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christopher James","key":"barnespau","last":"Barnes","locid":"369a0b39-cf9f-4240-b9b4-4eb69c878bcd","name":"Barnes, Christopher James","orcid":"0000-0001-6800-4233","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Blaine Gabriel","key":"fritzpau","last":"Fritz","locid":"c5199670-8c56-436d-ad51-c17f0a652973","name":"Fritz, Blaine Gabriel","orcid":"0000-0002-2085-894X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jonathan","key":"thorsenpau","last":"Thorsen","locid":"aea325d8-ff2c-43d7-8898-acc3a2846aa3","name":"Thorsen, Jonathan","orcid":"0000-0003-0200-0461","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marlene Elise Møller","key":"restruppau","last":"Restrup","name":"Restrup, Marlene Elise Møller","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Linett","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0543380d-1a58-4cdf-b490-9c1861185f30","name":"Rasmussen, Linett","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Johan Kløvgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Johan Kløvgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anne Brun","key":"hesselvigpau","last":"Hesselvig","name":"Hesselvig, Anne Brun","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"odgaardpau","last":"Odgaard","locid":"33eeba1f-407c-4aa4-bf69-5efb12863f82","name":"Odgaard, Anders","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Johannes","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"846e4329-bfc5-4ddb-968c-445cdb16825a","name":"Hansen, Anders Johannes","orcid":"0000-0002-1890-2702","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"bjarnsholtpau","last":"Bjarnsholt","locid":"cb3ccb7d-0415-40e5-9bba-c9bc26b6316d","name":"Bjarnsholt, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-8003-7414","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32047129"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1128/mbio.02945-19","issn":["21507511","21612129"],"issn_org":["21612129"],"issue":"1","journal":"mBio","paperid":"e02945-19","status":"p","title":"mBio","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85079339449"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-9144279a-c027-4365-8aee-4ddfa42baa9a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Universal Dermal Microbiome in Human Skin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-778396","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Detektorarkæologien på Lolland og Falster bringer i disse år talrige vidnesbyrd om tidligere tiders liv og levned frem i dagens lys. Bevæbnede med metaldetektorer hjælper lokale amatørarkæologiske ildsjæle med til at dokumentere og synliggøre de dele af vores fælles kulturarv, som under normale omstændigheder ellers ville ligge usete i mulden på marker og enge. Her er det ofte muligheden for at gøre et godt fund, som er drivkraften. Et enkelt ‘bip’ eller udsving fra metaldetektoren, der signalerer, at der ligger noget skjult under den fugtige jord. Et fund, som måske kan bidrage til vores viden om forhistorien. Denne artikel handler om netop sådanne spændende oldsager - skønne ting fra gamle dage.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-830402"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Lolland Falster","Metaldetektor","Oldtiden"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-KUM"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-KUM"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"spændende detektorfund fra lolland og falster","src":["kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","text":"Undefined","type":"url","url":"https://aabne-samlinger.dk/media/724411/mlf_2016_jan_ar.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-830402","ids":["kum-9ef35a01-268b-428f-b17d-1f34f0c138a4"],"keyword":["Lolland-Falster","Metaldetektor","Oldtiden"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7DB43C563760D7EA6D369902A397A2D4"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kum ministry of culture archives museums and royal library denmark","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-KUM","l3nn":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark","namevar":["Ministry of Culture Denmark, Museum Lolland-Falster"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-KUM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"831558a0-727f-45a9-bbbb-8f8b30058802","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6769-9122","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"X"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Undefined"]},"sid":["kum-9ef35a01-268b-428f-b17d-1f34f0c138a4"],"src":["KUM Ministry of Culture - Archives, Museums, and Royal Library Denmark"],"title":"Spændende detektorfund fra Lolland og Falster","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-830402","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Background: Intensive care unit (ICU)-acquired delirium is frequent and associated with poor short- and long-term outcomes for patients in ICUs. It therefore constitutes a major healthcare problem. Despite limited evidence, haloperidol is the most frequently used pharmacological intervention against ICU-acquired delirium. Agents intervening against Delirium in the ICU (AID-ICU) is an international, multicentre, randomised, blinded, placebo-controlled trial investigates benefits and harms of treatment with haloperidol in patients with ICU-acquired delirium. The current pre-planned one-year follow-up study of the AID-ICU trial population aims to explore the effects of haloperidol on one-year mortality and health related quality of life (HRQoL). Methods : The AID-ICU trial will include 1000 participants. One-year mortality will be obtained from the trial sites; we will validate the vital status of Danish participants using the Danish National Health Data Registers. Mortality will be analysed by Cox-regression and visualized by Kaplan-Meier curves tested for significance using the log-rank test. We will obtain HRQoL data using the EQ-5D instrument. HRQoL analysis will be performed using a general linear model adjusted for stratification variables. Deceased participants will be designated the worst possible value. Results: We expect to publish results of this study in 2022. Conclusion: We expect that this one-year follow-up study of participants with ICU-acquired delirium allocated to haloperidol vs. placebo will provide important information on the long-term consequences of delirium including the effects of haloperidol. We expect that our results will improve the care of this vulnerable patient group.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Mortensen, Camilla B.","Poulsen, Lone M.","Andersen-Ranberg, Nina C.","Perner, Anders","Lange, Theis","Estrup, S Stine","Ebdrup, Bjørn H.","Egerod, Ingrid","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Hästbacka, Johanna","Caballero, Jesús","Ci