9324"],"journal":"Climate of the Past","pages":"1565-1580","status":"p","title":"Climate of the Past","volume":"16"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85094944715"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-5efc10ca-3761-4c08-9cf8-2893d2a88fd9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Bipolar volcanic synchronization of abrupt climate change in Greenland and Antarctic ice cores during the last glacial period","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-450288","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Previous work on tabulation hashing by PÇtraşcu and Thorup from STOC'11 on simple tabulation and from SODA'13 on twisted tabulation offered Chernoff-style concentration bounds on hash based sums, e.g., the number of balls/keys hashing to a given bin, but under some quite severe restrictions on the expected values of these sums. The basic idea in tabulation hashing is to view a key as consisting of c=O(1) characters, e.g., a 64-bit key as c=8 characters of 8-bits. The character domain ς should be small enough that character tables of size |ς| fit in fast cache. The schemes then use O(1) tables of this size, so the space of tabulation hashing is O(|ς|). However, the concentration bounds by PÇtraşcu and Thorup only apply if the expected sums are g‰ |ς|. To see the problem, consider the very simple case where we use tabulation hashing to throw n balls into m bins and want to analyse the number of balls in a given bin. With their concentration bounds, we are fine if n=m, for then the expected value is 1. However, if m=2, as when tossing n unbiased coins, the expected value n/2 is ≫ |ς| for large data sets, e.g., data sets that do not fit in fast cache. To handle expectations that go beyond the limits of our small space, we need a much more advanced analysis of simple tabulation, plus a new tabulation technique that we call tabulation-permutation hashing which is at most twice as slow as simple tabulation. No other hashing scheme of comparable speed offers similar Chernoff-style concentration bounds.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Aamand, Anders","Houen, Jakob Bæk Tejs","Knudsen, Mathias Bæk Tejs","Rasmussen, Peter Michael Reichstein","Thorup, Mikkel"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-460189"],"event":{"acronym":"STOC","end":"2020-06-26","place":"Chicago, us","start":"2020-06-22","title":"52nd Annual ACM SIGACT Symposium on Theory of Computing, STOC 2020","year":"2020"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Concentration Bounds","Hashing","Sampling","Streaming algorithms"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["SupWiz"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fast hashing with strong concentration bounds","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3357713.3384259","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-460189","identifier":[{"id":"85086766216","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-6fb53196-f1d0-4037-bad0-29d099578c83"],"keyword":["Chernoff bounds","Concentration bounds","Hashing","Sampling","Streaming algorithms"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-10C7AE46D2F0BD9B3604857B2DC50702"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3357713.3384259","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/258498062/Fast_Hashing_with_Strong_Concentration_Bounds.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Algorithms and Complexity"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","na