{"abstract":"Rapporten rummer en systematisk sammenfatning af tidligere undersøgelser af sammenhængen mellem brug af digitale skærmmedier og henholdsvis daglig fysisk aktivitet og stillesiddende tid blandt børn og unge. Ligeledes er formålet at sammenfatte undersøgelser, der har undersøgt betydningen af brug af aktiv skærmtid (exergaming) for børn og unges daglige fysiske aktivitet og stillesiddende tid. Begrebet aktiv skærmtid dækker over en type af computerspil, der er udviklet til at integrere fysisk aktivitet ind i spillet, og det rummer derved et potentiale for at fremme børn og unges fysiske aktivitet. Litteraturgennemgangen er gennemført for Sundhedsstyrelsen af Institut for Idræt og Biomekanik, Syddansk Universitet, Odense.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Olesen, Line Grønholt","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-616787"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"sammenhængen mellem skærmtid og fysisk aktivitet og stillesiddende tid hos børn en systematisk litteraturgennemgang","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178796630/Skaermtid_og_hhv_fysisk_aktivitet_og_stillesiddende_tid.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-616787","ids":["sdu-982320c0-8448-4b90-b697-c01cc71991a0"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-80C891EBAAE2F48208E0FBE755FBC94F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sst.dk/da/Udgivelser/2020/Sammenhaengen-mellem-skaermtid-og-fysisk-aktivitet-og-stillesiddende-tid-hos-boern","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/178796630/Skaermtid_og_hhv_fysisk_aktivitet_og_stillesiddende_tid.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, RICH - Research In Childhood Health","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Grønholt","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"e9ad7180-8cce-4e88-9707-18dedc4c73e0","name":"Olesen, Line Grønholt","orcid":"0000-0002-6588-8878","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Lund","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"751d26de-66d4-4ef9-8183-880c48c96dc7","name":"Kristensen, Peter Lund","orcid":"0000-0002-5666-9614","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"8b86a1ef-e6c1-4de3-8300-e30d144bbf60","name":"Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","name_org":"Rasmussen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-2114-2185","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"grøntvedpau","last":"Grøntved","locid":"393b1ca1-e658-437c-9ca3-73aea925ad58","name":"Grøntved, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1584-679X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"116","place":"Odense","publisher":"Forskningsenheden Exercise Epidemiology & Center for Forskning i Børn og Unges Sundhed (RICH). Institut for Idræt og Biomekanik, Syddansk Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-982320c0-8448-4b90-b697-c01cc71991a0"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Sammenhængen mellem skærmtid og fysisk aktivitet og stillesiddende tid hos børn : en systematisk litteraturgennemgang","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-616787","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Children with cerebral palsy often exhibit an altered gait pattern; however, it is uncertain whether the use of an instrumented gait analysis in interdisciplinary interventions affects the perceived experience of family-centered service (FCS) and/or gross motor function. The aim of this study is to investigate whether individually tailored interdisciplinary interventions, based on an instrumented gait analysis report, has a superior effectiveness on perceived FCS and gross motor function in children with cerebral palsy, compared to 'care as usual' without the use of instrumented gait analysis. Furthermore, to investigate potential associations between perceived FCS and gross motor function improvement with the goal of improving future therapy on gross motor function. METHOD: This is a sequel analysis on tertiary outcome measures from a prospective, single blind, randomized, parallel group study including two groups of 30 children aged 5-8 years with spastic cerebral palsy at Gross Motor Function Classification System levels I-II (n = 60). The intervention group underwent a three-dimensional gait analysis, from which a clinical report was written with recommendations on interdisciplinary interventions, such as physical therapy, orthopedic surgery, orthotics or spasticity management. To assess effectiveness on perceived FCS and gross motor function, at baseline, 26 weeks and 52 weeks, the five domains in the Measure of Processes of Care (MPOC-20) (Enabling and partnership, Providing general information, Providing specific information about the child, Respectful and supportive service, and Coordinated and comprehensive care) and the Gross Motor Function Measurement (GMFM-66) were used as outcome measures. RESULTS: No significant differences in between-group change scores in any of the five MPOC-20 domains were observed (p = 0.40-0.97). In favor of the intervention group a significantly higher between-group change score in GMFM-66 (mean difference: 3.05 [95%CI: 1.12-4.98], p = 0.003) after 52 weeks was observed. CONCLUSION: The addition of an instrumented gait analysis report to 'care as usual' did not improve the parents' perceptions of FCS in treatment of children with cerebral palsy. However, superior improvement in the GMFM-66 was observed in the intervention group, suggesting meaningful gross motor function improvement. TRIAL REGISTRATION: Clinical Trials, NCT02160457 . Registered June 10th 2014.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fonvig, Christina Esmann","Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","Overgaard, Søren","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635588"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","Cerebral parese","GMFM 66","Instrumented gait analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effectiveness of instrumented gait analysis in interdisciplinary interventions on parents perception of family centered service and on gross motor function in children with cerebral palsy a randomized controlled trial","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-020-02315-2","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635588","identifier":[{"id":"PMC7461340","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32873289","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85090181536","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d9c88aa9-f220-45ae-a9cf-5f260a4f2e2a"],"keyword":["Cerebral palsy","Cerebral parese","Familie centreret tilgang","Family-centered service","GMFM-66","Gang analyse","Instrumented gait analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B58382850554567DFA1C757C1BE4C36B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/173032770/s12887_020_02315_2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-020-02315-2","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"esmannfonvigpau","last":"Esmann Fonvig","locid":"d9425e27-e948-4ed2-96e0-0c3157680896","name":"Fonvig, Christina Esmann","name_org":"Esmann Fonvig, Christina","orcid":"0000-0001-8978-7433","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Mätzke","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fc740e3e-3a84-4904-bd04-4db023a123db","name":"Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","orcid":"0000-0002-7522-8144","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Soren","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"b394ea8b-39e4-46bc-8651-f6321e37c2eb","name":"Overgaard, Søren","name_org":"Overgaard, Soren","orcid":"0000-0001-6829-4787","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["32873289"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12887-020-02315-2","issn":["14712431"],"journal":"BMC Pediatrics","paperid":"411","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"BMC Pediatrics","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85090181536"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d9c88aa9-f220-45ae-a9cf-5f260a4f2e2a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Effectiveness of instrumented gait analysis in interdisciplinary interventions on parents’ perception of family-centered service and on gross motor function in children with cerebral palsy: a randomized controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-635588","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Først i nyere tid er man blevet bevidst om, at det kunne være en vanskelighed at finde en begyndelse i filosofien, og både grunden til denne vanskelighed og muligheden for at løse den er blevet diskuteret på mangfoldig vis. Begyndelsen i filosofien må enten være noget formidlet eller noget umiddelbart, og det er let at vise, at begyndelsen hverken kan være det ene eller det andet. Hermed møder den ene eller den anden begyndelsesmåde sin gendrivelse.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jesper Lundsfryd","Poulsen, Anders Hee Nørbjerg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-697022"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Freiburg"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oversættelse af hegel hvormed må videnskabens begyndelse gøres 000000001832","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/res_cogitans/article/download/123666/170662/","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-697022","ids":["sdu-2fe1ba21-f1bb-463b-8db0-7f405040effd"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-182680FEC69CE9B35E183158F8FD66CA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/res_cogitans/article/view/123666","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/res_cogitans/article/download/123666/170662/","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of freiburg","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Freiburg","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture, Philosophy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Lundsfryd","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jesper Lundsfryd","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Hee Nørbjerg","key":"poulsenpau","last":"Poulsen","locid":"b8a87573-019a-46ef-a81d-3a95908a5b63","name":"Poulsen, Anders Hee Nørbjerg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["16038509"],"issue":"3","journal":"Res Cogitans","pages":"76-88","publisher":"Syddansk Universitet","status":"p","title":"Res Cogitans","volume":"14"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2fe1ba21-f1bb-463b-8db0-7f405040effd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Oversættelse af Hegel: \"Hvormed må videnskabens begyndelse gøres?\" (1832)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-697022","year":"2020","yearsub":"2020"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Background: The screen-media landscape has changed drastically during the last decade with wide-scale ownership and use of new portable touchscreen-based devices plausibly causing changes in the volume of screen media use and the way children and young people entertain themselves and communicate with friends and family members. This rapid development is not sufficiently mirrored in available tools for measuring children’s screen media use. The aim of this study was to develop and evaluate a parent-reported standardized questionnaire to assess 6–10-year old children’s multiple screen media use and habits, their screen media environment, and its plausible proximal correlates based on a suggested socio-ecological model. Methods: An iterative process was conducted developing the SCREENS questionnaire. Informed by the literature, media experts and end-users, a conceptual framework was made to guide the development of the questionnaire. Parents and media experts evaluated face and content validity. Pilot and field testing in the target group was conducted to assess test-retest reliability using Kappa statistics and intraclass correlation coefficients (ICC). Construct validity of relevant items was assessed using pairwise non-parametric correlations (Spearman’s). The SCREENS questionnaire is based on a multidimensional and formative model. Results: The SCREENS questionnaire covers six domains validated to be important factors of screen media use in children and comprises 19 questions and 92 items. Test-retest reliability (n = 37 parents) for continuous variables was moderate to substantial with ICC’s ranging from 0.67 to 0.90. For relevant nominal and ordinal data, kappa values were all above 0.50 with more than 80% of the values above 0.61 indicating good test-retest reliability. Internal consistency between two different time use variables (from n = 243) showed good correlations with rho ranging from 0.59 to 0.66. Response-time was within 15 min for all participants. Conclusions: SCREENS-Q is a comprehensive tool to assess children’s screen media habits, the screen media environment and possible related correlates. It is a feasible questionnaire with multiple validated constructs and moderate to substantial test-retest reliability of all evaluated items. The SCREENS-Q is a promising tool to investigate children screen media use. Keywords: Screen-media use, Children, Questionnaire, Correlates * Correspondence: hklakk@health.sdu.dk Heidi Klakk and Christian Tolstrup Wester shared first authorship 1Research Unit for Exercise Epidemiology, Centre of Research in Childhood Health, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, University of Southern Denmark, 5230 Odense M, Denmark 2Research Center for Applied Health Science, University College Lillebælt, 5230 Odense M, Denmark Klakk et al. BMC Public Health (2020) 20:664 https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-020-08810-6","author_count":8,"contributors":["Klakk, Heidi","Wester, Christian Tolstrup","Olesen, Line Grønholt","Rasmussen, Martin Gillies Banke","Kristensen, Peter Lund","Pedersen, Jesper","Grøntved, Anders"],"cuid":["S03-095.95-049221"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Børn og unge","Children","Correlates","Questionnaire","Screen media use","Spørgeskemaudvikling","Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet","Validering","children and youth","skærmtid"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCS"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the development of a questionnaire to assess leisure time screen based media use and its proximal correlates in children screens q","src":["sdu","ucl","ucsyd"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU","DI-UC-UCL","DI-UC-UCS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-020-08810-6","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-095.95-049221","identifier":[{"id":"85084625428","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC7216486","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"32397984","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-8c02fa4b-84d2-4c71-9e4f-c5724428c113","ucl-a8c821aa-6548-402b-82c8-f9503b9b76cf","ucsyd-e0b585df-2a8f-48a0-92ba-320fe4d3335a"],"keyword":["Børn og unge","Children","Correlates","Questionnaire","Screen-media use","Spørgeskemaudvikling","Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet","Validering","children and youth","skærmtid"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-338DD63ECF4E12B6DF93495039791809"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12889-020-08810-6","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/169842879/s12889_020_08810_6.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2020","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Sports Science and Clinical Biomechanics, Research Unit of Exercise Epidemiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ucl university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-UCL","l3nl":"UCL University College","l3nn":"UCL University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"UCL University College","namevar":["University College Lillebælt"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-UCL",