ecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"I.","key":"zychoripau","last":"Zychor","name":"Zychor, I.","rank":1251,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/1741-4326/ab2276","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"11","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","paperid":"112021","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"59"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85070875113"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-412de8ed-b09a-46d9-b4bf-aa62f2373904"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Overview of the JET preparation for deuterium-tritium operation with the ITER like-wall","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323976","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"The study of the power width in the scrape-off layer (SOL) is very important for the design and operation of ITER. In this paper, a 2D electrostatic turbulence code is employed to study the power width scaling in L-mode plasmas. It is found that the electron and ion turbulent transports dominate the radial heat fluxes, and the electron heat conduction and the ion heat advection dominate the parallel heat flux in the near and far SOL in L-mode plasmas. The simulated SOL power width agrees well with the Eich scaling [T. Eich et al., Nucl. Fusion 53, 093031 (2013)] and the predictions by the heuristic drift-based model [R. J. Goldston, Nucl. Fusion 52, 013009 (2012)] for selected EAST L-mode discharges. A numerical scaling has been performed based on one of these discharges. The scaling dependence on the safety factor is consistent with the Eich scaling and the scaling exponent of the edge electron temperature is close to that in the ASDEX-Upgrade L-mode scaling [B. Sieglin et al., Plasma Phys. Controlled Fusion 58, 055015 (2016)]. The investigation of the obtained numerical scaling for L-mode plasmas reveals that the SOL power width is influenced by the safety factor, the edge electron density, and the edge electron temperature through the parallel heat transports, the radial turbulent heat transports, and both the parallel and radial heat transports, respectively. The formulation of the turbulence model suggests that the scaling dependence on the poloidal magnetic field (or the plasma current) for the experimental scalings is essentially the scaling dependence on the ballooning length, q95R. Based on this idea, a further numerical scaling gives λ-q ∝ q951.30Bt−0.33R1.32 ∝ Bt−0.29(q95R)1.33, which has a strong scaling dependence on the major radius that is different from the Eich scaling.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Liu, X.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Naulin, Volker","Olsen, J.","Xia, T. Y.","Wang, L.","Deng, G. Z.","Wu, X. Q.","Liu, Y.","Wang, Y. M.","Li, Y. Y.","Zhang, Q.","Xu, G. S.","Li, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-354539"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Li, J."],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"study of power width scaling in scrape off layer with 000000000002d electrostatic turbulence code based on east l mode discharges","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.5083063","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-354539","identifier":[{"id":"85064970702","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-a776a51d-14f0-400c-8883-09a3025fe53f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DD6DA7E501E295476E0DA251A7876286"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/175438349/1.5083063.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1063/1.5083063","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"X.","key":"liuxpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, X.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A. H.","key":"nielsenandershenrypau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","name_org":"Nielsen, A. H.","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J. J.","key":"rasmussenjensjuulpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Rasmussen, J. J.","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinvolkerpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"olsenjpau","last":"Olsen","name":"Olsen, J.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"T. Y.","key":"xiatypau","last":"Xia","name":"Xia, T. Y.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"wanglpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, L.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G. Z.","key":"denggzpau","last":"Deng","name":"Deng, G. Z.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"X. Q.","key":"wuxqpau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, X. Q.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y.","key":"liuypau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, Y.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y. M.","key":"wangympau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Y. M.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Y. Y.","key":"liyypau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Y. Y.","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Q.","key":"zhangqpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Q.","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G. S.","key":"xugspau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, G. S.","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"lijpau","last":"Li","name":"Li, J.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/1.5083063","issn":["1070664X","10897674"],"issn_org":["1070664X"],"issue":"4","journal":"Physics of Plasmas","paperid":"042509","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Physics of Plasmas","volume":"26"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064970702"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-a776a51d-14f0-400c-8883-09a3025fe53f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Study of power width scaling in scrape-off layer with 2D electrostatic turbulence code based on EAST L-mode discharges","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-354539","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: Multiparametric imaging holds great potential for characterization of disease heterogeneity. For integrated PET/MR imaging, the combination of 18F-flourodeoxyglucose (FDG) PET and diffusion weighted imaging (DWI) has been suggested for the assessment of tumor heterogeneity. However, PET image resolution is limited and DWI is prone to image distortions. The aim of this study was to assess the influence of PET point spread function (PSF) modelling and DWI distortion correction on the voxelwise correlation between FDG-PET and DWI. METHODS: Data were collected from 11 patients with head and neck cancer, each undergoing PET/MR imaging twice. PET reconstructions with and without PSF modelling and DWI with and without distortion correction were derived. Tumor SUV was compared between PET reconstructions by linear regression. Geometric distortions of DWI with and without distortion correction were quantified by voxelwise correlation coefficients to an undistorted anatomical reference. The influence of PSF modelling and DWI distortion correction on a multiparametric analysis was assessed as a change of the voxelwise correlation coefficient between FDG-PET and DWI measured in tumors. RESULTS: The inclusion of PSF modelling in the PET reconstruction affected tumor quantification by a 10-20% increase in SUV. Distortion correction reduced DWI geometric distortions significantly. The impact of PET PSF modelling on the spatial correlation with DWI was insignificant. However, distortion correction of DWI had a significant effect on the spatial correlation with PET. CONCLUSIONS: Proper preparation of the imaging modalities is important for a correct analysis and interpretation of multiparametric PET/MR imaging of head and neck cancer.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Olin, Anders","Krogager, Louise","Rasmussen, Jacob H","Andersen, Flemming L","Specht, Lena","Beyer, Thomas","Kjaer, Andreas","Fischer, Barbara M","Hansen, Adam E"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-398521"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Diffusion Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Fluorodeoxyglucose F18","Head and Neck Neoplasms diagnostic imaging","Humans","Image Processing Computer Assisted","Multimodal Imaging","Positron Emission Tomography"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"preparing data for multiparametric pet mr imaging influence of pet point spread function modelling and epi distortion correction on the spatial correlation of 000000000018f fdg pet and diffusion weighted mri in head and neck cancer","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejmp.2019.04.006","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-398521","identifier":[{"id":"31151573","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85064249409","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-086e5c49-86b8-490c-89f0-2be24137a478"],"keyword":["Diffusion Magnetic Resonance Imaging","Fluorodeoxyglucose F18","Head and Neck Neoplasms/diagnostic imaging","Humans","Image Processing, Computer-Assisted","Multimodal Imaging","Positron-Emission Tomography"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1DE240C03FFF9EF40987135F1AA674D4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ejmp.2019.04.006","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/237417687/1_s2.0_S1120179719300821_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"olinpau","last":"Olin","name":"Olin, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Louise","key":"krogagerpau","last":"Krogager","name":"Krogager, Louise","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jacob H","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Jacob H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Flemming L","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Flemming L","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Lena","key":"spechtpau","last":"Specht","locid":"30cb94c3-320a-4750-a367-f34b2d98696a","name":"Specht, Lena","orcid":"0000-0002-6902-2190","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"beyerpau","last":"Beyer","name":"Beyer, Thomas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andreas","key":"kjaerpau","last":"Kjaer","name":"Kjaer, Andreas","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Barbara M","key":"fischerpau","last":"Fischer","name":"Fischer, Barbara M","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Adam E","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Adam E","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["31151573"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ejmp.2019.04.006","issn":["11201797","1724191X"],"issn_org":["11201797"],"journal":"Physica Medica","pages":"1-7","status":"p","title":"Physica Medica","volume":"61"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064249409"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-086e5c49-86b8-490c-89f0-2be24137a478"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Preparing data for multiparametric PET/MR imaging : Influence of PET point spread function modelling and EPI distortion correction on the spatial correlation of [18F]FDG-PET and diffusion-weighted MRI in head and neck cancer","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-398521","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Objective: Clinical observations over time of adults with growth hormone (GH) deficiency (GHD) have indicated a shift in patient characteristics at diagnosis. The objective of this study was to compare baseline characteristics of patients diagnosed with adult-onset GHD naive to GH replacement during t hree study periods (1994-1999 (P1), 2000-2004 (P2), and 2005-2012 (P3)) using the KIMS (Pfizer's International Metab olic) database. Methods: Data were retrieved for a total of 6069 patients with adult-on set GHD from six countries (Belgium, Germany, Netherlands, Spain, Sweden, and UK): P1 (n = 1705), P2 (n = 2397), and P3 (n = 1967). Results: The proportions of patients with pituitary/hypothalamic tumors and patients with multiple pituitary hormone deficiencies decreased per entry year period, while the proporti ons with hypertension and diabetes increased. The lag time from diagnosis of pituitary disease to start of GH treatme nt decreased by 2.9 years over the entry year periods. IGF-1 increased by 0.1 standard deviation score per entry year period. Maximum GH following various stimulation tests, BMI, and waist circumference increased. The use of radio therapy, glucocorticoid replacement doses, and the proportion of women >50 years on estrogen replacement therapy decreased. The effects of 1 year of GH replacement were similar over the entry year periods despite changes in the patients' baseline characteristics. An expected increase in fasting blood glucose was seen after 1 year of GH treatment. Conclusions: The degree of confirmed GHD became less pronounced and more pat ients with co-morbidities and diabetes were considered for GH replacement therapy, possibly r eflecting increased knowledge and confidence in GH therapy gained with time.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Höybye, Charlotte","Burman, Pia","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","Hey-Hadavi, Judith","Aydin, Ferah","Camacho-Hubner, Cecilia","Mattsson, Anders F."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-423673"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska Institutet","Pfizer","Skåne University Hospital"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"change in baseline characteristics over 000000000020 years of adults with growth hormone gh deficiency on gh replacement therapy","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-423673","identifier":[{"id":"85076528081","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31590143","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-32ced174-8bdf-4af3-8da8-58b313056f53"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-77D6782B52B49552D33EB70881B6EE74"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2020"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karolinska institutet","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karolinska Institutet","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"skåne university hospital","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Skåne University Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Internal Medicine: Endocrinology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"pfizer","loc":["United St