{"abstract":"A longstanding problem in facility based experiments is the time one must wait whilst changing sample temperature. This issue is most often confronted at cryogenic temperatures above 100 K, where thermal response times can be very slow. These can be drastically reduced by minimising the amount of material being controlled to as little as possible beyond the sample itself. Peltier elements provide an effective way to achieve this, but are mostly used to regulate with respect to room temperature. We report on the Huginn sub-cryostat, a cryostat insert with dual Peltier regulation, useable down to 100 K, that enables large and rapid temperature jumps of up of 10 K to 20 K in minutes or less. Moreover, temperature stability is improved by an order of magnitude in the presence of a variable background temperature.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Jakobsen, Bo","Holmes, Alexander","Rasmussen, Torben Steen","Schneider, Harald","Pettersson, Anders","Hiess, Arno","Niss, Kristine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-563462"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Spallation Source ERIC"],"keyword":["Cryostat","Neutron scattering"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"huginn a peltier based sub cryostat for neutron scattering","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/JNR-180093","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-563462","identifier":[{"id":"85066315317","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ruc-6fc4d0a5-23a7-45e6-950f-fe121551fc23"],"keyword":["Cryostat","Peltier","neutron scattering"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-12E3DE058244FE95625B29383B08B3E4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"loc","url":"https://rucforsk.ruc.dk/ws/files/65052538/jnr_2F2019_2F21_1_2_2Fjnr_21_1_2_jnr180093_2Fjnr_21_jnr180093.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3233/JNR-180093","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Glass and Time","Roskilde University, Department of Science and Environment, Mathematics and Physics (IMFUFA)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"european spallation source eric","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"European Spallation Source ERIC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Bo","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"02589e74-342a-45b9-9fff-4b3b1dfa1d2f","name":"Jakobsen, Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-4018-6431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Alexander","key":"holmespau","last":"Holmes","name":"Holmes, Alexander","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Torben Steen","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"986e5ef0-6109-4231-8a33-e7d7403c20e5","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Steen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Harald","key":"schneiderpau","last":"Schneider","name":"Schneider, Harald","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"petterssonpau","last":"Pettersson","name":"Pettersson, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Arno","key":"hiesspau","last":"Hiess","name":"Hiess, Arno","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Kristine","key":"nisspau","last":"Niss","locid":"0797b4a5-ad6b-48f3-97ff-983274d76a9a","name":"Niss, Kristine","orcid":"0000-0002-9391-0366","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3233/jnr-180093","issn":["10238166","14772655"],"issn_org":["10238166"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Journal of Neutron Research","pages":"47-57","status":"p","title":"Journal of Neutron Research","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85066315317"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-6fc4d0a5-23a7-45e6-950f-fe121551fc23"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"Huginn : A Peltier-based sub-cryostat for neutron scattering","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-563462","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"This workshop is dedicated to discuss and explore the specific interdisciplinary aspects of Bodily human robot interaction, and establish a common ground for this area as a recognized and continued research topic. Bodily interaction with robots and robotic devices is partially established in niche applications such as exoskeletons, assistive devices and advanced machines for physical training where bodily interaction is the application. Bodily interaction is expected to develop a broader role in human robot interaction, for instance in manufacturing and in social and entertainment robotics. The direct exchange of force and motion in bodily interaction create a range of engineering challenges, but also entwine engineering directly with topics that traditionally reside in the realm of health and humanistic science, from biomechanics to human's social responses to the prompting and responses of physical interaction.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Solis, Jorge","Sørensen, Anders Stengaard","Rasmussen, Gitte"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-624132"],"event":{"acronym":"HRI","end":"2019-03-14","place":"Daegu, kr","start":"2019-03-11","title":"14th Annual ACM/IEEE International Conference on Human-Robot Interaction, HRI 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karlstad University"],"keyword":["Assistive devices","Physical training"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"bodily human robot interaction","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85064000808","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-624132","identifier":[{"id":"85064000808","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-b1bbafec-eef2-4029-ad33-dd7423e7b88b"],"keyword":["assistive devices","physical HRI","physical training"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-754C2E3AAEB3FE028DDF911FD02C94F8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"se","key":"karlstad university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Karlstad University","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, The Maersk Mc-Kinney Moller Institute, SDU Health Informatics and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jorge","key":"solispau","last":"Solis","name":"Solis, Jorge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Stengaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"bbd0410a-e7d2-41fd-b535-5702797b1670","name":"Sørensen, Anders Stengaard","orcid":"0000-0003-0184-7281","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gitte","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"02206f50-a2a4-40ae-aee8-8a2fa9713ebb","name":"Rasmussen, Gitte","orcid":"0000-0002-2940-0839","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/hri.2019.8673132","eisbn":["9781538685556","9781538685549"],"isbn":["9781538685563"],"pages":"683-684","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"14th ACM/IEEE International Conference on Human-Robot Interaction (HRI)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85064000808"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-b1bbafec-eef2-4029-ad33-dd7423e7b88b"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bodily Human Robot Interaction","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-624132","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In the Danish retail industry, young workers employed in temporary positions for few hours a week constitutes more than half of the employees. For the main part of the young workers this employment is their first meeting with the labor market, they lack knowledge and awareness of the work environment, and at some workplaces the introduction is limited, ‘ad-hoc’ or ‘fast-track’ [1]. Often the young worker feel only limited involved in decisions regarding their work [2]. It may be beneficial both for short- and long-term performance and security to increase the young workers knowledge of and involvement in the work environment issues, as well as the employer’s awareness on the needs of the young workers.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Limborg, Hans Jørgen","Karstad, Kristina","Albertsen, Karen","Ekner, Dorte","Ørberg, Anders","Grøn, Sisse","Rasmussen, Charlotte Diana Nørregaard","Holtermann, Andreas","Jørgensen, Marie B.","Bagnara, Sebastiano","Tartaglia, Riccardo","Albolino, Sara","Alexander, Thomas","Fujita, Yushi"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-780362"],"event":{"end":"2018-08-28","place":"Florence, it","start":"2018-08-27","title":"The 20th Congress International Ergonomics Association (IEA)","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-OT"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"OT":["Team Arbejdsliv, København, Danmark."]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"juvenile workers or pocketmoney precariat the process and effect of establishing health and safety committees for juvenile workers in danish retail sector","src":["nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-780362","identifier":[{"id":"85051760426","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["nfa-38a7899d-2e36-4fc8-90c3-93ea0319f9c0"],"lang":"E