{"abstract":"In 2008-2009 a tick-borne encephalitis virus (TBEV) micro-focus was detected in Northern Zealand, Denmark. No new cases of TBE with an epidemiological link to Northern Zealand has been reported since. Here we undertook to investigate Ixodus ricinus ticks from this endemic micro-focus in 2016 and 2017. In addition to TBEV, I. ricinus ticks may host other pathogens that include Borrelia spp., Babesia spp., Rickettsia spp. and Neoehrlichia mikurensis, together with various endosymbiont microorganisms. To detect multiple organisms we used a metagenomics PanVirus microarray and next-generation sequencing to examine the persistence and evolution of other emerging viruses, bacteria and parasites. Here we report the rise and fall of the Danish TBEV micro-focus in Northern Zealand. However, we identify for the first time in Danish I. ricinus ticks the presence of Uukuniemi virus in addition to a tick-borne phlebovirus and a range of bacteria.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Petersen, Andreas","Worsøe Rosenstierne, Maiken","Rasmmussen, Morten","Fuursted, Kurt","Nielsen, Henrik Vedel","Andersen, Lee O'Brien","Bødker, Rene","Fomsgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-092.28-038087"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Petersen, Andreas"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Center for Disease Prevention and Control (ECDC)"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Ixodes ricinus","Micro focus","Tick borne encephalitis virus","Uukuniemi virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"field samplings of ixodus ricinus ticks from a tick borne encephalitis virus micro focus in northern zealand denmark","src":["dtu","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/153661730/Field_samplings_of_Ixodus_ricinus_ticks_from_a_tick_borne_encephalitis_virus_micro_focus_in_Northern_Zealand.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["We thank Susanne Lopez Rasmussen, Louise Borup, Randi Thøgersen for technical assistance and Maria Magdalena Lassaunière for editorial assistance. This study is part of the “Metagenomic Array Detection of emerging Virus in EU” (MAD-Vir) project, which is part of the European Joint Programme One Health EJP consortium, which has received funding from the European Union’s Horizon 2020 research and innovation programme under Grant Agreement No 773830 . Appendix A"],"id":"S02-092.28-038087","identifier":[{"id":"85066262911","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31151922","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-f789c347-9d19-42e8-94a6-fa7106dbff35","sdu-e9476c7b-a6db-4b8b-bd27-c82e1c7b0cc3"],"keyword":["Bacteria","Ixodes ricinus","Ixodus ricinus","Uukuniemi virus","micro-focus","tick-borne encephalitis virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AF0578A961314476ED8619FEEC4D740B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/180023288/ansa_1_s2.0_S1877959X18304205_main.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/153661730/Field_samplings_of_Ixodus_ricinus_ticks_from_a_tick_borne_encephalitis_virus_micro_focus_in_Northern_Zealand.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institut