{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Acutely ill adults with hypoxaemic respiratory failure are at risk of life-threatening hypoxia, and thus oxygen is often administered liberally. Excessive oxygen use may, however, increase the number of serious adverse events, including death. Establishing the optimal oxygenation level is important as existing evidence is of low quality. We hypothesise that targeting an arterial partial pressure of oxygen (PaO2 ) of 8 kPa is superior to targeting a PaO2 of 12 kPa in adult intensive care unit (ICU) patients with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure. METHODS: The Handling Oxygenation Targets in the ICU (HOT-ICU) trial is an outcome assessment blinded, multicentre, randomised, parallel-group trial targeting PaO2 in acutely ill adults with hypoxaemic respiratory failure within 12 hours after ICU admission. Patients are randomised 1:1 to one of the two PaO2 targets throughout ICU stay until a maximum of 90 days. The primary outcome is 90-day mortality. Secondary outcomes are serious adverse events in the ICU, days alive without organ support and days alive out of hospital in the 90-day period; mortality, health-related quality-of-life at 1-year follow-up as well as 1-year cognitive and pulmonary function in a subgroup; and an overall health economic analysis. To detect or reject a 20% relative risk reduction, we aim to include 2928 patients. An interim analysis is planned after 90-day follow-up of 1464 patients. CONCLUSION: The HOT-ICU trial will test the hypothesis that a lower oxygenation target reduces 90-day mortality compared with a higher oxygenation target in adult ICU patients with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Perner, Anders","Wetterslev, Jørn","Lange, Theis","Keus, Frederik","Laake, Jon H","Okkonen, Marjatta","Siegemund, Martin","Morgan, Matthew","Thormar, Katrin M","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"cuid":["S02-088.24-004958"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["HOT-ICU Investigators","and the HOT-ICU Investigators"],"keyword":["Critical Illness","Hyperoxia","Hypoxia","Intensive Care Units","Mortality","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Pragmatic clinical trial","Randomised controlled trial","Respiratory Insufficiency"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"handling oxygenation targets in the intensive care unit hot icu protocol for a randomised clinical trial comparing a lower vs a higher oxygenation target in adults with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85065176528&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-088.24-004958","identifier":[{"id":"30883686","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85065176528","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-66746747-c5fd-4aa1-b066-e84b94d9d0d5","ku-9a5e5b67-e927-4263-bfcd-90632eb73846"],"keyword":["critical illness","hyperoxia","hypoxia","intensive care units","mortality","oxygen inhalation therapy","pragmatic clinical trial","randomised controlled trial","respiratory insufficiency"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F8F9C798AD3B100DBFD7880E79D15D5C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Anæstesi, Børn, Kredsløb og Kvinder","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["Collaboration for Research in Intensive Care"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":4,"key":"and the hot icu investigators","name":"and the HOT-ICU Investigators","role":"oau"},{"affno":5,"key":"hot icu investigators","name":"HOT-ICU Investigators","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Olav L","key":"schjørringpau","last":"Schjørring","locid":"7dac619e-9b5c-46ac-9170-10ac13165da5","name":"Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","name_org":"Schjørring, Olav L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørn","key":"wetterslevpau","last":"Wetterslev","name":"Wetterslev, Jørn","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Theis","key":"langepau","last":"Lange","locid":"e4664578-01fc-4a93-8efd-1dbffb72cdd6","name":"Lange, Theis","orcid":"0000-0001-6807-8347","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Frederik","key":"keuspau","last":"Keus","name":"Keus, Frederik","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jon H","key":"laakepau","last":"Laake","name":"Laake, Jon H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Marjatta","key":"okkonenpau","last":"Okkonen","name":"Okkonen, Marjatta","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"siegemundpau","last":"Siegemund","name":"Siegemund, Martin","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matthew","key":"morganpau","last":"Morgan","name":"Morgan, Matthew","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Katrin M","key":"thormarpau","last":"Thormar","name":"Thormar, Katrin M","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil S","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3162c449-94c3-4d28-8dbb-c134d6eb76e1","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","name_org":"Rasmussen, Bodil S","orcid":"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30883686"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/aas.13356","issn":["00015172"],"issue":"7","journal":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","pages":"956-965","publisher":"Blackwell Munksgaard","status":"p","title":"Acta Anaesthesiologica Scandinavica","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85065176528"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Other Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","collaboration for research in intensive care"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-66746747-c5fd-4aa1-b066-e84b94d9d0d5","ku-9a5e5b67-e927-4263-bfcd-90632eb73846"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Handling Oxygenation Targets in the Intensive Care Unit (HOT-ICU)-Protocol for a randomised clinical trial comparing a lower vs a higher oxygenation target in adults with acute hypoxaemic respiratory failure","type":"Journal Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.24-004958","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In multiple sclerosis (MS), the Expanded Disability Status Scale (EDSS) reflects disease severity. Although parts of the EDSS are dependent on actual walking distance, self-reported statements are often applied. OBJECTIVES: The purpose of the present study was, therefore, to compare self-reported walking distance to actual walking distance to outline how this influences EDSS scoring. METHODS: MS patients with EDSS 4.0-7.5 ( n = 273) were included from the Danish MS hospitals rehabilitation study ( n = 427). All patients subjectively classified their maximal walking distance according to one of seven categories (>500; 300-499; 200-299; 100-199; 20-99; 5-19; 0-4 m). Subsequently, actual maximal walking distance was assessed and EDSS was determined from both self-reported walking distance (EDSSself-report) and actual walking distance (EDSSactual). RESULTS: In 145 patients (53%), self-reported walking distance was misclassified when compared to the actual walking distance. Misclassification was more frequent in patients using walking aids (64% vs. 44%, p < 0.05) and in patients with primary progressive MS (69%, p < 0.05). Misclassification of walking distance corresponded to incorrect EDSS scores (EDSSself-report vs EDSSactual) of ⩾0.5 point in 24%. CONCLUSION: In MS patients with EDSS 4.0-7.5, 53% misclassified their walking distance yielding incorrect EDSS scores in 24%. Therefore, correct EDSS determination must be based on measurement of actual walking distance.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Skjerbæk, Anders Guldhammer","Boesen, Finn","Petersen, Thor","Rasmussen, Peter Vestergaard","Stenager, Egon","Nørgaard, Michael","Feys, Peter","Jørgensen, Marie-Louise Kjeldgaard","Hvid, Lars G.","Dalgas, Ulrik"],"cuid":["S02-090.15-022004"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Hasselt University"],"keyword":["EDSS","Expanded disability status scale","Multiple sclerosis","Outcome measurement","Walking","primary progressive MS"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["The MS-Hospitals in Ry and Haslev, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can we trust self reported walking distance when determining edss scores in patients with multiple sclerosis the danish ms hospitals rehabilitation study","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85052565008","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-090.15-022004","identifier":[{"id":"000489170300013","type":"wos"},{"id":"30124106","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85052565008","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-800f1555-fe1b-4668-b938-9a8b272ed696","sdu-709733b2-be23-430d-b57e-946d2f0c08ba"],"keyword":["EDSS","Expanded Disability Status Scale","Outcome measurement","Walking","multiple sclerosis","primary progressive MS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A78D04678684DF1E575289418B127EEF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2019","yearSub":"2019"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"other hospitals","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-OTH","l3nl":"Other Hospitals","l3nn":"Other Hospitals","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Hospitals","namevar":["The Danish MS Hospitals"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["The MS-Hospitals in Ry and Haslev, Denmark."],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Esbjerg and Grindsted Hospital, Research Unit of Neurology (Esbjerg)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Hospital Sønderjylland, Research Unit of Neurology (Sønderborg)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Sygehus Lillebælt, Forskningsenhed for Neurologi (Kolding)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"be","key":"hasselt university","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Hasselt University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Guldhammer","key":"skjerbækpau","last":"Skjerbæk","name":"Sk