ddc-f443-468f-906a-27e30a5c509a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Pantoprazole in ICU patients at risk for gastrointestinal bleeding—1-year mortality in the SUP-ICU trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-093.62-005917","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Intravenous (IV) fluid is a key intervention in the management of septic shock. The benefits and harms of lower versus higher fluid volumes are unknown and thus clinical equipoise exists. We describe the protocol and detailed statistical analysis plan for the conservative versus liberal approach to fluid therapy of septic shock in the Intensive Care (CLASSIC) trial. The aim of the CLASSIC trial is to assess benefits and harms of IV fluid restriction versus standard care in adult intensive care unit (ICU) patients with septic shock. Methods: CLASSIC trial is an investigator-initiated, international, randomised, stratified, and analyst-blinded trial. We will allocate 1554 adult patients with septic shock, who are planned to be or are admitted to an ICU, to IV fluid restriction versus standard care. The primary outcome is mortality at day 90. Secondary outcomes are serious adverse events (SAEs), serious adverse reactions (SARs), days alive at day 90 without life support, days alive and out of the hospital at day 90 and mortality, health-related quality of life (HRQoL), and cognitive function at 1 year. We will conduct the statistical analyses according to a pre-defined statistical analysis plan, including three interim analyses. For the primary analysis, we will use logistic regression adjusted for the stratification variables comparing the two interventions in the intention-to-treat (ITT) population. Discussion: The CLASSIC trial results will provide important evidence to guide clinicians’ choice regarding the IV fluid therapy in adults with septic shock.","author_count":34,"contributors":["Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest","Hjortrup, Peter Buhl","Møller, Morten Hylander","Wetterslev, Jørn","Lange, Theis","Kjaer, Maj-Brit Nørregaard","Jonsson, Andreas Bender","Hjortsø, Carl Johan Steensen","Cronhjort, Maria","Laake, Jon Henrik","Jakob, Stephan M","Nalos, Marek","Pettilä, Ville","van der Horst, Iwan","Ostermann, Marlies","Mouncey, Paul","Rowan, Kathy","Cecconi, Maurizio","Ferrer, Ricard","Malbrain, Manu L N G","Ahlstedt, Christian","Hoffmann, Søren","Bestle, Morten Heiberg","Nebrich, Lars","Russell, Lene","Vang, Marianne","Rasmussen, Michael Lindhardt","Sølling, Christoffer","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Brøchner, Anne Craveiro","Perner, Anders"],"cuid":["S04-095.59-715786"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Meyhoff, Tine Sylvest"],"country":["Australia","Belgium","Czechia","Finland","Italy","Netherlands","Norway","Spain","Sweden","Switzerland","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Autonomous University of Barcelona","Czech Academy of Sciences","Department of Clinical Science and Education, Section of Anaesthesia and Intensive Care, Karolinska Institutet, Södersjukhuset,, Stockholm, Sweden.","Free University of Brussels","Guy's and St Thomas' NHS Foundation Trust","Helsinki University Hospital","Hospital Universitari Vall d'Hebron, Barcelona, Spain.","Humanitas Research Hospital","Intensive Care National Audit & Research Centre (ICNARC)","Intensive Care National Audit and Research Centre","Karolinska Institute","Karolinska Institutet","Karolinska University Hospital","Oslo University Hospital","University Hospital Bern","University Hospital Brussel","University Hospital of Bern","University Hospitals Brussels (UZB)","University Medical Center Groningen","University of Bern","University of Groningen","University of Helsinki","University of Melbourne","University of Oslo","University of Ostrava","University of Pisa","Vall d'Hebron University Hospital","Vrije Universiteit Brussel"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-SDR","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Departme