ructure and Dynamics of a Promiscuous Xanthan Lyase from Paenibacillus nanensis and the Design of Variants with Increased Stability and Activity","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-412532","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"During summer 2019, three patients residing by Tisvilde Hegn, Denmark were hospitalised with tick-borne encephalitis (TBE) after tick bites. A new TBE virus (TBEV) micro-focus was identified in tick nymphs collected around a playground in Tisvilde Hegn forest. Estimated TBEV prevalence was 8%, higher than in endemic areas around Europe. Whole genome sequencing showed clustering to a TBEV strain from Norway. This is the second time TBEV is found in Ixodes ricinus outside Bornholm, Denmark.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Agergaard, Charlotte N.","Rosenstierne, Maiken W.","Bødker, René","Rasmussen, Morten","Andersen, Peter H.S.","Fomsgaard, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-488736"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Denmark","Ixodes ricinus","Meningoencephalitis","Phylogenetic analysis","Tick borne encephalitis","Tick borne encephalitis virus"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"new tick borne encephalitis virus hot spot in northern zealand denmark october 000000002019","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2807/1560-7917.ES.2019.24.43.1900639","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-488736","identifier":[{"id":"85074287806","type":"scopus"},{"id":"31662158","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6820129","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-9f6e4162-b08d-409d-b34e-f49c193186bb"],"keyword":["Denmark","Ixodes ricinus","Northern Zealand","Tick-borne encephalitis","meningoencephalitis","phylogenetic analysis","tick-borne encephalitis virus"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E68B813CBCCB494938C859C3