ed Ergonomics","pages":"29-39","publisher":"Elsevier Limited","status":"p","title":"Applied Ergonomics","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85060485011"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Miscellaneous","Other Hospitals","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark","copenhagen university hospital - holbæk"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-cd48fa86-362f-48ff-9c20-8fd6e3e9296a","ku-39d72519-2ade-4a2f-9023-1be3c924a30b","nfa-66af2052-7c9c-4feb-8db7-3d72832df259","sdu-9fbbf722-60fc-413c-a9c7-4041e90fbb63"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The DPhacto cohort : An overview of technically measured physical activity at work and leisure in blue-collar sectors for practitioners and researchers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S04-099.11-767030","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"Background & aims: Intestinal insufficiency and intestinal failure are associated with malabsorption of micro- and macronutrients that may negatively influence bone metabolism and increase the risk for developing osteoporosis. However, information regarding prevalence and contribution of individual risk factors is scarce. We investigated the prevalence of osteoporosis in patients with intestinal insufficiency and intestinal failure and identified associated risk factors. Methods: This was a retrospective cross-sectional study including 167 clinically stable outpatients with intestinal insufficiency or intestinal failure. Bone mineral density (BMD) was measured by dual X-ray absorptiometry and the prevalence of osteoporosis was compared to a gender and age matched population. Several clinical and demographic parameters, including body mass index (BMI), vitamin-D, smoking habits and medications, were analyzed for association with BMD. Results: The prevalence of osteoporosis was 56.9% in the combined patient group compared to 24.1% in the control group (OR 4.2 [95% CI, 2.3 to 7.7]; p < 0.001). BMD in the hip was independently associated with BMI (0.13 [95% CI, 0.09 to 0.18]; p < 0.001) and vitamin-D levels (−0.41 [95% CI, −0.76 to −0.06]; p = 0.03). Similar associations were seen for BMD in the spine (0.15 [95% CI, 0.08 – 0.22]; p < 0.001) and (−0.60 [95% CI, −0.76 to −0.06]; p = 0.02), respectively. Trends for low BMD were observed in smokers, and in patients using glucocorticoids, opioids, and proton pump inhibitors. Conclusions: Patients with intestinal insufficiency and intestinal failure are at immense risk of developing osteoporosis. Low BMI and vitamin-D deficiency were identified as independent risk factors.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Andersen, Anders Skallerup","Olesen, Søren Schou","Køhler, Marianne","Vinter-Jensen, Lars","Kruse, Christian","Vestergaard, Peter","Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-103412"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Body Mass Index","Dual energy X ray absorptiometry","Home parenteral nutrition","Intestinal failure","Osteoporosis","Vitamin D"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"osteoporosis in patients with intestinal insufficiency and intestinal failure prevalence and clinical risk factors","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85027730887&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-103412","identifier":[{"id":"85027730887","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28823627","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-b7dbfa74-8a93-4753-b0d0-0833a65c92b4"],"keyword":["Body mass index","Dual energy X-ray absorptiometry","Home parenteral nutrition","Intestinal failure","Osteoporosis","Vitamin-D"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8CC63E05D9CB9E79A404A0C53A54133B"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Department of Gastroenterology and Hepatology","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin og Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","name_org":"Nygaard, Louis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"skalleruppau","last":"Skallerup","locid":"8839002b-110b-495b-a386-4df5b8d161e5","name":"Andersen, Anders Skallerup","name_org":"Skallerup, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Schou","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"0395fceb-e2ff-4fe2-8abc-c5486a437197","name":"Olesen, Søren Schou","orcid":"0000-0003-3916-3168","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"køhlerpau","last":"Køhler","locid":"344b7efa-d1ef-43bf-b4b4-1722e24a2ca3","name":"Køhler, Marianne","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"vinterjensenpau","last":"Vinter-Jensen","locid":"9bec0a4a-7fda-4f11-bbed-02e75dc2aa02","name":"Vinter-Jensen, Lars","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"krusepau","last":"Kruse","locid":"6d8dedc8-0eac-4eeb-88a5-85c4bc26d2be","name":"Kruse, Christian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"ad223cc8-3f85-4cdf-9da5-5ec44f6a1714","name":"Vestergaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9046-2967","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Højgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c242f457-53f4-4b88-82f3-d7fb297cf98c","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28823627"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnu.2017.07.018","issn":["02615614","15321983"],"issn_org":["02615614"],"issue":"5","journal":"Clinical Nutrition","pages":"1654-1660","publisher":"Churchill Livingstone","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85027730887"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b7dbfa74-8a93-4753-b0d0-0833a65c92b4"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Osteoporosis in patients with intestinal insufficiency and intestinal failure : Prevalence and clinical risk factors","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-103412","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we will demonstrate Response Surface Methodology (RSM) applied to process simulation of an offshore oil and gas separation plant. By performing surrogate experiments according to Design of Experiment (DoE) and subsequent construction of multiple linear regression models for the chosen responses, the overall separation process is optimised in terms of power consumption under the constraints of quality specification of gas and oil export, respectively The fluid treated in the separation plant is rich in NGL (Natural Gas Liquids) which causes challenges in meeting the export specifications. Further, the NGL causes increased condensate recycle in the compression system thereby increasing power consumption for the compressors as well as increased cooling for heat exchangers. Offshore the NGL is difficult to dispose, which makes fractionation unattractive and the NGL must be exported via the oil (partly stabilised) or via the gas (rich gas) or a combination of the two. Effectively, this violates the export specifications and the NGL must be extracted in on-shore facilities either at the oil or gas receiving facilities. By exploring different options, applying RSM, it is found that in terms of overall power consumption export of NGL with the gaseous products is more effective that exporting the NGL with the partly stabilised oil. The methodology used in the present paper can also be applied to existing production facilities as a generic optimisation tool. Due to the simplicity of the regression models mimicking the separation plant they can be coupled with the overall process control for potential on-line plant optimisation.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Andreasen, Anders","Rasmussen, Kasper Rønn","Mandø, Matthias"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-121925"],"event":{"end":"2018-06-01","place":"Esbjerg, dk","start":"2018-05-30","title":"3rd IFAC Workshop on Automatic Control in Offshore Oil and Gas Production OOGP 2018","year":"2018"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Model reduction","Optimization problems","Process simulators","Regression Analysis","Statistical design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-RAM"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-RAM","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plant wide oil and gas separation plant optimisation using response surface methodology","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320131762/1_s2.0_S2405896318307043_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-121925","identifier":[{"id":"85050162998","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f7597d6c-779f-4cbc-be40-4dc910b3e140"],"keyword":["Industrial Production Systems","Model reduction","Optimization problems","Process Simulators","Process parameter estimation","Regression Analysis","Statistical design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6BEE4C1165B0E941BED2D6B267EAB5AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/320131762/1_s2.0_S2405896318307043_main.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ramboll foundation","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-RAM","l3nn":"Ramboll Foundation","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ramboll Foundation","namevar":["Ramboll Foundation"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-RAM","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg Uni