{"abstract":"This article examines the relationship between the uses of literature and narrative medicine. Peter Seeberg’s short story “The Patient” is interpreted as an illness narrative in relation to Ludwig Wittgenstein’s therapeutic philosophy of language. Rasmussen suggests that Seeberg’s reliance on the use of everyday language in the short story is an analogy to a new position in literary studies where criticism and engagement, rationality and emotionality are united.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl"],"cuid":["S02-097.78-686244"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"litteraturens brugspotentiale peter seebergs patienten læst som en sygdomsfortælling","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/pas.v32i78.102955","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.78-686244","ids":["ku-4af73fba-2086-4b80-a990-fea6d1840375","sdu-31f3608a-2104-45fd-bc9f-68e833ccb017"],"keyword":["narrative medicine; uses of literature; philosophy of language; illness narrative"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-0B284D1A3F85200A64BD72EA3E8D2AF7"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/144977230/Litteraturens_brugspotentiale.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.7146/pas.v32i78.102955","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Cultural Studies","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Uses of Literature"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6612df8e-d9f9-4004-b959-a9c30b0762a5","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7718-5208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.7146/pas.v32i78.102955","issn":["09018883","19047797"],"issn_org":["09018883"],"issue":"78","journal":"Passage","pages":"83-96","publisher":"Det Kongelige Bibliotek","status":"p","title":"Passage","volume":"32"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-4af73fba-2086-4b80-a990-fea6d1840375","sdu-31f3608a-2104-45fd-bc9f-68e833ccb017"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Litteraturens brugspotentiale : Peter Seebergs “Patienten” læst som en sygdomsfortælling","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-097.78-686244","year":"2018","yearsub":2018}
{"abstract":"Background--The electrocardiographic interatrial block (IAB) has been associated with atrial fibrillation (AF). We aimed to test whether IAB can improve risk prediction of AF for the individual person. Methods and Results--Digital ECGs of 152 759 primary care patients aged 50 to 90 years were collected from 2001 to 2011. We identified individuals with P-wave ≥120 ms and the presence of none, 1, 2, or 3 biphasic P-waves in inferior leads. Data on comorbidity, medication, and outcomes were obtained from nationwide registries. We observed a dose-response relationship between the number of biphasic P-waves in inferior leads and the hazard of AF during follow-up. Discrimination of the 10-year outcome of AF, measured by time-dependent area under the curve, was increased by 1.09% (95% confidence interval 0.43-1.74%) for individuals with cardiovascular disease at baseline (CVD) and 1.01% (95% confidence interval 0.40-1.62%) for individuals without CVD, when IAB was added to a conventional risk model for AF. The highest effect of IAB on the absolute risk of AF was observed in individuals aged 60 to 70 years with CVD. In this subgroup, the 10-year risk of AF was 50% in those with advanced IAB compared with 10% in those with a normal P-wave. In general, individuals with advanced IAB and no CVD had a higher risk of AF than patients with CVD and no IAB. Conclusions--IAB improves risk prediction of AF when added to a conventional risk model. Clinicians may consider monitoring patients with IAB more closely for the occurrence of AF, especially for high-risk subgroups.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Skov, Morten W.","Ghouse, Jonas","Kühl, Jørgen T.","Platonov, Pyotr G.","Graff, Claus","Fuchs, Andreas","Rasmussen, Peter V.","Pietersen, Adrian","Nordestgaard, Børge G.","Torp-Pedersen, Christian","Hansen, Steen Møller","Olesen, Morten S.","Haunsø, Stig","Køber, Lars","Gerds, Thomas A.","Kofoed, Klaus F.","Svendsen, Jesper H.","Holst, Anders G.","Nielsen, Jonas B."],"cuid":["S02-100.00-002663"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Skåne University Hospital","University of Michigan, Ann Arbor"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","ECG","Epidemiology","Interatrial Block","Ischemic stroke","Risk prediction"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"risk prediction of atrial fibrillation based on electrocardiographic interatrial block","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.117.008247","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-002663","identifier":[{"id":"85047999051","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6015370","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"29848496","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-355e4ce2-48d7-4edd-a32c-6969eca59bba","ku-41b68f87-fc3c-410d-8337-f4749088194c"],"keyword":["Atrial fibrillation","ECG","Epidemiology","Interatrial","Interatrial block","Ischemic stroke","Risk prediction"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7E8DE60A4C72083EB5512659BA29C78F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1161/JAHA.117.008247","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/280188250/e008247.full.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capit