9 agonist MGN1703 triggers a potent type I interferon response in the sigmoid colon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-023268","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"{BackgroundRelatively} little is known about the role of maternal functioning in terms of attention deficit hyperactivity disorder ({ADHD}) symptoms, attachment style and resilience as predictive factors for treatment outcome when offspring are diagnosed with {ADHD}.{ObjectiveTo} investigate whether maternal functioning is associated with treatment outcome in children with {ADHD}.{MethodsThe} study formed part of a larger naturalistic observational study of children with {ADHD}. A battery of self-report measures was used to assess selected factors in maternal functioning at the point of referral (baseline data); adult {ADHD}-symptoms, adult attachment style and adult resilience. Associations between these domains and child treatment response were subsequently examined in a 1-year follow up.{ResultsMaternal} {ADHD}-symptoms and degree of resilience were significantly correlated to symptom reduction in offspring diagnosed with {ADHD}. However, the association between maternal attachment style and child treatment response as measured by the {ADHD}-{RS} did not reach statistical significance.{ConclusionTo} our knowledge, this is the first study to consider potential protective factors along with risk factors in maternal functioning and the impact on child treatment outcome. The study contributes to our knowledge of the potential role of maternal functioning in treatment outcome for children with {ADHD}.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Pernille Darling","Storebø, Ole Jakob","Shmueli-Goetz, Yael","Bojesen, Anders Bo","Simonsen, Erik","Bilenberg, Niels"],"cuid":["S03-099.54-045131"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Rasmussen, Pernille Darling"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Anna Freud National Centre for Children and Families"],"keyword":["ADHD","Attachment","Developmental outcome","Maternal functioning","Resilience"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"childhood adhd and treatment outcome the role of maternal functioning","src":["ku","sdu","vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13034-018-0234-3","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-099.54-045131","identifier":[{"id":"85048623295","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29983736","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC6003115","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-a88905ac-e4a5-4764-b965-5345ff8b2688","sdu-e9326b52-899e-4d8d-a71d-b4ba37f8fc3b","vive-31eb6c88-bf01-44e1-b2ca-b10433d0f327"],"keyword":["ADHD","Attachment","Developmental outcome","Maternal functioning","Resilience"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-86A526F777CEF69F0DA197178323750A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13034-018-0234-3","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141351061/Childhood_ADHD_and_treatment_outcome.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/199461734/document.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, Research Unit of Child and Adolescent Psychiatry (Southern Denmark)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS – Mental Health Services in Region Zealand"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"anna freud national centre for children and families","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Anna Freud National Centre for Children and Families","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["VIVE - The Danish Center for Social Science Research, VIVE Quantitative Methods"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Psychiatry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Darling","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a3bed430-277a-4f8d-9e44-38f7cb7e65f8","name":"Rasmussen, Pernille Darling","orcid":"0000-0002-4649-5745","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole Jakob","key":"storebøpau","last":"Storebø","locid":"fc9ed7a4-77cd-49cf-8a3f-679597f41d6f","name":"Storebø, Ole Jakob","orcid":"0000-0003-0204-7745","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Yael","key":"shmueligoetzpau","last":"Shmueli-Goetz","name":"Shmueli-Goetz, Yael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"056b6180-64df-40c2-8bc8-12867660066c","name":"Bojesen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0002-5321-6855","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Erik","key":"simonsenpau","last":"Simonsen","locid":"a00e5cad-92bc-40ab-8ebc-92298c919f9d","name":"Simonsen, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-6134-2392","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"bilenbergpau","last":"Bilenberg","locid":"c865af0f-affd-44a4-b9fa-39c26141d3e2","name":"Bilenberg, Niels","orcid":"0000-0002-5838-556X","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29983736"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13034-018-0234-3","issn":["17532000"],"issue":"1","journal":"Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Mental Health","pages":"31","publisher":"BioMed Central Ltd.","status":"p","title":"Child and Adolescent Psychiatry and Mental Health","volume":"12"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85048623295"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Region Zealand","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a88905ac-e4a5-4764-b965-5345ff8b2688","sdu-e9326b52-899e-4d8d-a71d-b4ba37f8fc3b","vive-31eb6c88-bf01-44e1-b2ca-b10433d0f327"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark","VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Childhood ADHD and treatment outcome : The role of maternal functioning","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-099.54-045131","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Helheim Glacier ranks among the fastest flowing and most ice discharging outlets of the Greenland Ice Sheet (GrIS). After undergoing rapid speed-up in the early 2000s, understanding its long-term mass balance and dynamic has become increasingly important. Here, we present the first record of direct Holocene ice-marginal changes of the Helheim Glacier following the initial deglaciation. By analysing cores from lakes adjacent to the present ice margin, we pinpoint periods of advance and retreat. We target threshold lakes, which receive glacial meltwater only when the margin is at an advanced position, similar to the present. We show that, during the period from 10.5 to 9.6 cal ka BP, the extent of Helheim Glacier was similar to that of todays, after which it remained retracted for most of the Holocene until a re-advance caused it to reach its present extent at c. 0.3 cal ka BP, during the Little Ice Age (LIA). Thus, Helheim Glacier's present extent is the largest since the last deglaciation, and its Holocene history shows that it is capable of recovering after several millennia of warming and retreat. Furthermore, the absence of advances beyond the present-day position during for example the 9.3 and 8.2 ka cold events as well as the early-Neoglacial suggest a substantial retreat during most of the Holocene.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bjørk, A.A","Larsen, N.K.","Olsen, J.","Goldsack, A.E.","Kjeldsen, K.K.","Morlighem, M.","Andresen, C.S.","Rasmussen, Peter","Oxfeldt, G.","Kjær, K.H."],"cuid":["S04-100.00-029124"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bjørk, A. A."],"country":["Greenland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","Swansea University","University of California","University of California at Irvine"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-GEUS","DI-GV-KUM"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-GEUS","DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"holocene history of the helheim glacier southeast greenland","src":["au","dtu","ku","kum"],"src-code":["DI-GV-KUM","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85048882783","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S04-100.00-029124","identifier":[{"id":"85048882783","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-e3086442-6e3b-4263-a3ad-6a5e40bd89ab","dtu-700dfbe6-9a0b-49b9-9ca8-c335e664f32d","ku-c4d61820-4a05-48a4-b92e-837f31df9174","kum-694d9fcb-d368-47f7-96cd-6eb4df4d78df"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-76EB1FCE0F0EC83FF6DD5F02883F56BB"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of california at irvine","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Irvine","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus