{"abstract":"Background and purpose - Threshold values defining 3 categories of passive range of motion are used in the Cerebral Palsy follow-Up Program to guide clinical decisions. The aim of this study was to investigate the threshold values by testing the hypothesis that passive range of motion in ankle dorsiflexion is associated with gross motor function and that function differs between the groups of participants in each category. Patients and methods - We analyzed data from 60 ambulatory children (aged 5-9 years) with spastic cerebral palsy. Outcomes were passive range of motion in ankle dorsiflexion with flexed and extended knee and gross motor function (Gait Deviation Index, Gait Variable Score of the ankle, peak dorsiflexion during gait, 1-minute walk, Gross Motor Function Measure, the Pediatric Quality of Life Inventory Cerebral Palsy Module, and Pediatric Outcomes Data Collection Instrument). Results - Significant (p < 0.05) and moderate correlations were documented for range of motion versus Gait Variable Score of the ankle (r = -0.37 and r = -0.37) and range of motion versus peak dorsiflexion (r = 0.49 and r = 0.55). Differences between the groups formed by the categories were shown for Gait Variable Score of the ankle and peak dorsiflexion (p < 0.05). No other significant correlations or differences between the categories were observed. Interpretation - The results suggest that threshold values for ankle dorsiflexion used in the Cerebral Palsy follow-Up Program are of limited clinical value in assessing overall gross motor function, but may be used to identify deviations in ankle-specific gait function.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","Svensson, Joachim","Thorning, Maria","Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","Overgaard, Søren","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586195"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Ankle Joint physiology","Child","Child Preschool","Cross Sectional Studies","Female","Gait physiology","Humans","Male","Motor Skills physiology","Range of Motion Articular physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"threshold values of ankle dorsiflexion and gross motor function in 000000000060 children with cerebral palsy a cross sectional study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17453674.2018.1456749","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586195","identifier":[{"id":"29589480","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85044447629","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC6066765","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-2d5cb4c8-4f91-47c5-8d28-5a22ec052bce"],"keyword":["Ankle Joint/physiology","Cerebral Palsy/physiopathology","Child","Child, Preschool","Cross-Sectional Studies","Female","Gait/physiology","Humans","Male","Motor Skills/physiology","Range of Motion, Articular/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7EC11A87CBB7C12E2CA0C3DBC4BE15B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/141531543/Threshold_values_of_ankle_dorsiflexion_and_gross_motor_function_in_60_children_with_cerebral_palsy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/17453674.2018.1456749","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle M","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fc740e3e-3a84-4904-bd04-4db023a123db","name":"Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","name_org":"Rasmussen, Helle M","orcid":"0000-0002-7522-8144","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","locid":"0ca7fd50-967c-4be6-a38a-710889b0069f","name":"Svensson, Joachim","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria","key":"thorningpau","last":"Thorning","locid":"9cc3883b-fce8-4dc5-865d-03f5cbd05795","name":"Thorning, Maria","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels W","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ed21518f-c0c3-4e67-9b9e-fd9f355c6612","name":"Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","name_org":"Pedersen, Niels W","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"b394ea8b-39e4-46bc-8651-f6321e37c2eb","name":"Overgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-6829-4787","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"holsgaardlarsenpau","last":"Holsgaard-Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29589480"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/17453674.2018.1456749","issn":["17453674","17453682"],"issn_org":["17453674"],"issue":"4","journal":"Acta Orthopaedica","pages":"437-442","publisher":"Medical Journals Sweden AB","status":"p","title":"Acta Orthopaedica","volume":"89"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85044447629"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2d5cb4c8-4f91-47c5-8d28-5a22ec052bce"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Threshold values of ankle dorsiflexion and gross motor function in 60 children with cerebral palsy : A cross-sectional study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-586195","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-628601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"keri leigh merritt masterless men poor whites and slavery in the antebellum south cambridge cambridge university press 000000002017 000000000361 pages isbn 000000000978 000000000001 000000000107 000000018424 000000000004","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djb","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22439/asca.v50i2.5784","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-628601","identifier":[{"id":"85046080866","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-c140d384-6859-471d-b1b4-40bf620c09fd"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E549B643D062F7BC5F9EBBEB8D20890C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22439/asca.v50i2.5784","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History, Center for American Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f284f3a3-297f-4882-81e1-b591c41ead80","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9817-9595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22439/asca.v50i2.5784","issn":["00448060"],"issue":"2","journal":"American Studies in Scandinavia","pages":"123-125","publisher":"University Press of Southern Denmark","status":"p","title":"American Studies in Scandinavia","volume":"50"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-c140d384-6859-471d-b1b4-40bf620c09fd"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Keri Leigh Merritt, \"Masterless Men: Poor Whites and Slavery in the Antebellum South. Cambridge: Cambridge University Press, 2017. 361 pages. ISBN: 978-1-107-18424-4","type":"Journal Book Review","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-628601","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Genotype estimates from short-read sequencing data are typically based on the alignment of reads to a linear reference, but reads originating from more complex variants (for example, structural variants) often align poorly, resulting in biased genotype estimates. This bias can be mitigated by first collecting a set of candidate variants across discovery methods, individuals and databases, and then realigning the reads to the variants and reference simultaneously. However, this realignment problem has proved computationally difficult. Here, we present a new method (BayesTyper) that uses exact alignment of read k-mers to a graph representation of the reference and variants to efficiently perform unbiased, probabilistic genotyping across the variation spectrum. We demonstrate that BayesTyper generally provides superior variant sensitivity and genotyping accuracy relative to existing methods when used to integrate variants across discovery approaches and individuals. Finally, we demonstrate that including a ‘variation-prior’ database containing already known variants significantly improves sensitivity.","author_count":56,"contributors":["Sibbesen, Jonas Andreas","Maretty, Lasse","Jensen, Jacob Malte","Petersen, Bent","Liu, Siyang","Villesen, Palle","Skov, Laurits","Belling, Kirstine C.","Theil Have, Christian","Gonzalez-Izarzugaza, Jose Maria","Grosjean, Marie","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Grove, Jakob","Dam-Als, Thomas","Huang, Shujia","Chang, Yuqi","Xu, Ruiqi","Ye, Weijian","Rao, Junhua","Guo, Xiaosen","Sun, Jihua","Cao, Hongzhi","Ye, Chen","van Beusekom, Johan","Espeseth, Thomas","Flindt, Esben","Friborg, Rune M.","Halager, Anders Egerup","Le Hellard, Stephanie","Hultman, Christina M.","Lescai, Francesco","Li, Shengting","Lund, Ole","Løngren, Peter","Mailund, Thomas","Matey-Hernandez, María Luisa","Mors, Ole","Pedersen, Christian N. S.","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Sullivan, Patrick","Ali, Syed","Westergaard, David","Yadav, Rachita","Li, Ning","Xu, Xun","Hansen, Torben","Krogh, Anders","Bolund, Lars","Sørensen, Thorkild I. A.","Pedersen, Oluf","Gupta, Ramneek","Rasmussen, Simon","Besenbacher, Søren","Børglum, Anders D.","Wang, Jun","Eiberg, Hans","Kristiansen, Karsten","Brunak, Søren","Schierup, Mikkel Heide","Krogh, Anders"],"cuid":["S02-089.12-034365"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Krogh, Anders"],"country":["China","Norway","Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Karolinska Institutet","South China University of Technology","University of Bergen","University of North Carolina at Chapel Hill","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"accurate genotyping across variant classes and lengths using variant graphs","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b0XJ0","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-089.12-034365","identifier":[{"id":"85048689124","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29915429","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-4f464272-6c62-4e3f-9c52-3f0ebb9ad7b9","ku-388b0498-530b-4f2b-acb3-5861f5e1057c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-3AFE62B7CF9EE958E1793F98FD7FAC4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rdcu.be/b0XJ0","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3