{"abstract":"New economic developments in the Arctic, such as shipping and oil exploitation, bring along unprecedented risks of marine oil spills. Microorganisms have played a central role in degrading and reducing the impact of the spilled oil during past oil disasters. However, in the Arctic, and in particular in its pristine areas, the self-cleaning capacity and biodegradation potential of the natural microbial communities have yet to be uncovered. This review compiles and investigates the current knowledge with respect to environmental parameters and biochemical constraints that control oil biodegradation in the Arctic. Hereby, seawaters off Greenland are considered as a case study. Key factors for biodegradation include the bioavailability of hydrocarbons, the presence of hydrocarbon-degrading bacteria and the availability of nutrients. We show how these key factors may be influenced by the physical oceanographic conditions in seawaters off Greenland and other environmental parameters including low temperature, sea ice, sunlight regime, suspended sediment plumes and phytoplankton blooms that characterize the Arctic. Based on the acquired insights, a first qualitative assessment of the biodegradation potential in seawaters off Greenland is presented. In addition to the most apparent Arctic characteristics, such as low temperature and sea ice, the impact of typical Arctic features such as the oligotrophic environment, poor microbial adaptation to hydrocarbon degradation, mixing of stratified water masses, and massive phytoplankton blooms and suspended sediment plumes merit to be topics of future investigation.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Vergeynst, Leendert","Wegeberg, Susse","Aamand, Jens","Lassen, Pia","Gosewinkel, Ulrich Bay","Fritt-Rasmussen, Janne","Gustavson, Kim","Mosbech, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-222065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Nordic"],"country":["Greenland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland"],"keyword":["Arctic","Biodegradation","Greenland","Hydrocarbon","Oil spill","Review"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"biodegradation of marine oil spills in the arctic with a greenland perspective","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85042940925","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-222065","identifier":[{"id":"85042940925","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29898532","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a2c16777-8d5e-4000-82e6-e6bb8c7dfb6a"],"keyword":["Arctic","Biodegradation","Greenland","Hydrocarbon","Oil spill","Review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9FE21A46EEAA44CE2B74D5FA9727DB14"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gl","key":"geological survey of denmark and greenland","loc":["Greenland","Nordic"],"name":"Geological Survey of Denmark and Greenland","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Leendert","key":"vergeynstpau","last":"Vergeynst","locid":"629af064-0cb1-4dba-9ba4-5c4ae60e9caa","name":"Vergeynst, Leendert","orcid":"0000-0002-4388-4315","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susse","key":"wegebergpau","last":"Wegeberg","locid":"05370847-e1d3-4253-b818-046251260ff5","name":"Wegeberg, Susse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"aamandpau","last":"Aamand","name":"Aamand, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Pia","key":"lassenpau","last":"Lassen","locid":"68ffe3e9-8396-4809-9a6d-c96548dc4947","name":"Lassen, Pia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrich Bay","key":"gosewinkelpau","last":"Gosewinkel","locid":"e7bbfd94-5560-4fd4-8b63-b8381cc78acb","name":"Gosewinkel, Ulrich Bay","orcid":"0000-0001-9848-9323","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne","key":"frittrasmussenpau","last":"Fritt-Rasmussen","locid":"ee0f4272-d879-4350-9617-affc0cc83535","name":"Fritt-Rasmussen, Janne","orcid":"0000-0002-6496-8032","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K","key":"gustavsonpau","last":"Gustavson","locid":"1ebbd6c1-641f-40c9-a30f-7652da2113f9","name":"Gustavson, Kim","name_org":"Gustavson, K","orcid":"0000-0001-8242-0276","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"mosbechpau","last":"Mosbech","locid":"0d8b3009-ff00-40a7-b738-abfa87e31ccf","name":"Mosbech, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-7581-7037","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["29898532"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.scitotenv.2018.01.173","issn":["00489697","18791026"],"issn_org":["00489697"],"journal":"Science of the Total Environment","pages":"1243-1258","publisher":"Elsevier BV","publisher_org":"Elsevier B.V.","status":"p","title":"Science of the Total Environment","volume":"626"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85042940925"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a2c16777-8d5e-4000-82e6-e6bb8c7dfb6a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Biodegradation of marine oil spills in the Arctic with a Greenland perspective","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222065","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The scrape-off layer (SOL) power fall-off length, λ q, for parameters relevant to ASDEX Upgrade (AUG) L-mode discharges is examined by means of numerical simulations. The simulation data is acquired using synthetic probe data from turbulence simulations, which gives a high temporal resolution on the full density and pressure fields, required for an accurate evaluation of λ q due to the strongly intermittent signals in the SOL. Electron conduction is found to dominate the parallel heat flux close to the separatrix, while ion convection dominates in the far SOL. Good agreement is found with the experimental scaling for AUG L-mode Sieglin et al (2016 Plasma Phys. Control. Fusion 58 055015), where λ q is found to scale almost linearly with the safety factor, q, and to be weakly dependent on the power across the last-closed flux surface (LCFS), P. However, P depends on a wide range of parameters. In this paper we trace this dependence and the resulting fit of λ q reveals a scaling proportional to the inverse square root of the electron temperature at the LCFS, , and a linear dependence on q.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Olsen, Jeppe Miki Busk","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Madsen, Jens","Eich, Thomas","Sieglin, Bernhard","Naulin, Volker"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-339762"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Olsen, Jeppe Miki Busk"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics"],"keyword":["Scrape off layer transport"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scrape off layer power fall off length from turbulence simulations of asdex upgrade l mode paper","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204992806/Olsen_Scrape.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-339762","identifier":[{"id":"85050406663","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-75cf955c-cd00-44b3-9b12-799a4c9eb652"],"keyword":["Scrape-off layer parallel heat flux","Scrape-off layer power fall-off length","Scrape-off layer transport"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B7D30E33D363DC19C4AA927FCD48147"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/204992806/Olsen_Scrape.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute for plasma physics","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute for Plasma Physics","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeppe","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"8cd18be3-5451-4463-8b96-a06469e1eca4","name":"Olsen, Jeppe Miki Busk","name_org":"Olsen, Jeppe","orcid":"0000-0002-4156-6671","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid