"last":"Kradin","name":"Kradin, Nikolay","rank":70,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten E.","key":"allentoftmortenepau","last":"Allentoft","name":"Allentoft, Morten E.","rank":71,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ludovic","key":"orlandoludovicpau","last":"Orlando","name":"Orlando, Ludovic","rank":72,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"nielsenrasmuspau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Rasmus","rank":73,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"sikoramartinpau","last":"Sikora","name":"Sikora, Martin","rank":74,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Evelyne","key":"heyerevelynepau","last":"Heyer","name":"Heyer, Evelyne","rank":75,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"35","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian","key":"kristiansenkristianpau","last":"Kristiansen","name":"Kristiansen, Kristian","rank":76,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Eske","key":"willersleveskepau","last":"Willerslev","name":"Willerslev, Eske","rank":77,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30166629"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/s41586-018-0488-1","issn":["00280836","14764687"],"issn_org":["00280836"],"journal":"Nature","publisher":"Nature Research","status":"p","title":"Nature","volume":"557"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85055785582"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-d52af8f5-616f-4101-a4d7-e62849a5e491"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Author Correction: 137 ancient human genomes from across the Eurasian steppes","type":"Journal Comment","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-368239","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In order to understand the mechanism of the confinement bifurcation and H-mode power threshold in magnetically confined plasma, a new dynamical model of the L–H transition based on edge instability phase transition (EIPT) has been developed. With the typical plasma parameters of the EAST tokamak, the self-consistent turbulence growth rate is analyzed using the simplest case of pressure-driven ballooning-type instability, which indicates that the L–H transition can be caused by the stabilization of the edge instability through EIPT. The weak E × B flow shear in L-mode is able to increase the ion inertia of the electrostatic motion by increasing the radial wave number of the tilted turbulence structures, which play an important role for accelerating the trigger process of EIPT rather than directly to suppress the turbulent transport. With the acceleration mechanism of E × B flow shear, fast L–H and H–L transitions are demonstrated under the control of the input heating power. Due to the simplified scrape-off-layer boundary condition applied, the ratio between the heating powers at the H–L and L–H transition respectively differs from the ratio by Nusselt number. The results of the modeling reveal a scaling of the power threshold of the L–H transition, PL−H ∝ n0.76B0.8 for deuterium plasma. It is found finite Larmor radius induces an isotope effect of the H-mode power threshold.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Wu, Xingquan","Xu, Guosheng","Wan, Baonian","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Chen, Liang","Ran, Chen","Ning, Yan","Linming, Shao"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-372735"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corresponding_author":["Wu, Xingquan"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["E x B flow shear","L H transition","Power threshold"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a new model of the l h transition and h mode power threshold","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85052329478","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-372735","identifier":[{"id":"85052329478","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-e40f9620-2da4-42da-bcc9-88a2fd8a83b4"],"keyword":["E x B flow shear","Edge instability","L-H transition","Power threshold","Turbulence suppression"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-021F1D0173E5D36449D1096BB9C4C550"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Xingquan","key":"wupau","last":"Wu","name":"Wu, Xingquan","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Guosheng","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, Guosheng","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Baonian","key":"wanpau","last":"Wan","name":"Wan, Baonian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Liang","key":"chenpau","last":"Chen","name":"Chen, Liang","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chen","key":"ranpau","last":"Ran","name":"Ran, Chen","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yan","key":"ningpau","last":"Ning","name":"Ning, Yan","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Shao","key":"linmingpau","last":"Linming","name":"Linming, Shao","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/2058-6272/aabb9e","issn":["10090630"],"issue":"9","journal":"Plasma Science and Technology","paperid":"094003","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Science and Technology","volume":"20"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052329478"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e40f9620-2da4-42da-bcc9-88a2fd8a83b4"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A new model of the L–H transition and H-mode power threshold","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-372735","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Survival of patients with high-grade osteosarcoma (HOS), the most common primary bone cancer, has not improved significantly the last 30 years and the disease remains a major challenge. The purpose of this study is to evaluate survival in relation to prognostic factors at time of diagnosis among patients diagnosed with primary appendicular HOS in East Denmark between 1990 and 2010. MATERIAL AND METHODS: 101 patients (median age = 20 years, female/male ratio = 56/45) diagnosed with primary appendicular high-grade osteosarcoma between 1990 and 2010 were included in this study. Initially, 156 patients diagnosed with osteosarcoma between 1990 and 2010 were identified through the population based Regional Database of Pathology, which covers a population of approximately 2.7 million (east Denmark). 55 patients were excluded due to (A) tumor was low grade (n = 22), (B) located in axial skeleton (n = 18), (C) incorrect diagnosis (n = 11) or (D) biopsy represented a tumor relapse from a former primary osteosarcoma (n = 4). Overall survival was evaluated using the Kaplan-Meier survival analysis and log-rank test. Prognostic factors were analyzed using uni- and multivariate cox-regression method with variables scored equally in the model. p Values <.05 were considered statistically significant. RESULTS: The probability of 5- and 10-year survival was 51% (95% CI: 41-61) and 46% (95% CI: 36-56), respectively. Metastatic stage at diagnosis and tumor size ≥10 cm measured radiologically at the largest diameter were independent prognostic factors for decreased survival with significant increased hazard-risks of 3.5 (95% CI: 1.9-6.5) and 1.97 (95% CI: 1.1-3.6), respectively. DISCUSSION: In this single institution evaluation of primary appendicular HOS we found 5-and 10-year survival rates consistent with international standards for this patient group. Distant metastases and tumor size ≥10 cm at the time of diagnosis were independent prognostic factors for decreased survival in our cohort. These results underline the importance of awareness and early referral from the primary sector.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Colding-Rasmussen, Thomas","Thorn, Andrea Pohly","Horstmann, Peter","Rechnitzer, Catherine","Hjalgrim, Lisa Lyngsie","Krarup-Hansen, Anders","Petersen, Michael Mørk"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-458514"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms mortality","Child","Denmark epidemiology","Female","Humans","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Young Adult"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"survival and prognostic factors at time of diagnosis in high grade appendicular osteosarcoma a 000000000021 year single institution evaluation from east denmark","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-458514","identifier":[{"id":"85025805256","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28741397","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-6cf5a1db-501e-4f85-ae3e-ac3d1101c5c9"],"keyword":["Adolescent","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Bone Neoplasms/mortality","Child","Denmark/epidemiology","Female","Humans","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Osteosarcoma/mortality","Prognosis","Proportional Hazards Models","Young Adult"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC8D672B4CE5CFBDC51351AABF380576"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Clinical Oncology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"coldingrasmussenpau","last":"Colding-Rasmussen","name":"Colding-Rasmussen, Thomas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrea Pohly","key":"thornpau","last":"Thorn","name":"Thorn, Andrea Pohly","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"horstmannpau","last":"Horstmann","name":"Horstmann, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Catherine","key":"rechnitzerpau","last":"Rechnitzer","name":"Rechnitzer, Catherine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lisa Lyngsie","key":"hjalgrimpau","last":"Hjalgrim","name":"Hjalgrim, Lisa Lyngsie","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kraruphansenpau","last":"Krarup-Hansen","locid":"5fb06b4f-2517-4150-923a-06d5cde8fc83","name":"Krarup-Hansen, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Michael Mørk","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"9eb5f936-2e76-4f2f-917e-a3b50f56f0e6","name":"Petersen, Michael Mørk","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28741397"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/0284186x.2017.1351620","issn":["0284186X","11001704"],"issn_org":["0284186X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Acta Oncologica","pages":"420-425","status":"p","title":"Acta Oncologica","volume":"57"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025805256"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-6cf5a1db-501e-4f85-ae3e-ac3d1101c5c9"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Survival and prognostic factors at time of diagnosis in high-grade appendicular osteosarcoma : a 21 year single institution evaluation from east Denmark","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-458514","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Bogen \"Under stadig skælven\" er styret af hypotesen om en filosofisk-religiøs enhed i forfatterskabet. Det er antagelsen, at de to mægtige og til dels modsatrettede livsanskuelser inden for den europæiske kulturs historie, nemlig kristendommen og nihilismen, konfronteres hos Seeberg med en klar bevidsthed om modsætningens potentiale. Det er formålet med bogen at dokumentere, analysere og diskutere, hvordan filosofiske kilder, religiøse kilder og litterære kilder bearbejdes i forfatterskabet. Fremstillingen hævder ingen steder at give den endegyldige fortolkning af de skønlitterære værker, der behandles. Med inddragelse af arkivets talrige (trykte som utrykte) manuskripter, oversættelser og papirer foruden den efterladte bogsamling tegnes til gengæld et tilstræbt fuldstændigt billede af det samlede værks intertekstualitet.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Juhl"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-580264"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Arkiv","Intertekstualitet","Peter Seeberg"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"under stadig skælven peter seebergs arkiv og værk","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.universitypress.dk/shop/under-stadig-skaelven-3713p.html","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-580264","ids":["sdu-188fefc6-ddbc-4b1e-8afa-f1e309c214cf"],"keyword":["Peter Seeberg","arkiv","intertekstualitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F28477DCD6993DBC432A580549B34B9"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department for the Study of Culture","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Cultural Studies","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Culture and Language, Uses of Literature"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"6612df8e-d9f9-4004-b959-a9c30b0762a5","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","orcid":"0000-0001-7718-5208","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788740831764"],"issn":["19012098"],"pages":"432","place":"Odense","publisher":"Syddansk Universitetsforlag","series":"University of Southern Denmark Studies in Scandinavian Languages and Literatures","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-188fefc6-ddbc-4b1e-8afa-f1e309c214cf"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Under stadig skælven : Peter Seebergs arkiv og værk","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-580264","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"In this master thesis, it is characterized what type of challenge, that we are facing in relation to global warming and climate change. The conclusion is, that we are facing a challenge that cannot be solved by the market or by technological advances, within the timeframe that we have left to act in relation to global warming and climate change. In other words, we are facing a Tragedy of the Commons Type of Challenge, which implies that political intervention is needed. Political intervention could take on many forms. It could be as a ban of fossil fuels, which is a very effective tool or a quota market, with tradable quotas for greenhouse gas emissions in a cap and trade type of market, which is a very cost-efficient tool. The cap of the market should be set within the limits of the carrying capacity. Many other types of political intervention are also imaginable. The cost of taking actions towards mitigating global warming and climate change are small. The additional annual extra cost of a fully renewable Danish energy system compared to a fossil one, would only add up to a cost of 150 Danish kroner per month per Dane. This is approximately the same as the cost of a monthly subscription for Netflix or Fitness World and it is less than what most people pay to insure themselves, their houses, cars, furniture, etc. The 150 Danish kroner per month could be seen as an insurance for having a livable planet in the future or it could be seen as an investment. By creating a fully renewable energy system focusing on no and low emission technologies, the annual societal health cost would be reduced by more than the invested 150 kroner a month. What holds us from taking action? The technology is ready and the benefits of taking early actions are big. The question is if the character of the challenge, that we are facing, keeps us from taking action.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Winther Mortensen, Anders","Dalgas Rasmussen, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-586287"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the tragedy of the planet characterizing climate change as a tragedy of the commons type of challenge","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"doi","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/144414143/Tragedy_of_the_planet_the_full_report.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-586287","ids":["sdu-2db4db19-8d24-40ad-9b24-326cb786fea8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-02A3EB1D67E1BA0FA029501A302CB789"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.sdu.dk/en/om_sdu/institutter_centre/lifecycleengineering/education/msc/18m40","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/144414143/Tragedy_of_the_planet_the_full_report.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT)","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Green Technology (IGT), SDU Life Cycle Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"winthermortensenpau","last":"Winther Mortensen","locid":"ebbcbd07-3eef-424a-b1de-c445aff55b37","name":"Winther Mortensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9510-4854","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"dalgasrasmussenpau","last":"Dalgas Rasmussen","locid":"75d6a28c-74bb-4f8a-8455-43130eeed994","name":"Dalgas Rasmussen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0002-8209-2871","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2db4db19-8d24-40ad-9b24-326cb786fea8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The tragedy of the planet? : Characterizing climate change as a tragedy of the commons type of challenge","type":"Other-Internet Publication","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-586287","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Mean arterial blood pressure (MAP) and/or pump flow during normothermic cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) are the most important factors of cerebral perfusion. The aim of this study was to explore the influence of CPB blood flow on cerebral blood flow (CBF) measured by dynamic positron emission tomography (PET) using 15O-labelled water with no pharmacological interventions to maintain the MAP. METHODS: Eight pigs (69-71 kg) were connected to normothermic CPB. After 60 minutes (min) with a CPB pump flow of 60 mL/kg/min, the pigs were changed to either 35 mL/kg/min or 47.5 mL/kg/min for 60 min and, thereafter, all the pigs returned to 60 mL/kg/min for another 60 min. The MAP was measured continuously and the CBF was measured by positron emission tomography (PET) during spontaneous circulation and at each CPB pump flow after 30 min of steady state. RESULTS: Two pigs were excluded due to complications. CBF increased from spontaneous circulation to a CPB pump flow of 60 mL/kg/min. A reduction in CPB pump flow to 47.5 mL/kg/min (n=3) resulted in only minor changes in CBF while a reduction to 35 mL/kg/min (n=3) caused a pronounced change (correlation coefficient (R2) 0.56). A return of CPB pump flow to 60 mL/kg/min was followed by an increase in CBF, except in the one pig with the lowest CBF during low flow (R2=0.44). CBF and MAP were not correlated (R2=0.20). CONCLUSION: In this experimental porcine study, a relationship was observed between pump flow and CBF under normothermic low-flow CPB. The effect of low pump flow on MAP showed substantial variations, with no correlation between CBF and MAP.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thomassen, Sisse Anette","Kjærgaard, Benedict","Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","Munk, Ole Lajord","Frøkiær, Jørgen","Larsson, Anders","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"cuid":["S02-096.05-011396"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University","Uppsala University Hospital"],"keyword":["Animal study","Animals","Blood Pressure","Body Temperature","Brain blood supply","Cardiopulmonary Bypass","Cardiopulmonary Bypass methods","Cerebral blood flow","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Female","Journal Article","Mean arterial blood pressure","Positron Emission Tomography","Positron Emission Tomography methods","Swine","pump flow"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cerebral blood flow measured by positron emission tomography during normothermic cardiopulmonary bypass an experimental porcine study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85041922035&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.05-011396","identifier":[{"id":"000434703000004","type":"wos"},{"id":"85041922035","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29380669","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-ee8d4fc5-fa87-430a-8262-e39b37204c3e","au-01957053-353f-4cea-837d-4a974f5b4cc1"],"keyword":["Animals","Blood Pressure","Body Temperature","Brain/blood supply","Cardiopulmonary Bypass/methods","Cerebrovascular Circulation","Female","Functional Neuroimaging/methods","Journal Article","Positron-Emission Tomography/methods","Swine","animal study","cardiopulmonary bypass","cerebral blood flow","mean arterial blood pressure","positron emission tomography","pump flow"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-E0AEA4B8D36ED8E67B9DFF60F29450E9"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2