I-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-ed2612bc-8a1e-4dd2-a45f-087b3ea5ddd7","ku-b570367f-a53b-43c4-be2c-0c78cbbd3870"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ancient hepatitis B viruses from the Bronze Age to the Medieval period","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.20-037867","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Muskoxen (Ovibos moschatus) are ruminants adapted to a high-fibre diet. There is increasing interest in the role that gut microbes play in the digestion and utilization of these specialized diets but only limited data available on the gut microbiome of high-Arctic animals. In this study, we metabarcoded the 16S rRNA region of faecal samples from muskoxen of Northeast Greenland, Northwest Greenland and Norway, and quantified the effects of physiological and temporal factors on bacterial composition. We found significant effects of body mass, year of sampling and location on the gut bacterial communities of North East Greenland muskoxen. These effects were however dwarfed by the effects of location, emphasizing the importance of the local ecology on the gut bacterial community. Habitat alterations and rising temperatures may therefore have a considerable impact on muskoxen health and reproductive success. Moreover, muskoxen are hunted and consumed in Greenland, Canada and Alaska; therefore, this study also screened for potential zoonoses of food safety interest. A total of 13 potentially zoonotic genera were identified, including the genera Erysipelothrix and Yersinia implicated in recent mass die-offs of the muskoxen themselves.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Andersen-Ranberg, Emilie Ulrikka","Barnes, CJ","Rasmussen, L","Salgado-Flores, A","Grøndahl, C","Mosbacher, Jesper Bruun","Hansen, AJ","Sundset, MA","Schmidt, Niels Martin","Sonne, Christian"],"cuid":["S02-099.90-027168"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["16S rRNA","Arctic","Clostridium difficile","Diet","Diversity","Erysipelothrix rhusiopathiae","Escherichia coli","Feces","Gastrointestinal tract","Gut microbiota","Metabarcoding","Muskoxen","Ovibos moschatus","Rumen","Volatile fatty acids","Zoonoses","faecal bacterial community"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a comparative study on the faecal bacterial community and potential zoonotic bacteria of muskoxen i ovibos moschatus i in northeast greenland northwest greenland and norway","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms6030076","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.90-027168","identifier":[{"id":"000446334200021","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC6164070","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"30044373","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85074977347","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c81e68be-5f9e-43c1-b354-fcb5cdbf67ee","ku-36870095-ecda-4a88-a03b-b3e5247c5f76"],"keyword":["16S rRNA","Arctic","CLOSTRIDIUM-DIFFICILE","DIET","DIVERSITY","ERYSIPELOTHRIX-RHUSIOPATHIAE","ESCHERICHIA-COLI","FECES","GASTROINTESTINAL-TRACT","GUT MICROBIOTA","Ovibos moschatus","RUMEN","VOLATILE FATTY-ACIDS","faecal bacterial community","metabarcoding","muskoxen","zoonoses"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-6AE378D88DE72B8A5F8F2788DC35F00F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3390/microorganisms6030076","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/131482323/microorganisms_06_00076_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"rem","url":"http://www.mdpi.com/2076-2607/6/3/76","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/209326419/microorganisms_06_00076_v2.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2018","yearSub":"2018"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Arctic Research Centre, Arctic Research Centre - Arctic Research Centre, Brendstrupgårdsvej"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emilie Ulrikka","key":"andersenranbergpau","last":"Andersen-Ranberg","locid":"8880ab20-9a48-436d-86da-da861a648383","name":"Andersen-Ranberg, Emilie Ulrikka","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Christopher","key":"barnespau","last":"Barnes","locid":"369a0b39-cf9f-4240-b9b4-4eb69c878bcd","name":"Barnes, Christopher James","name_org":"Barnes, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0001-6800-4233","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Linett","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0543380d-1a58-4cdf-b490-9c1861185f30","name":"Rasmussen, Linett","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"salgadoflorespau","last":"Salgado-Flores","name":"Salgado-Flores, A","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"grøndahlpau","last":"Grøndahl","name":"Grøndahl, C","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"JB","key":"mosbacherpau","last":"Mosbacher","locid":"9c13fa64-c01e-45a5-a610-91a95c7c080b","name":"Mosbacher, Jesper Bruun","name_org":"Mosbacher, JB","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"846e4329-bfc5-4ddb-968c-445cdb16825a","name":"Hansen, Anders Johannes","name_org":"Hansen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-1890-2702","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"MA","key":"sundsetpau","last":"Sundset","name":"Sundset, MA","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels Martin","key":"schmidtpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"b91704ca-e126-4c35-af20-95b2269d230a","name":"Schmidt, Niels Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-4166-6218","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C","key":"sonnepau","last":"Sonne","locid":"d9d824ac-a413-4a2a-bfbf-aff2aa7d406a","name":"Sonne, Christian","name_org":"Sonne, C","orcid":"0000-0001-5723-5263","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["30044373"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3390/microorganisms6030076","issn":["20762607"],"issue":"3","journal":"Microorganisms","paperid":"76","publisher":"MDPI AG","publisher_org":"M D P I AG","status":"p","title":"Microorganisms","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85074977347"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c81e68be-5f9e-43c1-b354-fcb5cdbf67ee","ku-36870095-ecda-4a88-a03b-b3e5247c5f76"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Comparative Study on the Faecal Bacterial Community and Potential Zoonotic Bacteria of Muskoxen (<i>Ovibos moschatus</i>) in Northeast Greenland, Northwest Greenland and Norway.","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.90-027168","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: In critically ill patients, hypoxaemia is a common clinical manifestation of inadequate gas exchange in the lungs. Supplemental oxygen is therefore given to all critically ill patients. This can result in hyperoxaemia, and some observational studies have identified harms with hyperoxia. The objective of this systematic review is to critically assess the evidence of randomised clinical trials on the effects of higher versus lower inspiratory oxygen fractions or targets of arterial oxygenation in critically ill adult patients. METHODS: We will search for randomised clinical trials in major international databases. Two authors will independently screen and select references for inclusion using Covidence, extract data and assess the methodological quality of the included randomised clinical trials using the Cochrane risk of bias tool. Any disagreement will be resolved by consensus. We will analyse the extracted data using Review Manager and Trial Sequential Analysis. To assess the quality of the evidence, we will create a 'Summary of Findings' table containing our primary and secondary outcomes using the GRADE assessment. DISCUSSION: Supplemental oxygen administration is widely recommended in international guidelines despite lack of robust evidence of its effectiveness. To our knowledge, no systematic review of randomised clinical trials has investigated the effects of oxygen supplementation in critically ill patients. This systematic review will provide reliable evidence to better inform future trialists and decision-makers on clinical practice on supplemental oxygen administration in critically ill patients.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Barbateskovic, M","Schjørring, Olav Lilleholt","Jakobsen, J C","Meyhoff, C S","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Perner, A","Wetterslev, J"],"cuid":["S03-090.77-672484"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"corresponding_author":["Barbateskovic, M."],"keyword":["Critically ill","Hypoxaemia","Intensive care","Supplemental oxygen","Systematic review","hyperoxaemia"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Copenhagen Trial Unit, Centre for Clinic alIntervention Research, CopenhagenUniversity Hospital, Copenhagen, Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oxygen supplementation for critically ill patients a protocol for a systematic review","src":["aau","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"djr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.13127","version":"Published Version"},"funding_acknowledgement":["Marija Barbateskovic is working as a PhD student and is funded by the public fund Innovation Fund Denmark; who had no role in the design of this protocol and will not have any role in the systematic review execution, analyses, interpretation of the data, or decision to submit results. No other sources of financial support were obtained for this protocol Marija Barbateskovic: PhD student at the Centre for Research in Intensive Care and Copenhagen Trial Unit. The PhD is funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark; which is a public fund. Olav L Schjørring: PhD student at the Centre for Research in Intensive Care and Aalborg University Hospital. The PhD is funded by the Innovation Fund Denmark; which is a public fund. Dr Schjørring is the co-ordination investigator of the HOT-ICU (Handling Oxygenation Targets in the Intensive Care Unit) trial investigating higher versus lower oxygenation targets in patients admitted to the ICU. Janus Christian Jakobsen: Director of Research, Chief Physician, Department of Cardiology, Holbæk Syge-hus, Holbæk, Denmark. Christian S Meyhoff: Head of Research at Department of Anaesthesiology and Intensive Care Medicine, Bispeb-jerg and Frederiksberg Hospital. The department directly and indirectly receives research funding from Ferring Pharmaceuticals, Boehringer Ingelheim, and Merck Sharp and Dohme. CM was the principal investigator of the PROXI trial (PeRioperative OXygen fraction) investigating higher versus lower concentrations of perioperative inspiratory oxygen (Meyhoff 2009). Furthermore, he is a principle investigator of the HOT-ICU trial. Bodil S Rasmussen: Head of Research in the ICU at Aalborg University Hospital. The ICU receives support for research from Ferring Pharmaceuticals. Dr Rasmussen is sponsor and a principle investigator of the HOT-ICU trial. Anders Perner: Head of Research in the ICU at Rigshospitalet. The ICU receives support for research from CSL Behring, Fresenius Kabi and Ferring Pharmaceuticals. Dr Perner is a member of the steering group of the HOT-ICU trial. Jørn Wetterslev: member of the Copenhagen Trial Unit task force for developing TSA theory, manual and software and he was also an investigator in the PROXI trial of higher versus lower concentrations of perioperative inspiratory oxygen (Meyhoff 2009). Furthermore, Dr Wetterslev is a member of the steering group of the HOT-ICU trial."],"id":"S03-090.77-672484","identifier":[{"id":"85046089650","type":"scopus"},{"id":"29708586","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-e6be7101-4a43-444f-bccf-e9766b735c9c","ku-a0311308-fa56-4e60-9474-1072a2ac8566","sdu-49c206c3-d57f-449f-8176-06f85397e8fb"],"keyword":["critically ill","hyperoxaemia","hypoxaemia","intensive care","supplemental oxygen","systematic review"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-F0071F4EE51A2E5E1720E03AE73B73A2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/aas.13127","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":