":"Hans Vammen 28. juli 1940 - 17. maj 2017","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-394019","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The medial prefrontal cortex (PFC) plays a major role in executive function by exerting a top-down control onto subcortical areas. Novelty-induced frontal cortex activation is 5-HT2A receptor (5-HT2AR) dependent. Here, we further investigated how blockade of 5-HT2ARs in mice exposed to a novel open-field arena affects medial PFC activation and basolateral amygdala (BLA) reactivity. We used c-Fos immunoreactivity (IR) as a marker of neuronal activation and stereological quantification for obtaining the total number of c-Fos-IR neurons as a measure of regional activation. We further examined the impact of 5-HT2AR blockade on the striatal-projecting BLA neurons. Systemic administration of ketanserin (0.5 mg/kg) prior to novel open-field exposure resulted in reduced total numbers of c-Fos-IR cells in dorsomedial PFC areas and the BLA. Moreover, there was a positive correlation between the relative time spent in the centre of the open-field and BLA c-Fos-IR in the ketanserin-treated animals. Unilateral medial PFC lesions blocked this effect, ascertaining an involvement of this frontal cortex area. On the other hand, medial PFC lesioning exacerbated the more anxiogenic-like behaviour of the ketanserin-treated animals, upholding its involvement in modulating averseness. Ketanserin did not affect the number of activated striatal-projecting BLA neurons (measured by number of Cholera Toxin b (CTb) retrograde labelled neurons also being c-Fos-IR) following CTb injection in the ventral striatum. These results support a role of 5-HT2AR activation in modulating mPFC and BLA activation during exposure to a novel environment, which may be interrelated. Conversely, 5-HT2AR blockade does not seem to affect the amygdala-striatal projection.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Hervig, Mona El Sayed","Jensen, Nadja Cecilie Hvid","Rasmussen, Nadja Bredo","Rydbirk, Rasmus","Olesen, Mikkel Vestergaard","Hay-Schmidt, Anders","Pakkenberg, Bente","Aznar, Susana"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-396360"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["5 HT2A receptor","Brain Mapping","Serotonin","Stereology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"involvement of serotonin 000000000002a receptor activation in modulating medial prefrontal cortex and amygdala neuronal activation during novelty exposure","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-396360","identifier":[{"id":"000401678300001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85014691865","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28263831","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-04d8f65a-2c10-4af4-b8c7-8a70ed9b42fd"],"keyword":["5-HT2A receptor","Averseness","Brain mapping","Frontolimbic pathway","Serotonin","Stereology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C210B5B0B4FCAE9B93AEC9149F0824D4"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Mona El-Sayed","key":"hervigpau","last":"Hervig","locid":"fe589ba9-8399-4ba3-850e-8afd02ca2bfc","name":"Hervig, Mona El Sayed","name_org":"Hervig, Mona El-Sayed","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nadja Cecilie Hvid","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Nadja Cecilie Hvid","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Nadja Bredo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Nadja Bredo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Rasmus","key":"rydbirkpau","last":"Rydbirk","name":"Rydbirk, Rasmus","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mikkel Vestergaard","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Mikkel Vestergaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"hayschmidtpau","last":"Hay-Schmidt","locid":"f0f495a2-fe48-4cdf-8f27-ea207182bda8","name":"Hay-Schmidt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9984-7014","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Bente","key":"pakkenbergpau","last":"Pakkenberg","locid":"437c7aac-d274-499d-a20f-91f2e7b5f080","name":"Pakkenberg, Bente","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Susana","key":"aznarpau","last":"Aznar","name":"Aznar, Susana","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28263831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.bbr.2017.02.050","issn":["01664328","18727549"],"issn_org":["01664328"],"journal":"Behavioural Brain Research","pages":"1-12","status":"p","title":"Behavioural Brain Research","volume":"326"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85014691865"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-04d8f65a-2c10-4af4-b8c7-8a70ed9b42fd"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Involvement of serotonin 2A receptor activation in modulating medial prefrontal cortex and amygdala neuronal activation during novelty-exposure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-396360","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"This article reviews the experimental progress in hybrid superconducting devices based on quantum wires, in the form of semiconductor nanowires or carbon nanotubes, which are coupled to superconducting electrodes. It also presents a series of recent examples which illustrate the key phenomena that have allowed detailed investigations of important scenarios, including individual impurities on superconductors and proximitized systems that may hold Majorana quasiparticles. After describing experimental aspects of hybrid devices, including materials and fabrication techniques, the article considers superconducting junctions with normal quantum dots (QDs). It then turns to experiments on superconductivity-enhanced QD spectroscopy, sub-gap states in hybrid QDs, and non-local signals in Cooper pair splitter devices. Finally, it discusses the growth of epitaxial semiconductor–superconductor nanowire hybrids.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Grove-Rasmussen, Kasper","Jespersen, Thomas Sand","Jellinggaard, Anders Robert","Nygård, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397722"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hybrid superconducting devices based on quantum wires","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-397722","ids":["ku-07162072-2db3-46ef-9729-6ee365dafdda"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-1B4C518834A93FAE712876BD210551DF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Condensed Matter Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Kasper","key":"groverasmussenpau","last":"Grove-Rasmussen","locid":"0978d760-cac6-4c02-8c3e-84a539f85317","name":"Grove-Rasmussen, Kasper","orcid":"0000-0003-2340-2048","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas Sand","key":"jespersenpau","last":"Jespersen","locid":"65fc2107-0d74-41f9-96cb-4ee1b8677f2e","name":"Jespersen, Thomas Sand","orcid":"0000-0002-7879-976X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Robert","key":"jellinggaardpau","last":"Jellinggaard","locid":"3df7e063-9aba-4d1b-b20e-f54ebbc6a1c5","name":"Jellinggaard, Anders Robert","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jesper","key":"nygårdpau","last":"Nygård","locid":"a9f6df21-02fe-407f-8472-6e4a496f8ec0","name":"Nygård, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-4639-5314","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"A.V.","key":"narlikarpedh","last":"Narlikar","name":"Narlikar, A.V.","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1093/oxfordhb/9780198738169.013.16","edition":"Oxford","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Chapter in The Oxford Handbook of Small Superconductors"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-07162072-2db3-46ef-9729-6ee365dafdda"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hybrid Superconducting Devices Based on Quantum Wires","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-397722","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
