{"abstract":"This letter presents an experimental study and a novel modelling approach of the wireless channel of smart utility meters placed in basements or sculleries. The experimental data consist of signal strength measurements of consumption report packets. Since such packets are only registered if they can be decoded by the receiver, the part of the signal strength distribution that falls below the receiver sensitivity threshold is not observable. We combine a Rician fading model with a bias function that captures the cut-off in the observed signal strength measurements. Two sets of experimental data are analysed. It is shown that the proposed method offers an approximation of the distribution of the signal strength measurements that is better than a naïve Rician fitting.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Kielgast, Mathias Rønholt","Rasmussen, Anders Charly","Laursen, Mathias Hjorth","Nielsen, Jimmy Jessen","Popovski, Petar","Krigslund, Rasmus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-104328"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-KAM"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-KAM","DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"estimation of received signal strength distribution for smart meters with biased measurement data set","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/LWC.2016.2619346","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-104328","identifier":[{"id":"000395868700001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85013626855","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-bb084e73-681c-4bb4-89c1-99e51949ea9e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FC82700EE5657D8001D04AC2D9539D1F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1610.05094.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/LWC.2016.2619346","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Electronic Systems, Antennas, propagation and radio networking"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"kamstrup","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-KAM","l3nn":"Kamstrup","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Kamstrup","namevar":["Kamstrup A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-KAM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Rønholt","key":"kielgastpau","last":"Kielgast","locid":"9eefa2ed-5f8d-4b2a-bf0a-221c5b9f32a9","name":"Kielgast, Mathias Rønholt","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Charly","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f9eb493f-9265-4936-a6ff-d6d92e67cdcb","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Charly","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mathias Hjorth","key":"laursenpau","last":"Laursen","locid":"1f3b1c68-3926-4baf-82c7-c16b20f961bd","name":"Laursen, Mathias Hjorth","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jimmy Jessen","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"49f52771-fa54-4f41-855d-0628e645479e","name":"Nielsen, Jimmy Jessen","orcid":"0000-0001-6664-7198","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Petar","key":"popovskipau","last":"Popovski","locid":"393886d2-0dbf-4356-84fe-3a1138a9c51f","name":"Popovski, Petar","orcid":"0000-0001-6195-4797","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"krigslundpau","last":"Krigslund","name":"Krigslund, Rasmus","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/lwc.2016.2619346","issn":["21622337"],"issue":"1","journal":"IEEE Wireless Communications Letters","pages":"2-5","publisher":"IEEE Communications Society","status":"p","title":"IEEE Wireless Communications Letters","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85013626855"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bb084e73-681c-4bb4-89c1-99e51949ea9e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Estimation of Received Signal Strength Distribution for Smart Meters with Biased Measurement Data Set","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-104328","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Emil","Hansen, Anders Sybrandt","Grue, Astrid","Johnsen, Ulrik Høj"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-223651"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"værdi","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/jf/issue/view/9058/1330","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-223651","ids":["au-a57edbaf-9ac5-4838-8271-d0f3689fccbd"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-49A8B845E0CD9CAFFA5FFD5DECC35113"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://tidsskrift.dk/jf/issue/view/9058/1330","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Emil","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Emil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Sybrandt","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"4962ee31-d4df-4c18-a98c-970ad9112588","name":"Hansen, Anders Sybrandt","orcid":"0000-0001-9252-4757","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Astrid","key":"gruepau","last":"Grue","name":"Grue, Astrid","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ulrik Høj","key":"johnsenpau","last":"Johnsen","locid":"85697344-2821-45e5-bdec-36fc1cbfee96","name":"Johnsen, Ulrik Høj","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00217484","25970674"],"issn_org":["00217484"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Jordens Folk","pages":"3-5","publisher":"Dansk Etnografisk Forening","status":"p","title":"Jordens Folk","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a57edbaf-9ac5-4838-8271-d0f3689fccbd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Værdi","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-223651","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Integrating the plasma core performance with an edge and scrape-off layer (SOL) that leads to tolerable heat and particle loads on the wall is a major challenge. The new European medium size tokamak task force (EU-MST) coordinates research on ASDEX Upgrade (AUG), MAST and TCV. This multi-machine approach within EU-MST, covering a wide parameter range, is instrumental to progress in the field, as ITER and DEMO core/pedestal and SOL parameters are not achievable simultaneously in present day devices. A two prong approach is adopted. On the one hand, scenarios with tolerable transient heat and particle loads, including active edge localised mode (ELM) control are developed. On the other hand, divertor solutions including advanced magnetic configurations are studied. Considerable progress has been made on both approaches, in particular in the fields of: ELM control with resonant magnetic perturbations (RMP), small ELM regimes, detachment onset and control, as well as filamentary scrape-off-layer transport. For example full ELM suppression has now been achieved on AUG at low collisionality with n  =  2 RMP maintaining good confinement HH(98,y2)≈0.95 Advances have been made with respect to detachment onset and control. Studies in advanced divertor configurations (Snowflake, Super-X and X-point target divertor) shed new light on SOL physics. Cross field filamentary transport has been characterised in a wide parameter regime on AUG, MAST and TCV progressing the theoretical and experimental understanding crucial for predicting first wall loads in ITER and DEMO. Conditions in the SOL also play a crucial role for ELM stability and access to small ELM regimes.","author_count":527,"contributors":["Meyer, H.","Eich, T.","Beurskens, M.","Coda, S.","Hakola, A.H.","Martin, P.","Adamek, J.","Agostini, M.","Aguiam, D.","Ahn, J.","Aho-Mantila, L.","Akers, R.","Albanese, R.","Aledda, R.","Alessi, E.","Allan, Jonathan S.","da Costa Alves Machado, Simone","Ambrosino, R.","Ami