"Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-9c536714-eedc-4a18-9e90-8849295f34b8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"“Patienter ‘on the road’ : Patientinvolvering og kronisk sygdom”","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-617986","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Academic Spin-Offs are given the mission to bring to society science and technology innovations. Nevertheless, the relative weak financial performance of these firms has recently been a focus of discussion. Prior research has explored factors that might explain the performance diversity, including aspects related to the academic entrepreneur (e.g. human capital), organizational (e.g. team characteristics, board composition, network of partners) and institutional factors (e.g. university context, support mechanisms). An under studied potential source of heterogeneity is the diversity of technologies that these firms are based on. Research has established that academic spin-offs exhibit a wide range of technologies, that novel technologies lead to the creation of new firms and that these firms are more innovative compared to their corporate counterparts. However, there is limited knowledge testing the relationship between innovativeness and firm performance. This study tests the relationship between innovativeness across different industries and future firm performance. This paper uses several market performance indicators to observe the variety of firm sales of academic spin-offs. A longitudinal sample, between 2000 and 2012, of 125 academic spin-offs of Norway provides valuable insights on how the origin of the technology impact differences in market performance. The results show how specific elements related to the ASOs’ product innovativeness contribute to its market performance. The findings provide insights for policy makers and university managers interested in understanding the effects of their policy choices on the underlying technological nature of academic spin-offs.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Giones, Ferran","Billström, Anders","Rasmussen, Einar","Novotny, Adam"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-634054"],"event":{"end":"2017-06-06","place":"Bologna, it","start":"2017-06-04","title":"University-Industry Collaborations and Academic Entrepreneurship: East Meets West","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Nord University"],"keyword":["Academic entrepreneurship","Entrepreneurship","Innovation","University industry collaboration"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a longitudinal study of the effects of innovativeness on academic spin offs performance","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-634054","ids":["sdu-d46938c2-c7f3-49fd-aaed-a47267c108b6"],"keyword":["Academic entrepreneurship","Entrepreneurship","Innovation","University-Industry Collaboration"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-DDA67E37257BF9A5EC4ECB02DBFB2423"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Department of Technology and Innovation, SDU Technology Entrepreneurship and Innovation","SDU, The Faculty of Engineering, Mads Clausen Institute (MCI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"nord university","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nord University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ferran","key":"gionespau","last":"Giones","locid":"907136be-386d-4797-a898-9e0fabf933ba","name":"Giones, Ferran","orcid":"0000-0002-1927-6918","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"billströmpau","last":"Billström","name":"Billström, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Einar","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Einar","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Adam","key":"novotnypau","last":"Novotny","name":"Novotny, Adam","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d46938c2-c7f3-49fd-aaed-a47267c108b6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A Longitudinal Study of the Effects of Innovativeness on Academic Spin-offs Performance","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-634054","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Emil"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-693761"],"filters":{"added":"2023-11","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"værdi på kanten af småt brændbart","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-693761","ids":["au-68004012-a399-4e34-a56f-c3c4f1cbb413"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-15AC8BB33EAC8A91262A1B6CF13FEFE3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Department of Anthropology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Emil","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"29fd4913-24ba-4f16-a5e1-6c84d4a64c83","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Emil","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00217484","25970674"],"issn_org":["00217484"],"issue":"1-2","journal":"Jordens Folk","pages":"38-46","paperid":"4","publisher":"Dansk Etnografisk Forening","status":"p","title":"Jordens Folk","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-68004012-a399-4e34-a56f-c3c4f1cbb413"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Værdi på kanten af småt brændbart","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-693761","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background.: Treatment with latency reversing agents (LRAs) enhances human immunodeficiency virus type 1 (HIV-1) transcription in vivo but leads to only modest reductions in the size of the reservoir, possibly due to insufficient immune-mediated elimination of infected cells. We hypothesized that a single drug molecule-a novel Toll-like receptor 9 (TLR9) agonist, MGN1703-could function as an enhancer of innate immunity and an LRA in vivo. Methods.: We conducted a single-arm, open-label study in which 15 virologically suppressed HIV-1-infected individuals on antiretroviral therapy received 60 mg MGN1703 subcutaneously twice weekly for 4 weeks. We characterized plasmacytoid dendritic cell, natural killer (NK), and T-cell activation using flow cytometry on baseline and after 4 weeks of treatment. HIV-1 transcription was quantified by measuring plasma HIV-1 RNA during MGN1703 administration. Results.: In accordance with the cell type-specific expression of TLR9, MGN1703 treatment led to pronounced activation of plasmacytoid dendritic cells and substantial increases in plasma interferon-α2 levels (P < .0001). Consistently, transcription of interferon-stimulated genes (eg, OAS1, ISG15, Mx1; each P < .0001) were upregulated in CD4+ T cells as demonstrated by RNA sequencing. Further, proportions of activated cytotoxic NK cells and CD8+ T cells increased significantly during MGN1703 dosing, suggesting an enhancement of cellular immune responses. In 6 of 15 participants, plasma HIV-1 RNA increased from <20 copies/mL to >1500 copies/mL (range, 21-1571 copies/mL) during treatment. Conclusions.: TLR9 agonist treatment in HIV infection has a dual potential by increasing HIV-1 transcription and enhancing cytotoxic NK cell activation, both of which are key outcomes in HIV-1 eradication therapy. Clinical Trials Registration.: NCT02443935.","author_count":33,"contributors":["Vibholm, Line K.","Schleimann, Mariane Høgsbjerg","Højen, Jesper Falkesgaard","Benfield, Thomas","Offersen, Rasmus","Rasmussen, Katrine","Olesen, Rikke","Dige, Anders","Agnholt, Jørgen","Grau, Judith","Buzon, Maria J","Wittig, Burghardt","Lichterfeld, Mathias","Petersen, Andreas Munk","Deng, Xutao","Abdel-Mohsen, Mohammed","Pillai, Satish K","Rutsaert, Sofie","Trypsteen, Wim","De Spiegelaere, Ward","Vandekerchove, Linos","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Rasmussen, Thomas A","Denton, Paul W","Tolstrup, Martin","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz"],"cuid":["S02-083.10-026750"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Germany","Spain","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Free University of Berlin","Ghent University","Harvard-MIT Division of Health Sciences and Technology","University of California at San Francisco","Vall d'Hebron Research Institute"],"keyword":["Antiretroviral Therapy Highly Active","CD8 Positive T Lymphocytes drug effects","Cytokines genetics","Dendritic Cells drug effects","Female","HIV 1 drug effects","HIV Infections drug therapy","Humans","Immunity Innate drug effects","Journal Article","Killer Cells Natural drug effects","Lymphocyte Activation drug effects","Male","Middle Aged","Myxovirus Resistance Proteins genetics","Toll Like Receptor 9 agonists"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short course toll like receptor 000000000009 agonist treatment impacts innate immunity and plasma viremia in individuals with human immunodeficiency virus infection","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85021100122","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-083.10-026750","identifier":[