{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: To investigate whether changes in muscle tissue perfusion measured with positron emission tomography would be reflected by parallel changes in muscle tissue oxygen saturation (StO2) measured using near-infrared spectroscopy during high and low blood flow levels achieved using cardiopulmonary bypass (CPB) in an animal model. DESIGN: A prospective, randomized study. SETTING: Research laboratory, single institution. PARTICIPANTS: Eight pigs (69-71 kg). INTERVENTIONS: In anesthetized pigs, normothermic CPB was established with a blood flow of 60 mL/kg/min for 1 hour. Thereafter, a low blood flow of either 47.5 or 35 mL/kg/min was applied for 1 hour followed by a blood flow of 60 mL/kg/min for an additional hour. Regional StO2 was measured continuously by placing a near-infrared spectroscopy electrode on the skin above the gracilis muscle of the noncannulated back leg. Muscle tissue perfusion was measured using positron emission tomography with (15)O-labeled water during spontaneous circulation and the different CPB blood flows. Systemic oxygen consumption was estimated by measurement of venous saturation and lactate levels. MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS: The results showed profound systemic ischemia during low CPB blood flow. StO2 remained high until muscle tissue perfusion decreased to about 50%, after which StO2 paralleled the linear decrease in muscle tissue perfusion. CONCLUSION: In an experimental CPB animal model, StO2 was stable until muscle tissue perfusion was reduced by about 50%, and at lower blood flow levels, there was almost a linear relationship between StO2 and muscle tissue perfusion.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Thomassen, Sisse Anette","Kjærgaard, Benedict","Olsen Alstrup, Aage Kristian","Munk, Ole Lajord","Frøkiær, Jørgen","Larsson, Anders","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-008069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Uppsala University"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"muscle tissue saturation compared with muscle tissue perfusion during low blood flows an experimental study","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85021854112","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-008069","identifier":[{"id":"000418210800024","type":"wos"},{"id":"85021854112","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28693932","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-a6cd33b0-8e6c-41f1-b0d0-503300234b00","au-bb172a29-d4ad-422b-b2f3-1d703ae172e2"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-768312E5344B1AB58740340E2FA94B13"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Anæstesi og Intensiv [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"central denmark region","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CDR","l3nl":"Central Denmark Region","l3nn":"Central Denmark Region","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Central Denmark Region","namevar":["Aarhus University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CDR","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sisse Anette","key":"thomassenpau","last":"Thomassen","locid":"73e2edc3-99c7-480b-830d-e5e7631b9179","name":"Thomassen, Sisse Anette","orcid":"0000-0003-0955-4600","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Benedict","key":"kjærgaardpau","last":"Kjærgaard","locid":"3afc0400-089d-4805-be84-ecdf45e6e318","name":"Kjærgaard, Benedict","orcid":"0000-0001-5797-7638","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Aage Kristian","key":"olsenalstruppau","last":"Olsen Alstrup","locid":"fa66f5b8-0468-4e85-b570-969776c5ebde","name":"Alstrup, Aage Kristian Olsen","name_org":"Olsen Alstrup, Aage Kristian","orcid":"0000-0002-0084-9122","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Lajord","key":"munkpau","last":"Munk","locid":"420e3a6e-40ef-462a-923a-d13976538a05","name":"Munk, Ole Lajord","orcid":"0000-0002-7232-5088","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen","key":"frøkiærpau","last":"Frøkiær","locid":"49d24192-9cad-4d32-88ee-cf46bb315b72","name":"Frøkiær, Jørgen","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"larssonpau","last":"Larsson","name":"Larsson, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil Steen","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3162c449-94c3-4d28-8dbb-c134d6eb76e1","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","orcid":"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28693932"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1053/j.jvca.2017.03.027","issn":["10530770","15328422"],"issn_org":["10530770"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Anesthesia","pages":"2065-2071","publisher":"WB  Saunders","publisher_org":"W.B. Saunders","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cardiothoracic and Vascular Anesthesia","volume":"31(6)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85021854112"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Central Denmark Region","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a6cd33b0-8e6c-41f1-b0d0-503300234b00","au-bb172a29-d4ad-422b-b2f3-1d703ae172e2"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Muscle Tissue Saturation Compared With Muscle Tissue Perfusion During Low Blood Flows : An Experimental Study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-008069","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The human Y-chromosome does not recombine across its male-specific part and is therefore an excellent marker of human migrations. It also plays an important role in male fertility. However, its evolution is difficult to fully understand because of repetitive sequences, inverted repeats and the potentially large role of gene conversion. Here we perform an evolutionary analysis of 62 Y-chromosomes of Danish descent sequenced using a wide range of library insert sizes and high coverage, thus allowing large regions of these chromosomes to be well assembled. These include 17 father-son pairs, which we use to validate variation calling. Using a recent method that can integrate variants based on both mapping and de novo assembly, we genotype 10898 SNVs and 2903 indels (max length of 27241 bp) in our sample and show by father-son concordance and experimental validation that the non-recurrent SNP and indel variation on the Y chromosome tree is called very accurately. This includes variation called in a 0.9 Mb centromeric heterochromatic region, which is by far the most variable in the Y chromosome. Among the variation is also longer sequence-stretches not present in the reference genome but shared with the chimpanzee Y chromosome. We analyzed 2.7 Mb of large inverted repeats (palindromes) for variation patterns among the two palindrome arms and identified 603 mutation and 416 gene conversions events. We find clear evidence for GC-biased gene conversion in the palindromes (and a balancing AT mutation bias), but irrespective of this, also a strong bias towards gene conversion towards the ancestral state, suggesting that palindromic gene conversion may alleviate Muller’s ratchet. Finally, we also find a large number of large-scale gene duplications and deletions in the palindromic regions (at least 24) and find that such events can consist of complex combinations of simultaneous insertions and deletions of long stretches of the Y chromosome.","author_count":45,"contributors":["Gonzalez-Izarzugaza, Jose Maria","Skov, Laurits","Maretty, Lasse","Jensen, Jacob Malte","Petersen, Bent","Andreas Sibbesen, Jonas","Liu, Siyang","Villesen, Palle","Belling, Kirstine C.","Theil Have, Christian","Gonzalez-Izarzugaza, Jose Maria","Grosjean, Marie","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Grove, Jakob","Als, Thomas D.","Huang, Shujia","Chang, Yuqi","Xu, Ruiqi","Ye, Weijian","Rao, Junhua","Guo, Xiaosen","Sun, Jihua","Cao, Hongzhi","Ye, Chen","van Beusekom, Johan","Espeseth, Thomas","Flindt, Esben","Friborg, Rune M.","Halager, Anders E.","Le Hellard, Stephanie","Hultman, Christina M.","Lescai, Francesco","Li, Shengting","Lund, Ole","Løngren, Peter","Mailund, Thomas","Matey-Hernandez, María Luisa","Mors, Ole","Pedersen, Christian N. S.","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Sullivan, Patrick F.","Ali, Syed","Westergaard, David","Yadav, Rachita","Li, Ning","Xu, Xun","Hansen, Torben","Krogh, Anders","Bolund, Lars","Sørensen, Thorkild I. A.","Pedersen, Oluf","Gupta, Ramneek","Rasmussen, Simon","Besenbacher, Søren","Børglum, Anders D.","Wang, Jun","Eiberg, Hans","Kristiansen, Karsten","Brunak, Søren","Schierup, Mikkel Heide"],"cuid":["S03-082.72-666064"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corpau":["Danish Pan Genome Consortium"],"corresponding_author":["Skov, Laurits"],"country":["China","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","Karolinska Institutet","University of Bergen","University of Bristol"],"keyword":["Alignment","Chromosomes Human Y genetics","Copy number variation","Denmark","Evolution","Evolution Molecular","Expression","Fathers","Genome","Heterochromatin genetics","Humans","INDEL Mutation genetics","Infertility Male genetics","Male","Male infertility","Mutation","Nuclear Family","Phylogeny","Polymorphism","Polymorphism Single Nucleotide","Population","Sequence"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analysis of 000000000062 hybrid assembled human y chromosomes exposes rapid structural changes and high rates of gene conversion","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1006834","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-082.72-666064","identifier":[{"id":"000408763800001","type":"wos"},{"id":"85028845628","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5591018","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"28846694","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-0695b9f3-994d-4ead-adcb-d561547e16d1","dtu-9093eec5-9cc8-4d51-82b2-e49aac0215b9","ku-0a9598b4-4a0a-4a39-b6f6-7fdd1bb7aee5"],"keyword":["ALIGNMENT","COPY NUMBER VARIATION","Chromosomes, Human, Y/genetics","Denmark","EVOLUTION","EXPRESSION","Evolution, Molecular","Fathers","GENOME","Gene Conversion/genetics","Heterochromatin/genetics","Humans","INDEL Mutation/genetics","Infertility, Male/genetics","Inverted Repeat Sequences/genetics","MALE-INFERTILITY","MUTATION","Male","Nuclear Family","POLYMORPHISM","POPULATION","Phylogeny","Polymorphism, Single Nucleotide","SEQUENCE"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C4A4A8F97C977E6F4436678ACB7F120D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/118727666/journal.pgen.1006834.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/138294168/journal.pgen.1006834.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pgen.1006834","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realise