:"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Jun","key":"wangjunpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, Jun","rank":56,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"8","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"eiberghanspau","last":"Eiberg","name":"Eiberg, Hans","rank":57,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren","key":"brunaksørenpau","last":"Brunak","locid":"9271e149-2d33-4911-bc53-8d5180f08c00","name":"Brunak, Søren","orcid":"0000-0003-0316-5866","rank":59,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28846694"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pgen.1006834","issn":["15537390","15537404"],"issn_org":["15537404"],"issue":"8","journal":"PLoS Genetics","paperid":"1006834","publisher":"Public Library of Science","status":"p","title":"PLoS Genetics","title_org":"P L o S Genetics (Online)","volume":"13"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85028845628"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","bgi europe a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-0695b9f3-994d-4ead-adcb-d561547e16d1","dtu-9093eec5-9cc8-4d51-82b2-e49aac0215b9","ku-0a9598b4-4a0a-4a39-b6f6-7fdd1bb7aee5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","DTU Technical University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analysis of 62 hybrid assembled human Y chromosomes exposes rapid structural changes and high rates of gene conversion","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-082.72-666064","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND AND AIMS: Intestinal failure (IF) is a serious and common complication of short bowel syndrome with patients depending on parental nutrition (PN) support. Effective nutrition management requires an accurate estimation of the patient's basal metabolic rate (BMR) to avoid underfeeding or overfeeding. However, indirect calorimetry, considered the gold standard for BMR assessment, is a time- and resource-consuming procedure. Consequently, several equations for prediction of BMR have been developed in different settings, but their accuracy in patients with IF are yet to be investigated. We evaluated the accuracy of predicted BMR in clinically stable patients with IF dependent on home parenteral nutrition (HPN). METHODS: In total, 103 patients with IF were included. We used indirect calorimetry for assessment of BMR and calculated predicted BMR using different equations based on anthropometric and/or bioelectrical impedance parameters. The accuracy of predicted BMR was evaluated using Bland-Altman analysis with measured BMR as the gold standard. RESULTS: The average measured BMR was 1272 ± 245 kcal/d. The most accurate estimations of BMR were obtained using the Harris-Benedict equation (mean bias, 14 kcal/d [P = .28]; limits of agreement [LoA], -238 to 266 kcal/d) and the Johnstone equation (mean bias, -16 kcal/d [P = .24]; LoA, -285 to 253 kcal/d). For both equations, 67% of patients had a predicted BMR from 90%-110% All other equations demonstrated a statistically and clinically significant difference between measured and predicted BMR. CONCLUSIONS: The Harris-Benedict and Johnstone equations reliably predict BMR in two-thirds of clinically stable patients with IF on HPN.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Andersen, Anders Skallerup","Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Olesen, Søren Schou","Vinter-Jensen, Lars","Køhler, Marianne","Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-058562"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can we rely on predicted basal metabolic rate in patients with intestinal failure on home parenteral nutrition","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-058562","identifier":[{"id":"27358330","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000413493900008","type":"wos"},{"id":"85032871719","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-1d2ee054-4970-4969-a2dc-fe31deccb663"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C888C98B3CFC4D77667DB7AEC03CC6D6"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Medicinske Mave- og Tarmsygdomme (Gastroenterologi og Hepatologi) [Klinik Medicin]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Skallerup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8839002b-110b-495b-a386-4df5b8d161e5","name":"Andersen, Anders Skallerup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Schou","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"0395fceb-e2ff-4fe2-8abc-c5486a437197","name":"Olesen, Søren Schou","orcid":"0000-0003-3916-3168","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"vinterjensenpau","last":"Vinter-Jensen","locid":"9bec0a4a-7fda-4f11-bbed-02e75dc2aa02","name":"Vinter-Jensen, Lars","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"køhlerpau","last":"Køhler","locid":"344b7efa-d1ef-43bf-b4b4-1722e24a2ca3","name":"Køhler, Marianne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Højgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c242f457-53f4-4b88-82f3-d7fb297cf98c","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27358330"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0148607116657648","issn":["01486071","19412444"],"issn_org":["01486071"],"issue":"7","journal":"Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition","pages":"1139-1145","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Parenteral and Enteral Nutrition","volume":"41"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85032871719"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-1d2ee054-4970-4969-a2dc-fe31deccb663"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Can We Rely on Predicted Basal Metabolic Rate in Patients With Intestinal Failure on Home Parenteral Nutrition?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-058562","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: The aim of this study was to investigate whether there is a similar mortality and thrombo-embolic risk, after an atrial ablation procedure, compared with an atrial fibrillation (AF) procedure. METHODS AND RESULTS: Using data from nationwide Danish health registries, we identified patients aged 18-75 years undergoing a first-time atrial flutter or an AF ablation procedure in the period 2000-13. Cox proportional hazards regression was used to calculate hazard ratios (HRs) after 5 years of follow-up, adjusting for concomitant risk factors. A total of 1096 and 2266 patients underwent an ablation for atrial flutter or AF, respectively. Age distribution was similar in the two, but atrial flutter patients had more co-morbidities. During 5 years of follow-up, we observed 38 and 36 deaths in the atrial flutter and AF groups, corresponding to an almost two-fold higher mortality rate among atrial flutter patients [crude HR 1.92, 95% confidence interval (CI) 1.22-3.03]. The higher mortality rate persisted after adjustment for age, sex, diabetes mellitus, and hypertension (adjusted HR 1.68, 95% CI 1.05-2.69). The rate of thrombo-embolic events was similar in the two groups (crude HR 1.34, 95% CI 0.71-2.56; adjusted HR 1.22, 95% CI 0.62-2.41). CONCLUSION: In this observational study, patients with atrial flutter had a significantly higher all-cause mortality rate compared with those with AF after an ablation procedure, but similar thrombo-embolic event rates. Future studies should elucidate the reason for this difference in mortality.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Vadmann, Henrik","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Hjortshøj, Søren Pihlkjær","Riahi, Sam","Lip, Gregory Y H","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-095916"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"death and thrombo embolic risk after ablation of atrial flutter compared with atrial fibrillation a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-095916","identifier":[{"id":"000404444200031","type":"wos"},{"id":"27738075","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85027418366","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-9e2e0864-8e7a-4aca-9b5e-294287264d39"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C0373FE97996818DF001B09E6908D115"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Aalborg AF Study Group","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"vadmannpau","last":