{"abstract":"Context: Members of the insulin-like growth factor (IGF) system are primarily produced in the liver and secreted into the circulation, but they are also produced, recruited, and activated locally in tissues. Objective: To compare activity and concentrations of IGF system components in pleural fluid and blood. Design: Pathological pleural fluid, secondary to lung cancer or nonmalignant disease, and matching blood samples were collected from 24 patients ages 66.7 to 81.9 years. Methods: IGF-related proteins and cytokine levels were measured by immunoassays or immunoblotting. Bioactive IGF was measured by an IGF-1 receptor phosphorylation assay. Results: Total IGF-1 concentration did not differ between the compartments, but concentrations of free IGF-1 and bioactive IGF were more than threefold higher in pleural fluid than in corresponding serum samples (P = 0.0004), regardless of etiology. Median pregnancy-associated plasma protein-A (PAPP-A) and interleukin (IL)-6 levels were increased 47-fold and 143-fold, respectively, in pleural fluid compared with plasma (P , 0.0001). PAPP-A and IL-6 concentrations correlated positively (r = 0.46; P = 0.02). In pleural fluid, levels of PAPP-A-generated IGF binding protein-4 fragments correlated inversely with that of stanniocalcin-2 (r # 20.42; P # 0.05), a PAPP-A inhibitor; such correlations were absent in plasma. Conclusion: Pathological pleural fluid is characterized by increased in vitro IGF bioactivity and elevated concentrations of PAPP-A, an IGF-activating proteinase. Thus, the tissue activity of the IGF system may differ substantially from that of the circulating IGF system. The correlation between IL-6 and PAPP-A indicates that inflammation plays a role in promoting local tissue IGF activity.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Espelund, Ulrick","Bjerre, Mette","Hjortebjerg, Rikke","Rasmussen, Torben Riis","Lundby, Anders","Hoeflich, Andreas","Folkersen, Birgitte Holst","Oxvig, Claus","Frystyk, Jan"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-013149"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Leibniz Institute for Farm Animal Biology"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NOVO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-NOVO","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"insulin like growth factor bioactivity stanniocalcin 000000000002 pregnancy associated plasma protein a and igf binding protein 000000000004 in pleural fluid and serum from patients with pulmonary disease","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85031107500","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-013149","identifier":[{"id":"28911149","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85031107500","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-078bafcd-6b87-431a-96d5-991dbfd862aa","sdu-84b4522e-4e3c-4b08-8081-110563156215"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1D79A2952B7FB7BE2B308E3D3D2BADAF"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Medical Research Laboratory"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"novo nordisk","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-NOVO","l3nl":"Novo Nordisk","l3nn":"Novo Nordisk","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Novo Nordisk","namevar":["Novo Nordisk A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-NOVO","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"leibniz institute for farm animal biology","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz Institute for Farm Animal Biology","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Endocrinology (Odense)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of SDCO - Steno Diabetes Center Odense"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrick Skipper","key":"espelundpau","last":"Espelund","locid":"d6406dea-1bcb-447c-88ae-926841ba574d","name":"Espelund, Ulrick","name_org":"Espelund, Ulrick Skipper","orcid":"0000-0002-3659-650X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","locid":"1337eaca-a3a1-4837-a772-261478be9f37","name":"Bjerre, Mette","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rikke","key":"hjortebjergpau","last":"Hjortebjerg","locid":"d7f05783-92a6-4c22-9d46-9bd0128122b4","name":"Hjortebjerg, Rikke","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Riis","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"311942d4-5b0f-4c92-879f-8d32a246ebf6","name":"Rasmussen, Torben Riis","orcid":"0000-0002-7030-9260","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"lundbypau","last":"Lundby","name":"Lundby, Anders","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Andreas","key":"hoeflichpau","last":"Hoeflich","name":"Hoeflich, Andreas","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Birgitte Holst","key":"folkersenpau","last":"Folkersen","name":"Folkersen, Birgitte Holst","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Claus","key":"oxvigpau","last":"Oxvig","locid":"ed472b6b-b72e-45f7-9d27-09bc23d0db9d","name":"Oxvig, Claus","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jan","key":"frystykpau","last":"Frystyk","locid":"e3650a02-322d-46c8-9d0e-d467831ea56a","name":"Frystyk, Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-5379-0961","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28911149"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1210/jc.2017-00033","issn":["0021972X","19457197"],"issn_org":["0021972X"],"issue":"9","journal":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","pages":"3526-3534","publisher":"Endocrine Society","status":"p","title":"Journal of Clinical Endocrinology and Metabolism","title_org":"The Journal of Clinical Endocrinology & Metabolism","volume":"102"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85031107500"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Novo Nordisk","Private Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-078bafcd-6b87-431a-96d5-991dbfd862aa","sdu-84b4522e-4e3c-4b08-8081-110563156215"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Insulin-Like Growth Factor Bioactivity, Stanniocalcin-2, Pregnancy-Associated Plasma Protein-A, and IGF-Binding Protein-4 in Pleural Fluid and Serum From Patients With Pulmonary Disease","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-013149","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Abstract Daily dialogue between leaders and workers on traditional construction sites is primarily focused on production, quality and time issues, and rarely involves occupational safety and health (OSH) issues. A leadership training program entitled 'Toolbox-training' was developed to improve construction foremen’s knowledge and communication skills in daily planning of work tasks and their related OSH risks on construction sites. The program builds on the popular 'toolbox meeting' concept, however there is very little research evaluating these types of meetings. This article describes the development, implementation and feasibility of the Toolbox-training program, and the results of the process evaluation and outcome evaluation. A total of 57 foremen from 12 companies participated in the training in five successive groups during 2014–2015. Following each group, the program was continuously evaluated and revised until the final version after the fifth group. The evaluation utilized an action research strategy with a mixed–methods approach of triangulating questionnaire, interview, and observation data. Process evaluation results showed that the eight Toolbox-training topics were relevant and useful for the majority of the foremen, who experienced positive changes in their daily work methods and interactions with their crews, colleagues, leaders, customers and other construction professions. The program is a unique contribution to leadership training in the construction industry, and can potentially be applied and adapted in many other sectors. However, there is still a need for testing the long-term effects of the program on safety climate, injuries and business in future studies.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jeschke, Katharina Christiane","Kines, Pete","Rasmussen, Liselotte","Andersen, Lars Peter Sønderbo","Dyreborg, Johnny","Ajslev, Jeppe","Kabel, Anders","Jensen, Ester","Andersen, Lars L."],"cuid":["S04-099.96-766713"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":4,"corresponding_author":["Jeschke, Katharina Christiane"],"keyword":["Leadership training","Lean construction","Safety communication","Safety training","Toolbox meetings","Toolbox talks"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH"],"OT":["Danish Ramazzini Center, Department of Occupational Medicine, Herning, Denmark."],"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-NIRA","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-PR-NIRA","DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"process evaluation of a toolbox training program for construction foremen in denmark","src":["aau","au","cbs","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-CBS"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ssci.2017.01.010","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S04-099.96-766713","identifier":[{"id":"000395843800015","type":"wos"},{"id":"85011043615","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-5d1bb1c3-02c5-4529-a3ce-fd7dd201c8cf","au-0ec179de-ac61-4e8b-9477-90424f14a55e","cbs-24c35a89-1c13-4c8e-b1f4-4b826a89e566","nfa-37cbd1c8-15a9-49d1-8c20-4c0528db7b25"],"keyword":["Leadership training","Lean construction","Safety communication","Safety training","Toolbox meetings","Toolbox talks"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-7-C1C7706952CFB403BBDE6A1E2AD8E5F5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://research-api.cbs.dk/ws/files/55560945/katharina_christiane_jeschke_process_evaluation_publishersversion.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type"