{"abstract":"Aims and Scope: This collection of essays provides an exemplary overview of the diversity and relevance of current scholarship on German Idealism. The importance of German Idealism for contemporary philosophy has received growing attention and acknowledgment throughout competing fields of contemporary philosophy. Part of the growing interest rests on the claim that the works of Kant, Fichte, Schelling, Hegel remain of considerable interest for cultural studies, sociology, theology, aesthetics and other areas of interest. In the domain of philosophy, the renaissance of innovative readings of German Idealism has taken scholarly debates beyond merely antiquarian perspectives. This renaissance has been a major factor of current efforts to bridge the gap between so-called \"analytic\" and so-called \"continental\" philosophy. The volume provides a selection of well-chosen examples of readings that contribute to systematic treatments of philosophical problems. It contains (among others) contributions by Markus Gabriel, Robert Pippin, Anders Moe Rasmussen, Sebastian Rödl.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gabriel, Markus","Rasmussen, Anders Moe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-179301"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Bonn"],"keyword":["German idealism","Kant Immanuel"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"german idealism today","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85046504700","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-179301","identifier":[{"id":"85046504700","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-57a2b91d-f189-4b5a-a3bb-00846ab5a31e"],"keyword":["Fichte, Johann Gottlie","German idealism","Hegel, Georg Wilhelm Friedrich","Kant, Immanuel"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-3-7EBC43224DC3FA7EE23D58BFA20B46A2"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"university of bonn","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bonn","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Philosophy, subject"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus","key":"gabrielped","last":"Gabriel","name":"Gabriel, Markus","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Moe","key":"rasmussenped","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"e9773c7c-a46d-4591-b659-4151bea40a43","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Moe","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1515/9783110498615","edition":"1 udgave","eisbn":["9783110497519"],"isbn":["9783110500288"],"pages":"232","place":"Berlin/Boston","publisher":"De Gruyter","status":"p","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85046504700"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-57a2b91d-f189-4b5a-a3bb-00846ab5a31e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"German Idealism Today","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-179301","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Leukotoxin is a well-known virulence factor of animal isolates of Fusobacterium necrophorum subspecies necrophorum, and is also expressed by animal isolates of subspecies funduliforme, whereas its presence in isolates from humans has not been fully established. In this study we found that the leukotoxin gene was present in all tested F. necrophorum isolates from humans. Three sequence variants were found, two of which have not been described previously. The sequence types correlated to source of infection. Further studies are needed to examine the role of the leukotoxin in human infections.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holm, Karin","Collin, Mattias","Kristensen, Lena Hagelskjær","Jensen, Anders","Rasmussen, Magnus"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-206387"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Lund University"],"keyword":["Fusobacterium necrophorum","Lemierre","Leukotoxin","Pharyngotonsillitis","Sequencing"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"three variants of the leukotoxin gene in human isolates of fusobacterium necrophorum subspecies funduliforme","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85016519093","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-206387","identifier":[{"id":"85016519093","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28330774","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-86f6d52a-75b0-4908-b584-03a4f224c71c"],"keyword":["Fusobacterium necrophorum","Lemierre","Leukocidin","Leukotoxin","Pharyngotonsillitis","Sequencing"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2AB6E69B283CF57C3496