5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Ekstimitet versus transparens : - eller hvorfor digte heldigvis altid falder ved siden af","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-406168","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Early assessment of necrotising soft tissue infection (NSTI) is challenging. Analysis of inflammatory markers could provide important information about disease severity and guide decision making. For this purpose, we investigated the association between cytokine levels and the Laboratory Risk Indicator for Necrotising Fasciitis (LRINEC)-score, disease severity and mortality in NSTI patients. In 159 patients, plasma was analysed for IL-1β, IL-6, IL-10 and TNF-α upon admission. The severity of NSTI was assessed by SAPS, SOFA score, septic shock, microbial aetiology, renal replacement therapy and amputation. We found no significant difference in cytokine levels according to a LRINEC- score above or below 6 (IL-1β: 3.0 vs. 1.3; IL-6: 607 vs. 289; IL-10: 38.4 vs. 38.8; TNF-α: 15.1 vs. 7.8 pg/mL, P > 0.05). Patients with β-haemolytic streptococcal infection had higher level of particularly IL-6. There was no difference in mortality between patients with a LRINEC-score above or below 6. In the adjusted analysis assessing 30-day mortality, the association was strongest for IL-1β (OR 3.86 [95% CI, 1.43-10.40], P = 0.008) and IL-10 (4.80 [1.67-13.78], P = 0.004). In conclusion, we found no significant association between the LRINEC-score and cytokine levels on admission. IL-6 was consistently associated with disease severity, whereas IL-1β had the strongest association with 30-day mortality.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hansen, Marco Bo","Rasmussen, Lars S","Svensson, Mattias","Chakrakodi, Bhavya","Bruun, Trond","Madsen, Martin Bruun","Perner, Anders","Garred, Peter","Hyldegaard, Ole","Norrby-Teglund, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-420803"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["INFECT Study Group"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"association between cytokine response the lrinec score and outcome in patients with necrotising soft tissue infection a multicentre prospective study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42179","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-420803","identifier":[{"id":"85012000645","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28176831","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC5296880","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-2de444e8-1492-47e1-a740-f6b3f5db1ac5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9302354DBC22FEC2771047DEC3FA3CE1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/srep42179","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/194811464/srep42179_1.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Anaesthesiology","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"infect study group","name":"INFECT Study Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Marco Bo","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Marco Bo","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37e36b99-34dd-471f-b09b-d93e72940ec0","name":"Rasmussen, Lars S","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars Simon","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mattias","key":"svenssonpau","last":"Svensson","name":"Svensson, Mattias","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Bhavya","key":"chakrakodipau","last":"Chakrakodi","name":"Chakrakodi, Bhavya","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Trond","key":"bruunpau","last":"Bruun","name":"Bruun, Trond","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Martin Bruun","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","name":"Madsen, Martin Bruun","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"garredpau","last":"Garred","locid":"854d72a7-c955-43b5-b455-b7ea1f9bcb1e","name":"Garred, Peter","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ole","key":"hyldegaardpau","last":"Hyldegaard","locid":"b3f6c355-9c6b-4db3-84c2-870d09643475","name":"Hyldegaard, Ole","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"norrbyteglundpau","last":"Norrby-Teglund","name":"Norrby-Teglund, Anna","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28176831"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/srep42179","issn":["20452322"],"journal":"Scientific Reports","paperid":"42179","status":"p","title":"Scientific Reports","volume":"7"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85012000645"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-2de444e8-1492-47e1-a740-f6b3f5db1ac5"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Association between cytokine response, the LRINEC score and outcome in patients with necrotising soft tissue infection : a multicentre, prospective study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-420803","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Few genome-wide association studies (GWAS) account for environmental exposures, like smoking, potentially impacting the overall trait variance when investigating the genetic contribution to obesity-related traits. Here, we use GWAS data from 51,080 current smokers and 190,178 nonsmokers (87% European descent) to identify loci influencing BMI and central adiposity, measured as waist circumference and waist-to-hip ratio both adjusted for BMI. We identify 23 novel genetic loci, and 9 loci with convincing evidence of gene-smoking interaction (GxSMK) on obesity-related traits. We show consistent direction of effect for all identified loci and significance for 18 novel and for 5 interaction loci in an independent study sample. These loci highlight novel biological functions, including response to oxidative stress, addictive behaviour, and regulatory functions emphasizing the importance of accounting for environment in genetic analyses. Our results suggest that tobacco smoking may alter the genetic susceptibility to overall adiposity and body fat distribution.","author_count":317,"contributors":["Justice, Anne E","Winkler, Thomas W","Feitosa, Mary F","Graff, Misa","Fisher, Virginia A","Young, Kristin L","Barata, Llilda","Deng, Xuan","Czajkowski, Jacek","Hadley, David","Ngwa, Julius S","Ahluwalia, Tarun Veer Singh","Chu, Audrey Y","Heard-Costa, Nancy L","Lim, Elise","Perez, Jeremiah","Eicher, John D","Kutalik, Zoltan","Xue, Luting","Mahajan, Anubha","Renström, Frida","Wu, Joseph C","Qi, Qibin","Ahmad, Shafqat","Alfred, Tamuno","Amin, Najaf","Bielak, Lawrence F","Bonnefond, Amélie","Bragg-Gresham, Jennifer L","Cadby, Gemma","Chittani, Martina","Coggeshall, Scott","Corre, Tanguy","Direk, Nese","Eriksson, Joel","Fischer, Krista","Gorski, Mathias","Neergaard Harder, Marie","Horikoshi, Momoko","Huang, Tao-wei","Huffman, Jennifer E","Jackson, Anne U","Justesen, Johanne Marie","Kanoni, Stavroula","Kinnunen, Leena","Kleber, Marcus E","Komulainen, Pirjo","Kumari, Meena"