,"first":"Anders","key":"lindskogpau","last":"Lindskog","name":"Lindskog, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Maria Mafalda","key":"canasportelacostapau","last":"Canas Portela Costa","locid":"f392e28f-23d4-45a8-8f55-ce3e706f4ef3","name":"Canas Portela Costa, Maria Mafalda","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian","key":"macørumrasmussenpau","last":"Mac Ørum Rasmussen","locid":"0b668780-f8e1-4def-bc48-8c6f6a6a6e43","name":"Mac Ørum Rasmussen, Christian","orcid":"0000-0003-2982-9931","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"James","key":"connellypau","last":"Connelly","locid":"2dedeb3e-90ce-49fb-90a8-22fac963c7fe","name":"Connelly, James","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Mats E.","key":"erikssonpau","last":"Eriksson","name":"Eriksson, Mats E.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28117834"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ncomms14066","issn":["20411723"],"journal":"Nature Communications","paperid":"14066","status":"p","title":"Nature Communications","volume":"8"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85010934002"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7ba5435f-bbd1-497f-b175-309cee0ca8e7"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Refined Ordovician timescale reveals no link between asteroid breakup and biodiversification","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-467488","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"Background and aim: Normal articulation before school start is a main objective in cleft palate treatment. The aim was to investigate if differences exist in consonant proficiency at age 5 years between children with unilateral cleft lip and palate (UCLP) randomised to different surgical protocols for primary palatal repair. A secondary aim was to estimate burden of care in terms of received additional secondary surgeries and speech therapy. Design: Three parallel group, randomised clinical trials were undertaken as an international multicentre study by 10 cleft teams in five countries: Denmark, Finland, Norway, Sweden, and the UK. Methods: Three different surgical protocols for primary palatal repair were tested against a common procedure in the total cohort of 448 children born with non-syndromic UCLP. Speech audio- and video-recordings of 391 children (136 girls and 255 boys) were available and transcribed phonetically. The main outcome measure was Percent Consonants Correct (PCC) from blinded assessments. Results: In Trial 1, arm A showed statistically significant higher PCC scores (82%) than arm B (78%) (p =.045). No significant differences were found between prevalences in Trial 2, A: 79%, C: 82%; or Trial 3, A: 80%, D: 85%. Across all trials, girls achieved better PCC scores, excluding s-errors, than boys (91.0% and 87.5%, respectively) (p =.01). Conclusions: PCC scores were higher in arm A than B in Trial 1, whereas no differences were found between arms in Trials 2 or 3. The burden of care in terms of secondary pharyngeal surgeries, number of fistulae, and speech therapy visits differed. Trial registration: ISRCTN29932826.","author_count":29,"contributors":["Willadsen, Elisabeth","Lohmander, Anette","Persson, Christina","Lundeborg, Inger","Alaluusua, Suvi","Aukner, Ragnhild","Bau, Anja","Boers, Maria","Bowden, Melanie","Davies, Julie","Emborg, Berit","Havstam, Christina","Hayden, Christine","Henningsson, Gunilla","Holmefjord, Anders","Hölttä, Elina","Kisling-Møller, Mia","Kjøll, Lillian","Lundberg, Maria","McAleer, Eilish","Nyberg, Jill","Paaso, Marjukka","Pedersen, Nina Helen","Rasmussen, Therese","Reisæter, Sigvor","Andersen, Helene Søgaard","Schöps, Antje","Tørdal, Inger Beate","Semb, Gunvor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-475250"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Norway","Sweden","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Karolinska University Hospital","Linköping University","Royal Hospital for Sick Children","Royal Manchester Children's Hospital","Statped Vest","Statped sørøst","University of Gothenburg","University of Helsinki","University of Manchester"],"keyword":["Consonant proficiency","Primary palatal repair","Randomised clinical trial","unilateral cleft lip and palate"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Copenhagen Cleft Palate Center"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"scandcleft randomised trials of primary surgery for unilateral cleft lip and palate 000000000005 speech outcomes in 000000000005 year olds consonant proficiency and errors","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-475250","identifier":[{"id":"85013414613","type":"scopus"},{"id":"28218556","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-88ca8f05-e312-4b71-bdd6-d442eac5d118"],"keyword":["Primary palatal repair","cleft speech characteristics","consonant proficiency","randomised clinical trial","unilateral cleft lip and palate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B2529CF962A1CF81D0B6911233E3AC6F"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l