{"abstract":"Cortical spreading depression is associated with activation of NMDA receptors, which interact with the postsynaptic density protein 95 (PSD-95) that binds to nitric oxide synthase (nNOS). Here, we tested whether inhibition of the nNOS/PSD-95/NMDA receptor complex formation by anti-ischemic compound, UCCB01-144 (Tat-N-dimer) ameliorates the persistent effects of cortical spreading depression on cortical function. Using in vivo two-photon microscopy in somatosensory cortex in mice, we show that fluorescently labelled Tat-N-dimer readily crosses blood-brain barrier and accumulates in nerve cells during the first hour after i.v. injection. The Tat-N-dimer suppressed stimulation-evoked synaptic activity by 2-20%, while cortical blood flow and cerebral oxygen metabolic (CMRO2) responses were preserved. During cortical spreading depression, the Tat-N-dimer reduced the average amplitude of the negative shift in direct current potential by 33% (4.1 mV). Furthermore, the compound diminished the average depression of spontaneous electrocorticographic activity by 11% during first 40 min of post-cortical spreading depression recovery, but did not mitigate the suppressing effect of cortical spreading depression on cortical blood flow and CMRO2 We suggest that uncoupling of PSD-95 from NMDA receptors reduces overall neuronal excitability and the amplitude of the spreading depolarisation wave. These findings may be of interest for understanding the neuroprotective effects of the nNOS/PSD-95 uncoupling in stroke.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Kucharz, Krzysztof","Søndergaard Rasmussen, Ida","Bach, Anders","Strømgaard, Kristian","Lauritzen, Martin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-499782"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"psd 000000000095 uncoupling from nmda receptors by tat n dimer ameliorates neuronal depolarization in cortical spreading depression","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5435282?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-499782","identifier":[{"id":"27107027","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85018764807","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC5435282","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-b2159a8c-33ab-4a35-ade2-beee46bcb672"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C594730AA4050DCA5ABC1BF692CD8914"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"http://europepmc.org/Copyright","type":"rem","url":"http://europepmc.org/articles/pmc5435282?pdf=render","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Neuronal Signalling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Krzysztof","key":"kucharzpau","last":"Kucharz","locid":"273037f0-7883-47f8-844a-645b739b8206","name":"Kucharz, Krzysztof","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ida","key":"søndergaardrasmussenpau","last":"Søndergaard Rasmussen","locid":"5016e048-0aaa-4b5d-8323-8f99d8c6d793","name":"Søndergaard Rasmussen, Ida","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","locid":"44d88cbf-9cb6-41c6-84a4-5ddda26517d8","name":"Bach, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4305-9910","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kristian","key":"strømgaardpau","last":"Strømgaard","locid":"78f1a438-9c1e-4795-bf55-b266b5d2cde4","name":"Strømgaard, Kristian","orcid":"0000-0003-2206-4737","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Martin","key":"lauritzenpau","last":"Lauritzen","locid":"9271b6ef-3aff-41b4-991b-17a7c0396c5f","name":"Lauritzen, Martin","orcid":"0000-0002-1517-1131","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27107027"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1177/0271678x16645595","issn":["0271678X","15597016"],"issn_org":["0271678X"],"issue":"5","journal":"Journal of Cerebral Blood Flow and Metabolism","pages":"1820-1828","status":"p","title":"Journal of Cerebral Blood Flow and Metabolism","volume":"37"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85018764807"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-b2159a8c-33ab-4a35-ade2-beee46bcb672"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"PSD-95 uncoupling from NMDA receptors by Tat-N-dimer ameliorates neuronal depolarization in cortical spreading depression","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-499782","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-507062"],"filters":{"added":"2022-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tekstforhold og noter","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-507062","ids":["ku-be6795f6-0355-4407-8ced-e9d659dbc14a"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-74CF7D336B074CFB6259C68229231B0A"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jeppe Lindquist","key":"barnwellpau","last":"Barnwell","locid":"50916516-bf5a-460e-94b1-77cf4f11c535","name":"Barnwell, Jeppe Lindquist","orcid":"0009-0001-8395-1818","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jeppe","key":"barnwellpedh","last":"Barnwell","name":"Barnwell, Jeppe","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jesper G.","key":"nielsenpedh","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Jesper G.","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Juhl","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Juhl","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788702244809"],"pages":"289-330","publisher":"Gyldendal","status":"p","subtitle":"Peter Seebergs romaner, noveller og kortprosa","title":"Om fjorten dage"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-be6795f6-0355-4407-8ced-e9d659dbc14a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tekstforhold og noter","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-507062","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The presence of thyroid antibodies in pregnancy has been associated with preterm birth. In the non-pregnant population, the implementation of the Danish iodine fortification program has increased the prevalence of thyroid antibodies. This study investigated the prevalence of thyroid peroxidase antibodies (TPOAbs) and thyroglobulin antibodies (TgAbs) in pregnant Danish women before, during and after implementation of the iodine fortification program and association with preterm birth. DESIGN: Comparative cohort study of 1368 pregnancies from three cohorts gathered before (1996-1998), during (2000-2003) and after (2008-2009) the iodine fortification program. METHODS: In cohort 1 (n = 297), TPOAbs were measured (DYNOtest (BRAHMS)). In cohorts 2 (n = 148) and 3 (n = 923), both TPOAbs and TgAbs were measured (Kryptor immunofluorescent assay (BRAHMS)). The prevalence and effect of antibody positivity were explored using three cut-offs: TPOAbs and/or TgAbs >100 kU/L, TPOAbs and/or TgAbs >60 kU/L and TPOAbs >30 and/or TgAbs >20 kU/L. National preterm birth data were extracted from the National Birth Registry. RESULTS: In the three cohorts, TPOAb levels >60 kU/L were found in 5.4, 8.1 and 12.0% (χ2(2, n = 1367) = 11.7, P = 0.003) respectively, and TPOAbs and/or TgAbs >60 kU/L in 8.1 and 16.2% in cohorts 2 and 3 respectively (χ2(2, n = 1070) = 6.5, P = 0.01). TgAb levels (>20 kU/L) had increased plenty-fold from cohort 2 to 3 (χ2(1, n = 1071) = 136.5, P < 0.001). Preterm birth occurred in 4.1% of all pregnancies with no effect from antibody positivity (TPOAbs and/or TgAbs >60 kU/L, χ2(1, n = 1039) = 0.0, P = 0.98, aOR = 1.1, 95% CI (0.4-2.7)). The national preterm birth-rate showed no increase over the same period. CONCLUSIONS: Thyroid antibody positivity in Danish pregnant women has more than doubled upon the implementation of the iodine fortification program without an increase in preterm birth-rate.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bliddal, Sofie","Boas, Malene","Hilsted, Linda","Friis-Hansen, Lennart","Juul, Anders","Larsen, Torben","Tabor, Ann","Faber, Jens","Precht, Dorthe Hansen","Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-526667"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Autoantibodies","Autoimmune Diseases","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Food Fortified","Humans","Iodide Peroxidase","Iodine","Journal Article","Longitudinal Studies","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications","Premature Birth","Prospective Studies","Thyroglobulin","Thyroid Diseases"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"increase in thyroglobulin antibody and thyroid peroxidase antibody levels but not preterm birth rate in pregnant danish women upon iodine fortification","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-526667","identifier":[{"id":"28348022","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85016399604","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-df0c1dff-9144-4dfc-8071-77a90207e84c"],"keyword":["Adult","Autoantibodies","Autoimmune Diseases","Cohort Studies","Denmark","Female","Food, Fortified","Humans","Iodide Peroxidase","Iodine","Journal Article","Longitudinal Studies","Pregnancy","Pregnancy Complications","Premature Birth","Prospective Studies","Thyroglobulin","Thyroid Diseases"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4F1DC5E900B6C59B2BBC24A5FADB7444"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Paediatrics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Sofie","key":"bliddalpau","last":"Bliddal","name":"Bliddal, Sofie","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Malene","key":"boaspau","last":"Boas","name":"Boas, Malene","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Linda","key":"hilstedpau","last":"Hilsted","name":"Hilsted, Linda","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lennart","key":"friishansenpau","last":"Friis-Hansen","name":"Friis-Hansen, Lennart","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"juulpau","last":"Juul","locid":"f9b11983-c7c8-4111-b119-4de471572898","name":"Juul, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-0534-4350","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Torben","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"7de9d59b-d853-44c3-a410-b23e77078074","name":"Larsen, Torben","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ann","key":"taborpau","last":"Tabor","locid":"812e3aa1-0156-4e1e-a597-44ec3164413a","name":"Tabor, Ann","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens","key":"faberpau","last":"Faber","locid":"42925e6e-5e0c-475f-aca8-13159f10abc7","name":"Faber, Jens","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Hansen","key":"prechtpau","last":"Precht","name":"Precht, Dorthe Hansen","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Ulla","key":"feldtrasmussenpau","last":"Feldt-Rasmussen","locid":"b5898535-d448-4e2f-9f41-d5199873676b","name":"Feldt-Rasmussen, Ulla","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["28348022"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1530/eje-16-0987","issn":["08044643","1479683X"],"issn_org":["08044643"],"issue":"5","journal":"European Journal of Endocrinology","pages":"603-612","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Endocrinology","volume":"176"},"review":"Peer Reviewe