ngsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-007845","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The haemodynamic consequences of fluid resuscitation in septic shock have not been fully elucidated. Therefore, we assessed circulatory effects in the first 24 h of restriction of resuscitation fluid as compared to standard care in intensive care unit (ICU) patients with septic shock. METHODS: This was a post-hoc analysis of the multicentre CLASSIC randomised trial in which patients with septic shock, who had received the initial fluid resuscitation, were randomised to a protocol restricting resuscitation fluid or a standard care protocol in nine ICUs. The highest plasma lactate, highest dose of noradrenaline, and the urinary output were recorded in five time frames in the first 24 h after randomisation. We used multiple linear mixed effects models to compare the two groups. RESULTS: We included all 151 randomised patients; the cumulated fluid resuscitation volume in the first 24 h after randomisation was median 500 ml (Interquartile range (IQR) 0-1500) and 1250 ml (500-2500) in the fluid restriction group and standard care group, respectively. The estimated differences in the fluid restriction group vs. the standard care group were 0.1 mM (95% confidence interval -0.7 to 0.9; P = 0.86) for lactate, 0.01 μg/kg/min (-0.02 to 0.05; P = 0.48) for dose of noradrenaline, and -0.1 ml/kg/h (-0.3 to 0.2; P = 0.70) for urinary output during the first 24 h after randomisation. CONCLUSIONS: We observed no indications of worsening of measures of circulatory efficacy in the first 24 h of restriction of resuscitation fluid as compared with standard care in adults with septic shock who had received initial resuscitation.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Hjortrup, P. B.","Haase, Nicolai","Wetterslev, Jørn","Lange, T","Bundgaard, H.","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Dey, Nilanjan","Wilkman, Erika","Christensen, L","Lodahl, D. C.","Bestle, Morten","Perner, A."],"cuid":["S03-093.51-005364"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Hjortrup, P. B."],"country":["China","Finland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Helsinki University Hospital","Peking University","University of Helsinki"],"keyword":["Critically ill patients","Definitions","Intensive care","Journal Article","Management","Mortality","Resuscitation","Sepsis","TRIAL"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA"],"OT":["Department of Intensive Care, Randers Hospital, Randers, Denmark."],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-HO-OTH","DI-HO-ZEA","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"effects of fluid restriction on measures of circulatory efficacy in adults with septic shock","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85011706211","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-093.51-005364","identifier":[{"id":"85011706211","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000395382600007","type":"wos"},{"id":"28150304","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-6e8ecf1d-f1d3-46fb-9722-8dcc2167a15b","au-95f6194d-ce79-4624-b2ed-87a5a8002192","ku-d6e9bb9e-f551-41e4-84b4-58bc1eeb4e5d"],"keyword":["BOLUS THERAPY","CRITICALLY-ILL PATIENTS","DEFINITIONS","INTENSIVE-CARE","Journal Article","MANAGEMENT","MORTALITY","MYOCARDIAL DEPRESSION","RESUSCITATION","SEPSIS","TRIAL"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-DF297E423A6972CD7C1BA64A3556844A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2017","yearSub":"2017"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI