{"abstract":"We investigate oscillating shock waves in a tube using a higher order weakly nonlinear acoustic model. The model includes thermoviscous effects and is non isentropic. The oscillating shock waves are generated at one end of the tube by a sinusoidal driver. Numerical simulations show that at resonance a stationary state arise consisting of multiple oscillating shock waves. Off resonance driving leads to a nearly linear oscillating ground state but superimposed by bursts of a fast oscillating shock wave. Based on a travelling wave ansatz for the fluid velocity potential with an added 2'nd order polynomial in the space and time variables, we find analytical approximations to the observed single shock waves in an infinitely long tube. Using perturbation theory for the driven acoustic system approximative analytical solutions for the off resonant case are determined.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gaididei, Yuri","Rasmussen, Anders Rønne","Christiansen, Peter Leth","Sørensen, Mads Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319399"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU"],"country":["Ukraine"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","NASU - Bogolyubov Institute for Theoretical Physics"],"keyword":["Mathematics","Nonlinear acoustics","Nonlinear waves","Propagation","Resonances","Shock waves"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["GreenHydrogen.dk"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"oscillating nonlinear acoustic shock waves","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85026730933","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319399","identifier":[{"id":"85026730933","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-31e4ee68-02d0-4d34-9a62-6173f33020db"],"keyword":["MATHEMATICS,","Nonlinear acoustics","PROPAGATION","RESONANCES","nonlinear waves","shock waves"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C7C77247141CB1919F8C787C5358356A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"ua","key":"nasu bogolyubov institute for theoretical physics","loc":["Ukraine","Europe, Non-EU"],"name":"NASU - Bogolyubov Institute for Theoretical Physics","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["GreenHydrogen.dk"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Applied Mathematics and Computer Science","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Yuri","key":"gaidideipau","last":"Gaididei","name":"Gaididei, Yuri","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Rønne","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Rønne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Leth","key":"christiansenpau","last":"Christiansen","locid":"3b3fdeaf-d129-4067-bde8-00498361d5b7","name":"Christiansen, Peter Leth","orcid":"0000-0002-1465-9987","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mads Peter","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"651b67f7-1e41-4719-8369-01b34075cd6b","name":"Sørensen, Mads Peter","orcid":"0000-0003-0820-8722","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.3934/eect.2016009","issn":["21632472","21632480"],"issn_org":["21632480"],"issue":"3","journal":"Evolution Equations and Control Theory","pages":"367-381","publisher":"American Institute of Mathematical Sciences  AIMS Press)","publisher_org":"American Institute of Mathematical Sciences (A I M S Press)","status":"p","title":"Evolution Equations and Control Theory","title_org":"Evolution Equations and Control Theory (Online)","volume":"5"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85026730933"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-31e4ee68-02d0-4d34-9a62-6173f33020db"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Oscillating nonlinear acoustic shock waves","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319399","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Drift ordered fluid models are widely applied in studies of low-frequency turbulence in the edge and scrape-off layer regions of magnetically confined plasmas. Here, we show how collisional transport across the magnetic field is self-consistently incorporated into drift-fluid models without altering the drift-fluid energy integral. We demonstrate that the inclusion of collisional transport in drift-fluid models gives rise to diffusion of particle density, momentum, and pressures in drift-fluid turbulence models and, thereby, obviates the customary use of artificial diffusion in turbulence simulations. We further derive a computationally efficient, two-dimensional model, which can be time integrated for several turbulence de-correlation times using only limited computational resources. The model describes interchange turbulence in a two-dimensional plane perpendicular to the magnetic field located at the outboard midplane of a tokamak. The model domain has two regions modeling open and closed field lines. The model employs a computational expedient model for collisional transport. Numerical simulations show good agreement between the full and the simplified model for collisional transport.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Madsen, Jens","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-324418"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"collisional transport across the magnetic field in drift fluid models","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123457188/1.4943199.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-324418","identifier":[{"id":"84961741489","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-42a982c6-73dc-456f-acfc-3fa42c6aa90e"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AFA1A95A9117001D64ADC1CC13FADDB2"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123457188/1.4943199.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1063/1.4943199","issn":["1070664X","10897674"],"issn_org":["1070664X"],"issue":"3","journal":"Physics of Plasmas","paperid":"032306","publisher":"American Institute of Physics","status":"p","title":"Physics of Plasmas","volume":"23"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961741489"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-42a982c6-73dc-456f-acfc-3fa42c6aa90e"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Collisional transport across the magnetic field in drift-fluid models","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-324418","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"AIMS: Abuse of anabolic androgenic steroids (AAS) is highly prevalent among male recreational athletes. The objective of this study was to investigate the impact of AAS abuse on reproductive hormone levels and symptoms suggestive of hypogonadism in current and former AAS abusers. METHODS: This study had a cross-sectional case-control design and involved 37 current AAS abusers, 33 former AAS abusers (mean (95%CI) elapsed duration since AAS cessation: 2.5 (1.7; 3.7) years) and 30 healthy control participants. All participants were aged 18-50 years and were involved in recreational strength training. Reproductive hormones (FSH, LH, testosterone, inhibin B and anti-Müllerian hormone (AMH)) were measured using morning blood samples. Symptoms of hypogonadism (depressive symptoms, fatigue, decreased libido and erectile dysfunction) were recorded systematically. RESULTS: Former AAS abusers exhibited significantly lower median (25th -75th percentiles) total and free testosterone levels than control participants (total testosterone: 14.4 (11.9-17.7) nmol/l vs. 18.8 (16.6-22.0) nmol/l) (P < 0.01). Overall, 27.2% (13.3; 45.5) of former AAS abusers exhibited plasma total testosterone levels below the lower reference limit (12.1 nmol/l) whereas no control participants exhibited testosterone below this limit (P < 0.01). Gonadotropins were significantly suppressed, and inhibin B and AMH were significantly decreased in current AAS abusers compared with former AAS abusers and control participants (P < 0.01). The group of former AAS abusers had higher proportions of participants with depressive symptoms ((24.2%) (11.1; 42.2)), erectile dysfunction ((27.3%) (13.3; 45.6)) and decreased libido ((40.1%) (23.2; 57.0)) than the other two groups (trend analyses: P < 0.05). CONCLUSIONS: Former AAS abusers exhibited significantly lower plasma testosterone levels and higher frequencies of symptoms suggestive of hypogonadism than healthy control participants years after AAS cessation. Current AAS abusers exhibited severely decreased AMH and inhibin B indicative of impaired spermatogenesis.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jon Bjarke Jarløv","Selmer, Christian","Østergren, Peter Busch","Pedersen, Karen Boje","Schou, Morten","Gustafsson, Finn","Faber, Jens","Juul, Anders","Kistorp, Caroline"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-395739"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"former abusers of anabolic androgenic steroids exhibit decreased testosterone levels and hypogonadal symptoms years after cessation a case control study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0161208","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-395739","identifier":[{"id":"27532478","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4988681","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84984819133","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-03c8c724-75b2-412f-92d7-122f6a738643"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1E6B6D1B97A7C670338FA27CABF1546C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/178289032/journal.pone.0161208.PDF","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0161208","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","na