hagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"A disintegrin and metalloprotease-17 and galectin-9 are important regulators of local 4-1BB activity and disease outcome in rheumatoid arthritis","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-096.08-027886","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND & AIM: Patients with intestinal failure (IF) are dependent on parenteral nutrition delivered through central access such as Hickman™ catheters. The peripherally inserted central catheter (PICC) is becoming increasingly popular for the purpose. The aim of the present study was to compare complication rates between the two types of catheters. PATIENTS AND METHODS: Over a six-year period (2008-2014), we included 136 patients with IF receiving home parenteral nutrition (HPN). These patients had a total of 295 catheters (169 Hickman™ catheters and 126 PICCs). Data were collected by reviewing their medical records. Incidences are given per 1000 catheter days. Data are given as means ± standard deviation (SD) and compared using independent student's t-tests, Mann-Whitney-Wilcoxon, and X(2)-tests. A survival analysis for time to the first infection was conducted using Cox regression. RESULTS: The total number of catheter days was 54,912 days for Hickman™ catheters (mean dwell time 325 ± 402) and 15,974 days for PICCs (mean dwell time 127 ± 121), respectively. The incidence of catheter-related blood stream infection (CRBSI) per 1000 catheter days was significantly lower for Hickman™ catheters compared to PICCs (0.56 vs. 1.63, p < 0.05). The mean time to first CRBSI was significantly shorter for PICCs compared to Hickman™ catheters (84 ± 94 days vs. 297 ± 387 days, p < 0.05), which was confirmed with a cox analysis corrected for age and gender. A total of 75 catheters were removed due to CRBSI, 49 Hickman™ catheters and 26 PICCs respectively. In addition, PICCs were more often removed due to local infection/phlebitis and mechanical causes (p < 0.001). CONCLUSION: We found a higher risk and shorter time to first CRBSI in PICCs compared to Hickman catheters supporting that PICCs should mainly be chosen for planned HPN up to 3-6 months. We therefore conclude that the choice of catheter must still be determined on an individual basis.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Christensen, Line Dahlstrøm","Holst, Mette","Bech, Laura Fuglsang","Drustrup, Lotte","Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","Andersen, Anders Skallerup","Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","Vinter-Jensen, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-050535"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"comparison of complications associated with peripherally inserted central catheters and hickman catheters in patients with intestinal failure receiving home parenteral nutrition six year follow up study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-050535","identifier":[{"id":"26269383","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000378447500019","type":"wos"},{"id":"84939832640","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-01c09aae-972c-47fa-9b7b-a33cd52ca339"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9D8346583E9B10E828863F6F4A6663FE"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Medicin","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Medicinske Mave- og Tarmsygdomme (Gastroenterologi og Hepatologi) [Klinik Medicin]"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Dahlstrøm","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"cbe70b8f-f52b-4fb6-91e1-96cd008c7a2e","name":"Christensen, Line Dahlstrøm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mette","key":"holstpau","last":"Holst","locid":"28beee90-db56-4b02-8832-fef8820eb5f4","name":"Holst, Mette","orcid":"0000-0002-7458-9458","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Laura Fuglsang","key":"bechpau","last":"Bech","locid":"bbabcd88-f9cb-4345-a92f-62d113aa5910","name":"Bech, Laura Fuglsang","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lotte","key":"drustruppau","last":"Drustrup","locid":"06e5d6e4-b418-4f80-adbf-ff1b241b6078","name":"Drustrup, Lotte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louis Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Skallerup","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"8839002b-110b-495b-a386-4df5b8d161e5","name":"Andersen, Anders Skallerup","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Højgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c242f457-53f4-4b88-82f3-d7fb297cf98c","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"vinterjensenpau","last":"Vinter-Jensen","locid":"9bec0a4a-7fda-4f11-bbed-02e75dc2aa02","name":"Vinter-Jensen, Lars","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26269383"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clnu.2015.06.009","issn":["02615614","15321983"],"issn_org":["02615614"],"issue":"4","journal":"Clinical Nutrition","pages":"912-917","publisher":"Churchill Livingstone","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84939832640"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-01c09aae-972c-47fa-9b7b-a33cd52ca339"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Comparison of complications associated with peripherally inserted central catheters and Hickman™ catheters in patients with intestinal failure receiving home parenteral nutrition. Six-year follow up study","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-050535","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The risk of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death among heart failure patients previously diagnosed with diabetes mellitus is poorly described. We evaluated the risk of these endpoints among heart failure patients without diagnosed atrial fibrillation according to the presence of diabetes mellitus. METHODS: Population-based nationwide cohort study of non-anticoagulated patients diagnosed with incident heart failure during 2000-2012, identified by record linkage between nationwide registries in Denmark. We calculated relative risks after 1year to evaluate the association between diabetes and risk of events in 39,357 heart failure patients, among whom 18.1% had diabetes. Analysis took into account competing risks of death. RESULTS: Absolute risks of all endpoints were higher in patients with diabetes compared to patients without diabetes after 1-year follow-up (ischemic stroke: 4.1% vs. 2.8%; systemic thromboembolism: 11.9% vs. 8.6%; all-cause death: 22.1% vs. 21.4%). Diabetes was significantly associated with an increased risk of ischemic stroke (adjusted relative risk [RR]: 1.27, 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.07-1.51); systemic thromboembolism (RR: 1.20, 95% CI: 1.11-1.30); and all-cause death (RR: 1.17, 95% CI: 1.11-1.23). Additionally, time since diabetes diagnosis was associated with higher adjusted cumulative incidences of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death (p for trend, p<0.001). CONCLUSIONS: Among heart failure patients without atrial fibrillation, diabetes was associated with a significantly increased risk of ischemic stroke, systemic thromboembolism, and all-cause death compared to those without diabetes, even after adjustment for concomitant cardiovascular risk factors. Increased focus on secondary prevention in heart failure patients with diabetes may be warranted.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Søgaard, Peter","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Lip, Gregory Y H","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-080829"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"diabetes mellitus and risk of ischemic stroke in patients with heart failure and no atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-080829","identifier":[{"id":"84961572517","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26874450","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000372530700001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-69e51b01-d13c-4384-a2fb-1a96d661e100"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-FE874AA829D397D0C6EF9E917BB5B2FD"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"city hospital in birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City Hospital in Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"søgaardpau","last":"Søgaard","locid":"30606c01-a86b-4eee-90ef-b4268fedaee9","name":"Søgaard, Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26874450"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ijcard.2016.02.004","issn":["01675273","18741754"],"issn_org":["01675273"],"journal":"International Journal of Cardiology","pages":"1-6","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"International Journal of Cardiology","volume":"209"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84961572517"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-69e51b01-d13c-4384-a2fb-1a96d661e100"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Diabetes mellitus and risk of ischemic stroke in patients with heart failure and no atrial fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.