 Morten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","eisbn":["9788793041356"],"isbn":["9788793041257"],"pages":"195-223","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Forlaget Philosophia","status":"p","subtitle":"En indføring i den tyske idealismes hovedpositioner","title":"System, frihed og virkelighed","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-b5f03ec0-62d4-4805-9a62-2a832f7c2d9a"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Kierkegaard : Eksistensen mellem tænkning og lidenskab","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-102863","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: The perceived usefulness of incident reporting systems is an important motivational factor for reporting. The usefulness may be facilitated by well-established feedback mechanisms and by learning processes. The aim of this study was to investigate how feedback mechanisms and learning processes were implemented at four Danish hospital units all located in one of the five Danish regions. METHODS: Based on the concepts of feedback and learning from incident processes, a questionnaire was developed and distributed to 335 patient safety representatives from 200 departments at four Danish hospital units in one of the five Danish regions. RESULTS: The study showed that external reporters were rarely contacted for dialogue, grouped front-line staff were sparsely involved in the learning process, few evaluated the effectiveness of implemented interventions and personal factors were frequently perceived as a primary contributory factor to these incidents. In contrast, the patient safety representatives perceived their competencies as sufficient for the job, internal reporters were often contacted for dialogue, evaluation was widely used and management supported the work with incident reports. CONCLUSIONS: The results of the study identified several shortcomings in the implementation of learning processes and feedback mechanisms. The apparent existence of a person-focused approach stands out as an element of notice. The insufficient implementation we observed indicates that there is room for improvement in the efforts made to maximise learning from incidents in the investigated population. FUNDING: not relevant. TRIAL REGISTRATION: not relevant.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Møller, Anders Damgaard","Rasmussen, Kurt","Nielsen, Kent Jacob"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-235840"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"learning and feedback from the danish patient safety incident reporting system can be improved","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84971612261","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-235840","identifier":[{"id":"84971612261","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27264943","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-ba8adf3e-7c24-4f06-9b38-d884f65eeb58"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-794395364CC01C44A3ACAFBEB1B4E65E"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Diagnostisk Center, Universitetsklinik for Innovative Patientforløb, Silkeborg"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Damgaard","key":"moellerpau","last":"Moeller","locid":"bf5f1414-c4db-4389-8181-de70cd4fcb6f","name":"Møller, Anders Damgaard","name_org":"Moeller, Anders Damgaard","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kurt","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fc33835c-f372-4291-89a4-801c16786c29","name":"Rasmussen, Kurt","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kent Jacob","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"b11fecf5-8895-4034-a7b1-d5eb0399ea93","name":"Nielsen, Kent Jacob","orcid":"0000-0002-4643-5697","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27264943"],"pub":{"issn":["09078916","22451919"],"issn_org":["22451919"],"issue":"6","journal":"Danish Medical Journal","pages":"1-5","paperid":"A5242","publisher":"Almindelige Danske Lægeforening","status":"p","title":"Danish Medical Journal","volume":"63"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84971612261"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ba8adf3e-7c24-4f06-9b38-d884f65eeb58"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Learning and feedback from the Danish patient safety incident reporting system can be improved","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-235840","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jes","Gustavson, Kim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-248607"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"com","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"kemikalier og forurening af vandressourcer mulige påvirkninger af overfladevand af udledning af spildevand fra frakturering","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dra","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://naturstyrelsen.dk/media/180800/videnskabelig-udredning-af-international-viden-om-skifergas-relateret-til-en-dansk-kontekst.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-248607","ids":["au-d0b8fe71-8913-490c-adab-1ffbbcec7f40"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Commissioned","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A1F42645746C495976564752A49C0E5A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://naturstyrelsen.dk/media/180800/videnskabelig-udredning-af-international-viden-om-skifergas-relateret-til-en-dansk-kontekst.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Bioscience - Stream and Wetland Ecology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jes","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1f62ae59-0b9d-4a1e-84c3-25bb14747f25","name":"Rasmussen, Jes","orcid":"0000-0002-5932-3125","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"gustavsonpau","last":"Gustavson","locid":"1ebbd6c1-641f-40c9-a30f-7652da2113f9","name":"Gustavson, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-8242-0276","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Steffen Foss","key":"hansenpedh","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Steffen Foss","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"johnsenpedh","last":"Johnsen","name":"Johnsen, Anders","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Poul Nordemann","key":"jensenpedh","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Poul Nordemann","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Mads H.","key":"odgaardpedh","last":"Odgaard","name":"Odgaard, Mads H.","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"95-97","publisher":"DTU","status":"p","title":"Videnskabelig udredning af international viden om skifergas relateret til en dansk kontekst"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d0b8fe71-8913-490c-adab-1ffbbcec7f40"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Kemikalier og forurening af vandressourcer - mulige påvirkninger af overfladevand af udledning af spildevand fra frakturering","type":"Report Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-248607","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: The study aimed to investigate sacral peripheral nerve function and continuity of pudendal nerve in patients with chronic spinal cord injury (SCI) using pelvic floor electrophysiological tests. METHODS: Twelve patients with low cervical or thoracic SCI were prospectively included. Quantitative external anal sphincter (EAS) muscle electromyography (EMG), pudendal nerve terminal motor latency (PNTML) testing, bulbocavernosus reflex (BCR) testing and pudendal short-latency somatosensory-evoked potential (SEP) measurement were performed. RESULTS: In EAS muscle EMG, two patients had abnormal increased spontaneous activity and seven prolonged motor unit potential duration. PNTML was normal in 10 patients. BCR was present with normal latency in 11 patients and with prolonged latency in one. The second component of BCR could be recorded in four patients. SEPs showed absent cortical responses in 11 patients and normal latency in one. CONCLUSIONS: Pudendal nerve and sacral lower motor neuron involvement are significantly associated with chronic SCI, most prominently in EAS muscle EMG. The frequent finding of normal PNTML latencies supports earlier concerns on the utility of this test; however, BCR and pudendal SEPs may have clinical relevance. SIGNIFICANCE: As intact peripheral nerves including pudendal nerve are essential for efficient supportive therapies, pelvic floor electrophysiological testing prior to these interventions is highly recommended.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Tankisi, Hatice","Pugdahl, Kirsten","Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","Clemmensen, Dorte","Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","Christensen, Peter","Krogh, Klaus","Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-266800"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electromyography","Spinal cord injury"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pelvic floor electrophysiology in spinal cord injury","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84960193448","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-266800","identifier":[{"id":"26975618","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84960193448","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f0e9499c-0a7d-446c-b9bd-74bcbd45fbf0"],"keyword":["Bulbocavernosus reflex","Electromyography","Pelvic floor electrophysiology","Pudendal nerve terminal motor latency","Spinal cord injury"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4A154DBED1991B81B5A2B3575B684751"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Neurophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"H","key":"tankisipau","last":"Tankisi","locid":"2b3f7bfd-71e0-4e1e-9a63-62cf6d26d1ea","name":"Tankisi, Hatice","name_org":"Tankisi, H","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K","key":"pugdahlpau","last":"Pugdahl","locid":"31c88d8a-8ff0-4cce-92bf-7d295700ad8e","name":"Pugdahl, Kirsten","name_org":"Pugdahl, K","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"M M","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0a611a7f-8a19-41f3-9221-58fe673b3ef1","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","name_org":"Rasmussen, M M","orcid":"0000-0002-4768-7255","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"D","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"826b8629-1e7d-42d6-8e46-7f9a993bf743","name":"Clemmensen, Dorte","name_org":"Clemmensen, D","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Y F","key":"rawashdehpau","last":"Rawashdeh","locid":"dd97020c-c4f8-4898-8b08-a088d13d45de","name":"Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","name_org":"Rawashdeh, Y F","orcid":"0000-0002-5517-2980","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"P","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"456d99d5-ee96-4333-afef-d1596a62cf74","name":"Christensen, Peter","name_org":"Christensen, P","orcid":"0000-0002-6611-3935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"K","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"e69f7028-9eb1-4f3a-ab4e-c684c234bf2e","name":"Krogh, Klaus","name_org":"Krogh, K","orcid":"0000-0001-9168-2403","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"A","key":"fuglsangfrederiksenpau","last":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen","locid":"9dbd8297-9ebb-41f0-ab0b-8ddfef8c33bd","name":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders","name_org":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen, A","orcid":"0000-0003-3926-5287","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26975618"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.clinph.2015.12.022","issn":["13882457"],"issue":"5","journal":"Clinical Neurophysiology","pages":"2319-2324","publisher":"Elsevier Ireland Ltd","status":"p","title":"Clinical Neurophysiology","title_org":"Clinical neurophysiology : official journal of the International Federation of Clinical Neurophysiology","volume":"127"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84960193448"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f0e9499c-0a7d-446c-b9bd-74bcbd45fbf0"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pelvic floor electrophysiology in spinal cord injury","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-266800","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Kapitlet fokuserer på tre aspekter ved Fichtes tænkning: Hans bestræbelse på at etablere filosofien som et videnskabeligt system; hans analyse af selvbevidstheden som fri, aktiv selvsætten, og endelig hans forsøg på at forklare, hvorledes en sådan fri, aktiv selvsætten legitimt kan blive påvirket af en udefrakommende andethed. Disse tre temaer behandles med udgangspunkt i tre tekster, som Fichte skrev og publicerede umiddelbart før og under sin ansættelse som professor ved universitetet i Jena i perioden 1794- 1799: \"Über den Begriff der Wissenschaftslehre oder der sogenannten Philosophie\" (\"Om videnskabslærens begreb eller den såkaldte filosofi\") fra foråret 1794; de første paragraffer i \"Grundlage der gesamten Wissenschaftslehre\" (\"Grundlaget for den samlede videnskablære\") fra 1794/95, samt de indledende paragraffer i Fichtes retsfilosofiske hovedværk, \"Grundlage des Naturrechts nach Principien der Wissenschaftslehre\" (\"Naturrettens grundlag ud fra videnskabslærens principper\") fra 1796-97.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Nielsen, Carsten Fogh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-269495"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Fichte","Frihed","Idealisme","Selvbevidsthed"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"fichte system selvbevidsthed frihed om udgangspunktet for fichtes videnskabslære","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-269495","ids":["au-f5baac74-5b8a-4bc9-9f6e-f87127ca2a1e"],"keyword":["Fichte","Frihed","Idealisme","Selvbevidsthed"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-66F61E15299398030B2CFCE210C41DC0"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Philosophy of Education, Aarhus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Carsten Fogh","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"aa9aab60-5389-498d-8d9a-6513747fd9be","name":"Nielsen, Carsten Fogh","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Moe","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Moe","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Morten","key":"ziethenpedh","last":"Ziethen","name":"Ziethen, Morten","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788793041257"],"pages":"79-121","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Forlaget Philosophia","status":"p","subtitle":"en indføring i den tyske idealismes hovedpositioner","title":"System, frihed og virkelighed"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-f5baac74-5b8a-4bc9-9f6e-f87127ca2a1e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Fichte : system, selvbevidsthed, frihed : om udgangspunktet for Fichtes videnskabslære","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-269495","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Aquatic toxicity testing of nanoparticles (NPs) is challenged by their dynamic behavior in test suspensions. The resulting difficulties in controlling and characterizing exposure concentrations are detrimental to the generation of concentration-response data needed for hazard identification of NPs. This study explores the applicability of short-term (1, 2 and 3 h) pulse exposures as means to keep the exposure stable and at the same time disclose acute and chronic effects of AgNPs and CuONPs in D. magna. Dissolution, agglomeration and sedimentation were found to have less influence on exposure concentrations during 1–3 h pulses than for 24–48 h continuous exposures. For AgNPs, preparation of test suspensions in medium 24 h before toxicity testing (aging) increased stability during the short-term pulses. In pulse tests, organisms were exposed to the test materials, AgNPs and CuONPs for 1, 2 and 3 h, and afterwards transferred to clean medium and observed for 48 h (post-exposure period) for acute effects and for 21 d for chronic effects. AgNO3 and CuCl2 were used as reference materials for dissolved silver and copper, respectively. For all test materials, a 3 h pulse caused comparable immobility in D. magna (observed after 48 h post-exposure) as 24 h continuous exposure, as evidenced by overlapping 95% confidence intervals of EC50-values. In the 21 d post-exposure period, no trends in mortality or body length were identified. AgNP and AgNO3 pulses had no effect on the number of moltings, days to first live offspring or cumulated number of offspring, but the number of offspring increased for AgNPs (3 h pulse only). In contrast, CuONP and CuCl2 pulses decreased the number of moltings and offspring, and for CuONPs the time to first live offspring was prolonged. After CuONP exposures, the offspring production decreased more with increasing concentrations than for CuCl2 exposures when taking the measured dissolved copper into account. This indicates a nanoparticle-specific effect for CuONPs, possibly related to the CuONPs accumulated in the gut of D. magna during the pulse exposure. Pulse exposure is an environmentally relevant exposure scenario for NPs, which for AgNPs and CuONPs enables more stable exposures and cause acute immobility of D. magna comparable to continuous 24 h exposures. Pulse exposure is likely relevant and applicable for other toxic and dissolving metal NPs, but this requires further research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Sørensen, Sara Nørgaard","Lützhøft, Hans-Christian Holten","Rasmussen, Rose","Baun, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311522"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Endpoints","Exposure control","Hazard identification","Nanoecotoxicology","Pulse exposure"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"acute and chronic effects from pulse exposure of d magna to silver and copper oxide nanoparticles","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126528493/Postprint_Orbit_Pulse_11_10_2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311522","identifier":[{"id":"84991491340","type":"scopus"},{"id":"27736693","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-17108624-6474-42e8-98a5-07ff080d7c2f"],"keyword":["Endpoints","Exposure control","Hazard identification","Nanoecotoxicology","Pulse exposure"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9B30FBACF575295E5D8FF8A37AAF8DBE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/126528493/Postprint_Orbit_Pulse_11_10_2016.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Environmental Chemistry"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sara Nørgaard","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"1c9842d3-875f-49e3-84a0-d9895fa754fd","name":"Sørensen, Sara Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-3673-9483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans-Christian Holten","key":"lützhøftpau","last":"Lützhøft","locid":"94dcd543-6be3-4fed-8ff3-35070bf2adb9","name":"Lützhøft, Hans-Christian Holten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rose","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Rose","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"baunpau","last":"Baun","locid":"f3cdf4a9-bfc7-4e0e-bf46-df0da8134f0d","name":"Baun, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1396-408X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27736693"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.aquatox.2016.10.004","issn":["0166445X","18791514"],"issn_org":["0166445X"],"journal":"Aquatic Toxicology","pages":"209-217","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Aquatic Toxicology","volume":"180"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84991491340"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-17108624-6474-42e8-98a5-07ff080d7c2f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Acute and chronic effects from pulse exposure of D. magna to silver and copper oxide nanoparticles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311522","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":11,"contributors":["Costea, S.","Carralero, D.","Madsen, Jens","Vianello, N.","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Schrittwieser, R.","Ionita, C.","Spolaore, M.","Kovacic, J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-323888"],"event":{"end":"2016-07-08","place":"Leuven, be","start":"2016-07-04","title":"43rd EPS Conference on Plasma Physics","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany","Italy","Slovenia","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Consorzio RFX","Josef Stefan Institute","Max Planck Institute","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","University of Innsbruck"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"inter elm filamentary studies during density shoulder formation in asdex upgrade","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128856894/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-323888","ids":["dtu-40f0ac9a-780d-4d99-b003-ff9962d50d5f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-9FE157E132C9B1E031A53F22B3EC7269"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128856894/Untitled.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"it","key":"consorzio rfx","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Consorzio RFX","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"si","key":"josef stefan institute","loc":["Slovenia","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Josef Stefan Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"S.","key":"costeapau","last":"Costea","name":"Costea, S.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"D.","key":"carraleropau","last":"Carralero","name":"Carralero, D.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"N.","key":"vianellopau","last":"Vianello","name":"Vianello, N.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"schrittwieserpau","last":"Schrittwieser","name":"Schrittwieser, R.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"ionitapau","last":"Ionita","name":"Ionita, C.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"spolaorepau","last":"Spolaore","name":"Spolaore, M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"J.","key":"kovacicpau","last":"Kovacic","name":"Kovacic, J.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-40f0ac9a-780d-4d99-b003-ff9962d50d5f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Inter-ELM filamentary studies during density “shoulder” formation in ASDEX Upgrade","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-323888","year":"2016","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"A new model for the low-to-high (L-H) confinement transition has been developed based on a new paradigm for turbulence suppression by velocity shear [G. M. Staebler et al., Phys. Rev. Lett.110, 055003 (2013)]. The model indicates that the L-H transition can be mediated by a shift in the radial wave number spectrum of turbulence, as evidenced here, for the first time, by the direct observation of a turbulence radial wave number spectral shift and turbulence structure tilting prior to the L-H transition at tokamak edge by direct probing. This new mechanism does not require a pretransition overshoot in the turbulent Reynolds stress, shunting turbulence energy to zonal flows for turbulence suppression as demonstrated in the experiment.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Xu, G. S.","Wan, B. N.","Wang, H. Q.","Guo, H. Y.","Naulin, Volker","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Wu, X. Q.","Yan, Ning","Chen, L.","Shao, L. M.","Chen, R.","Wang, L.","Zhang, W."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-364951"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low to high confinement transition mediated by turbulence radial wave number spectral shift in a fusion plasma","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/123506807/PhysRevLett.116.095002.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-364951","identifier":[{"id":"84960510361","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26991181","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-ca237083-f48b-4d03-afbd-f9ae0a0fe50f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["S