{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The application of therapeutic hypothermia (TH) for 12 to 24 hours following out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) has been associated with decreased mortality and improved neurological function. However, the optimal duration of cooling is not known. We aimed to investigate whether targeted temperature management (TTM) at 33 ± 1 °C for 48 hours compared to 24 hours results in a better long-term neurological outcome. METHODS: The TTH48 trial is an investigator-initiated pragmatic international trial in which patients resuscitated from OHCA are randomised to TTM at 33 ± 1 °C for either 24 or 48 hours. Inclusion criteria are: age older than 17 and below 80 years; presumed cardiac origin of arrest; and Glasgow Coma Score (GCS) <8, on admission. The primary outcome is neurological outcome at 6 months using the Cerebral Performance Category score (CPC) by an assessor blinded to treatment allocation and dichotomised to good (CPC 1-2) or poor (CPC 3-5) outcome. Secondary outcomes are: 6-month mortality, incidence of infection, bleeding and organ failure and CPC at hospital discharge, at day 28 and at day 90 following OHCA. Assuming that 50 % of the patients treated for 24 hours will have a poor outcome at 6 months, a study including 350 patients (175/arm) will have 80 % power (with a significance level of 5 %) to detect an absolute 15 % difference in primary outcome between treatment groups. A safety interim analysis was performed after the inclusion of 175 patients. DISCUSSION: This is the first randomised trial to investigate the effect of the duration of TTM at 33 ± 1 °C in adult OHCA patients. We anticipate that the results of this trial will add significant knowledge regarding the management of cooling procedures in OHCA patients. TRIAL REGISTRATION: NCT01689077.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Kirkegaard, Hans","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","de Haas, Inge","Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","Ilkjær, Susanne","Kaltoft, Anne","Jeppesen, Anni Nørregaard","Grejs, Anders","Duez, Christophe Henri Valdemar","Larsen, Alf Inge","Pettilä, Ville","Toome, Valdo","Arus, Urmet","Taccone, Fabio Silvio","Storm, Christian","Skrifvars, Markus B","Søreide, Eldar"],"cuid":["S02-088.41-665928"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Mild therapeutic hypothermia","Out of hospital cardiac arrest","Target temperature management"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"time differentiated target temperature management after out of hospital cardiac arrest a multicentre randomised parallel group assessor blinded clinical trial the tth000000000048 trial study protocol for a randomised controlled trial","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-016-1338-9","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-088.41-665928","identifier":[{"id":"000375341800003","type":"wos"},{"id":"27142588","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4855491","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84977624101","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-afa9a065-cc29-4ac7-a95b-e40d8ad30d07","au-92f57702-a5fb-4d62-9af0-83f41eaf997f"],"keyword":["Mild therapeutic hypothermia","Out-of-hospital cardiac arrest","Prolonged target temperature management","Target temperature management"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-2078D23F802CE07DBD0A9B5B8C4AE09B"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4855491/pdf/13063_2016_Article_1338.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13063-016-1338-9","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Research Center for Emergency Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Anæstesi og Intensiv [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Akut"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hans","key":"kirkegaardpau","last":"Kirkegaard","locid":"911be177-8ade-45ff-93ef-6f631e537119","name":"Kirkegaard, Hans","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil S","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3162c449-94c3-4d28-8dbb-c134d6eb76e1","name":"Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","name_org":"Rasmussen, Bodil S","orcid":"0000-0003-2190-145X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Inge","key":"dehaaspau","last":"de Haas","locid":"2fac47d2-b504-4519-ace8-f4b0183d5cc7","name":"de Haas, Inge","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jørgen Feldbæk","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3fb25b9f-381b-44a6-a8dd-26eacf839d37","name":"Nielsen, Jørgen Feldbæk","orcid":"0000-0001-5339-171X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"ilkjærpau","last":"Ilkjær","locid":"9ef9dc36-f921-49ee-b385-073a625d5fd4","name":"Ilkjær, Susanne","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne","key":"kaltoftpau","last":"Kaltoft","locid":"f680344a-f4b6-4df3-99cb-2524eb5820ad","name":"Kaltoft, Anne","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anni Nørregaard","key":"jeppesenpau","last":"Jeppesen","locid":"dfd79e06-3eec-4851-9ca9-96ac6abcb7d1","name":"Jeppesen, Anni Nørgaard","name_org":"Jeppesen, Anni Nørregaard","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"grejspau","last":"Grejs","locid":"5566be9c-2b0c-484c-aab2-e82ede0fde19","name":"Grejs, Anders Morten","name_org":"Grejs, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8850-2982","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christophe Henri Valdemar","key":"duezpau","last":"Duez","locid":"c83d9eab-d5e9-4efd-9525-2f8a2c35c52b","name":"Duez, Christophe Henri Valdemar","orcid":"0000-0001-7560-9214","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Alf Inge","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","name":"Larsen, Alf Inge","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ville","key":"pettiläpau","last":"Pettilä","name":"Pettilä, Ville","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Valdo","key":"toomepau","last":"Toome","name":"Toome, Valdo","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Urmet","key":"aruspau","last":"Arus","name":"Arus, Urmet","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Fabio Silvio","key":"tacconepau","last":"Taccone","name":"Taccone, Fabio Silvio","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"stormpau","last":"Storm","name":"Storm, Christian","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Markus B","key":"skrifvarspau","last":"Skrifvars","name":"Skrifvars, Markus B","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Eldar","key":"søreidepau","last":"Søreide","name":"Søreide, Eldar","rank":17,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["27142588"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s13063-016-1338-9","issn":["14686708","17456215"],"issue":"1","journal":"Trials","pages":"228","paperid":"228","publisher":"BioMed Central","status":"p","title":"Trials","title_org":"Current Controlled Trials in Cardiovascular Medicine (Print)","volume":"17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84977624101"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-afa9a065-cc29-4ac7-a95b-e40d8ad30d07","au-92f57702-a5fb-4d62-9af0-83f41eaf997f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Time-differentiated target temperature management after out-of-hospital cardiac arrest : a multicentre, randomised, parallel-group, assessor-blinded clinical trial (the TTH48 trial): study protocol for a randomised controlled trial","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-088.41-665928","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: The TTH48 trial aims to determine whether prolonged duration (48 hours) of targeted temperature management (TTM) at 33 (±1) °C results in better neurological outcomes compared to standard duration (24 hours) after six months in comatose out-of-hospital cardiac arrest (OHCA) patients. METHODS: TTH48 is an investigator-initiated, multicentre, assessor-blinded, randomised, controlled superiority trial of 24 and 48 hours of TTM at 33 (±1) ° C performed in 355 comatose OHCA patients aged 18 to 80 years who were admitted to ten intensive care units (ICUs) in six Northern European countries. The primary outcome of the study is the Cerebral Performance Category (CPC) score observed at six months after cardiac arrest. CPC scores of 1 and 2 are defined as good neurological outcomes, and CPC scores of 3, 4 and 5 are defined as poor neurological outcomes. The secondary outcomes are as follows: mortality within six months after cardiac arrest, CPC at hospital discharge, Glasgow Coma Scale (GCS) score on day 4, length of stay in ICU and at hospital and the presence of any adverse events such as cerebral, circulatory, respiratory, gastrointestinal, renal, metabolic measures, infection or bleeding. With the planned sample size, we have 80% power to detect a 15% improvement in good neurological outcomes at a two-sided statistical significance level of 5%. DISCUSSION: We present a detailed statistical analysis protocol (SAP) that specifies how primary and secondary outcomes should be evaluated. We also predetermine covariates for adjusted analyses and pre-specify sub-groups for sensitivity analyses. This pre-planned SAP will reduce analysis bias and add validity to the findings of this trial on the effect of length of TTM on important clinical outcomes after cardiac arrest. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT01689077 , 17 September 2012.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Kirkegaard, Hans","Pedersen, Asger Roer","Pettilä, Ville","Hjort, Jakob","Rasmu