9002b-110b-495b-a386-4df5b8d161e5","name":"Andersen, Anders Skallerup","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Louis Nygaard","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"83ec3a19-2857-407d-9edb-77812a7c1bcf","name":"Pedersen, Louis Nygaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Christian","key":"krusepau","last":"Kruse","locid":"6d8dedc8-0eac-4eeb-88a5-85c4bc26d2be","name":"Kruse, Christian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Schou","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","locid":"0395fceb-e2ff-4fe2-8abc-c5486a437197","name":"Olesen, Søren Schou","orcid":"0000-0003-3916-3168","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars","key":"vinterjensenpau","last":"Vinter-Jensen","locid":"9bec0a4a-7fda-4f11-bbed-02e75dc2aa02","name":"Vinter-Jensen, Lars","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"ad223cc8-3f85-4cdf-9da5-5ec44f6a1714","name":"Vestergaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-9046-2967","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik Højgaard","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"c242f457-53f4-4b88-82f3-d7fb297cf98c","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Højgaard","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/s0261-5614(16)30769-5","issn":["02615614","15321983"],"issn_org":["02615614"],"issue":"S1","journal":"Clinical Nutrition","paperid":"MON-P135","publisher":"Churchill Livingstone","status":"p","title":"Clinical Nutrition","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d8dae29f-1e24-4218-acb3-0a68b9f5a432"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Body composition and osteoporosis in patients with intestinal failure","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-113072","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Whether during spontaneous breathing arterial pressure variations (APV) can detect a volume deficit is not established. We hypothesized that amplification of intra-thoracic pressure oscillations by breathing through resistors would enhance APV to allow identification of a reduced cardiac output (CO). This study tested that hypothesis in healthy volunteers exposed to central hypovolemia by head-up tilt. METHODS: Thirteen healthy volunteers were exposed to central hypovolemia by 45° head-up tilt while breathing through a facemask with 7.5 cmH2O inspiratory and/or expiratory resistors. A brachial arterial catheter was used to measure blood pressure and thus systolic pressure variation (SPV), pulse pressure variation and stroke volume variation . Pulse contour analysis determined stroke volume (SV) and CO and we evaluated whether APV could detect a 10 % decrease in CO. RESULTS: During head-up tilt SV decreased form 91 (±46) to 55 (±24) mL (mean ± SD) and CO from 5.8 (±2.9) to 4.0 (±1.8) L/min (p < 0.05), while heart rate increased (65 (±11) to 75 (±13) bpm; P < 0.05). Systolic pressure decreased from 127 (±14) to 121 (±13) mmHg during head-up tilt, while SPV tended to increase (from 21 (±15)% to 30 (±13)%). Yet during head-up tilt, a SPV ≥ 37 % predicted a decrease in CO ≥ 10 % with a sensitivity and specificity of 78 % and 100 %, respectively. CONCLUSION: In spontaneously breathing healthy volunteers combined inspiratory and expiratory resistors enhance SPV during head-up tilted induced central hypovolemia and allow identifying a 10 % reduction in CO. Applying inspiratory and expiratory resistors might detect a fluid deficit in spontaneously breathing patients. TRIAL REGISTRATION: ClinicalTrials.gov number NCT02549482 Registered September 10(th) 2015.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Dahl, Michael","Hayes, Chris Frederick","Rasmussen, Bodil Steen","Larsson, Anders","Secher, Niels H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-114388"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Journal Article"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"can a central blood volume deficit be detected by systolic pressure variation during spontaneous breathing","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12871-016-0224-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-114388","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4982018","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"27515038","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84981328304","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000381573600001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-dd37625d-2ceb-4ef8-a222-b48112434fbd"],"keyword":["Journal Article"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-905CCA334014463DC9D0A0A2A45E2E0E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"rem","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC4982018/pdf/12871_2016_Article_224.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12871-016-0224-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Anæstesi og Intensiv [Klinik Akut]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Aku