{"abstract":"A persistent critique of the museum as an institution has concerned the museum’s apparent lack of life. The argument goes that, with its focus on storing and displaying objects, the museum brings life to death by freezing the intentionality and flow of life into categories and harsh material objectivity (Ames 1992; Boon 1991; Duncan 1995). Andrea Witcomb (2003) has used Theodor Adorno’s notion of the museum as a mausoleum to describe the ways in which the museum ‘encloses objects, separating them from the life forces which gave them their original social and political meanings’ (Witcomb 2003: 104).","author_count":5,"contributors":["Bjerregaard, Peter","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-197611"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oslo"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assembling the spark of life","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85062594378","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-197611","identifier":[{"id":"85062594378","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-77645832-1375-402e-809f-620f8c322ba3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-37796E0F69BE047829656F4DF614582E"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university