cle","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-502834","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Erklæringstypen \"udvidet gennemgang\" er i dag en realistisk alternativ valgmulighed i forhold til at vælge en revisionspåtegning for en række mindre og mellemstore virksomheder. Denne særlige danske erklæring er indført, for at selskaberne kan spare på de administrative byrder. Allerede ved indførelsen blev der fra forskellige sider rejst tvivl, om der rent faktisk ville blive tale om besparelser. En undersøgelse af bankernes holdning hertil viser at 73,7% af bankfolkene mener, at en erklæringsskifte fra revision til udvidet gennemgang har en negativ betydning for kreditvurdering af kunden.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Lund, Anders","Warming-Rasmussen, Bent","Raalskov, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-577529"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Ecomentor - Statsautoriseret Revisionsaktieselskab"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"er udvidet gennemgang et holdbart alternativ til revision","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-577529","ids":["sdu-0f2c20fe-9b72-4581-9bb7-ab1a9ceb3940"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3B17F475A461E3DC479C22BE4B821859"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Social Science (SOC)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Ecomentor - Statsautoriseret Revisionsaktieselskab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Business and Social Sciences, Department of Business and Sustainability"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"lundpau","last":"Lund","name":"Lund, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bent","key":"warmingrasmussenpau","last":"Warming-Rasmussen","locid":"25b46844-13f5-4969-8963-d2927679eba3","name":"Warming-Rasmussen, Bent","orcid":"0000-0001-9256-0993","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jesper","key":"raalskovpau","last":"Raalskov","locid":"90a8a542-6f3f-468a-adba-f1ec37ce7c22","name":"Raalskov, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-3013-7273","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["00346918"],"issue":"1","journal":"Revision & Regnskabsvaesen","pages":"20-24","publisher":"Forlaget Thomson AS","publisher_org":"Forlaget Thomson A/S","status":"p","title":"Revision & Regnskabsvaesen","title_org":"Revision & Regnskabsvæsen","volume":"85"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-0f2c20fe-9b72-4581-9bb7-ab1a9ceb3940"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Er udvidet gennemgang et holdbart alternativ til revision?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-577529","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Objectives: Using multidetector computed tomography, we aimed to assess the early response of neoadjuvant drug therapy for locally advanced colon cancer. Methods: Computed tomography with IV contrast was acquired from 67 patients before and after up to three cycles of preoperative treatment. All patients had histologically confirmed colon cancer, a T4 or T3 tumour with extramural invasion ≥ 5 mm and no distant metastases or peritoneal nodules. The patients were treated with oxaliplatin and capecitabine. In addition, those with no mutations in the KRAS, BRAF and PIK3CA genes were also treated with panitumumab. Before and after treatment, we measured the tumour diameter in two different planes, the extension of the extramural tumour invasion, and the number and size of enlarged lymph nodes. Results: The mean tumour length was 7.8 cm (95% confidence interval (CI): 5.3-10.4) at baseline and 4.34 cm (95% CI: 4.0- 4.9) after treatment. The mean extramural tumour invasion was 10.6 mm (95% CI: 9.5-11.8) at baseline and 5.7 mm (95% CI: 4.7-6.7) after treatment. The mean number of enlarged lymph nodes was 4.1 (95% CI: 3.4-4.9) at baseline and 2.1 (95% CI: 1.4-2.7) after treatment. According to RECIST 1.1, 45% (95% CI: 34-57) of the patients had a response and 55% (95% CI: 43-67) had stable disease. None of the patients showed progressive disease. Conclusion: Using MDCT, we report a significant reduction in tumour size, extramural tumour invasion, and number and size of pathological regional lymph nodes following neoadjuvant treatment of locally advanced colon cancer. NEC may induce not only tumour down-sizing, but may bring about a significant prolongation of disease-free survival and eventually improve overall survival. The shown early response to NEC leads to hope for improvement in the outcome of locally advanced colon cancer patients, and clinical follow-up data are warranted.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Dam, Claus","Lund-Rasmussen, Vera","Pløen, John","Jakobsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-615223"],"event":{"end":"2016-12-13","place":"Amsterdam, nl","start":"2016-12-11","title":"8th European Multidisciplinary Colorectal Cancer Congress","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CT","Chemotherapy","Colorectal cancer","RECIST","respons"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ct assessment of early response to neoadjuvant therapy in colon cancer","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dco","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121912428/Abstract_book_posters_EMCCC_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-615223","ids":["sdu-928c5402-9562-4903-88e1-b06e765e57c5"],"keyword":["CT","Chemotherapy","Colorectal Cancer","RECIST","respons"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-14E4EADAE6F905DBC9C0CC805BD89794"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/121912428/Abstract_book_posters_EMCCC_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Vejle Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"103f5188-29ea-414d-ac02-ab5253a7e41b","name":"Dam, Claus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Vera","key":"lundrasmussenpau","last":"Lund-Rasmussen","name":"Lund-Rasmussen, Vera","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"pløenpau","last":"Pløen","locid":"66df5d1a-fea1-429b-954d-c635ef4364bb","name":"Pløen, John","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"6c772581-e8fe-48bc-a932-1d1c5122c25a","name":"Jakobsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-2110-2615","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-928c5402-9562-4903-88e1-b06e765e57c5"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"CT assessment of early response to neoadjuvant therapy in colon cancer","type":"Conference Poster","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-615223","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"We use unique and rich register data of 88,948 sick-listed workers to investigate the effect of active labor market measures on the duration until returning to non-subsidized employment and the duration of this employment. To identify causal treatment effects, we exploit over-time variation in 98 job centers’ use of active labor market measures. We find that ordinary education and especially subsidized job training have statistically significant positive employment effects. Subsidized job training has a large, statistically significant positive effect on the transition into employment but no effect on the subsequent employment duration. In contrast, ordinary education has a statistically significant positive effect on employment duration but no effect on the transition to employment. This null effect consists of a large positive effect of having completed education and a large negative lock-in effect, with low re-employment chances during program participation. Moreover, non-formal education (e.g., shorter courses) and subsidized internships have no or even negative employment effects.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Holm, Anders","Høgelund, Jan","Gørtz, Mette","Rasmussen, Kristin Storck","Houlberg, Helle Sophie Bøje"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-664092"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-UND"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE","DI-U-UND"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"employment effects of active labor market measures for sick listed workers","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dw","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/476645/WP_02_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-664092","ids":["vive-89e6101e-41ad-47ee-aab1-7ed181d809fb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-14B325FC8BAC783BE8C6B9D7DAAC79FA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.vive.dk/ws/files/476645/WP_02_2016.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["The Danish National Institute for Social Research, Vulnerable Children, Day Care and Schooling"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"unclear universities","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-UND","l3nl":"Undetermined","l3nn":"Unclear Universities","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Unclear Universities","namevar":["Økonomisk Institut","Økonomisk Studienævn"],"nora_code":"DI-U-UND","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"holmpau","last":"Holm","locid":"6da5e940-c8e5-47be-ab86-20d35f017cf3","name":"Holm, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jan","key":"høgelundpau","last":"Høgelund","locid":"3a3cb5db-51dc-4516-a2f6-0e876ea82e23","name":"Høgelund, Jan","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mette","key":"gørtzpau","last":"Gørtz","name":"Gørtz, Mette","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristin Storck","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"7c508a0a-72a7-4ed2-963a-603c04127d7b","name":"Rasmussen, Kristin Storck","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Sophie Bøje","key":"houlbergpau","last":"Houlberg","locid":"dab3d5fb-ec7c-4c16-896c-4d8030051454","name":"Houlberg, Helle Sophie Bøje","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issue":"02:2016","place":"København","publisher":"SFI - Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Velfærd","series":"SFI Working Paper","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Undetermined","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-89e6101e-41ad-47ee-aab1-7ed181d809fb"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Employment effects of active labor market measures for sick-listed workers","type":"Working Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-664092","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"By taking advantage of the ability of (64)Cu to bind non-specifically to gold surfaces, we have developed a new methodology to embed this radionuclide inside gold nanoparticles (AuNPs). (64)Cu enables the in vivo imaging of AuNPs by positron emission tomography (PET). AuNPs have a multitude of uses within health technology and are useful tools for general nanoparticle research. (64)Cu-AuNPs were prepared by incubating AuNP seeds with (64)Cu(2+), followed by the entrapment of the radionuclide by grafting a second layer of gold on the surface. This resulted in radiolabeling efficiencies of 53 ± 6%. The radiolabel showed excellent stability when challenging with EDTA for two days (>95% radioactivity retention) and showed no loss of (64)Cu when incubated with 50% mouse serum for two days. The methodology was chelator-free, and circumvents traditional concerns over chelator instability and altered AuNP properties due to surface modification. Radiolabeled (64)Cu-AuNP cores were prepared in a biomedically relevant size of 30 nm and used to investigate the in vivo stability of three different AuNP coatings by PET imaging in a murine xenograft tumor model. We found the longest plasma half-life (T½ = 9 hours) and highest tumor accumulation (3.9 %ID/g) by using polyethylene glycol (PEG) coating, while faster elimination from the bloodstream was observed with both a Tween 20-stabilized coating and a zwitterionic coating based on a mixture of sulfonic acids and quaternary amines, which has previously been reported to be superior to PEG. The new embedding method provides the utilization of PET imaging in combination with the multituide of uses that AuNPs have found in health technology, and the method can equally well be utilized for therapeutic copper radioisotopes for use in radiotherapy.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Frellsen, Anders Floor","Hansen, Anders Elias","Jølck, Rasmus Irming","Kempen, Paul","Severin, Gregory","Rasmussen, Palle","Kjær, Andreas","Jensen, Andreas Tue Ingemann","Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"cuid":["S02-086.48-038216"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Coating Materials","Copper 64","Gold nanoparticles","Intrinsic Radiolabeling","PET"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a mouse positron emission tomography study of the biodistribution of gold nanoparticles with different surface coatings using embedded copper 000000000064","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84997498799","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-086.48-038216","identifier":[{"id":"27754658","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84997498799","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-fe470551-2a5b-4aa0-b3a0-ed9fc481f916","ku-c24dadd4-13c5-42d6-8cce-e7a6124937cc"],"keyword":["Coating Materials","Copper-64","Gold Nanoparticles","Intrinsic Radiolabeling","PET"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-00F29A19929AC056242838CC27F7AC66"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2016","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l