{"abstract":"Nærværende rapport beskriver resultaterne fra en undersøgelse af hvordan – og i hvilket omfang – pædagoger i danske daginstitutioner inddrager de pædagogiske læreplaner i deres faglige refleksioner og praksis. Således belyser undersøgelsen på sin vis et centralt aspekt af pædagogen som didaktiker. Metodisk er undersøgelsen gennemført som en elektronisk baseret spørgeskemaundersøgelse med en blanding af kvantitative og kvalitative elementer. Muligheder for uddybende fritekstsvar supplerede fastlagte udsagn som respondenten skulle forhold sig til på en Likert skala. Det teoretiske udgangspunkt var dynamisk didaktik (Broström, Hansen, Jensen & Svinth, 2015), og således en forståelse af didaktik som refleksion over, gennemførsel og evaluering af planlagt pædagogisk praksis. Resultaterne peger samlet på, at de pædagogiske læreplaner spiller en væsentlig rolle for pædagogerne i deres arbejde, primært i forhold til den overordnede planlægning og refleksion, samt i forhold til dokumentation og evaluering. Læreplanerne opleves som ressourcekrævende, men som et redskab til at løfte fagligheden og kvaliteten af det pædagogiske indhold, primært indenfor det almenpædagogiske område. De fleste pædagoger oplever at have mulighed for at deltage i, og således præge, det løbende arbejde med at revidere og justere institutionens læreplan. Da resultaterne også peger på en (relativt) svag forbindelse mellem læreplanen og hverdagens planlægning, er en implikation af denne undersøgelse en videre udforskning af netop læreplanens rolle i den konkrete pædagogiske praksis.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Broström, Stig","Jensen, Anders Skriver","Kirkegaard, Sara","Belling, Maria Nøhr","Rasmussen, Kjeld"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-159046"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dagtilbud","Forskning","Læreplaner","Læringsledelse","Pædagogprofession"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"pædagogiske læreplaner i dagtilbud hvordan og i hvilket omfang inddrager pædagoger i danske daginstitutioner læreplanerne i faglige refleksioner og praksis","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://edu.au.dk/fileadmin/edu/Forskning/Ebog_-_Paedagogiske_laereplaner_i_dagtilbud.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-159046","ids":["au-33f71ba4-d53a-4577-9aaf-256d51d3b2a5"],"keyword":["Dagtilbud","Forskning","Læreplaner","Læringsledelse","Pædagogprofession"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-2F2D6411449D5BE0567471ADA04C8100"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.au.dk/ws/files/98297569/Belling_Kirkegaard_Brostr_m_Jensen_og_Rasmussen_2016_L_replaner_i_dagtilbud._Endelig_udg..pdf.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://edu.au.dk/fileadmin/edu/Forskning/Ebog_-_Paedagogiske_laereplaner_i_dagtilbud.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - General Education, Emdrup","Aarhus University, Arts, Danish School of Education, Danish School of Education - Research Programme in Learning for Care, Sustainability and Health"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stig","key":"broströmpau","last":"Broström","locid":"62b32da3-814a-4776-aef6-505a551d2ff1","name":"Broström, Stig","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Skriver","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"19868618-1afb-44ba-9f21-5fc226e76f77","name":"Jensen, Anders Skriver","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sara","key":"kirkegaardpau","last":"Kirkegaard","locid":"65c11ed7-b3fd-45b3-8a10-a9e57c4e10c7","name":"Kirkegaard, Sara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Maria Nøhr","key":"bellingpau","last":"Belling","locid":"8e636d76-0b78-4fd0-9c2b-7a4dbfcffb9b","name":"Belling, Maria Nøhr","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Kjeld","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"29","place":"København","publisher":"DPU, Aarhus Universitet","status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-33f71ba4-d53a-4577-9aaf-256d51d3b2a5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Pædagogiske læreplaner i dagtilbud : hvordan – og i hvilket omfang – inddrager pædagoger i danske daginstitutioner læreplanerne i faglige refleksioner og praksis?","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-159046","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"PURPOSE: To evaluate and compare the diagnostic performance of whole-body planar bone scintigraphy (WBS), single photon emission computed tomography (SPECT), SPECT/low-dose computerized tomography (SPECT/ldCT) and SPECT/contrast enhanced diagnostic CT (SPECT/cdCT) in the staging of patients with advanced breast cancer. METHODS: Seventy-eight patients with recurrence of biopsy-proven breast cancer and suspicion of disseminated disease were investigated with WBS, SPECT, SPECT/ldCT, SPECT/cdCT and MRI performed on the same day in this prospective study. Images were separately analysed in a blinded fashion by radiologists and nuclear medicine physicians regarding the presence of pathological findings. MRI served as reference standard. RESULTS: According to reference standard, 38 of 73 patients had bone metastases. The sensitivity was 87%, 87%, 79%, and 84% and specificity 63%, 71%, 63% and 83% for WBS, SPECT, SPECT/ldCT and SPECT/cdCT. A significantly increased specificity of SPECT/cdCT compared to WBS and SPECT/ldCT was found, and other parameters did not differ significantly between modalities. Additional two patients had bone metastases solely located outside the MRI scan field and seven patients had soft tissue metastases, but no skeletal changes on MRI. CONCLUSION: WBS, SPECT and SPECT/ldCT were less sensitive than MRI and equally specific for the detection of bone metastases in patients with advanced breast cancer. Based on our findings, we suggest that initial staging include WBS, MRI of the spine and CT for soft tissue evaluation. Further studies may clarify the potential benefits of whole-body MRI and 18F-NaF PET/CT or 18F-FDG PET/CT.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Haraldsen, Ate","Bluhme, Henrik","Røhl, Lisbeth","Pedersen, Erik Morre","Jensen, Anders Bonde","Ebert, Eva Boysen Fynboe","Nellemann, Hanne Marie","Rasmussen, Finn","Morsing, Anni"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-224400"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bone metastases","Bone scintigraphy","Breast cancer","Magnetic Resonance Imaging","SPECT CT"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"single photon emission computed tomography spect and spect low dose computerized tomography did not increase sensitivity or specificity compared to planar bone scintigraphy for detection of bone metastases in advanced breast cancer","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cpf.12191","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-224400","identifier":[{"id":"84954451655","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25257661","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-a6c99222-0151-4c27-a71c-382339f33399"],"keyword":["Bone metastases","Bone scintigraphy","Breast cancer","Magnetic resonance imaging","SPECT/CT"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F82A9455CD8DAFCFF4ED0D8DB52B571"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/cpf.12191","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Nuclear Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ate","key":"haraldsenpau","last":"Haraldsen","locid":"286e2f7c-a90b-4ded-b058-9d0fd9d8a0de","name":"Haraldsen, Ate","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"coun