{"abstract":"Reminiscens er en socialfaglig tilgang, der anvendes til at styrke erindringer, færdigheder og livskvalitet hos mennesker med demens. Kapitlet beskriver, hvad der karakteriserer en omsorgspraksis baseret på reminiscens set i forhold til hverdagsliv, samt hvordan kultur og livshistorien spiller sammen med reminiscens. Kapitlet tager udgangspunkt i praksis på plejecentre og ved museumsbesøg, men reminiscens kan dog let anvendes i samvær med mennesker med demens i andre sammenhænge. Plejecenterrammen er valgt, fordi vi gerne vil understrege, at også mennesker, der er langt i deres demensforløb, kan have glæde af reminiscens, og at det som medarbejder er et værdifuldt redskab at kende til i en hverdag med udfordringer ift. kommunikation. De kulturhistoriske frilandsmuseer er oplagte samarbejdspartnere for plejepersonalet, da museerne har hele miljøer med interiør og genstande fra 1950’erne, 60’erne og 70’erne, der, som vi vil beskrive, potentielt giver en totaloplevelse med mange erindringsglimt. Oplevelserne på museet kan give plejepersonalet vigtig viden om livshistorie og minder, oplysninger, der kan være nyttige i det daglige arbejde på plejecentret. Ligeledes kan museumsbesøget forhåbentlig inspirere plejepersonalet til forskellige aktiviteter, der kan gennemføres på plejecenteret.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Jensen, Anders Møller","Bollerup Overgaard, Susanne","Amlund Rasmussen, Agnete"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-784463"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Demens","Livskvalitet","Sundhed ernæring og livskvalitet"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-UC"],"level3":{"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reminiscens samvær og livskvalitet i demensomsorgen","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://danskgerontologi.dk/wp-content/uploads/2018/09/AtSkabeGodeDage_webversion_131118.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-784463","ids":["via-389241a4-bf9f-4039-949f-569ec1fdfb71"],"keyword":["Sundhed, ernæring og livskvalitet","demens","livskvalitet"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-98FF635D281D7C624B27D302995F4B32"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Sundhed og velfærdsteknologi, Program for aldring"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Møller","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b5aef190-7e7d-47c1-957a-462dece271c3","name":"Jensen, Anders Møller","orcid":"0000-0002-0692-9959","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Susanne","key":"bollerupovergaardpau","last":"Bollerup Overgaard","name":"Bollerup Overgaard, Susanne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Agnete","key":"amlundrasmussenpau","last":"Amlund Rasmussen","name":"Amlund Rasmussen, Agnete","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Marie","key":"beckpedh","last":"Beck","name":"Beck, Anne Marie","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Birgitte","key":"højlundpedh","last":"Højlund","name":"Højlund, Birgitte","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Louise Scheel","key":"thomasenpedh","last":"Thomasen","name":"Thomasen, Louise Scheel","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1. udgave","eisbn":["9788798140771"],"isbn":["9788798140719"],"pages":"83-92","publisher":"Dansk Gerontologisk Selskab","status":"p","subtitle":"Hverdagsliv i et gerontologisk perspektiv","title":"At skabe gode dage"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-389241a4-bf9f-4039-949f-569ec1fdfb71"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Reminiscens : Samvær og livskvalitet i demensomsorgen","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-784463","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"INTRODUCTION: Exercise is an important countermeasure to limb muscle dysfunction in COPD. The two major training modalities in COPD rehabilitation, endurance training (ET) and resistance training (RT), may both be efficient in improving muscle strength, exercise capacity, and health-related quality of life, but the effects on quadriceps muscle characteristics have not been thoroughly described. METHODS: Thirty COPD patients (forced expiratory volume in 1 second: 56% of predicted, standard deviation [SD] 14) were randomized to 8 weeks of ET or RT. Vastus lateralis muscle biopsies were obtained before and after the training intervention to assess muscle morphology and metabolic and angiogenic factors. Symptom burden, exercise capacity (6-minute walking and cycle ergometer tests), and vascular function were also assessed. RESULTS: Both training modalities improved symptom burden and exercise capacity with no difference between the two groups. The mean (SD) proportion of glycolytic type IIa muscle fibers was reduced after ET (from 48% [SD 11] to 42% [SD 10], P<0.05), whereas there was no significant change in muscle fiber distribution with RT. There was no effect of either training modality on muscle capillarization, angiogenic factors, or vascular function. After ET the muscle protein content of phosphofructokinase was reduced (P<0.05) and the citrate synthase content tended increase (P=0.08) but no change was observed after RT. CONCLUSION: Although both ET and RT improve symptoms and exercise capacity, ET induces a more oxidative quadriceps muscle phenotype, counteracting muscle dysfunction in COPD.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Iepsen, Ulrik Winning","Munch, Gregers Druedal Wibe","Rugbjerg, Mette","Rinnov, Anders Rasmussen","Zacho, Morten","Mortensen, Stefan Peter","Secher, Niels H.","Ringbæk, Thomas","Pedersen, Bente Klarlund","Hellsten, Ylva","Lange, Peter","Thaning, Pia"],"cuid":["S02-087.41-042103"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Globa