{"abstract":"Introduction: Upper motor neuron disorders are believed to leave the peripheral nervous system (PNS) intact. In this study we examined whether there is evidence of PNS involvement in spinal cord injury (SCI). Methods: Twelve subjects with chronic low cervical or thoracic SCI were included prospectively. Needle electromyography was done in 10 different muscles in each subject bilaterally. Nerve conduction studies (NCS) were conducted in the fibular, tibial, and femoral motor and fibular and sural sensory nerves. Results: Half the subjects had widespread abnormal spontaneous activity (SA), and the amount of SA correlated inversely with reflex activity and nerve length. Fibular nerve entrapment across the knee was seen in 6 subjects, and sciatic nerve entrapment was seen in 1. Apart from entrapment neuropathies, NCS changes were found predominantly in motor nerves. Conclusion: The presence of widespread electrophysiologic changes outside entrapment sites indicates that SCI has a significant impact on the entire PNS, affecting the motor part predominantly.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Tankisi, Hatice","Pugdahl, Kirsten","Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","Clemmensen, Dorte","Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","Christensen, Peter","Krogh, Klaus","Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-197314"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electromyography","Nerve conduction study","Peripheral nervous system","Spinal cord injury","Spontaneous activity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"peripheral nervous system involvement in chronic spinal cord injury","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84955216805","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-197314","identifier":[{"id":"25758550","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84940907571","type":"scopus"},{"id":"84955216805","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-76efc96e-baa8-403d-b0ca-2f70d0abdb15"],"keyword":["Electromyography","Nerve conduction study","Peripheral nervous system","Spinal cord injury","Spontaneous activity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EA8624B24167C0D05036F0444267E663"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Clinical Neurophysiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hatice","key":"tankisipau","last":"Tankisi","locid":"2b3f7bfd-71e0-4e1e-9a63-62cf6d26d1ea","name":"Tankisi, Hatice","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kirsten","key":"pugdahlpau","last":"Pugdahl","locid":"31c88d8a-8ff0-4cce-92bf-7d295700ad8e","name":"Pugdahl, Kirsten","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Mylius","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0a611a7f-8a19-41f3-9221-58fe673b3ef1","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","orcid":"0000-0002-4768-7255","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"826b8629-1e7d-42d6-8e46-7f9a993bf743","name":"Clemmensen, Dorte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yazan F. H.","key":"rawashdehpau","last":"Rawashdeh","locid":"dd97020c-c4f8-4898-8b08-a088d13d45de","name":"Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","name_org":"Rawashdeh, Yazan F. H.","orcid":"0000-0002-5517-2980","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"456d99d5-ee96-4333-afef-d1596a62cf74","name":"Christensen, Peter","orcid":"0000-0002-6611-3935","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klaus","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"e69f7028-9eb1-4f3a-ab4e-c684c234bf2e","name":"Krogh, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0001-9168-2403","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"fuglsangfrederiksenpau","last":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen","locid":"9dbd8297-9ebb-41f0-ab0b-8ddfef8c33bd","name":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-3926-5287","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25758550"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/mus.24644","issn":["0148639X","10974598"],"issn_org":["0148639X"],"issue":"6","journal":"Muscle & Nerve","pages":"1016-1022","publisher":"John Wiley & Sons Inc.","status":"p","title":"Muscle & Nerve","volume":"52"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84955216805"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-76efc96e-baa8-403d-b0ca-2f70d0abdb15"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Peripheral nervous system involvement in chronic spinal cord injury","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-197314","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Two cases: A 66-year-old woman was referred to the hospital due to dyspnoea and cough. Seven months prior to referral, the patient had choked on a chunk of nut and grain-filled bread. She had daily cough and dyspnoea. The patient was convinced of an airway foreign body and she contacted her general practitioner and the emergency service several times; they all found this unlikely. Fibre optic bronchoscopy revealed two obstructing nut-like foreign bodies in the right upper and lower lobe, respectively. A 77-year-old man with sarcoidosis developed increased dyspnoea and sputum production. Three weeks earlier, the patient had choked on a magnesium tablet. Everyone was convinced that the tablet had dissolved. Infection was suspected. Chest CT scan was performed showing no obvious signs of infection or progression in sarcoidosis. After the CT scan, the patient coughed up the remains of the tablet and his symptoms resolved. Retrospective evaluation of the CT scan revealed the tablet.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Møller, Janne","Rasmussen, Finn","Hilberg, Ole","Løkke, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-252836"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"airway foreign body aspiration common yet easily overlooked two interesting cases","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84930965749","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-252836","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4442167","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84930965749","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26002666","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-d84c1fa2-8832-4f15-a533-2649aae1c6d9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2EED1F4ABB8EA7DDFB4F489FC474783F"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - Department of Respiratory Diseases and Allergy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Janne","key":"møllerpau","last":"Møller","locid":"966ca400-a4a9-45a7-afd0-3825b52e1032","name":"Møller, Janne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Finn","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1c4dadf5-d001-4c6c-9f23-347af298c53d","name":"Rasmussen, Finn","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole","key":"hilbergpau","last":"Hilberg","locid":"4cec668c-4042-4069-9e37-b09fe84ed3b1","name":"Hilberg, Ole","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Løkke","key":"ottesenpau","last":"Ottesen","locid":"93e030be-623c-4143-ab57-fb097315970e","name":"Løkke, Anders","name_org":"Ottesen, Anders Løkke","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26002666"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1136/bcr-2014-209240","issn":["1757790X"],"journal":"BMJ Case Reports","publisher":"BMJ Publishing Group","status":"p","title":"BMJ Case Reports","title_org":"B M J Case Reports","volume":"2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84930965749"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-d84c1fa2-8832-4f15-a533-2649aae1c6d9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Airway foreign body aspiration : common, yet easily overlooked! Two interesting cases","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-252836","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Five white-beaked dolphins Lagenorhynchus albirostris with outwardly vertebral kyphosis, kyphoscoliosis or lordosis were identified during a photo-identification survey of over 400 individuals (2002-2013) in Faxafloi and Skjalfandi Bays, Iceland. In addition, 3 stranding reports from Denmark, The Netherlands and the UK were analysed, providing both external observation and post mortem details of axial deviations of the vertebral column in this species. Two of the free-ranging cases and 2 of the stranded specimens appeared to have an acquired disease, either as a direct result of trauma, or indirectly from trauma/wound and subsequent infection and bony proliferation, although we were unable to specifically identify the causes. Our data represent a starting point to understand vertebral column deformations and their implications in white-beaked dolphins from the eastern North Atlantic. We recommend for future necropsy cases to conduct macro- and microscopic evaluation of muscle from both sides of the deformed region, in order to assess chronic or acute conditions related to the vertebral deformations and cause of death.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Bertulli, Chiara G.","Galatius, Anders","Kinze, Carl C.","Rasmussen, Marianne H.","Deaville, Rob","Jepson, Paul","Vedder, Elisabeth J.","Contreras, Guillermo J. Sanchez","Sabin, Richard C.","Watson, Alastair"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-272069"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"corresponding_author":["Bertulli, Chiara G."],"country":["Iceland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Oklahoma State University","The Natural History Museum, London","University of Iceland","Zoological Society of London"],"keyword":["BOTTLE NOSED DOLPHINS","Injuries","Kyphosis","Lagenorhynchus albirostris","Lordosis","Reproduction","SCARS","Skin lesions","Survival","Tursiops truncatus","WATERS","White beaked dolphin"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Unspecified organisation"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"vertebral column deformities in white beaked dolphins from the eastern north atlantic","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84942024147","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-272069","identifier":[{"id":"26378408","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84942024147","type":"scopus"},{"id":"000361823800006","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-fa3b7e00-bc68-44c1-9ab5-dff429c44b1c"],"keyword":["ALBIROSTRIS","BOTTLE-NOSED DOLPHINS","INJURIES","Kyphoscoliosis","Kyphosis","Lagenorhynchus albirostris","Lordosis","PHYSICAL DEFORMITIES","REPRODUCTION","SCARS","SKIN-LESIONS","SURVIVAL","TURSIOPS-TRUNCATUS","Vertebral column deformity","WATERS","White-beaked dolphin"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-41F40BCA6C9CCC8262EABB1C1761236C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"is","key":"university of iceland","loc":["Iceland","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Iceland","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Technical Sciences, Department of Ecoscience, Department of Ecoscience - Marine Mammal Research 1"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"zoological society of london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Zoological Society of London","used":1},{"affno":"4","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Unspecified organisation"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"gb","key":"the natural history museum london","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"The Natural History Museum, London","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"us","key":"oklahoma state university","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Oklahoma State University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Chiara G.","key":"bertullipau","last":"Bertulli","name":"Bertulli, Chiara G.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"galatiuspau","last":"Galatius","locid":"34804171-9f60-4314-a4f4-70df2c4fe2bf","name":"Galatius, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Carl C.","key":"kinzepau","last":"Kinze","name":"Kinze, Carl C.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne H.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Marianne H.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rob","key":"deavillepau","last":"Deaville","name":"Deaville, Rob","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Paul","key":"jepsonpau","last":"Jepson","name":"Jepson, Paul","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Elisabeth J.","key":"vedderpau","last":"Vedder","name":"Vedder, Elisabeth J.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Guillermo J. Sanchez","key":"contreraspau","last":"Contreras","name":"Contreras, Guillermo J. Sanchez","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Richard C.","key":"sabinpau","last":"Sabin","name":"Sabin, Richard C.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Alastair","key":"watsonpau","last":"Watson","name":"Watson, Alastair","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26378408"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3354/dao02904","issn":["01775103","16161580"],"issn_org":["01775103"],"issue":"1","journal":"Diseases of Aquatic Organisms","pages":"59-67","publisher":"Inter-Research","publisher_org":"Inter Research","status":"p","title":"Diseases of Aquatic Organisms","title_org":"Diseases of Aquatic Organisms (Online)","volume":"116"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84942024147"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-fa3b7e00-bc68-44c1-9ab5-dff429c44b1c"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Vertebral column deformities in white-beaked dolphins from the eastern North Atlantic","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-272069","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Adjunct therapy with the histone deacetylase inhibitor (HDACi) romidepsin increases plasma viremia in HIV patients on combination antiretroviral therapy (cART). However, a potential concern is that reversing HIV latency with an HDACi may reactivate the virus in anatomical compartments with sub-optimal cART concentrations leading to de novo infection of susceptible cells in these sites. We tested physiologically relevant romidepsin concentrations known to reactivate latent HIV in order to definitively address this concern. We found that romidepsin significantly inhibited HIV infection in PBMCs and CD4+ T cells, but not in monocyte-derived-macrophages. In addition, romidepsin impaired HIV spreading in CD4+ T cell cultures. When we evaluated the impact of romidepsin on quantitative viral outgrowth assays with primary resting CD4+ T cells, we found that resting CD4+ T cells exposed to romidepsin exhibited reduced proliferation and viability. This significantly lowered assay sensitivity when measuring the efficacy of romidepsin as an HIV latency reversal agent. All together our data indicate that romidepsin-based HIV eradication strategies are unlikely to reseed a latent T cell reservoir, even under sub-optimal cART conditions, because romidepsin profoundly restricts de novo HIV infections.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Jønsson, Kasper L","Tolstrup, Martin","Vad-Nielsen, Johan","Kjær, Kathrine","Laustsen, Anders","Andersen, Morten Nørgaard","Rasmussen, Thomas A","Søgaard, Ole Schmeltz","Østergaard, Lars Jørgen","Denton, Paul W","Jakobsen, Martin Roelsgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-274483"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"histone deacetylase inhibitor romidepsin inhibits de novo hiv 000000000001 infections","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/AAC.00574-15","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-274483","identifier":[{"id":"25896701","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4468708","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84935868889","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-fe639b51-8e41-4153-b0e1-347d4cd501f1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C81A65159D28045B81F19B43D93FA0EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1128/AAC.00574-15","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Research and Education, Bartholin Building"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper L","key":"jønssonpau","last":"Jønsson","locid":"e54512e8-5a1d-4147-9406-566cdd39a2b5","name":"Jønsson, Kasper L","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Martin","key":"tolstruppau","last":"Tolstrup","locid":"36e9f1d5-608c-46b7-8d41-2505c02086fc","name":"Tolstrup, Martin","orcid":"0000-0001-7020-5173","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Johan","key":"vadnielsenpau","last":"Vad-Nielsen","locid":"4e820f9a-3d0a-4675-bf78-3ffa9749a20f","name":"Vad-Nielsen, Johan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kathrine","key":"kjærpau","last":"Kjær","locid":"b0bfbbc0-128a-4a79-b881-653f10e7ee85","name":"Kjær, Kathrine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first