rk, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten Bagge","key":"laustsenpau","last":"Laustsen","locid":"aa36f752-c94a-4d5d-97f0-4737352db596","name":"Laustsen, Carsten Bagge","orcid":"0000-0003-3602-8921","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael Hviid","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Michael Hviid","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael Hviid","key":"jacobsenpedh","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Michael Hviid","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Kasper","key":"lippertrasmussenpedh","last":"Lippert-Rasmussen","name":"Lippert-Rasmussen, Kasper","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"nedergaardpedh","last":"Nedergaard","name":"Nedergaard, Peter","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"3.","isbn":["9788741263199"],"pages":"287-325","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","title":"Videnskabsteori i statskundskab, sociologi og forvaltning"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-426bb7ec-4eda-434e-b64b-38be7fb1efd8","ku-98f92d9c-80b2-47a2-a3fa-4c485755fea3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Strukturalisme og poststrukturalisme","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-091.07-017507","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Kennewick Man, referred to as the Ancient One by Native Americans, is a male human skeleton discovered in Washington state (USA) in 1996 and initially radiocarbon dated to 8,340-9,200 calibrated years before present (BP). His population affinities have been the subject of scientific debate and legal controversy. Based on an initial study of cranial morphology it was asserted that Kennewick Man was neither Native American nor closely related to the claimant Plateau tribes of the Pacific Northwest, who claimed ancestral relationship and requested repatriation under the Native American Graves Protection and Repatriation Act (NAGPRA). The morphological analysis was important to judicial decisions that Kennewick Man was not Native American and that therefore NAGPRA did not apply. Instead of repatriation, additional studies of the remains were permitted. Subsequent craniometric analysis affirmed Kennewick Man to be more closely related to circumpacific groups such as the Ainu and Polynesians than he is to modern Native Americans. In order to resolve Kennewick Man's ancestry and affiliations, we have sequenced his genome to ∼1× coverage and compared it to worldwide genomic data including for the Ainu and Polynesians. We find that Kennewick Man is closer to modern Native Americans than to any other population worldwide. Among the Native American groups for whom genome-wide data are available for comparison, several seem to be descended from a population closely related to that of Kennewick Man, including the Confederated Tribes of the Colville Reservation (Colville), one of the five tribes claiming Kennewick Man. We revisit the cranial analyses and find that, as opposed to genome-wide comparisons, it is not possible on that basis to affiliate Kennewick Man to specific contemporary groups. We therefore conclude based on genetic comparisons that Kennewick Man shows continuity with Native North Americans over at least the last eight millennia.","author_count":22,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Morten","Sikora, Martin","Albrechtsen, Anders","Korneliussen, Thorfinn Sand","Moreno-Mayar, J. Victor","Poznik, G. David","Zollikofer, Christoph P. E.","de Leon, Marcia S. Ponce","Allentoft, Morten E.","Moltke, Ida","Jónsson, Hákon","Valdiosera, Cristina","Malhi, Ripan S.","Orlando, Ludovic","Bustamante, Carlos D.","Stafford, Thomas W.","Meltzer, David J.","Nielsen, Rasmus","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S02-097.14-030286"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD","Oceania"],"corresponding_author":["Willerslev, Eske"],"country":["Australia","Switzerland","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","La Trobe University","Southern Methodist University","Stanford University","University of California at Berkeley","University of Illinois at Urbana-Champaign","University of Zurich"],"keyword":["America","DNA","Genome","History","Population"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the ancestry and affiliations of kennewick man","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/nature14625","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-097.14-030286","identifier":[{"id":"26087396","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000358378900035","type":"wos"},{"id":"PMC4878456","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84937475681","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-f3e3501a-0d84-4c0b-ac6e-2194ee1c62f4","ku-87c1f71b-aeeb-430e-afe0-508260b1deb3"],"keyword":["AMERICA","DNA","GENOME","GORDON CREEK WOMAN","HISTORY","POPULATION"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-94B23C8F1D9A05E3BF8A9C9F9950