{"abstract":"PURPOSE: The artificial somato-autonomic reflex arch (Xiao procedure) was proposed as treatment for neurogenic bladder dysfunction. We investigated the effects of the procedure on lower urinary tract function. MATERIALS AND METHODS: Seven and 3 patients with a median age of 46 years (range 19 to 64) had AIS A and B spinal cord injury, respectively. In these patients an anastomosis was created between the ventral (motor) part of L5 and the ventral part of the S2 root. Urodynamics were performed and a standard questionnaire was completed at baseline and 18 months postoperatively. RESULTS: Artificial reflex arch stimulation did not initiate voiding or increase bladder pressure. Maximum bladder capacity did not change significantly from baseline to followup (median 427.5 ml, range 168 to 581 vs 498.5, range 271 to 580, p = 0.09). Likewise, bladder compliance did not significantly differ at baseline and followup (median 16.9 ml/cm H2O, range 15.0 to 65.0 vs 25.1, range 17.5 to 50.0, p = 0.95). No difference was found in awareness of bladder emptying, incontinence episodes, bladder emptying method or medication use for neurogenic bladder dysfunction. The only statistically significant change was a decreased incidence of leakage at followup on urodynamics (p = 0.03). Postoperatively decreased genital sensation and erectile dysfunction developed in 1 patient and another experienced a minor cerebrovascular accident with no long-term complications. CONCLUSIONS: In contrast to earlier findings, creation of an artificial somato-autonomic reflex arch in patients with spinal cord injury had no clinically relevant effect on lower urinary tract function.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","Clemmensen, Dorte","Tankisi, Hatice","Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders","Krogh, Klaus","Christensen, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-238419"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-FILA"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-FILA","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the artificial somato autonomic reflex arch does not improve lower urinary tract function in patients with spinal cord lesions","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.juro.2014.08.090","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-238419","identifier":[{"id":"25158270","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84920731239","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-bf25d2fa-13c4-4dc6-9a4f-eb49b44b4fc3"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-82D72F8636A10900F99421AD330F3D41"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.juro.2014.08.090","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine - The Department of Neurosurgery"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"filadelfia danish epilepsy hospital","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-FILA","l3nn":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Filadelfia - Danish Epilepsy Hospital","namevar":["Danish Epilepsy Centre, Dianalund"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-FILA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikkel Mylius","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0a611a7f-8a19-41f3-9221-58fe673b3ef1","name":"Rasmussen, Mikkel Mylius","orcid":"0000-0002-4768-7255","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Yazan F","key":"rawashdehpau","last":"Rawashdeh","locid":"dd97020c-c4f8-4898-8b08-a088d13d45de","name":"Rawashdeh, Yazan F.","name_org":"Rawashdeh, Yazan F","orcid":"0000-0002-5517-2980","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"clemmensenpau","last":"Clemmensen","locid":"826b8629-1e7d-42d6-8e46-7f9a993bf743","name":"Clemmensen, Dorte","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hatice","key":"tankisipau","last":"Tankisi","locid":"2b3f7bfd-71e0-4e1e-9a63-62cf6d26d1ea","name":"Tankisi, Hatice","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"fuglsangfrederiksenpau","last":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen","locid":"9dbd8297-9ebb-41f0-ab0b-8ddfef8c33bd","name":"Fuglsang-Frederiksen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-3926-5287","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Klaus","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"e69f7028-9eb1-4f3a-ab4e-c684c234bf2e","name":"Krogh, Klaus","orcid":"0000-0001-9168-2403","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Peter","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25158270"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.juro.2014.08.090","issn":["00225347","11338245"],"issn_org":["00225347"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of Urology","pages":"598-604","publisher":"Wolters Kluwer Health","status":"p","title":"Journal of Urology","volume":"193"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84920731239"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-bf25d2fa-13c4-4dc6-9a4f-eb49b44b4fc3"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Artificial Somato-Autonomic Reflex Arch Does Not Improve Lower Urinary Tract Function in Patients with Spinal Cord Lesions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-238419","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Introduction: Despite its central role as a reservoir for active tuberculosis disease (TB), latent Mycobacterium tuberculosis (Mtb) infections and the underlying persistence mechanisms are poorly understood. The Mtb genome in latently infected individuals may hold the key to understanding the processes that lead to reactivation and progression to clinical disease. Methods: We studied genomic relationships among 14 isolates of Mtb from historical and recent Danish clinical strain collections, spanning more than three decades, to investigate 6 putative cases of Mtb reactivation, inferred from IS6110 profiles. Single-nucleotide polymorphism (SNPs) patterns were analyzed to identify true cases of TB re-activation, as well as the underlying mutational patterns. Results: Two parallel cases of latent TB reactivation were identified. We found an average mutation rate of 0.2 – 0.3 over 33 years, as well as evidence for distinct processes such as oxidative damage or natural selection having contributed to mutation accumulation. Conclusions: Our study shows that distinct processes can shape Mtb genomes during latent infection. Most importantly, we document substantial molecular evolution of Mtb over three decades, with mutation rates similar to observations from cases of active disease. Our study thus emphasizes the importance of identifying and controlling latent cases.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Lillebaek, Troels","Norman, Anders","Rasmussen, Erik Michael","B. Folkvardsen, Dorte","Marvig, Rasmus","Bengaard Andersen, Åse","Jelsbak, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-373606"],"event":{"end":"2015-11-09","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-11-09","title":"The Danish Microbiological Society Annual Congress 2015","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"substantial molecular evolution in prolonged latent i mycobacterium tuberculosis i infections in humans","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-373606","ids":["dtu-e6f06051-2e33-423a-849c-21e64a6a4e89"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-F761A76B5B60F6D233C6785707E57B75"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Infection Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Troels","key":"lillebaekpau","last":"Lillebaek","name":"Lillebaek, Troels","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"normanpau","last":"Norman","locid":"01abb082-e735-40c1-ae3b-0cfac5bfe1f4","name":"Norman, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-1282-394X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik Michael","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Erik Michael","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorte","key":"bfolkvardsenpau","last":"B. Folkvardsen","name":"B. Folkvardsen, Dorte","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmus","key":"marvigpau","last":"Marvig","name":"Marvig, Rasmus","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Åse","key":"bengaardandersenpau","last":"Bengaard Andersen","name":"Bengaard Andersen, Åse","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars","key":"jelsbakpau","last":"Jelsbak","locid":"0f152051-d6ff-4b86-b98f-2ce118ee9ee1","name":"Jelsbak, Lars","orcid":"0000-0002-5759-9769","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"50-50","place":"Copenhagen","status":"p","subtitle":"Programme &amp; Abstracts","title":"The Danish Microbiological Society Annual Congress 2015"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-e6f06051-2e33-423a-849c-21e64a6a4e89"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Substantial Molecular Evolution In Prolonged Latent <i>Mycobacterium Tuberculosis </i>Infections In Humans","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-373606","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Viden om stenrev (Naturtypen 1170) og deres betydning for gyde- og opvækstområder for fisk er i dag sparsom. Der er ikke tidligere gennemført undersøgelser, der har dokumenteret, hvordan et stenrevs størrelse, struktur og placering spiller ind på dets betydning som gyde- og opvækstområde for fisk. Det er derfor i dag ikke muligt kvantitativt at redegøre for stenrevs betydning for fiskeressourcerne eller udarbejde målrettede natur-genopretningsplaner for stenrev med det formål at genskabe gyde- og opvækstområder for fisk. Det vil Projektet RevFisk forsøge at råde bod på. Centrale spørgsmål i projektet er: Hvilke fiskearter findes på revet? Hvornår er fiskene der? Hvilke fisk er nøglearter på revet? Hvad er faunaudbuddet? Hvad spiser nøglefiskearterne? Hvor stor del af fiskenes føde stammer fra stenrevet? Hvad er rovfiskenes adfærd og opholdstider på stenrev? Er der inter- og intraspecifik konkurrence mellem nøglefiskearterne? Hvor hurtigt vokser fiskene? Hvad er spredningsvejene for fisk til og fra et givent stenrev? Hvordan forvaltes stenrev nationalt og internationalt? Målet med projektet er at opbygge viden om marine stenrevs biologiske funktion for fisk og deres betydning som gyde og opvækstområde. Viden indsamlet i løbet af projektet vil implementeres til at udvikle forvaltningsværktøjer, der dels kan anvendes ved etablering af nye samt reetablerede stenrev og dels til at forvalte eksisterende stenrev. Der vil udvikles modelværktøjer, der kvantificerer stenrevs betydning for fisk som funktion af stenrevets tilstand, størrelse og dybdeplacering. Stenrevs betydning som donor til det omkringliggende område belyses igennem driftsanalyser af spredningsveje. Denne vidensopbygning vil blive brugt til at udvikle guidelines i forhold til design, form og placering ved naturgenopretning af stenrev.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Stenberg, Claus","Christoffersen, Mads","Aarestrup, Kim","van Deurs, Mikael","Støttrup, Josianne","Nielsen, Anders","Andersen, Niels Gerner","Mariani, Patrizio","Baktoft, Henrik","Pedersen, Martin Wæver","Dahl, Karsten","Lundsteen, Steffen","Stæhr, Peter","Rasmussen, Michael Bo","Mohn, Christian","Møhlenberg, Flemming","Hansen, Flemming Thorbjørn","Uhrenholt, Thomas","Middelboe, Anne Lise","Mandviwalla, Xerxes Rohinton"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381090"],"event":{"end":"2015-01-30","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2015-01-28","title":"18. Danske Havforskermøde","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-DHYI"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-DHYI","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"revfisk et projekt som kvantificerer stenrevs et lavtliggende stenrev i den fotiske zone og et dybere liggende stenrev i den afotiske zone betydning for fisk","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-381090","ids":["dtu-ff7e2f3c-35e0-4515-8710-77150074fd27"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5E5E51483959B5B4E50C9D1BFFF2F0E5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources","Technical University of Denmark, National Institute of Aquatic Resources, Section for Ecosystem based Marine Management"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark