{"abstract":"Der stilles i stigende grad krav til socialt arbejde som vidensbaseret profession. Men det er ofte uklart, hvad viden mere præcist betyder i en socialfaglig kontekst. På den ene side efterspørges en evidensbaseret indsats med dokumenteret effekt. På den anden side er de fleste enige om, at evidensbaseret viden kun dækker en mindre del af den samlede viden, der trækkes på i socialt arbejde, og at en mere praksisfunderet og erfaringsbaseret viden spiller en væsentlig rolle. Denne bog er en introduktion til centrale begreber og diskussioner om viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde. Med inddragelse af konkrete og praksisrelevante problemstillinger behandles en række klassiske videnskabsteoretiske sondringer med relevans for socialt arbejde. Derudover behandles spørgsmålet om, hvad der er gyldig og nyttig viden, ud fra videnssociologiske, filosofiske og praksisrettede perspektiver. Hensigten er at tilbyde et begrebsapparat, der kvalificerer studerende og socialarbejdere til at forholde sig til de mange former for viden, de præsenteres for på uddannelserne og i praksis.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Anders Bøggild","Rasmussen, Tove","Olesen, Søren Peter","Jørgensen, Sabine"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-661248"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Videnskabsteori"],"level":"pop","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde","src":["via"],"src-code":["DI-UC-VIA"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-661248","ids":["via-e19b2d1e-f38f-4cbb-a9f5-85d93febd979"],"keyword":["videnskabsteori"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","noi":["Local-1-1-0FBE71F8B32651BE6BCE698CEE17D1C7"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA, Forskning og udvikling, Forsk.center Pædagogik og dannelse","VIA, Uddannelser, Social- og samfundsuddannelserne, Socialrådgiveruddannelsen Aarhus C"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Bøggild","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"15d3eb85-8ffe-4c32-b970-43d444374d12","name":"Christensen, Anders Bøggild","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Tove","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"5b42d1f0-0ade-42de-b87e-72e91f26d0af","name":"Rasmussen, Tove","orcid":"0000-0002-6599-884X","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Peter","key":"olesenpau","last":"Olesen","name":"Olesen, Søren Peter","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sabine","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Sabine","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788741256757"],"pages":"275","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-e19b2d1e-f38f-4cbb-a9f5-85d93febd979"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-661248","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Understanding alterations in HIV-specific immune responses during antiretroviral therapy (ART), such as antibody-dependent cellular cytotoxicity (ADCC), is important in the development of novel strategies to control HIV-1 infection. This study included 53 HIV-1 positive individuals. We evaluated the ability of effector cells and antibodies to mediate ADCC separately and in combination using the ADCC-PanToxiLux assay. The ability of the peripheral blood mononuclear cells (PBMCs) to mediate ADCC was significantly higher in individuals who had been treated with ART before seroconversion, compared to the individuals initiating ART at a low CD4+ T cell count (<350 cells/μl blood) and the ART-naïve individuals. The frequency of CD16 expressing natural killer (NK) cells correlated with both the duration of ART and Granzyme B (GzB) activity. In contrast, the plasma titer of antibodies mediating ADCC declined during ART. These findings suggest improved cytotoxic function of the NK cells if initiating ART early during infection, while the levels of ADCC mediating antibodies declined during ART.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Jensen, Sanne Skov","Fomsgaard, Anders","Borggren, Marie","Tingstedt, Jeanette Linnea","Gerstoft, Jan","Kronborg, Gitte","Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","Pedersen, Court","Karlsson, Ingrid"],"cuid":["S02-086.80-666977"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-SSI"],"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-SSI","DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hiv specific antibody dependent cellular cytotoxicity adcc mediating antibodies decline while nk cell function increases during antiretroviral therapy art","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0145249","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.80-666977","identifier":[{"id":"26696395","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4692281","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84957578087","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e5979fd2-aa1b-4e19-99bd-18f93d80e6ec","sdu-08595bb8-90e9-4945-a474-455b1a5bf39a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FC12CE49E9525B48F125F0E35306EBB8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0145249","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Infectious Diseases (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ssi statens serum institut","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-SSI","l3nn":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SSI Statens Serum Institut","namevar":["Statens Serum Institut"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-SSI","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Sanne","key":"skovjensenpau","last":"Skov Jensen","locid":"663175e0-7a71-44ed-9879-cc84b7877a57","name":"Jensen, Sanne Skov","name_org":"Skov Jensen, Sanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sanne Skov","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, Sanne Skov","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"fomsgaardpau","last":"Fomsgaard","locid":"93452d67-94e6-4877-bb80-1fac3c624f4f","name":"Fomsgaard, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-4304-0603","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie","key":"borggrenpau","last":"Borggren","name":"Borggren, Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette Linnea","key":"tingstedtpau","last":"Tingstedt","name":"Tingstedt, Jeanette Linnea","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Jan","key":"gerstoftpau","last":"Gerstoft","locid":"c7e948db-fe0f-4a67-9b86-7ccc43ae64f5","name":"Gerstoft, Jan","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","first":"Gitte","key":"kronborgpau","last":"Kronborg","locid":"6dfd64b6-b92a-46ff-9008-4c065e9cbddb","name":"Kronborg, Gitte","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line Dahlerup","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"a0349aeb-56d9-4984-86b0-4829aee2a04b","name":"Rasmussen, Line Dahlerup","orcid":"0000-0003-0853-0893","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Court","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"7f2e0dec-1687-4283-ac30-53e73c124437","name":"Pedersen, Court","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ingrid","key":"karlssonpau","last":"Karlsson","name":"Karlsson, Ingrid","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26696395"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1371/journal.pone.0145249","issn":["19326203"],"issue":"12","journal":"PLOS ONE","pages":"1-15","paperid":"e0145249","status":"p","title":"PLOS ONE","title_org":"P L o S One","volume":"10"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84957578087"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Hospitals","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-e5979fd2-aa1b-4e19-99bd-18f93d80e6ec","sdu-08595bb8-90e9-4945-a474-455b1a5bf39a"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"HIV-Specific Antibody-Dependent Cellular Cytotoxicity (ADCC) - Mediating Antibodies Decline while NK Cell Function Increases during Antiretroviral Therapy (ART)","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.80-666977","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Selecting appropriate ways of bringing engineered nanoparticles (ENP) into aqueous dispersion is a main obstacle for testing, and thus for understanding and evaluating, their potential adverse effects to the environment and human health. Using different methods to prepare (stock) dispersions of the same ENP may be a source of variation in the toxicity measured. Harmonization and standardization of dispersion methods applied in mammalian and ecotoxicity testing are needed to ensure a comparable data quality and to minimize test artifacts produced by modifications of ENP during the dispersion preparation process. Such harmonization and standardization will also enhance comparability among tests, labs, and studies on different types of ENP. The scope of this review was to critically discuss the essential parameters in dispersion protocols for ENP. The parameters are identified from individual scientific studies and from consensus reached in larger scale research projects and international organizations. A step-wise approach is proposed to develop tailored dispersion protocols for ecotoxicological and mammalian toxicological testing of ENP. The recommendations of this analysis may serve as a guide to researchers, companies, and regulators when selecting, developing, and evaluating the appropriateness of dispersion methods applied in mammalian and ecotoxicity testing. However, additional experimentation is needed to further document the protocol parameters and investigate to what extent different stock dispersion methods affect ecotoxicological and mammalian toxicological responses of ENP.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hartmann, Nanna B.","Jensen, Keld Alstrup","Baun, Anders","Rasmussen, Kirsten","Rauscher, Hubert","Tantra, Ratna","Cupi, Denisa","Gilliland, Douglas","Pianella, Francesca","Riego Sintes, Juan M."],"cuid":["S02-099.44-768326"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","European Commission Joint Research Centre Institute","National Physical Laboratory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci","soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-U"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-WORK"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"techniques and protocols for dispersing nanoparticle powders in aqueous media is there a rationale for harmonization","src":["dtu","nfa"],"src-code":["DI-GV-WORK","DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127836227/Resubmitted_dispersion_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-099.44-768326","identifier":[{"id":"84949530102","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26397955","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["dtu-8aa40758-e22a-4dd1-a17d-c2e1cdbb4a3d","nfa-fc678677-36a8-4fd9-8fe2-7c4cc714237f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology","Social Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-DCD8C638F37F64034B357B0556899A4E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/127836227/Resubmitted_dispersion_paper.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Environmental Engineering, Environmental Chemistry","Technical University of Denmark, National Food Institute"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"nfa national research centre for the working environment","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-WORK","l3nn":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment","namevar":["The National Research Centre for the Working Environment, Directors, Chemical Working Environment, Toxicology, Nanosafety, and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-WORK","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"be","key":"european commission joint research centre institute","loc":["Belgium","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"European Commission Joint Research Centre Institute","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"national physical laboratory","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"National Physical Laboratory","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nanna B.","key":"hartmannpau","last":"Hartmann","locid":"8dccdf12-c16c-4cd8-a41f-a58c6a0b6dfc","name":"Hartmann, Nanna B.","orcid":"0000-0002-0442-245X","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Keld Alstrup","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b93ba18-9ef8-4419-8d4f-5b7c9634ba2f","name":"Jensen, Keld Alstrup","orcid":"0000-0002-2764-3634","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"baunpau","last":"Baun","locid":"f3cdf4a9-bfc7-4e0e-bf46-df0da8134f0d","name":"Baun, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-1396-408X","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Kirsten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Kirsten","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Hubert","key":"rauscherpau","last":"Rauscher","name":"Rauscher, Hubert","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Ratna","key":"tantrapau","last":"Tantra","name":"Tantra, Ratna","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Denisa","key":"cupipau","last":"Cupi","locid":"be9fb519-4dcb-4e62-bde6-2d93f43d9cef","name":"Cupi, Denisa","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Douglas","key":"gillilandpau","last":"Gilliland","name":"Gilliland, Douglas","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Francesca","key":"pianellapau","last":"Pianella","name":"Pianella, Francesca","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Juan M.","key":"riegosintespau","last":"Riego Sintes","name":"Riego Sintes, Juan M.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26397955"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/10937404.2015.1074969","issn":["01615548","10937404"],"issn_org":["10937404"],"issue":"6","journal":"Journal of Toxicology and Environmental Health - Part B: Critical Reviews","pages":"299-326","publisher":"Taylor & Francis Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Toxicology and Environmental Health - Part B: Critical Reviews","title_org":"Journal of Toxicology and Environmental Health. Part B: Critical Reviews","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84949530102"],"sdg":["3. Good Health and Well-being","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Governmental Institutions","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-8aa40758-e22a-4dd1-a17d-c2e1cdbb4a3d","nfa-fc678677-36a8-4fd9-8fe2-7c4cc714237f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark","NFA National Research Centre for the Working Environment"],"title":"Techniques and Protocols for Dispersing Nanoparticle Powders in Aqueous Media—is there a Rationale for Harmonization?","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.44-768326","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Since the first report of the enhanced permeability and retention (EPR) effect, the research in nanocarrier based antitumor drugs has been intense. The field has been devoted to treatment of cancer by exploiting EPR-based accumulation of nanocarriers in solid tumors, which for many years was considered to be a ubiquitous phenomenon. However, the understanding of differences in the EPR-effect between tumor types, heterogeneities within each patient group, and dependency on tumor development stage in humans is sparse. It is therefore important to enhance our understanding of the EPR-effect in large animals and humans with spontaneously developed cancer. In the present paper, we describe a novel loading method of copper-64 into PEGylated liposomes and use these liposomes to evaluate the EPR-effect in 11 canine cancer patients with spontaneous solid tumors by PET/CT imaging. We thereby provide the first high-resolution analysis of EPR-based tumor accumulation in large animals. We find that the EPR-effect is strong in some tumor types but cannot be considered a general feature of solid malignant tumors since we observed a high degree of accumulation heterogeneity between tumors. Six of seven included carcinomas displayed high uptake levels of liposomes, whereas one of four sarcomas displayed signs of liposome retention. We conclude that nanocarrier-radiotracers could be important in identifying cancer patients that will benefit from nanocarrier-based therapeutics in clinical practice.","author_count":10,"contributors":["Hansen, Anders Elias","Petersen, Anncatrine Luisa","Henriksen, Jonas Rosager","Børresen, Betina","Rasmussen, Palle","Elema, Dennis Ringkjøbing","Rosenschöld, Per Munck af","Kristensen, Annemarie T.","Kjær, Andreas","Andresen, Thomas Lars"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-034419"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cancer","Drug delivery","EPR effect","Imaging","Liposomes","Nanomedicine","Nanoparticles"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"positron emission tomography based elucidation of the enhanced permeability and retention effect in dogs with cancer using copper 000000000064 liposomes","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128524546/Positron_Emission_Tomography.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-034419","identifier":[{"id":"26022907","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84934337555","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-518c22d4-ee71-4ea7-b66c-92bc656ba040","ku-e956cabb-999d-4ed2-8a3e-b77924a791f9"],"keyword":["Cancer","Drug delivery","EPR-effect","Imaging","Liposomes","Nanomedicine","Nanoparticles"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-B11E19AB160FFF6E04D401998876B02F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128524546/Positron_Emission_Tomography.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1021/acsnano.5b01324","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Na