{"abstract":"Precision phase readout of optical beat note signals is one of the core techniques required for inter-satellite laser interferometry. Future space based gravitational wave detectors like eLISA require such a readout over a wide range of MHz frequencies, due to orbit induced Doppler shifts, with a precision in the order of µ rad/root Hz at frequencies between 0.1 mHz and 1 Hz. In this paper, we present phase readout systems, so-called phasemeters, that are able to achieve such precisions and we discuss various means that have been employed to reduce noise in the analogue circuit domain and during digitisation. We also discuss the influence of some non-linear noise sources in the analogue domain of such phasemeters. And finally, we present the performance that was achieved during testing of the elegant breadboard model of the LISA phasemeter, which was developed in the scope of a European Space Agency technology development activity. (C) 2015 AIP Publishing LLC.","author_count":19,"contributors":["Gerberding, Oliver","Diekmann, Christian","Kullmann, Joachim","Troebs, Michael","Bykov, Ioury","Barke, Simon","Brause, Nils Christopher","Delgado, Juan Jose Esteban","Schwarze, Thomas S.","Reiche, Jens","Danzmann, Karsten","Rasmussen, Torben","Hansen, Torben Vendt","Enggaard, Anders","Pedersen, Søren Møller","Jennrich, Oliver","Suess, Martin","Sodnik, Zoran","Heinzel, Gerhard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-331889"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany","Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","ESTEC","Leibniz University Hannover"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"readout for intersatellite laser interferometry measuring low frequency phase fluctuations of high frequency signals with microradian precision","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84937787192","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-331889","identifier":[{"id":"26233398","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84937787192","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5beae1e0-c2e4-4084-b399-12ac7c8dad3d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-15B2C17E2EC2B268EFF33983E6F7268C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"de","key":"leibniz university hannover","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Leibniz University Hannover","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Axcon ApS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Mechanical Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"nl","key":"estec","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"ESTEC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Oliver","key":"gerberdingpau","last":"Gerberding","name":"Gerberding, Oliver","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christian","key":"diekmannpau","last":"Diekmann","name":"Diekmann, Christian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joachim","key":