{"abstract":"The transition dynamics from the low (L) to the high (H) confinement mode in magnetically confined plasmas is investigated using a first-principles four-field fluid model. Numerical results are in agreement with measurements from the Experimental Advanced Superconducting Tokamak - EAST. Particularly, the slow transition with an intermediate dithering phase is well reproduced at proper parameters. The model recovers the power threshold for the L-H transition as well as the decrease in power threshold switching from single to double null configuration observed experimentally. The results are highly relevant for developing predictive models of the transition, essential for understanding and optimizing future fusion power reactors.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders Henry","Xu, G. S.","Madsen, Jens","Naulin, Volker","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Wan, B. N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-334626"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"keyword":["Braginskii equations","Fluid simulations","L H transition","Turbulence and flows"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"simulation of transition dynamics to high confinement in fusion plasmas","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/129906625/physLetA2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-334626","identifier":[{"id":"84946121241","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-64cb7013-ba5f-4078-851c-9c922e4a3cc3"],"keyword":["Braginskii equations","Fluid simulations","L-H transition","Turbulence and flows"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E973C638968E737ECDBBE88523F890BA"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"Ikke-specificeret","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/129906625/physLetA2.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G. S.","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, G. S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B. N.","key":"wanpau","last":"Wan","name":"Wan, B. N.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.physleta.2015.10.004","issn":["03759601","18732429"],"issn_org":["03759601"],"issue":"47-48","journal":"Physics Letters A","pages":"3097-3101","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Physics Letters A","volume":"379"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84946121241"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-64cb7013-ba5f-4078-851c-9c922e4a3cc3"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Simulation of transition dynamics to high confinement in fusion plasmas","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-334626","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"An equation governing potential vorticity in a magnetized plasmas is derived. The equation is analogous to Ertel's theorem. In the long wave-length limit the potential vorticity equals the ratio of the gyro-frequency plus the E × B- and diamagnetic polarization densities to the particle density. The equation is relevant for transport barriers in magnetically confined plasmas because particle density, ion temperature and the radial electric field are mutually coupled through the potential vorticity. The potential vorticity equation is derived from an energy conserving, four-field, electrostatic, full-F gyrofluid model. It is shown that the gyrofluid model possesses two exact Lagrangian invariants. In systems where mixing uniformly distribute the Lagrangian invariants we derive the corresponding turbulent equipartion states. It is shown that the system is driven towards constant potential vorticity. Given particle density and magnetic field profiles we infer ion temperature and electric potential profiles from the derived turbulent equipartion states.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Madsen, Jens","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Treue, Frederik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349643"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Electric fields","Electric potential","Gyrofluid","Lagrange multipliers","Potential vorticity","Tokamak devices","Transport barrier","Vorticity","Zonal flows"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gyrofluid potential vorticity equation and turbulent equipartion states paper","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/129906471/TEP.pdf","version":"A