ensen, Sabine","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Bøggild","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Anders Bøggild","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tove","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Tove","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788741256757"],"place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p","title":"Viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde","volume":"1"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["via-bdf29aba-2398-43a0-94f9-e0c1b05e30d1"],"src":["VIA University College"],"title":"Evidensprogrammer og praksisforskning","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-660277","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Supplemental oxygen therapy is used for intensive care (ICU) patients with severe sepsis, but with no general guidelines and few safety data. The aim of this observational study was to describe the variability in oxygen administration as well as the association between partial pressure of arterial oxygen (PaO2 ) and mortality. METHODS: We extracted data from two Scandinavian clinical trials of ICU patients with severe sepsis or septic shock. We calculated average PaO2 and fraction of inspired oxygen (FiO2 ) from trial inclusion and the following 5 days, and assessed the association between PaO2 and 90-day mortality. RESULTS: The median PaO2 was 9.8 kPa [5-95% range 6.4-19.9] and FiO2 was 0.51 [5-95% range 0.27-1.00], respectively. Eight hundred and five of 1,770 patients (45%) died. The relative risk of mortality was 1.43 [95% CI: 1.19-1.65] in patients with average PaO2 < 8 kPa and 1.29 [95% CI: 0.84-1.68] in patients with average PaO2 ≥ 16 kPa, as compared to patients with average PaO2 10-12 kPa. The relative risk of mortality was 1.38 [95% CI: 1.17-1.58] in patients with an average FiO2 0.60-0.80 and 2.10 [95% CI: 1.88-2.23] in patients with an average FiO2 ≥ 0.80 as compared to patients with an average FiO2 ≤ 0.40. CONCLUSION: Administration of oxygen in patients with severe sepsis resulted in a wide range of PaO2 . Significantly higher mortality was observed in patients with an average PaO2 < 8 kPa and FiO2 ≥ 0.60. The results do not imply causation and the associations between average PaO2 and adverse outcomes have to be assessed further.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Dahl, R. M.","Grønlykke, L.","Haase, N.","Holst, L. B.","Perner, Anders","Wetterslev, Jørn","Rasmussen, B. S.","Meyhoff, Christian S."],"cuid":["S02-085.94-003716"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["6S-Trial and TRISS Trial investigators"],"keyword":["Aged","Blood Gas Analysis","Critical care","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Partial Pressure","Scandinavian and Nordic Countries","Sepsis","Shock Septic"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"variability in targeted arterial oxygenation levels in patients with severe sepsis or septic shock","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S02-085.94-003716","identifier":[{"id":"84937024228","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000357969800005","type":"wos"},{"id":"25914095","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-4c04fe61-5a2b-4777-9570-99bb3f46adea","ku-eba4453c-f0ad-4ad5-b0d2-71d20980d8cb"],"keyword":["Aged","Blood Gas Analysis","Critical Care","Female","Humans","Male","Middle Aged","Oxygen","Oxygen Inhalation Therapy","Partial Pressure","Scandinavian and Nordic Countries","Sepsis","Shock, Septic"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-FD5CE8A8CDBE17EA1B7908DC4CE69A34"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine",