{"abstract":"The bacteria Yersinia pestis is the etiological agent of plague and has caused human pandemics with millions of deaths in historic times. How and when it originated remains contentious. Here, we report the oldest direct evidence of Yersinia pestis identified by ancient DNA in human teeth from Asia and Europe dating from 2,800 to 5,000 years ago. By sequencing the genomes, we find that these ancient plague strains are basal to all known Yersinia pestis. We find the origins of the Yersinia pestis lineage to be at least two times older than previous estimates. We also identify a temporal sequence of genetic changes that lead to increased virulence and the emergence of the bubonic plague. Our results show that plague infection was endemic in the human populations of Eurasia at least 3,000 years before any historical recordings of pandemics.","author_count":32,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Simon","Allentoft, Morten Erik","Nielsen, Kasper","Orlando, Ludovic","Sikora, Martin","Sjögren, Karl-Göran","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Schubert, Mikkel","Van Dam, Alex","Kapel, Christian Moliin Outzen","Nielsen, Henrik Bjørn","Brunak, Søren","Avetisyan, Pavel","Epimakhov, Andrey","Khalyapin, Mikhail Viktorovich","Gnuni, Artak","Kriiska, Aivar","Lasak, Irena","Metspalu, Mait","Moiseyev, Vyacheslav","Gromov, Andrei","Pokutta, Dalia","Saag, Lehti","Varul, Liivi","Yepiskoposyan, Levon","Sicheritz-Pontén, Thomas","Foley, Robert A","Lahr, Marta Mirazón","Nielsen, Rasmus","Kristiansen, Kristian","Willerslev, Eske"],"cuid":["S02-099.18-038078"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Asia, Central","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Armenia","Estonia","Poland","Russia","Sweden","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","National Academy of Sciences of the Republic of Armenia","Orenburg Museum of Fine Arts","Peter the Great Museum of Anthropology and Ethnography","South Ural State University","University of California at San Diego","University of Cambridge","University of Gothenburg","University of Tartu","University of Wrocław","Yerevan State University"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Technical University"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"early divergent strains of i yersinia pestis i in eurasia 000000000005 000000000000 years ago","src":["dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.10.009","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-099.18-038078","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4644222","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"26496604","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84975744563","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-f73471e1-2d39-4025-967c-d9030d86eedc","ku-d0db0bca-bb22-49c3-ad16-5559ab73ea15"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-A7079B076306BC7E80B97A7EB1DACFC8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/118025845/Early_Divergent_Strains_of_Yersinia_pestis_in_Eurasia_5_000_Years_Ago.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.10.009","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/161216502/S0092867415013227.htm","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Techni