,{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Jørgen","key":"elmlarsenpau","last":"Elm Larsen","name":"Elm Larsen, Jørgen","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Maja","key":"lundemarkpau","last":"Lundemark","name":"Lundemark, Maja","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Louise","key":"harkespau","last":"Harkes","locid":"dd9d13d7-bcba-49eb-b2cd-fd3d8ef8c005","name":"Harkes, Louise","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"bengtssonpau","last":"Bengtsson","name":"Bengtsson, Steen","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Tanja Dall","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"b3b74de7-4051-435b-9ff9-243f85184b50","name":"Dall, Tanja","name_org":"Jensen, Tanja Dall","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Tina","key":"bømlerpau","last":"Bømler","name":"Bømler, Tina","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788741260518"],"pages":"317","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Governmental Institutions","KP","UCL University College","Universities","University Colleges","University of Copenhagen","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-0521bbc6-4cf2-4e87-b324-71a299d77502","ucl-0521bbc6-4cf2-4e87-b324-71a299d77502","via-0521bbc6-4cf2-4e87-b324-71a299d77502"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen","UCL University College","VIA University College"],"title":"Sociale problemer","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-100.00-038440","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Importance: The CHA2DS2-VASc score (congestive heart failure, hypertension, age ≥75 years [doubled], diabetes, stroke/transient ischemic attack/thromboembolism [doubled], vascular disease [prior myocardial infarction, peripheral artery disease, or aortic plaque], age 65-75 years, sex category [female]) is used clinically for stroke risk stratification in atrial fibrillation (AF). Its usefulness in a population of patients with heart failure (HF) is unclear. Objective: To investigate whether CHA2DS2-VASc predicts ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death in a cohort of patients with HF with and without AF. Design, Setting, and Population: Nationwide prospective cohort study using Danish registries, including 42 987 patients (21.9% with concomitant AF) not receiving anticoagulation who were diagnosed as having incident HF during 2000-2012. End of follow-up was December 31, 2012. Exposures: Levels of the CHA2DS2-VASc score (based on 10 possible points, with higher scores indicating higher risk), stratified by concomitant AF at baseline. Analyses took into account the competing risk of death. Main Outcomes and Measures: Ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death within 1 year after HF diagnosis. Results: In patients without AF, the risks of ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death were 3.1% (n = 977), 9.9% (n = 3187), and 21.8% (n = 6956), respectively; risks were greater with increasing CHA2DS2-VASc scores as follows, for scores of 1 through 6, respectively: (1) ischemic stroke with concomitant AF: 4.5%, 3.7%, 3.2%, 4.3%, 5.6%, and 8.4%; without concomitant AF: 1.5%, 1.5%, 2.0%, 3.0%, 3.7%, and 7% and (2) all-cause death with concomitant AF: 19.8%, 19.5%, 26.1%, 35.1%, 37.7%, and 45.5%; without concomitant AF: 7.6%, 8.3%, 17.8%, 25.6%, 27.9%, and 35.0%. At high CHA2DS2-VASc scores (≥4), the absolute risk of thromboembolism was high regardless of presence of AF (for a score of 4, 9.7% vs 8.2% for patients without and with concomitant AF, respectively; overall P<.001 for interaction). C statistics and negative predictive values indicate that the CHA2DS2-VASc score performed modestly in this HF population with and without AF (for ischemic stroke, 1-year C statistics, 0.67 [95% CI, 0.65-0.68] and 0.64 [95% CI, 0.61-0.67], respectively; 1-year negative predictive values, 92% [95% CI, 91%-93%] and 91% [95% CI, 88%-95%], respectively). Conclusions and Relevance: Among patients with incident HF with or without AF, the CHA2DS2-VASc score was associated with risk of ischemic stroke, thromboembolism, and death. The absolute risk of thromboembolic complications was higher among patients without AF compared with patients with concomitant AF at high CHA2DS2-VASc scores. However, predictive accuracy was modest, and the clinical utility of the CHA2DS2-VASc score in patients with HF remains to be determined.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Lane, Deidre A","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-054337"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"assessment of the cha000000000002ds000000000002 vasc score in predicting ischemic stroke thromboembolism and death in patients with heart failure with and without atrial fibrillation","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-054337","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000360840700015","type":"wos"},{"id":"26318604","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84941625442","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-0eb4a28a-09ba-45a2-a38a-03f69de3bc9f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-725B979272E032E64624906562442DDF"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Deidre A","key":"lanepau","last":"Lane","name":"Lane, Deidre A","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26318604"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1001/jama.2015.10725","issn":["00987484","01851160"],"issn_org":["00987484"],"issue":"10","journal":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","pages":"1030-1038","publisher":"American Medical Association","status":"p","title":"JAMA  The Journal of the American Medical Association","title_org":"JAMA: The Journal of the American Medical Association","volume":"314"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84941625442"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-0eb4a28a-09ba-45a2-a38a-03f69de3bc9f"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Assessment of the CHA2DS2-VASc Score in Predicting Ischemic Stroke, Thromboembolism, and Death in Patients With Heart Failure With and Without Atrial Fibrillation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-054337","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Stroke in patients with heart failure is associated with poor outcomes. Risk stratification schemes may improve clinical decision making in this patient population. This study investigated whether female sex is a risk factor for stroke in patients with heart failure in sinus rhythm. METHODS: This is a population-based cohort study of patients diagnosed with heart failure during 2000 to 2012, identified by record linkage between nationwide Danish registries. Our primary outcome was stroke, and secondary outcome was thromboembolic event. We used relative risks (RRs) after 1 and 5 years to compare males with females within each of the following age groups: 50 to 59 years, 60 to 69 years, 70 to 79 years, 80 to 89 years, and 90+ years. Analyses took into account the competing risks of death. RESULTS: During the study period, 84,142 patients were diagnosed with heart failure, of which 39,946 (47.5%) were females. At 5-year follow-up, female sex was associated with a lower risk of stroke compared with males (adjusted overall hazard ratio 0.91, 95% CI 0.85-0.96). The observed lower risks of stroke in females were not present in the older age groups, where the competing risk of death was substantial among males in particular. When considering a more broadly defined thromboembolic end point, a decreased risk among females persisted across nearly all age groups after 5-year follow-up (adjusted overall hazard ratio 0.93, 95% CI 0.91-0.96). CONCLUSIONS: We found an association between female sex and decreased stroke risk in patients with heart failure, which persisted after adjustment for concomitant cardiovascular risk factors. The association was attenuated with increasing age, possibly because of competing risks of death.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Melgaard, Line","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Lip, Gregory Y H","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-068402"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"female sex is associated with a lower risk of stroke in patients with heart failure","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-068402","identifier":[{"id":"25728730","type":"pmid"},{"id":"WOS:000351486800012","type":"wos"},{"id":"84926171158","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-3f6af908-d10f-45d0-a433-d09070313d92"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D6B106954439431E743388327C8206E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"city hospital in birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City Hospital in Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Line","key":"melgaardpau","last":"Melgaard","locid":"88687b9c-5b56-4584-a89a-89fdeca4fd54","name":"Melgaard, Line","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2 3","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","locid":"8fa30e84-7381-41b4-8037-afc032238a3d","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25728730"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.ahj.2014.12.004","issn":["00028703","10976744"],"issn_org":["00028703"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Heart Journal","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"American Heart Journal","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926171158"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-3f6af908-d10f-45d0-a433-d09070313d92"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Female sex is associated with a lower risk of stroke in patients with heart failure","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-068402","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Christensen, Anders Bøggild","Jørgensen, Sabine","Olesen, Søren Peter","Tove, Rasmussen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-076922"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-UC"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-VIA"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-UC-VIA"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde en introduktion til centrale temaer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://ibog3.gyldendal.dk/videnogvidenskabsteoriisocialtarbejde#/double/1/","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-076922","ids":["aau-5c8c7b01-07e5-476d-9ca8-976a5492bb33"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8B9CF586D3514FAEF0CE4A207DBFCCBD"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Social Sciences, Department of Political Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"via university college","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-VIA","l3nl":"VIA University College","l3nn":"VIA University College","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIA University College","namevar":["VIA University College"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-VIA","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Bøggild","key":"christensenped","last":"Christensen","locid":"693476d0-17af-4458-a334-38f924541ecb","name":"Christensen, Anders Bøggild","rank":1,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Sabine","key":"jørgensenped","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"b3e3e455-8401-4119-b886-2fbf82d48706","name":"Jørgensen, Sabine","orcid":"0000-0002-8754-5163","rank":2,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Peter","key":"olesenped","last":"Olesen","locid":"a3ded050-4b18-49b5-8a7e-11e14b5d57c6","name":"Olesen, Søren Peter","rank":3,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Rasmussen","key":"toveped","last":"Tove","name":"Tove, Rasmussen","rank":4,"role":"Editor","rolecode":"ped"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788741256757"],"pages":"275","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzels Forlag","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","Universities","University Colleges","VIA University College"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-5c8c7b01-07e5-476d-9ca8-976a5492bb33"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Viden og videnskabsteori i socialt arbejde : En introduktion til centrale temaer","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-076922","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"We aimed to determine whether not using a tourniquet in cemented TKA would affect migration of the tibial component measured by radiosterometric analysis (RSA). Seventy patients were randomized into a tourniquet group and a non-tourniquet group and using model-based RSA, the migration of the tibial component was analyzed. Primary and secondary outcome measures were maximum total point motion (MTPM) and translations and rotations. Follow-up period was 2years. The tibial component was well fixated in both groups and no significant difference in migration between the two groups was detected (P=0.632). Mean MTPM (SD) was 0.47mm (0.16) in the tourniquet group and 0.45mm (0.21) in the non-tourniquet group. Absence of tourniquet indicates that stable fixation of the tibial component can be achieved in cemented TKA.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Ejaz, Ashir","Laursen, Anders Christian","Jakobsen, Thomas","Rasmussen, Sten","Nielsen, Poul Torben","Laursen, Mogens Berg"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-118979"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"absence of a tourniquet does not affect fixation of cemented tka a randomized rsa study of 000000000070 patients","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-118979","identifier":[{"id":"26162514","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84952876987","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000366161300016","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-ed21f7aa-3635-4268-8f2a-9d225242aace"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7755172FB6F50B65640A63ACB9F1525E"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","