6a09a15"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"In the Absence of the Gift : New Forms of Value and Personhood in a Papua New Guinea Community","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-273339","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Climate change is likely to decrease crop yields worldwide. Developing climate resilient cultivars is one way to combat this production scarcity, however, little is known of crop response to future climate conditions and in particular the variability within crops.In Scandinavia, barley is widely cultivated, but yields have stagnated since the start of this century. In this study we cultivated 138 spring barley accessions in a climate phytotron under four treatments mimicking forecasted levels of temperature, carbon dioxide concentration ([CO2]) and ozone ([O3]) at the end of the 21st century1. The ambient control had 19/12°C (day/night) and [CO2] at 385ppm. Three single-factor treatments had elevated temperature +5°C day/night, [CO2] at 700ppm or [O3] at 120 ppb, and in a two-factor treatment the combination of elevated temperature and [CO2] was applied.Treatment effects were assessed on grain yield, grain protein concentration, grain protein harvested, number of grains, number of ears, aboveground vegetative biomass and harvest index. In addition, stability of the production was calculated over the applied treatments for the assessed parameters.In the climate scenario of elevated temperature and [CO2] the grain yield of barley decreased 29% and harvested grain protein declined 22%. Vast variation was identified among the individual barley accessions, which should be exploited by plant breeders in the development of climate resilient cultivars.A genome-wide association study (GWAS) of recorded phenotypes and 3967 SNP-markers identified 60 marker-trait associations (-logp>2.95)2. Markers were found associated with grain yield under all three single factor treatments temperature, [CO2] and [O3], as well as with stability over treatments.To our knowledge, this is the first study that evaluates numerous barley accessions under future climate conditions and identifies candidate markers for abiotic stress tolerance - markers that could be used in the development of cultivars to secure future primary production.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Ingvordsen, Cathrine Heinz","Backes, G.","Lyngkjær, M. F.","Peltonen-Sainio, P.","Jensen, J. D.","Jalli, M.","Jahoor, A.","Rasmussen, M.","Mikkelsen, Teis Nørgaard","Stockmarr, Anders","Jørgensen, R. B."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-316640"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Finland","Germany","Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","MTT Agrifood Research","Nordic Genetic Resource Center","University of Kassel"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gwas of barley phenotypes established under future climate conditions of elevated temperature co000000000002 o000000000003 and elevated temperature and co000000000002 combined","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.proenv.2015.07.241","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-316640","ids":["dtu-2893d57d-555f-4ca0-b47e-fc3f21bfef84"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-4EF695593EEDF2BA2054B860B9DC4AED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.proenv.2015.07.241","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/119239180/filestore.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, Ecosystems Programme"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"university of kassel","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Kassel","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"fi","key":"mtt agrifood research","loc":["Finland","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"MTT Agrifood Research","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"other companies","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-OTH","l3nl":"Other Companies","l3nn":"Other Companies","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Other Companies","namevar":["Nordic Seed A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-OTH","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"se","key":"nordic genetic resource center","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Nordic Genetic Resource Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Cathrine Heinz","key":"ingvordsenpau","last":"Ingvordsen","locid":"8f53ec3c-a7b0-4195-aa56-79d4a7acf890","name":"Ingvordsen, Cathrine Heinz","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G.","key":"backespau","last":"Backes","name":"Backes, G.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"M. F.","key":"lyngkjærpau","last":"Lyngkjær","name":"Lyngkjær, M. F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"peltonensainiopau","last":"Peltonen-Sainio","name":"Peltonen-Sainio, P.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"J. D.","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","name":"Jensen, J. D.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"jallipau","last":"Jalli","name":"Jalli, M.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"jahoorpau","last":"Jahoor","name":"Jahoor, A.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"M.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, M.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Teis Nørgaard","key":"mikkelsenpau","last":"Mikkelsen","locid":"f64f4970-f39b-4fec-aee3-60475a33914e","name":"Mikkelsen, Teis Nørgaard","orcid":"0000-0001-7470-6522","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"stockmarrpau","last":"Stockmarr","locid":"f8ce8f15-f38a-4f99-a8c6-08b0cd7b0f6a","name":"Stockmarr, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8681-2370","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R. B.","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, R. B.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.proenv.2015.07.241","issn":["18780296"],"journal":"Procedia Environmental Sciences","pages":"164-165","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Procedia Environmental Sciences","volume":"29"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","sdg":["13. Climate Action","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Other Companies","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","nordic seed a/s"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-2893d57d-555f-4ca0-b47e-fc3f21bfef84"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"GWAS of Barley Phenotypes Established Under Future Climate Conditions of Elevated Temperature, CO2, O3 and Elevated Temperature and CO2 Combined","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-316640","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"An overview of the plasma dynamics in the Scrape-off-Layer (SOL) of magnetically confined plasma is presented. The SOL is the exhaust channel of the warm plasma from the core, and the understanding of the SOL plasma dynamics is one of the key issues in contemporary fusion research. It is essential for operation of fusion experiments and ultimately fusion power plants. Recent results clearly demonstrate that the plasma transport through the SOL is dominated by turbulent intermittent fluctuations organized into filamentary structures convecting particles, energy, and momentum through the SOL region. Thus, the transport cannot be described and parametrized by simple diffusive type models. The transport leads to strong localized power loads on the first wall and the plasma facing components, which have serious lasting influence.","author_count":15,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Madsen, Jens","Tophøj, Laust Emil Hjerrild","Christensen, A.S.","Magnussen, Michael Løiten","Garcia, O.E.","Schrittwieser, R.","Ionita, C.","Costea, S.","Schneider, B.S.","Vianello, N.","Yan, N.","Xu, G.S."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-351472"],"event":{"end":"2015-07-31","place":"Iasi, ro","start":"2015-07-26","title":"35th International conference on Phenomena in Ionized gases","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Austria","China","Norway","Switzerland"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","University of Innsbruck","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"plasma transport in the scrape off layer of magnetically confined plasma and the plasma exhaust","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128049086/J_J_Rasmussen_Topical_Review.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-351472","ids":["dtu-9d4ec184-5be4-4395-b2d6-5030ef3b2a8a"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-242CC2237DB03F083FD6263F90863468"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/128049086/J_J_Rasmussen_Topical_Review.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"no","key":"university of tromsø the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ch","key":"swiss federal institute of technology lausanne","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swiss Federal Institute of Technology Lausanne","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Juul","key":"rasmussenpa2","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-