{"abstract":"Unprecedented insight into the carbonylation of dimethyl ether over Mordenite is provided through the identification of ketene (CH2CO) as a reaction intermediate. The formation of ketene is predicted by detailed DFT calculations and verified experimentally by the observation of doubly deuterated acetic acid (CH2DCOOD), when D2O is introduced in the feed during the carbonylation reaction.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Dominik Bjørn","Christensen, Jakob Munkholt","Temel, Burcin","Studt, Felix","Moses, Poul Georg","Rossmeisl, Jan","Riisager, Anders","Jensen, Anker Degn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-359853"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","SUNCAT Center for Interface Science and Catalysis"],"keyword":["Carbonylation","Density functional calculations","Heterogeneous catalysis","Reaction mechanisms","Zeolites"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-HLT"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-HLT","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ketene as a reaction intermediate in the carbonylation of dimethyl ether to methyl acetate over mordenite","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85027929297","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-359853","identifier":[{"id":"25967363","type":"pmid"},{"id":"85027929297","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-b8e3a3a6-a4e0-43bc-b7e4-76b2ab4fc80b"],"keyword":["Carbonylation","Density functional calculations","Heterogeneous catalysis","Reaction mechanisms","Zeolites"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0122F8895FB0A7BCE1945C62D3788E24"],"o