{"abstract":"The paper outlines the analysis of speech genres synchronically and diachronically and exemplifies how speech genres are emulated and transformed in an analysis of a piece of literary fiction by the Danish author Katrine Marie Guldager","author_count":4,"contributors":["Gregersen, Frans"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-452953"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Corpus linguistics","Faculty of Humanities","Genre analysis","Speech genres"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genre and everyday conversation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/140536975/3._Genre_and_Everyday_Conversation.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-452953","ids":["ku-637dd062-4c5a-4706-b389-0959d4419ccb"],"keyword":["Corpus linguistics","Faculty of Humanities","Genre analysis","Linguistic and literary genres","Speech genres"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-53F0D48403A785FA4F87E84C2C4D5321"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/140536975/3._Genre_and_Everyday_Conversation.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Nordic Studies and Linguistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Frans","key":"gregersenpau","last":"Gregersen","locid":"b77e4f24-1caa-446e-819b-8760f2f58623","name":"Gregersen, Frans","orcid":"0000-0002-5175-3673","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sune","key":"aukenpedh","last":"Auken","name":"Auken, Sune","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Palle","key":"schantzlauridsenpedh","last":"Schantz Lauridsen","name":"Schantz Lauridsen, Palle","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"juhlrasmussenpedh","last":"Juhl Rasmussen","name":"Juhl Rasmussen, Anders","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9788799589951"],"pages":"56-98","place":"København","publisher":"Ekbatana","series":"Copenhagen Studies in Genre","status":"p","title":"Genre and ..."},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-637dd062-4c5a-4706-b389-0959d4419ccb"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Genre and Everyday Conversation","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-452953","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Formal thought disorder is a major feature of schizophrenia and other psychotic disorders. It is heritable, found in healthy relatives of patients with schizophrenia and other mental disorders but knowledge of specific genetic factors is lacking. The aim of this study was to search for biologically relevant high-risk variants. Formal thought disorder was assessed in participants in the Copenhagen Schizophrenia Linkage Study (N=236), a unique high-risk family study comprised of six large pedigrees. Microsatellite linkage analysis of formal thought disorder was performed and subsequent haplotype analysis of the implicated region using phased microsatellite and SNP genotypes. Whole genome sequencing (N=3) was used in the attempt to identify causative variants in the linkage region. Linkage analysis of formal thought disorder resulted in a single peak at chromosome 6(q26-q27) centred on marker D6S1277, with a maximum LOD score of 4.0. Phasing and fine mapping of the linkage peak identified a 5.5Mb haplotype (chr6:162242322-167753547, hg18) in 31 individuals, all belonging to the same pedigree sharing the haplotype from a common ancestor. The haplotype segregated with increased total thought disorder index score (P=4.9 × 10(-5)) and qualitatively severe forms of thought disturbances. Whole genome sequencing identified a novel nucleotide deletion (chr6:164377205 AG>A, hg18) predicted to disrupt the potential binding of the transcription factor MEF2A. The MEF2A binding site is located between two genes previously reported to associate with schizophrenia, QKI (HGNC:21100) and PDE10A (HGNC:8772). The findings are consistent with MEF2A deregulation conferring risk of formal thought disorder.","author_count":12,"contributors":["Thygesen, Johan Hilge","Zambach, Sine Katharina","Ingason, Andrés","Lundin, Pär","Hansen, Thomas","Bertalan, Marcelo","Rosengren, Anders","Bjerre, Ditte","Ferrero-Miliani, Laura","Rasmussen, Henrik Berg","Parnas, Josef","Werge, Thomas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-453668"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"linkage and whole genome sequencing identify a locus on 000000000006q000000000025 000000000026 for formal thought disorder and implicate mef000000000002a regulation","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-453668","identifier":[{"id":"84951831180","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26421691","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-64cb6f9c-f1d8-4457-8fe2-e33c14bcdb0c"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4B4D8C653E26EB72BE9D811AF6BD6C04"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Immunology and Microbiology, Department of Immunology and Microbiology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Johan Hilge","key":"thygesenpau","last":"Thygesen","name":"Thygesen, Johan Hilge","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sine Katharina","key":"zambachpau","last":"Zambach","name":"Zambach, Sine Katharina","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrés","key":"ingasonpau","last":"Ingason","name":"Ingason, Andrés","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pär","key":"lundinpau","last":"Lundin","name":"Lundin, Pär","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomas","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Thomas","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Marcelo","key":"bertalanpau","last":"Bertalan","name":"Bertalan, Marcelo","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"rosengrenpau","last":"Rosengren","name":"Rosengren, Anders","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ditte","key":"bjerrepau","last":"Bjerre","name":"Bjerre, Ditte","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Laura","key":"ferreromilianipau","last":"Ferrero-Miliani","name":"Ferrero-Miliani, Laura","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Henrik Berg","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0277448f-93be-4c07-9f68-bb5de39ab3cf","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik Berg","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Josef","key":"parnaspau","last":"Parnas","locid":"ac1b6de7-1c1a-4a77-8bd1-4f3eff5bd82c","name":"Parnas, Josef","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Thomas","key":"wergepau","last":"Werge","locid":"905c01bb-6319-4ce6-a38e-ceb5bf73d2f6","name":"Werge, Thomas","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26421691"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.schres.2015.08.037","issn":["09209964","15732509"],"issn_org":["09209964"],"issue":"1-3","journal":"Schizophrenia Research","pages":"441-6","status":"p","title":"Schizophrenia Research","volume":"169"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84951831180"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-64cb6f9c-f1d8-4457-8fe2-e33c14bcdb0c"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Linkage and whole genome sequencing identify a locus on 6q25-26 for formal thought disorder and implicate MEF2A regulation","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-453668","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Hanne Nina","Ræbild, Anders","Nielsen, Christian Nørgaard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-468898"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"edu","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT"],"level3":{"OT":["SkovByKon"]},"level3all":[]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tree biology and arboriculture","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dln","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-468898","ids":["ku-7dfc615e-0280-440b-a809-dcdc04bfb223"],"lang":"English","level":"Educational","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A0FB55A78B6F5DA6CB2F1AEC77DA84B1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["SkovByKon"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Hanne Nina","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3d9a5aa1-c232-468d-9b54-e24669fe718d","name":"Rasmussen, Hanne Nina","orcid":"0000-0002-0181-9304","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders","key":"ræbildpau","last":"Ræbild","locid":"599ea842-1926-48bd-b897-1bc32e9b4912","name":"Ræbild, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-8793-5663","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Christian Nørgaard","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","name":"Nielsen, Christian Nørgaard","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"edition":"6","pages":"216","place":"Frederiksberg","publisher":"Academic Books","status":"p"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-7dfc615e-0280-440b-a809-dcdc04bfb223"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Tree Biology and Arboriculture","type":"Lecture Notes","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-468898","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Application of the principles of total mesorectal excision to colon cancer by undertaking complete mesocolic excision (CME) has been proposed to improve oncological outcomes. We aimed to investigate whether implementation of CME improved disease-free survival compared with conventional colon resection. METHODS: Data for all patients who underwent elective resection for Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) stage I-III colon adenocarcinomas in the Capital Region of Denmark between June 1, 2008, and Dec 31, 2011, were retrieved for this population-based study. The CME group consisted of patients who underwent CME surgery in a centre validated to perform such surgery; the control group consisted of patients undergoing conventional colon resection in three other hospitals. Data were collected from the Danish Colorectal Cancer Group (DCCG) database and medical charts. Patients were excluded if they had stage IV disease, metachronous colorectal cancer, rectal cancer (≤ 15 cm from anal verge) in the absence of synchronous colon adenocarcinoma, tumour of the appendix, or R2 resections. Survival data were collected on Nov 13, 2014, from the DCCG database, which is continuously updated by the National Central Office of Civil Registration. FINDINGS: The CME group consisted of 364 patients and the non-CME group consisted of 1031 patients. For all patients, 4-year disease-free survival was 85.8% (95% CI 81.4-90.1) after CME and 75.9% (72.2-79.7) after non-CME surgery (log-rank p=0.0010). 4-year disease-free survival for patients with UICC stage I disease in the CME group was 100% compared with 89.8% (83.1-96.6) in the non-CME group (log-rank p=0.046). For patients with UICC stage II disease, 4-year disease-free survival was 91.9% (95% CI 87.2-96.6) in the CME group compared with 77.9% (71.6-84.1) in the non-CME group (log-rank p=0.0033), and for patients with UICC stage III disease, it was 73.5% (63.6-83.5) in the CME group compared with 67.5% (61.8-73.2) in the non-CME group (log-rank p=0.13). Multivariable Cox regression showed that CME surgery was a significant, independent predictive factor for higher disease-free survival for all patients (hazard ratio 0.59, 95% CI 0.42-0.83), and also for patients with UICC stage II (0.44, 0.23-0.86) and stage III disease (0.64, 0.42-1.00). After propensity score matching, disease-free survival was significantly higher after CME, irrespective of UICC stage, with 4-year disease-free survival of 85.8% (95% CI 81.4-90.1) after CME and 73.4% (66.2-80.6) after non-CME (log-rank p=0·0014). INTERPRETATION: Our data indicate that CME surgery is associated with better disease-free survival than is conventional colon cancer resection for patients with stage I-III colon adenocarcinoma. Implementation of CME surgery might improve outcomes for patients with colon cancer. FUNDING: Tvergaards Fund and Edgar and Hustru Gilberte Schnohrs Fund.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Bertelsen, Claus Anders","Neuenschwander, Anders Ulrich","Jansen, Jens Einar","Wilhelmsen, Michael","Kirkegaard-Klitbo, Anders","Tenma, Jutaka Reilin","Bols, Birgitte","Ingeholm, Peter","Rasmussen, Leif Ahrenst","Jepsen, Lars Vedel","Iversen, Else Refsgaard","Kristensen, Bent","Gögenur, Ismail"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-511496"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"corpau":["Danish Colorectal Cancer Group"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma","Adenocarcinoma Mucinous","Aged","Carcinoma Medullary","Carcinoma Signet Ring Cell","Colonic Neoplasms","Comparative Study","Denmark","Disease Free Survival","Female","Follow Up Studies","Humans","Journal Article","Lymphatic Metastasis","Male","Mesocolon","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Research Support Non U S Gov t","Retrospective Studies","Survival Rate"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"disease free survival after complete mesocolic excision compared with conventional colon cancer surgery a retrospective population based study","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-511496","identifier":[{"id":"84921773252","type":"scopus"},{"id":"25555421","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-c5c8161e-d23e-495c-b73c-08ed021c67ad"],"keyword":["Adenocarcinoma","Adenocarcinoma, Mucinous","Aged","Carcinoma, Medullary","Carcinoma, Signet Ring Cell","Colonic Neoplasms","Comparative Study","Denmark","Disease-Free Survival","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Humans","Journal Article","Lymphatic Metastasis","Male","Mesocolon","Middle Aged","Neoplasm Staging","Prognosis","Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't","Retrospective Studies","Survival Rate"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F2108A1E2D74EC891F18C855EC78C2F2"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2016"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":2,"key":"danish colorectal cancer group","name":"Danish Colorectal Cancer Group","role":"oau"}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Claus Anders","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","name":"Bertelsen, Claus Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Ulrich","key":"neuenschwanderpau","last":"Neuenschwander","locid":"8d40d754-671e-4be6-8778-c21bff9ad5b5","name":"Neuenschwander, Anders Ulrich","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jens Erik","key":"jansenpau","last":"Jansen","locid":"6051311