{"abstract":"Purpose: Neoadjuvant drug therapy is presumed to improve outcome in colon cancer. Using multi-detector computed tomography (MDCT) we aimed to assess the early response of neoadjuvant drug therapy for locally advanced colon cancer. Material and Methods: MDCT with i.v. contrast were acquired from consecutive 67 patients before and after preoperative drug therapy. All patients had at baseline histologically confirmed colon cancer with ctT4 or ctT3 tumour with extramural invasion ≥5mm and without distant metastases or peritoneal nodules. The tumour diameter in 2 different planes, extension of extramural tumour invasion and number and size of enlarged lymph nodes were measured before and after the therapy. Results: Mean tumour length was 7.8 cm (95% CI: 5.3–10.4) at baseline and 4.34 cm (95%, CI: 4.0–4.9) after therapy. Mean extramural tumour invasion was 10.6 mm (95% CI: 9.5–11.8) at baseline and 5.7 mm (95% CI: 4.7–6.7) after therapy. Mean number of enlarged lymph nodes was 4.1 (95% CI: 3.4– 4.9) at baseline and 2.1 (95% CI: 1.4–2.7) after therapy. According to the RECIST criteria 45% (95% CI: 34–57) of the patients had response and 55% (95% CI: 43–67) had stable disease. No one showed progressive disease. Conclusion: Using MDCT we demonstrate a significant reduction in tumour size, extramural tumour invasion, number and size of enlarged lymph nodes following neoadjuvant therapy for colon cancer. Using the RESIST criteria 45% had a response.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","Dam, Claus","Lund-Rasmussen, Vera","Pløen, John","Jakobsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-605268"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-12","place":"Paris, fr","start":"2015-06-09","title":"European Society of Gastrointestinal Radiology","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["CT","Colon cancer"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ct in the assessment of early response to neoadjuvant therapy of colon","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13244-015-0412-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-605268","ids":["sdu-700cc1bf-f594-4c25-81cd-3ea08f0f072a"],"keyword":["CT","Colon Cancer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-E1E3119191444090CAE49CC2F5A78523"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13244-015-0412-2","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Radiology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Vejle Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren Rafael","key":"rafaelsenpau","last":"Rafaelsen","locid":"89253a87-a28b-4cb9-aa20-ded9a9d49536","name":"Rafaelsen, Søren Rafael","orcid":"0000-0001-5182-5545","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Claus","key":"dampau","last":"Dam","locid":"103f5188-29ea-414d-ac02-ab5253a7e41b","name":"Dam, Claus","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Vera","key":"lundrasmussenpau","last":"Lund-Rasmussen","name":"Lund-Rasmussen, Vera","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"John","key":"pløenpau","last":"Pløen","locid":"66df5d1a-fea1-429b-954d-c635ef4364bb","name":"Pløen, John","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"jakobsenpau","last":"Jakobsen","locid":"6c772581-e8fe-48bc-a932-1d1c5122c25a","name":"Jakobsen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0003-2110-2615","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","Capital Region of Denmark","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-700cc1bf-f594-4c25-81cd-3ea08f0f072a"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"CT in the assessment of early response to neoadjuvant therapy of colon","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-605268","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The Gait Deviation Index (GDI) and Gait Profile Score (GPS) are the most used summary measures of gait in children with cerebral palsy (CP). However, the reliability and agreement of these indices have not been investigated, limiting their clinimetric quality for research and clinical practice. The aim of this study was to investigate the intra-rater reliability and agreement of summary measures of gait (GDI; GPS; and the Gait Variable Score (GVS) derived from the GPS). The intra-rater reliability and agreement were investigated across two repeated sessions in 18 children aged 5-12 years diagnosed with spastic CP. No systematic bias was observed between the sessions and no heteroscedasticity was observed in Bland-Altman plots. For the GDI and GPS, excellent reliability with intraclass correlation coefficient (ICC) values of 0.8-0.9 was found, while the GVS was found to have fair to good reliability with ICCs of 0.4-0.7. The agreement for the GDI and the logarithmically transformed GPS, in terms of the standard error of measurement as a percentage of the grand mean (SEM%) varied from 4.1 to 6.7%, whilst the smallest detectable change in percent (SDC%) ranged from 11.3 to 18.5%. For the logarithmically transformed GVS, we found a fair to large variation in SEM% from 7 to 29% and in SDC% from 18 to 81%. The GDI and GPS demonstrated excellent reliability and acceptable agreement proving that they can both be used in research and clinical practice. However, the observed large variability for some of the GVS requires cautious consideration when selecting outcome measures.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","Nielsen, Dennis Brandborg","Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","Overgaard, Søren","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-635320"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Biomechanical Phenomena physiology","Cerebral palsy","Cerebral parese","Child","Child Preschool","Female","Gait","Gait Deviation Index","Humans","Instrumented gait analysis","Male","Observer Variation","Outcome Assessment Health Care","Reliability","Reproducibility of Results"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gait deviation index gait profile score and gait variable score in children with spastic cerebral palsy intra rater reliability and agreement across two repeated sessions","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84937812610","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-635320","identifier":[{"id":"26043670","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84937812610","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-d8da35b1-e2b1-4fce-853b-4974667705e3"],"keyword":["Biomechanical Phenomena/physiology","Cerebal palsy","Cerebral Palsy/classification","Cerebral palsy","Child","Child, Preschool","Female","Gait","Gait Disorders, Neurologic/classification","Gait deviation index","Gait profile score","Humans","Instrumented gait analysis","Male","Observer Variation","Outcome Assessment, Health Care","Reliability","Reproducibility of Results","cerebral parese","gangundersøgelse"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-7390E0ADE75D2E6057D8D7F4C3440AD5"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Mätzke","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fc740e3e-3a84-4904-bd04-4db023a123db","name":"Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","orcid":"0000-0002-7522-8144","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Dennis Brandborg","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"196dd8e9-a6c1-4b81-b9c1-175e516ae16d","name":"Nielsen, Dennis Brandborg","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Wisbech","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ed21518f-c0c3-4e67-9b9e-fd9f355c6612","name":"Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"overgaardpau","last":"Overgaard","locid":"b394ea8b-39e4-46bc-8651-f6321e37c2eb","name":"Overgaard, Søren","orcid":"0000-0001-6829-4787","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Holsgaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"3c1cf5a4-81b1-49f3-ad79-d086b74b1561","name":"Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders","name_org":"Larsen, Anders Holsgaard","orcid":"0000-0003-4106-6930","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["26043670"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.gaitpost.2015.04.019","issn":["09666362","18792219"],"issn_org":["09666362"],"issue":"2","journal":"Gait & Posture","pages":"133-137","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Gait & Posture","volume":"42"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84937812610"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-d8da35b1-e2b1-4fce-853b-4974667705e3"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Gait Deviation Index, Gait Profile Score and Gait Variable Score in children with spastic cerebral palsy : Intra-rater reliability and agreement across two repeated sessions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-635320","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background: Children with cerebral palsy (CP) often have an altered gait. Orthopaedic surgery, spasticity management, physical therapy and orthotics are used to improve the gait. Interventions are individually tailored and are planned on the basis of clinical examinations and standardised measurements to assess walking ('care as usual'). However, these measurements do not describe features in the gait that reflect underlying neuro-musculoskeletal impairments. This can be done with 3-dimensional instrumented gait analysis (IGA). The aim of this study is to test the hypothesis that improvements in gait following individually tailored interventions when IGA is used are superior to those following 'care as usual'. Methods/Design: A prospective, single blind, randomised, parallel group study will be conducted. Children aged 5 to 8 years with spastic CP, classified at Gross Motor Function Classification System levels I or II, will be included. The interventions under investigation are: 1) individually tailored interdisciplinary interventions based on the use of IGA, and 2) 'care as usual'. The primary outcome is gait measured by the Gait Deviation Index. Secondary outcome measures are: walking performance (1-min walk test) and patient-reported outcomes of functional mobility (Pediatric Evaluation of Disability Inventory), health-related quality of life (The Pediatric Quality of Life Inventory Cerebral Palsy Module) and overall health, pain and participation (The Pediatric Outcome Data Collection Instrument). The primary endpoint for assessing the outcome of the two interventions will be 52 weeks after start of intervention. A follow up will also be performed at 26 weeks; however, exclusively for the patient-reported outcomes. Discussion: To our knowledge, this is the first randomised controlled trial comparing the effects of an individually tailored interdisciplinary intervention based on the use of IGA versus 'care as usual' in children with CP. Consequently, the study will provide novel evidence for the use of IGA.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","Overgaard, Søren","Hansen, Lars Kjærsgaard","Dunkhase-Heinl, Ulrike","Petkov, Yanko","Engell, Vilhelm","Baker, Richard","Holsgaard-Larsen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-636583"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Salford"],"keyword":["Cerebral Palsy diagnosis","Cerebral palsy","Child","Child Preschool","Disability Evaluation","Disabled Persons rehabilitation","Female","Follow Up Studies","Gait Deviation Index","Gait analysis","Gait physiology","Humans","Male","Motor Skills physiology","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","Single Blind Method","Study protocol","Walking physiology"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the use of instrumented gait analysis for individually tailored interdisciplinary interventions in children with cerebral palsy a randomised controlled trial protocol","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129582705/The_use_of_instrumented_gait_analysis_for_individually_tailored_interdisciplinary_interventions_in_children_with_cerebral_palsy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-636583","identifier":[{"id":"26643822","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84949256959","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC4671214","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["sdu-dd475899-e0d6-4a38-87e4-441a2e7a7e6d"],"keyword":["Cerebral Palsy","Cerebral Palsy/diagnosis","Child","Child, Preschool","Disability Evaluation","Disabled Persons/rehabilitation","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Gait Deviation Index","Gait analysis","Gait/physiology","Humans","Male","Motor Skills/physiology","Physical Therapy Modalities/instrumentation","Prospective Studies","Quality of Life","Single-Blind Method","Study protocol","Walking/physiology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-736571C54E218577726266210B9D1A66"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://findresearcher.sdu.dk/ws/files/129582705/The_use_of_instrumented_gait_analysis_for_individually_tailored_interdisciplinary_interventions_in_children_with_cerebral_palsy.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12887-015-0520-7","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2015","yearSub":"2015"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of orthopaedic surgery (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of salford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Salford","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Helle Mätzke","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fc740e3e-3a84-4904-bd04-4db023a123db","name":"Rasmussen, Helle Mätzke","orcid":"0000-0002-7522-8144","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Niels Wisbech","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"ed21518f-c0c3-4e67-9b9e-fd9f355c6612","name":"Pedersen, Niels Wisbech","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1"