{"abstract":"Undervisningsbog om sociale problemer, der tager afsæt i danske forhold, og som primært er rettet mod de sociale bacheloruddannelser og de dertil knyttede diplomuddannelser.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Bengtsson, Steen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-665479"],"filters":{"added":"2022-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Handicap","Sociale problemer"],"level":"edu","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GV"],"level3":{"GV":["DI-GV-ALL","DI-GV-VIVE"]},"level3all":["DI-GV-VIVE"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"funktionsnedsættelse handicap","src":["vive"],"src-code":["DI-GV-VIVE"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-665479","ids":["vive-f2330f53-0c53-448d-8b80-accf1b1a5cb8"],"keyword":["handicap","sociale problemer"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Educational","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-4E0C42F4BCC73C6EEBF56399EB8DD8F3"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"vive the danish center for social science research","l2":"DI-GV","l2n":"Governmental Institutions","l3":"DI-GV-VIVE","l3nn":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research","namevar":["The Danish National Institute for Social Research, Social Policy and Welfare"],"nora_code":"DI-GV-VIVE","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Steen","key":"bengtssonpau","last":"Bengtsson","locid":"89fd474c-d2bd-4a23-80d5-3ab74135f498","name":"Bengtsson, Steen","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Peter","key":"bundesenpedh","last":"Bundesen","name":"Bundesen, Peter","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Anders Bøggild","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Anders Bøggild","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Tove","key":"rasmussenpedh","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Tove","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788741260518"],"pages":"155-178","place":"København","publisher":"Hans Reitzel","status":"p","title":"Sociale problemer"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Governmental Institutions","DI-ALL","DI-GV","DI-GV-ALL","Governmental Institutions"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["vive-f2330f53-0c53-448d-8b80-accf1b1a5cb8"],"src":["VIVE The Danish Center for Social Science Research"],"title":"Funktionsnedsættelse / handicap","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-665479","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"The aim of this publication is to bring together the knowledge and experiences of entrepreneurship education of the Danish Foundation for Entrepreneurship - Young Enterprise (hereafter the Foundation) and present various perspectives on what entrepreneurship education is and how it can be produced and evaluated as educational practice. We aim to construct an alignment between the overall purpose and learning goals of entrepreneurship education, the content and progression the teaching should have and the feedback, evaluation and assessment that will support student learning. At the same time, we seek to describe how this can be manifested as pedagogical practice in a diverse educational system with different levels, curricula and traditions. This text is intended for teachers, leaders and decision makers at all levels of education - from primary school to higher education. With this broad aim, we seek to create a common thread throughout the educational system and a common understanding of the phenomenon of entrepreneurship education. This also implies that the individual educational institution will need to interpret the text in a way which creates a link between its academic objectives and the entrepreneurial dimensions and goals that form the basis for the understanding in the text. This publication is part of the Foundation’s work as a knowledge centre, and is based on the previously published progression model and the research and impact studies the Foundation has developed and implemented in the field of entrepreneurship education. Models and research findings are available on the Foundation’s website: www.ffe-ye.dk This publication will be updated regularly as new knowledge is acquired and new models are developed","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders","Moberg, Kåre","Jensen, Christine Revsbech"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-679947"],"filters":{"added":"2023-08","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Fonden for Entreprenørskab"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-RUC"]},"level3all":["DI-U-RUC"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a taxonomy of entrepreneurship education perspectives on goals teaching and evaluation","src":["ruc"],"src-code":["DI-U-RUC"],"type":"db","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eng.ffe-ye.dk/media/785766/taxonomy-en.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-679947","ids":["ruc-d3c45fa9-b202-430e-9379-6139c31083f8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-8AD1DBCDFFD76CF84B9225935C9F4F1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://eng.ffe-ye.dk/media/785766/taxonomy-en.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Fonden for Entreprenørskab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ruc roskilde university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-RUC","l3nl":"Roskilde University","l3nn":"RUC Roskilde University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"RUC Roskilde University","namevar":["Roskilde University, Department of People and Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-RUC","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kåre","key":"mobergpau","last":"Moberg","name":"Moberg, Kåre","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","country":"dk","first":"Christine Revsbech","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"8e52a3fb-db44-46a2-977c-4f631c544938","name":"Jensen, Christine Revsbech","orcid":"0000-0002-9995-6293","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"isbn":["9788790386214"],"pages":"50","publisher":"Fonden for Entreprenørskab","status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Roskilde University","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ruc-d3c45fa9-b202-430e-9379-6139c31083f8"],"src":["RUC Roskilde University"],"title":"A Taxonomy of Entrepreneurship Education : Perspectives on goals, teaching and evaluation","type":"Book","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-679947","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"Background Comprehensive recognition of genomic variation in one individual is important for understanding disease and developing personalized medication and treatment. Many tools based on DNA re-sequencing exist for identification of single nucleotide polymorphisms, small insertions and deletions (indels) as well as large deletions. However, these approaches consistently display a substantial bias against the recovery of complex structural variants and novel sequence in individual genomes and do not provide interpretation information such as the annotation of ancestral state and formation mechanism. Findings We present a novel approach implemented in a single software package, AsmVar, to discover, genotype and characterize different forms of structural variation and novel sequence from population-scale de novo genome assemblies up to nucleotide resolution. Application of AsmVar to several human de novo genome assemblies captures a wide spectrum of structural variants and novel sequences present in the human population in high sensitivity and specificity. Conclusions Our method provides a direct solution for investigating structural variants and novel sequences from de novo genome assemblies, facilitating the construction of population-scale pan-genomes. Our study also highlights the usefulness of the de novo assembly strategy for definition of genome structure. Keywords: de novo assembly; Structural variation; Novel sequence","author_count":26,"contributors":["Liu, Siyang","Huang, Shujia","Rao, Junhua","Ye, Weijian","Schierup, Mikkel H.","Villesen, Palle","Xu, Xun","Li, Ning","Kristiansen, Karsten","Sørensen, Thorkild I. A.","Hansen, Torben","Pedersen, Oluf","Brunak, Søren","Gupta, Ramneek","Rasmussen, Simon","Lund, Ole","Bolund, Lars","Børglum, Anders D.","Eiberg, Hans","Nørgaard Flindt, Esben","Xu, Ruiqi","Sun, Jihua","Liu, Hao","Jiang, Hui","Wang, Ou","Cheng, Xiaofang","Demontis, Ditte","Besenbacher, Søren","Mailund, Thomas","Friborg, Rune M.","Pedersen, Christian N. S.","Liu, Siyang","Chang, Yuqi","Li, Shengting","Guo, Xiaosen","Cao, Hongzhi","Ye, Chen","Maretty, Lasse","Andreas Sibbesen, Jonas","Albrechtsen, Anders","Bork-Jensen, Jette","Theil Have, Christian","Gonzalez-Izarzugaza, Jose Maria","Belling, Kirstine C.","Yadav, Rachita","Grove, Jakob","Dam-Als, Thomas","Lescai, Francesco","Krogh, Anders","Wang, Jun"],"cuid":["S03-086.46-024038"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"continent":["Asia, East"],"corpau":["Danish Pan Genome Consortium","Genome Denmark Consortium (Anders Børglum, member of -)"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","BGI Group","BGI-Shenzhen"],"keyword":["De novo assembly","Novel sequence","Structural variation"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-OTH"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-OTH","DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"discovery genotyping and characterization of structural variation and novel sequence at single nucleotide resolution from de novo genome assemblies on a population scale","src":["au","dtu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-DTU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s13742-015-0103-4","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S03-086.46-024038","identifier":[{"id":"PMC4690232","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84991529236","type":"scopus"},{"id":"26705468","type":"pmid"},{"id":"000367318100001","type":"wos"}],"ids":["au-9bf3a00c-f247-4307-8d1b-32070931c760","dtu-c4dae3e6-00da-4741-96e1-4a17d7417944","ku-afd8ae62-313d-477e-906f-7fba547a05ee"],"keyword":["De novo assembly","Novel sequence","Structural variation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technolog