 University of Denmark","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Discovery, genotyping and characterization of structural variation and novel sequence at single nucleotide resolution from de novo genome assemblies on a population scale","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S03-086.46-024038","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: This register-based observational study compares dabigatran to warfarin for secondary stroke prevention in atrial fibrillation patients among both 'new starters' on dabigatran and 'switchers' to dabigatran from warfarin. METHODS: We identified in nationwide Danish registries 2,398 patients with atrial fibrillation and a history of stroke/TIA, making a first-time purchase of dabigatran 110mg bid (D110) and 150mg bid (D150). Patients were categorized as either vitamin K antagonist (VKA) naïve or experienced. Warfarin controls were identified using a complete (for VKA-naïve dabigatran patients) or matched sampling approach (for VKA-experienced dabigatran patients). Subjects were followed for an average of 12.6 months for stroke and transient ischemic attacks. Confounder-adjusted Cox regression models were used to compare event rates between treatments. RESULTS: Among patients with a history of stroke/ transient ischemic attack and prior VKA experience, switching to dabigatran was associated with an increased stroke/ transient ischemic attack rate for both dabigatran doses compared to continuing on warfarin (D110 hazard ratio [HR] 1.99, 95% confidence interval [CI]: 1.42-2.78; D150 HR 2.34, 95% CI: 1.60-3.41). Among prior stroke/ transient ischemic attack patients who were new starters on dabigatran or warfarin, the rate of stroke/ transient ischemic attack for both doses of dabigatran was similar to or lower than warfarin (D110 HR 0.64, 95% CI: 0.50-0.80; D150 HR 0.92, 95% CI: 0.73-1.15). CONCLUSIONS: In this register-based study, VKA-experienced patients with a history of stroke or transient ischemic attack who switched to dabigatran therapy had an increased rate of stroke compared to patients persisting with warfarin therapy.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Skjøth, Flemming","Lane, Deirdre","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-086776"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dabigatran and warfarin for secondary prevention of stroke in atrial fibrillation patients a nationwide cohort study","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-086776","identifier":[{"id":"84919667464","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000346029400034","type":"wos"},{"id":"25193361","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-7e423ecb-6943-4530-9046-b4ef00f58898"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F965BB73B2C7BD717931E125BE0B483C"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"n