01-000.00-183786","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The haptoglobin-hemoglobin receptor CD163 and proTNF-α are transmembrane macrophage proteins subjected to cleavage by the inflammation-responsive protease AD-AM17. This leads to release of soluble CD163 (sCD163) and bioactive TNF-α. Sequence comparison of the juxtamembrane region identified similar palindromic sequences in human CD163 (1044Arg-Ser-Ser-Arg) and proTNF-α (78Arg-Ser-Ser-Ser-Arg). In proTNF-α the Arg-Ser-Ser-Ser-Arg sequence is situated next to the previously established ADAM17 cleavage site. Site-directed mutagenesis revealed that the sequences harbor essential information for efficient cleavage of the two proteins upon AD-AM17 stimulation. This was further evidenced by analysis of mouse CD163 that, like CD163 in other non-primates, does not contain the palin-dromic CD163 sequence in the juxtamembrane region. Mouse CD163 resisted endotoxin and phorbol ester-induced shedding and ex-vivo analysis of knock-in of the Arg-Ser-Ser-Arg sequence in mouse CD163 revealed a receptor shedding comparable to that of human CD163. In conclusion, we have identified an es-sential substrate motif for ADAM17-mediated CD163 and proTNF-α cleavage in macrophag-es. In addition, the present data indicate that CD163, by incorporation of this motif in late evolution, undervent a modification that allows for an instant downregulation of surface CD163 expression and inhibition of hemoglobin uptake. This regulatory modality seems to have coincided with the evolution of an enhanced hemoglobin-protecting role of the haptoglobin-CD163 system in primates.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Etzerodt, Anders","Rasmussen, Mie Rostved","Svendsen, Pia","Chalaris, Athena","Schwarz, Jeanette","Galea, Ian","Møller, Holger Jon","Moestrup, Søren Kragh"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-218507"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"structural basis for inflammation driven shedding of cd000000000163 and tumor necrosis factor α in macrophages","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M113.520213","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-218507","identifier":[{"id":"PMC3887204","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"24275664","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84891945600","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9c93fb31-f5c5-42c3-800b-ded592ac83c9"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3E6D9C61CCDB0ADB33D0063B7ED53D81"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1074/jbc.M113.520213","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Department of Biomedicine, Department of Biomedicine - Forskning og uddannelse, Vest"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"etzerodtpau","last":"Etzerodt","locid":"c0b60588-6275-45c0-8ad2-bb91a248ff22","name":"Etzerodt, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-6757-2068","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mie Rostved","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"adca4964-8371-42b2-9e09-cd02f6749962","name":"Rasmussen, Mie Rostved","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pia","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"0a6a1bb6-da6c-42af-9878-392147417eaf","name":"Svendsen, Pia","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Athena","key":"chalarispau","last":"Chalaris","name":"Chalaris, Athena","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Jeanette","key":"schwarzpau","last":"Schwarz","name":"Schwarz, Jeanette","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ian","key":"galeapau","last":"Galea","name":"Galea, Ian","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Holger Jon","key":"mollerpau","last":"Moller","locid":"b08dc9ce-d595-49c6-833a-4ec9b4223a05","name":"Møller, Holger Jon","name_org":"Moller, Holger Jon","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Soren Kragh","key":"moestruppau","last":"Moestrup","locid":"84b91217-5ed8-4507-8a92-00c1815e2c81","name":"Moestrup, Søren Kragh","name_org":"Moestrup, Soren Kragh","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24275664"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1074/jbc.m113.520213","issn":["00219258","10678816"],"issn_org":["00219258"],"journal":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","pages":"778-788","publisher":"American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Biological Chemistry","volume":"289"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84891945600"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9c93fb31-f5c5-42c3-800b-ded592ac83c9"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Structural Basis for inflammation-Driven Shedding of CD163 and Tumor Necrosis Factor-α in Macrophages","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-218507","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Classical swine fever virus (CSFV) strain “Koslov” is highly virulent with a mortality rate of up to 100% in pigs. In this study, we modified non-functional cDNAs generated from the blood of Koslov virus infected pigs bysite-directed mutagenesis, removing non-synonymous mutations step-by-step, thereby producing genomes encoding the consensus amino acid sequence. Viruses rescued from the construct corresponding to the inferred parental form were highly virulent, when tested in pigs, with infected animals displaying pronounced clinical symptoms leading to high mortality. The reconstruction therefore gave rise to a functional cDNA corresponding to the highly virulent Koslov strain of CSFV. It could be demonstrated that two single amino acid changes (S763L and P968H) in the surface structural protein E2 resulted in attenuation in the porcine infection system while another single amino acid change within the nonstructural protein NS3 (D2183G) reduced virus growth within cells in vitro.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Fahnøe, Ulrik","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Risager, Peter Christian","Nielsen, Jens","Belsham, Graham","Höper, Dirk","Beer, Martin","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-309023"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"rescue of the highly virulent classical swine fever virus strain koslov from cloned cdna and first insights into genome variations relevant for virulence","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virol.2014.08.021","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-309023","identifier":[{"id":"25240324","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84907462400","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-0ebd2aed-7d6a-4e82-849f-9bfb7971d00d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8A886EEB9ED7400D2933C4B10DC0FD4D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.virol.2014.08.021","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis, Molecular Evolution","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Systems Biotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"friedrich loeffler institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"fahnøepau","last":"Fahnøe","locid":"409de6f2-ff5a-4623-8c2e-4bb18ee9c505","name":"Fahnøe, Ulrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Gorm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bb3513aa-fb20-46ef-ba14-9c150c929cf1","name":"Pedersen, Anders Gorm","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-8965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Peter Christian","key":"risagerpau","last":"Risager","locid":"d1e49b18-7ac1-4e71-85a1-48e90f57cd7f","name":"Risager, Peter Christian","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"34511f38-e2d9-41d2-a82f-1044f16d784c","name":"Nielsen, Jens","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Graham","key":"belshampau","last":"Belsham","locid":"72bf708e-8dd0-4270-b384-13f0ba640905","name":"Belsham, Graham","orcid":"0000-0003-1187-4873","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dirk","key":"höperpau","last":"Höper","name":"Höper, Dirk","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"beerpau","last":"Beer","name":"Beer, Martin","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Bruun","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ac10aec0-1a8a-4f66-a5c6-2275ddf1726e","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-4241-1559","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25240324"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.virol.2014.08.021","issn":["00426822","1089862X"],"issn_org":["00426822"],"journal":"Virology","pages":"379-387","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Virology","volume":"468-470"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84907462400"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-0ebd2aed-7d6a-4e82-849f-9bfb7971d00d"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Rescue of the highly virulent classical swine fever virus strain “Koslov” from cloned cDNA and first insights into genome variations relevant for virulence","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-309023","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The input-queued (IQ) switch architecture is favoured for designing multicast high-speed switches because of its scalability and low implementation complexity. However, using the first-in-first-out (FIFO) queueing discipline at each input of the switch may cause the head-of-line (HOL) blocking problem. Using a separate queue for each output port at an input to reduce the HOL blocking, that is, the virtual output queuing discipline, increases the implementation complexity, which limits the scalability. Given the increasing link speed and network capacity, a low-complexity yet efficient multicast scheduling algorithm is required for next generation high-speed networks. This study proposes the novel efficient round-robin multicast scheduling algorithm for IQ architectures and demonstrates how this algorithm can be implemented as a hardware solution, which alleviates the multicast HOL blocking issue by means of queue look-ahead. Simulation results demonstrate that this FIFO-based IQ multicast architecture is able to achieve significant improvements in terms of multicast latency requirements by searching through a small number of cells beyond the HOL cells in the input queues. Furthermore, hardware synthesis results show that the proposed algorithm can be very efficiently implemented in hardware to perform multicast scheduling at very high speeds with only modest resource requirements.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders","Yu, Hao","Ruepp, Sarah Renée","Berger, Michael Stübert","Dittmann, Lars"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-350551"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Multicast","Scheduling"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"efficient round robin multicast scheduling for input queued switches","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1049/iet-net.2012.0172","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-350551","identifier":[{"id":"84953252052","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-9a40750e-849f-4789-9e01-2c40c43cd64d"],"keyword":["High-speed network","Input-queued","Multicast","Scheduling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0CFE62569AA9D23CBBBBDBDFE3C67D78"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1049/iet-net.2012.0172","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87986f01-324c-411f-b6e1-968b73835d8d","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Hao","key":"yupau","last":"Yu","locid":"d31421ff-c774-4cd0-963c-bef6b0351797","name":"Yu, Hao","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","n