culture : 5.revised edition","type":"Lecture Notes","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-449573","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND: Following activation, platelets release small vesicles called platelet-derived microparticles (PMPs). PMPs accelerate thrombin generation and thus clot formation at sites of injury by exposing the procoagulant membrane phospholipid phosphatidylserine (PS). The role of PMPs in coagulopathy and hemorrhage following trauma remains elusive. We hypothesized that low levels of PS-positive PMPs (PS + PMPs) would be associated with impaired clot formation. METHODS: This is a prospective observational study of 210 trauma patients admitted directly to a Level 1 trauma center. Plasma levels of PS + PMPs were determined by flow cytometry. Coagulation status was assessed by rotational thrombelastometry, and impaired clot formation was defined by an α angle less than 63 degrees using the tissue factor-based EXTEM reagent. Transfusion requirement was assessed by number of units of red blood cells (RBCs) transfused within 24 hours of admission; platelet aggregation capacity was evaluated by the Multiplate assay; and injury severity was determined by the Injury Severity Score (ISS). RESULTS: The median ISS was 17, and blood samples were obtained after a median of 65 minutes following injury. Significantly lower levels of PS + PMPs were found in patients with impaired clot formation (p < 0.001). A low level of PS + PMPs was associated with a higher number of RBCs transfused during the initial 24 hours after admission (p < 0.03) when corrected for risk factors, for example, platelet count, hemoglobin level, and ISS. Platelet aggregation and PS + PMPs did not correlate significantly. CONCLUSION: Low levels of PMPs were associated with impaired clot formation in trauma patients at admission and also with the number of RBC transfusions. This suggests that PMPs may play an important and not previously investigated role in trauma-induced coagulopathy. LEVEL OF EVIDENCE: Prognostic study, level III.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Windeløv, Nis Agerlin","Johansson, Pär Ingemar","Sørensen, Anne Marie","Perner, Anders","Wanscher, Michael","Larsen, Claus Falck","Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","Rasmussen, Lars S"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-451469"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"low level of procoagulant platelet microparticles is associated with impaired coagulation and transfusion requirements in trauma patients","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/TA.0000000000000437","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-451469","identifier":[{"id":"25494419","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84925517847","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-60f794e3-7748-40b1-b01a-65eb2242381d"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-876393E50DC1DC3EF3D06D85D9F3F232"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/TA.0000000000000437","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Clinical Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Nis Agerlin","key":"windeløvpau","last":"Windeløv","name":"Windeløv, Nis Agerlin","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Pär Ingemar","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Pär Ingemar","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anne Marie","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","name":"Sørensen, Anne Marie","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"pernerpau","last":"Perner","locid":"8a389541-d529-4ee3-8364-66bfc85f77c9","name":"Perner, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Michael","key":"wanscherpau","last":"Wanscher","name":"Wanscher, Michael","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Claus Falck","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9884e6dd-2a29-45b2-bf54-56ac2970cd89","name":"Larsen, Claus Falck","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Sisse Rye","key":"ostrowskipau","last":"Ostrowski","name":"Ostrowski, Sisse Rye","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Lars Simon","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"37e36b99-34dd-471f-b09b-d93e72940ec0","name":"Rasmussen, Lars S","name_org":"Rasmussen, Lars Simon","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25494419"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1097/ta.0000000000000437","issn":["00225282","21630763"],"issn_org":["00225282"],"issue":"5","journal":"The Journal of Trauma and Acute Care Surgery","pages":"692-700","status":"p","title":"The Journal of Trauma and Acute Care Surgery","volume":"77"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84925517847"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-60f794e3-7748-40b1-b01a-65eb2242381d"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Low level of procoagulant platelet microparticles is associated with impaired coagulation and transfusion requirements in trauma patients","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-451469","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Building chronological frameworks for proxy sequences spanning 130e60 ka b2k is plagued by difficulties and uncertainties. Recent developments in the North Atlantic region, however, affirm the potential offered by tephrochronology and specifically the search for cryptotephra. Here we review the potential offered by tephrostratigraphy for sequences spanning 130e60 ka b2k. We combine newly identified cryptotephra deposits from the NGRIP ice-core and a marine core from the Iceland Basin with previously published data from the ice and marine realms to construct the first tephrostratigraphical framework for this time-interval. Forty-three tephra or cryptotephra deposits are incorporated into this framework; twenty three tephra deposits are found in the Greenland ice-cores, including nine new NGRIP tephras, and twenty separate deposits are preserved in various North Atlantic marine sequences. Major, minor and trace element results are presented for the new NGRIP horizons together with age estimates based on their position within the ice-core record. Basaltic tephras of Icelandic origin dominate the framework with only eight tephras of rhyolitic composition found. New results from marine core MD99-2253 also illustrate some of the complexities and challenges of assessing the depositional integrity of marine cryptotephra deposits. Tephra-based correlations in the marine environment provide independent tie-points for this time-interval and highlight the potential of widening the application of tephrochronology. Further investigations, however, are required, that combine robust geochemical fingerprinting and a rigorous assessment of tephra depositional processes, in order to trace coeval events between the two depositional realms","author_count":11,"contributors":["Siwan M., Davis","Peter M., Abbott","Rhian H., Meara","Nicholas J.G., Pearce","William E. N., Austin","Mark R., Chapman","Svensson, Anders","Bigler, Matthias","Rasmussen, Tine L.","Rasmussen, Sune Olander","Farmer, Elizabeth J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-545580"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Norway","United Kingdom"],"glorg":["Aberystwyth University","All Global Affiliations","Department of Geography, College of Science, Swansea University, Swansea, UK","University of East Anglia","University of St Andrews","University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a north atlantic tephrostratigraphical framework for 000000000130 000000000060 ka b000000000002k new tephra discoveries marine based correlations and future challenges","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quascirev.2014.03.024","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-545580","identifier":[{"id":"84924369708","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-fefc5009-61bb-4495-b648-a511be3dbe01"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-BF27736409A1A7040645D0DC9C2D28B9"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quascirev.2014.03.024","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"department of geography college of science swansea university swansea uk","name":"Department of Geography, College of Science, Swansea University, Swansea, UK","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"aberystwyth university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Aberystwyth University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of st andrews","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of St Andrews","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"gb","key":"university of east anglia","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of East Anglia","used":1},{"affno":"5","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"no","key":"university of tromsø the arctic university of norway","loc":["Norway","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"University of Tromsø – The Arctic University of Norway","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Davis","key":"siwanmdavispau","last":"Siwan M.","name":"Siwan M., Davis","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Abbott","key":"petermabbottpau","last":"Peter M.","name":"Peter M., Abbott","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Meara","key":"rhianhmearapau","last":"Rhian H.","name":"Rhian H., Meara","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Pearce","key":"nicholasjgpearcepau","last":"Nicholas J.G.","name":"Nicholas J.G., Pearce","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Austin","key":"williamenaustinpau","last":"William E. N.","name":"William E. N., Austin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Chapman","key":"markrchapmanpau","last":"Mark R.","name":"Mark R., Chapman","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Anders","key":"svenssonanderspau","last":"Svensson","locid":"e0501b84-a817-417e-9c70-9601c6b26cb8","name":"Svensson, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-4364-6085","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Matthias","key":"biglermatthiaspau","last":"Bigler","locid":"2714d296-3b40-421f-b5b1-a3a783f462e0","name":"Bigler, Matthias","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","first":"T