{"abstract":"This article provides two examples of the Americanization of Danish journalism through an examination of Danish journalists' adaptation of New Journalism and investigative journalism as seen through the pages of the Danish Union of Journalists' periodical Journalisten. The article answers Daniel Hallin and Paolo Mancini's call for more \"concrete\" studies of the Americanization process. The study demonstrates how news media in the United States, in the two examples provided, have served as an important source of methodological inspiration for Danish journalists from the late 1960s forward.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-584191"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Americanization","Investigative journalism","Journalism education","Journalism practice","New journalism","Transnationalization"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the americanization of danish journalism","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2478/nor-2014-0002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-584191","identifier":[{"id":"84902357351","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-263f9da1-7fdf-48b3-b024-3f1308fc57b8"],"keyword":["Americanization","Investigative journalism","Journalism education","Journalism practice","New journalism","Transnationalization"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-8188C015E3BE31D8A70BC286F97FBBA0"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.2478/nor-2014-0002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History, Center for American Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f284f3a3-297f-4882-81e1-b591c41ead80","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9817-9595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.2478/nor-2014-0002","issn":["14031108","20015119"],"issn_org":["14031108"],"issue":"1","journal":"Nordicom Review","pages":"17-31","publisher":"Nordicom","status":"p","title":"Nordicom Review","volume":"35"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84902357351"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-263f9da1-7fdf-48b3-b024-3f1308fc57b8"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Americanization of Danish Journalism","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-584191","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"We present a synchronization of the NGRIP, GRIP and GISP2 ice cores onto a master chronology extending back to 104ka before present, providing a consistent chronological framework for these three Greenland records. The synchronization aligns distinct peaks in volcanic proxy records and other impurity records (chemo-stratigraphic matching) and assumes that these layers of elevated impurity content represent the same, instantaneous event in the past at all three sites. More than 900 marker horizons between the three cores have been identified and our matching is independently confirmed by 24 new and previously identified volcanic ash (tephra) tie-points. Using the reference horizons, we transfer the widely used Greenland ice-core chronology, GICC05modelext, to the two Summit cores, GRIP and GISP2. Furthermore, we provide gas chronologies for the Summit cores that are consistent with the GICC05modelext timescale by utilizing both existing and new gas data (CH4concentration and δ15N of N2). We infer that the accumulation contrast between the stadial and interstadial phases of the glacial period was ~10% greater at Summit compared to at NGRIP. The δ18O temperature-proxy records from NGRIP, GRIP, and GISP2 are generally very similar and display synchronous behaviour at climate transitions. The δ18O differences between Summit and NGRIP, however, changed slowly over the Last Glacial-Interglacial cycle and also underwent abrupt millennial-to-centennial-scale variations. We suggest that this observed latitudinal δ18O gradient in Greenland during the glacial period is the result of 1) relatively higher degree of precipitation with a Pacific signature at NGRIP, 2) increased summer bias in precipitation at Summit, and 3) enhanced Rayleigh distillation due to an increased source-to-site distance and a potentially larger source-to-site temperature gradient. We propose that these processes are governed by changes in the North American Ice Sheet (NAIS) volume and North Atlantic sea-ice extent and/or sea-surface temperatures (SST) on orbital timescales, and that changing sea-ice extent and SSTs are the driving mechanisms on shorter timescales. Finally, we observe that maxima in the Summit-NGRIP δ18O difference are roughly coincident with prominent Heinrich events. This suggests that the climatic reorganization that takes place during stadials with Heinrich events, possibly driven by a southward expansion of sea ice and low SSTs in the North Atlantic, are recorded in the ice-core records.","author_count":20,"contributors":["Seierstad, Inger Kathrine","Abbott, Peter M.","Bigler, Matthias","Blunier, Thomas","Bourne, Anna J.","Brook, Edward","Buchardt, Susanne Lilja","Buizert, Christo","Clausen, Henrik Brink","Cook, Eliza","Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","Davies, Siwan M.","Guillevic, Myriam","Johnsen, Sigfus Johann","Pedersen, Desirée S.","Popp, Trevor James","Rasmussen, Sune Olander","Severinghaus, Jeffrey P.","Svensson, Anders","Vinther, Bo Møllesøe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-695720"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["Switzerland","United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Swansea University","University of Bern","University of California at Berkeley","University of Oregon"],"keyword":["Greenland ice cores","Heinrich event","Paleoclimate","Regional climate"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"consistently dated records from the greenland grip gisp000000000002 and ngrip ice cores for the past 000000000104 ka reveal regional millennial scale δ sup 000000000018 sup o gradients with possible heinrich event imprint","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-695720","identifier":[{"id":"84924425344","type":"scopus"},{"id":"{pubmed}","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-42af6fe4-a247-48b2-9952-5f4037942523"],"keyword":["GICC05 chronology","Greenland ice cores","Heinrich event","Paleoclimate","Regional climate","Tephra isochrons","Water isotopes (δ18O)"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-35EDA5EE1EC87F85E5D8D5B1FBC0E29A"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"swansea university","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"Swansea University","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ch","key":"university of bern","loc":["Switzerland","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Bern","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"us","key":"university of oregon","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Oregon","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of california at berkeley","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at Berkeley","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Inger K.","key":"seierstadpau","last":"Seierstad","locid":"719f8491-e2c2-438a-9b6a-99a14512be74","name":"Seierstad, Inger Kathrine","name_org":"Seierstad, Inger K.","orcid":"0000-0003-1294-2292","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Peter M.","key":"abbottpau","last":"Abbott","name":"Abbott, Peter M.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","first":"Matthias","key":"biglerpau","last":"Bigler","name":"Bigler, Matthias","rank":3,"roleco