{"abstract":"Background/Objectives:The evidence regarding fatty acids and breast cancer risk is inconclusive. Adipose tissue fatty acids can be used as biomarkers of fatty acid intake and of endogenous fatty acid exposure. Fatty acids in adipose tissue are correlated owing to common dietary sources and shared metabolic pathways, which group fatty acids into naturally occurring patterns. We aimed to prospectively investigate associations between adipose tissue fatty acid patterns and long-term risk of total breast cancer and breast cancer subtypes characterised by oestrogen and progesterone receptor status (ER and PR).Subjects/Methods:This case-cohort study was based on data from the Danish cohort Diet, Cancer and Health. At baseline, a fat biopsy and information on lifestyle and reproductive factors were collected. From the 31 original fatty acids measured, patterns of fatty acids were identified using the treelet transform. During a median follow-up of 5.3 years, 474 breast cancer cases were identified. Hazard ratios and 95% confidence intervals of risk of total breast cancer and of subtypes according to quintiles of factor score were determined by weighted Cox proportional hazards regression.Results:After adjustment for potential confounders, factor scores for the seven patterns identified by the treelet transform were not associated with risk of total breast cancer, nor with risk of ER+, ER-, PR+ or PR- tumours.Conclusions:No clear associations between the patterns of fatty acids at baseline and long-term risk of total breast cancer or ER+, ER-, PR+ or PR- tumours were observed.European Journal of Clinical Nutrition advance online publication, 19 March 2014; doi:10.1038/ejcn.2014.28.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Schmidt, J A","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Nyström, P W","Christensen, Jeppe Hagstrup","Schmidt, Erik Berg","Dethlefsen, Claus","Tjønneland, A","Overvad, Kim","Dahm, C C"],"cuid":["S02-099.06-003894"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Department of Oncology, University Hospital of Uppsala, Uppsala, Sweden.","Uppsala University"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-U"],"level3":{"NP":["DI-NP-ALL","DI-NP-CAN"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-NP-CAN","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"baseline patterns of adipose tissue fatty acids and long term risk of breast cancer a case cohort study in the danish cohort diet cancer and health","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejcn.2014.28","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-099.06-003894","identifier":[{"id":"24642780","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84926153969","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000342736200002","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-4fbeb4b4-2294-4e35-8ad5-6e6157e15a8b","au-733924c0-cc90-4ca0-9033-3ac75234a3cb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-18632C1FDB9E714178C5ACB3D3077D48"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/ejcn.2014.28","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Health, Studienævnene på HE, Studienævnene på HE - Board of Studies, Health Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Hjertemedicin (Kardiologi) [Klinik Hjerte-Lunge]","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Aalborg University Hospital, Klinik Hjerte-Lunge"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"se","key":"department of oncology university hospital of uppsala uppsala sweden","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Department of Oncology, University Hospital of Uppsala, Uppsala, Sweden.","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"se","key":"uppsala university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Uppsala University","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"dk","key":"dcrc danish cancer society research center","l2":"DI-NP","l2n":"Non-Profit Organisations","l3":"DI-NP-CAN","l3nn":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DCRC Danish Cancer Society Research Center","namevar":["Danish Cancer Society"],"nora_code":"DI-NP-CAN","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J A","key":"schmidtjulieapau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"bdb7dc37-213b-4a5f-8075-0dd77b5100bc","name":"Schmidt, Julie A.","name_org":"Schmidt, J A","orcid":"0000-0002-7733-8750","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"gorstrasmussenanderspau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","name_org":"Gorst-Rasmussen, A","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"P W","key":"nyströmpwpau","last":"Nyström","name":"Nyström, P W","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"J H","key":"christensenjeppehagstruppau","last":"Christensen","locid":"8b0514a3-d3aa-4fa6-acd2-2d32e219593f","name":"Christensen, Jeppe Hagstrup","name_org":"Christensen, J H","orcid":"0000-0003-1208-833X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"E B","key":"schmidterikbergpau","last":"Schmidt","locid":"3eff6ccc-90b4-48ee-b121-8df4865f0342","name":"Schmidt, Erik Berg","name_org":"Schmidt, E B","orcid":"0000-0002-0623-5666","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"C","key":"dethlefsenclauspau","last":"Dethlefsen","locid":"0c974fc9-162c-443f-95b9-5325087e16a5","name":"Dethlefsen, Claus","name_org":"Dethlefsen, C","orcid":"0000-0003-3994-6189","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"A","key":"tjønnelandapau","last":"Tjønneland","name":"Tjønneland, A","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"K","key":"overvadkimpau","last":"Overvad","locid":"7ca4bfca-d3a3-484e-8ee5-d7cb6ad7314b","name":"Overvad, Kim","name_org":"Overvad, K","orcid":"0000-0001-6429-7921","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"C C","key":"dahmchristinacpau","last":"Dahm","locid":"99090c31-2a55-406a-a3a0-fe4e9c7ab98b","name":"Dahm, Christina C","name_org":"Dahm, C C","orcid":"0000-0003-0481-2893","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["24642780"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1038/ejcn.2014.28","issn":["09543007","14765640"],"issn_org":["09543007"],"issue":"10","journal":"European Journal of Clinical Nutrition","pages":"1088-94","publisher":"Springer Nature","status":"p","title":"European Journal of Clinical Nutrition","volume":"68"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84926153969"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Non-Profit Organisations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-NP","DI-NP-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Non-Profit Organisations","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-4fbeb4b4-2294-4e35-8ad5-6e6157e15a8b","au-733924c0-cc90-4ca0-9033-3ac75234a3cb"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Baseline patterns of adipose tissue fatty acids and long-term risk of breast cancer : a case-cohort study in the Danish cohort Diet, Cancer and Health","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-099.06-003894","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Epigenetic information is available from contemporary organisms, but is difficult to track back in evolutionary time. Here, we show that genome-wide epigenetic information can be gathered directly from next-generation sequence reads of DNA isolated from ancient remains. Using the genome sequence data generated from hair shafts of a 4000-yr-old Paleo-Eskimo belonging to the Saqqaq culture, we generate the first ancient nucleosome map coupled with a genome-wide survey of cytosine methylation levels. The validity of both nucleosome map and methylation levels were confirmed by the recovery of the expected signals at promoter regions, exon/intron boundaries, and CTCF sites. The top-scoring nucleosome calls revealed distinct DNA positioning biases, attesting to nucleotide-level accuracy. The ancient methylation levels exhibited high conservation over time, clustering closely with modern hair tissues. Using ancient methylation information, we estimated the age at death of the Saqqaq individual and illustrate how epigenetic information can be used to infer ancient gene expression. Similar epigenetic signatures were found in other fossil material, such as 110,000- to 130,000-yr-old bones, supporting the contention that ancient epigenomic information can be reconstructed from a deep past. Our findings lay the foundation for extracting epigenomic information from ancient samples, allowing shifts in epialleles to be tracked through evolutionary time, as well as providing an original window into modern epigenomics.","author_count":21,"contributors":["Pedersen, Jakob Skou","Valen, Eivind","Velazquez, Amhed M Vargas","Parker, Brian John","Rasmussen, Morten","Lindgreen, Stinus","Lilje, Berit","Tobin, Desmond J","Kelly, Theresa K","Vang, Søren","Andersson, Robin","Jones, Peter A","Hoover, Cindi A","Tikhonov, Alexei","Prokhortchouk, Egor","Rubin, Edward M","Sandelin, Albin Gustav","Gilbert, M Thomas P","Krogh, Anders","Willerslev, Eske","Orlando, Ludovic Antoine Alexandr