{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Hansen, Anders Peder Lysholm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-094462"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["soc"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udviklingen af en problembaseret mba inden for de eksisterende institutionelle rammer","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aauforlag.dk/Shop/laering-og-uddannelse/problembaseret-erhvervsoekonomi-en-antologi-o.aspx","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-094462","ids":["aau-9922511d-da0e-4e92-a2f9-2870b4a0c84e"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Social Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3030C7CB827F1E219215663F3B9575B1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aauforlag.dk/Shop/laering-og-uddannelse/problembaseret-erhvervsoekonomi-en-antologi-o.aspx","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG), Center for Industrial Production (department)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG), Center for Industrial Production (department), Forskningsgruppen Sourcing Excellence"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Peder Lysholm","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"feb84980-1012-4fe9-8702-72313b3d54af","name":"Hansen, Anders Peder Lysholm","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jørgen","key":"gulddahlrasmussenpedh","last":"Gulddahl Rasmussen","name":"Gulddahl Rasmussen, Jørgen","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1.","isbn":["9788771121476"],"issn":["22465804"],"pages":"115-129","place":"Aalborg","publisher":"Aalborg Universitetsforlag","series":"Studier i problembaseret læring ved videregående uddannelser","status":"p","subtitle":"En antologi om praksis i problembaseret læring","title":"Problembaseret Erhvervsøkonomi"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-9922511d-da0e-4e92-a2f9-2870b4a0c84e"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Udviklingen af en problembaseret MBA inden for de eksisterende institutionelle rammer","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-094462","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Abstract: Background:The risk of ischemic stroke/thromboembolic events after an intracranial haemorrhage (ICH) in atrial fibrillation (AF) patients on warfarin treatment is poorly characterised. The aim of this study was to assess the association between the risk of ischaemic stroke/thromboembolic events and ICH. Methods:Linkage of three Danish nationwide administrative registries in the period between 1999-2012 identified AF patients on warfarin treatment. Event rate ratios of stroke/thromboembolic events, major bleeding and all-cause mortality stratified by ICH were calculated, and Cox proportional hazard models were used to compare event rates among ICH survivors. A matched odds ratio (OR) was calculated for ICH occurrences within 0-3 months relative to 3-6 months prior to a stroke/thromboembolic event. A rate ratio of claimed warfarin prescriptions in a 3-month period pre- and post-ICH was also calculated. Results:We studied 58,815 AF patients (median age 72.6 years; 60% male). When compared to the non-ICH group, the ICH group was at increased risk for stroke/SE/TIA [Rate Ratio 3.67 (95% confidence interval [CI], 3.12 to 4.31] and mortality [5.55 (95% CI, 5.20 to 5.92)], but not for major bleeding [1.06 (95% CI, 0.81 to 1.39)]. The matched OR of ICH occurrences prior to a stroke/SE/TIA was 4.33 (95% CI, 2.44 to 8.15). The rate ratio of claimed warfarin prescriptions post and pre-ICH event was 0.28 (95% CI, 0.24 to 0.33). Conclusion:In this large-scale study of AF patients treated with warfarin, first-time ICH was associated with an increased rate of ischaemic stroke/SE/TIA and mortality compared to the non-ICH group. There was a decrease in the warfarin prescription purchase rate post-ICH period compared to pre-ICH, which may partly explain the excess risk. Background: The risk of ischemic stroke/thromboembolic events after an intracranial haemorrhage (ICH) in atrial fibrillation (AF) patients on warfarin treatment is poorly characterised. The aim of this study was to assess the association between the risk of ischaemic stroke/thromboembolic events and ICH. Methods: Linkage of three Danish nationwide administrative registries in the period between 1999-2012 identified AF patients on warfarin treatment. Event rate ratios of stroke/thromboembolic events, major bleeding and all-cause mortality stratified by ICH were calculated, and Cox proportional hazard models were used to compare event rates among ICH survivors. A matched odds ratio (OR) was calculated for ICH occurrences within 0-3 months relative to 3-6 months prior to a stroke/thromboembolic event. A rate ratio of claimed warfarin prescriptions in a 3-month period pre- and post-ICH was also calculated. Results: We studied 58,815 AF patients (median age 72.6 years; 60% male). When compared to the non-ICH group, the ICH group was at increased risk for stroke/SE/TIA [Rate Ratio 3.67 (95% confidence interval [CI], 3.12 to 4.31] and mortality [5.55 (95% CI, 5.20 to 5.92)], but not for major bleeding [1.06 (95% CI, 0.81 to 1.39)]. The matched OR of ICH occurrences prior to a stroke/SE/TIA was 4.33 (95% CI, 2.44 to 8.15). The rate ratio of claimed warfarin prescriptions post and pre-ICH event was 0.28 (95% CI, 0.24 to 0.33). Conclusion: In this large-scale study of AF patients treated with warfarin, first-time ICH was associated with an increased rate of ischaemic stroke/SE/TIA and mortality compared to the non-ICH group. There was a decrease in the warfarin prescription purchase rate post-ICH period compared to pre-ICH, which may partly explain the excess risk.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Skjøth, Flemming","Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","Lip, Gregory Y H"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-105458"],"event":{"end":"2014-09-03","place":"Barcelona, es","start":"2014-08-30","title":"ESC Congress 2014","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","City Hospital in Birmingham","University of Birmingham"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"intracranial haemorrhage and subsequent ischemic stroke in patients with atrial fibrillation what does real world registry data tell us","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://congress365.escardio.org/Session/13768#.VIbZPzGG8tN","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-105458","ids":["aau-bf27b2db-1158-4f64-9bfd-1d9d85346119"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1E851B24520299006C4C7FC7505DEA5C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://congress365.escardio.org/Session/13768#.VIbZPzGG8tN","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.escardio.org/congresses/esc-2014/Pages/welcome.aspx?hit=nav","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Medicine, Department of Clinical Medicine, Aalborg Thrombosis Research Unit"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Birmingham","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"city hospital in birmingham","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"City Hospital in Birmingham","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter Brønnum","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"3ce5c24a-cc41-4e4c-a071-9a41f036faf8","name":"Nielsen, Peter Brønnum","orcid":"0000-0003-2922-6970","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Torben Bjerregaard","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"a3c6747f-b9db-488b-8eb9-887d38742880","name":"Larsen, Torben Bjerregaard","orcid":"0000-0002-8485-8674","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Flemming","key":"skjøthpau","last":"Skjøth","locid":"6166e832-f5f5-47be-82bb-07962be7c943","name":"Skjøth, Flemming","orcid":"0000-0003-2975-647X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lars Hvilsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"20cfd847-7f3e-4c77-88c0-32d3432496ed","name":"Rasmussen, Lars Hvilsted","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","corresponding":null,"first":"Gregory Y H","key":"lippau","last":"Lip","name":"Lip, Gregory Y H","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-bf27b2db-1158-4f64-9bfd-1d9d85346119"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Intracranial haemorrhage and subsequent ischemic stroke in patients with atrial fibrillation : what does 'real world' registry data tell us","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-105458","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Surgical resection enhances long-term survival after lung cancer, but survivors face functional deficits and report on poor quality of life long time after surgery. This study evaluated short and long-term effects of supervised group exercise training on health-related quality of life and physical performance in patients, who were radically operated for lung cancer.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brocki, Barbara C.","Andreasen, Jane","Nielsen, Lene Rodkjaer","Nekrasas, Vytautas","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Westerdahl, Elisabeth"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-107524"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"short and long term effects of supervised versus unsupervised exercise training on health related quality of life and functional outcomes following lung cancer surgery a randomized controlled trial","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lungcan.2013.10.015","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-107524","identifier":[{"id":"84891738419","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000330153200017","type":"wos"},{"id":"24246508","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-c605c3ed-5ade-46a2-b98b-e66dad116ed5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC9024848DD49812120EE05919A1E813"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.lungcan.2013.10.015","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":