{"abstract":"BackgroundFibropapillomatosis (FP) is a neoplastic disease characterized by cutaneous tumours that has been documented to infect all sea turtle species. Chelonid fibropapilloma-associated herpesvirus (CFPHV) is believed to be the aetiological agent of FP, based principally on consistent PCR-based detection of herpesvirus DNA sequences from FP tumours. We used a recently described PCR-based assay that targets 3 conserved CFPHV genes, to survey 208 green turtles (Chelonia mydas). This included both FP tumour exhibiting and clinically healthy individuals. An additional 129 globally distributed clinically healthy individual sea turtles; representing four other species were also screened.ResultsCFPHV DNA sequences were obtained from 37/37 (100%) FP exhibiting green turtles, and 45/300 (15%) clinically healthy animals spanning all five species. Although the frequency of infected individuals per turtle population varied considerably, most global populations contained at least one CFPHV positive individual, with the exception of various turtle species from the Arabian Gulf, Northern Indian Ocean and Puerto Rico.Haplotype analysis of the different gene markers clustered the CFPHV DNA sequences for two of the markers (UL18 and UL22) in turtles from Turks and Caicos separate to all others, regardless of host species or geographic origin.ConclusionPresence of CFPHV DNA within globally distributed samples for all five species of sea turtle was confirmed. While 100% of the FP exhibiting green turtles yielded CFPHV sequences, surprisingly, so did 15% of the clinically healthy turtles. We hypothesize that turtle populations with zero (0%) CFPHV frequency may be attributed to possible environmental differences, diet and/or genetic resistance in these individuals. Our results provide first data on the prevalence of CFPHV among seemingly healthy turtles; a factor that may not be directly correlated to the disease incidence, but may suggest of a long-term co-evolutionary latent infection interaction between CFPHV and its turtle-host across species. Finally, computational analysis of amino acid variants within the Turks and Caicos samples suggest potential functional importance in a substitution for marker UL18 that encodes the major capsid protein gene, which potentially could explain differences in pathogenicity. Nevertheless, such a theory remains to be validated by further research.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Alfaro Nuñez, Luis Alonso","Bertelsen, Mads Frost","Bojesen, Anders Miki","Rasmussen, Isabel","Zepeda Mendoza, Marie Lisandra","Olsen, Morten Tange","Gilbert, M. Thomas P."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-508461"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Co evolution","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Fibropapillomatosis","Herpesvirus","Latency","Sea turtles"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"global distribution of chelonid fibropapilloma associated herpesvirus among clinically healthy sea turtles","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12862-014-0206-z","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-508461","identifier":[{"id":"25342462","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC4219010","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84964312882","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-c0c245fa-715c-417d-a7a0-352dfd06e6ca"],"keyword":["CFPHV","Co-evolution","Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences","Fibropapillomatosis","Herpesvirus","Latency","Sea turtles","Tunours"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-44C5675693BC6B5FCA69F8245A7DDCA4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/132046483/Global_distribution_of_Chelonid_fibropapilloma_associated_herpesvirus_among_clinically_healthy_sea_turtles.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1186/s12862-014-0206-z","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, The Natural History Museum, Natural History Museum of Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Luis Alonso","key":"alfaronuñezpau","last":"Alfaro Nuñez","locid":"00c0da84-6d66-4701-a6c3-927b6783dc11","name":"Alfaro Nuñez, Luis Alonso","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mads Frost","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"37d31086-f61f-47da-814e-5351f7b1af6d","name":"Bertelsen, Mads Frost","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Miki","key":"bojesenpau","last":"Bojesen","locid":"404f5838-4d57-4c72-809d-ba35461a74e8","name":"Bojesen, Anders Miki","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Isabel","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Isabel","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Marie Lisandra","key":"zepedamendozapau","last":"Zepeda Mendoza","locid":"75a07311-3ea4-4d54-bffb-0d5795e69d8c","name":"Zepeda Mendoza, Marie Lisandra","orcid":"0000-0002-1126-8219","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten Tange","key":"olsenpau","last":"Olsen","locid":"203c401b-0cc9-418f-bdfb-4bb555154ec1","name":"Olsen, Morten Tange","orcid":"0000-0001-6716-6345","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"M. Thomas P.","key":"gilbertpau","last":"Gilbert","locid":"58c97189-c7e9-4486-afb1-e7669608599e","name":"Gilbert, M. Thomas P.","orcid":"0000-0002-5805-7195","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["25342462"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1186/s12862-014-0206-z","issn":["14712148"],"journal":"BMC Evolutionary Biology","paperid":"206","status":"p","title":"BMC Evolutionary Biology","title_org":"B M C Evolutionary Biology","volume":"14"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84964312882"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-c0c245fa-715c-417d-a7a0-352dfd06e6ca"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Global distribution of Chelonid fibropapilloma-associated herpesvirus among clinically healthy sea turtles","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-508461","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"Working from previously unknown sources in Danish archives, this article establishes for the first time the important role that the island of St. Croix played in the Lincoln Administration’s considerations on colonizing African Americans abroad. The paper argues that U.S. Secretary of State William H. Seward, commonly viewed as an anti-colonizationist, was at least a mild proponent of colonization in its earliest stages. The paper demonstrates further that in the summer of 1862 the St. Croix colonization project was an important stepping stone in the Lincoln administration’s legal justification for emancipation, and that it was recognized as such by high-ranking Confederates. The negotiations failed for reasons that had little to do with Lincoln or his opinion on the matter. Rather, the plan fell through because the Danes slowly turned against it for economic and political reasons. The substantial conclusion of the paper is that, contrary to earlier perceptions in the historiography, African American colonization during the Civil War was not led and directed entirely from Washington. Rather, in this case, the Danish minister proposed a colonization plan and then worked with the United States government to attempt to see it through","author_count":2,"contributors":["J. Douma, Michael","Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-627964"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["African American colonization","Denmark","Emancipation","St Croix"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the danish st croix project revisiting the lincoln colonization program with foreign language sources","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14664658.2014.964916","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-627964","identifier":[{"id":"84923281874","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-bf02d6ee-c692-42c8-8a95-28d9190bf47f"],"keyword":["Abraham Lincoln","African American colonization;","Denmark","Emancipation","St Croix","St. Croix; Denmark","William H. Seward"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4B84B337AAAFFDA65D5C9935A0B692CC"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1080/14664658.2014.964916","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["University of Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"jdoumapau","last":"J. Douma","name":"J. Douma, Michael","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f284f3a3-297f-4882-81e1-b591c41ead80","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9817-9595","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1080/14664658.2014.964916","issn":["14664658","17437903"],"issn_org":["14664658"],"issue":"3","journal":"American Nineteenth Century History","pages":"311-342","publisher":"Routledge","status":"p","title":"American Nineteenth Century History","volume":"15"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84923281874"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-bf02d6ee-c692-42c8-8a95-28d9190bf47f"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"The Danish St. Croix Project : Revisiting the Lincoln Colonization Program with Foreign-Language Sources","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-627964","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
