lity and the Origin of Time","status":"p","title":"Mediating and Remediating Death"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-6e3d820a-c9df-428c-908c-721805934653"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Infinity in a Spear : Things as Mediations among the Mbuke (Papua New Guinea)","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-192235","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"author_count":2,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Moe"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-228665"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"håb","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-228665","ids":["au-ae2f0774-40e5-4a59-9501-937e528b0ea5"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3C2545911D64D2907887289C5B558098"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Culture and Society, School of Culture and Society - Philosophy, subject"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Moe","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"e9773c7c-a46d-4591-b659-4151bea40a43","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Moe","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hans- Jørgen","key":"schanzpedh","last":"Schanz","name":"Schanz, Hans- Jørgen","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"edition":"1","isbn":["9788771240993"],"pages":"79-83","place":"Aarhus","publisher":"Aarhus Universitetsforlag","status":"p","title":"50 ideer der ændrede verden","volume":"1"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-ae2f0774-40e5-4a59-9501-937e528b0ea5"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Håb","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-228665","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we propose a scheme for reducing the energy consumption of optical links by means of adaptive forward error correction (FEC). The scheme works by performing on the fly adjustments to the code rate of the FEC, adding extra parity bits to the data stream whenever extra capacity is available. We show that this additional parity information decreases the number of necessary decoding iterations and thus reduces the power consumption in iterative decoders during periods of low load. The code rate adjustments can be done on a frame-by-frame basis and thus make it possible to manipulate the balance between effective data rate and FEC coding gain without any disruption to the live traffic. As a consequence, these automatic adjustments can be performed very often based on the current traffic demand and bit error rate performance of the links through the network. The FEC scheme itself is designed to work as a transparent add-on to transceivers running the optical transport network (OTN) protocol, adding an extra layer of elastic soft-decision FEC to the built-in hard-decision FEC implemented in OTN, while retaining interoperability with existing OTN equipment. In order to facilitate dynamic code rate adaptation, we propose a programmable encoder and decoder design approach, which can implement various codes depending on the desired code rate using the same basic circuitry. This design ensures optimal coding gain performance with a modest overhead for supporting multiple codes with minimal impact on the area and power requirements of the decoder.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders","Yankov, Metodi Plamenov","Berger, Michael Stübert","Larsen, Knud J.","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337504"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Bit error rate","Bit error rate BER performance","Codes symbols","Communication Networking and Broadcast Technologies","Computer","Convolutional codes","Decoding","Elastic optical networks","Encoding","Energy efficiency","Energy utilization","Forward error correction","Iterative decoding","OPTICS","Optical fiber communication","Optical transport networks","Photonics and Electrooptics","Signal systems","Switching circuits","Telecommunications"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"improved energy efficiency for optical transport networks by elastic forward error correction","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1364/JOCN.6.000397","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-337504","identifier":[{"id":"84901944522","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6e34a343-8d04-4926-a899-d92feb029554"],"keyword":["Adaptive forward error correction","Automatic adjustment","Bit error rate","Bit error rate (BER) performance","COMPUTER","CONVOLUTIONAL-CODES","Codes (symbols)","Communication, Networking and Broadcast Technologies","Decoding","Elastic optical networks","Encoding","Energy efficiency","Energy utilization","FIBER TRANSMISSION-SYSTEMS","Forward error correction","Frame-by-frame basis","Iterative decoding","OPTICS","Optical fiber communication","Optical transport networks","Optically switched networks","Parity information","Photonics and Electrooptics","Rate adaptive forward error correction","Signal systems","Switched networks","Switching circuits","TELECOMMUNICATIONS"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-840CE8D3446CB0795BDD626B1B1A07CB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1364/JOCN.6.000397","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87986f01-324c-411f-b6e1-968b73835d8d","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Metodi Plamenov","key":"yankovpau","last":"Yankov","locid":"de50ac7c-fdfe-499a-812a-79c5d429a9a6","name":"Yankov, Metodi Plamenov","orcid":"0000-0003-0682-7001","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud J.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9135c2bf-9882-4f7c-95dc-66c9609d836a","name":"Larsen, Knud J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2367-6383","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1364/jocn.6.000397","issn":["19430620","19430639"],"issn_org":["19430620"],"issue":"4","journal":"Journal of Optical Communications and Networking","pages":"397-407","publisher":"Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers Inc.","status":"p","title":"Journal of Optical Communications and Networking","volume":"6"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84901944522"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-6e34a343-8d04-4926-a899-d92feb029554"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Improved Energy Efficiency for Optical Transport Networks by Elastic Forward Error Correction","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-337504","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"The turbulence and flows at the plasma edge during the L-I-H, L-I-L and single-step L-H transitions have been measured directly using two reciprocating Langmuir probe systems at the outer midplane with several newly designed probe arrays in the EAST superconducting tokamak. The E × B velocity, turbulence level and turbulent Reynolds stress at ~1 cm inside the separatrix ramp-up in the last ~20 ms preceding the single-step L-H transition, but remain nearly constant near the separatrix, indicating an increase in the radial gradients at the plasma edge. The kinetic energy transfer rate from the edge turbulence to the E × B flows is significantly enhanced only in the last ~10 ms and peaks just prior to the L-H transition. The E × B velocity measured inside the separatrix, which is typically in the electron diamagnetic drift direction in the L-mode, decays towards the ion diamagnetic drift direction in response to fluctuation suppression at the onset of the single-step L-H, L-I-L as well as L-I-H transitions. One important distinction between the L-I-H and the L-I-L transitions has been observed, with respect to the evolution of the edge pressure gradient and mean E × B flow during the I-phase. Both of them ramp up gradually during the L-I-H transition, but change little during the L-I-L transition, which may indicate that a gradual buildup of the edge pedestal and mean E × B flow during the I-phase leads to the final transition into the H-mode. In addition, the transition data in EAST strongly suggest that the divertor pumping capability is an important ingredient in determining the transition behaviour and power threshold.","author_count":30,"contributors":["Xu, G. S.","Wang, H. Q.","Xu, M.","Wan, B. N.","Guo, H. Y.","Diamond, P. H.","Tynan, G. R.","Chen, R.","Yan, Ning","Kong, D. F.","Zhao, H. L.","Liu, A. D.","Lan, T.","Naulin, Volker","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Miki, K.","Manz, P.","Zhang, W.","Wang, L.","Shao, L. M.","Liu, S. C.","Chen, Leifeng","Ding, S. Y.","Zhao, N.","Li, Y. L.","Liu, Y. L.","Hu, G. H.","Wu, X. Q.","Gong, X. Z."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-337538"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["China","Germany","Japan","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Japan Atomic Energy Agency","Max Planck Institute","Southwestern Institute of Physics","University of California at San Diego","University of Science and Technology of China"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"dynamics of l h transition and i phase in east","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0029-5515/54/10/103002","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-337538","identifier":[{"id":"84907937842","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-6e58c262-31a4-46f6-8633-3264d0e0c86b"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4E26F0B20EEA22039197AC6650E8FA6F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0029-5515/54/10/103002","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"southwestern institute of physics","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Southwestern Institute of Physics","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"us","key":"university of california at san diego","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of California at San Diego","