{"abstract":"Alcoholic hepatitis (AH) has a severe prognosis due to hepatic inflammatory injury. The cytokine interleukin-22 (IL-22) is reported to exert anti-apoptotic and proliferative effects, but IL-22 has not been studied during the course of AH. IL-22 is mainly produced by CD4(+) (helper) T cells, including Th17 cells. In addition, Th17 cells produce the proinflammatory cytokine IL-17A, which has been implicated in AH.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Støy, Sidsel","Sandahl, Thomas Damgaard","Dige, Anders","Agnholt, Jørgen","Rasmussen, Tue Kruse","Grønbæk, Henning","Deleuran, Bent","Vilstrup, Hendrik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-159888"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antigens CD4","Antigens CD45","Female","Hepatitis Alcoholic","Humans","Interleukin 17","Interleukin 23","Interleukins","Male","Middle Aged","T Lymphocytes Helper Inducer"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"highest frequencies of interleukin 000000000022 producing t helper cells in alcoholic hepatitis patients with a favourable short term course","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1371/journal.pone.0055101","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-159888","identifier":[{"id":"84872849622","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3555927","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"23372820","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-3576f902-cf4d-4961-bedc-3350256d864a"],"keyword":["Adult","Aged","Antigens, CD4","Antigens, CD45","Female","Hepatitis, Alcoholic","Humans","Interleukin-17","Interleukin-23","Interleukins","Male","Middle Aged","T-Lymphocytes, Helper-Inducer"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AF605B7FDC15D