{"abstract":"In this paper we present a first principle global two-dimensional fluid model. The HESEL (Hot Edge SOL Electrostatic) model is a 2D numerical fluid code, based on interchange dynamics and includes besides electron also the ion pressure dynamic. In the limit of cold ions the model almost reduces to the so-called ESEL model, which has successfully modeled profiles in JET [1], and profiles and fluctuations in MAST [2], EAST [3] and TCV [4]. It is a four-field Braginskii model including generalized vorticity, density, electron and ion pressure equations. The generalized vorticity consist of an ExB vorticity as well as the ion diamagnetic vorticity. The 2D domain includes both open and closed field lines and is located on the out-board midplane of a tokamak. On open field field lines the parallel dynamics are parametrized as sink terms depending on the dynamic quantities; density, electron and ion pressures and generalized vorticity.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Nielsen, Anders Henry","Madsen, Jens","Xu, G. S.","Naulin, Volker","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Yan, Ning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-365559"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-05","place":"Espoo, fi","start":"2013-07-01","title":"40th European Physical Society Conference on Plasma Physics","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"000000000002d fluid simulations of interchange turbulence with ion dynamics","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84905658531","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-365559","identifier":[{"id":"84905658531","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-cc49098c-4b20-42f9-84c5-36e741046bff"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1258C2895FFBAC961AB68FE7F3683B35"],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenpau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G. S.","key":"xupau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, G. S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"juulrasmussenpau","last":"Juul Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Juul Rasmussen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ning","key":"yanpau","last":"Yan","locid":"dfb24816-8d8b-4f0b-98e4-b357080e74a9","name":"Yan, Ning","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["03782271"],"journal":"Europhysics Conference Abstracts","paperid":"P5.173","publisher":"European Physical Society","status":"p","title":"Europhysics Conference Abstracts","volume":"37D"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-cc49098c-4b20-42f9-84c5-36e741046bff"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"2D fluid simulations of interchange turbulence with ion dynamics","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-365559","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Denne rapport er en midtvejsrapport i en længerevarende evaluering af Landsbyggefondens 2006-10-pulje. Landsbyggefonden har i perioden mellem 2006 og 2010 uddelt 2,2 mia. kr. til boligsociale indsatser og huslejestøtte i udsatte boligområder. Formålet er at vende og modvirke en negativ udvikling i områderne. Rapporten består af en effektevaluering af de foreløbige effekter af at de indsatser, der er finansieret af puljen, og en procesevaluering, som har fokus på organisering og samarbejde i det boligsociale arbejde.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Aner, Louise Glerup","Kirkedal, Ian","Lunde Rasmussen, Christine","Høst, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-387113"],"filters":{"added":"2023-02","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Socialt udsatte"],"level":"sci","oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-UC"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-RAM"],"UC":["DI-UC-ALL","DI-UC-KP"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-RAM","DI-UC-KP"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"boligsociale indsatser og huslejestøtte midtvejsevaluering af landsbyggefondens 000000002006 000000002010 pulje","src":["kp"],"src-code":["DI-UC-KP"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.sfi.dk/rapportoplysninger-4681.aspx?Action=1&NewsId=4167&PID=9267","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-387113","ids":["kp-401b7ed0-e3c1-4cbd-ae95-72995fe179e3"],"keyword":["socialt udsatte"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","noi":["Local-1-1-7307D6A5E550A1FB31A57BD14E6E5E02"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"kp university college copenhagen","l2":"DI-UC","l2n":"University Colleges","l3":"DI-UC-KP","l3nl":"KP","l3nn":"KP University College Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KP University College Copenhagen","namevar":["Professionshøjskolen Metropol (ophørt), Socialrådgiveruddannelserne (ophørt)"],"nora_code":"DI-UC-KP","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ramboll group","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-RAM","l3nl":"Rambøll Group","l3nn":"Ramboll Group","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Ramboll Group","namevar":["Attractor, Rambøl"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-RAM","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Louise Glerup","key":"anerpau","last":"Aner","locid":"5ef477af-dd3c-4a06-bc52-6d62858dc78f","name":"Aner, Louise Glerup","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Ian","key":"kirkedalpau","last":"Kirkedal","name":"Kirkedal, Ian","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Christine","key":"lunderasmussenpau","last":"Lunde Rasmussen","name":"Lunde Rasmussen, Christine","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"høstpau","last":"Høst","name":"Høst, Anders","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"220","publisher":"Det Nationale Forskningscenter for Velfærd","status":"p","volume":"13:41"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All University Colleges","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-UC","DI-UC-ALL","KP","Private Research","Rambøll Group","University Colleges"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["kp-401b7ed0-e3c1-4cbd-ae95-72995fe179e3"],"src":["KP University College Copenhagen"],"title":"Boligsociale indsatser og huslejestøtte : Midtvejsevaluering af Landsbyggefondens 2006-2010-pulje","type":"Report","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-387113","year":"2013","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"BACKGROUND:Post-transcriptional regulation of gene expression by small RNAs and RNA binding proteins is of fundamental importance in development of complex organisms, and dysregulation of regulatory RNAs can influence onset, progression and potentially be target for treatment of many diseases. Post-transcriptional regulation by small RNAs is mediated through partial complementary binding to messenger RNAs leaving nucleotide signatures or motifs throughout the entire transcriptome. Computational methods for discovery and analysis of sequence motifs in high-throughput mRNA expression profiling experiments are becoming increasingly important tools for the identification of post-transcriptional regulatory motifs and the inference of the regulators and their targets. RESULTS:cWords is a method designed for regulatory motif discovery in differential case-control mRNA expression datasets. We have improved the algorithms and statistical methods of cWords, resulting in at least a factor 100 speed gain over the previous implementation. On a benchmark dataset of 19 microRNA (miRNA) perturbation experiments cWords showed equal or better performance than two comparable methods, miReduce and Sylamer. We have developed rigorous motif clustering and visualization that accompany the cWords analysis for more intuitive and effective data interpretation. To demonstrate the versatility of cWords we show that it can also be used for identification of potential siRNA off-target binding. Moreover, cWords analysis of an experiment profiling mRNAs bound by Argonaute ribonucleoprotein particles discovered endogenous miRNA binding motifs. CONCLUSIONS:cWords is an unbiased, flexible and easy-to-use tool designed for regulatory motif discovery in differential case-control mRNA expression datasets. cWords is based on rigorous statistical methods that demonstrate comparable or better performance than other existing methods. Rich visualization of results promotes intuitive and efficient interpretation of data. cWords is available as a stand-alone Open Source program at Github https://github.com/simras/cWords webcite and as a web-service at: http://servers.binf.ku.dk/cwords/ webcite.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","Jacobsen, Anders","Krogh, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-403756"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cwords systematic microrna regulatory motif discovery from mrna expression data","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.silencejournal.com/content/4/1/2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-403756","identifier":[{"id":"84877849011","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-11696616-ec7d-467b-90a3-2c4b77aeaf32"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5AD58E413B246AA7A878858855E4700A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.silencejournal.com/content/4/1/2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"memorial sloan kettering cancer center","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Memorial Sloan-Kettering Cancer Center","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Simon Horskjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1d3d8554-8895-4ff5-b6f2-8cd7aa419374","name":"Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Anders","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Anders","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"109cd77e-27eb-47b9-997f-eab877a0f429","name":"Krogh, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5147-6282","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"issn":["1758907X"],"issue":"2","journal":"Silence","status":"p","title":"Silence","volume":"4"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84877849011"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-11696616-ec7d-467b-90a3-2c4b77aeaf32"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"cWords - systematic microRNA regulatory motif discovery from mRNA expression data","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-403756","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
