{"abstract":"We show how a bird’s-eye view of genomic structure can be obtained at ∼1-kb resolution from long (∼2 Mb) DNA molecules extracted from whole chromosomes in a nanofluidic laboratoryon-a-chip. We use an improved single-molecule denaturation mapping approach to detect repetitive elements and known as well as unique structural variation. Following its mapping, a molecule of interest was rescued fromthe chip;amplified and localized to a chromosome by FISH; and interrogated down to 1-bp resolution with a commercial sequencer, thereby reconciling haplotype-phased chromosome substructure with sequence.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Marie, Rodolphe","Pedersen, Jonas Nyvold","L. V. Bauer, David","Rasmussen, Kristian Hagsted","Yusuf, Mohammed","Volpi, Emanuela","Flyvbjerg, Henrik","Kristensen, Anders","U. Mirb, Kalim"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-347703"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"keyword":["Biological sciences","Genetics","Physical Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated view of genome structure and sequence of a single dna molecule in a nanofluidic device","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1214570110","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-347703","identifier":[{"id":"23479649","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84875493834","type":"scopus"},{"id":"PMC3612670","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["dtu-90a2551e-548b-4a13-b251-dffb4d1ea1b1"],"keyword":["Applied Physical Sciences","Biological Sciences","Genetics","Physical Sciences"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-019B8A8B8F7BFB8BA141F30EB2704558"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1214570110","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, Optofluidics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Rodolphe","key":"mariepau","last":"Marie","locid":"0e01d976-5d97-42d2-9b08-d7a8f8fb48f7","name":"Marie, Rodolphe","orcid":"0000-0002-8338-1990","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas Nyvold","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bafd597a-c1ed-4c65-b484-741359d87d7f","name":"Pedersen, Jonas Nyvold","orcid":"0000-0001-7642-8212","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"David","key":"lvbauerpau","last":"L. V. Bauer","name":"L. V. Bauer, David","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kristian Hagsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f8079726-bd61-4d72-801c-f70ecafc96b3","name":"Rasmussen, Kristian Hagsted","orcid":"0000-0002-3662-2069","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Mohammed","key":"yusufpau","last":"Yusuf","name":"Yusuf, Mohammed","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Emanuela","key":"volpipau","last":"Volpi","name":"Volpi, Emanuela","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik","key":"flyvbjergpau","last":"Flyvbjerg","locid":"98ce7eab-dc93-40f3-8bcd-76ea8772f11a","name":"Flyvbjerg, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0002-1691-9367","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3c79a020-2c73-4e30-ac42-aee3ff272bcd","name":"Kristensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9567-1656","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalim","key":"umirbpau","last":"U. Mirb","name":"U. Mirb, Kalim","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23479649"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1073/pnas.1214570110","issn":["00278424","10916490"],"issn_org":["00278424"],"issue":"13","journal":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","pages":"4893-4898","publisher":"National Academy of Sciences","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the National Academy of Sciences of the United States of America","volume":"110"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84875493834"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-90a2551e-548b-4a13-b251-dffb4d1ea1b1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Integrated view of genome structure and sequence of a single DNA molecule in a nanofluidic device","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-347703","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The development of high-throughput sequencing technologies has revolutionized the way we study genomes and gene regulation. In a single experiment, millions of reads are produced. To gain knowledge from these experiments the first thing to be done is finding the genomic origin of the reads, i.e., mapping the reads to a reference genome. In this new situation, conventional alignment tools are obsolete, as they cannot handle this huge amount of data in a reasonable amount of time. Thus, new mapping algorithms have been developed, which are fast at the expense of a small decrease in accuracy. In this chapter we discuss the current problems in short read mapping and show that mapping reads correctly is a nontrivial task. Through simple experiments with both real and synthetic data, we demonstrate that different mappers can give different results depending on the type of data, and that a considerable fraction of uniquely mapped reads is potentially mapped to an incorrect location. Furthermore, we provide simple statistical results on the expected number of random matches in a genome (E-value) and the probability of a random match as a function of read length. Finally, we show that quality scores contain valuable information for mapping and why mapping quality should be evaluated in a probabilistic manner. In the end, we discuss the potential of improving the performance of current methods by considering these quality scores in a probabilistic mapping program.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Menzel, Peter","Frellsen, Jes","Plass, Mireya","Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","Krogh, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-435065"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"on the accuracy of short read mapping","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-62703-514-9_3","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-435065","identifier":[{"id":"84881104632","type":"scopus"},{"id":"23872968","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-45c0618e-44fa-43de-893e-dcdbdfd28d02"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5DEF00244B62C26BE940FA046734CC8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-62703-514-9_3","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Computational and RNA Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Karl Peter","key":"menzelpau","last":"Menzel","locid":"04848519-0676-4ab8-a076-608eb130ec3f","name":"Menzel, Peter","name_org":"Menzel, Karl Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jes","key":"frellsenpau","last":"Frellsen","locid":"43667347-08f0-4828-87db-bf26f6de01ab","name":"Frellsen, Jes","orcid":"0000-0001-9224-1271","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Mireya","key":"plasspau","last":"Plass","locid":"0910ed7c-2582-4dd4-ab89-7f14e6dcd7ed","name":"Plass, Mireya","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Simon Horskjær","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"1d3d8554-8895-4ff5-b6f2-8cd7aa419374","name":"Rasmussen, Simon Horskjær","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"109cd77e-27eb-47b9-997f-eab877a0f429","name":"Krogh, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5147-6282","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Noam","key":"shomronpedh","last":"Shomron"