{"abstract":"Background In colorectal cancer MLH1 deficiency causes microsatellite instability, which is relevant for the patient's prognosis and treatment, and its putative heredity. Dysfunction of MLH1 is caused by sporadic gene promoter hypermethylation or by hereditary mutations as seen in Lynch Syndrome. The aim of this study was to determine in detail how DNA methylation regulates MLH1 expression and impacts clinical management. Methods Colorectal cancer samples were collected from 210 patients. The laboratory methods used to study these samples included methylation specific multiplex ligation-dependent probe amplification (MS-MLPA), real-time quantitative PCR (qPCR), and immunohistochemistry (IHC). Results We found that the MLH1 mRNA and protein expression levels were highly related. MS-MLPA was successful in tumors from 195 patients. In these tumors, hypermethylation was observed in promoter regions A (n =57), B (n =30), C (n =28), and D (n =47), and in intron 1 (n =25). The promoter region C and intron 1 methylation levels were found to be excellently suited for discriminating between low and high gene expression levels, whereas those of promoter regions A, B and D were less specific. Hypermethylation in any region (n =77) served as an independent prognostic factor (hazard ratio 0.56, 95 % confidence interval 0.36-0.89, p =0.01). Conclusions MLH1 inactivation through hypermethylation was found to be related to improved survival. Hypermethylation in promoter region C and intron 1 served as the most specific markers for this inactivation.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Jensen, Lars Henrik","Rasmussen, Anders Aamann","Byriel, Lene","Kuramochi, Hidekazu","Crüger, Dorthe Gylling","Lindebjerg, Jan","Danenberg, Peter V","Jakobsen, Anders","Danenberg, Kathleen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-573682"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Colorectal cancer","Gene expression","MLH1","Mismatch repair","Promoter hypermethylation","qPCR"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"regulation of mlh000000000001 mrna and protein expression by promoter methylation in primary colorectal cancer a descriptive and prognostic cancer marker study","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13402-013-0148-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-573682","identifier":[{"id":"84892694027","type":"scopus"},{"id":"24027018","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["sdu-0181d977-077b-4b09-9136-b5fe19ee8bf0"],"keyword":["Colorectal cancer","Gene expression","MLH1","Methylation specificMLPA","Mismatch repair","Promoter hypermethylation","QPCR"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1C4FE028EFAAC2545B87AF43633239D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s13402-013-0148-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Oncology (Vejle)","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, Vejle Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lars Henrik","key":"jensenlarshenrikpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"5b427622-91b5-4f6e-b14f-2945da9dad8c","name":"Jensen, Lars Henrik","orcid":"0000-000