{"abstract":"Serotonin (5-HT) is one of the main transmitters in the nervous system. Serotonergic neurons in the raphe nuclei in the brainstem innervate most parts of the central nervous system including motoneurons in the spinal cord and brainstem. This review will focus on the modulatory role that 5-HT exerts on motoneurons and its physiological consequences. The somato-dendritic compartments of motoneurons are densely innervated by serotonergic synaptic boutons and several receptors are expressed in the membrane of motoneurons including 5-HT1A, 5-HT1B, 5-HT1D, 5-HT2A, 5-HT2B, 5-HT2C and 5-HT5A. The activation of serotonergic receptors induces a general increase of the excitability of motoneurons through the modulation of several classes of ion channels. 5-HT depolarizes motoneurons towards the threshold for action potentials by inhibiting leak conductances and promoting a hyperpolarization activated cationic current. At the same time, 5-HT increases the firing frequency by inhibiting the small Ca2+ activated K+ conductance (SK) responsible for the medium afterhyperpolarization (AHP) following action potentials. 5-HT also promotes persistent inward currents mediated by voltage sensitive Ca2+ and Na+ conductances, producing a sustained depolarization and an amplification of synaptic inputs. Under pathological conditions, such as after a spinal cord injury, the promotion of persistent inward currents by serotonin and/or the overexpression of autoactive serotonergic receptors may contribute to motoneuronal excitability, muscle spasms and spasticity and hence, impairment of stereotyped motor behaviors such as locomotion, ejaculation and micturition.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Perrier, Jean-Francois Marie","Rasmussen, Hanne Borger","Christensen, Rasmus Kordt","Petersen, Anders Victor"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-518655"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Action Potentials","Animals","Humans","Motor Neurons","Raphe Nuclei","Receptors Serotonin","Serotonin","Species Specificity","Spinal Cord Injuries"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"modulation of the intrinsic properties of motoneurons by serotonin","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-518655","identifier":[{"id":"23360270","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84878639761","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-d186d87f-9792-4aab-8ea0-9aef6c04be30"],"keyword":["Action Potentials","Animals","Humans","Motor Neurons","Raphe Nuclei","Receptors, Serotonin","Serotonin","Species Specificity","Spinal Cord Injuries"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-47A3AABBAC9C42F9BE0F6B6149532429"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Neuroscience, Neuronal Signalling"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Jean-François","key":"perrierpau","last":"Perrier","locid":"71b8f851-db1f-4222-89be-5a20d8ac9c1c","name":"Perrier, Jean-Francois Marie","name_org":"Perrier, Jean-François","orcid":"0000-0002-9189-3574","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Hanne Borger","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"705ed7ec-50a9-4399-a21e-8c54e8e13b30","name":"Rasmussen, Hanne Borger","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Rasmus Kordt","key":"christensenpau","last":"Christensen","locid":"be8f610a-1a4d-459a-843c-69cfe5b92519","name":"Christensen, Rasmus Kordt","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Victor","key":"petersenpau","last":"Petersen","locid":"567799a9-aaef-4a71-a998-f766c955426f","name":"Petersen, Anders Victor","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["23360270"],"pub":{"doi":"10.2174/13816128113199990341","issn":["13816128","18734286"],"issn_org":["13816128"],"issue":"24","journal":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","pages":"4371-84","status":"p","title":"Current Pharmaceutical Design","volume":"19"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84878639761"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d186d87f-9792-4aab-8ea0-9aef6c04be30"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Modulation of the intrinsic properties of motoneurons by serotonin","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-518655","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Colloidal and interfacial phenomena lie at the core of drug formulation, drug delivery, as well as drug binding and action at diseased sites, e.g., in cancer therapy. We review a class of liposome-based drug-delivery systems whose design and functional properties are intimately controlled by the stability of sub-micron structures, lipid-bilayer interfaces, and interfacially activated enzymes that can be exploited to target and deliver drugs. Moreover these drugs can themselves be special lipid molecules in the form of lipid prodrugs that both form the liposomal carrier as well as the substrate for endogenously upregulated lipases that turn the prodrugs into potent drugs precisely at the diseased site.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Arouri, Ahmad","Hansen, Anders H.","Rasmussen, Thomas Elmelund","Mouritsen, Ole G."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613059"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Drug delivery","Interface","Liposome","Phospholipase","Prodrug"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"lipases liposomes and lipid prodrugs","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84882264988","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-613059","identifier":[{"id":"84882264988","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-8b00aa25-8907-4a05-9a92-f81f6d086c10"],"keyword":["Drug delivery","Interface","Liposome","Phospholipase","Prodrug"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57C5618A4E2BDE5E73477322E1C5FE83"],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ahmad","key":"arouripau","last":"Arouri","locid":"e00bba0c-7a57-49be-a6eb-276647c16711","name":"Arouri, Ahmad","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders H.","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Anders H.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Thomas Elmelund","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"59f7d825-fc42-4c32-8e5b-29542ab66bea","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Elmelund","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ole G.","key":"mouritsenpau","last":"Mouritsen","locid":"002542de-b944-4408-b94d-0b792a546682","name":"Mouritsen, Ole G.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.cocis.2013.06.001","issn":["13590294","18790399"],"issn_org":["13590294"],"issue":"5","journal":"Current Opinion in Colloid & Interface Science","pages":"419-431","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Current Opinion in Colloid & Interface Science","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84882264988"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8b00aa25-8907-4a05-9a92-f81f6d086c10"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Lipases, Liposomes and Lipid-prodrugs","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613059","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
