{"abstract":"In data sets with many more features than observations, independent screening based on all univariate regression models leads to a computationally convenient variable selection method. Recent efforts have shown that, in the case of generalized linear models, independent screening may suffice to capture all relevant features with high probability, even in ultrahigh dimension. It is unclear whether this formal sure screening property is attainable when the response is a right-censored survival time. We propose a computationally very efficient independent screening method for survival data which can be viewed as the natural survival equivalent of correlation screening. We state conditions under which the method admits the sure screening property within a class of single-index hazard rate models with ultrahigh dimensional features and describe the generally detrimental effect of censoring on performance. An iterative variant of the method is also described which combines screening with penalized regression to handle more complex feature covariance structures. The methodology is evaluated through simulation studies and through application to a real gene expression data set.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Scheike, Thomas"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007838"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Survival data","Variable selection"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Institut for Folkesundhedsvidenskab"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"independent screening for single index hazard rate models with ultrahigh dimensional features","src":["aau","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2012.01039.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007838","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000314659400002","type":"wos"},{"id":"84873282464","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-a23073f7-802a-4b79-a082-6bf793b4007b","ku-8567d447-72ee-4b96-a7fc-42b4400a0308"],"keyword":["Additive hazards model","Independent screening","Survival data","Ultrahigh dimension","Variable selection"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-F0AD8B00C17A5B0B6E10CB51574CE0C4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1467-9868.2012.01039.x","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=84873282464&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science (ENG)","Aalborg University, The Faculty of Engineering and Science, Department of Mathematical Sciences"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Health and Medical Sciences, Department of Public Health, Section of Biostatistics"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Institut for Folkesundhedsvidenskab"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders","key":"gorstrasmussenpau","last":"Gorst-Rasmussen","locid":"2aa85786-c0b1-42ec-93d4-eb7a75696409","name":"Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 3","first":"Thomas","key":"scheikepau","last":"Scheike","locid":"53de2123-e34e-44a3-945f-265fce28de25","name":"Scheike, Thomas","orcid":"0000-0002-2148-4740","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1467-9868.2012.01039.x","issn":["13697412","14679868"],"issn_org":["13697412"],"issue":"2","journal":"Journal of the Royal Statistical Society, Series B","pages":"217-245","publisher":"Oxford University Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of the Royal Statistical Society, Series B","title_org":"Journal of the Royal Statistical Society, Series B (Statistical Methodology)","volume":"75"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873282464"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-a23073f7-802a-4b79-a082-6bf793b4007b","ku-8567d447-72ee-4b96-a7fc-42b4400a0308"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Independent screening for single-index hazard rate models with ultrahigh dimensional features","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-007838","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the study is to investigate the association between gestational age, birth size, and the long-term risk of maternal diabetes. We conducted a nation-wide prospective follow-up study of the cohort of all Danish women with a singleton delivery in 1982/1983 (index delivery) and no history of diabetes (n = 100,669). Registries were used to extract information on patients with a hospital or outpatient diagnosis of diabetes, subsequent deliveries, and death/emigration in the period from the index delivery until the end of 2006. The association between the maternal risk of diabetes and the index gestational age and index offspring birth size (birth weight adjusted for gestational age) was investigated by using Cox proportional hazards regression models stratified according to young (≤33 years) and old age (>33 years). During a median follow-up period of 24 years, 2,021 women (2.0 %) were diagnosed as having diabetes. The risk of maternal diabetes was positively associated with increasing index birth size and negatively associated with increasing duration of index gestation in both age strata. Among young women, the highest hazard ratios were found for the exposure category of large index offspring birth size (adjusted HR 9.0, 95 % CI 6.17-13.12) and a preterm delivery at 32-37 weeks (adjusted HR 2.22, 95 % CI 1.46-3.40). Offspring preterm birth and large size for gestational age at birth are associated with increased risk of maternal diabetes.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Naver, Klara Vinsand","Secher, Niels Jørgen","Ovesen, Per Glud","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","Nilas, Lisbeth"],"cuid":["S03-099.36-006778"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Adult","Birth Weight","Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus Type 2","Female","Follow Up Studies","Gestational Age","Humans","Infant Newborn","Logistic Models","Population Surveillance","Pregnancy","Premature Birth","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","Registries","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Socioeconomic Factors"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-HO-CDR","DI-HO-NDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"offspring preterm birth and birth size are related to long term risk of maternal diabetes","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-013-9805-z","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-099.36-006778","identifier":[{"id":"23612744","type":"pmid"},{"id":"84879021799","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000319998000007","type":"wos"}],"ids":["aau-8bcf8795-cf4e-41d5-8dde-7fc63385bee2","au-3e18f468-8833-42e6-8003-3e7bbb04f04c","ku-cc6fbc06-3de4-43b7-8494-7c9860996757"],"keyword":["Adult","Birth Weight","Denmark","Diabetes Mellitus, Type 2","Female","Follow-Up Studies","Gestational Age","Humans","Infant, Newborn","Logistic Models","Population Surveillance","Pregnancy","Premature Birth","Proportional Hazards Models","Prospective Studies","Registries","Risk Assessment","Risk Factors","Socioeconomic Factors"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-6-C304B2312F2121163054B1E892375B53"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s10654-013-9805-z","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Medicine (MED)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"