{"abstract":"In this paper we propose a novel scheme for on the fly code rate adjustment for forward error correcting (FEC) codes on optical links. The proposed scheme makes it possible to adjust the code rate independently for each optical frame. This allows for seamless rate adaption based on the link state of the optical light path and the required amount of throughput going towards the destination node. The result is a dynamic FEC, which can be used to optimize the connections for throughput and/or energy efficiency, depending on the current demand.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders","Ruepp, Sarah Renée","Berger, Michael Stübert","Larsen, Knud J."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-311965"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-11","place":"Taipei, tw","start":"2013-07-08","title":"14th IEEE International Conference on High Performance Switching and Routing (HPSR 2013)","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"adaptive forward error correction for energy efficient optical transport networks","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/HPSR.2013.6602316","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-311965","identifier":[{"id":"84889074962","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-18903bce-9f13-471e-9cc2-75c1502b4cb7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-3F6EA79A27176CB63A292E62D36B1087"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/HPSR.2013.6602316","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87986f01-324c-411f-b6e1-968b73835d8d","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud J.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9135c2bf-9882-4f7c-95dc-66c9609d836a","name":"Larsen, Knud J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2367-6383","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/hpsr.2013.6602316","isbn":["9781467346207"],"pages":"215-216","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2013 IEEE 14th International Conference on High Performance Switching and Routing (HPSR)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84889074962"],"sdg":["7. Affordable and Clean Energy","All UN SDG Classification"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-18903bce-9f13-471e-9cc2-75c1502b4cb7"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Adaptive Forward Error Correction for Energy Efficient Optical Transport Networks","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-311965","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We build a forward error correction (FEC) module and implement it in an optical signal processing experiment. The experiment consists of two cascaded nonlinear optical signal processes, 160 Gbit/s all optical wavelength conversion based on the cross phase modulation (XPM) in a silicon nanowire and subsequent 160 Gbit/s-to-10 Gbit/s demultiplexing in a highly nonlinear fiber (HNLF). The XPM based all optical wavelength conversion in silicon is achieved by off-center filtering the red shifted sideband on the CW probe. We thoroughly demonstrate and verify that the FEC code operates correctly after the optical signal processing, yielding truly error-free 150 Gbit/s (excl. overhead) optically signal processed data after the two cascaded nonlinear processes. © 2013 Optical Society of America.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Hu, Hao","Andersen, Jakob Dahl","Rasmussen, Anders","Sørensen, Brian Michael","Dalgaard, Kjeld","Galili, Michael","Pu, Minhao","Yvind, Kresten","Larsen, Knud J.","Forchhammer, Søren","Oxenløwe, Leif Katsuo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-319542"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"forward error correction supported 000000000150 gbit s error free wavelength conversion based on cross phase modulation in silicon","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53118335/oe_21_3_3152.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-319542","identifier":[{"id":"84874044255","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-3253beb5-e536-426f-ae19-fd5ba2751379"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-C9414AE4531B8B3202E2CE34673F3D43"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1364/OE.21.003152","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/53118335/oe_21_3_3152.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Realised","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Ultra-fast Optical Communication"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Hao","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","locid":"ac686760-c537-4304-a9e0-57398f5ebd5f","name":"Hu, Hao","orcid":"0000-0002-8859-0986","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jakob Dahl","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","locid":"7c26b9d5-07b2-444c-816c-c8f46fbb067c","name":"Andersen, Jakob Dahl","orcid":"0000-0001-8097-4507","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87986f01-324c-411f-b6e1-968b73835d8d","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Brian Michael","key":"sørensenpau","last":"Sørensen","locid":"2bf7899b-6af5-4acd-b83f-5404b4b3f483","name":"Sørensen, Brian Michael","orcid":"0000-0003-2823-4549","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kjeld","key":"dalgaardpau","last":"Dalgaard","locid":"f28d3daf-b2ae-41ff-a4d0-243a6f8f28d7","name":"Dalgaard, Kjeld","orcid":"0000-0001-8682-3435","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael","key":"galilipau","last":"Galili","locid":"b8ca0448-17ae-4db3-b1bb-5ad05978a513","name":"Galili, Michael","orcid":"0000-0002-3514-8510","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Minhao","key":"pupau","last":"Pu","locid":"a784ff99-0987-43a2-9cd9-6ae78b1079d0","name":"Pu, Minhao","orcid":"0000-0002-4993-4299","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kresten","key":"yvindpau","last":"Yvind","locid":"9474484f-21c6-444f-8a24-71ee5f098ae3","name":"Yvind, Kresten","orcid":"0000-0001-8013-1606","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Knud J.","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"9135c2bf-9882-4f7c-95dc-66c9609d836a","name":"Larsen, Knud J.","orcid":"0000-0002-2367-6383","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"forchhammerpau","last":"Forchhammer","locid":"8c1bfb32-33c3-4746-bff9-9a6e0349c774","name":"Forchhammer, Søren","orcid":"0000-0002-6698-8870","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Leif Katsuo","key":"oxenløwepau","last":"Oxenløwe","locid":"da9a5ec7-12b0-4550-9571-68edf38a9fa1","name":"Oxenløwe, Leif Katsuo","orcid":"0000-0001-6013-3639","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1364/oe.21.003152","issn":["10944087"],"issue":"3","journal":"Optics Express","pages":"3152-3160","publisher":"Optica Publishing Group (formerly OSA)","status":"p","title":"Optics Express","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84874044255"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-3253beb5-e536-426f-ae19-fd5ba2751379"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Forward error correction supported 150 Gbit/s error-free wavelength conversion based on cross phase modulation in silicon","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-319542","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"The radial turbulent particle flux and the Reynolds stress in the scrape-off layer (SOL) of ASDEX Upgrade were investigated for two limited L-mode (low confinement) and one ELMy H-mode (high confinement) discharge. A fast reciprocating probe was used with a probe head containing five Langmuir probes. One of the probe pins was protruding radially above the other pins. The radial electric field component was derived from the difference of the floating potentials of the protruding pin and another pin nearby. The poloidal electric field component was derived from the difference of the floating potentials of two probes on the same poloidal meridian. In both cases, equal electron temperatures on all probe pins had to be assumed. Of the other pins one was biased to ion saturation (-70 V), whereas one was swept to record the current-voltage characteristic. A detailed statistical analysis of the plasma conditions in L- and H-modes and, more specifically, also during and in between type-I edge-localized mode (ELM) events is presented. We found evidence for similarities in the statistics of transport in L-mode, during ELM events and in between ELMs, suggesting that in all three cases the transport is undertaken by blobs and filamentary structures, respectively. During the intervals in between ELMs the blob structures appear to be relatively smaller as compared with the L-mode. © 2013 IAEA, Vienna.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Ionita, C.","Naulin, Volker","Mehlmann, F.","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Müller, H.W.","Schrittwieser, R.","Rohde, V.","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Maszl, Ch.","Balan, P.","Herrmann, A."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-325154"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Max Planck Institute","University of Innsbruck"],"keyword":["Electric fields","Plasmas","Probes","Reynolds number","Sols"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"radial transport in the far scrape off layer of asdex upgrade during l mode and elmy h mode","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0029-5515/53/4/043021","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-325154","identifier":[{"id":"84876137770","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-452a9a6b-6e0a-4b44-985c-f908119bfdfd"],"keyword":["Electric fields","Plasmas","Probes","Reynolds number","Sols"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-F1C2FA2D5F64F89A917CB69C2D29BC61"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0029-5515/53/4/043021","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"de","key":"max planck institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Max Planck Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"C.","key":"ionitapau","last":"Ionita","name":"Ionita, C.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"F.","key":"mehlmannpau","last":"Mehlmann","name":"Mehlmann, F.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"juulrasmussenpau","last":"Juul Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Juul Rasmussen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"H.W.","key":"mullerpau","last":"Müller","name":"Müller, H.W.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"R.","key":"schrittwieserpau","last":"Schrittwieser","name":"Schrittwieser, R.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"V.","key":"rohdepau","last":"Rohde","name":"Rohde, V.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ch.","key":"maszlpau","last":"Maszl","name":"Maszl, Ch.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"P.","key":"balanpau","last":"Balan","name":"Balan, P.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"herrmannpau","last":"Herrmann","name":"Herrmann, A.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/0029-5515/53/4/043021","issn":["00295515","10185577"],"issn_org":["00295515"],"issue":"4","journal":"Nuclear Fusion","pages":"043021","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Nuclear Fusion","volume":"53"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84876137770"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-452a9a6b-6e0a-4b44-985c-f908119bfdfd"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Radial transport in the far scrape-off layer of ASDEX upgrade during L-mode and ELMy H-mode","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-325154","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"We propose a new control scheme to maintain a constant strain rate of the mid-filament diameter in a filament stretching rheometer for polymer melts. The scheme is cast as a velocity algorithm and consists of a feed-back and a feed-forward contribution. The performance of the controller is demonstrated on a commercial low density polyethylene. Several strain rates and experimental conditions are tested to demonstrate the necessity of the control parameters and the limits of both the control scheme and the experimental apparatus. When the control parameters are properly tuned, the algorithm ensures that the applied strain stays within 2% of the set point and measurements can be made up to Hencky strains of 6.5.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Román Marín, José Manuel","Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted","Javier Alvarez, Nicolas","Huang, Qian","Rasmussen, Henrik K.","Bach, Anders","Skov, Anne Ladegaard","Hassager, Ole"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-356816"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Extensional rheometry","Filament stretching rheometer","Low density polyethylene"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-U"],"level3":{"PR":["DI-PR-ALL","DI-PR-COLO"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-PR-COLO","DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a control scheme for filament stretching rheometers with application to polymer melts","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnnfm.2012.10.007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-356816","identifier":[{"id":"84873848296","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-aee4b300-c676-4048-a5b8-e882ffffe575"],"keyword":["Extensional rheometry","Feed-back and feed-forward control","Filament stretching rheometer","Low-density polyethylene"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-ABAEB0EBB7DAE310710B4504CB6B67B8"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jnnfm.2012.10.007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Chemical and Biochemical Engineering, The Danish Polymer Centre"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"coloplast","l2":"DI-PR","l2n":"Private Research","l3":"DI-PR-COLO","l3nl":"Coloplast Group","l3nn":"Coloplast","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Coloplast","namevar":["Coloplast Danmark AS"],"nora_code":"DI-PR-COLO","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"José Manuel","key":"románmarínpau","last":"Román Marín","locid":"2115fa74-5a6e-4e55-8254-8754266c5927","name":"Román Marín, José Manuel","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jakob Kjøbsted","key":"huusompau","last":"Huusom","locid":"0107490a-4116-4fac-ac2c-00ccf7ffe337","name":"Huusom, Jakob Kjøbsted","orcid":"0000-0002-1367-7235","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Nicolas","key":"javieralvarezpau","last":"Javier Alvarez","locid":"2b12628c-5a9b-45d4-8b20-1fa79611c7fc","name":"Javier Alvarez, Nicolas","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Qian","key":"huangpau","last":"Huang","locid":"435173a6-3f5e-4dbc-9245-c7fdaa5edc11","name":"Huang, Qian","orcid":"0000-0001-8777-4241","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henrik K.","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"0f7d9a9e-758e-4b0f-b344-188567ec6044","name":"Rasmussen, Henrik K.","orcid":"0000-0001-7274-2239","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"bachpau","last":"Bach","name":"Bach, Anders","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anne Ladegaard","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"adf20979-309f-41da-a6d0-9c149674f23b","name":"Skov, Anne Ladegaard","orcid":"0000-0003-1223-6638","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole","key":"hassagerpau","last":"Hassager","locid":"b3b2f7bb-1e38-4937-ba11-7f4d63f0012d","name":"Hassager, Ole","orcid":"0000-0003-2695-6791","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jnnfm.2012.10.007","issn":["03770257","18732631"],"issn_org":["03770257"],"journal":"Journal of Non-Newtonian Fluid Mechanics","pages":"14-22","publisher":"Elsevier","status":"p","title":"Journal of Non-Newtonian Fluid Mechanics","volume":"194"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84873848296"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Private Research","All Universities","Coloplast Group","DI-ALL","DI-PR","DI-PR-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Private Research","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-aee4b300-c676-4048-a5b8-e882ffffe575"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A control scheme for filament stretching rheometers with application to polymer melts","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-356816","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Classical swine fever virus (CSFV) may be highly virulent in pigs with a mortality rate close to 100%. The CSFV “Koslov strain” is known to be one of the most virulent CSFV, but so far a functional cloned cDNA of this strain has not been described. We suggest that this may be due to the error-prone nature of the RNA-dependent RNA polymerase resulting in the majority of circulating forms being non-functional. However, since any infectious virus particle should necessarily be the offspring of a functional virus, we hypothesized that it should be possible to synthesize a highly virulent form by reconstructing ancestral sequences. To test this hypothesis, we inferred sequences that correspond to ancestral nodes in a phylogenetic tree built from full-length nucleotide sequences of non-functional Koslov cDNAs and then proceeded to test the reconstructions. Specifically, we altered a non-functional cDNA by site directed mutagenesis, removing non-synonymous mutations step by step. In vitro testing of modified constructs did indeed lead to fully functional viruses with similar growth kinetics as the wild-type strain. Moreover, viruses rescued from the construct had the ancestral amino acid sequence and, when tested in pigs, were at least as virulent as the Koslov strain. The ancestral reconstruction therefore proved to give rise to a functional cDNA of the highly virulent Koslov strain. In vivo studies confirmed our methods and enabled us to identify nucleotide positions within the viral genome important for virulence.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Fahnøe, Ulrik","Pedersen, Anders Gorm","Nielsen, Jens","Höper, Dirk","Beer, Martin","Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-358205"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-11","place":"Chicago, IL, us","start":"2013-07-07","title":"SMBE 2013 – Annual Meeting of the Society for Molecular Biology and Evolution","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Germany"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"reconstructing the highly virulent classical swine fever virus strain koslov","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59741841/prod11383206077048.SMBE_abstract_Ulrik_Fahn_e_final_1_.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-358205","ids":["dtu-b385ef91-3cbc-46a3-87b8-d44185be4147"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-3D1B8971B8C57C873C4E91A312FCCCE5"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/59741841/prod11383206077048.SMBE_abstract_Ulrik_Fahn_e_final_1_.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Systems Biology, Center for Biological Sequence Analysis, Molecular Evolution","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute","Technical University of Denmark, National Veterinary Institute, Section for Virology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"de","key":"friedrich loeffler institute","loc":["Germany","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Friedrich-Loeffler-Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ulrik","key":"fahnøepau","last":"Fahnøe","locid":"409de6f2-ff5a-4623-8c2e-4bb18ee9c505","name":"Fahnøe, Ulrik","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Gorm","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"bb3513aa-fb20-46ef-ba14-9c150c929cf1","name":"Pedersen, Anders Gorm","orcid":"0000-0001-9650-8965","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jens","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"34511f38-e2d9-41d2-a82f-1044f16d784c","name":"Nielsen, Jens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Dirk","key":"höperpau","last":"Höper","name":"Höper, Dirk","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Martin","key":"beerpau","last":"Beer","name":"Beer, Martin","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Thomas Bruun","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"ac10aec0-1a8a-4f66-a5c6-2275ddf1726e","name":"Rasmussen, Thomas Bruun","orcid":"0000-0002-4241-1559","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-b385ef91-3cbc-46a3-87b8-d44185be4147"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Reconstructing the highly virulent Classical Swine Fever Virus strain Koslov","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-358205","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a new TCAM-based method for determining the Longest Prefix Match (LPM) in an IP routing table. The method is based on modifying the address encoder of the standard TCAM design to take the prefix lengths of the IP routing entries into account while performing multi-match resolution, thus allowing prefixes to be inserted in any random order. This enables full utilization of the TCAM address space while greatly simplifying the updating procedure as complex software sorting algorithms and extensive table modifications are avoided. The result is faster table updates and consequently a higher throughput of the network search engine, since the TCAM down time caused by incremental updates is eliminated. The LPM scheme is described in HDL for FPGA implementation and compared to an existing scheme for customized CAM circuits. The paper shows that the proposed scheme can process more packets per second, has less per-lookup power consumption and is easier to expand to larger routing tables than the existing implementation. The latency of the LPM operation is only log2 N clock cycles, where N is the maximum number of prefixes in the TCAM, and in a pipelined implementation the throughput of the system is one Longest Prefix Match lookup per clock cycle.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders","Kragelund, A.","Berger, Michael Stübert","Wessing, Henrik","Ruepp, Sarah Renée"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-362967"],"event":{"end":"2013-07-11","place":"Taipei, tw","start":"2013-07-08","title":"14th IEEE International Conference on High Performance Switching and Routing (HPSR 2013)","year":"2013"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tcam based high speed longest prefix matching with fast incremental table updates","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/HPSR.2013.6602288","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-362967","identifier":[{"id":"84889045496","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-c34e54e9-f7a5-4502-b8f3-52877f6d15e1"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6B44B6B58734197A0675230D1DC078F3"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1109/HPSR.2013.6602288","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Photonics Engineering, Networks Technology and Service Platforms"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"87986f01-324c-411f-b6e1-968b73835d8d","name":"Rasmussen, Anders","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"A.","key":"kragelundpau","last":"Kragelund","name":"Kragelund, A.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Stübert","key":"bergerpau","last":"Berger","locid":"7b367889-bde0-4e40-893f-0a22e4d32371","name":"Berger, Michael Stübert","orcid":"0000-0003-4575-7261","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Henrik","key":"wessingpau","last":"Wessing","locid":"9d363138-c28b-40ad-8ee3-21971269cabc","name":"Wessing, Henrik","orcid":"0000-0001-8504-8561","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah Renée","key":"ruepppau","last":"Ruepp","locid":"92dfeab4-28ff-437d-9f5d-e7d8d6a67b93","name":"Ruepp, Sarah Renée","orcid":"0000-0003-0205-5067","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1109/hpsr.2013.6602288","isbn":["9781467346207"],"pages":"43-48","publisher":"IEEE","status":"p","title":"2013 IEEE 14th International Conference on High Performance Switching and Routing (HPSR)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84889045496"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-c34e54e9-f7a5-4502-b8f3-52877f6d15e1"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"TCAM-based High Speed Longest Prefix Matching with Fast Incremental Table Updates","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-362967","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"In Ohmic heated low confinement mode (L-mode) discharges, the intermittent statistical characteristics of turbulent fluctuations have been investigated in the edge and the scrape-off layer (SOL) plasma on EAST (the experimental advanced superconducting tokamak) by fast reciprocating Langmuir probe measurements. Plasma structures (blobs and holes) are observed and found to originate together inside the edge shear layer where the skewness (S) of the ion-saturation current fluctuations is close to zero. The probability density functions of the density fluctuations in edge and SOL plasma show a well-defined parabolic relation between the S and the kurtosis (K). In edge plasma with holes, the geodesic acoustic mode (GAM) is identified with a dominant frequency fpeak ∼ 5–7 kHz both in floating potential fluctuations and ion-saturation current fluctuations. However, the GAM can only be detected in the floating potential fluctuations rather than the ion-saturation current fluctuations in the edge plasma with blobs. The ESEL (edge-SOL electrostatic) code based on interchange dynamics is used to simulate the experimental results on EAST. Reasonable agreement between the ESEL simulation and the EAST experiment is reached. Experimentally, the parallel SOL flow shows a remarkable dependence on the plasma density, which resembles the theoretical predicted Pfirsch–Schlüter flow but with a much higher magnitude at the outboard mid-plane of EAST.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Yan, Ning","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Xu, G.S.","Naulin, Volker","Rasmussen, Jens Juul","Madsen, Jens","Wang, H. Q.","Liu, S. C.","Zhang, W.","Wang, L.","Wan, B. N."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-371375"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East"],"country":["China"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"statistical characterization of turbulence in the boundary plasma of east","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0741-3335/55/11/115007","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-371375","identifier":[{"id":"84886891426","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-df673cde-75ae-4bca-a5e8-d2f79e4d100f"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-4EB94A34DD2054D200D34897F3F495AD"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1088/0741-3335/55/11/115007","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Science / Technology (SCI)"],"yearPub":"2013","yearSub":"2013"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ning","key":"yanningpau","last":"Yan","locid":"dfb24816-8d8b-4f0b-98e4-b357080e74a9","name":"Yan, Ning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Henry","key":"nielsenandershenrypau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"1d9aa958-9d84-4a3b-8300-f6fe9b0be73e","name":"Nielsen, Anders Henry","orcid":"0000-0003-3642-3905","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"G.S.","key":"xugspau","last":"Xu","name":"Xu, G.S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinvolkerpau","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","name":"Naulin, Volker","orcid":"0000-0001-5452-9215","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"rasmussenjensjuulpau","last":"Juul Rasmussen","locid":"125b9658-f84c-4e0e-859e-5899413288ee","name":"Rasmussen, Jens Juul","name_org":"Juul Rasmussen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-3543-690X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens","key":"madsenjenspau","last":"Madsen","locid":"ed287c2f-88ab-4d2f-8609-c89f2c2f7633","name":"Madsen, Jens","orcid":"0000-0002-6874-2970","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"H. Q.","key":"wanghqpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, H. Q.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"S. C.","key":"liuscpau","last":"Liu","name":"Liu, S. C.","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"W.","key":"zhangwpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, W.","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"L.","key":"wanglpau","last":"Wang","name":"Wang, L.","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"B. N.","key":"wanbnpau","last":"Wan","name":"Wan, B. N.","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1088/0741-3335/55/11/115007","issn":["07413335","13616587"],"issn_org":["07413335"],"issue":"11","journal":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","paperid":"115007","publisher":"IOP Publishing","status":"p","title":"Plasma Physics and Controlled Fusion","volume":"55"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84886891426"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-df673cde-75ae-4bca-a5e8-d2f79e4d100f"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"Statistical characterization of turbulence in the boundary plasma of EAST","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-371375","year":"2013","yearsub":"2013"}
{"abstract":"Efforts to extract a Greenland ice core with a complete record of the Eemian interglacial (130,000 to 115,000 years ago) have until now been unsuccessful. The response of the Greenland ice sheet to the warmer-than-present climate of the Eemian has thus remained unclear. Here we present the new North Greenland Eemian Ice Drilling ('NEEM') ice core and show only a modest ice-sheet response to the strong warming in the early Eemian. We reconstructed the Eemian record from folded ice using globally homogeneous parameters known from dated Greenland and Antarctic ice-core records. On the basis of water stable isotopes, NEEM surface temperatures after the onset of the Eemian (126,000 years ago) peaked at 8 ± 4 degrees Celsius above the mean of the past millennium, followed by a gradual cooling that was probably driven by the decreasing summer insolation. Between 128,000 and 122,000 years ago, the thickness of the northwest Greenland ice sheet decreased by 400 ± 250 metres, reaching surface elevations 122,000 years ago of 130 ± 300 metres lower than the present. Extensive surface melt occurred at the NEEM site during the Eemian, a phenomenon witnessed when melt layers formed again at NEEM during the exceptional heat of July 2012. With additional warming, surface melt might become more common in the future.","author_count":133,"contributors":["Dahl-Jensen, Dorthe","Albert, M. R.","Aldahan, A.","Azuma, N.","Balslev-Clausen, David Morten","Baumgartner, M.","Berggren, A.-M.","Bigler, M.","Binder, Thomas","Blunier, Thomas","Bourgeois, J.C.","Brook, E.J.","Buchardt, Susanne Lilja","Buizert, Christo","Capron, E.","Chappellaz, J.","Chung, J.","Clausen, Henrik Brink","Cvijanovic, Ivana","Davies, S.M.","Ditlevsen, Peter","Eicher, O.","Fischer, H.","Fisher, D. A.","Fleet, L.G.","Gfeller, G.","Gkinis, Vasileios","Gogineni, S.","Goto-Azuma, K.","Grinsted, Aslak","Gudlaugsdottir, H.","Guillevic, Myriam","Hansen, S. B.","Hansson, M.","Hirabayashi, M.","Hong, S.","Hur, S.D.","Huybrechts, P.","Hvidberg, Christine S.","Iizuka, Y.","Jenk, Theo Manuel","Johnsen, Sigfus Johann","Jones, T.R.","Jouzel, J.","Karlsson, Nanna Bjørnholt","Kawamura, K.","Keegan, K.","Kettner, Ernesto","Kipfstuhl, S.","Kjær, Helle Astrid","Koutnik, M.","Kuramoto, T.","Köhler, P.","Laepple, T.","Landais, A.","Langen, Peter Lang","Larsen, Lars Berg","Leuenberger, D.","Leuenberger, M.","Leuschen, C.","Li, J.","Lipenkov, V.","Martinerie, P.","Maselli, O. J.","Masson-Delmotte, V.","McConnell, J. R.","Miller, H.","Mini, O.","Miyamoto, A.","Montagnat-Rentier, M.","Mulvaney, R.","Muscheler, R.","Orsi, A.J.","Paden, J.","Panton, Christian","Pattyn, F.","Petit, J.-R.","Pol, K.","Popp, Trevor James","Possnert, G.","Prié, F.","Prokopiou, M.","Quiquet, A.","Rasmussen, Sune Olander","Raynaud, D.","Ren, J.","Reutenauer, Corentin","Ritz, C.","Röckmann, T.","Rosen, J.L.","Rubino, Mauro","Rybak, O.","Samyn, D.","Sapart, C.J.","Schilt, A.","Schmidt, Astrid Mariah Zelma","Schwander, J.","Schüpbach, S.","Seierstad, Inger Kathrine","Severinghaus, J. P.","Sheldon, S.","Simonsen, Sebastian Bjerregaard","Sjolte, Jesper","Solgaard, Anne Munck","Sowers, T.","Sperlich, Peter","Steen-Larsen, Hans Christian","Steffen, K.","Steffensen, Jørgen Peder","Steinhage, D.","Stocker, T.F.","Stowasser, Christopher","Sturevik, A.S.","Sturges, W.T.","Sveinbjörnsdottir, A.","Svensson, Anders","Tison, J.-L.","Uetake, J.","Vallelonga, Paul","Van De Wal, R.S.W.","Van Der Wel, G.","Vaughn, B.H.","Vinther, Bo Møllesøe","Waddington, E.","Wegner, A.","Weikusat, I.","White, J. W. C.","Wilhelms, F.","Winstrup, Mai","Witrant, E.","Wolff, E.W.","Xiao, C.","Zheng, Jin"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-409200"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"51-200 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Asia, East","Asia, Middle East","Europe, EU","Europe, Non-EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Belgium","Canada","China","France","Germany","Iceland","Japan","Netherlands","Russia","South Korea"