{"abstract":"The time and space averaged profiles of temperature, particle density, and momentum are in the scrape off layer determined by the intermittent transport generated at the edge shear layer. The distinction between profiles and fluctuations becomes arbitrary for situations where the transport is highly intermittent and shows long range correlations. Without this distinction the full range in parameter variability has to be taken into account for simulations, posing extreme demands on the used models. Numerical investigations and experimental results show how the interplay between radially propagating structures and parallel transport sets up the observed profiles and how intermittency influences edge conditions. The filamentary blob structures also transport and generate currents in the SOL, which can be investigated by means of local magnetic diagnostics. Finally, the ratio of ion to electron temperature in the SOL is an important measure for the influence of finite larmor radius effects on the propagation properties of blobs. Numerical investigations indicate that these effects can lead to an increased self confinement and radial reach of these structures. © 2012 WILEY-VCH Verlag GmbH & Co. KGaA, Weinheim","author_count":11,"contributors":["Naulin, Volker","Xu, G.","Vianello, N.","Madsen, Jens","Schrittwieser, R.","Ionita, C.","Maszl, C.","Mehlmann, F.","Yan, Ning","Nielsen, Anders Henry","Rasmussen, Jens Juul"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-332826"],"event":{"end":"2011-09-21","place":"South Lake Tahoe, us","start":"2011-09-19","title":"13th International Workshop on Plasma Edge Theory in Fusion Devices","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Asia, East","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","China","Italy"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Chinese Academy of Sciences","Consorzio RFX","University of Innsbruck"],"keyword":["Edge","Fusionsenergiforskning","Scrape off layer","Simulations","Turbulence"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"profiles and fluctuations in edge and sol turbulence","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ctpp.201210022","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-332826","identifier":[{"id":"84863100670","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-5ee3e418-f9ce-4916-92ec-8fc901c19acd"],"keyword":["Edge","Fusionsenergiforskning","Scrape-off layer","Simulations","Turbulence"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-2DD46686A951C6EF3974C3594A27253A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/ctpp.201210022","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Physics, Plasma Physics and Fusion Energy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"cn","key":"chinese academy of sciences","loc":["China","Asia, East"],"name":"Chinese Academy of Sciences","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"it","key":"consorzio rfx","loc":["Italy","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Consorzio RFX","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"at","key":"university of innsbruck","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Innsbruck","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Volker","key":"naulinpa2","last":"Naulin","locid":"68cb67c0-c64d-4fef-a301-67ab58d8ace6","nam