{"abstract":"The INTIMATE protocol for the correlation of marine ice core and terrestrial records is here updated, reflecting recent developments in palaeoclimate research. Originally focussed on Last Glacial to Interglacial Transition (LGIT: 22,000-11,500 years B.P.), the INTIMATE group has now extended its study period back to 60,000 years. As a first step, the INTIMATE event stratigraphy has now been extended to include 8000-48,000 b2k based on a combined NGRIP and GRIP isotope profile against a GICC05 chronology and key tephra horizons from Iceland and continental European volcanic sources. In this lead article of this INTIMATE special issue we introduce some of the recent achievements of the INTIMATE community and discuss the challenges associated with extending the INTIMATE approach back in time, focussing in particular on the chronological problems inherent in comparing different proxy records. The INTIMATE approach has thus far been limited predominantly to the North Atlantic and Australasian regions and we also discuss the potential to extend the INTIMATE protocol beyond these regions.","author_count":11,"contributors":["Blockley, S.P.E.","Lane, C.S.","Hardiman, M.","Rasmussen, Sune Olander","Seierstad, Inger Kathrine","Steffensen, Jørgen Peder","Svensson, Anders","Lotter, A.F.","Turney, C.S.M.","Ramsey, C.B.","INTIMATE members, no-firstname"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-397090"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"synchronisation of palaeoenvironmental records over the last 000000000060 000000000000 years and an extended intimate event stratigraphy to 000000000048 000000000000 b000000000002k","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quascirev.2011.09.017","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-397090","identifier":[{"id":"84857367263","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-06122382-20cc-45a0-8200-ab5cf3807582"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-5B4B20BA189735EC0EDB4281D87F87EE"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1016/j.quascirev.2011.09.017","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.quascirev.2011.09.017","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Niels Bohr Institute, Physics of Ice, Climate and Earth"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"S.P.E.","key":"blockleypau","last":"Blockley","name":"Blockley, S.P.E.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"C.S.","key":"lanepau","last":"Lane","name":"Lane, C.S.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"M.","key":"hardimanpau","last":"Hardiman","name":"Hardiman, M.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sune Olander","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"3f1d51b2-26a1-4a40-af3f-05f030c7bb9d","name":"Rasmussen, Sune Olander","orcid":"0000-0002-4177-3611","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Inger Kathrine","key":"seierstadpau","last":"Seierstad","locid":"719f8491-e2c2-438a-9b6a-99a14512be74","name":"Seierstad, Inger Kathrine","orcid":"0000-0003-1294-2292","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jørgen Peder","key":"steffensenpau","last":"Steffensen","locid":"688738da-b41f-4ff3-bb45-9870e6db5c7e","name":"Steffensen, Jørgen Peder","orcid":"0000-0002-5516-1093","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1",