{"abstract":"American President Harry S. Truman called the Cold War a \"struggle for the minds of men,\" and assigned journalists an important role in the conflict. This study finds that the U.S. Depeartment of State, via the American Embassy in Copenhagen, consciously attempted to shape Danish journalits' view of Aemrica directly and indirectly.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-591861"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Americanization","Cold War","Cultural Diplomacy"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"educational exchange as a cold war weapon american influence on danish journalists after world war ii","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rauli.cbs.dk/index.php/assc/article/download/4914/5349","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-591861","ids":["sdu-410374e9-0dbd-4485-bf78-73cfb41715da"],"keyword":["Americanization","Cold War","Cultural Diplomacy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-827E461F48989640763B3F0358273BE4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://rauli.cbs.dk/index.php/assc/article/download/4914/5349","version":"Published Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Blocked","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History","SDU, Faculty of Humanitie