{"abstract":"We describe the structure and operation of a micro/nanofluidic device in which individual metaphase chromosomes can be isolated and processed without being displaced during exchange of reagents. The change in chromosome morphology as a result of introducing protease into the device was observed by time-lapse imaging; pressure-driven flow was then used to shunt the chromosomal DNA package into a nanoslit. A long linear DNA strand (>1.3 Mbp) was seen to stretch out from the DNA package and along the length of the nanoslit. Delivery of DNA in its native metaphase chromosome package as well as the microfluidic environment prevented DNA from shearing and will be important for preparing ultra-long lengths of DNA for nanofluidic analysis.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Kristian Hagsted","Marie, Rodolphe","Moresco, Jacob Lange","Svendsen, Winnie Edith","Kristensen, Anders","Mir, Kalim U."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-329919"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Oxford"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a device for extraction manipulation and stretching of dna from single human chromosomes","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5588851/rsc%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-329919","identifier":[{"id":"21350789","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79953224851","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-554c4ba4-d941-45b4-ac6f-1725ec355899"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-273A53B67FC6A2F15460343E98BC98CF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://backend.orbit.dtu.dk/ws/files/5588851/rsc%5B1%5D.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1039/c0lc00603c","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, NanoSystemsEngineering Section","Technical University of Denmark, Department of Micro- and Nanotechnology, NanoSystemsEngineering Section, NSE-Optofluidics Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"gb","key":"university of oxford","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Oxford","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristian Hagsted","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f8079726-bd61-4d72-801c-f70ecafc96b3","name":"Rasmussen, Kristian Hagsted","orcid":"0000-0002-3662-2069","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rodolphe","key":"mariepau","last":"Marie","locid":"0e01d976-5d97-42d2-9b08-d7a8f8fb48f7","name":"Marie, Rodolphe","orcid":"0000-0002-8338-1990","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jacob Lange","key":"morescopau","last":"Moresco","locid":"eb7016a2-1ccd-440d-9ade-a94f03817d5d","name":"Moresco, Jacob Lange","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Winnie Edith","key":"svendsenpau","last":"Svendsen","locid":"98034411-a48a-4b80-91a3-14f88255a2fc","name":"Svendsen, Winnie Edith","orcid":"0000-0002-9197-6505","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders","key":"kristensenpau","last":"Kristensen","locid":"3c79a020-2c73-4e30-ac42-aee3ff272bcd","name":"Kristensen, Anders","orcid":"0000-0001-9567-1656","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kalim U.","key":"mirpau","last":"Mir","name":"Mir, Kalim U.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21350789"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1039/c0lc00603c","issn":["14730189","14730197"],"issn_org":["14730197"],"issue":"8","journal":"Lab on a Chip","pages":"1431-1433","publisher":"Royal Society of Chemistry","status":"p","title":"Lab on a Chip","volume":"11"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79953224851"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Technical University of Denmark","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["dtu-554c4ba4-d941-45b4-ac6f-1725ec355899"],"src":["DTU Technical University of Denmark"],"title":"A device for extraction, manipulation and stretching of DNA from single human chromosomes","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-329919","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we formulate the vehicle routing problem with time windows and temporal dependencies. The problem is an extension of the well studied vehicle routing problem with time windows. In addition to the usual constraints, a scheduled time of one visit may restrain the scheduling options of other visits. Special cases of temporal dependencies are synchronization and precedence constraints. Two compact formulations of the problem are introduced and the Dantzig–Wolfe decompositions of these formulations are presented to allow for a column generation‐based solution approach. Temporal dependencies are modeled by generalized precedence constraints. Four different master problem formulations are proposed and it is shown that the formulations can be ranked according to the tightness with which they describe the solution space. A tailored time window branching is used to enforce feasibility on the relaxed master problems. Finally, a computational study is performed to quantitatively reveal strengths and weaknesses of the proposed formulations. It is concluded that, depending on the problem at hand, the best performance is achieved either by relaxing the generalized precedence constraints in the master problem, or by using a time‐indexed model, where generalized precedence constraints are added as cuts when they become severely violated. © 2011 Wiley Periodicals, Inc. NETWORKS, Vol. 58(4), 273–289 2011","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dohn, Anders Høeg","Rasmussen, Matias Sevel","Larsen, Jesper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-349279"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Branch and cut and price","Branch and price","Column generation","Integer programming","Relaxation","Set partitioning"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-DTU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-DTU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the vehicle routing problem with time windows and temporal dependencies","src":["dtu"],"src-code":["DI-U-DTU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/net.20472","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-349279","identifier":[{"id":"80755188936","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["dtu-95eb54dc-d28f-4c54-8f7a-2bb0336c75d3"],"keyword":["branch‐and‐cut‐and‐price","branch‐and‐price","column generation","generalized precedence constraints","integer programming.","relaxation","set covering","set partitioning","temporal dependency","time‐window branching","vehicle routing with time windows"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AB931AE6FDF0EBC34E823C2D32FB6BAF"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1002/net.20472","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"dtu technical university of denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-DTU","l3nl":"Technical University of Denmark","l3nn":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"DTU Technical University of Denmark","namevar":["Technical University of Denmark, Department of Management Engineering"],"nora_code":"DI-U-DTU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Høeg","key":"dohnpau","last":"Dohn","locid":"7047c488-612a-498d-a5c1-ec880769c499","name":"Dohn, Anders Høeg","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Matias Sevel","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"fae6c0fe-1ce6-46e6-b271-b6609f9c42d5","name":"Rasmussen, Matias Sevel","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper","key":"larsenpau","last":"Larsen","locid":"d1af4d26-e92b-414c-b534-25b2b607a0d9","name":"Larsen, Jesper","orcid":"0000-0002-9119-3586","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1002/net.20472","issn":["00283045","10970037"],"issn_org