{"abstract":"High-resolution genomic microarrays enable simultaneous detection of copy-number aberrations such as the known recurrent aberrations in chronic lymphocytic leukemia [del(11q), del(13q), del(17p) and trisomy 12], and copy-number neutral loss of heterozygosity. Moreover, comparison of genomic profiles from sequential patients' samples allows detection of clonal evolution.","author_count":17,"contributors":["Gunnarsson, Rebeqa","Mansouri, Larry","Isaksson, Anders","Göransson, Hanna","Cahill, Nicola","Jansson, Mattias","Rasmussen, Markus","Lundin, Jeanette De Sparra","Norin, Stefan","Buhl, Anne Mette","Smedby, Karin Ekström","Hjalgrim, Henrik","Karlsson, Karin","Jurlander, Jesper","Geisler, Christian H","Juliusson, Gunnar","Rosenquist, Richard"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-440321"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"array based genomic screening at diagnosis and during follow up in chronic lymphocytic leukemia","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2010.039768","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-440321","identifier":[{"id":"79961059215","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-4e98100c-d0e3-49b6-b6b6-d3618f633850"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-7C6E85AF8AB2BADB08FAA70118AB3775"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3324/haematol.2010.039768","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":1,"key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"