{"abstract":"OBJECTIVE: It is believed that 24-40% of ovarian cancers have dysfunction in the BRCA1 or BRCA2 (BRCAness) genes, due to either inherited or somatic mutations or due to epigenetic inactivation. Demonstration of ovarian cancers with BRCAness is becoming important both due to the possibility of offering genetic counseling and due to beneficial effects of polyadenosine diphosphate ribose polymerase inhibitor treatment in this group. As DNA sequencing is expensive and time consuming, efforts have been devoted to develop more indirect methods for BRCA screening that can improve the selection of patients for sequence-based BRCA testing. DESIGN: BRCA1 immunohistochemistry, fluorescence in situ hybridization (FISH) and methylation analyses were performed on formalin-fixed, paraffin-embedded ovarian cancer tissue. SAMPLE: Fifty-four ovarian cancers; 15 BRCA1 cancers, four BRCA2 cancers, 10 cancers from patients with a family history but no mutation detected, and 25 ovarian cancers with unknown BRCA1 status. RESULTS: Abnormal BRCA1 immunohistochemistry was found to indicate BRCA mutations with a sensitivity of 80%, a specificity of 93% and an estimated positive predictive value of 73%. The FISH analyses supported the diagnosis in most cases. Methylation analyses could indicate BRCA deficiency in combination with one of the other methods. CONCLUSIONS: BRCA1 immunohistochemistry is a promising screening method for BRCA1 mutation detection.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Skytte, Anne-Bine Semma","Waldstrøm, Marianne","Rasmussen, Anders A","Crüger, Dorthe","Woodward, Emma R","Kølvraa, Steen"],"cuid":["S02-084.87-027258"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["BRCA1 Protein","DNA methylation","Female","Gene Expression Regulation Neoplastic","Genes BRCA1","Genes BRCA2","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Germ Line Mutation","Heterozygote","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","In Situ Hybridization Fluorescence","Ovarian Neoplasms","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Predictive Value of Tests","Sensitivity and Specificity"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of brca000000000001 deficient ovarian cancers","src":["au","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0412.2011.01121.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-084.87-027258","identifier":[{"id":"21371001","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79956201393","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c9235a2a-be84-4a8f-8539-bb5ca86edb61","sdu-b43a3e43-fed4-4a1e-88a3-16755b90eaac"],"keyword":["BRCA1 Protein","DNA Methylation","Female","Gene Expression Regulation, Neoplastic","Genes, BRCA1","Genes, BRCA2","Genetic Predisposition to Disease","Germ-Line Mutation","Heterozygote","Humans","Immunohistochemistry","In Situ Hybridization, Fluorescence","Ovarian Neoplasms","Polymerase Chain Reaction","Predictive Value of Tests","Sensitivity and Specificity"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-0A2FBF866773FDD84AF9F29DE90A17B4"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1600-0412.2011.01121.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences","SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Regional Health Research, IRS - Lillebælt Hospital, Research Unit of Human Genetics (Vejle)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Central Administration, AU IT, AU IT - AU IT Skyen, Roskilde"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anne-Bine","key":"skyttepau","last":"Skytte","locid":"96b98a09-03ac-4052-9da0-010f7c92bd08","name":"Skytte, Anne-Bine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marianne","key":"waldstrømpau","last":"Waldstrøm","locid":"0cb33589-3f3f-4e6b-b5e6-d1f0f4f96583","name":"Waldstrøm, Marianne","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Aamann","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f1d85e30-f7bb-4592-9c4d-6f0a7bc42c7f","name":"Rasmussen, Anders A","name_org":"Rasmussen, Anders Aamann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Dorthe","key":"crügerpau","last":"Crüger","name":"Crüger, Dorthe","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Emma R","key":"woodwardpau","last":"Woodward","name":"Woodward, Emma R","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2 1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"kølvraapau","last":"Kølvraa","locid":"2e1d9b97-d4d2-47eb-8ff4-705eaa193048","name":"Kølvraa, Steen","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21371001"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1111/j.1600-0412.2011.01121.x","issn":["00016349"],"issue":"6","journal":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","pages":"593-9","publisher":"Wiley-Blackwell","status":"p","title":"Acta Obstetricia et Gynecologica Scandinavica","volume":"90"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79956201393"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-c9235a2a-be84-4a8f-8539-bb5ca86edb61","sdu-b43a3e43-fed4-4a1e-88a3-16755b90eaac"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Identification of BRCA1-deficient ovarian cancers","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.87-027258","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"A trio of genome-wide association studies recently reported sequence variants at three loci to be significantly associated with schizophrenia. No sequence polymorphism had been unequivocally (P<5 × 10-8) associated with schizophrenia earlier. However, one variant, rs1344706[T], had come very close. This polymorphism, located in an intron of ZNF804A, was reported to associate with schizophrenia with a P-value of 1.6 × 10-7, and with psychosis (schizophrenia plus bipolar disorder) with a P-value of 1.0 × 10-8. In this study, using 5164 schizophrenia cases and 20¿709 controls, we replicated the association with schizophrenia (odds ratio OR=1.08, P=0.0029) and, by adding bipolar disorder patients, we also confirmed the association with psychosis (added N=609, OR=1.09, P=0.00065). Furthermore, as it has been proposed that variants such as rs1344706[T]—common and with low relative risk—may also serve to identify regions harboring less common, higher-risk susceptibility alleles, we searched ZNF804A for large copy number variants (CNVs) in 4235 psychosis patients, 1173 patients with other psychiatric disorders and 39¿481 controls. We identified two CNVs including at least part of ZNF804A in psychosis patients and no ZNF804A CNVs in controls (P=0.013 for association with psychosis). In addition, we found a ZNF804A CNV in an anxiety patient (P=0.0016 for association with the larger set of psychiatric disorders).","author_count":50,"contributors":["Steinberg, S","Mors, Ole","Børglum, Anders D","Gustafsson, O","Werge, Thomas","Mortensen, Preben Bo","Andreassen, O A","Sigurdsson, E","Thorgeirsson, Thrøstur","Böttcher, Y","Olason, P","Ophoff, R A","Cichon, S","Gudjonsdottir, I H","Pietiläinen, O P H","Nyegaard, Mette","Tuulio-Henriksson, A","Ingason, A","Hansen, T","Athanasiu, L","Suvisaari, J","Lonnqvist, J","Paunio, T","Hartmann, A.","Jürgens, G","Nordentoft, M","Hougaard, D M","Norgaard-Pedersen, B","Breuer, R","Möller, H-J","Giegling, I","Glenthøj, Andreas Birkedal","Rasmussen, H B","Mattheisen, M","Bitter, I","Réthelyi, J M","Sigmundsson, T","Fossdal, R","Thorsteinsdottir, U","Ruggeri, M","Tosato, S","Strengman, E","Kiemeney, L A","Melle, I","Djurovic, S","Abramova, L","Kaleda, V","Walshe, M","Bramon, E","Vassos, E"],"cuid":["S02-092.38-026658"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"corpau":["Genetic Risk and Outcome in Psychosis"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expanding the range of znf000000000804a variants conferring risk of psychosis","src":["au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/mp.2009.149","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.38-026658","identifier":[{"id":"20048749","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3242031","type":"pmcid"},{"id":"84947649726","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-c0b388f9-9f83-42c4-ace6-fc1471cc05e4","ku-5c45b73e-fa34-444c-8d3b-f8ed9f670ae4"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-9F439EB2EC54B410BE70546D259129ED"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1038/mp.2009.149","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Centre for Psychiatric Research"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Regi