{"abstract":"We present a high-quality (>100× depth) Illumina genome sequence of the leaf-cutting ant Acromyrmex echinatior, a model species for symbiosis and reproductive conflict studies. We compare this genome with three previously sequenced genomes of ants from different subfamilies and focus our analyses on aspects of the genome likely to be associated with known evolutionary changes. The first is the specialized fungal diet of A. echinatior, where we find gene loss in the ant's arginine synthesis pathway, loss of detoxification genes, and expansion of a group of peptidase proteins. One of these is a unique ant-derived contribution to the fecal fluid, which otherwise consists of \"garden manuring\" fungal enzymes that are unaffected by ant digestion. The second is multiple mating of queens and ejaculate competition, which may be associated with a greatly expanded nardilysin-like peptidase gene family. The third is sex determination, where we could identify only a single homolog of the feminizer gene. As other ants and the honeybee have duplications of this gene, we hypothesize that this may partly explain the frequent production of diploid male larvae in A. echinatior. The fourth is the evolution of eusociality, where we find a highly conserved ant-specific profile of neuropeptide genes that may be related to caste determination. These first analyses of the A. echinatior genome indicate that considerable genetic changes are likely to have accompanied the transition from hunter-gathering to agricultural food production 50 million years ago, and the transition from single to multiple queen mating 10 million years ago.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Nygaard, Sanne","Zhang, Guojie","Schiøtt, Morten","Li, Cai","Wurm, Yannick","Hu, Haofu","Zhou, Jiajian","Ji, Lu","Qiu, Feng","Rasmussen, Morten","Pan, Hailin","Hauser, Frank","Krogh, Anders","Grimmelikhuijzen, Cornelis","Wang, Jun","Boomsma, Jacobus Jan"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-541435"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the genome of the leaf cutting ant em acromyrmex echinatior em suggests key adaptations to advanced social life and fungus farming","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-541435","identifier":[{"id":"80051559742","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21719571","type":"pmid"},{"id":"PMC3149500","type":"pmcid"}],"ids":["ku-f7e4c8bf-4f17-4291-9efc-a081f0fae6e0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-D2BAE8BE37A9A2795B4B9EFB55469229"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Biology, Ecology and Evolution"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sanne","key":"nygaardpau","last":"Nygaard","locid":"7bb86612-6b78-4244-8f09-fa22fe6fa720","name":"Nygaard, Sanne","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Guojie","key":"zhangpau","last":"Zhang","name":"Zhang, Guojie","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"schiøttpau","last":"Schiøtt","locid":"45a0e8bb-8368-4050-aaed-35ce3b077296","name":"Schiøtt, Morten","orcid":"0000-0002-4309-8090","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Cai","key":"lipau","last":"Li","name":"Li, Cai","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Yannick","key":"wurmpau","last":"Wurm","name":"Wurm, Yannick","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Haofu","key":"hupau","last":"Hu","name":"Hu, Haofu","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jiajian","key":"zhoupau","last":"Zhou","name":"Zhou, Jiajian","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Lu","key":"jipau","last":"Ji","name":"Ji, Lu","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Feng","key":"qiupau","last":"Qiu","name":"Qiu, Feng","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Morten","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"888dabb7-a178-4041-8be2-3beb7b8efda3","name":"Rasmussen, Morten","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Hailin","key":"panpau","last":"Pan","name":"Pan, Hailin","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Frank","key":"hauserpau","last":"Hauser","locid":"329cfd6d-bb0c-483b-820f-dd44d32e77a6","name":"Hauser, Frank","orcid":"0000-0001-5563-2345","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders","key":"kroghpau","last":"Krogh","locid":"109cd77e-27eb-47b9-997f-eab877a0f429","name":"Krogh, Anders","orcid":"0000-0002-5147-6282","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Cornelis (Cok)","key":"grimmelikhuijzenpau","last":"Grimmelikhuijzen","locid":"d3f0727a-8fc5-4944-b7cc-a75ff53fab63","name":"Grimmelikhuijzen, Cornelis","name_org":"Grimmelikhuijzen, Cornelis (Cok)","orcid":"0000-0001-6486-2046","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jun","key":"wangpau","last":"Wang","locid":"5dee6edc-2876-496f-a341-4a07933f9928","name":"Wang, Jun","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Jacobus Jan","key":"boomsmapau","last":"Boomsma","locid":"bf2786c8-6e04-4853-ba15-ced76aceb8aa","name":"Boomsma, Jacobus Jan","orcid":"0000-0002-3598-1609","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21719571"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1101/gr.121392.111","issn":["10889051","15495469"],"issue":"8","journal":"Genome Research","pages":"1339-1348","status":"p","title":"Genome Research","volume":"21"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-80051559742"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f7e4c8bf-4f17-4291-9efc-a081f0fae6e0"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The genome of the leaf-cutting ant <em>Acromyrmex echinatior</em> suggests key adaptations to advanced social life and fungus farming","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-541435","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The minimal requirements for a living system are often listed as follows: i) a living system must have a specific identity and be able to preserve it (compartmentalization) ; ii) it must sustain itself by using energy from its environment to manufacture at least some of its components from resources in the environment (metabolism) ; iii) the system must be capable of growth and self-replication (a prerequisite here being a genetic building plan); finally iv) it must be capable of adaptation (open-ended evolvability). The design of artificial chemical systems or protocells from the bottom up (Szostak, 2001), fulfilling these requirements has been the subject of numerous studies. Usually such chemical systems are conceived around the encapsulation of a set of genes along with the transcription-translation machinery within liposomes/vesicles (Yutetsu, 2009). The generated artificial systems have many of the basic characteristics of a living system, but usually lack the gene mediated regulation functions that natural cells possess. To address this issue, we are attempting a systemic approach (Rasmussen, 2004) in implementing a simple, chemical system that contains three major types of molecules (information-bearing, metabolic and amphiphile molecules). These molecules through self-assembly processes will aggregate to form a complete protocell with its own information, metabolism and container components. This system should be capable of performing independently all the necessary metabolic steps, e.g., amphiphile production and non-enzymatic polymerization of the information building blocks, which will lead to its replication. Our proposed system is composed of a chemical mixture of fatty acids that form bilayers (compartments), nucleic acids (NAs) with a hydrophobic moiety, and metabolic complexes or photosensitizers which can harvest energy. To truly simplify our design while fulfilling the design requirements, the regulation of the metabolism is mediated by information molecules. That is, the NAs acts as a sequence-specific, metabolic mediator by serving as electron relay to a ruthenium complex, the photosensitizer/catalyst. The metabolic catalytic unit converts the hydrophobic container precursor molecules into amphiphiles or into nucleic acid oligomers that can be non-enzymatically ligated, thus directly linking the metabolism with information. We will report on the major steps towards the realization of the design and the already demonstrated advantages of the systemic approach in unravelling interactions (Declue, 2009; Maurer, 2011) between the components and their significances for the self-maintenance and self-replication of a protocell. References DeClue, MS, Monnard, P-A, Bailey, JA, Maurer, SE, Collis, GE, Ziock, H-J, Rasmussen, S, and Boncella, JM (2009) J. Am. Chem. Soc., 131, 931-933. Maurer, SE, Declue, MS, Albertsen, AN, Dörr, M, Kuiper, DS, Ziock, H, Rasmussen, S, Boncella, JM, and Monnard, P-A (2011) ChemPhysChem, in press. Yutetsu, K, Pasquale, S, Ueda, T, and Luisi, PL, (2009) Biochim. Biophys. Acta, 1788, 567- 574. Rasmussen S, Chen L, Deamer D, Krakauer, DC, Packard, NH, Stadler, PF and Bedau, MA (2004) Science, 303, 963-965. Szostak, JW, Bartel, DP and Luisi, PL (2001) Nature, 409, 387-390.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Albertsen, Anders N.","Maurer, Sarah Elisabeth","Cape, Jonathan","Edson, Joseph B.","Rasmussen, Steen","Ziock, Hans","Boncella, James M.","Monnard, Pierre-Alain"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-583617"],"event":{"end":"2011-07-08","place":"Montpellier, fr","start":"2011-07-03","title":"ISSOL 2011","year":"2011"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","OECD"],"country":["United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Los Alamos National Laboratory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"attempt at a systemic design of a protocell connecting information metabolism and container","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-583617","ids":["sdu-2457a100-67ff-4ba4-937b-0c59231b4ac7"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-A9E3724A51E4683E9EBF3286FC1ABC00"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy","SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Physics, Chemistry and Pharmacy, Center for Fundamental Living Technology (FLinT)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"los alamos national laboratory","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Los Alamos National Laboratory","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders N.","key":"albertsenpau","last":"Albertsen","locid":"3792cbe7-d045-4de7-98a8-acd8139984aa","name":"Albertsen, Anders N.","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Sarah","key":"maurerpau","last":"Maurer","locid":"9af25acb-b46e-4ce2-bffb-4aee1f394fb2","name":"Maurer, Sarah Elisabeth","name_org":"Maurer, Sarah","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonathan","key":"capepau","last":"Cape","name":"Cape, Jonathan","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Joseph B.","key":"edsonpau","last":"Edson","name":"Edson, Joseph B.","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Steen","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"2601890b-b919-4cbf-b46f-7867f89312c9","name":"Rasmussen, Steen","orcid":"0000-0002-3336-843X","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Hans","key":"ziockpau","last":"Ziock","name":"Ziock, Hans","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"James M.","key":"boncellapau","last":"Boncella","name":"Boncella, James M.","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pierre-Alain","key":"monnardpau","last":"Monnard","locid":"014842e8-63fb-496d-acc9-cb017cabc961","name":"Monnard, Pierre-Alain","orcid":"0000-0003-4679-3950","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-2457a100-67ff-4ba4-937b-0c59231b4ac7"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Attempt at a Systemic Design of a Protocell: Connecting information, Metabolism and Container","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-583617","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"In this study, we investigate patterns in interactions between children with communicative disabilities and their parents. The purpose is to demonstrate how, in play activities at home, parents with varying degrees of success make their children’s contributions sensible. A Conversation Analytic approach to interaction underlies our demonstration. We show that parents’ actions may be finely tuned and fine-grained, as well as locally situated with regard to treating their children’s actions as sensible contributions to an ongoing activity. Finally, we discuss the implications of our findings in relation to early communication intervention.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Brouwer, Catherine E.","Day, Dennis","Ferm, Ulrika","Hougaard, Anders","Rasmussen, Gitte","Thunberg, Gunilla"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-587922"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Sahlgrenska University Hospital"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"treating the actions of children as sensible investigating structures in interactions between children with disabilities and their parents","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-587922","ids":["sdu-3351e4a5-b781-485b-95c1-3cd5164281c5"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-27F854C938270F39EE3FF4DCDF95CCB1"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":[