orresponding":null,"first":"Kent","key":"nielsenpau","last":"Nielsen","locid":"6d820a44-9c38-4c7f-b8cb-e642240df876","name":"Nielsen, Kent","rank":12,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Pernille Lykke","key":"pedersenpau","last":"Pedersen","locid":"8815683a-d896-4fda-ac9e-7ae88d3dceae","name":"Pedersen, Pernille Lykke","rank":13,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Carsten","key":"svaneborgpau","last":"Svaneborg","locid":"2f5d9263-9d08-4b4e-817a-2f0b8e8f708b","name":"Svaneborg, Carsten","orcid":"0000-0003-4301-3365","rank":14,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Michael Chr.","key":"wambergpau","last":"Wamberg","locid":"2c3fdc3e-02ba-4fbf-a437-e5204bd52e8a","name":"Wamberg, Michael Chr.","rank":15,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Rafal","key":"wieczorekpau","last":"Wieczorek","locid":"9577d735-fd63-48af-a95c-7e65b0febbf0","name":"Wieczorek, Rafal","rank":16,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-e1325655-8518-4d8f-b7d5-e54f86607630"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Bottom up assembly of minimal life","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-637725","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"To investigate whether distance from a patient's home to the nearest invasive centre influenced the invasive treatment strategy in acute coronary syndrome (ACS). Methods This was an observational cohort study using nationwide registries involving 24¿910 patients admitted with ACS (median age 67, range 30–90 years). All persons were grouped in tertiles according to the distance from their residence to the invasive centre. Cox proportional hazard models were applied to estimate the differences in coronary angiography and revascularisation rate within 60 days of admission according to the distance to the centre. The end points were coronary angiography and subsequent revascularisation. Results Of 24¿910 patients with a first ACS, 33% resided <21 km from one of the five invasive centres in Denmark, 33% lived between 21 and 64 km away and 34% lived >64 km away. The incidence of coronary angiography was 68% for long distance versus 77% for short distance (p<0.05), with an HR of 0.78 (95% CI 0.75 to 0.81, p<0.0001). Adjustment for patient characteristics such as age, sex, co-morbidity and socioeconomic status did not attenuate the difference (HR 0.74, 95% CI 0.71 to 0.77, p<0.0001). Furthermore, revascularisation in the subgroup examined with coronary angiography was less likely for those residing a long distance from the invasive centre compared with those living nearer (adjusted HR of 0.82 (95% CI 0.78 to 0.85, p<0.0001). Conclusions In patients hospitalised with ACS, invasive examination and treatment were less likely the further away from an invasive centre the patients resided, thus equal and uniform invasive examination and treatment was not found.","author_count":13,"contributors":["Hvelplund, Anders","Galatius, Søren","Madsen, Mette","Rasmussen, Jeppe Nørgaard","Sørensen, Rikke","Fosbøl, Emil Loldrup","Madsen, Jan Kyst","Rasmussen, Søren","Jørgensen, Erik","Thuesen, Leif","Møller, Christian Holflod","Abildstrøm, Steen Zabell"],"cuid":["S03-092.54-012601"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Acute coronary syndrome","Adult","Aged","Aged 80 and over","Angioplasty Balloon Coronary","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Care Units","Coronary artery disease","Denmark","Female","Health Services Accessibility","Humans","Kaplan Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardial Revascularization","Socioeconomic Factors","Transportation of Patients","Treatment Outcome"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"influence of distance from home to invasive centre on invasive treatment after acute coronary syndrome a nationwide study of 000000000024 000000000910 patients","src":["au","ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1136/hrt.2010.203901","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-092.54-012601","identifier":[{"id":"78651233253","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21051459","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["au-006e4875-0080-4b23-9b3c-e9a8420d1ab2","ku-5ff47123-f525-4ec6-a4cc-c22615110565","sdu-207fea8e-13d7-46d8-96a5-cc284d01d0d9"],"keyword":["Acute Coronary Syndrome","Adult","Aged","Aged, 80 and over","Angioplasty, Balloon, Coronary","Coronary Angiography","Coronary Artery Disease","Coronary Care Units","Denmark","Female","Health Services Accessibility","Humans","Kaplan-Meier Estimate","Male","Middle Aged","Myocardial Infarction","Myocardial Revascularization","Socioeconomic Factors","Transportation of Patients","Treatment Outcome"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E86910464AE253A552C4655714036C3F"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://