{"abstract":"Complete characterization of a biomolecule's chemical structure is crucial in the full understanding of the relations between their structure and function. The dominating components in ribosomes are ribosomal RNAs (rRNAs), and the entire rRNA-but a single modified nucleoside at position 2501 in 23S rRNA-has previously been characterized in the bacterium Escherichia coli. Despite a first report nearly 20 years ago, the chemical nature of the modification at position 2501 has remained elusive, and attempts to isolate it have so far been unsuccessful. We unambiguously identify this last unknown modification as 5-hydroxycytidine-a novel modification in RNA. Identification of 5-hydroxycytidine was completed by liquid chromatography under nonoxidizing conditions using a graphitized carbon stationary phase in combination with ion trap tandem mass spectrometry and by comparing the fragmentation behavior of the natural nucleoside with that of a chemically synthesized ditto. Furthermore, we show that 5-hydroxycytidine is also present in the equivalent position of 23S rRNA from the bacterium Deinococcus radiodurans. Given the unstable nature of 5-hydroxycytidine, this modification might be found in other RNAs when applying the proper analytical conditions as described here.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Havelund, Jesper F","Giessing, Anders","Hansen, Trine Møller","Rasmussen, Anette","Scott, Lincoln Greyson","Kirpekar, Finn"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-604515"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identification of 000000000005 hydroxycytidine at position 000000002501 concludes characterization of modified nucleotides in e coli 000000000023s rrna","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmb.2011.06.036","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-604515","identifier":[{"id":"21723290","type":"pmid"},{"id":"79960896599","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["sdu-6d8260ad-a616-4d2a-afdb-862b7bb285f6"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A13299EC85EC8B179A22EB395BA6975D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jmb.2011.06.036","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Science, Department of Biochemistry and Molecular Biology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jesper Foged","key":"havelundpau","last":"Havelund","locid":"89a02ac8-5f47-4c65-9d0b-1557a63aabf2","name":"Havelund, Jesper F","name_org":"Havelund, Jesper Foged","orcid":"0000-0002-9797-5431","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anders Michael Bernth","key":"giessingpau","last":"Giessing","locid":"152b0e2c-5377-47a1-a197-82902800cc15","name":"Giessing, Anders","name_org":"Giessing, Anders Michael Bernth","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Trine Møller","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"0180b985-32d1-411c-9eb5-3de16c2e6e1f","name":"Hansen, Trine Møller","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anette","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anette","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Lincoln Greyson","key":"scottpau","last":"Scott","name":"Scott, Lincoln Greyson","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Finn","key":"kirpekarpau","last":"Kirpekar","locid":"5a936580-b4b8-47cd-8407-7ab6c6ca5a43","name":"Kirpekar, Finn","orcid":"0000-0003-1901-2266","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21723290"],"pub":{"doi":"10.1016/j.jmb.2011.06.036","issn":["00222836","10898638"],"issn_org":["00222836"],"issue":"3","journal":"Journal of Molecular Biology","pages":"529-536","publisher":"Academic Press","status":"p","title":"Journal of Molecular Biology","volume":"411"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79960896599"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-6d8260ad-a616-4d2a-afdb-862b7bb285f6"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Identification of 5-hydroxycytidine at position 2501 concludes characterization of modified nucleotides in E. coli 23S rRNA","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-604515","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"Article on Danish Immigrant pastor who served in the 15th Wisconsin Infantry Regiment during the American Civil War","author_count":1,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Anders Bo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-613034"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Civil war","Ethnicity"],"level":"pop","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"und","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feltpræsten fra ærø","src":["sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-613034","ids":["sdu-8aeb425c-17e3-4708-96d0-9d862f434523"],"keyword":["Civil War","Ethnicity"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Popular","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-D61785F8D81CAF42C50D56C7C455AE91"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History","SDU, Faculty of Humanities, Department of History, Center for American Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Anders Bo","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"f284f3a3-297f-4882-81e1-b591c41ead80","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Bo","orcid":"0000-0001-9817-9595","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"pages":"54-60","publisher":"Ærø Museum","status":"p","title":"Årbog 2011 Ærø Museum"},"review":"Undetermined","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["sdu-8aeb425c-17e3-4708-96d0-9d862f434523"],"src":["SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Feltpræsten fra Ærø","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-613034","year":"2011","yearsub":"2011"}
{"abstract":"The disease phenotype of transthyretin (TTR) is dramatically influenced by single point mutations in the TTR gene. Herein, we report on a novel mutation D99N (Asp99Asn) in TTR found in a Danish kindred. None of the family members carrying this mutation have so far shown any clinical signs of amyloidosis. One carrier found compound heterozygous for TTR D99N and L111M (Leu111Met) associated with cardiac amyloid is asymptomatic (42 years). Disease severity can often be linked to both the kinetics of fibril formation and the degree of destabilisation of the native state. In this study, we show that the thermodynamic stability and rate of tetramer dissociation of the variant TTR D99N is unchanged or slightly more stable than wild type (WT) TTR. Furthermore, the in vitro fibrillation kinetics of the variant reveals an unchanged or slightly suppressed tendency to form fibrils compared to WT. Thus, the in vitro experiments support the lack of clinical symptoms observed so far for the TTR D99N carriers. In line with this, studies on kinetic stability and fibrillation kinetics reveal indistinguishable stability of TTR heterotetramers D99N/L111M compared to the heterotetramers WT/L111M. In conclusion, TTR D99N is predicted to be a non-pathogenic benign mutation with WT properties.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Jensen, Minna Grønning","Campos, Raul I.","Fagerberg, Christina","Rasmussen, Anders Aamann","Eriksen, Ulrik H.","Powers, Evant T.","Hammarström, Per"],"cuid":["S02-096.15-046403"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Linköping University","Scripps Research Institute"],"keyword":["Denmark","Female","Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences","Genetics Population","Humans","Kinetics","Male","Models Molecular","Pedigree","Point Mutation","Prealbumin","Protein Conformation","Protein Denaturation","Protein Folding","Thermodynamics"],"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-SDR"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-SDR","DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"thermodynamic stability and denaturation kinetics of a benign natural transthyretin mutant identified in a danish kindred","src":["ku","sdu"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU","DI-U-SDU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/13506129.2011.560215","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-096.15-046403","identifier":[{"id":"79955797861","type":"scopus"},{"id":"21406045","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["ku-d16a8555-1671-4101-a8bd-36c32144fa4b","sdu-8cdae294-ee79-43e1-851b-faf0ad91c5a3"],"keyword":["Denmark","Female","Former Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences","Genetics, Population","Humans","Kinetics","Male","Models, Molecular","Pedigree","Point Mutation","Prealbumin","Protein Conformation","Protein Denaturation","Protein Folding","Thermodynamics"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-855673492632A921CBC129BF40C50D69"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.3109/13506129.2011.560215","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Pharmaceutical Sciences, Department of Pharmacy"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"linköping university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Linköping University","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"sdu university of southern denmark","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-SDU","l3nl":"University of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"SDU University of Southern Denmark","namevar":["SDU, The Faculty of Health Sciences, Department of Clinical Research, KI, OUH, Research unit of Clinical Genetics (Odense)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-SDU","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"dk","key":"region of southern denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-SDR","l3nl":"Region of Southern Denmark","l3nn":"Region of Southern Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Region of Southern Denmark","namevar":["Lillebaelt University Hospital"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-SDR","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"scripps research institute","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Scripps Research Institute","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Minna Grønning","key":"jensenpau","last":"Jensen","locid":"61b8949d-34da-425d-86be-5e5a97dbd482","name":"Jensen, Minna Grønning","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Minna","key":"groenningpau","last":"Groenning","name":"Groenning, Minna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Raul I.","key":"campospau","last":"Campos","name":"Campos, Raul I.","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3 4","corresponding":null,"first":"Christina","key":"fagerbergpau","last":"Fagerberg","locid":"93aebc29-7681-4e3d-b613-867bd3a7eb65","name":"Fagerberg, Christina","orcid":"0000-0002-5206-4327","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Anders Aamann","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","name":"Rasmussen, Anders Aamann","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","first":"Ulrik H.","key":"eriksenpau","last":"Eriksen","name":"Eriksen, Ulrik H.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","first":"Evant T.","key":"powerspau","last":"Powers","name":"Powers, Evant T.","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Per","key":"hammarströmpau","last":"Hammarström","name":"Hammarström, Per","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pmid":["21406045"],"pub":{"doi":"10.3109/13506129.2011.560215","issn":["13506129","17442818"],"issn_org":["13506129"],"issue":"2","journal":"Amyloid: the Journal of Protein Folding Disorders","pages":"35-46","publisher":"Informa Healthcare","status":"p","title":"Amyloid: the Journal of Protein Folding Disorders","title_org":"Amyloid","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-79955797861"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Hospitals","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-HO-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Hospitals","Region of Southern Denmark","Universities","University of Copenhagen","University of Southern Denmark"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-d16a8555-1671-4101-a8bd-36c32144fa4b","sdu-8cdae294-ee79-43e1-851b-faf0ad91c5a3"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen","SDU University of Southern Denmark"],"title":"Thermodynamic stability and denaturation kinetics of a benign natural transthyretin mutant identified in a Danish kindred","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-096.15-046403","year":"2011","yearsub":2012}
{"abstract":"Aims  The purpose was to elucidate the association between parity and the incidence of diabetes using national register data. Methods  The study population consisted of all Danish women with a singleton delivery in 1982/1983 (n = 100 669), who subsequently had 74 966 deliveries. The included women were followed up via registries until the end of 2006 for subsequent deliveries, diagnosis of diabetes and death/emigration. Results  A total of 2021 cases (2.0%) were diagnosed with diabetes in connection with hospitalization or outpatient treatment during follow-up. Analyses were adjusted for fetal weight and duration of gestation, both at index pregnancy. Cox regression analysis with parity as a time-varying exposure, stratified in two age groups, showed an association between parity and risk of a diagnosis of diabetes. In women <33 years of age, parity 2, 3 and 4 + were associated with an increased risk of being diagnosed with diabetes compared with parity 1 [relative risks: 1.6 (95% confidence interval 1.1–2.3), 2.8 (1.8–4.3) and 2.5 (1.3–4.8), respectively]. Among women >33 years of age, parity 2 was associated with a significantly lower risk of diabetes diagnosis compared with parity 1, whereas parity 4 + was associated with a significantly higher risk of diabetes diagnosis compared with parity 1. Conclusions  The study shows that the risk of diabetes diagnosis increases with parity in young Danish women. This may support a causal association between diabetes and parity.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Naver, K.V.","Lundbye-Christensen, Søren","Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Nilas, L.","Secher, N.J.","Rasmussen, S.","Ovesen, P."],"cuid":["S03-094.64-001867"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":3,"keyword":["Cohort","Diabetes","Multiparity","Parity","Pregnancy"],"level":"sci","mra":["med","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CDR"],"OT":["Kardiologisk Afdeling, Aalborg Sygehus, Århus Universitetshospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CDR","DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"parity and risk of diabetes in a danish nationwide birth cohort","src":["aau","au","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2010.03169.x","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S03-094.64-001867","identifier":[{"id":"WOS:000285752700008","type":"wos"},{"id":"21166844","type":"pmid"},{"id":"78650254801","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-25151cdc-da8c-4b10-a11a-35f65bd4bce9","au-d48ba047-25bd-41ac-83b4-53c67a696d58","ku-bebd2ee2-ced5-40c7-abb2-882a9f028c2c"],"keyword":["cohort","diabetes","multiparity","parity","pregnancy"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E8AD0068BDA4A4A13B4C817B248D8D1E"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2010.03169.x/abstract","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1464-5491.2010.03169.x","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Aarhus University, Faculty of Health Sciences, Kardiologisk Afdeling, Aalborg Sygehus"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["Kardiologisk Afdeling, Aalborg Sygehus, Århus Universi