{"abstract":"The treelet transform (TT) is a recent data reduction technique from the field of machine learning. Sharing many similarities with principal components analysis (PCA), TT can reduce a multidimensional data set to the projections on a small number of directions or components which account for much of the variation in the original data. However, in contrast to PCA, TT produces sparse components. This can greatly simplify interpretation. We describe the tt Stata add-on for performing TT. The add-on includes a Mata implementation of the TT algorithm, alongside other functionality to aid the practical application of TT. We show how a basic exploratory data analysis using the tt add-on might look.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-116736"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Dimension reduction","Factor analysis","PCA","treelet"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"tt treelet transform with stata","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dr","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/53333477/R_2011_09.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-116736","ids":["aau-e56c2a7e-b003-4d50-85de-fdc3cd8640d3"],"keyword":["PCA","dimension reduction","factor analysis","treelet"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-1F4C4EB3DF795E647A9419643A4220A1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/53333477/R_2011_09.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nor