{"abstract":"We thank Imamura and Jacques (1) for their insightful commentary on our article (2), in which they go beyond the treelet transform (TT) to critically discuss the relevance of sparsity in dietary pattern analysis. ... (1) Imamura F, Jacques PF. Invited commentary: dietary pattern analysis. Am J Epidemiol 2011;173(0):000-000. (2) Gorst-Rasmussen A, Dahm CC, Dethlefsen C, et al. Exploring dietary patterns by using the treelet transform. Am J Epidemiol 2011;173(0):000-000.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Gorst-Rasmussen, Anders","Dahm, Christina C","Dethlefsen, Claus","Scheike, Thomas","Overvad, Kim"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-007234"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"level":"sci","mra":["med"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["Kardiovaskulært Forskningscenter, Aalborg Sygehus, Aarhus Universitetshospital"],"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"gorst rasmussen et al respond to dietary pattern analysis","src":["aau","au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-AU"],"type":"djc","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/aje/kwr059","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-007234","identifier":[{"id":"79955755519","type":"scopus"},{"id":"WOS:000290323400003","type":"wos"},{"id":"21474586","type":"pmid"}],"ids":["aau-955fb0f4-c70a-4773-a3eb-d5fbc5834b2b","au-316462a5-b507-4d78-a67e-efd612ea11b8"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Medical Science"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-9330067AD4DA18EB7979E10CAFF3F527"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1093/aje/kwr059","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://aje.oxfordjournals.org/content/early/2011/04/07/aje.kwr059.full.pdf+html","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1",